aci = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say/said) (d:<a> and <ci> written as one word: he or she says, said; before a noun, the one who says or the thing that is called so) (j:a/ci) (r:zd:15581/zd:21701/zd:12327) (q:draft)
aci nuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:mean/intend to say) (d:<aci>, he says, and <nuam>, want: want to say, that is mean; stands after the words that give the meaning, or after <bang>, what, to ask what someone means; with other persons {ka ci nuam}, I mean) (r:zd:21701/zd:20406) (q:draft)
aciah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:went back/returned/who returns) (d:<a> and <ciah> written as one word: he went home, or the one who goes back) (j:a/ciah) (r:zd:15296/zd:25322) (q:draft)
