aciahkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:leave/go home/depart) (d:<a> and <ciahkhia>, leave for home, written as one word: he or they left, or the one who leaves) (j:a/ciahkhia) (r:zd:14699/zd:11389/zd:21338) (q:draft)
aciahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:leave/depart/go home) (d:<a> and <ciahkhiat> written as one word: he or they leave a place, used before words such as <ciangin> and <nading>) (j:a/ciahkhiat) (r:zd:11389/zd:19063) (q:draft)
aciahkhiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:to leave/will leave) (d:<a>, <ciahkhiat> and <ding> written as one word: that he or they leave, their leaving that is yet to happen; with <phallo>, not allowed to leave) (j:a/ciahkhiat/ding) (r:zd:11642/zd:11736) (q:draft)
aciahkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:have returned/have gone back) (d:<a> and <ciahkhin> written as one word: he has gone back, those who have already gone back) (j:a/ciahkhin) (r:zd:20912) (q:draft)
aciahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:return/go back/come back) (d:<a> and <ciahkik> written as one word: he, she or they return, or the one who returns) (j:a/ciahkik) (r:zd:21035/zd:11986/zd:16710) (q:draft)
aciahkikding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:will return/be going to go back) (d:<a>, <ciahkik> and <ding> written as one word: that he or they will go back, or the going back that is to come) (j:a/ciahkik/ding) (r:zd:20181/zd:14881) (q:draft)
aciahlam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/everyday) (w:on the way back/on the way home) (d:<a>, <ciah>, return, and <lam>, way, written as one word: while he, she or they were going back home, often followed by <in>) (j:a/ciah/lam) (r:zd:12261/zd:19465/zd:15228) (q:draft)
aciahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:his return/his way home) (d:<a> and <ciahna> written as one word: his or her going home; {aciahna lampi} is the way by which he goes home) (j:a/ciahna) (r:zd:11269/zd:11350) (q:draft)
