adalna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/home) (w:barrier/divider/screen) (d:<a> and <dalna> written as one word: the thing that blocks or screens, placed before the name of the barrier, as in {lamzikpi adalna Road Divider}, the divider of the highway) (j:a/dalna) (r:zd:12523/zd:20535/zd:19112) (q:draft)
adamkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:recover/get well again) (d:<a> and <damkik> written as one word: he or she recovers, those who recover) (j:a/damkik) (r:zd:25180) (q:draft)
adamkiktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be able to recover/can get well again) (d:<a>, <dam> and <kiktheih> written as one word: that he or she can get well again; before <nading>, so that he or she may recover) (j:a/dam/kiktheih) (r:zd:12304/zd:17372) (q:draft)
adamlai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/everyday) (w:still alive/surviving/while alive) (d:<a> and <damlai> written as one word: who is still alive, the surviving members of a family; {adamlai in} is while he was alive) (j:a/damlai) (r:zd:17838/zd:19523) (q:draft)
adamlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:sick/ill/the sick one) (d:<a> and <damlo> written as one word: who is sick, the one who is not well) (j:a/damlo) (r:zd:13110/zd:17949/zd:12267) (q:draft)
adamloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be unwell/be sick) (d:<a> and <damloh> written as one word: he or she is unwell, used before words such as <ciangin> and <sung>) (j:a/damloh) (r:zd:17448/zd:24029) (q:draft)
adammawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:sick/ill/unwell) (d:<a> and <dammawh> written as one word: the one who is sick, sick) (j:a/dammawh) (r:zd:17049/zd:11648) (q:draft)
adamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:heal/cure/relieve) (d:<a> and <damsak> written as one word: he or it heals, that which cures; {adamsak nadingin} is in order to cure) (j:a/damsak) (r:zd:16849) (q:draft)
adamsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:recover completely/be fully healed) (d:<a> and <damsiang>, be completely healed, written as one word: he or she is fully cured, or that an illness is fully cured) (j:a/damsiang) (r:zd:12600/zd:19493) (q:draft)
adan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:its way/its manner/condition) (d:<a> and <dan> written as one word: the way, manner or condition of it; often paired as {adan leh azia}) (j:a/dan) (r:zd:19453/zd:17060) (q:draft)
adang = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:other/another/the rest) (d:<dang>, other, with the prefix <a>, written as one word: stands before a noun or a number, as in {adang mi 17}, 17 other people, or alone for the others or something else) (s:dang) (r:zd:15368/zd:24289/zd:23590) (q:draft)
adang khatpa = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:the other one/the other man) (d:{a dang}, the other, and <khatpa>, one man: the second of two men just spoken of, often after a sentence about the first; followed by <pen> or <in> as the subject) (r:zd:15828/zd:11984/zd:15167) (q:draft)
adangdang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:other/various other/the others) (d:<a> and <dangdang> written as one word: the various others, other ones of any kind) (j:a/dangdang) (r:zd:12647/zd:17841/zd:17643) (q:draft)
adangkhat = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:another/another one/the other one) (d:<a>, <dang> and <khat> written as one word: one more person or thing, different from the one already named) (j:a/dang/khat) (r:zd:20076/zd:23977/zd:12630) (q:draft)
adangkhatpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:the other one/the remaining one) (d:<adangkhat>, the other one, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: as for the other one, said after the first one or the others have been named) (j:adangkhat/pen) (r:zd:11420/zd:11721) (q:draft)
adangkhatzong = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:another one too/yet another) (d:<adangkhat>, another one, and <zong>, also, written as one word after a noun: another one as well) (j:adangkhat/zong) (r:zd:20225/zd:18116) (q:draft)
adangzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:others too/also other/in addition) (d:<a>, <dang>, other, and <zong>, also, written as one word: others as well, in addition to those already named; in news reports before the number of further people) (j:a/dang/zong) (r:zd:13089/zd:19745) (q:draft)
adawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:stick out/show/appear) (d:<a> and <dawk> written as one word: it sticks out, shows or comes into view; of a name, appear, and of the body, be exposed) (j:a/dawk) (r:zd:12341/zd:13314) (q:draft)
adawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/politics) (w:floor/storey/level) (d:<a> and <dawl> written as one word: the floor or storey of a building, and a level or tier; {adawl tungnung} is the upper floor, also said of the upper house of a parliament) (j:a/dawl) (r:zd:21327/zd:17295) (q:draft)
adawldawl = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:level by level/in stages/step by step) (d:<a> with <dawl>, level, said twice: one level after another, in stages; usually with <in>) (j:a/dawl) (r:zd:25275/zd:17383) (q:draft)
adawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:drink) (d:<a> and <dawn>, drink, written as one word: he or she drinks, what one drinks; {anek adawn} is food and drink) (j:a/dawn) (r:zd:16832/zd:21025) (q:draft)
adawn = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:answer/reply) (d:<a> with <dawn>, here the form of <dawng>, answer, used before <kik>: {adawn kikna} is his or their reply) (j:a/dawn) (r:zd:12280) (q:draft, low confidence)
adawnding = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:food) (w:to drink/for drinking) (d:<a> and <dawnding> written as one word: what he is to drink, his drink) (j:a/dawnding) (r:zd:12093/zd:11941) (q:draft)
adawnding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel/family) (w:meet/fetch/pick up) (d:<a>, <dawn>, go to meet, and <ding> written as one word: in order to meet or fetch someone who is arriving) (j:a/dawn/ding) (r:zd:13034/zd:15756) (q:draft)
adawng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:answer/reply) (d:<a> and <dawng>, answer, written as one word: he or she answered, or the one who answers) (j:a/dawng) (r:zd:21655/zd:24361/zd:17271) (q:draft)
adawnkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:drank/who drank) (d:<a> and <dawnkha> written as one word: the one who came to drink something, mostly something harmful drunk unawares) (j:a/dawnkha) (r:zd:17605/zd:17538) (q:draft)
adawnkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:happen to drink/have drunk) (d:<a>, <dawn>, drink, and <khak>, happen to, written as one word: he came to drink something; {adawnkhak manin} is because of having drunk it) (j:a/dawn/khak) (r:zd:17538/zd:17605) (q:draft)
adawnkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:after drinking/have drunk) (d:<adawn>, he or she drinks, and <khit>, after, written as one word; {adawnkhit ciangin} is after he or she had drunk it) (j:adawn/khit) (r:zd:17605) (q:draft)
adawnkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:his reply/her reply/answer) (d:<a> and <dawnkikna>, reply, written as one word: his or her reply; {adawnkikna ah} is in reply) (j:a/dawnkikna) (r:zd:19579/zd:22828) (q:draft)
adawnlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:tip/top end/far end) (d:<a>, <dawn>, tip, and <lam>, side, written as one word: the top or far end of a long thing; of a clan, the younger branch as against <bul>, the root) (j:a/dawn/lam) (r:zd:16045/zd:17175) (q:draft)
adawnna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:reply/answer/response) (d:<a> and <dawnna> written as one word, here from <dawng>, answer, and not from drinking: his or their reply) (j:a/dawnna) (r:zd:25918/zd:11463) (q:draft)
adawnsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:give to drink/make drink) (d:<a> and <dawnsak> written as one word: he or she made someone drink, the one who or the thing that was given to drink) (j:a/dawnsak) (r:zd:14772/zd:16961) (q:draft)
adawt = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:stab) (d:<a> and <dawt>, stab, written as one word: he stabbed, the one who stabbed; {temtawh adawt} is who stabbed with a knife) (j:a/dawt) (r:zd:12972/zd:13061) (q:draft)
adawtgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:stab repeatedly/stab badly) (d:<a>, <dawt> and <gawp> written as one word: stabbed someone many times or severely, and the one who did so) (j:a/dawt/gawp) (r:zd:19437/zd:17701) (q:draft)
adawtgawppa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:the one who stabbed/stabber) (d:<a>, <dawt>, stab, and <gawppa>, the man who does it severely, written as one word: the man who stabbed someone badly or many times) (j:a/dawt/gawppa) (r:zd:17701/zd:20282) (q:draft)
adawtlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:stab to death) (d:<a>, <dawt> and <lum>, here to death, written as one word: he or she stabbed someone to death, or the one who did so) (j:a/dawt/lum) (r:zd:17701/zd:16834) (q:draft)
adawtlumpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:man who stabbed to death/stabber) (d:<adawtlum> with <pa>, which marks a man, written as one word: the man who stabbed someone to death; in news reports also said of the man who stabbed a person who lived) (j:adawtlum/pa) (r:zd:11814/zd:20282) (q:draft)
adawtlup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:stab/stab down) (d:<a> and <dawtlup> written as one word: he stabbed someone down, or the one who was stabbed) (j:a/dawtlup) (r:zd:11904/zd:12738) (q:draft)
adawtpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:stabber/attacker) (d:<a>, <dawt>, stab, and <pa>, man, written as one word: the man who stabbed someone) (j:a/dawt/pa) (r:zd:16698/zd:16899) (q:draft)
addict = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/social) (w:addict/addiction) (d:a person who cannot stop taking or doing something, or the state of being so; placed after the thing, as in {phone addict}) (o:English) (r:zd:20060/zd:9448) (q:draft)
adding = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (j:ading) (r:zd:22746/zd:21690) (q:draft)
address = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/it) (w:address) (d:the address of a home, a workplace or an email account) (o:English) (r:zd:10892/zd:19188/zd:21015) (q:draft)
adeih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want/like) (d:<a> and <deih>, want, written as one word: he wants, what one wants, the one who wants; {adeih huai} is desirable) (j:a/deih) (r:zd:11400/zd:25616) (q:draft)
adeihbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as he wishes/as they please) (d:<a> and <deihbang> written as one word: in whatever way he or they want, usually followed by <in>) (j:a/deihbang) (r:zd:12553/zd:20132) (q:draft)
adeihdeih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:whatever one wants/anything one likes) (d:<a> and <deihdeih> written as one word: whatever he, she or they want, each thing that is wanted) (j:a/deihdeih) (r:zd:15358/zd:25919) (q:draft)
adeihhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:desirable/agreeable) (d:<a> and <deihhuai> written as one word: that is to be wished for; with <lohna>, a thing that is not desirable about something) (j:a/deihhuai) (r:zd:11166/zd:12341) (q:draft)
adeihlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:not want/oppose/dislike) (d:<a> and <deihlo> written as one word: who does not want or accept something, the one who is against it) (j:a/deihlo) (r:zd:25625) (q:draft)
adeihloh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unwanted/disliked/not wanted) (d:<a> and <deihloh>, not wanted, written as one word: what someone does not want or like) (j:a/deihloh) (r:zd:19427/zd:12553) (q:draft)
adeihlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:his opposition/their objection) (d:<a> and <deihlohna> written as one word: his, her or their not wanting something, their opposition to it) (j:a/deihlohna) (r:zd:24234) (q:draft)
adeihmahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want very much/like very much) (d:<a> and <deihmahmah> written as one word: what he, she or they want very much, the one much wanted) (j:a/deihmahmah) (r:zd:18054/zd:25768) (q:draft)
adeihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:meaning/sense) (d:<a> and <deihna> written as one word: what a word, name or saying means, what is meant by it) (j:a/deihna) (r:zd:19418/zd:19299) (q:draft)
adeihna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:wish/will/purpose) (d:<a> and <deihna> written as one word: what he or she wants, his or her will or purpose) (j:a/deihna) (r:zd:19257/zd:23437) (q:draft)
adeihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:care for/wish well/support) (d:<a> and <deihsak> written as one word: he wishes someone or something well, or the one who cares for and supports a person or a cause) (j:a/deihsak) (r:zd:22079/zd:13207) (q:draft)
adeihte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who want/whoever wishes) (d:<a> and <deihte> written as one word: those who want it, anyone who wishes) (j:a/deihte) (r:zd:10993/zd:20620) (q:draft)
adeihteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:all that one wants/everything wanted) (d:<a> and <deihteng> written as one word: all that he, she or they want) (j:a/deihteng) (r:zd:12628/zd:19738) (q:draft)
adeihzah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:amount wanted/as much as one wants) (d:<a> and <deihzah> written as one word: the amount or number that he or they want) (j:a/deihzah) (r:zd:16968/zd:24946) (q:draft)
Adelaide = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Adelaide) (d:city in the south of Australia where a Zomi community lives) (r:zd:20244/zd:18890) (q:draft)
adelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:chase/pursue/go after/rush to) (d:<a> and <delh>, pursue, written as one word: he or she chases someone, or hurries to a place or an event; also the one who does so) (j:a/delh) (r:zd:11761/zd:19134/zd:20176) (q:draft)
adelhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/politics) (w:pursuit/chase) (d:<a> and <delhna>, pursuit, written as one word: his or their chasing of someone; also the rushing of police or reporters to the place of an event) (j:a/delhna) (r:zd:21341/zd:19854) (q:draft)
adelhpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:rush to/go after at once) (d:<a> and <delhpah> written as one word: he or they hurried there at once, went straight after someone) (j:a/delhpah) (r:zd:17703/zd:18145) (q:draft)
adem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:contend/compete/rival) (d:<a> and <dem>, contend, written as one word: the one who contends or competes, as for an office; {adem omlo} is without a rival) (j:a/dem) (r:zd:12183/zd:12055) (q:draft, low confidence)
aden = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:later/afterwards/in the end) (d:after a while, at a later point in what is told, mostly as {aden ciangin} or {aden teh}, later on; this is not the sense always of <den>) (r:zd:15199/zd:17313) (q:draft)
adenciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:later/afterwards/after a while) (d:<aden> and <ciang> written as one word: later on, after some time) (j:aden/ciang) (r:zd:17782/zd:11717) (q:draft)
adendeuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:a little later/somewhat later) (d:<aden>, later, and <deuh>, somewhat, written as one word, mostly before <ciangin>: a little later on) (j:aden/deuh) (r:zd:12494/zd:16834) (q:draft)
adengkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hit/strike) (d:<a> and <dengkha> written as one word: it hit, said of something that falls or flies and strikes a person or a vehicle) (j:a/dengkha) (r:zd:16111/zd:17256) (q:draft)
adenglum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:strike dead/crush to death) (d:<a> and <denglum> written as one word: of a heavy thing that falls, it struck someone dead) (j:a/denglum) (r:zd:14818/zd:16007) (q:draft)
adenkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be struck by/be hit by/fall on) (d:<a>, <den> and <khak> written as one word, the form of <dengkha> before a noun: the person or thing that something falling or flying has struck) (j:a/den/khak) (r:zd:18028/zd:18074/zd:11532) (q:draft)
adenkhakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:impact/being struck) (d:<adenkhak> with the noun ending {-na}: the event of something falling on and striking people or things, or the place where it struck) (b:adenkhak) (r:zd:14628/zd:19692) (q:draft)
adenlup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:strike down/crush/that was struck down) (d:<a> and <denlup>, strike down or crush, written as one word: it struck down, and the one that was struck down, said of lightning and of falling things) (j:a/denlup) (r:zd:19646) (q:draft)
adenlupkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be struck down/be crushed) (d:<a>, <denlup> and <khak> written as one word: the one whom a falling thing or lightning happened to strike down) (j:a/denlup/khak) (r:zd:13138/zd:19088) (q:draft)
adiakdiak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:especially/in particular/above all) (d:<adiak> and <diak> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: most especially, above all) (j:adiak/diak) (r:zd:11759/zd:18099/zd:21961) (q:draft)
adiakdiakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:especially/above all/in particular) (d:<a> and <diakdiakin> written as one word: most especially, standing before the person or thing that is singled out) (j:a/diakdiakin) (r:zd:24029/zd:23301/zd:23554) (q:draft)
adiakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:especially/in particular) (d:<a> and <diakin> written as one word, often at the start of a sentence: especially, above all) (j:a/diakin) (r:zd:17055/zd:23148) (q:draft)
adikkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:inhale/breathe in) (d:<a> and <dikkha> written as one word: he breathed it in, or before <te> and <mi> those who breathed in smoke or gas) (j:a/dikkha) (r:zd:15481/zd:13009) (q:draft)
adikleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if it is right/if correct) (d:<a>, <dik> and <leh>, if, written as one word: if it is correct) (j:a/dik/leh) (r:zd:12336) (q:draft)
adiklo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/education) (w:wrong/incorrect/not right) (d:<adik>, what is right, and <lo>, not, written as one word: that which is not right, a mistake) (j:adik/lo) (r:zd:15489/zd:15814) (q:draft)
adim = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:full/filled) (d:<a> and <dim>, full, written as one word: full, that which is full; {adim in} is in full or filling the place, and {adim phitphet} is brimful) (j:a/dim) (r:ts:3882/zd:12790/zd:25097) (q:draft)
adimin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:full/in full load) (d:<adim>, full, and <in> written as one word: filling the place or the vehicle, with a full load of what is named before it) (j:adim/in) (r:zd:14895/zd:15331/zd:14722) (q:draft)
adimtak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/travel) (w:full/fully loaded) (d:<a> and <dimtak> written as one word; {adimtak in} is to the full, with a full load) (j:a/dimtak) (r:zd:14628/zd:12790) (q:draft)
adingbek = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:only for/just for) (d:<ading> and <bek> written as one word: for that one only) (j:ading/bek) (r:zd:19257/zd:12269) (q:draft)
adinginzong = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:also for/even for) (d:<adingin>, for, and <zong>, also, written as one word after a noun: for that one too) (j:adingin/zong) (r:zd:22107/zd:15935) (q:draft)
adingzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be able to stand/be established) (d:<a>, <ding>, stand, and <zo>, be able, written as one word: it manages to stand, to be set up or to hold its place) (j:a/ding/zo) (r:zd:22361/zd:16337) (q:draft)
adinkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:set out/depart/get up and leave) (d:<a> and <dinkhiat> written as one word: its setting out, of a plane or ship, or a person getting up to leave) (j:a/dinkhiat) (r:zd:20501/zd:17844) (q:draft)
adinlaitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:while standing) (d:<a>, <din> and <laitak> written as one word: at the very time when he or she was standing somewhere) (j:a/din/laitak) (r:zd:15437/zd:19667) (q:draft)
adinmun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:situation/position/status/standing) (d:<a> and <dinmun> written as one word: his, her, its or their situation, position or standing) (j:a/dinmun) (r:zd:11587/zd:25923/zd:14791) (q:draft)
adjust = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:adjust/fit to) (d:bring into line with something else, used after <tawh>) (o:English) (r:zd:16037) (q:draft, low confidence)
Administration = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:administration/government) (d:the governing of a town, district or country and the office that does it, as in {Tedim Administration zumpi}; after the name of a president, his government) (o:English) (r:zd:20883/zd:24909) (q:draft, low confidence)
Administrator = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:administrator) (d:an official who runs an office, a district or an organisation) (o:English) (r:zd:21843) (q:draft, low confidence)
admission = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/travel) (w:admission/enrolment) (d:acceptance into a school or university, with <bawl>, <ngah> or <pia>; also the admitting of people into a country) (o:English) (r:zd:15622/zd:23533) (q:draft)
ado = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:fight/attack/who fights) (d:<a> and <do> written as one word: he or they fight, the one who fights against; {gal ado} is wage war) (j:a/do) (r:zd:25582/zd:12179) (q:draft)
adodo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:keep fighting/keep opposing) (d:<ado>, he or they fight, with <do> said again, written as one word: goes on fighting or opposing, the ones who keep fighting; {gal adodo} is keep waging war) (j:ado/do) (r:zd:15874/ts:7989) (q:draft)
adon = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:pay attention/care for/attend to) (d:<a> and <don> written as one word: he heeds or attends to, the one who heeds; {adon lo} is who disregards) (j:a/don) (r:zd:14791/zd:13114) (q:draft)
adong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:ask/inquire) (d:<a> and <dong> written as one word: he or she asks, or the one who asks) (j:a/dong) (r:zd:24502/zd:21655) (q:draft)
adot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ask/he asked) (d:<a> and <dot> written as one word: he or she asks, used before <leh>, <hangin> and <ciangin>) (j:a/dot) (r:zd:12669/zd:20289/zd:23136) (q:draft)
adotleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:when he asked/when she asked) (d:<adot> and <leh> written as one word: when he or she asked, followed by the answer) (j:adot/leh) (r:zd:12085) (q:draft)
aduh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:like/crave/want) (d:<a> and <duh> written as one word: he or she likes or craves it, what one craves, or with <te> those who like it; <duh> here is to want or be fond of, mostly of food) (j:a/duh) (r:zd:21961/zd:19447) (q:draft)
aduhleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:if he wants/if he craves) (d:<aduh>, he wants or craves it, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if he or she wants it) (j:aduh/leh) (r:zd:14879) (q:draft)
aduhlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:not like/not want) (d:<a> and <duhlo> written as one word: he or she does not like or want it; with <te>, those who do not like it) (j:a/duhlo) (r:zd:19447/zd:17022) (q:draft)
adum = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:blue/the blue one) (d:<a> and <dum>, blue, written as one word: what is blue, the blue colour; also said of violet) (j:a/dum) (r:zd:22289/zd:21703) (q:draft, low confidence)
advance = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:advanced/ahead) (d:further on in knowledge or development; {advance zaw} is more advanced) (o:English) (r:zd:21134/zd:15274) (q:draft, low confidence)
advertise = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/work) (w:advertise/advertisement) (d:make goods known to the public in order to sell them, also the notice itself) (o:English) (r:zd:20207) (q:draft, low confidence)
advertisement = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:advertisement/advertising) (d:a public notice that makes goods or a company known, in Zolai also called {kyawngia} from Burmese) (o:English) (r:zd:20207/zd:16748) (q:draft)
advice = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:advice/counsel) (d:guidance given by someone who knows the matter, mostly of legal, medical or official advice; said with <pia>, give) (o:English) (r:zd:18159/zd:17903) (q:draft)
adviser = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:adviser/advisor) (d:a person who gives advice, as a post in a government or an organisation) (o:English) (r:zd:17838) (q:draft, low confidence)
Advisors = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:advisers/advisors) (d:the English plural used in Zolai for the people who advise a leader or the committee of an organisation) (o:English) (r:zd:21217/zd:24333) (q:draft, low confidence)
Advocate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:advocate/lawyer) (d:a lawyer admitted to plead in court, also used as a title before a name; also someone who speaks up for a cause) (o:English) (r:zd:16210) (q:draft, low confidence)
Aedes = (i:1) (t:name) (f:health/nature) (w:Aedes) (d:the kind of mosquito that carries dengue and the Zika virus, written with <thokang> or <tho> after it) (o:Latin) (r:zd:14650/zd:12941) (q:draft)
Afarica = (i:1) (t:name) (f:travel/politics) (j:Africa) (r:zd:17495) (q:draft)
Afghan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics) (w:Afghan) (d:of Afghanistan or its people; {Afghan mi} is an Afghan) (r:zd:11180/zd:10877/zd:12759) (q:draft)
Afghanistan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics) (w:Afghanistan) (d:country in Central Asia) (r:zd:26163/zd:12176) (q:draft)
AFPFL = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:AFPFL/Anti-Fascist People's Freedom League) (d:the party that governed Burma after independence, known in Burmese as Pha-Sa-Pa-La; in 1958 it split into the Clean and the Stable AFPFL) (o:English) (r:zd:24714/zd:25263) (q:draft)
Africa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Africa) (d:the continent of Africa, mostly as {Africa gam}; also in the names of its countries, as South Africa) (r:zd:23754/zd:20334) (q:draft)
African = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:African) (d:of Africa or its people, the English word used before a noun or with <te>; {African te} are the Africans) (o:English) (r:zd:14502/zd:11027) (q:draft)
agaal = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (j:agal) (r:zd:10694) (q:draft)
agah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/everyday) (w:its fruit/its result) (d:<a> and <gah> written as one word: the fruit of a plant, or the result of work or conduct; before a verb also it bears fruit) (j:a/gah) (r:zd:21822/zd:11251/zd:20657) (q:draft)
agahte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/everyday) (w:its fruits/its results/those that bear fruit) (d:<a> and <gahte> written as one word: the fruits or results of it; after the name of a tree also those that bear fruit) (j:a/gahte) (r:zd:11837/zd:24029) (q:draft)
agai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:be pregnant/conceive) (d:<a> and <gai> written as one word: she is pregnant, and her being pregnant; {agai lam} is the fact that she is pregnant) (j:a/gai) (r:zd:17372/zd:21793/zd:15286) (q:draft)
agaikhah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/health) (w:heavily pregnant/far gone in pregnancy) (d:said of a woman far on in pregnancy, mostly as {nupi agaikhah mahmah}, a heavily pregnant woman; <agai>, she is pregnant, with a second part that is not explained) (r:zd:14599/zd:11729) (q:draft, low confidence)
agaisak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/health) (w:one who made pregnant) (d:<a> and <gaisak>, make pregnant, written as one word before a noun: the man who made her pregnant) (j:a/gaisak) (r:zd:11782) (q:draft)
agal = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:across/at a distance/from afar) (d:<a> and <gal>, the far side, written as one word: the other side, a place some way off; {agal panin} is from across or from a distance, and {agal et} is look on from afar) (j:a/gal) (r:zd:12564/zd:21439) (q:draft)
agalkap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:his soldiers/their troops) (d:<a> and <galkap> written as one word: his soldiers, their army) (j:a/galkap) (r:zd:10746/zd:18142) (q:draft)
agalkap = (i:2) (t:v) (f:media) (w:shoot at/fire at) (d:in reports of shootings, after <thautawh>, with a gun: shoot at someone, apparently <agal>, from a distance, with <kap>, shoot) (j:agal/kap) (r:zd:17491/zd:15976) (q:draft, low confidence)
agalkapte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:his soldiers/its troops) (d:<a> and <galkapte> written as one word: his or their soldiers) (j:a/galkapte) (r:zd:10746/zd:12183) (q:draft)
agalkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:the other side/the opposite side/a distance) (d:<a> and <galkhat> written as one word: the side across from a place, or a place some way off, as in {agalkhat panin}, from across the way) (j:a/galkhat) (r:zd:12345/zd:17664) (q:draft)
agallam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:opposite side/across from) (d:<a> and <gallam> written as one word: the side across from a place; after a place name with <ah>, across from it) (j:a/gallam) (r:zd:15539/zd:14906) (q:draft)
