aisan = (i:2) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:cast lots/divine) (d:the same word used as a verb, followed by <uh> or <in>: cast lots or read omens to find out or decide something) (r:zd:15384/zd:23928) (q:draft)
ait = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:love/hold dear) (d:<a> and <it> written as one word: he loves, or the one who loves; {Zomi ait} is one who loves the Zomi) (j:a/it) (r:zd:23974/zd:24481) (q:draft)
aitam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:I wonder) (d:word that ends a question and gives it a tone of wondering or doubt: I wonder, could it be; a form of everyday speech, compare <ahitam>) (r:zd:15926/zd:24289/zd:24427) (q:draft, low confidence)
aitang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:representative/substitute/stand-in) (d:one who stands in the place of another or of a group; {aitang in} is on behalf of, in place of, and {aitang dingin} is to represent, to replace) (r:zd:17965/ts:5469/ts:10215) (q:draft)
aitangin = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:social/politics) (w:on behalf of/representing/in the name of) (d:<ai> and <tangin> written as one word, placed after the name of a group or land: acting or speaking for it, as its representative) (s:tangin) (j:ai/tangin) (r:zd:16340/zd:24171/zd:21161) (q:draft)
Aizawl = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Aizawl) (d:capital city of Mizoram State in India) (r:zd:17168/ts:2349/zd:23856) (q:draft)
aizong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:however/but/even so) (d:spoken form of {ahi zong}, though it is so: however, but, placed at the beginning of a sentence; repeated after two words it means whether the one or the other) (r:zd:17760/zd:23086/zd:26097) (q:draft)
aizongin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:however/but/even so) (d:<aizong> with <in>, the spoken form of <ahizongin>: however, but; {bangbang aizongin} is whatever the case may be) (s:ahizongin) (b:aizong) (r:zd:11259/zd:16897) (q:draft)
Ajil = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:politics/travel) (w:Ajil) (d:place in Hulu Terengganu, Malaysia, known for its immigration detention centre) (r:zd:15356/zd:15165) (q:draft)
ak = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature/food) (w:chicken/fowl/rooster) (d:the domestic fowl, a chicken; {ak a khuang} is the rooster crows) (s:aak/aklui) (q:draft)
akaan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:exceed/be in excess) (d:<a> with a verb meaning go beyond, which is not <kaan>, white, written as one word; found in the pair {aval akaan}, beyond what is needed, to excess, beside <aval>) (r:zd:19453/zd:23090) (q:draft, low confidence)
akahding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/education) (w:who is to attend/in order to attend) (d:<a> and <kahding> written as one word: the one who is to attend, or with <in>, in order to attend a school, a meeting or a program) (j:a/kahding) (r:zd:12805/zd:16809) (q:draft)
akahkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:education) (w:one who attends) (d:<a>, <kah> and <khat> written as one word, after <sang>, school: one who goes to school, a student at the place named) (j:a/kah/khat) (r:zd:19465/zd:11783) (q:draft)
akahlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:be still attending/while at school) (d:<a> and <kahlai> written as one word: he or she is still attending school, while he or she was attending) (j:a/kahlai) (r:zd:14552/zd:16946) (q:draft)
akahlaitak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:be attending/be studying in) (d:<a> with <kah> in the sense attend school, and <laitak>, at the very time, written as one word after the name of a class or school: who is in that class at the time; {Tan 9 akahlaitak} is one who is in Grade 9) (j:a/kah/laitak) (r:zd:13320/zd:15828) (q:draft)
akahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:weeping/crying) (d:<a> and <kahna> written as one word: his, her or their weeping; {akahna aw} is the sound of their crying) (j:a/kahna) (r:zd:11672) (q:draft)
akahna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:climbing/going up/attending) (d:<a> with <kah>, go up, and the noun ending {-na}, written as one word: his or their climbing of a building, coming into office, or attending of a school) (j:a/kah) (r:zd:19707/zd:16710) (q:draft)
akahngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:once attended/used to attend) (d:<a>, <kah>, attend, and <ngei>, ever, written as one word: who has attended a school before) (j:a/kah/ngei) (r:zd:17750) (q:draft)
akahpan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:be attending/have just started attending) (d:<a>, <kah>, attend, and <pan>, here only just, written as one word, placed after the name of a school or class: one who is now attending it, who has just begun there) (j:a/kah/pan) (r:zd:11995/zd:17505) (q:draft, low confidence)
akahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/family) (w:send to school/attend school) (d:<a> and <kahsak> written as one word: he or she sends a child to school; also said of the child who attends) (j:a/kahsak) (r:zd:11758/zd:15994) (q:draft)
akahto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:climb up/go up) (d:<a> and <kahto> written as one word: he climbs up, the one who climbs up; {akahto te} are those who climb) (j:a/kahto) (r:zd:15501/zd:21426) (q:draft)
akahtoh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go up/climb/rise) (d:<a> and <kahtoh> written as one word: he, she or it goes up, climbs or rises, before words such as <ciangin> and {laitak in}) (j:a/kahtoh) (r:zd:15756/zd:17143/zd:14829) (q:draft)
akahtohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:his going up/where one climbed up) (d:<a> and <kahtohna> written as one word: his going up, or the place he climbed up to) (j:a/kahtohna) (r:zd:21929/zd:19763) (q:draft)
akai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:pull/draw/tow) (d:<a> and <kai>, pull, written as one word: that pulls or draws, as the horse that pulls a cart) (j:a/kai) (r:zd:15974/zd:14557) (q:draft)
akaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:pull/draw) (d:<a> and <kaih>, pull, written as one word: he pulls, or that which someone or something pulls; also in set phrases such as {dai akaih}, cordon off) (j:a/kaih) (r:zd:13328/zd:19428) (q:draft)
akaihkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:pull out/drag out) (d:<a> and <kaihkhiat> written as one word: he or they pull someone or something out, before words such as <ciangin>, <nadingin> and <laitak>) (j:a/kaihkhiat) (r:zd:17517/zd:18872) (q:draft)
akaihkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:collect/gather) (d:<a> and <kaihkhop>, the form of <kaikhawm>, collect, written as one word: what he or they collected, or the collecting of it, said of money and of things) (j:a/kaihkhop) (r:zd:16257/zd:24074) (q:draft)
akaikhawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:collector/gatherer/recruiter) (d:<a> and <kaikhawm> written as one word: one who gathers or collects things or money, or who recruits people) (j:a/kaikhawm) (r:zd:24068/zd:20505) (q:draft)
akaikhawmkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:who keeps recruiting/who keeps gathering) (d:<a>, <kai>, pull, and <khawmkhawm>, keep gathering, written as one word: the ones who go on gathering or recruiting people) (j:a/kai/khawmkhawm) (r:zd:11906/zd:18123) (q:draft)
akaikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:pull out/drag out) (d:<a> and <kaikhia> written as one word: he pulls or drags out, the one who dragged out) (j:a/kaikhia) (r:zd:12224) (q:draft)
akalkawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:groin/crotch/private parts) (d:<a> and <kalkawm> written as one word: his or her groin, the part of the body between the legs; in the articles a polite word for the private parts) (j:a/kalkawm) (r:zd:16047/zd:14748) (q:draft)
akalsuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:proceed/go forward/walk) (d:<a> and <kalsuan>, take steps, written as one word; in the articles mostly of a country, a group or a plan that goes forward on a chosen course) (j:a/kalsuan) (r:zd:24743/zd:11994) (q:draft)
akam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his mouth/her mouth) (d:<a>, his, her or its, and <kam>, mouth, written as one word; {akam panin} is by mouth, and {akam pha} is he or she is lucky) (j:a/kam) (r:zd:11681/zd:17501) (q:draft)
akamciam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:he promised/she promised/they promised) (d:<a> and <kamciam> written as one word: he, she or they promised) (j:a/kamciam) (r:zd:17572/zd:11917) (q:draft)
akammal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (w:word/wording) (d:<a> and <kammal> written as one word: his, her or its word or words) (j:a/kammal) (r:zd:22658/zd:22595) (q:draft)
akampau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:his speech/his words/way of speaking) (d:<a> and <kampau> written as one word: what he or she says, or the way he or she speaks; also the speaking itself) (j:a/kampau) (r:zd:21659/zd:14768/zd:20746) (q:draft)
akamsung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his mouth/inside of its mouth) (d:<a> and <kamsung> written as one word: his, her or its mouth, the inside of the mouth) (j:a/kamsung) (r:zd:15283/zd:22178/zd:15067) (q:draft)
akamtam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:talkative) (d:<a> and <kamtam> written as one word: one who talks much, is talkative) (j:a/kamtam) (r:zd:21463) (q:draft)
akamtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:body/everyday) (w:with his mouth/with her mouth/by mouth/verbally) (d:<akam> and <tawh> written as one word: with his, her or its mouth, also in words) (j:akam/tawh) (r:zd:15067/zd:12594) (q:draft)
akamzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:body) (w:his mouth also/its mouth too) (d:<akam> and <zong> written as one word: his, her or its mouth as well) (j:akam/zong) (r:zd:16976/zd:15911) (q:draft)
akancian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate/look into/examine) (d:<a>, <kan> and <cian> written as one word: look closely and thoroughly into a matter, said of police and other authorities) (j:a/kan/cian) (r:zd:12647/zd:19540/zd:20514) (q:draft)
akancianding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:will investigate/is to look into) (d:<akancian>, investigate thoroughly, and <ding>, will, written as one word: that they will or are to look closely into a matter) (j:akancian/ding) (r:zd:16490/zd:12557) (q:draft)
akanciansan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate/look into closely) (d:<a>, <kan>, inquire, and <cian>, clearly, with the ending {-san}, written as one word: he or they are looking closely into a matter; {akanciansan laitak} is the investigation is under way) (r:zd:20982/zd:13056) (q:draft)
akanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:to investigate/to inquire into/to look for) (d:<a>, <kan> and <ding> written as one word: in order to look into a matter, cover news or search for a person) (j:a/kan/ding) (r:zd:14818/zd:20050) (q:draft)
akanding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:to cross) (d:{a kan ding} written as one word, with <kan> in the sense of cross over: in order to cross a road) (r:zd:14709) (q:draft, low confidence)
akang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/nature) (w:burn/catch fire) (d:<a> and <kang> written as one word: it burns or burned; {mei akang} is a fire broke out, and before a noun it is the thing that burned) (j:a/kang) (r:zd:12502/zd:13009) (q:draft)
akang = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:white) (d:<a> and <kang> written as one word: white, the white one) (j:a/kang) (r:zd:14890/zd:14583) (q:draft)
akanggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:burn badly/be gutted by fire/be scorched) (d:<a> and <kanggawp>, burn badly, written as one word: it burned badly or burned down, or the thing that did; {mei akanggawp} is was destroyed by fire) (j:a/kanggawp) (r:zd:13222/zd:18947/zd:13213) (q:draft)
akangkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/travel) (w:a white one) (d:<akang> and <khat> written as one word after a noun: one that is white, as in {mawtaw akangkhat}, a white car) (j:akang/khat) (r:zd:16826/zd:14799) (q:draft)
akanglum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:burn to death) (d:<a> and <kanglum> written as one word: who burned to death, or the fire killed them) (j:a/kanglum) (r:zd:12048/zd:15820) (q:draft)
akangtum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:burn down/be burnt up) (d:<a> and <kangtum> written as one word: burned down, the one that was destroyed by fire) (j:a/kangtum) (r:zd:16621/zd:11383/zd:15410) (q:draft)
akankan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:investigate/look into/study) (d:<a> and <kankan> written as one word: he or they keep searching into a matter) (j:a/kankan) (r:zd:15180/zd:23329) (q:draft)
akankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate/who investigates) (d:<a> and <kankhia>, search out, written as one word: he investigates, or the one who investigates a case or a crime) (j:a/kankhia) (r:zd:19801/zd:20526/zd:16720) (q:draft)
akankhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:to investigate/who will investigate) (d:<a> and <kankhiading> written as one word: the one that is to investigate a matter, or in order to investigate it) (j:a/kankhiading) (r:zd:15362/zd:12708) (q:draft)
akankhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate/find out/look into) (d:<a> and <kankhiat> written as one word: he or they investigate, what was found out; {akankhiat uhciangin} is when they looked into it) (j:a/kankhiat) (r:zd:14726/zd:14720) (q:draft)
akankhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:investigation/inquiry) (d:<a> and <kankhiatna> written as one word: his or their investigation; {akankhiatna ah} is according to their investigation) (j:a/kankhiatna) (r:zd:16143/zd:20099) (q:draft)
akankhiatsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:be investigating/be looking into) (d:<akankhiat>, investigate, with an ending that shows the action is going on, mostly before <laitak>: {akankhiatsan laitak} is they are investigating it at present) (b:akankhiat) (r:zd:21581/zd:15178) (q:draft)
akanlaitak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:while crossing) (d:<a>, <kan>, here cross a road, and <laitak>, while, written as one word: just as he or she was crossing the road) (j:a/kan/laitak) (r:zd:13188/zd:11350) (q:draft)
akanphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:cross/go across) (d:<a>, <kan>, here cross over, and <phei>, across, written as one word: he or she crosses a road or a railway, or the one crossing) (j:a/kan/phei) (r:zd:15451/zd:14709) (q:draft)
akansan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate/be investigating) (d:<a> with <kansan>, look closely into a matter, written as one word: they investigate it; said of police and authorities, often followed by <laitak>, be in the course of) (j:a/kansan) (r:zd:20282/zd:15461) (q:draft)
akansawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:try to investigate/intend to look into) (d:<a>, <kan>, look into, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: the ones who set out to investigate a matter) (j:a/kan/sawm) (r:zd:19801) (q:draft, low confidence)
akantan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:cross/pass through) (d:<a> with <kantan>, cross, written as one word: he or she crosses, or the one who crosses a road, a river or a stage) (j:a/kantan) (r:zd:14638/zd:15836/zd:17213) (q:draft)
akap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:weep/the one who weeps) (d:<a> and <kap>, weep, written as one word: the one who weeps; {adah akap khempeuh} is all who grieve and weep, the bereaved, in words of condolence) (j:a/kap) (r:zd:20263/zd:23471) (q:draft)
akapgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:shoot/open fire on/gun down) (d:<a> and <kapgawp> written as one word: he or they shot at people, firing many shots; also the one who shot) (j:a/kapgawp) (r:zd:12803/zd:15554) (q:draft)
akapgawp = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:cry hard/wail) (d:<a> with <kap>, weep, and <gawp> written as one word: he or she cried very hard) (j:a/kap/gawp) (r:zd:19565) (q:draft, low confidence)
