akiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:to fall/to serve) (d:<a>, <kia> and <ding> written as one word: that will or should fall; with <thong>, to serve a prison term, and of a person thought to have fallen) (j:a/kia/ding) (r:zd:22056/zd:16961) (q:draft)
akiakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:fall out/fall off) (d:<a> and <kiakhia> written as one word: it fell out or off, or the thing that fell off) (j:a/kiakhia) (r:zd:19902) (q:draft)
akiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:decrease/be reduced) (d:<a> and <kiam> written as one word: it has decreased, what is less, the one that is reduced) (j:a/kiam) (r:zd:15274/zd:25068/zd:23988) (q:draft)
akiamtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be able to decrease/can be reduced) (d:<akiam> and <theih>, be able, written as one word, before <nadingin>: so that it can go down) (j:akiam/theih) (r:zd:16715/zd:13184) (q:draft)
akiang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:nearby/beside it/near it) (d:<a> and <kiang> written as one word: the place beside him or it, its neighbourhood; {akim akiang} is the area all around) (j:a/kiang) (r:zd:24038/zd:14867) (q:draft)
akiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:the man who fell) (d:<akia>, the one that fell, and <pa>, man, written as one word: the man who fell) (j:akia/pa) (r:zd:12281) (q:draft)
akiasuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:fall down/fall out) (d:<a>, <kia>, fall, and <suak> written as one word: he or it fell down or out from a height, as from a roof or a window; perhaps only another spelling of <akiasuk>) (j:a/kia/suak) (r:zd:14572/zd:17517) (q:draft, low confidence)
akiasuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:fall down/fallen) (d:<a> and <kiasuk> written as one word: he or it fell down, or the one that fell down) (j:a/kiasuk) (r:zd:15489/zd:17115) (q:draft)
akiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fall/crash) (d:<a> and <kiat>, the form of <kia>, fall, written as one word: it fell, its falling; of an aircraft, crash; {akiat laitak} is the moment it fell) (j:a/kiat) (r:zd:11532/zd:16651) (q:draft)
akiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:will serve in prison/will fall) (d:<akiat>, he falls, and <ding>, will, written as one word: after <thong> and a length of time, the prison term he is to serve; elsewhere that it will fall) (j:akiat/ding) (r:zd:16717/zd:18139) (q:draft)
akiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:may be sentenced/can fall) (d:<a> and <kiathei> written as one word: that may fall; after <thong> and a length of time, liable to be sent to prison for that long) (j:a/kiathei) (r:zd:11594/zd:20300) (q:draft)
akiatkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:fall out/fall off) (d:<a>, <kiat> and <khiat> written as one word: the form of <akiakhia>, it fell out or off, used before words such as <laitak>, while) (j:a/kiat/khiat) (r:zd:19902/zd:17763) (q:draft)
akiatkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:after falling/have fallen) (d:<a>, <kiat>, fall, and <khit>, finished, written as one word: after it fell or crashed, mostly before <ciangin> or <phetin>) (j:a/kiat/khit) (r:zd:17517/zd:12831) (q:draft)
akiatlam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:that it fell/the falling) (d:<a>, <kiat>, fall, and <lam> written as one word: the fact that someone or something fell or dropped, as the thing known, noticed or reported) (j:a/kiat/lam) (r:zd:15715/zd:12831/zd:14799) (q:draft)
akiatleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if it falls/whether it falls) (d:<akiat> and <leh>, if, written as one word: if or whether it falls; {thong akiatleh akiatlohding} is whether he will go to prison or not) (j:akiat/leh) (r:zd:19725) (q:draft, low confidence)
akiatlian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:fall/crash) (d:<akiat>, it fell, with <lian>, which here means exactly and not large, written as one word: mostly in {akiatlian laitak}, at the very moment it fell or crashed) (j:akiat/lian) (r:zd:17713/zd:16007) (q:draft)
akiatlohding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will not fall/not to fall) (d:<akiat> and <lohding> written as one word: that it will not fall; after <akiatleh>, or not, as in {thong akiatleh akiatlohding}, whether he will go to prison or not) (j:akiat/lohding) (r:zd:19671) (q:draft, low confidence)
akiatma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:before it fell/before the crash) (d:<akiat> and <ma> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: before it or she fell, before an aircraft crashed) (j:akiat/ma) (r:zd:19480/zd:11376) (q:draft)
akiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:fall/crash/place of falling) (d:<a> and <kiatna> written as one word: its falling, said of an aircraft that crashes or a bomb that lands; {akiatna mun} is the place where it fell) (j:a/kiatna) (r:zd:18091/zd:13084/zd:19182) (q:draft)
akiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:sentence/bring down) (d:<a> and <kiatsak> written as one word: he or they made it fall; {thong akiatsak} is the prison term that was passed) (j:a/kiatsak) (r:zd:13127) (q:draft, low confidence)
akiatsuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:drop/let fall) (d:<a> and <kiatsuah> written as one word: he or she drops it, the thing that was dropped) (j:a/kiatsuah) (r:zd:26097/zd:19991) (q:draft)
akiatsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fall down/crash down) (d:<a>, <kiat> and <suk> written as one word: he, she or it falls down; {akiatsuk ciangin} is when it fell down) (j:a/kiat/suk) (r:zd:17713/zd:17079/zd:15372) (q:draft)
akiatsukna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:fall/place of the fall) (d:<a>, <kiat>, <suk> and <na> written as one word: his or its falling down, or, before a noun, where it fell down) (j:a/kiat/suk/na) (r:zd:17517/zd:11783) (q:draft)
akiatzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:after falling/after it fell) (d:<akiat>, it fell, and <zawh>, after, written as one word: after the fall of a person or the crash of an aircraft) (j:akiat/zawh) (r:zd:15403/zd:13110) (q:draft)
akiau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (j:akiu) (r:zd:11248/zd:15084) (q:draft)
akibang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:same/alike/similar) (d:<a> and <kibang> written as one word: that is the same, that is like; <tawh akibang> is like, similar to) (j:a/kibang) (r:zd:17162/zd:22802/zd:15754) (q:draft)
akibangding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to be like/so as to resemble) (d:<akibang>, alike, and <ding> written as one word: so as to be the same; {tawh akibangding in} is so that it is like) (j:akibang/ding) (r:zd:14795) (q:draft)
akibangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:equally/alike/likewise) (d:<a> and <kibangin> written as one word: in the same way; after <tawh>, together with and in the same way as) (j:a/kibangin) (r:zd:15996/zd:25110/zd:11296) (q:draft)
akibanglo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:different/unlike/not the same) (d:<a>, <kibang> and <lo> written as one word: that which is not alike, different) (j:a/kibang/lo) (r:zd:14865/zd:24064/zd:25562) (q:draft)
akibangpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the same one/what is like) (d:<akibang>, the same or alike, with the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the one that is the same, or with <tawh> the thing that is like something) (j:akibang/pen) (r:zd:12336/zd:19447) (q:draft)
akibangpian = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:resembling/similar-looking/something like) (d:<akibang>, that is like, and <pian>, likeness, written as one word: that looks like or is of the same kind as the thing named before it with <tawh>) (j:akibang/pian) (r:zd:16970/zd:18063) (q:draft)
akibat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:alike/similar/the same) (d:<a> and <kibat>, be alike, written as one word; with <tawh> it means be like something, and with <loh> or <kei> not be the same) (j:a/kibat) (r:zd:14581/zd:24381/zd:24068) (q:draft)
akibatloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be different/not be alike) (d:<a> and <kibatloh> written as one word: its not being alike; with <hang>, although not the same, and with <ciangin>, when it differs) (j:a/kibatloh) (r:zd:11852/zd:21369) (q:draft)
akibatlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:difference/unlikeness) (d:<a> and <kibatlohna> written as one word: the difference, their being unlike) (j:a/kibatlohna) (r:zd:21739/zd:24279) (q:draft)
akibatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be the same as/share/be alike with) (d:<a> and <kibatpih> written as one word: the one that is like another or has the same thing in common, as in {biakna akibatpih}, of the same religion) (j:a/kibatpih) (r:zd:15091/zd:15732) (q:draft)
akibawlbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health/work) (w:keep being done/be under way) (d:<a> and <kibawlbawl> written as one word: something is being done again and again or is going on, as treatment, an inspection or repair work; with {laitak in}, while it was being done) (j:a/kibawlbawl) (r:zd:12359/zd:21244) (q:draft)
akibawlbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:be made in addition/be added/be done further) (d:<a> and <kibawlbeh> written as one word: more of something was made or done, as a further charge in court) (j:a/kibawlbeh) (r:zd:20676/zd:16621) (q:draft)
akibawlcil = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:when first made/at first) (d:<akibawl> and <cil>, at the beginning, written as one word: when it was first made, or when a matter was first handled) (j:akibawl/cil) (r:zd:11506/zd:12142) (q:draft)
akibawlding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be held/be done/be treated) (d:<a>, <kibawl> and <ding> written as one word: that will be held or done; of an injured person taken to hospital, to be treated) (j:a/kibawl/ding) (r:zd:12827/zd:17234/zd:13034) (q:draft)
akibawlhiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:whether it was made/whether it is done) (d:<akibawl>, that is made or done, and the question word <hiam> written as one word: whether something was made or done, in an indirect question before <cih>) (j:akibawl/hiam) (r:zd:11433/zd:20008) (q:draft)
akibawlkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:while being treated/while being done) (d:<a>, <kibawl>, be done or be treated, and <kawm>, while, written as one word and followed by <in>: while it is being done, while he is being treated) (j:a/kibawl/kawm) (r:zd:12490/zd:14624) (q:draft)
akibawlkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:be recorded/happen to be made) (d:<a>, <kibawl>, be made, and <kha>, happen to, written as one word: that happened to be made; in news reports of a video recording that a camera happened to make of an event) (j:a/kibawl/kha) (r:zd:19465/zd:13078/zd:16137) (q:draft)
akibawlkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be manufactured/be produced/be made) (d:<akibawl> and <khia> written as one word: that is made or produced, said of goods from a company or a country) (j:akibawl/khia) (r:zd:13161/zd:20345) (q:draft)
akibawlkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:have been done/be finished/be completed) (d:<a>, <kibawl>, be done, and <khit>, finished, written as one word: when it has been done; {akibawlkhit ciangin} is after it was done and {akibawlkhit asawtlo} not long after it was done) (j:a/kibawl/khit) (r:zd:20535/zd:17239/zd:16045) (q:draft)
akibawllai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:while being done/still being done) (d:<a>, <kibawl>, be done, and <lai>, the time when, written as one word and followed by <in>: while it is being done or held) (j:a/kibawl/lai) (r:zd:20263) (q:draft)
akibawlleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:when it is done/if it is done) (d:<akibawl>, it is done or made, and <leh>, if or when, written as one word: when or if a thing such as an operation or a court case is carried out) (j:akibawl/leh) (r:zd:17085) (q:draft)
akibawlma = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:before it was done/before it is carried out) (d:<akibawl>, it is made or done, and <ma>, before, written as one word: before something is carried out, often followed by <in>) (j:akibawl/ma) (r:zd:12996/zd:11681) (q:draft)
akibawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:where it is done/its being done) (d:<a> and <kibawlna> written as one word: the place, time or occasion at which something is made, done or held) (j:a/kibawlna) (r:zd:21551/zd:13355) (q:draft)
akibawlni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:day it was held/day it was made) (d:<akibawl>, that is made or held, and <ni>, day, written as one word: the day on which a thing was done or held, as a report, an operation or an election) (j:akibawl/ni) (r:zd:11484/zd:20320) (q:draft)
akibawlpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:what was made/what was held) (d:<akibawl>, that which is made or done, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the thing made, the event held or the act done, as the topic of the sentence) (j:akibawl/pen) (r:zd:16563/zd:13133) (q:draft)
akibawlsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:ready-made/already made/prepared) (d:<a> and <kibawlsa>, already made, written as one word: that has been made, prepared or registered beforehand) (j:a/kibawlsa) (r:zd:23925/zd:22193/zd:19818) (q:draft)
akibawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be done for/be made for/be performed on) (d:<a> and <kibawlsak> written as one word: that which is made, done or carried out for or on someone, as an operation, a test or a document) (j:a/kibawlsak) (r:zd:19981/zd:13215) (q:draft)
akibawlsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be under way/be being done) (d:<akibawl>, is made or done, with an added ending whose sense is not certain; before <laitak> it says that something is being carried out at this very time) (b:akibawl) (r:zd:20721/zd:20732) (q:draft, low confidence)
akibawlsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be planned/be attempted/be about to be held) (d:<aki> and <bawlsawm> written as one word: that was planned or attempted, that people intended to hold or carry out) (j:aki/bawlsawm) (r:zd:15602/zd:20254) (q:draft)
akibawlsia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be mistreated/be abused) (d:<a> and <kibawlsia> written as one word: who is mistreated or abused, the one harmed; with {nang leh nang}, harming yourself) (j:a/kibawlsia) (r:zd:22812/zd:22778) (q:draft)
akibawlsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:be persecuted/be mistreated) (d:<a> and <kibawlsiat> written as one word: who is persecuted or abused, the fact of being mistreated) (j:a/kibawlsiat) (r:zd:14947) (q:draft)
akibawlsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:persecution/mistreatment/abuse) (d:<a> and <kibawlsiatna> written as one word: the mistreatment that he, she or they suffered, the fact of their being persecuted) (j:a/kibawlsiatna) (r:zd:21476/zd:15045) (q:draft)
akibawltawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:man-made/artificial/fake) (d:<a> and <kibawltawm> written as one word: made by people, not natural; after <atuh> it says that goods are counterfeit) (j:a/kibawltawm) (r:zd:11438/zd:22805/zd:19307) (q:draft)
akibawlte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those made/things done) (d:<akibawl> with the plural <te>, written as one word: the things that were made or done, the ones that were made) (j:akibawl/te) (r:zd:20367/zd:22457) (q:draft)
akibawltheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:can be made/can be done) (d:<akibawl> and <theih> written as one word: that it can be made or carried out; {akibawltheih nadingin} is so that it can be done) (j:akibawl/theih) (r:zd:14519/zd:15397) (q:draft)
akibawlzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:have been made/be carried out/be completed) (d:<a> and <kibawlzawh> written as one word: that has been made or done, after it was done; {akibawlzawh nading} is so that it can be done) (j:a/kibawlzawh) (r:zd:17017/zd:11076/zd:19493) (q:draft)
akibawlzong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:also be made/also be done) (d:<akibawl>, that which is made or done, and <zong>, also, written as one word: some are also made or done so, those also made) (j:akibawl/zong) (r:zd:12280/zd:11167) (q:draft)
akibehlap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be added/increase) (d:<a> and <kibehlap> written as one word: it is added, or before a noun what has been added; {akibehlap toto} is keeps increasing) (j:a/kibehlap) (r:zd:16942/zd:11707/zd:24141) (q:draft)
akibehlapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:the addition/the increase) (d:<a> and <kibehlapna> written as one word: the adding of something, or the place or time at which more was added) (j:a/kibehlapna) (r:zd:17572) (q:draft)
akibeng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be struck/be beaten/be knocked) (d:<a> and <kibeng> written as one word: that is struck or beaten, the one being beaten; of a coffin, being knocked on) (j:a/kibeng) (r:zd:16926/zd:17779) (q:draft, low confidence)
akibuai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:be in turmoil/be in conflict/be in commotion) (d:<a> and <kibuai> written as one word: it is in trouble or uproar, or the one that is in turmoil; said of a place in conflict and of people in a commotion) (j:a/kibuai) (r:zd:25622/zd:15043) (q:draft)
akibuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:be raped) (d:<a> and <kibuan> written as one word: was raped, the one who was raped) (j:a/kibuan) (r:zd:17510/zd:11193) (q:draft)
akibuangawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:fight/brawl/grapple) (d:<a> and <kibuan>, grapple with each other, with <gawp>, violently, written as one word: they fought hand to hand, seizing and striking one another) (j:a/kibuan/gawp) (r:zd:15577/zd:19151) (q:draft)
akibuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:struggle/assault) (d:<a> and <kibuanna> written as one word: their struggling with each other, or the place or occasion of an assault) (j:a/kibuanna) (r:zd:16504) (q:draft, low confidence)
akibucip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be hidden/hide oneself) (d:<aki> and <bucip> written as one word: that is hidden, he is hiding) (j:aki/bucip) (r:zd:18161/zd:19262) (q:draft)
akibuding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:in order to hide) (d:<a>, <kibu> and <ding> written as one word, usually before <in>: so as to hide oneself, to take cover) (j:a/kibu/ding) (r:zd:14919/zd:14611) (q:draft)
akibung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:overturn/capsize/roll over) (d:<a>, <ki> and <bung> written as one word: a vehicle or boat that turned over, the one that overturned) (j:a/ki/bung) (r:zd:16334/zd:14888/zd:12906) (q:draft)
akibut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:overturn/turn over/derail) (d:<a> with <kibut>, of a vehicle or a train: it turned over or left the track, the one that overturned) (j:a/kibut) (r:zd:16334/zd:13171) (q:draft, low confidence)
akicial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be hired/be employed) (d:<a> and <kicial> written as one word: he, she or they were hired for pay; the one who is hired) (j:a/kicial) (r:zd:11934/zd:20197/zd:12434) (q:draft)
akiciamteh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:be recorded/be regarded as/be listed) (d:<a> and <kiciamteh> written as one word: that is recorded or regarded; after <in> it means recorded as, regarded as) (j:a/kiciamteh) (r:zd:12567/zd:16784/zd:15397) (q:draft)
akician = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:exact/definite/certain/detailed) (d:<a> and <kician>, firm and sure, written as one word: what is definite and reliable; {akician in} is exactly, in detail, said of knowing or telling a matter) (j:a/kician) (r:zd:22618/zd:23977/zd:20203) (q:draft)
akiciangtan = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:limited/fixed/set/restricted) (d:<a> and <kiciangtan> written as one word: that which is limited or fixed, as {akiciangtan hun}, the set time) (j:a/kiciangtan) (r:zd:23670/zd:12557) (q:draft)
akicianin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:exactly/in detail/for certain) (d:<akician> and <in> written as one word: exactly, in detail, said of knowing, telling or examining a matter) (j:akician/in) (r:zd:11048/zd:15788) (q:draft)
akicianlian = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:exact/precise) (d:<akician>, definite, with <lian>, here exactly, written as one word: the exact one; {akicianlian in} is exactly, precisely) (j:akician/lian) (r:zd:20850/zd:13034) (q:draft)
akiciantak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:clearly/definitely/exactly) (d:<a> and <kiciantak> written as one word: clear and definite, in a definite way) (j:a/kiciantak) (r:ts:5132/zd:19373) (q:draft)
akicianzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:media/everyday) (w:more exact/more detailed/clearer) (d:<a>, <kician> and <zaw> written as one word: the more exact or fuller one; {akicianzaw in} is in more detail) (j:a/kician/zaw) (r:zd:11532/zd:20492/zd:19222) (q:draft)
akiciaptehna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:record/commemoration) (d:<a> and <kiciaptehna> written as one word: the record of something, the place or the day in which it is noted and remembered) (j:a/kiciaptehna) (r:zd:11262/zd:24134) (q:draft)
akicih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be called/be said) (d:<a> and <kicih> written as one word: what is called, that it is said, used before nouns and endings) (j:a/kicih) (r:zd:21369/zd:13348/zd:25173) (q:draft)
akicihna = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:so-called/the place called) (d:<a> and <kicihna> written as one word, placed after a name: that which is called by this name, as {Lake Abaya akicihna}, the place called Lake Abaya) (j:a/kicihna) (r:zd:20076/zd:16225) (q:draft)
akiciliang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:that is even called/so-called) (d:<a> and <kiciliang> written as one word, placed after a name or description: that is even called so, that goes by that name) (j:a/kiciliang) (r:zd:15890/zd:18872) (q:draft)
akicim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:collapse/that collapsed) (d:<a> and <kicim> written as one word: it collapsed, or the one that collapsed, said of buildings, roads and bridges) (j:a/kicim) (r:zd:17584/zd:20749) (q:draft)
akicimsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:collapse/fall in) (d:<a> and <kicimsuk> written as one word: it collapsed, or the one that collapsed, said of buildings, ceilings and ground) (j:a/kicimsuk) (r:zd:17256/zd:14969/zd:21244) (q:draft)
akicin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be complete/be fulfilled/be enough) (d:<a> and <kicin> written as one word: it is complete, fulfilled or sufficient; {akicin lohna} is where something is lacking) (j:a/kicin) (r:zd:15572/zd:20045/ts:10698) (q:draft)
akicing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:complete/sufficient/full) (d:<a> and <kicing> written as one word: what is complete or enough; {akicing in} or {akicing takin} is in full, sufficiently) (j:a/kicing) (r:zd:23988/zd:14831/zd:24316) (q:draft)
akicingin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:fully/completely/in full) (d:<a> and <kicingin> written as one word: in full, with nothing lacking; {athu akicingin} is the whole of the matter, in full detail) (j:a/kicingin) (r:zd:18046/zd:17166) (q:draft)
akicinglo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:insufficient/incomplete/lacking) (d:<a> and <kicinglo> written as one word: that which is not enough or not complete) (j:a/kicinglo) (r:zd:14831/zd:15941) (q:draft)
akicingtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:fully/sufficiently/in full) (d:<a> and <kicingtak> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: in full, enough, as of time that is given) (j:a/kicingtak) (r:zd:16009/zd:20365) (q:draft)
akicingzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:more complete/fuller) (d:<a> and <kicingzaw> written as one word: the fuller one; {akicingzaw in} is more fully, in full) (j:a/kicingzaw) (r:zd:11405/zd:16325/zd:17877) (q:draft)
akicinu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the woman called/woman named) (d:<akici>, that is called, and <nu>, woman, written as one word after a name: the woman so called) (j:akici/nu) (r:zd:11943) (q:draft)
akicip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:collapse/cave in) (d:<a> and <kicip> written as one word: it collapses, said of a building, a wall or the ground) (j:a/kicip) (r:zd:20749/ts:2349/zd:17777) (q:draft)
akicipa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the man called/man named) (d:<a> and <kicipa> written as one word: the man who is called by the name that stands before it) (j:a/kicipa) (r:zd:20000/zd:16924) (q:draft)
akicipen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the one called/the so-called) (d:<akici>, that is called, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, placed after a name: the one called by that name, as the topic of the sentence) (j:akici/pen) (r:zd:20023/zd:13332) (q:draft)
akicipna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:collapse/place of collapse) (d:<a> and <kicipna> written as one word: the collapsing of a building, a tower or the ground, or the place where it gave way) (j:a/kicipna) (r:zd:19303/zd:20456) (q:draft)
akicipsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:collapse/fall in/cave in) (d:<akicip>, it collapses, with <suk>, down, written as one word: it collapses downward, said of a building, a tower or a ceiling) (j:akicip/suk) (r:zd:19303/zd:19002) (q:draft)
akicite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:those called/the so-called) (d:<a> and <kicite> written as one word and placed after a name: those who are called by that name, the so-called) (j:a/kicite) (r:zd:12425/zd:11558) (q:draft)
akidal = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be protected/be shielded) (d:<a> and <kidal> written as one word: it is shielded or protected, or shields itself, from something) (j:a/kidal) (r:zd:12589/zd:16450) (q:draft)
akidalna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:barrier/divider/guardrail/fence) (d:<a> and <kidalna> written as one word: what screens or blocks off, in the news mostly the divider or guardrail of a road) (j:a/kidalna) (r:zd:17856/zd:14581) (q:draft)
akidawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/home) (w:laid across/stretched out/spanning) (d:<a> and <kidawh> written as one word: that is stretched or laid out, said of a bridge, flyover or pier built across something and of a cloth held out) (j:a/kidawh) (r:zd:20749/zd:15362) (q:draft)
akidawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be seen/be exposed/stick out) (d:<a> and <kidawk> written as one word: that shows, that is exposed or sticks out) (j:a/kidawk) (r:zd:21013/zd:14997) (q:draft)
akidawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be careful/what is guarded against) (d:<a> and <kidawm> written as one word: he is careful, the one who takes care, or the thing one guards against) (j:a/kidawm) (r:zd:11759/zd:11574) (q:draft)
akidawt = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be stabbed/was stabbed) (d:<a>, <ki> and <dawt> written as one word: he or she was stabbed) (j:a/ki/dawt) (r:zd:12823/zd:22267) (q:draft)
akidawtliam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/health) (w:be stabbed and wounded) (d:<a>, <ki> and <dawtliam> written as one word: he or she was wounded by stabbing) (j:a/ki/dawtliam) (r:zd:22030) (q:draft)
akidawtlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be stabbed to death) (d:<a>, <ki>, <dawt>, stab, and <lum>, to death, written as one word: was stabbed to death, the one stabbed to death; with {amah leh amah}, stabbed himself or herself to death) (j:a/ki/dawt/lum) (r:zd:17701/zd:16968) (q:draft)
akidawtna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/media) (w:stab wound/stabbing/being stabbed) (d:<akidawt>, was stabbed, with the ending {-na} written as one word: the place where a person was stabbed, the wound, or the stabbing itself) (j:akidawt/na) (r:zd:17609/zd:20282) (q:draft)
akideih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be wanted/be needed/be popular) (d:<a> and <kideih> written as one word: it is wanted or required; of a person, wanted by the police, or much liked) (j:a/kideih) (r:zd:14740/zd:12623) (q:draft)
akidelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:rush to/give chase/chase one another) (d:<a> and <kidelh> written as one word: they hurry to a place, or they chase one another) (j:a/kidelh) (r:zd:16450/zd:22142) (q:draft)
akidelhleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<a>, <kidelh> and <leh> written as one word: when they chased one another) (j:a/kidelh/leh) (r:zd:16922) (q:draft, low confidence)
akidelhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/travel) (w:chase/pursuit) (d:<aki> and <delhna>, pursuit, written as one word: the chasing of someone, a chase; {akidelhna panin} is in the course of the chase) (j:aki/delhna) (r:zd:16450/zd:12921) (q:draft)
akidem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:compete/contest/run for) (d:<a> and <kidem> written as one word: competes, the one who competes, said of rivals in business, a contest or an election) (j:a/kidem) (r:zd:11844/zd:23597/zd:24354) (q:draft)
akidim = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:full of/filled with) (d:<a> and <kidim>, be filled, written as one word: that is full; after a noun with <tawh> it means full of or filled with that thing) (j:a/kidim) (r:zd:21426/zd:25433/zd:10992) (q:draft)
akido = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:fight/be at war) (d:<a> and <kido> written as one word: they fight each other, or the ones fighting; {gal akido} is they wage war) (j:a/kido) (r:zd:22597/zd:11862/ts:11323) (q:draft)
akidong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be asked/be questioned) (d:<a>, the verb prefix <ki> and <dong>, ask, written as one word: was asked, the one who was asked; of money, was asked for, collected) (j:a/ki/dong) (r:zd:21400/zd:19805) (q:draft)
akidop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be careful/take care/be on guard) (d:<a> and <kidop> written as one word: that someone is careful; {akidop nadingin} is so that they take care) (j:a/kidop) (r:ts:8105/zd:20008) (q:draft)
akidot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be asked/be questioned) (d:<a> and <kidot> written as one word, mostly as {akidot ciangin}: when he was asked) (j:a/kidot) (r:zd:12619/zd:11700) (q:draft)
akigak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:be tight/be crowded/be tense) (d:<a> and <kigak> written as one word: of time short, of a place or vehicle packed full, of relations between countries tense) (j:a/kigak) (r:zd:10660/zd:25068) (q:draft)
akigam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:be far from/be distant) (d:<a> and <kigam> written as one word, the first part of <kigamla>: that is far from something, after <tawh>) (j:a/kigam) (r:zd:22550) (q:draft)
akigam = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:akigawm) (r:zd:15820) (q:draft, low confidence)
akigamla = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:be far from/be distant/be at a distance of) (d:<a> and <kigamla> written as one word: that is far from, lying at the distance named; {akigamla lo} is not far away) (j:a/kigamla) (r:zd:20322/zd:21426/zd:19262) (q:draft)
akigamlatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:at a distance of/the distance away) (d:<a> and <kigamlatna>, distance apart, written as one word: after a measure, that lies so far away, as in {tai 3 akigamlatna}, three miles away) (j:a/kigamlatna) (r:zd:19262/zd:23281) (q:draft)
akigawm = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in total/altogether/combined) (d:<a> and <kigawm> written as one word: what is joined or added together; {akigawm in} is in total, altogether, and before a noun it means that has joined) (j:a/kigawm) (r:zd:20387/zd:11582/zd:15905) (q:draft)
akigawmkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:joined together/united/combined) (d:<a> and <kigawmkhawm> written as one word: that are joined into one, united) (j:a/kigawmkhawm) (r:zd:17630/zd:25097) (q:draft)
akigeel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:be planned/be intended) (d:<a> and <kigeel>, be planned, written as one word: that is planned, it is planned; {dingin akigeel} is it is planned to) (j:a/kigeel) (r:zd:17668/zd:14888) (q:draft)
akigeelsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/travel) (w:be planned/be scheduled) (d:<akigeel>, it is planned, with <sa>, already: it had been planned or scheduled, often of a plan that did not come about) (j:akigeel/sa) (r:zd:17476/zd:17733) (q:draft)
akigel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be planned/be arranged) (d:<a> and <kigel>, be planned, written as one word: it is planned, that which is planned) (j:a/kigel) (r:ts:11162/zd:15726) (q:draft)
akigelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:be written/be recorded) (d:<a> and <kigelh> written as one word: it is written, or that which is written) (j:a/kigelh) (r:zd:22557/zd:12707/zd:15554) (q:draft)
akigelhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:where it is written/what is written) (d:<a> and <kigelhna> written as one word: the place or text in which something is written, mostly as {akigelhna ah}, in what is written) (j:a/kigelhna) (r:zd:13320/zd:13278) (q:draft)
akigen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be said/be spoken of/be told) (d:<a> and <kigen> written as one word: it is said, what is said or spoken of) (j:a/kigen) (r:zd:19602/zd:11714) (q:draft)
akigenkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:be stated/be announced) (d:<a> and <kigenkhia> written as one word: what has been stated or made known) (j:a/kigenkhia) (r:zd:14914/zd:11217) (q:draft)
akigenna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:what is said/report/account) (d:<a> and <kigenna>, the telling, written as one word: what is said or reported about something; {athu akigenna ah} is according to what is reported) (j:a/kigenna) (r:zd:21793/zd:16910) (q:draft)
akigenna ah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:according to reports/as reported/it is said that) (d:<akigenna>, what is said, and <ah>, in: in what is told, according to the report; it opens a news sentence, mostly as {athu akigenna ah}, and the sentence often ends in <kici> or <cihi>) (r:zd:21793/zd:22828) (q:draft)
akigensa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:already said/stated before/foretold) (d:<a> and <kigensa> written as one word: what has already been said or laid down; {akigensa ahihi} is it has been stated) (j:a/kigensa) (r:zd:13151/zd:19679) (q:draft)
akigin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:prepare/get ready) (d:<a> and <kigin>, get ready, written as one word: he or they get ready) (j:a/kigin) (r:zd:19164/zd:13270) (q:draft)
akiging = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be ready/be prepared) (d:<a> and <kiging> written as one word: is ready, the one who is prepared) (j:a/kiging) (r:zd:24068/zd:19947) (q:draft)
akigingsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:ready/prepared/on standby) (d:<a> and <kigingsa> written as one word, mostly followed by <in> and a form of <om>: in readiness, on the alert) (j:a/kigingsa) (r:zd:12420/zd:15811) (q:draft)
akigu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be stolen) (d:<a> and <kigu> written as one word: it was stolen, or beside a noun the one that was stolen) (j:a/kigu) (r:zd:19929/zd:17614) (q:draft)
akigual = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:line up/queue) (d:<a> and <kigual> written as one word: those who are lined up or standing in a queue) (j:a/kigual) (r:zd:19197/zd:20653/zd:12309) (q:draft)
akigukhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:was stolen/stolen) (d:<a> and <kigukhia>, be stolen away, written as one word: it was stolen, the thing that was stolen) (j:a/kigukhia) (r:zd:20661/zd:15568) (q:draft)
akihal = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be burned/be set on fire/burn) (d:<a> and <kihal>, be burned, written as one word: it was burning, or that which was set on fire; of a fire also one that was lit on purpose) (j:a/kihal) (r:zd:16772/zd:15288/zd:18145) (q:draft)
akihalsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be set on fire/be burned on purpose) (d:<a> and <kihalsak> written as one word: it was set on fire by someone, said of a fire that was started deliberately) (j:a/kihalsak) (r:zd:15461/zd:20717) (q:draft)
akihawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be distributed/be allotted/be shared out) (d:<a> and <kihawm> written as one word: that is divided or given out) (j:a/kihawm) (r:zd:20263/zd:24325/zd:24489) (q:draft)
akihawmkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:released/published/distributed) (d:<a> and <kihawmkhia> written as one word: that was released or published, of a film or of news) (j:a/kihawmkhia) (r:zd:14890) (q:draft)
akihel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be included/take part/be involved) (d:<a> and <kihel> written as one word: who takes part, that is included or involved, said of people in an event and of things in a whole) (j:a/kihel) (r:zd:11064/zd:21168/zd:11504) (q:draft)
akihelding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:will take part/be involved/be included) (d:<a>, <kihel>, take part, and <ding>, will, written as one word: who or what will take part or be included; {akihelding in aki ummawh} is suspected of being involved) (j:a/kihel/ding) (r:zd:20446/zd:14795/zd:14740) (q:draft)
akihelkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be involved/be included/be among) (d:<a>, <kihel> and <kha> written as one word: that happens to be involved or included in something) (j:a/kihel/kha) (r:zd:19082/zd:16598/zd:19127) (q:draft)
akihelkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:one who took part/one of those involved) (d:<akihel>, who takes part, and <khat>, one, written as one word: one who was involved in something or one who belongs to a group) (j:akihel/khat) (r:zd:16702/zd:16998) (q:draft)
akihelkhate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:participants/those involved/those who take part) (d:<akihelkha> with the plural <te>: the people who are involved in or take part in something) (b:akihelkha) (r:zd:20587/zd:22812) (q:draft)
akihello = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be included/be without) (d:<a> and <kihello> written as one word: the one that is not included, that which has nothing mixed in) (j:a/kihello) (r:ts:4909/zd:11941) (q:draft)
akihelna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:participation/involvement) (d:<a> and <kihelna> written as one word: his or their taking part, or that in which someone is involved) (j:a/kihelna) (r:ts:12037/zd:17760) (q:draft)
akihelte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:participants/members/those included) (d:<akihel> with the plural <te> written as one word: those who take part or are included) (j:akihel/te) (r:ts:11162/zd:17635) (q:draft)
akihelthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:can take part/who is able to join) (d:<a> and <kihelthei> written as one word: who can take part or is included, will be able to attend) (j:a/kihelthei) (r:ts:1405/zd:17377) (q:draft)
akihelzel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:take part regularly/be regularly included) (d:<a>, <kihel> and <zel> written as one word: one that is regularly included or regularly takes part) (j:a/kihel/zel) (r:zd:16313/zd:10662) (q:draft)
akihemkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:be evacuated/be moved out/be removed) (d:<a> and <kihemkhia> written as one word: who moved or were moved away from a place of danger, also of animals taken away) (j:a/kihemkhia) (r:zd:14712/zd:14871) (q:draft)
akihep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:move aside/get out of the way/step aside) (d:<a> and <kihep> written as one word: move to one side, clear out of the way, as a person off a railway track or a crowd off the road) (j:a/kihep) (r:zd:11780/zd:12347) (q:draft, low confidence)
akihhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:disgusting/loathsome/detestable) (d:<a> and <kihhuai> written as one word: disgusting, that which is loathsome) (j:a/kihhuai) (r:zd:16949/zd:24014) (q:draft)
