akitung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:reach/arrive at/come to) (d:<a> and <kitung> written as one word: it is reached, things have come as far as the point named) (j:a/kitung) (r:zd:24946) (q:draft, low confidence)
akitunna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:wrapping/covering) (d:<a> and <kitunna> written as one word: that in which someone is wrapped; {akitunna puanza} is the blanket he is wrapped in) (j:a/kitunna) (r:zd:25433) (q:draft, low confidence)
akitunna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:reaching/arriving at) (d:<a>, the verb prefix <ki> and <tunna>, arrival, written as one word: the fact of having come to a state or point, as in {hiciang dinmun akitunna}, having reached this situation) (j:aki/tunna) (r:zd:24950) (q:draft, low confidence)
akiu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:corner/its corner/edge) (d:<a> and <kiu>, corner, written as one word: the corner or edge of a thing or place; {akiu khat} is a corner somewhere) (j:a/kiu) (r:zd:10929/zd:15437) (q:draft)
akiva = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/education) (w:be skilled/be expert) (d:<a> and <kiva> written as one word: he is skilled in it, the one who is good at it) (j:a/kiva) (r:zd:13121/zd:17129) (q:draft)
akivaihawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:be organised/be arranged/be managed) (d:<a>, the passive <ki> and <vaihawm> written as one word: that is organised, arranged or run by someone) (j:a/ki/vaihawm) (r:zd:20276/zd:11392) (q:draft)
akivak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:make a living/live on) (d:<a> and <kivak> written as one word: who makes a living, the work marked by <tawh> or <in>) (j:a/kivak) (r:zd:12567/zd:16979/zd:12715) (q:draft)
akivawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be named/be called) (d:<a> and <kivawh> written as one word: that is named, when a name is given) (j:a/kivawh) (r:zd:23667) (q:draft)
akivel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:be examined/be checked) (d:<a> and <kivel> written as one word, mostly before <ciangin>: when it was examined) (j:a/kivel) (r:zd:16849/zd:17479) (q:draft)
akivui = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be buried) (d:<a> and <kivui> written as one word: he is buried, the one who is being buried) (j:a/kivui) (r:zd:15344/zd:20589) (q:draft)
