akizangthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:usable/that can be used) (d:<a>, <kizang>, be used, and <thei>, can, written as one word: what can be used, or it can be used) (j:a/kizang/thei) (r:zd:11383/zd:14869/zd:17607) (q:draft)
akizangzang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be in use/be being used) (d:<aki> and <zangzang> written as one word: it is in use all along, the one that is currently used) (j:aki/zangzang) (r:zd:12456/zd:15307) (q:draft)
akizasak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:be informed/be notified/be reported) (d:<a> and <kizasak> written as one word: who was informed, or that was reported) (j:a/kizasak) (r:zd:21627/zd:19447) (q:draft)
akizat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be used) (d:<a> and <kizat> written as one word: that it is used, its being used; before <theih>, <hangin> and similar words) (j:a/kizat) (r:zd:24544/zd:17355) (q:draft)
akizatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:use/usage) (d:<a> and <kizatna> written as one word: its being used, the use made of it; {akizatna mun} is the place where it is used) (j:a/kizatna) (r:ts:8477/zd:19824/zd:22864) (q:draft)
akizatsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be intended for use/be going to be used) (d:<aki> and <zatsawm> written as one word: what is planned to be used) (j:aki/zatsawm) (r:zd:12420/zd:20609) (q:draft)
akizatzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time/travel) (w:since it came into use/time in service) (d:<a>, <kizat> and <zawh> written as one word: from the time a thing began to be used; a length of time follows, as hours flown or years in service) (j:a/kizat/zawh) (r:zd:19480/zd:15031) (q:draft)
akizawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be finished/be completed) (d:<a> and <kizawh> written as one word: it is finished; {akizawh khit ciangin} is after it was finished) (j:a/kizawh) (r:zd:14579/zd:16433) (q:draft)
akizawh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:be defeated/be overcome) (d:<a> and <kizawh> written as one word, of an enemy: until he is defeated) (j:a/kizawh) (r:ts:4775) (q:draft, low confidence)
