anawkgawpna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/nature) (w:ramming/battering) (d:<a>, <nawkgawp> and the noun suffix <na> written as one word: its striking hard against something, of a vehicle or of flood water) (j:a/nawkgawp/na) (r:zd:19369/zd:12283) (q:draft)
anawkkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:hit/run into/knock down) (d:<a> and <nawkkha> written as one word: of a car, bus or train, strike a person or thing on its way) (j:a/nawkkha) (r:zd:15619/zd:21294) (q:draft)
anawkkha = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:pass by/pass through/go past) (d:<a> and <nawkkha> written as one word: come past a place on the way; {anawkkha te} are the passers-by, those who went through) (j:a/nawkkha) (r:zd:14694/zd:22641/zd:14662) (q:draft)
anawkkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:hit/run into/knock down) (d:<a>, <nawk> and <khak> written as one word: it hit, it ran into; said of a car, bus or train that strikes a person or another vehicle) (j:a/nawk/khak) (r:zd:13188/zd:17659/zd:14709) (q:draft)
anawkkhakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/nature) (w:collision/impact/being struck) (d:<a>, <nawk> and <khakna> written as one word: the hitting of something by a vehicle, or the sweeping of a fire over a place; with <hangin>, because it was hit) (j:a/nawk/khakna) (r:zd:14676/zd:20129) (q:draft)
anawkkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:after it hit/after it struck) (d:<a>, <nawk>, strike, and <khit> written as one word, followed by <ciangin>: after it struck, said of a vehicle or a storm) (j:a/nawk/khit) (r:zd:15245/zd:15074) (q:draft)
anawkna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:striking/hitting/onslaught) (d:<a> and <nawkna> written as one word: the striking of a place by a storm, flood, earthquake or other disaster; {huihpi in anawkna hangin} is because the storm struck) (j:a/nawkna) (r:zd:16858/zd:17717) (q:draft)
anawknawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:keep striking/keep passing/batter) (d:<a> and <nawk> said twice, written as one word: keep hitting or rushing past, of a storm or of vehicles) (j:a/nawk) (r:zd:17909/zd:11725) (q:draft, low confidence)
anawkphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:run into/plough through/rush across) (d:<a>, <nawk>, rush against, and <phei>, here across, written as one word: it drove or rushed across or through something, hitting what was in the way) (j:a/nawk/phei) (r:zd:20129/zd:19351/zd:16828) (q:draft)
anawkpheikha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:run into/crash into/hit) (d:<anawkphei> and <kha> written as one word: a vehicle happens to run into someone or something) (j:anawkphei/kha) (r:zd:17455/zd:17560) (q:draft)
anawksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:try to ram/attempt to rush into) (d:<a>, <nawk> and <sawm> written as one word: he tried or intended to drive into people, or to force a way into a place) (j:a/nawk/sawm) (r:zd:15454/zd:11880) (q:draft)
anawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:edge/side/roadside) (d:<a> and <nawl> written as one word: the edge or side of something; {lamzikpi anawl} is the side of the road) (j:a/nawl) (r:zd:18030/zd:12089) (q:draft)
anawngkai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be troublesome/trouble/disturb) (d:<a> and <nawngkai> written as one word: what is troublesome or a nuisance; {anawngkai sak} is disturb or cause trouble to someone) (j:a/nawngkai) (r:zd:17058/zd:15606) (q:draft)
anawngkaisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:trouble/disturb/affect) (d:<a> and <nawngkaisak> written as one word: it troubles, or the one that causes trouble to someone) (j:a/nawngkaisak) (r:zd:22877/zd:19499) (q:draft)
anawt = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:brush/scrub/wipe) (d:<a> and <nawt>, rub, written as one word: he or she rubs or scrubs a surface; {ha anawt} is brushes the teeth) (j:a/nawt) (r:zd:14587) (q:draft, low confidence)
anawt = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:advance/go forward/press on) (d:<a> and <nawt> written as one word after <ma>, front: he or she goes forward) (j:a/nawt) (r:zd:23959) (q:draft, low confidence)
anbel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/home) (w:cooking pot/food pot/food container) (d:pot in which food is cooked or carried, from <an>, food, and <beel>, pot; {sun-anbel} is a lunch box) (r:zd:14606/zd:20851) (q:draft)
anbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/food) (w:kitchen) (d:<an>, food, with <buk>, hut or shelter: a place where food is cooked) (q:draft)
anbuuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/food) (w:kitchen/cookhouse) (d:<an>, food, with <buuk>, hut or room: the room or building where food is cooked) (r:zd:11758/zd:15972) (q:draft)
Andaman = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/nature) (w:Andaman) (d:the Andaman Sea, south of Myanmar and west of Thailand, and the Andaman Islands of India) (r:zd:19054/zd:17649) (q:draft)
Andazih = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (j:Andru) (r:zd:22544) (q:draft)
Andhra = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Andhra Pradesh) (d:in the name Andhra Pradesh, a state in the south of India) (r:zd:19646) (q:draft)
anding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:food/feed) (d:<an>, food, and <ding>, for, written as one word: food for someone or for an animal; {sakol anding} is horse feed) (j:an/ding) (r:zd:21426/zd:11920) (q:draft)
Android = (i:1) (t:name) (f:it) (w:Android) (d:the operating system of Google for mobile phones, and the phones and applications that use it) (o:English) (r:zd:25824/zd:23049) (q:draft)
ane = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:eat/who eats) (d:<a> and <ne>, eat, written as one word: he or she eats, or the one who eats; {golhguk ane} is one who takes a bribe) (j:a/ne) (r:zd:15283/zd:14665/zd:21961) (q:draft)
aneding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:to eat/for eating) (d:<a> and <neding> written as one word: for him, her or it to eat; {aneding in} is in order to eat) (j:a/neding) (r:zd:19831/zd:13129) (q:draft)
aneek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:eat) (d:<a> and <neek> written as one word: he eats, what he eats; {aneek ding} is his food) (j:a/neek) (r:zd:19266/zd:15972) (q:draft)
anehphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:approach/go up to/come up to) (d:<a> and <nehphei> written as one word: he or they go up close to someone or something) (j:a/nehphei) (r:zd:12955/zd:19536) (q:draft)
anei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:having/who has/that has) (d:<a> and <nei> written as one word: he has, or before a noun the one who has; {lainatna anei mi} is a person who has compassion) (j:a/nei) (r:zd:17958/zd:26625/zd:20816) (q:draft)
aneiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will have/be going to have) (d:<a>, <nei>, have, and the future marker <ding> written as one word: he, she or they will have, or the one who is to have or is thought to have something) (j:a/nei/ding) (r:zd:22377/zd:21603) (q:draft)
aneih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have/possess) (d:<a> and <neih> written as one word: that he or she has, what one has, the having of it) (j:a/neih) (r:zd:23191/zd:15853) (q:draft)
aneihbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:have in addition/have another) (d:<a> and <neihbeh> written as one word: he or she has one more, or holds something once more) (j:a/neihbeh) (r:zd:18077/zd:20363) (q:draft)
aneihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:to have/be going to have) (d:<a> and <neihding> written as one word: that he or she is to have or is about to have; {pasal aneihding} is to take a husband) (j:a/neihding) (r:zd:15830/zd:20363) (q:draft)
aneihiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:whether he has/does he have) (d:<a> and <neihiam> written as one word: does he have, whether he or they have, closing a question) (j:a/neihiam) (r:zd:18161/zd:12099) (q:draft)
aneihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to have/should have) (d:<a> and <neihkhak> written as one word: he or they happen to have or to hold; before <zenzenleh>, if it should happen) (j:a/neihkhak) (r:zd:16259/zd:18908) (q:draft)
aneihkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:after having/after holding) (d:<a>, <neih>, have or hold, and <khit>, finished, written as one word, mostly before <uhciangin>: after they have had or held something, as an inspection, a protest or a child) (j:a/neih/khit) (r:zd:11115/zd:12985/zd:17731) (q:draft)
aneihlaitak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:while holding/while carrying out) (d:<a>, <neih> in the sense hold or conduct and <laitak> written as one word: at the very time when they were holding a prayer, a repair or a training) (j:a/neih/laitak) (r:zd:16794/zd:18024) (q:draft)
aneihlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (d:<a> and <neihlam> written as one word: that he, she or they have something, as the thing known, seen or found out) (j:a/neihlam) (r:zd:11918/zd:12996) (q:draft)
aneihleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if he has/if there is) (d:<a> and <neihleh> written as one word: if he, she or it has) (j:a/neihleh) (r:zd:13096) (q:draft)
aneihloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not have/lack) (d:<a>, <neih> and <loh> written as one word: his or their not having, used before words such as <hangin>, although, and <ciangin>, when) (j:a/neih/loh) (r:zd:24381/zd:11619) (q:draft)
aneihman = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:because of having/because he has) (d:<a> and <neihman> written as one word: because he, she or they have or hold) (j:a/neihman) (r:zd:16257/zd:25768) (q:draft)
aneihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:his having/their having) (d:<a> and <neihna> written as one word: the fact that someone has a thing, such as love, a concern or an aim; {itna aneihna} is the love he has) (j:a/neihna) (r:zd:19159/zd:17663) (q:draft)
aneihpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the having/that he has) (d:<a>, <neih> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the fact that someone has or holds something, as the topic of the sentence) (j:a/neih/pen) (r:zd:13114/zd:11074) (q:draft)
aneihsa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:his possessions/her property) (d:<a>, his or her, and <neihsa> written as one word: what he or she owns) (j:a/neihsa) (r:zd:21040/zd:18054) (q:draft)
aneihsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:be holding/be carrying on) (d:<a> and <neih>, have or hold, with the ending {-san}, written as one word: {thusitna aneihsan laitak} is while the inquiry is being held) (r:zd:16600) (q:draft, low confidence)
aneihsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:plan to hold/try to carry out/be about to have) (d:<a> and <neihsawm> written as one word: who plans to have something, or sets about holding a check, a protest or a search) (j:a/neihsawm) (r:zd:11450/zd:17030) (q:draft)
aneihsun = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/religion) (w:his only/her only/only) (d:<a> and <neihsun>, only, written as one word: the only one that he or she has, as an only son) (j:a/neihsun) (r:zd:15384/zd:19733) (q:draft)
aneihte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who have/the ones he has) (d:<aneih> with the plural <te> written as one word: those who have something, or the ones that he, she or it has) (j:aneih/te) (r:zd:15178/zd:20150) (q:draft)
aneihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can have/be able to have) (d:<a> and <neihtheih> written as one word: he or they can have, mostly before <nadingin>, so that they may have) (j:a/neihtheih) (r:zd:20293/zd:14597/zd:13260) (q:draft)
aneihzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:since having/after getting) (d:<a>, <neih>, have, and <zawh>, after, written as one word, before a count of years: the time since he or she got something, as {pasal aneihzawh}, since she married) (j:a/neih/zawh) (r:zd:21603/zd:18270) (q:draft)
aneikhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:one who has) (d:<a>, <nei>, have, and <khat>, one, written as one word: one who has or owns what is named before it; mostly before <ahihi>, is) (j:a/nei/khat) (r:zd:16236/zd:12954/zd:19021) (q:draft)
aneikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:already have) (d:<a> and <neikhin> written as one word: he or she already has, said mostly of a wife, a husband or children) (j:a/neikhin) (r:zd:15915/zd:19324) (q:draft)
aneikhinsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:who already has/having already) (d:<anei>, who has, and <khinsa>, already, written as one word: one who already has something, as children or experience) (j:anei/khinsa) (r:zd:12512/zd:20850) (q:draft)
aneikik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:have again/take another) (d:<a> and <neikik>, have again, written as one word: he or she has one again, in the articles mostly of taking a new husband or wife) (j:a/neikik) (r:zd:12630/zd:17709) (q:draft)
aneilai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:who still has/still having) (d:<a> and <neilai>, still have, written as one word: the one who still has) (j:a/neilai) (r:zd:20316/zd:19347) (q:draft)
aneilo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:without/not having/lacking) (d:<a> and <neilo> written as one word: that does not have, one who is without; placed after the thing that is lacking, as {pilna aneilo}, uneducated) (j:a/neilo) (r:zd:23825/zd:22557/zd:13165) (q:draft)
aneilopi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:without having/without) (d:<a> and <neilopi>, without having, written as one word after the thing lacking: while he or they do not have it) (j:a/neilopi) (r:zd:15397/zd:13241) (q:draft)
aneilote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:those who do not have/those without) (d:<a> and <neilote> written as one word: those who do not have what is named before it) (j:a/neilote) (r:zd:25572/zd:25206/zd:10676) (q:draft)
aneimah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really have/indeed have) (d:<anei> and the emphatic <mah> written as one word: truly has, often in a question or doubt whether someone really has a thing) (j:anei/mah) (r:zd:16152/zd:13297) (q:draft)
aneinawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:no longer have/who no longer has) (d:<a>, <nei> and <nawnlo> written as one word: no longer having, the one who no longer has) (j:a/nei/nawnlo) (r:zd:21020/zd:10993) (q:draft)
aneingei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:who has had before/has had) (d:<a> and <neingei> written as one word: he or she has had it at some time before) (j:a/neingei) (r:zd:17058/zd:11799) (q:draft)
aneinu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:owner/woman who owns) (d:<a> and <neinu> written as one word: the woman who owns the thing just spoken of; {mawtaw aneinu} is the woman who owns the car) (j:a/neinu) (r:zd:15431/zd:16794) (q:draft)
aneipa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:the owner/its owner) (d:<a> and <neipa> written as one word: the man who owns the thing named before it) (j:a/neipa) (r:zd:12785/zd:19560/zd:19468) (q:draft)
aneipan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family) (w:having just got/newly having) (d:<anei>, who has, and <pan> written as one word, said of a couple or parent with young children: who has only just come to have them) (j:anei/pan) (r:zd:16321/zd:19396) (q:draft, low confidence)
aneipen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:owner/the one who has) (d:<a>, <nei> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the one who has or owns it, the owner, as the topic of the sentence) (j:a/nei/pen) (r:zd:15431/zd:20734) (q:draft)
aneisa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:having/who already has/have already) (d:<a> and <neisa> written as one word: that already has, the one who has; at the end of a statement, has already had or made) (j:a/neisa) (r:zd:17897/zd:16774) (q:draft)
aneisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:let have/cause to have/hold) (d:<a> and <neisak> written as one word: he lets or makes someone have a thing; also he has an event held) (j:a/neisak) (r:zd:12402/zd:14928) (q:draft)
aneite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who have/owners) (d:<a> and <neite> written as one word: those who have something, placed after the thing they have) (j:a/neite) (r:zd:10935/zd:13165) (q:draft)
aneithei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can have/be able to have) (d:<a> and <neithei> written as one word: he or they can have, the one who can have) (j:a/neithei) (r:zd:20444/zd:20503) (q:draft)
aneizo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to have/manage to have) (d:<a> and <neizo> written as one word: he or they manage to have, or the one who is able to have) (j:a/neizo) (r:zd:12341/zd:10682) (q:draft)
anek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:eat/he eats) (d:<a> and <nek> written as one word: he or it eats, what one eats, the eating; {anek adawn} is what one eats and drinks) (j:a/nek) (r:zd:12541/zd:17313/zd:21025) (q:draft)
anekding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:food/something to eat) (d:<a> and <nekding> written as one word: what he or they are to eat, their food; also for him to eat) (j:a/nekding) (r:zd:12174/zd:20076) (q:draft)
anekha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:who ate/who happened to eat) (d:<a> and <nekha>, eat or happen to eat, written as one word: the one who ate it; {anekha te} are those who ate it) (j:a/nekha) (r:zd:17974/zd:12561) (q:draft)
anekkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:eat by mistake/happen to eat/swallow) (d:<a> and <nekkhak> written as one word: he happened to eat it, or the thing that was eaten without knowing) (j:a/nekkhak) (r:zd:18058/zd:15067) (q:draft)
anekkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:after eating/have eaten) (d:<a> and <nekkhit> written as one word: he has finished eating; with <ciangin>, after he or they had eaten) (j:a/nekkhit) (r:zd:12475/zd:21954) (q:draft)
anekna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:his eating/where he ate/that he ate) (d:<a> and <nekna>, eating, written as one word: the eating of something by the one spoken of, also describing the place or the film of it) (j:a/nekna) (r:zd:14885/zd:18093) (q:draft)
aneknek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:keep eating/be taking) (d:<a> and <neknek> written as one word: that he keeps eating, his habit of eating something; with <zatui>, be taking medicine regularly) (j:a/neknek) (r:zd:17372/zd:11508) (q:draft)
anekngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:used to eat/eat as before) (d:<anek> and <ngei>, as is usual, written as one word: what he used to eat, or eating as he always has) (j:anek/ngei) (r:zd:11508/zd:11269) (q:draft, low confidence)
aneksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:fed/gave to eat/ate up) (d:<a> and <neksak> written as one word: the one he or she gave to eat, or it ate up what belonged to someone) (j:a/neksak) (r:zd:21937) (q:draft)
anekzawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:food/time) (w:after eating) (d:<anek>, he or she eats, with <zawh>, after: after eating something) (j:anek/zawh) (r:zd:14535/zd:18093) (q:draft)
anekzawh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:food) (w:be able to eat/can eat) (d:<anek> with <zawh>, be able: what one can eat; {anekzawh zahzah} is as much as they can eat) (j:anek/zawh) (r:zd:15996) (q:draft, low confidence)
anene = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:eat/who eats) (d:<a> and <nene> written as one word: the one who eats or keeps eating something, those who eat it) (j:a/nene) (r:zd:22193/zd:13197) (q:draft)
aneng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:detail/small part) (d:<a> and <neng>, a small bit, written as one word: the small parts of a matter; {aneng atawng in} is in every detail, thoroughly) (j:a/neng) (r:zd:25342/zd:23977/zd:17883) (q:draft)
aneu = (i:2) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:verse) (d:a verse of a Bible chapter, written with its number after it as {aneu 8} or {aneu 4-na}; not the small one of the other sense) (r:zd:23771/zd:9453) (q:draft)
aneucik = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:tiny/very small/little) (d:<a> and <neucik> written as one word: that is very small, the very small one) (j:a/neucik) (r:zd:20461/zd:16259) (q:draft)
aneukhat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:a small one/a small) (d:<a> and <neukhat> written as one word after a noun: a small one of that kind) (j:a/neukhat) (r:zd:19036/zd:16126) (q:draft)
aneulai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/family) (w:in his childhood/when he was small) (d:<a> and <neulai> written as one word: his or her childhood, the time when he or she was small, mostly followed by <in>) (j:a/neulai) (r:zd:17371/zd:16257/zd:13157) (q:draft)
aneuneu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:small ones/minor ones) (d:<a> and <neuneu> written as one word: the small ones, those that are each small) (j:a/neuneu) (r:zd:17927/zd:19383) (q:draft)
aneuno = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:small/little/tiny) (d:<a> and <neuno>, small, written as one word: a small one, what is small or slight) (j:a/neuno) (r:zd:14791/zd:21291) (q:draft)
aneupen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/everyday) (w:youngest/smallest/least) (d:<a> and <neupen> written as one word: the smallest or the youngest one; {atanu aneupen} is his youngest daughter) (j:a/neupen) (r:zd:12470/zd:15946) (q:draft)
aneute = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:small ones/the smaller ones) (d:<aneu>, the small one, with the plural <te>: the small ones; after a noun, small, as in {vanleng aneute}, small aircraft) (j:aneu/te) (r:zd:18099/zd:20248) (q:draft)
aneutung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/time) (w:his childhood/her childhood) (d:<a> and <neutung> written as one word: his or her childhood; {aneutung akipan} is since he was small) (j:a/neutung) (r:zd:19962/zd:13343/zd:11269) (q:draft)
aneuzaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (w:the younger one/the smaller one) (d:<a> and <neuzaw> written as one word: the younger or smaller of two, said of children) (j:a/neuzaw) (r:zd:17936/zd:17945) (q:draft)
angah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:get/receive/obtain/win) (d:the particle <a> written together with <ngah>, get: he, she or they got, or the one who got; follows the thing gained, as {gualzawhna angah}, won the victory, and is not <ang>, bosom) (r:zd:24354/zd:24906/zd:14770) (q:draft)
angahding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will get/be going to receive) (d:<a>, <ngah> and <ding> written as one word: that he or she will get, or in order to get) (j:a/ngah/ding) (r:zd:15435/zd:16817/zd:12434) (q:draft)
angahkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:catch/contract/come to get) (d:<a> <ngah> <kha> written as one word: the one who has caught a disease or has come to get something) (j:a/ngah/kha) (r:zd:14664/zd:11644) (q:draft)
angahkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:one who has received/one who has won) (d:<angah>, the one who gets, with <khat>, one, written as one word: a person who has received or won something) (j:angah/khat) (r:zd:16302/zd:11348) (q:draft)
angahkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:win/obtain/gain) (d:<a> and <ngahkhia> written as one word: he or they won or obtained a prize, a place or a contract, or the one who won it) (j:a/ngahkhia) (r:zd:14928/zd:11348) (q:draft)
angahkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have already received/have already got) (d:<a> and <ngahkhin>, have already received, written as one word; before a noun or <te>, the one who has already received or caught it) (j:a/ngahkhin) (r:zd:17304/zd:14654) (q:draft)
angahkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have received/after getting) (d:<a> and <ngahkhit> written as one word: he or they have received; with <ciangin>, after receiving; not <angah>, in the arms) (j:a/ngahkhit) (r:zd:20595/zd:15966) (q:draft)
angahlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not get/not receive/be without) (d:<a> and <ngahlo> written as one word: who does not get or has not received, those without) (j:a/ngahlo) (r:zd:12066/zd:23863) (q:draft)
angahloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not get/not receive) (d:<a> and <ngahloh> written as one word: his or her not getting, when or so that one does not get) (j:a/ngahloh) (r:zd:21900/zd:20547) (q:draft)
angahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:his getting/his obtaining/his winning) (d:<a> and <ngahna> written as one word: the fact, the time or the place of his getting something, as a post, a degree or a job) (j:a/ngahna) (r:zd:18882/zd:22736) (q:draft)
angahpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the one that gets/those who get) (d:<angah> in the sense get and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the one who gets or has something, as the topic of the sentence) (j:angah/pen) (r:zd:17854/zd:16259) (q:draft, low confidence)
angahsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:obtained/having received) (d:<a> and <ngahsa> written as one word: the one who has already received something, or what has been obtained) (j:a/ngahsa) (r:zd:17841/zd:23821) (q:draft)
angahte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who receive/recipients/those who got) (d:<a> and <ngahte> written as one word: the people who received, got or earn something) (j:a/ngahte) (r:zd:23037/zd:20587) (q:draft)
angahthak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics/work) (w:newly appointed/who has just won) (d:<a> and <ngahthak> written as one word, placed after an office or a thing gained: the one who has newly received it) (j:a/ngahthak) (r:zd:19775/zd:19614) (q:draft)
angahthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can get/be able to receive) (d:<a> and <ngahthei> written as one word: he or they can get it, the one who can get it) (j:a/ngahthei) (r:zd:10936/zd:20595) (q:draft)
angahtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to get/can obtain) (d:<a> and <ngahtheih> written as one word, before <nadingin>: so that he, she or they can get it) (j:a/ngahtheih) (r:zd:20093/zd:14543) (q:draft)
angahzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:after getting/manage to get/win) (d:<a> and <ngahzawh> written as one word: after he got it, or he managed to get or win it; with <nawnloh>, no longer able to win) (j:a/ngahzawh) (r:zd:19966/zd:19619) (q:draft)
angai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:listen to/heed) (d:<a> and <ngai> written as one word: who listens to, the one that listens; {angai nuam} is those who want to listen) (j:a/ngai) (r:zd:24164/zd:17047) (q:draft)
angai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:love/be fond of/long for) (d:<a> and <ngai> written as one word, where <ngai> means love or miss a person: who loves, the one who is fond of) (j:a/ngai) (r:zd:16832) (q:draft, low confidence)
angaih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/social) (w:beloved/dear/lovely) (d:<a> and <ngaih> written as one word: the one who is loved and longed for, mostly in the pair {a it angaih}, loved and dear; of a song, lovely) (j:a/ngaih) (r:zd:19191/zd:15396/zd:25225) (q:draft)
angaihsun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:think/consider) (d:<a> and <ngaihsun> written as one word: he or she thinks, or the one who thinks of something) (j:a/ngaihsun) (r:zd:19833/zd:16178) (q:draft)
angaihsut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:think/consider/regard) (d:<a> and <ngaihsut> written as one word: he or they think, what is thought, regard someone as something; {angaihsut huai} is worth thinking about) (j:a/ngaihsut) (r:zd:21461/zd:15274) (q:draft)
angaihsutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:his thought/what one thinks) (d:<a> and <ngaihsutna> written as one word: his, her or their thought, what is in the mind) (j:a/ngaihsutna) (r:zd:14791/zd:13144) (q:draft)
angak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wait/wait for/guard) (d:<a> and <ngak> written as one word: he or she waits, or the one who waits for or keeps watch over something; {thonginn angak palik} is a policeman guarding a prison) (j:a/ngak) (r:zd:15305/zd:18054/zd:14694) (q:draft)
angakkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:after waiting/having waited) (d:<a>, <ngak> and <khit> written as one word, before <ciangin> or <uhciangin>: after he or they had waited for the time named) (j:a/ngak/khit) (r:zd:19324/zd:17886) (q:draft)
angaklah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:long for/wait eagerly for) (d:<a> and <ngaklah> written as one word: he, she or they wait eagerly, or the one who longs for something) (j:a/ngaklah) (r:zd:13072/zd:10861) (q:draft)
angakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:waiting place/waiting/resting place) (d:<a> and <ngakna> written as one word: the place where they wait or where a thing rests, their waiting) (j:a/ngakna) (r:zd:17249/zd:23670) (q:draft)
angakngak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep waiting/wait and wait) (d:<a> and <ngakngak> written as one word: he or she keeps waiting, or the one who has been waiting) (j:a/ngakngak) (r:zd:17886) (q:draft)
angawng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:neck/his neck/her neck) (d:<a> and <ngawng> written as one word: his, her or its neck) (j:a/ngawng) (r:zd:26097/zd:15505/zd:11764) (q:draft)
angei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as usual/as before/the usual) (d:<a> and <ngei> written as one word, <ngei> here meaning usual or former: the way it used to be; mostly as {angei bangin} or {angei mah bang}, as usual, just as before) (j:a/ngei) (r:zd:20855/zd:11994/zd:25919) (q:draft)
angeina = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:usual/normal/ordinary) (d:<a> and <ngeina> written as one word: what is usual or normal; {angeina bang in} is as usual and {angeina hilo} is not normal) (j:a/ngeina) (r:zd:20855/zd:23533/zd:23812) (q:draft)
angeinai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (j:ageinai) (r:zd:19478/zd:21618) (q:draft)
angek = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/everyday) (w:very young/tiny/the little one) (d:<a> and <ngek>, tender, written as one word: very small and young, as a newborn; also the smallest or least one) (j:a/ngek) (r:zd:13268/zd:12296) (q:draft)
angen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ask for/request) (d:<a> and <ngen> written as one word: he asks for, the one who asks for or applies for) (j:a/ngen) (r:zd:25918/zd:25064) (q:draft)
anget = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:ask for/request) (d:<a> and <nget> written as one word: he asks for, or that which he asks for) (j:a/nget) (r:zd:18107/zd:25064) (q:draft)
angetna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:his request/their request/the request) (d:<a> and <ngetna> written as one word: what he or they asked for, the asking; {huhna angetna} is a request for help) (j:a/ngetna) (r:zd:14681/zd:25918) (q:draft)
angetsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:pray for/intercede) (d:<a> and <ngetsak> written as one word: he or she prays for someone, or the one who prays for) (j:a/ngetsak) (r:zd:21042/zd:25329) (q:draft)
angetzah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:the amount he asked/as much as they asked) (d:<a> and <ngetzah>, amount asked, written as one word: as much as he, she or they asked for) (j:a/ngetzah) (r:zd:16968) (q:draft)
angim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:aim at/intend/plan) (d:<a> and <ngim> written as one word: he aims at, intends, or what is aimed at; {angim atup} is the aim and purpose) (j:a/ngim) (r:zd:19335/zd:17256) (q:draft)
angimna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:his aim/their goal/its purpose) (d:<a> and <ngimna> written as one word: his, her or their aim; often paired as {atup angimna}) (j:a/ngimna) (r:zd:24502/zd:22719) (q:draft)
angkawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:spouse/wife/beloved) (d:respectful and poetic word for a spouse, mostly a wife, the one held in the arms, from <ang> and <kawi>) (r:zd:14942/zd:19812) (q:draft)
anglai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/religion) (w:bosom/arms/embrace) (d:the bosom or arms in which a loved one is held; {Sian anglai ah}, in the bosom of God, is said of someone who has died) (s:ang) (r:zd:19866/zd:24850) (q:draft)
Anglican = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Anglican/Church of England) (d:the Anglican church, or a member of it; {Anglican pawlpi} is the Anglican church) (o:English) (r:ts:7051/zd:21717/zd:9251) (q:draft)
anglum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:bosom/embrace/warm care) (d:the warm bosom of someone who holds and cares for another, above all of a mother or of God; from <ang>, bosom, and <lum>, warm) (r:zd:19589/zd:20530) (q:draft)
ango = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:white/fair) (d:<a> and <ngo>, white, written as one word: white, or so as to be white; said of skin made lighter) (j:a/ngo) (r:zd:17129) (q:draft)
angong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social/politics) (w:violently/brutally/roughly) (d:<a> and <ngong> written as one word, mostly before <gamtat>: in a violent, harsh way; {angong gamtatna} is violent behaviour) (s:ngongtat) (j:a/ngong) (r:zd:14947/zd:19247) (q:draft)
angongtat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:violent/terrorist) (d:<a> and <ngongtat> written as one word: one who acts with violence; {angongtat migilo} is used for terrorists) (j:a/ngongtat) (r:zd:14711/zd:15045) (q:draft)
angongtatsawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:plotting violence/planning an attack) (d:<a> and <ngongtatsawm> written as one word, placed before or after <migilo>: who plots or attempts a violent attack) (j:a/ngongtatsawm) (r:zd:20250/zd:14846) (q:draft)
angpom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:embrace/hug/cherish) (d:<ang>, bosom, with <pom>, hold: take into the arms, embrace; also hold dear, and of a child, held to the bosom, beloved) (j:ang/pom) (r:zd:26495/zd:23554) (q:draft)
angsungkhualna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:selfishness/self-interest) (d:<angsung>, one's own good, and <khualna>, regard, written as one word: caring only for oneself) (j:angsung/khualna) (r:zd:23670/zd:24250) (q:draft)
angtanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:pride/boast/glory) (d:<angtang>, be proud, with the noun suffix {-na}: pride in someone or something, or the thing one is proud of) (b:angtang) (r:zd:22371/zd:16797) (q:draft)
angvaanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/social) (j:angvanna) (r:zd:11110) (q:draft)
anhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:cook/prepare food) (d:cook food, prepare a meal. From <an>, food, with <huan>, cook) (r:1.40.1) (q:draft)
anhuanbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/food) (w:kitchen/cookhouse) (d:<anhuan>, cook food, with <buk>, here hut or shelter: the room or building where food is cooked) (s:anbuk) (r:zd:24595/zd:15803/zd:12059) (q:draft)
anhuanzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/home) (w:way of cooking/cooking method) (d:<anhuan>, cook, and <zia>, way, written as one word: how food is cooked) (j:anhuan/zia) (r:zd:19932/zd:24036) (q:draft)
Anhui = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Anhui) (d:a province in the east of China) (r:zd:14635) (q:draft)
ani = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:date/day) (d:<a> and <ni> written as one word: the day or date of something, common as the heading for the date in notices) (j:a/ni) (r:zd:25918/zd:23343) (q:draft)
anial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:refuse/reject/deny) (d:<a> and <nial> written as one word: he or she refuses or denies it, the one who rejects it) (j:a/nial) (r:zd:22873/zd:11400) (q:draft)
aniampen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:lowest/the lowest) (d:<a> and <niampen> written as one word: the lowest in place or rank) (j:a/niampen) (r:zd:19779/zd:15946) (q:draft)
anih = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:both/the two) (d:<a> and <nih> written as one word: the two, both of them, as in {anih un}, the two of them; before <veina> it means the second time) (j:a/nih) (r:zd:18086/zd:22683/ts:617) (q:draft)
anihna = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:second/the second/secondly) (d:<a> and <nihna>, second, written as one word: the second one; {anihna ah} and {anihna in} are secondly) (j:a/nihna) (r:zd:18927/zd:23944/zd:11782) (q:draft)
anihtuak = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:both/each of the two) (d:<anih> and <tuak.2> written as one word: both of the two, each of them alike) (j:anih/tuak) (r:zd:13082/zd:23127) (q:draft)
anihvei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:the second time/a second time/second) (d:<a> and <nihvei> written as one word: the second time, for the second time) (j:a/nihvei) (r:zd:16490/zd:11333) (q:draft)
anihveina = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday/time) (w:the second time/second) (d:<a> and <nihveina> written as one word: the second time, the second occasion of something) (j:a/nihveina) (r:zd:15743/zd:12271/zd:20148) (q:draft)
anik = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:her skirt/his sarong) (d:<a>, his or her, and <nik>, skirt or sarong, written as one word; {anik apuan} is one's clothes) (j:a/nik) (r:zd:21826/zd:15048) (q:draft)
anikbawk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:skirt/lower garment) (d:<a>, her or his, written as one word with <nikbawk>, the garment worn on the lower body: a woman's skirt, and also said of what a man wears below the waist) (r:zd:19707/zd:11783) (q:draft)
anikbawknuai = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home/body) (w:under her skirt) (d:<a>, <nikbawk> and <nuai> written as one word: the place beneath the skirt a woman is wearing) (j:a/nikbawk/nuai) (r:zd:14566) (q:draft)
animasa = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:the first day/first) (d:<a>, <ni> and <masa> written as one word: its first day, often followed by <ni> again as {animasa ni}) (j:a/ni/masa) (r:zd:14633) (q:draft, low confidence)
animna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:dye) (d:<a> and {nimna}, dye, written as one word: the dye for cloth or thread, named together with <khau>, thread, as what a weaver needs) (r:zd:21102) (q:draft, low confidence)
anin = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/home) (w:dirty/filthy/unclean) (d:<a> and <nin> written as one word: dirty, what is dirty, dirt; {khasim anin pai} is said of a woman having her monthly period) (j:a/nin) (r:zd:25390/zd:20577) (q:draft)
anini = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:day by day/day after day) (d:<ani>, the day, and <ni>, day, written as one word, mostly with <in>: {anini in} is day by day, more each day) (j:ani/ni) (r:zd:15517/ts:11162) (q:draft)
anip = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:soft) (d:<a> and <nip> written as one word: soft, what is soft) (j:a/nip) (r:zd:21826/zd:23853) (q:draft)
anipen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:the day/the date) (d:<a> and <nipen> written as one word: the day of it, as the topic of the sentence, after a word that says what the day is for) (j:a/nipen) (r:zd:17097/zd:11501) (q:draft)
anitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:in the evening/that evening) (d:<a> and <nitak>, evening, written as one word: in the evening of that day) (j:a/nitak) (r:zd:14804/zd:24029) (q:draft)
ankam = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food/health) (w:appetite) (d:the relish for food, from <an>, food, and <kam>, mouth, and not the mustard plant: {ankam lim} is have a good appetite and {ankam limlo} is have no appetite, often named beside sleep as a sign of health) (r:zd:20942/zd:12436/zd:19098) (q:draft)
Ankambulnek = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:food/nature) (w:carrot) (d:a root vegetable; the name is <ankam>, mustard, <bul>, root, and <nek>, eaten: the mustard whose root is eaten) (r:zd:20004) (q:draft)
ankamlimna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/health) (w:appetite/good appetite/relish for food) (d:<ankam>, appetite, and <limna>, taste, written as one word: the enjoyment of food, a good appetite) (j:ankam/limna) (r:zd:24276/zd:20647) (q:draft)
ankamteh = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:food) (w:mustard greens/leaf vegetable/lettuce) (d:the leaf of <ankam>, mustard, eaten as a vegetable; also used of lettuce and similar leafy greens) (r:zd:19499/zd:15527) (q:draft)
ankham = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:food) (w:full/well fed/satisfied with food) (d:<an> and <kham> written as one word: having eaten enough; the pair {zukham ankham}, drunk and gorged, is said of a drunken person) (j:an/kham) (r:ts:3375/zd:14805/zd:24682) (q:draft)
ankhing = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food/home) (w:leftover food/leftovers/food in store) (d:food left over or kept from before, cooked food from an earlier meal or grain kept in store, named beside <mehkhing>, leftover curry; {ankhing kham} is having enough food to last) (r:zd:15652/zd:18241/zd:12337) (q:draft)
anki = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:food) (d:<an>, food, and the verb prefix <ki> written as one word before a verb: {anki ne} is food is eaten) (j:an/ki) (r:zd:20162) (q:draft, low confidence)
ankuang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food/social) (w:feast/meal/dinner) (d:a meal or feast to which people are invited, not the vessel: {ankuang lui} is to give a feast and {ankuang umkhopna} is a meal eaten together at a celebration or gathering) (r:zd:12862/zd:14579/zd:22935) (q:draft)
ankuangsung = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:food/home) (w:in the dish/in the bowl) (d:<ankuang> and <sung> written as one word: inside the dish that food is eaten from) (j:ankuang/sung) (r:zd:22922) (q:draft)
anlaak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/nature) (j:anlak) (r:zd:22922/zd:21862) (q:draft)
anlak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/time) (w:harvest/reaping) (d:the gathering in of the grain; {anlak hun} is harvest time and {anlak na sem} is work at the harvest) (s:atna) (r:41.12.2) (q:draft)
Anlangh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:social) (w:Anlangh) (d:a Zomi village in the Tedim area of the Chin Hills, {Anlangh khua}; written after the name of a person it shows the home village) (r:zd:11064/zd:23512) (q:draft)
anletuite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:food and drink/foods and drinks) (d:<anletui>, food and drink, with the plural <te>: the things one eats and drinks) (b:anletui) (r:zd:25150/zd:19400) (q:draft)
anlimlim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:tasty food/good food/delicacies) (d:<anlim>, tasty food, with <lim>, tasty, said again, written as one word: all the tasty food, only the good things to eat) (j:anlim/lim) (r:zd:19932) (q:draft)
Anlun = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Anlun) (d:village in Tonzang township in the Chin State of Myanmar; also written after a personal name to show the home village) (r:zd:12342) (q:draft)
ann = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (j:an) (r:zd:20639/zd:23083/zd:24029) (q:draft)
ann pia = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work/food) (w:meals provided/food provided) (d:<ann>, food, and <pia>, give: food is given; a formula of job advertisements, mostly after <omna pia>, lodging provided, saying that the employer gives the meals; {ann pia lo} is meals not provided) (r:zd:11789/zd:11908) (q:draft)
annam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:kind of food/foods) (d:<an>, food, and <nam>, kind, written as one word: a kind of food, foods of some kind) (j:an/nam) (r:zd:20433/zd:24276) (q:draft)
annamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:kinds of food/foods) (d:<an>, food, and <namte>, kinds, written as one word) (j:an/namte) (r:zd:24276/zd:22740) (q:draft)
annbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/food) (j:anbuk) (r:zd:11908/zd:20172/zd:10794) (q:draft)
anneding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:to eat/will eat a meal) (d:<anne>, eat a meal, and <ding> written as one word: in order to eat, those who come to eat) (j:anne/ding) (r:zd:17886/zd:16007) (q:draft)
annek tuidawn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:food and drink/provisions) (d:<annek>, eating, and <tuidawn>, drinking: a pair that names food and drink together, what a person or household needs to live on) (r:zd:23821/zd:22203) (q:draft)
annekding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:meal/food to eat) (d:<annek>, eating of food, and <ding>, for, written as one word: food to eat, a meal, or the eating of a meal; {nitak annekding} is the evening meal) (j:annek/ding) (r:zd:21937/zd:12708) (q:draft)
annekkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:have eaten/finish eating) (d:<an> and <nekkhit> written as one word: have finished a meal; with {phet ciangin}, right after eating) (j:an/nekkhit) (r:zd:20841/zd:16665) (q:draft)
annekma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:food/time) (w:before eating/before a meal) (d:<annek> and <ma> written as one word: before the meal, before food is eaten) (j:annek/ma) (r:zd:24276/zd:16665) (q:draft)
annekna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:meal/eating) (d:<annek>, eat food, with the noun suffix <na>: the eating of a meal; {annekna sabuai} is the table for a meal and {annekna mun} a banquet hall) (s:nekna/anneek) (b:annek) (r:17.7.8) (q:draft)
annekzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/health) (w:diet/way of eating/eating habits) (d:<an> and <nekzia> written as one word: what and how a person eats) (j:an/nekzia) (r:zd:21306/zd:21032) (q:draft)
anngawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:go without food/go hungry/fast) (d:<an>, food, and <ngawl>, go without, written as one word: go without food, by choice or from want) (j:an/ngawl) (r:zd:23639/zd:21974) (q:draft)
annhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/home) (j:anhuan) (r:zd:20172/zd:25452) (q:draft)
annkuang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/social) (w:meal/table/dish of food) (d:a dish or table of food, and so a meal; {annkuang um khop} is to share a meal together, and {Topa Nitak Annkuang} is the Lord's Supper) (j:ankuang) (r:zd:23483/zd:25768) (q:draft)
Announcement = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:announcement/public notice) (s:tangkona) (o:English) (r:zd:15031/zd:15629) (q:draft)
announcer = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:announcer/master of ceremonies) (d:the person who announces the items of a programme or a feast; {announcer sem} is act as announcer) (o:English) (r:zd:16173/zd:17234) (q:draft, low confidence)
annsai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/work) (w:restaurant/eating house/food shop) (d:<an>, food, with <sai>, shop: a place that sells cooked meals; often named in job notices, as {Sen annsai}, a Chinese restaurant) (r:zd:19320/zd:11789) (q:draft)
ano = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/family) (w:its young/offspring/baby) (d:<a> and <no>, here young one, written as one word: the young of an animal, its offspring; with <suaksak>, make money bear young, that is earn interest) (j:a/no) (r:zd:14780/zd:14959/zd:25917) (q:draft, the row of the keyword no has only the sense you, not the sense young)
anop = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:pleasant/enjoyable/comfortable) (d:<a> and <nop>, the form of <nuam>, pleasant, used before another word, written as one word: pleasant, enjoyable; {anop penpen} is the most enjoyable, and {na ci anop keileh} is if you feel unwell) (j:a/nop) (r:zd:24365/zd:12630) (q:draft)
anopci = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/travel) (w:pleasant/enjoyable/delightful) (d:<a> and <nopci> written as one word: pleasant, or that which is pleasant, said of places and events) (j:a/nopci) (r:zd:21667/zd:17649) (q:draft)
anopcipen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/travel) (w:most enjoyable/most pleasant/the most fun) (d:<anopci>, enjoyable, and the superlative <pen> written as one word: the most enjoyable, the liveliest) (j:anopci/pen) (r:zd:14575/zd:11506) (q:draft)
anopcizaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:more enjoyable/more pleasant/more comfortable) (d:<anopci>, pleasant, and <zaw>, more, written as one word: more pleasant than before or than another) (j:anopci/zaw) (r:zd:19018) (q:draft)
anopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:its pleasure/the joy of it/happiness) (d:<a> and <nopna> written as one word: the pleasure or enjoyment of something, or a person's happiness) (j:a/nopna) (r:zd:19697/zd:15996/zd:22037) (q:draft)
anoptuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be better off/benefit/get relief) (d:<a> and <noptuam> written as one word: it is a benefit or relief, he or it gets better) (j:a/noptuam) (r:zd:17572/zd:12264) (q:draft)
anpham = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/food) (w:handful of rice/rice offering) (d:<an>, rice or food, with the word for a handful, as in {khutpham khat}, one handful: a handful of rice set aside and given as an offering or as alms; {anpham khutpham} is the handful of rice offering kept by some churches) (r:zd:21258/zd:24015) (q:draft, low confidence)
anphel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/social) (w:food pack/food ration/portion of food) (d:<an>, food, with <phel>, piece or part: a portion or pack of food handed out to people in need) (r:zd:22779/zd:17411) (q:draft, low confidence)
anpuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/social) (w:bring food/deliver food) (d:<an>, food, and <puak>, send or bring, written as one word: take food to someone; {anpuak nasep} is the work of bringing food to people) (j:an/puak) (r:zd:21028/zd:24003) (q:draft)
ansaal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/work) (j:ansal) (r:zd:21178/zd:21436) (q:draft)
ansaikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/work) (w:a restaurant/an eating place) (d:<an>, food, <sai>, shop, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a restaurant or food shop) (j:an/sai/khat) (r:zd:19932/zd:16817) (q:draft)
ansaipi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/work) (w:restaurant/big restaurant) (d:<an>, food, and <saipi>, big shop, written as one word: a restaurant) (j:an/saipi) (r:zd:12487/zd:18213) (q:draft, low confidence)
ansuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/work) (w:pounding grain/rice pounding) (d:<an>, grain, with a second part meaning pound: the work of pounding grain in a mortar to husk it; {ansuk ansep} is pounding and winnowing) (r:ts:3375) (q:draft, low confidence)
antaang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (j:antang) (r:zd:24714) (q:draft)
Antalya = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Antalya) (d:a city and province on the south coast of Turkey) (r:zd:13276) (q:draft)
antang = (i:2) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:fast) (d:<an>, food, with <tang>, go without: go without food as a religious act, in {antang in thungen}, pray with fasting; not the noun for rice or grain) (s:antan) (r:zd:23725/zd:8375) (q:draft, low confidence)
antanhun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/time) (w:fasting period/time of fasting) (d:<antan>, fast, and <hun>, time, written as one word: the time of fasting, in the articles the Muslim fasting month of Ramadan) (j:antan/hun) (r:zd:19695/zd:12708) (q:draft)
anteh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:vegetable/greens) (d:leafy plants eaten as food; {anteh huan} is a vegetable garden) (s:mehteh) (r:20.15.17) (q:draft)
antha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/health) (w:nutrition/nourishment) (d:<an>, food, and <tha>, strength, written as one word: the nourishment that food gives, and food in the stomach as a source of strength) (j:an/tha) (r:zd:22019/zd:22026) (q:draft)
antibiotics = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:antibiotics) (d:medicine that kills bacteria, explained in Zolai as {lungno thahna zatui}) (o:English) (r:zd:24046/zd:22977) (q:draft)
Antwerp = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Antwerp) (d:a port city in Belgium) (r:zd:17265/zd:11880) (q:draft)
anu = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his mother/her mother/the mother) (d:<a>, his or her, and <nu>, mother, written as one word: the mother of a person just spoken of, often paired with <apa>, the father; unlike the sense female, said of animals) (r:zd:15443/zd:24123/zd:15286) (q:draft)
anu apa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:parents/his parents/her parents) (d:<nu>, mother, and <pa>, father, each with the prefix <a>, his or her, written as one word: the mother and father of the person spoken of, his or her parents; often followed by the plural <te>; not the sense of <anu> and <apa> as female and male of animals) (s:nu leh pa) (r:zd:15425/zd:13110/zd:19563) (q:draft)
anuai aa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:following/below) (d:another spelling of <anuai-a>, that which is below, with <aa>, of: points to what comes next in the text; stands before a noun or before <bang>, as in {anuai aa bangin}, as follows) (s:anuai-a) (r:zd:23812/zd:20176/zd:17060) (q:draft)
anuai abang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:as follows/as below) (d:<anuai>, that which is below, with <abang>, like: formula that introduces a list or details that come next; it closes the sentence with <ahihi> or <hi>, or takes <in> before a verb, {anuai abang in}, in the following way) (r:zd:18150/zd:12311/zd:25109) (q:draft)
anuai abangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:as follows/as below) (d:<anuai>, what is below, and <abangin>, in the way of: as follows; placed before the verb to announce a list, a text or details that come next) (r:zd:24182/zd:12336/zd:25265) (q:draft)
anuaia = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (j:anuai-a) (r:zd:24394/zd:15384) (q:draft)
anuaidawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:floor below/lower floor/ground level) (d:<a>, <nuai>, below, and <dawl>, floor, written as one word: the floor or level below, the ground level under a building) (j:a/nuai/dawl) (r:zd:20440/zd:15167) (q:draft)
anuailam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:lower part/underside/bottom) (d:<a> and <nuailam> written as one word: the lower part or underside of a thing, the place below it; with <ah>, at the bottom of, beneath) (j:a/nuailam) (r:zd:20153/zd:14954/zd:21330) (q:draft)
anuaipan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:from below/from underneath) (d:<a>, <nuai>, under, and <pan>, from, written as one word: from under it, from below) (j:a/nuai/pan) (r:zd:15920/zd:22129) (q:draft)
anuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:take offence/sulk/be in opposition) (d:<a> and <nuak>, take offence, written as one word: the one who takes offence and stands apart; in politics {anuak pawl} seems to be the opposition) (j:a/nuak) (r:zd:26620/zd:26252) (q:draft, low confidence)
anuam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:pleasant/enjoyable/comfortable) (d:<a> and <nuam> written as one word: pleasant, what is pleasant or enjoyable) (j:a/nuam) (r:zd:23037/zd:15671) (q:draft)
anuamlua = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very pleasant/very glad) (d:<anuam> and <lua> written as one word: very pleasant, very glad) (j:anuam/lua) (r:zd:23956/zd:16033) (q:draft)
anuampen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:the most pleasant/the most comfortable) (d:<a> and <nuampen> written as one word: the one that is most pleasant or comfortable) (j:a/nuampen) (r:zd:23784/zd:23432) (q:draft)
anuamzawding = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:better/more comfortable) (d:<a>, <nuamzaw.2> and <ding> written as one word: that will be more pleasant, mostly in {nuntak khuasakna anuamzawding}, a better living) (j:a/nuamzaw/ding) (r:zd:20244/zd:16747) (q:draft)
anui = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:laugh) (d:<a> and <nui>, laugh, written as one word: he or she laughs, the one who laughs) (j:a/nui) (r:zd:24139/zd:21463) (q:draft)
anuih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:laugh/smile) (d:<a> and <nuih>, the form of laugh, written as one word: {anuih mai} is she smiles, and {anuih zak} is be laughable) (j:a/nuih) (r:zd:11653) (q:draft, low confidence)
anuihmai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:smile/smiling) (d:<a> and <nuihmai> written as one word: he or she smiles, his or her smile, the one who smiles) (j:a/nuihmai) (r:zd:16308/zd:16922) (q:draft)
anuihzak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:laugh) (d:<a> and <nuihzak> written as one word; {anuihzak huai} is laughable, funny) (j:a/nuihzak) (r:zd:25232) (q:draft)
anukik = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:stepmother) (d:<a>, his or her, and <nukik>, stepmother, written as one word: his or her stepmother) (j:a/nukik) (r:zd:17731) (q:draft)
anul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wipe) (d:<a> and <nul> written as one word: he or she wipes) (j:a/nul) (r:zd:16832) (q:draft, low confidence)
anuleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:his mother and/her mother and) (d:<a>, <nu> and <leh> written as one word, in {anuleh apa}: his or her mother and father, the parents) (j:a/nu/leh) (r:zd:12942/zd:11918) (q:draft)
anulepa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his parents/her parents/their parents) (d:<a> and <nulepa> written as one word: his, her or their mother and father) (j:a/nulepa) (r:zd:11083/zd:22658) (q:draft)
anumei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:the woman/female) (d:<a> and <numei> written as one word: the woman, the female one; {anumei apasal} is women and men alike) (j:a/numei) (r:zd:21421/zd:25342) (q:draft)
anumeivan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:her private parts/female genitals) (d:<a>, <numei> and <van> written as one word: the private parts of the woman) (j:a/numei/van) (r:zd:16047) (q:draft, low confidence)
anung = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:back/rear/behind) (d:the prefix <a> written together with <nung>, back: the place behind someone or something, with <ah>, behind, or <panin>, from behind; set against <amai>, the front) (a:amai) (r:zd:25937/zd:19036/zd:24381) (q:draft)
anungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:behind/at the back/afterwards/later) (d:<a> and <nungah> written as one word: behind him or it, on his back; of time, afterwards, later) (j:a/nungah) (r:zd:11495/zd:11244) (q:draft)
anungciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:afterwards/later/in the future) (d:<anung>, after, and <ciang>, when, written as one word: later on, in time to come) (s:anung) (j:anung/ciang) (r:zd:25924/zd:22272) (q:draft)
anunglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:back/rear/behind) (d:<a> and <nunglam> written as one word: its back, the rear of it; {anunglam panin} is from behind) (j:a/nunglam) (r:zd:15667/zd:22557) (q:draft)
anunglampan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:from behind/from the back) (d:<anunglam> and <pan> written as one word: from the back of it, from behind him or her) (j:anunglam/pan) (r:zd:16774/zd:11783) (q:draft)
anunglian = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:right behind/directly behind) (d:<a> and <nung>, the back, with <lian>, exactly, written as one word: the place right behind someone or something; mostly as {anunglian ah}, right behind it) (j:a/nung/lian) (r:zd:15649/zd:17952) (q:draft)
anungpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:from behind) (d:<a>, <nung>, back, and <pan>, from, written as one word: from behind him, her or it; often followed by <in>) (j:a/nung/pan) (r:zd:15953/zd:19180/zd:14626) (q:draft)
anungpanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:from behind) (d:<anung>, the back, and <panin>, from, written as one word: from behind) (j:anung/panin) (r:zd:20425/zd:19036) (q:draft)
anungsang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:afterwards/later) (d:<a> and <nungsang> written as one word: after it, afterwards, mostly as {anungsang ah}) (j:a/nungsang) (r:zd:24697/zd:15163) (q:draft)
anungta pasian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:the living God) (d:<anungta>, living, and <Pasian>, God: the living God, a fixed title in sermons and prayers, set against idols and spirits; written with one or two capitals) (r:zd:16765/zd:23361/zd:8375) (q:draft)
anungtalai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/media) (w:still alive/surviving/survivor) (d:<a> and <nungtalai> written as one word: the one who is still alive; {anungtalai in kimu} is was found alive) (j:a/nungtalai) (r:zd:20734/zd:19396) (q:draft)
anungzang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his back/the back) (d:<a> and <nungzang> written as one word: his or her back, the back of the body) (j:a/nungzang) (r:zd:11994/zd:15437) (q:draft)
anungzui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:his follower/follower/assistant) (d:<a> and <nungzui> written as one word: his follower or disciple, the one who follows him; also the helper who rides with a driver) (j:a/nungzui) (r:zd:20970/zd:14646/zd:17279) (q:draft)
anungzuipa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:his follower/his assistant/his disciple) (d:<a> and <nungzuipa> written as one word: his follower or assistant, the man who comes after him) (j:a/nungzuipa) (r:zd:17786) (q:draft)
anungzuite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/social) (w:his disciples/his followers) (d:<a>, his, and <nungzuite> written as one word: his or her disciples or followers) (j:a/nungzuite) (r:zd:19111/zd:23432) (q:draft)
anunna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/everyday) (w:his life/her life) (d:<a>, his or her, with a short form of <nuntakna>, life, written as one word; {anunna bei} is his life ends) (r:zd:15647/zd:13117) (q:draft)
anuntak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:live/be alive) (d:<a> and <nuntak>, live, written as one word: he or she lives, the time or the fact of living) (j:a/nuntak) (r:zd:19174/zd:17760) (q:draft)
anuntakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:to live/to survive) (d:<a>, <nuntak> and <ding> written as one word: that he will live, his living on or surviving) (j:a/nuntak/ding) (r:zd:20150/zd:22932/zd:17161) (q:draft)
anuntakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:his life/her life) (d:<a> and <nuntakna> written as one word: his, her or its life) (j:a/nuntakna) (r:zd:22590/zd:20076) (q:draft)
anuntakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:live with/share life with) (d:<a> and <nuntakpih> written as one word: he or she lives together with someone, goes through life with them) (j:a/nuntakpih) (r:zd:15816) (q:draft, low confidence)
anuntaksung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:during his life/in her lifetime) (d:<a> and <nuntaksung>, lifetime, written as one word, mostly before <in>: while he or she lived) (j:a/nuntaksung) (r:zd:20150/zd:17838) (q:draft)
anunung = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/time) (w:last/final/latest) (d:<a> and <nunung> written as one word: the last, the latest; <anunung ah> and {anunung ciangin} are in the end, finally, and {anunung pen} is the very last or latest) (j:a/nunung) (r:zd:17930/zd:15664/zd:21965) (q:draft)
anunung ah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:in the end/finally/eventually) (d:<anunung>, the last, and <ah>, at: opens a sentence that tells how a series of events ended, in the end, at last) (r:zd:17800/zd:13094) (q:draft)
anunungpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/everyday) (w:last/latest/most recent/final) (d:<a> and <nunungpen> written as one word: the last one or the most recent one, also for the last time) (j:a/nunungpen) (r:zd:10687/zd:11265) (q:draft)
anunungpen hunzatkhop = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:last farewell/final viewing/last time together) (d:<anunungpen>, the last, and <hunzatkhop>, spend time together: in a funeral notice the last gathering with the one who died, before the burial; the name or {luanghawm tawh}, with the body, stands before it and <ding> with the day and hour after it) (r:zd:21139/zd:25541) (q:draft)
anunungpenpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time) (w:the very last/the most recent) (d:<anunung>, last or latest, and <penpen>, the very most, written as one word: the most recent of all, the very last one) (j:anunung/penpen) (r:zd:19860) (q:draft)
anupa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:the couple/husband and wife) (d:<a> and <nupa> written as one word: the couple, the two of them as husband and wife) (j:a/nupa) (r:zd:15114/zd:24502) (q:draft)
anupen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:his mother/her mother) (d:<a>, his or her, <nu>, mother, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: his mother or her mother as the one the sentence is about) (j:a/nu/pen) (r:zd:20764/zd:15186/zd:15816) (q:draft)
anusia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:leave/leave behind/abandon) (d:<a> and <nusia> written as one word: he or she left or abandoned, and the one who left or the one left behind) (j:a/nusia) (r:zd:14944/zd:11062) (q:draft)
anusiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:leave behind/left behind) (d:<a> and <nusiat> written as one word: he leaves, which he left; {anusiat innkuanpihte} is the family that a dead person leaves behind) (j:a/nusiat) (r:zd:23533/zd:24068) (q:draft)
anuta = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:mother and child) (d:<a> and <nuta> written as one word: the mother and her child together; with <un> they are the subject) (j:a/nuta) (r:zd:22658) (q:draft)
anutawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:with his mother/with her mother) (d:<a>, <nu>, mother, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: together with his or her mother) (j:a/nu/tawh) (r:zd:12567/zd:12110/zd:17899) (q:draft)
anute = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his mother's family/her parents) (d:<a>, his or her, and <nute> written as one word: his or her mother and those with her, the mother's household, and so the parents) (j:a/nute) (r:zd:9218/zd:11133) (q:draft)
anutektek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his own mother/her own mother) (d:<anu>, his or her mother, and <tektek>, very or own, written as one word: his very own mother, used with <apianna>, who bore him) (j:anu/tektek) (r:zd:17123) (q:draft)
anutsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:leave behind/leave/abandon) (d:<a> and <nutsiat> written as one word: he or she left it behind, or the one that was left behind) (j:a/nutsiat) (r:zd:12040/zd:11786/zd:21937) (q:draft)
anutsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:his leaving behind/what he left) (d:<a> and <nutsiatna> written as one word: his or her leaving of someone or something behind, the thing left, or the place where it was left; {lai anutsiatna} is the note he left) (j:a/nutsiatna) (r:zd:11729/zd:11251) (q:draft)
anuzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:his mother also/her mother too) (d:<a>, his or her, <nu>, mother, and <zong>, also, written as one word) (j:a/nu/zong) (r:zd:12192/zd:14678) (q:draft)
Anvaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/work) (j:anvak) (r:zd:23037) (q:draft)
anvak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/food) (w:provide meals/feed/board) (d:give a person his meals, as an employer does for a worker or a host for a guest; in job notices {omna pia anvak} is lodging and meals provided; the other sense is said of animals) (r:zd:24039/zd:23394) (q:draft)
anzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:food) (d:<an>, food, and <zong>, also, written as one word: food also, the food too) (j:an/zong) (r:zd:17862/zd:22569) (q:draft)
anzuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/work) (w:food stall/eatery/food outlet) (d:<an> and <zuakna> written as one word: a place where food is sold, or the selling of food) (j:an/zuakna) (r:zd:11248/zd:20468/ts:3546) (q:draft)
aom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is/exist/be) (d:<a> and <om> written as one word: there is, or before a noun the one that is in a place) (j:a/om) (r:zd:17120/zd:15800/zd:19964) (q:draft)
aombangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as there is/according to) (d:<a> and <ombangin> written as one word: as there is, in keeping with what there is of the thing named before it) (j:a/ombangin) (r:zd:20236/zd:16360) (q:draft)
aomciang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:when there is/whenever there is) (d:<a>, <om> and <ciang> written as one word: when there is, at the time something exists or takes place) (j:a/om/ciang) (r:zd:11405/zd:18079) (q:draft)
aomciangin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:when there is/when one is) (d:<a>, <om> and <ciangin> written as one word: when there is something, or when someone is in a place or state) (j:a/om/ciangin) (r:zd:19763/zd:19151) (q:draft)
aomcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:stay/remain/live) (d:<a> and <omcip>, stay on, written as one word: he or she stays in a place and remains there, lives there for the time) (j:a/omcip) (r:zd:12087/zd:11335/zd:11124) (q:draft)
aomdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:his condition/their behaviour/how he is) (d:<a> and <omdan> written as one word: how he, she or they behave, or how someone is feeling) (j:a/omdan) (r:zd:19180/zd:16287) (q:draft)
aomden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always be there/remain/keep on being) (d:<a> and <omden> written as one word: there always is, or he or she stays so continually; {akigingsa in aomden} is remain on the alert) (j:a/omden) (r:zd:12405/zd:16741/zd:16811) (q:draft)
aomdenzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:mostly stay/usually be there) (d:<aom> and <denzaw> written as one word: he or she is there most of the time, usually stays there) (j:aom/denzaw) (r:zd:19125) (q:draft, low confidence)
aomdiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is there/will there be) (d:<aom>, there is, and the question word <diam>, written as one word at the end of a question or an indirect question: is there, will there be) (j:aom/diam) (r:zd:12274/zd:11790) (q:draft)
aomding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be/be present/exist) (d:<a>, <om> and <ding> written as one word: that there should be, for there to be, to be in a place) (j:a/om/ding) (r:zd:11117/zd:21954/zd:20416) (q:draft)
aomhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is there/are there) (d:<aom> and the question word <hia> written as one word: is there any, does it exist) (j:aom/hia) (r:zd:16442/zd:16337) (q:draft)
aomhiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is there) (d:<a>, <om> and the question particle <hiam> written as one word: is there any, whether there is) (j:a/om/hiam) (r:zd:16360/zd:14881/zd:14537) (q:draft)
aomkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is not/not exist) (d:<a> and <omkei> written as one word: there is none, mostly before a word for if or even if) (j:a/omkei) (r:zd:14709/zd:11997) (q:draft)
aomkeileh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if there is no/unless there is) (d:<aom>, there is, and <keileh>, if not, written as one word: if there is none, in the absence of) (j:aom/keileh) (r:zd:10759/zd:19586/zd:15939) (q:draft)
aomkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to be/be present) (d:<a> and <omkha> written as one word: who happens to be in a place, those who are there) (j:a/omkha) (r:zd:15257/zd:14944/zd:15159) (q:draft)
aomkhadiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:whether there might be) (d:<aom>, there is, and <khadiam>, might it perhaps, written as one word before <cih> or {ci'n}: whether there may happen to be someone or something) (j:aom/khadiam) (r:zd:16912/zd:13324) (q:draft)
aomkhahiam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:whether there is/whether there might be) (d:<aomkha> and the question particle <hiam> written as one word: whether there happens to be any, said of what is being searched for or checked) (j:aomkha/hiam) (r:zd:15089/zd:19109) (q:draft)
aomkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to be there/should there be) (d:<a> and <omkhak> written as one word: one who happens to be there, or, before <zenzenleh> and <leh>, if there should happen to be) (j:a/omkhak) (r:zd:13303/zd:15811) (q:draft)
aomkhakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there might be/might happen to be) (d:<a>, <omkhak> and <ding> written as one word: that there may happen to be, said of something feared or guarded against, before words such as <lauhuai>, it is to be feared) (j:a/omkhak/ding) (r:zd:13046/zd:14914) (q:draft)
aomkhakleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if there should be/in case there is) (d:<aom>, there is, with <khakleh>, if it happens that, written as one word: if there should happen to be such a person or event) (j:aom/khakleh) (r:zd:11658/zd:14595) (q:draft)
aomkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:one who lives in/one who is in) (d:<a>, <om> and <khat> written as one word: one who is or lives in the place named before it) (j:a/om/khat) (r:zd:19414/zd:11306) (q:draft)
aomkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:live together/stay together/be together) (d:<a> and <omkhawm> written as one word: they live or stay together, the ones who live together; <tawh> marks the companion) (j:a/omkhawm) (r:zd:16688/zd:17768) (q:draft)
aomkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have already been/already exist) (d:<a> and <omkhin> written as one word: has already been or lived somewhere, is already there) (j:a/omkhin) (r:zd:16708/zd:15814) (q:draft)
aomkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have been/have happened/have stayed) (d:<a> and <omkhit> written as one word; mostly in {aomkhit ciangin}, after it had happened or after staying) (j:a/omkhit) (r:zd:12429/zd:14931) (q:draft)
aomkhitzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time/everyday) (w:after there was/since it occurred) (d:<aom> and <khitzawh> written as one word: after something has been or has happened) (j:aom/khitzawh) (r:zd:16304/zd:11219) (q:draft)
aomkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:be together/stay together) (d:<a> and <omkhop> written as one word: they are together; in news reports {aomkhop laitak}, while they were together, is said of a man and a woman being intimate) (j:a/omkhop) (r:zd:12418/zd:18125) (q:draft)
aomkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen again/be again/be restored) (d:<a> and <omkik> written as one word: it is there again or happens again; {aomkik lohding} is so that it does not happen again, and {aomkik nadingin} so that it may return) (j:a/omkik) (r:zd:12115/zd:10768) (q:draft)
aomlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still be/remain/be left) (d:<a> with <omlai>, still be there, written as one word: still exists or is still there; {aomlai in} is while staying at a place, and {aomlai te} are those who remain) (j:a/omlai) (r:zd:24594/zd:11945) (q:draft)
aomlaihiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:whether there still is) (d:<aomlai>, still be there, with the question particle <hiam>, written as one word: is there still any, whether any remains) (j:aomlai/hiam) (r:zd:15084/zd:19635) (q:draft)
aomlaitak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:while he was there/while being) (d:<a>, <om>, be, and <laitak>, at the very time, written as one word: just when someone was in a place or in a state) (j:a/om/laitak) (r:zd:18211/zd:14981) (q:draft)
aomlak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:among those there are) (d:<aom> and <lak> written as one word, after a number and before <ah>: among the so many that exist) (j:aom/lak) (r:zd:17770/zd:11837) (q:draft)
aomlam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:that there is) (d:<a> and <omlam> written as one word: the fact that someone or something is there, before a verb of knowing, seeing or finding) (j:a/omlam) (r:zd:12422/zd:12274) (q:draft)
aomleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if there is) (d:<a>, <om> and <leh> written as one word: if there is, if any comes up) (j:a/om/leh) (r:zd:11532/zd:21837/zd:14720) (q:draft)
aomlehzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:even if there is/should there be any) (d:<aom>, there is, and <lehzong>, even if, written as one word: even if there is one, should anyone or anything of the kind turn up; in public notices followed by what is then to be done) (j:aom/lehzong) (r:zd:12420/zd:15385) (q:draft)
aomlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:without/lacking/absent) (d:<a>, <om> and <lo> written as one word: that is not there, that has none, after the thing that is lacking) (j:a/om/lo) (r:zd:19383/zd:15968) (q:draft)
aomloding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:so that there is no/that there be none) (d:<aomlo>, there is not, and <ding>, will, written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: so that there will be none of the thing named before it, without any) (j:aomlo/ding) (r:zd:11889/zd:20425/zd:16302) (q:draft)
aomloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is not/be absent/not exist) (d:<a>, <om> and <loh> written as one word: there not being, used before words such as <hangin>, <ciangin>, <laitak> and <nading>) (j:a/om/loh) (r:zd:21937/zd:20514/zd:11382) (q:draft)
aomloh nadingin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:so that there is no/to prevent/lest there be) (d:<aomloh>, there is not, and <nadingin>, in order that: placed after a noun or a list of things that are not wanted, it gives the purpose of the action that follows, that such things may not be or happen) (r:zd:16916/zd:14701) (q:draft)
aomlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:absence/where there is none/lack) (d:<a> and <omlohna> written as one word: the fact that something is not there; before a noun of place, where there is none, as in {kuamah aomlohna}, where there is nobody) (j:a/omlohna) (r:zd:15236/zd:12996) (q:draft)
aomm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:aom) (r:zd:19644/zd:12723) (q:draft)
aomman = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:because there is/because of being) (d:<a>, <om>, be, and <man>, short for <manin>, because, written as one word and often followed by <mahin>: because there is, because someone is so) (j:a/om/man) (r:zd:11980/zd:16840) (q:draft)
aomman = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have been/have stayed) (d:<a>, <om>, be, and the completive <man> written as one word: has already been in a place or state for the time named) (j:a/om/man) (r:zd:19385) (q:draft, low confidence)
aommawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/social) (w:naughty/restless/unruly) (d:<a> and <ommawh> written as one word: who is restless or naughty, said of a child) (j:a/ommawh) (r:zd:15756/zd:19465) (q:draft)
aomna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:where he lives/whereabouts/place where there is) (d:<a> and <omna> written as one word: the place where someone or something is or lives; before a noun, the place where such people or things are) (j:a/omna) (r:zd:17711/zd:12042/zd:11058) (q:draft)
aomnading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:so that there is/in order to have) (d:<a>, <om> and <nading> written as one word: for there to be, so that something exists or is kept, as in {lungmuanna aomnading}, to keep the peace) (j:a/om/nading) (r:zd:16702/zd:15512) (q:draft)
aomnang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/politics) (w:so that there is/in order that there be) (d:<aom>, there is, with a shortened form of <nading>, in order to, written as one word: so that there may be) (j:aom/nading) (r:zd:14924) (q:draft, low confidence)
aomnawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is no longer/be no more) (d:<a> and <omnawnlo> written as one word: there is no longer any, or the one that no longer has or is) (j:a/omnawnlo) (r:zd:14831/zd:21321) (q:draft)
aomnawnloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be no longer/be no more) (d:<a>, <omnawn> be any more and the negative <loh> written as one word, the form used before <ciangin>, <manin> and <nadingin>: no longer being there, so that there is no more of it) (j:a/omnawn/loh) (r:zd:17653/zd:20186/zd:12214) (q:draft)
aomngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have been/once was/have lived) (d:<a> and <omngei> written as one word: has been or has lived somewhere before, has existed before; {aomngei nailo} is that has never been) (j:a/omngei) (r:zd:13157/zd:20203/zd:12327) (q:draft)
aompa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:the man who is/the man who lives) (d:<a> and <ompa> written as one word: the man who is or lives in a place) (j:a/ompa) (r:zd:17311/zd:15033) (q:draft)
aompen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the one that is/being) (d:<a>, <om>, be, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the one that is there, or the fact that something is or stays, as the topic of the sentence) (j:a/om/pen) (r:zd:16511/zd:20012/zd:14587) (q:draft)
aomphial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:even if there is) (d:<aom> and <phial> written as one word, followed by <zongin>: even if there is, even if there should be) (j:aom/phial) (r:zd:15949/zd:14618) (q:draft)
aompih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/social) (w:live with/stay with) (d:<a> and <ompih> written as one word: who lives or stays with someone, the person one lives with) (j:a/ompih) (r:zd:11637/zd:16700) (q:draft)
aomsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:existing/already there) (d:<a> and <omsa>, already there, written as one word: that which already exists, those who are already there) (j:a/omsa) (r:zd:16817/zd:15134/zd:25243) (q:draft)
aomsam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there are indeed/there certainly are) (d:<a> and <omsam> written as one word: there are, to be sure; usually before <hang> or <hangin>, although, granting a point before a contrast) (j:a/omsam) (r:zd:12325/zd:22873) (q:draft)
aomsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:stay on/remain/overstay) (d:<a> and <omsuak>, stay on, written as one word: go on staying in a place, in the articles mostly in a country after a visa has run out) (j:a/omsuak) (r:zd:15165/zd:26495) (q:draft)
aomsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:while there/during the stay) (d:<aom>, he is there, and <sung>, during, written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: while he or she was in a place) (j:aom/sung) (r:zd:12674/zd:26495) (q:draft)
aomte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who are/those who live) (d:<a> and <omte> written as one word: those who are or live in a place or state; {gamdang ah aomte} is those who are abroad) (j:a/omte) (r:zd:11685/zd:10842) (q:draft)
aomteng = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:all who are in/everything in) (d:<a> and <omteng> written as one word: all those who are in a place, everything that is there) (j:a/omteng) (r:zd:16137/zd:18042) (q:draft)
aomthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can happen/can be/occur) (d:<a> and <omthei> written as one word: can be or can happen; {aomthei zelzel} is it happens again and again) (j:a/omthei) (r:zd:19002/zd:11126) (q:draft)
aomtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to be/may be) (d:<a> and <omtheih> written as one word; {aomtheih nadingin} is so that there may be, so that one can stay) (j:a/omtheih) (r:zd:21552/zd:21409/zd:17593) (q:draft)
aomzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:have been/have stayed/since there is) (d:<a> and <omzawh> written as one word: the time that he, she or it has been in a place or state, followed by a length of time; also since something came to be there) (j:a/omzawh) (r:zd:12329/zd:20278/zd:11768) (q:draft)
aomzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:its condition/his behaviour/the way it is) (d:<a>, his, her or its, and <omzia>, condition or way of being, written as one word: how a person or thing is, looks or behaves) (j:a/omzia) (r:zd:18007/zd:16976) (q:draft)
aomzong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:even if there is/those who also are) (d:<aom>, there is, and <zong>, also or even, written as one word: even when there is, or those who are there as well) (j:aom/zong) (r:zd:20046/zd:20023) (q:draft)
apa = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:father/his father/her father) (d:<a>, his or her, and <pa>, father, written as one word: the father of the person spoken of, often paired with <anu>, the mother, as in <anu apa>, the parents; not the male animal of the other sense) (r:zd:17731/zd:17028/zd:19563) (q:draft)
apaai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:be pregnant/carry a child) (d:<a> and <paai> written as one word, in {nau apaai}: she is pregnant, her being with child) (j:a/paai) (r:zd:13346/zd:23479) (q:draft)
apaai = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work) (w:means/goods/resources) (d:only in the pair {asum apaai}, money and means: the funds and goods that a work needs; the second word is that of {sum leh paai}, money and goods, not the verb <paai>, throw) (j:a/paai) (r:zd:20550/zd:23315) (q:draft, low confidence)
apaailam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/health) (w:that she is pregnant) (d:<a>, <paai>, carry a child, and <lam>, the fact, written as one word after <nau>: the fact that she is pregnant) (j:a/paai/lam) (r:zd:14931/zd:16332) (q:draft)
apaaizawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:have been pregnant for) (d:<apaai>, she is pregnant, and <zawh>, after, since, written as one word, in {nau apaaizawh} before a number of months: the time since she became pregnant) (j:apaai/zawh) (r:zd:16946/zd:14613) (q:draft)
apaak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:its flower/blossom) (d:<a> and <paak>, flower, written as one word: its flower, the flower of; before <hun> its flowering, as in {apaak hun}, the time when it blooms) (j:a/paak) (r:zd:21822/zd:22581) (q:draft)
apaam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:surroundings/neighbourhood) (d:<a> and <paam> written as one word, second half of the pairs {akiim apaam}, all around it, and {aveng apaam}, the neighbours) (j:a/paam) (r:zd:14935/zd:19453/zd:19392) (q:draft)
apaang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his cheek/her cheek) (d:<a> and <paang> written as one word: his, her or their cheek, mostly of a cheek that is slapped) (j:a/paang) (r:zd:15280/zd:17818) (q:draft)
apahtawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:honor/esteem) (d:<a> and <pahtawi> written as one word: he honors, the one who honors or is to be honored; {apahtawi taak} is worthy of honor) (j:a/pahtawi) (r:zd:22371/zd:23554) (q:draft)
apahtawina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:honoring/honor) (d:<a> and <pahtawina> written as one word: their honoring of someone, the honor given) (j:a/pahtawina) (r:zd:23882/zd:24123) (q:draft)
apai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go) (d:<a> and <pai> written as one word: he or they go, or the one who goes) (j:a/pai) (r:zd:12801/zd:21965/zd:15649) (q:draft)
apaiciang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/travel) (w:when going/when he goes) (d:<a>, <pai>, go, and <ciang>, when, written as one word and often followed by <in>: when he, she or they go or walk) (j:a/pai/ciang) (r:zd:25926/zd:12117) (q:draft)
apaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:will go/be going to) (d:<a>, <pai>, go, and <ding> written as one word: he or she will go, the one who is to go, or his or her going; {apaiding phallo} is not allow to go) (j:a/pai/ding) (r:zd:15761/zd:17258/zd:16232) (q:draft)
apaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:throw away/dump/discard) (d:<a> and <paih>, throw away, written as one word: they threw it away, what was thrown away) (j:a/paih) (r:zd:22142) (q:draft)
apaihkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:throw away/discard/discharge) (d:<a> and <paihkhiat> written as one word, before a noun: that someone has thrown away or let out) (j:a/paihkhiat) (r:zd:16257/zd:11860) (q:draft)
apaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:throw away/dump/throw down) (d:<a> and <paihsak> written as one word: who threw away or dumped something that belongs to another, or what was thrown away) (j:a/paihsak) (r:zd:16365) (q:draft)
apaihsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:intend to throw away/try to dump) (d:<a>, <paih>, throw away, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: he plans to throw it away, or the one who tried to throw it away) (j:a/paih/sawm) (r:zd:11872) (q:draft)
apaikawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:while going/on the way) (d:<a> and <paikawm> written as one word: while he is going, as he goes; usually followed by <in>) (j:a/paikawm) (r:zd:20013/zd:18007) (q:draft)
apaikhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go together/accompany) (d:<a> and <paikhawm> written as one word: they went together, or those who go together) (j:a/paikhawm) (r:zd:12094/zd:15491) (q:draft)
apaikhempeuh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel/everyday) (w:all who go/all that pass) (d:<apai>, the one who goes, and <khempeuh>, all, written as one word: everyone who goes or comes, every vehicle that passes) (j:apai/khempeuh) (r:zd:15487/zd:16696) (q:draft)
apaikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go out/leave/depart) (d:<a> and <paikhia> written as one word: he went out, the one or the thing that goes out) (j:a/paikhia) (r:zd:20461/zd:25927) (q:draft)
apaikhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:be due to leave/be about to depart/will go out) (d:<apaikhia>, he or it goes out, with <ding>, will, written as one word: that is about to leave, said often of a train or vehicle due to set off) (j:apaikhia/ding) (r:zd:19719/zd:19712) (q:draft)
apaikhial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:go astray/go wrong) (d:<a> and <paikhial> written as one word: he or they go astray, or the one who has gone wrong) (j:a/paikhial) (r:zd:20454/zd:24289) (q:draft)
apaikhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go out/leave/depart) (d:<a> and <paikhiat> written as one word: he or she goes out or leaves; {apaikhiat laitak} is just as he was leaving) (j:a/paikhiat) (r:zd:12347/zd:17442/zd:11823) (q:draft)
apaikhiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:about to leave/to go out) (d:<apaikhiat> and <ding> written as one word: his or her going out that is still to come; with <ciangin>, when about to leave) (j:apaikhiat/ding) (r:zd:16826/zd:19614) (q:draft)
apaikhiatma = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel/everyday) (w:before leaving/before setting out) (d:<apaikhiat>, he or she leaves, and <ma>, before, written as one word and followed by <in>: before he, she or it leaves) (j:apaikhiat/ma) (r:zd:14521) (q:draft)
apaikhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:its departure/place of departure/starting point) (d:<a> and <paikhiatna> written as one word: the leaving of a person or a train, or the place from which it set out) (j:a/paikhiatna) (r:zd:14726/zd:25609) (q:draft)
apaikhiatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:lead out/take out/bring out) (d:<a> and <paikhiatpih> written as one word: he, she or they go out taking someone along) (j:a/paikhiatpih) (r:zd:15384) (q:draft)
apaikhiatsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:be about to leave/try to go out) (d:<a>, <paikhiat>, go out, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: he or it was about to leave or tried to get away) (j:a/paikhiat/sawm) (r:zd:15419/zd:16511) (q:draft)
apaikhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/time) (w:have gone/have passed) (d:<a> and <paikhit> written as one word: after he or she has gone, or after a time or distance has passed; mostly before <ciangin>) (j:a/paikhit) (r:zd:18943/zd:15236) (q:draft)
apaikhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go together/walk together) (d:<a> and <paikhop> written as one word: they go along together, mostly before <laitak>, while) (j:a/paikhop) (r:zd:15114/zd:11342) (q:draft)
apaikik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go back/return/come back) (d:<a> and <paikik> written as one word: he or they go back, it comes back) (j:a/paikik) (r:zd:11729/zd:16360) (q:draft)
apailai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:be going/be on the way/be travelling) (d:<a>, <pai> and <lai> written as one word: while still going, or the one who is on the way; of electricity, be running) (j:a/pai/lai) (r:zd:13138/zd:22873) (q:draft)
apailaitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/everyday) (w:while going/on the way) (d:<a>, <pai> and <laitak> written as one word: at the very time he, she or it was going or travelling) (j:a/pai/laitak) (r:zd:13330/zd:19536) (q:draft)
apailam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:going/coming/the fact of going) (d:<a> and <pailam> written as one word: that someone or something goes or comes, the fact of having gone; {apailam in} is on going, on the way there) (j:a/pailam) (r:zd:11780/zd:13328) (q:draft)
apaileh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:when he went/as he went) (d:<a>, <pai>, go, and <leh>, when, written as one word: when or as he or she went, followed by what was found or what happened there) (j:a/pai/leh) (r:zd:16254/zd:14635) (q:draft)
apailoh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not go/not come/not flow) (d:<a> and <pailoh> written as one word: he does not come, or of water it does not flow; used before words such as <ciangin>) (j:a/pailoh) (r:zd:17834/zd:19197) (q:draft)
apaina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:where he goes/his way/his going) (d:<a> and <paina> written as one word: the place or way where someone goes, or his going; {apaina peuhah} is wherever she goes) (j:a/paina) (r:zd:16757/zd:12942/zd:14583) (q:draft)
apainading = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:destination) (d:<a>, <pai>, go, and <nading>, for, written as one word: where someone or something is going, the place or way to be gone to) (j:a/pai/nading) (r:zd:21366/zd:17930) (q:draft)
apainop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:want to go/like to visit) (d:<a> and <painop> written as one word: they want to go, mostly as {apainop mahmahna mun}, a place people very much like to visit) (j:a/painop) (r:zd:15822/zd:17239) (q:draft)
apainopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:destination/place one wants to go) (d:<a> and <painopna> written as one word: the place where he or she wants to go) (j:a/painopna) (r:zd:19338/zd:15822) (q:draft)
apainuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:want to go/who wants to go) (d:<a> and <painuam> written as one word: he wants to go, or the one who wants to go) (j:a/painuam) (r:zd:17994/zd:23437) (q:draft)
apaipa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:the man who went/the one who goes) (d:<a> and <paipa> written as one word: the man who went or who is walking along) (j:a/paipa) (r:zd:15913) (q:draft)
apaipai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:keep going/go along) (d:<a> and <paipai>, keep going, written as one word: he, she or it is going along, is on the move; {apaipai laitak in} is while it was going along) (j:a/paipai) (r:zd:11392/zd:12790/zd:11217) (q:draft)
apaipaita = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:be already moving/be on its way) (d:<a>, <paipai>, keep going, and <ta>, now, written as one word: it is already moving along) (j:a/paipai/ta) (r:zd:19807/zd:16164) (q:draft)
apaipak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go for a while/go quickly) (d:<a> and <paipak> written as one word: he or she went out for a short while) (j:a/paipak) (r:zd:12742/zd:14935) (q:draft)
apaipen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/travel) (w:the one who goes/those who went) (d:<apai>, the one who goes, and the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: as for the one who went, or as for his going) (j:apai/pen) (r:zd:14646/zd:17332) (q:draft)
apaiphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go over to/go across/head toward) (d:<a> and <paiphei>, go across, written as one word: he or she goes over toward a place or person, or the one that is going across) (j:a/paiphei) (r:zd:21294/zd:16598) (q:draft)
apaipih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:take along/bring/take to) (d:<a> and <paipih> written as one word: he, she or they took someone or something along to a place; also the one taken along or the one who takes) (j:a/paipih) (r:zd:20215/zd:17782) (q:draft)
apaisawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:intend to go/be about to go) (d:<a> and <paisawm> written as one word: who was planning to go or was on the way to a place) (j:a/paisawm) (r:zd:12906/zd:13063/zd:17067) (q:draft)
apaisuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:going down/heading down) (d:<a> and <paisuk> written as one word: that goes down, of a vehicle or a traveller heading down to a lower place; {apaisuk apaito} is those going down and those going up) (j:a/paisuk) (r:zd:15693/zd:17067) (q:draft)
apaite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:those who go/travellers) (d:<a> and <paite> written as one word: the people who go or travel; {khetawh apaite} are those going on foot, pedestrians) (j:a/paite) (r:zd:11668/zd:16782) (q:draft)
apaithei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:can go/be able to walk) (d:<a> and <paithei> written as one word: he or they can go, or the one who can go or walk) (j:a/paithei) (r:zd:17304/zd:12355) (q:draft)
apaitheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:be able to go/be able to come) (d:<a> and <paitheih> written as one word: that he, she or they can go; mostly in {apaitheih nadingin}, so that they can go) (j:a/paitheih) (r:zd:17729/zd:17115) (q:draft)
apaito = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:go up/travel up) (d:<a> and <paito> written as one word: the one going up, of travellers and vehicles on the way up to a place; {apaisuk apaito} are those going down and those going up) (j:a/paito) (r:zd:15715/zd:11803) (q:draft)
apaizia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:way/course/manner) (d:<a> and <paizia> written as one word: the way it goes, how a thing proceeds or is done) (j:a/paizia) (r:zd:26444/zd:11587) (q:draft)
apakik = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:stepfather) (d:<a>, <pa>, father, and <kik>, again, written as one word: his or her stepfather) (j:a/pa/kik) (r:zd:12618) (q:draft, low confidence)
apalsat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:violate/break/transgress) (d:<a> and <palsat> written as one word: he breaks a law or rule, or the one who breaks it) (j:a/palsat) (r:zd:14846) (q:draft)
apam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:vicinity/surroundings/nearby) (d:<a> and <pam> written as one word: the place beside it; paired as {akiim apam}, {agei apam} and {aveng apam}, all around, the neighbours) (j:a/pam) (r:zd:25680/zd:13324/zd:16832) (q:draft)
apamdeuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:a little way off/close by/just beside) (d:<apam>, the place beside it, and <deuh>, somewhat, written as one word: a short distance to the side, near by) (j:apam/deuh) (r:zd:20629/zd:20615) (q:draft)
apan = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday/time) (w:from/since) (d:<a> and <pan>, from, written as one word after a noun or a time word: from that place or time on; {ka neu apan} is since I was small) (j:a/pan) (r:zd:17478/zd:12177/zd:21439) (q:draft)
apan = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:take part/join in) (d:<a> with <pan>, the form of <pang>, take part or take a side, written as one word: one who takes part; {apan pihnuam} is one who wants to join in and help) (j:a/pan) (r:zd:23833) (q:draft, low confidence)
apaneu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his uncle/her uncle/paternal uncle) (d:<a>, his or her, with {paneu}, the younger brother of a father, written as one word: his or her father's younger brother) (j:a/pa/neu) (r:zd:11557) (q:draft)
apang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:side) (d:<pang>, side, with the prefix <a> written as one word: the side of the thing named before it, as in {inn apang}, the side of a house) (r:zd:15021/zd:17777/zd:16878) (q:draft)
apang = (i:3) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:take part/work for/contribute) (d:the verb <pang> with the prefix <a> written as one word, after <ma>: <ma apang> is who takes an active part in a cause or works for it) (r:zd:23742/zd:22046/zd:23643) (q:draft)
apangkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:one side of it/one side) (d:<a> and <pangkhat> written as one word: one side of a house, a box or a road) (j:a/pangkhat) (r:zd:15021/zd:18030) (q:draft)
