aphialkap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:shoot at random/open fire indiscriminately) (d:with <thautawh> or <thau> before it: fire a gun at people without aim, shooting whoever is there; the prefix <a>, <phial> and <kap>, shoot, written as one word) (r:zd:17032/zd:19752) (q:draft)
aphialkapgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:shoot indiscriminately/open fire at random) (d:<a>, <phial> and <kapgawp> written as one word: he fired in all directions at whoever was there, said of a gunman in a mass shooting) (j:a/phial/kapgawp) (r:zd:17750/zd:19745) (q:draft)
aphiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home) (w:sweep) (d:<a> and <phiat> written as one word: he or she sweeps; {inn aphiat} is sweeps the floor) (j:a/phiat) (r:zd:14646/zd:12785) (q:draft)
aphu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:revenge/vengeance) (d:<a> and <phu.1>, revenge, written as one word: revenge for him or for it; {aphu la} is take revenge, avenge) (j:a/phu) (r:zd:19579/zd:19805/zd:15301) (q:draft)
aphu = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:face/stand up to/withstand) (d:<a> and <phu.2>, push against, written as one word: meet a hardship or an opponent head on) (j:a/phu) (r:zd:24376/zd:12607) (q:draft, low confidence)
aphuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:compose/make up/coin) (d:<a> and <phuah> written as one word: that he composed, said of a song, or made up, said of a name) (j:a/phuah) (r:zd:15396/zd:24594) (q:draft)
aphuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:compose/name/make up) (d:<a> and <phuak> written as one word: he composed a song or gave a name, or the one who composed it) (j:a/phuak) (r:zd:25318/zd:15996) (q:draft)
aphuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:composers/authors/makers) (d:<a> and <phuakte> written as one word: those who composed or made it; {Late aphuakte} is the writers of the Psalms) (j:a/phuakte) (r:zd:25200/zd:23135) (q:draft)
aphual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the scene/the spot/the place itself) (d:<a> and <phual> written as one word: the very place where something happened; {aphual ah} is on the spot, at the scene) (j:a/phual) (r:zd:13161/zd:17166/zd:24481) (q:draft)
aphual mahah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:media) (w:on the spot/at the scene) (d:<aphual>, the very place, and <mahah>, right at: on the spot, at the scene; in reports of accidents and attacks, of a person who dies where it happened) (r:zd:12992/zd:15631) (q:draft)
aphualmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:on the spot/at the very place) (d:<aphual>, the scene, and the emphatic <mah> written as one word, followed by <ah>: right there where it happened, as in {aphualmah ah sipah}, died on the spot) (j:aphual/mah) (r:zd:14873/zd:16942) (q:draft)
aphualphual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:each spot/each place) (d:<aphual> with <phual> repeated, often after <munmun>: each place in turn, every place where people are) (b:aphual) (r:zd:24062/zd:24024) (q:draft, low confidence)
aphualpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:main station/headquarters/centre) (d:<a> and <phualpi> in the sense main site written as one word: its main plant or central seat, as in {tuihawmkhiatna aphualpi}, the main water distribution plant) (j:a/phualpi) (r:zd:18042/zd:18024) (q:draft, low confidence)
aphualzang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:on the very spot/right at the scene) (d:<aphual>, the scene, with <zang.2>, the very middle: right at the place where the thing happened; {aphualzang mahah sipah} is died at once on the spot) (b:aphual) (r:zd:21334/zd:22688) (q:draft)
aphuankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:founder/who founded) (d:<a> and <phuankhia> written as one word: the one who founded or started something) (j:a/phuankhia) (r:zd:15777/zd:25589) (q:draft)
aphugawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:crash into/ram/smash into) (d:<a> and <phugawp> written as one word: of a vehicle or its driver, run hard into something or someone) (j:a/phugawp) (r:zd:17874/zd:12347) (q:draft)
aphukha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:hit/crash into/collide with) (d:<a> and <phukha> written as one word: ran into, struck, said mostly of a vehicle; also the one that hit) (j:a/phukha) (r:zd:11479/zd:15619/zd:17149) (q:draft)
aphulgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:ram into/plough into) (d:<a> and <phulgawp> written as one word: it rammed into, drove into with force) (j:a/phulgawp) (r:zd:11646/zd:11856) (q:draft)
aphulkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:well up/spring from/come out of) (d:<a> and <phulkhia> written as one word: that wells up or comes out from within, said of thoughts, effort or knowledge) (j:a/phulkhia) (r:zd:12571/zd:16343) (q:draft)
aphum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:bury/lay in the ground) (d:<a> and <phum> written as one word: that someone buried, what is laid under the ground) (j:a/phum) (r:zd:16604/zd:12422) (q:draft)
aphum = (i:2) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:baptize/immerse) (d:<a> and <phum> written as one word, with <tui>, water: baptizing) (j:a/phum) (r:zd:20076) (q:draft, low confidence)
aphumsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:bury/have buried) (d:<a>, <phum>, bury, and the causative <sak> written as one word: the one who buried someone or had someone buried in the ground) (j:a/phum/sak) (r:zd:12450) (q:draft, low confidence)
aphumsak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:plunge/immerse) (d:<a>, <phum>, immerse, and the causative <sak> written as one word: the one who pushed something under a liquid) (j:a/phum/sak) (r:zd:21601) (q:draft, low confidence)
aphun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:grumble/complain) (d:<a> and <phun> written as one word: he grumbles, or one who grumbles) (j:a/phun) (r:zd:15743) (q:draft)
aphung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:his clan/his lineage) (d:<a> and <phung> written as one word: his or her clan, mostly in the pair {abeh aphung}, his family and clan) (j:a/phung) (r:zd:18107/zd:15259) (q:draft)
aphunphun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:complain/grumble/those who complain) (d:<a> and <phunphun> written as one word: the people who keep complaining, or their complaining; often after the words of the complaint and {ci'n}) (j:a/phunphun) (r:zd:16817/zd:16608) (q:draft)
aphusuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:crash into/run into) (d:<a>, <phu.2>, push against, and <suk>, down, written as one word: a vehicle runs into another, here from behind) (j:a/phu/suk) (r:zd:17149/zd:14644) (q:draft)
aphut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:found/establish/set up) (d:<a> and <phut> written as one word: he or they found or set up, as in {gam aphut}, found a country) (j:a/phut) (r:zd:20125/zd:11697) (q:draft)
aphut = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:hit/crash into/collide with) (d:<a> and <phut> written as one word, said of a vehicle: it runs into a person or thing) (j:a/phut) (r:zd:15727) (q:draft, low confidence)
aphutkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:hit/crashed into/came up against) (d:<a> and <phutkhak> written as one word: what something ran into or collided with, mostly in reports of road accidents; also what one has come up against) (j:a/phutkhak) (r:zd:19002/zd:20767/zd:11646) (q:draft)
aphutkhakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:the place it hit/its collision) (d:<a> and <phutkhakna>, collision, written as one word: the collision of a vehicle, or the spot where it struck) (j:a/phutkhakna) (r:zd:19127/zd:12475) (q:draft)
aphutkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:found/establish/set up) (d:<a> and <phutkhia> written as one word: the one who founded it, he or she founded) (j:a/phutkhia) (r:zd:17526) (q:draft)
aphutsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:ram into/crash into) (d:<a> with <phut>, run into, and <sak>, written as one word, in road accident reports: a vehicle rams into another, as {anunglam aphutsak}, it rammed into the rear) (j:a/phut/sak) (r:zd:19127) (q:draft, low confidence)
api = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:grandmother) (d:<a> and <pi.2> written as one word: his or her grandmother, often named together with <apu>, his or her grandfather) (j:a/pi) (r:zd:16688/zd:21815) (q:draft)
apia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give/the one who gives) (d:<a> and <pia> written as one word: he gives or gave, or before a noun the one that gives) (j:a/pia) (r:zd:23670/ts:3992/zd:17224) (q:draft)
apiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to give/who will give) (d:<a>, <pia> and <ding> written as one word: the one who will give, or in order to give; {Security apiading} is to provide security) (j:a/pia/ding) (r:zd:12293/zd:19868/zd:11209) (q:draft)
apiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give/that is given) (d:<a> and <piak>, give, written as one word: he gives or it is given, and before a noun what someone gave) (j:a/piak) (r:zd:24157/zd:21690/zd:22293) (q:draft)
apiakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:to be given/to be paid) (d:<a>, <piak> and <ding> written as one word: what he is to give or what is to be given, said often of money to be paid) (j:a/piak/ding) (r:zd:13270/zd:14877) (q:draft)
apiakha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:happen to give/who has paid) (d:<a> and <piakha> written as one word: he happened to give, or the one who has ended up giving or paying) (j:a/piakha) (r:zd:14505/zd:19871) (q:draft)
apiakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:give/give away/donate) (d:<a> and <piakhia> written as one word: he gave away, the one who gives or what is given) (j:a/piakhia) (r:zd:14716/zd:14975/zd:25928) (q:draft)
apiakhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:who will donate/to give out) (d:<a>, <piakhia>, give away, and <ding>, will, written as one word: the one who is to give something away, a donor of blood or of an organ) (j:a/piakhia/ding) (r:zd:15489/zd:15305) (q:draft)
apiakhiazo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:be able to give/be able to give out) (d:<a>, <piakhia>, give out, and <zo>, be able, written as one word; in thanks to donors, {apiakhiazo semsem dingin} is that they may be able to give more and more) (j:a/piakhia/zo) (r:zd:22212) (q:draft)
apiakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:give out/donate/hand over) (d:<a> and <piakkhiat> written as one word: he gives out, what he has given or handed over) (j:a/piakkhiat) (r:zd:11775/zd:14975) (q:draft)
apiakkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have given/after giving) (d:<a> and <piakkhit> written as one word: he or she has given; {apiakkhit ciangin} is after giving) (j:a/piakkhit) (r:zd:23201/zd:11803) (q:draft)
apiakkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:must pay/have to give) (d:<a> and <piakkul> written as one word: he or they must give or pay it) (j:a/piakkul) (r:zd:20912/zd:19563) (q:draft)
apiakloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not give/not pay) (d:<a>, <piak> and <loh> written as one word: that he does not give or pay, what has not been given or paid) (j:a/piak/loh) (r:zd:15443/zd:16809/zd:13350) (q:draft)
apiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:giving/the giving of) (d:<a> and <piakna> written as one word: his or their giving of something, the act or occasion of giving; {tha apiakna} is his encouragement) (j:a/piakna) (r:zd:12196/zd:21514) (q:draft)
apiaknop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:want to give/wish to give) (d:<a> and <piaknop> written as one word: he wants to give) (j:a/piaknop) (r:zd:18107/zd:19662) (q:draft)
apiakpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what was given/the giving) (d:<a>, <piak> and <pen> written as one word: what he gave, or the fact that he gave, as the topic of the sentence) (j:a/piak/pen) (r:zd:20300/zd:16809) (q:draft)
apiaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:given/already given/paid) (d:<a> and <piaksa> written as one word: that has already been given, paid or issued, or the one who has given it) (j:a/piaksa) (r:zd:11635/zd:19563) (q:draft)
apiaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:make pay/pay for/give for) (d:<a> and <piaksak> written as one word: he gave or paid it for someone, or made someone give or pay it, as a fine or a cost) (j:a/piaksak) (r:zd:12959) (q:draft, low confidence)
apiaksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to give/offer/intend to give) (d:<a> and <piaksawm>, be about to give, written as one word: he or she tries or plans to give, and before a noun what was offered) (j:a/piaksawm) (r:zd:16389/zd:16651) (q:draft)
apiakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those given/the ones he gave) (d:<apiak> and the plural <te> written as one word: the things that someone gave or that are given) (j:apiak/te) (r:zd:25089) (q:draft)
apiaktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can give/that can be given) (d:<a> and <piaktheih> written as one word: that someone can give; with <nading> or <dingin>, so that it can be given) (j:a/piaktheih) (r:zd:16205/zd:16170) (q:draft)
apial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:turn aside/stray/deviate) (d:<a> and <pial> written as one word: he or they turn aside from a way or an agreement) (j:a/pial) (r:zd:26945/ts:3992) (q:draft)
apialkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:go off/leave the track/stray from) (d:<a> and <pialkhia> written as one word: it turned off its way, said of a train that left the rails or an aeroplane that ran off the runway, and of people who depart from a belief) (j:a/pialkhia) (r:zd:14888/zd:17235) (q:draft)
apialo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not give/not pay) (d:<a>, <pia>, give, and <lo>, not, written as one word: who does not give or pay, that which does not give) (j:a/pia/lo) (r:zd:12190/zd:16809/zd:15970) (q:draft)
apianciang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:when it happens/when it happened) (d:<a>, <pian> and <ciang> written as one word, mostly before <in>: when an event comes about) (j:a/pian/ciang) (r:zd:11416/zd:10968) (q:draft)
apiancil = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:at the beginning/when it first happened/at first) (d:<a> and <piancil>, beginning, written as one word: when a thing first happened or came into being; {apiancil akipan} is from birth) (j:a/piancil) (r:zd:12910/zd:11619) (q:draft)
apianding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:will happen/be going to happen) (d:<a>, <pian> and <ding> written as one word: that will happen, the happening of something yet to come) (j:a/pian/ding) (r:zd:15539/zd:12042) (q:draft)
apiang = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:happen/occur/take place) (d:the prefix <a> written together with <piang> in its meaning come about: happen, said of trouble, an accident or any event, as in {buaina apiang}; not be born) (r:zd:21050/zd:19973/zd:20520) (q:draft)
apiangding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will happen/will be born/will become) (d:<a> and <piangding>, will happen, written as one word: that which will happen, be born or come to be) (j:a/piangding) (r:zd:11783/zd:16294) (q:draft)
apianggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:break out/erupt/happen violently) (d:<a> and <pianggawp> written as one word: it broke out, of a shooting, a jam or other trouble) (j:a/pianggawp) (r:zd:15539/zd:15667) (q:draft)
apiangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:be born from/come out of/originate) (d:<a> and <piangkhia> written as one word: born of, coming or produced out of; with <pan> or <sungpan> for the source) (j:a/piangkhia) (r:ts:3160/zd:15315) (q:draft)
apiangkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:happen again/recur) (d:<apiang>, happen, with <kik>, again, written as one word: of an accident or other event, take place once more) (j:apiang/kik) (r:zd:19646/zd:13328) (q:draft)
apiangna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:place where it happens/birthplace/source) (d:<apiang>, come into being, with the noun suffix <na>, placed before a word of place: where something happens or is produced; {apiangna khua} is the village of his birth) (b:apiang) (r:zd:19662/zd:12823) (q:draft)
apiangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cause/bring about/produce) (d:<a> and <piangsak> written as one word: it causes, or the one that causes; {buaina apiangsak} is the one who caused the trouble) (j:a/piangsak) (r:zd:21276/zd:14802) (q:draft)
apiangsakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:will cause/to bring about) (d:<apiangsak>, cause, and <ding>, will, written as one word; {buaina apiangsakding in} is in order to cause trouble) (j:apiangsak/ding) (r:zd:15602/zd:16637) (q:draft)
apiangsakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the one who caused/perpetrator/creator) (d:<a> and <piangsakpa> written as one word: the man who brought something about, as {buaina apiangsakpa}, the man who caused the trouble; of God, the creator) (j:a/piangsakpa) (r:zd:11883/zd:21916) (q:draft)
apiangsakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:those who cause/the things that cause) (d:<apiangsak> and the plural <te> written as one word: the people or things that bring something about) (j:apiangsak/te) (r:zd:12093/zd:21565) (q:draft)
apiangsakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:can cause/able to bring about) (d:<a> and <piangsakthei>, can cause, written as one word: that can cause, the thing that can give rise to) (j:a/piangsakthei) (r:zd:20234/zd:15807) (q:draft)
apiangta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have happened/have become) (d:<apiang> and <ta>, now or already, written as one word: it has now happened, it has become) (j:apiang/ta) (r:zd:14969/zd:16145) (q:draft)
apiangtakpi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:really happen/truly happen) (d:<a>, <piang>, happen, and <takpi>, truly, written as one word: it really did happen) (j:a/piang/takpi) (r:zd:16934/zd:16851) (q:draft)
apiangte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those born/those that occur) (d:<apiang> and the plural <te> written as one word: those who are born, or the things or cases that come about) (j:apiang/te) (r:zd:11604/zd:15839) (q:draft)
apiangthak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:be born again/the born-again) (d:<a> and <piangthak> written as one word: who is born again, the born-again person) (j:a/piangthak) (r:zd:21042/zd:25919) (q:draft)
apiangthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can happen/possible/can occur) (d:<a> and <piangthei> written as one word: that can happen or come about; {apiangthei lo} is the impossible) (j:a/piangthei) (r:zd:22203/zd:12359/zd:17694) (q:draft)
apianhun = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time/media) (w:time of occurrence/when it happened) (d:<a>, <pian>, happen, and <hun>, time, written as one word: the time at which an event happened, in news reports followed by the hour or date) (j:a/pian/hun) (r:zd:17844/zd:17100) (q:draft)
apiankhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:come into being/arise) (d:<a> and <piankhiat> written as one word: it came into being, its coming about) (j:a/piankhiat) (r:zd:11244) (q:draft)
apiankhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have happened/after it happened) (d:<a> and <piankhit> written as one word; {buaina apiankhit ciangin} is after the trouble had happened) (j:a/piankhit) (r:zd:16749/zd:16109) (q:draft)
apiankhitzawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/media) (w:after it happened) (d:<a>, <pian> and <khitzawh> written as one word: after an event has taken place; with <akipan>, since it happened) (j:a/pian/khitzawh) (r:zd:12803/zd:14995) (q:draft)
apiankik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen again/recur) (d:<a>, <pian>, come about, and <kik>, again, written as one word: that it happens again) (j:a/pian/kik) (r:zd:20490/zd:16463) (q:draft)
apianlaitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/media) (w:when it happened/at the time of) (d:<a>, <pian>, come about, and <laitak>, at the very time, written as one word: at the time when an event took place) (j:a/pian/laitak) (r:zd:14781/zd:13140) (q:draft)
apianlam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:that it happened/how it happened) (d:<a>, <pian> and <lam> written as one word: the fact that something happened or the way it came about, as the thing told or known) (j:a/pian/lam) (r:zd:12493/zd:21035) (q:draft)
apianloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:not happen/not arise) (d:<a> and <pianloh> written as one word, before <nading> or <nadingin>: so that something does not happen) (j:a/pianloh) (r:zd:17630/zd:12860) (q:draft)
apianma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:before it happened/before it came into being) (d:<a> and <pianma> written as one word, placed after the event or thing named: before it happened, before it was born or founded) (j:a/pianma) (r:zd:19779/zd:19788) (q:draft)
apianna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:its occurrence/his birth) (d:<a> and <pianna> written as one word: the happening of an event or the birth of a person; {apianna mun} is the place where it happened, {apianna gam} his native land and {apianna anu} his own mother) (j:a/pianna) (r:zd:17143/zd:21426/zd:12192) (q:draft)
apianni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/media) (w:the day it happened/day of the event) (d:<a>, <pian> and <ni> written as one word: the day on which an event took place) (j:a/pian/ni) (r:zd:12525/zd:15807) (q:draft)
apianpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:the occurrence/when it happened) (d:<a>, <pian> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the happening of it, used to say when or where an event took place) (j:a/pian/pen) (r:zd:12841/zd:17094) (q:draft)
apianpih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/body) (w:inborn/by birth/native/own) (d:<a> and <pianpih> written as one word before a noun: what one has from birth; {apianpih asanggam} is his own brothers and sisters by birth, {apianpih kampau} the mother tongue) (j:a/pianpih) (r:zd:23974/zd:12192/zd:11555) (q:draft)
apiansak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cause/bring about/create) (d:<a> and <piansak> written as one word: he causes, the one who brings about, that which is created) (j:a/piansak) (r:zd:11827/zd:21464) (q:draft)
apianthak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:be born again) (d:<a> and <pianthak> written as one word: he or she was born again in the Christian sense) (j:a/pianthak) (r:zd:19866/zd:18955) (q:draft)
apiantheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can come about/be possible) (d:<a> and <piantheih> written as one word; {apiantheih nadingin} is so that it can come about, in order to bring it into being) (j:a/piantheih) (r:zd:16308/zd:12420) (q:draft)
apianuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:want to give/who wants to give) (d:<a> and <pianuam> written as one word: he wants to give, or the one who wants to give) (j:a/pianuam) (r:zd:17945/zd:16170) (q:draft)
apianzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time/media) (w:since it happened/after it happened) (d:<a> and <pianzawh> written as one word: the time since an event took place, often followed by a length of time) (j:a/pianzawh) (r:zd:11880/zd:19562/zd:21601) (q:draft)
apianzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:how it happened/the way it came about) (d:<a> and <pianzia> written as one word, here from <piang>, happen, with <zia>, manner: the way something happened, as an accident; also the form a thing has) (j:a/pianzia) (r:zd:15194/zd:15078) (q:draft)
apiapia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep giving/the one who keeps giving) (d:<a> and <piapia>, keep giving, written as one word: he or they go on giving, or the one who keeps giving) (j:a/piapia) (r:zd:19562/zd:11652) (q:draft)
apiate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:givers/donors/those who give) (d:<a> and <piate> written as one word: the ones who give, in the articles those who give money to a cause) (j:a/piate) (r:zd:16031/zd:22964) (q:draft)
apicing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:mature/full-grown/complete) (d:<a> and <picing> written as one word: mature, the mature one, said of a person, a life or a faith; also full, complete) (j:a/picing) (r:zd:11395/zd:14791) (q:draft)
apil = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:the wise/the learned/wise) (d:<a> and <pil>, wise, written as one word: one who is wise or learned; {apil asiam} is the learned and the skilled, the educated people) (j:a/pil) (r:zd:21340/zd:24282/zd:12391) (q:draft)
apilding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:become learned/do well in learning) (d:<a>, <pil>, wise or learned, and <ding> written as one word: that he or she should become learned or do well at school) (j:a/pil/ding) (r:zd:18244/zd:12296) (q:draft)
apilna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:knowledge/education/wisdom) (d:<a>, his or her, and <pilna> written as one word: his or her knowledge, learning or education) (j:a/pilna) (r:zd:17224/zd:24574/zd:16126) (q:draft)
apilte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:the wise/the learned) (d:<a> and <pilte>, the wise ones, written as one word: those who are wise or learned) (j:a/pilte) (r:zd:20979/zd:25089) (q:draft)
apilzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:education/everyday) (w:wiser/more learned) (d:<a> and <pilzaw> written as one word: wiser, the one who is wiser, with <sangin>, than) (j:a/pilzaw) (r:zd:20125/zd:17965) (q:draft)
apkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:hand over/give up/surrender) (d:<ap> and <khia> written as one word: hand over to someone; with <ki>, be handed over or give oneself up) (j:ap/khia) (r:zd:19939/zd:20000) (q:draft)
apkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:have handed over/have handed in) (d:<ap>, hand over or entrust, with <khin>, already, written as one word: have already handed something or oneself over) (j:ap/khin) (r:zd:15913/zd:12229) (q:draft, low confidence)
aplo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:not hand over/not surrender) (d:<ap>, hand over, and <lo>, not, written as one word: does not hand over, as power; {ki aplo} is does not give oneself up) (j:ap/lo) (r:zd:23476/zd:16157) (q:draft)
apo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:growing/that grows) (d:<a> and <po> written as one word: that grows or stands growing, said of a plant or tree) (j:a/po) (r:zd:18005/zd:23554) (q:draft)
apoi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:matter/be a loss) (d:<a> and <poi> written as one word; with a negative, as in {apoi hi kei}, it does not matter, it is no loss) (j:a/poi) (r:zd:11403) (q:draft, low confidence)
apologist = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:apologist) (d:a person who defends the Christian faith by argument) (o:English) (r:zd:23086) (q:draft)
apom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:accept/hold to/recognise) (d:<a> and <pom> written as one word: he accepts or holds to it, or the one who accepts; said of a belief, a rule, a result or a government that is recognised) (j:a/pom) (r:zd:11571/zd:16651) (q:draft)
app = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:app/application) (d:a program for a mobile phone or computer) (o:English) (r:zd:16489/zd:25052/zd:25280) (q:draft)
appah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:hand over at once/hand over) (d:<ap>, hand over, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: hand someone or something over straight away, with <tungah> or {khutsung ah} for the one who receives) (j:ap/pah) (r:zd:17501/zd:16126) (q:draft)
appeal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:appeal) (d:a written request to have a decision looked at again, in the articles to UNHCR after a refused claim; {appeal at} is write an appeal) (o:English) (r:zd:21664) (q:draft)
application = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:application/written request) (d:a formal request made on a form, as for a job, a visa or a permit; often beside <ngetna>, request) (o:English) (r:zd:11602/zd:19818/zd:13201) (q:draft)
apply = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:apply) (d:put something to use in a case, the English word used as a Zolai verb) (o:English) (r:ts:3506/zd:23655) (q:draft, low confidence)
appoinment = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (j:appointment) (r:zd:22608/zd:25205) (q:draft)
appointed = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:appointed) (d:named to an office by someone in authority and not chosen by vote; set against <elected>) (o:English) (r:zd:25937/zd:24743) (q:draft, low confidence)
appointment = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:appointment) (d:a fixed day and time to be seen at an office or clinic, in the articles mostly at the UN refugee office; {appointment la} is make an appointment) (o:English) (r:zd:23486/zd:12552) (q:draft)
approve = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:approve) (d:give official approval to an application, a document or a product; {approve sa} is already approved) (o:English) (r:zd:20859/zd:24808) (q:draft)
approved = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:approve/be approved) (d:the English word used as a verb for official approval of a visa, a document or a medicine) (o:English) (r:zd:20620/zd:22070) (q:draft, low confidence)
apps = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:app/application) (d:a program for a phone or computer; the English plural form is written for one or for many) (o:English) (r:zd:24399/zd:25280/zd:20060) (q:draft)
apsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:hand over/pass on/refer) (d:<ap>, hand over, and <sawn>, onward, written as one word: pass a person or a matter on to another authority; with <ki>, be handed over) (j:ap/sawn) (r:zd:11819/zd:19991) (q:draft)
aptheilai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:can still hand over/can still surrender) (d:<ap>, hand over, and <theilai>, still able, written as one word; with <ki>, {ki aptheilai} is can still give oneself up to the authorities) (j:ap/theilai) (r:zd:20276) (q:draft, low confidence)
apu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his grandfather/her grandfather/grandfather) (d:<a> and <pu> written as one word: his, her or their grandfather; {apu apa} is their forefathers and {api apu} grandmother and grandfather) (j:a/pu) (r:zd:24594/zd:16688/ts:479) (q:draft)
apua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:carry/the one carrying) (d:<a> and <pua>, carry, written as one word: he carries, or before a noun the one that carries it or has it with him) (j:a/pua) (r:zd:16321/zd:16815/zd:20915) (q:draft)
apua = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:outside/the outside) (d:<a> and <pua>, outside, written as one word, mostly as {apua lam}, the outside, outdoors) (j:a/pua) (r:zd:22658/zd:24129/zd:23933) (q:draft)
apuading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/travel) (w:to carry/to transport/to fetch) (d:<a> and <puading> written as one word: in order to carry or transport it, or the one that is to carry it) (j:a/puading) (r:zd:15078/zd:14503) (q:draft)
apuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/home) (w:repair/mend) (d:<a> and <puah> written as one word: he repairs, the one who repairs or improves it) (j:a/puah) (r:zd:17402/zd:21102/zd:9134) (q:draft)
apuahding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:to repair it/one who will tend) (d:<a> and <puahding> written as one word: in order to repair it, or the one who will repair or tend it) (j:a/puahding) (r:zd:20186/zd:14928) (q:draft)
apuahkhapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:explosion/place of the blast/eruption) (d:<a> and <puahkhapna> written as one word: its bursting, the place where a bomb went off, a volcano erupted or a thing broke apart) (j:a/puahkhapna) (r:zd:19514/zd:17472) (q:draft)
apuahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/home) (w:repair/restore) (d:<a> and <puahkik> written as one word: he or they repair it, put it back in good order) (j:a/puahkik) (r:zd:17584/zd:20008) (q:draft)
apuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:carry/bring/send/deliver) (d:<a> and <puak> written as one word: he or she carries, brings or sends, and what is carried or sent; {van apuak} is one who delivers goods. In {apuak kham} it is a different word, burst or explode) (j:a/puak) (r:zd:21965/zd:16323/zd:12561) (q:draft)
apuakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/travel) (w:deliver/bring/carry) (d:<a>, <puak> and <ding> written as one word: to deliver or bring, the thing that is to be delivered or brought) (j:a/puak/ding) (r:zd:13151/zd:15602/zd:11138) (q:draft)
apuakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:carry out/take away) (d:<a> and <puakhia>, carry out, written as one word: he or they carried it out of a place) (j:a/puakhia) (r:zd:19906) (q:draft, low confidence)
apuakkham = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:explode/blow up/explosion) (d:<a> and <puakkham> written as one word: it exploded; also that which explodes, an explosion or bomb, as in {apuakkham om}, there was an explosion) (j:a/puakkham) (r:zd:15354/zd:17707/zd:24532) (q:draft)
apuakkhamding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/media) (w:will explode/will erupt/about to explode) (d:<apuakkham>, it explodes, and <ding> written as one word: that it will explode or erupt, of a bomb or a volcano) (j:apuakkham/ding) (r:zd:15382/zd:16834) (q:draft)
apuakkhampen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:the explosion/what exploded) (d:<apuakkham>, what exploded or the explosion, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word) (j:apuakkham/pen) (r:zd:19927/zd:17911) (q:draft)
apuakkhamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:detonate/blow up/set off) (d:<a>, <puakkham>, burst, explode, and the causative <sak> written as one word: he or they made a bomb or the like explode, or the one who did so) (j:a/puakkham/sak) (r:zd:16840/zd:18215) (q:draft)
apuakkhamthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:media/politics) (w:explosive) (d:<a>, <puakkham> and <thei> written as one word: that can explode; alone or before <van>, thing, it names an explosive or a bomb) (j:a/puakkham/thei) (r:zd:16669/zd:11717/zd:19912) (q:draft)
apuakkhap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:explode/blow up) (d:<a> and <puakkhap> written as one word: it exploded, the exploding of a bomb, a gas cylinder or a volcano; {apuakkhap laitak} is at the moment it exploded) (j:a/puakkhap) (r:zd:13034/zd:18215/zd:20668) (q:draft)
apuakkhapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/politics) (w:explosion/blast/eruption) (d:<a> and <puakkhapna>, explosion, written as one word: its exploding, the blast of a bomb or the eruption of a volcano; {apuakkhapna mun} is the place where it exploded) (j:a/puakkhapna) (r:zd:17836/zd:16391) (q:draft)
apuaklam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/travel) (w:that he was carrying) (d:<apuak> and <lam> written as one word: the fact that he or she carries or brings something, as the thing that is noticed, found or told) (j:apuak/lam) (r:zd:12146/zd:12274) (q:draft)
apuakman = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/politics) (w:for carrying/because of carrying) (d:<a>, <puak>, carry, and <man>, short for <manin>, because, written as one word and followed by <in>: because he carried or brought something) (j:a/puak/man) (r:zd:11786) (q:draft, low confidence)
apuakman = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:carrying fee/delivery fee) (d:<a>, <puak>, carry, and <man>, price, written as one word: the payment for carrying or delivering something) (j:a/puak/man) (r:zd:17407) (q:draft, low confidence)
apuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:have carry/make bear/send by) (d:<a> and <puaksak> written as one word: he made someone carry or bear a thing, or it was carried that way) (j:a/puaksak) (r:zd:17407) (q:draft, low confidence)
apuaksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:try to bring/intend to carry/try to send) (d:<apuak>, he carries or sends, and <sawm>, intend or try, written as one word: he tried or meant to carry, bring in or send it; also the one who tried to, and what was to be sent) (j:apuak/sawm) (r:zd:16869/zd:10936) (q:draft)
apuakteng = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/travel) (w:all that is carried) (d:<apuak> and <teng>, all, written as one word: everything that he, she or it carries or has along) (j:apuak/teng) (r:zd:18876/zd:15878) (q:draft)
apualam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:outside/the outside/exterior) (d:<a> and <pualam> written as one word: the outside of it; {apualam ah} is outside and {apualam panin} from outside) (j:a/pualam) (r:zd:14954/zd:15609/zd:14852) (q:draft)
apuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:identity/particulars) (d:found only in the pair <amin apuam>, his name and particulars: the full identity of a person, as in news reports where it has not been made known) (r:zd:11635/zd:15531/zd:23639) (q:draft)
apuampen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/media) (w:identity/particulars) (d:<apuam> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, after <amin>: his name and particulars, his full identity) (j:apuam/pen) (r:zd:18161) (q:draft)
apuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:clothes/clothing) (d:<a> and <puan> written as one word: his, her or their clothes) (j:a/puan) (r:zd:26097/zd:22658/zd:12477) (q:draft)
apuansilh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/body) (w:his clothes/her clothes/their clothes) (d:<a>, his, her or their, and <puansilh>, clothing, written as one word: the clothes that the person spoken of is wearing or owns) (j:a/puansilh) (r:zd:11938/zd:19902/zd:15443) (q:draft)
apuante = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:his clothes/their clothes) (d:<a> and <puante> written as one word: his, her or their clothes) (j:a/puante) (r:zd:22159/zd:21025) (q:draft)
apuanteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:all his clothes/all her clothes) (d:<a> and <puanteng> written as one word: all the clothes a person has on; {apuanteng suahkhia} is take off all his clothes) (j:a/puanteng) (r:zd:16122/zd:11217) (q:draft)
apuapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:carrier/the man carrying) (d:<a> and <puapa> written as one word: the man who carried or brought a thing, named before it) (j:a/puapa) (r:zd:15560) (q:draft)
apuasim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/social) (w:smuggle/carry secretly) (d:<a> and <pua>, carry, with {-sim}, secretly, written as one word: carry something in secret, said of smuggling drugs or gold; before a noun, the one who smuggles) (r:zd:18876/zd:12519) (q:draft)
apuate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:those carrying/bearers) (d:<a> and <puate> written as one word: the ones who carry what is named before it; of a vehicle, that carries so many people) (j:a/puate) (r:zd:20170/zd:23077) (q:draft)
apuatham = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:outward appearance/surface/the outside) (d:<a> and <puatham> written as one word: the outward side of a thing; {apuatham en} is look at the surface only) (j:a/puatham) (r:zd:11994/zd:24327) (q:draft)
apuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:fell/fall down) (d:<a> and <puk>, fall, written as one word: it fell, or the one that fell; said here mostly of a tree falling over) (j:a/puk) (r:zd:18003/zd:18028/zd:19925) (q:draft)
apukna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/nature) (w:fall/falling) (d:<a> and <pukna>, fall, written as one word: the falling of the thing spoken of, as of a tree) (j:a/pukna) (r:zd:18028) (q:draft)
apuksuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:fall down/collapse/topple) (d:<a> and <puksuk> written as one word: it falls down, or the one that fell down, as a tree or a building) (j:a/puksuk) (r:zd:20188/zd:14301) (q:draft)
apulaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:declare/state/make known) (d:<a> and <pulaak> written as one word: he declares, the one that declares or makes known) (j:a/pulaak) (r:zd:25641/zd:23513) (q:draft)
