asawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:send/order) (d:<a> and <sawl> written as one word: he sent or ordered, the one who sends, what he orders) (j:a/sawl) (r:zd:25918/zd:14941) (q:draft)
asawlkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:send out/the one who sent) (d:<a> and <sawlkhia> written as one word: he sent out, or the one who sent someone out to do a thing) (j:a/sawlkhia) (r:zd:18292/zd:11345) (q:draft)
asawlkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:send out/dispatch) (d:<a> and <sawlkhiat> written as one word: he sent them out, the one who sent them out) (j:a/sawlkhiat) (r:zd:11600/zd:18231) (q:draft)
asawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/politics) (w:his command/his sending/order) (d:<a> and <sawlna> written as one word: his, her or their command, the order someone gave) (j:a/sawlna) (r:zd:25609) (q:draft)
asawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:intend/plan/try) (d:<a> and <sawm> written as one word, placed after a verb or noun: he or they intend, plan or try to do it; {atup asawm} is what one aims at and plans) (j:a/sawm) (r:zd:25919/zd:20300/zd:21321) (q:draft)
asawm = (i:2) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:ten/tens) (d:<a> and <sawm>, ten, written as one word: the ten, by tens; with {-na} it forms the ordinals of the tens) (j:a/sawm) (r:zd:21904) (q:draft, low confidence)
asawnkhiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:the man who pushed) (d:<a>, <sawnkhia>, push out, and <pa>, the man who, written as one word: the man who pushed someone out or off) (j:a/sawnkhia/pa) (r:zd:15888) (q:draft)
asawnkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:push out/push off) (d:<a> and <sawnkhiat> written as one word: he or she pushes someone out or off) (j:a/sawnkhiat) (r:zd:15888) (q:draft)
asawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/everyday) (w:wash) (d:<a> and <sawp>, wash, written as one word: he or she washes, the one who washes) (j:a/sawp) (r:zd:19910/zd:19932) (q:draft)
asawt = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time) (w:long/long-lasting/for a long time) (d:<a> and <sawt> written as one word: it lasts long, or what is long in time; {asawt lo in} is before long and {asawt ciangin} after a long time) (j:a/sawt) (r:zd:11714/zd:16820/zd:16216) (q:draft)
asawt loin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:soon/before long/shortly) (d:<asawt>, lasting long, and <loin>, without: before long, soon; stands before the clause, and after a clause with <zawh>, as in {atun zawh uh asawt loin}, means not long after) (r:zd:24333/zd:26097/zd:23556) (q:draft)
asawtkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (w:have already been long/have lasted) (d:<asawt>, it lasts long, and <khin>, already, written as one word; after a number of years, it has already been that long) (j:asawt/khin) (r:zd:19215) (q:draft)
asawtkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (w:have passed/be long past) (d:<asawt>, it lasts long, and <khit>, after, written as one word, said of time: {nai 6 bang asawtkhit ciangin} is after about six hours had passed) (j:asawt/khit) (r:zd:16367/zd:17097) (q:draft)
asawtlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:soon/before long/shortly) (d:<a>, <sawt>, long, and <lo>, not, written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: {asawtlo in} is not long after, soon) (j:a/sawt/lo) (r:zd:13138/zd:22167/zd:25589) (q:draft)
asawtna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:its length/duration/how long) (d:<a> and <sawtna> written as one word: the length of time a thing lasts; {asawtna ciangin} is in the end, after a long while) (j:a/sawtna) (r:zd:16126/zd:10797) (q:draft)
asawtnailo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:recently/not long ago) (d:<a>, <sawt>, long, and <nailo>, not yet, written as one word: not long ago; also before <hun> as {asawtnailo hunsung}, in recent times) (j:a/sawt/nailo) (r:zd:12029/zd:19644/zd:12387) (q:draft)
asawtsawt = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:in the long run/eventually/after a long while) (d:<a> and <sawtsawt> written as one word: as time goes on, after a long time) (j:a/sawtsawt) (r:zd:17988/zd:15571) (q:draft)
ASEAN = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:ASEAN) (d:the Association of Southeast Asian Nations, a union of ten countries of which Myanmar is a member) (o:English) (r:zd:20250/zd:25322) (q:draft)
aseem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (j:asem) (r:zd:15458) (q:draft)
asel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hide/conceal) (d:<a> and <sel>, hide, written as one word: he hides a thing, the one who hides) (j:a/sel) (r:zd:12121) (q:draft, low confidence)
asel = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:sprout/put out shoots) (d:<a> and <sel>, sprout, written as one word; {asel ding te} is those that should sprout) (j:a/sel) (r:zd:11323) (q:draft, low confidence)
aselcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:hide/conceal/keep hidden) (d:<a> and <selcip> written as one word: he or she hides a thing or a person away so that it is not found, or the one who does so) (j:a/selcip) (r:zd:19191/zd:19247) (q:draft)
aselsim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:hide/conceal) (d:<a> and <selsim>, secret, used as a verb and written as one word: he hides it secretly; before a noun, the hidden one or the one who hides) (j:a/selsim) (r:zd:16937/zd:17243) (q:draft)
asemding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:who will serve as/to work as) (d:<a>, <sem>, work, and the future marker <ding> written as one word: the one who will do a job or hold an office, or in order to do it) (j:a/sem/ding) (r:zd:11934/zd:19543) (q:draft)
asemkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:also work as/work at the same time) (d:<a> and <semkawm> written as one word: who does a job alongside something else) (j:a/semkawm) (r:zd:11251/zd:15814) (q:draft)
asemkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:one who works/worker) (d:<a>, <sem> and <khat> written as one word, after <nasep> or a place of work: one who works as, a person employed at) (j:a/sem/khat) (r:zd:11906/zd:18154) (q:draft)
asemkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:work together/work with) (d:<a> and <semkhawm> written as one word: they work together, the one who works with; <tawh> marks the partner) (j:a/semkhawm) (r:zd:16600/zd:21554) (q:draft)
asemkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:he carries out/he does) (d:<a> and <semkhia> written as one word: he or she carries out or brings about something, or the one who does so) (j:a/semkhia) (r:zd:11918/zd:24157) (q:draft)
asemkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:have worked/have served) (d:<a> and <semkhin>, have done, written as one word: one who has already worked or served, often after a length of time) (j:a/semkhin) (r:zd:14772/zd:19586) (q:draft)
asemlaitak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:currently serving/now working) (d:<asem> and <laitak> written as one word: who is serving or working at this very time, said of the present holder of a post, as in {President asemlaitak}, the serving President) (j:asem/laitak) (r:zd:18191/zd:19215) (q:draft)
asemlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:not do/one who does not do) (d:<a>, <sem>, do or work, and <lo>, not, written as one word: one who does not do it; {bangmah asemlo} is one who does nothing) (j:a/sem/lo) (r:zd:16606/zd:24544) (q:draft)
asemlui = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics/work) (w:former/ex-) (d:<a>, <sem>, serve, and <lui>, old, written as one word, placed after the name of an office: the one who held it before, as in {Prime Minister asemlui}, the former Prime Minister) (j:a/sem/lui) (r:zd:19602/zd:20236) (q:draft)
asemngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:formerly serve as/former) (d:<a> and <semngei>, have served before, written as one word, placed after the name of an office: the one who once held it, as {Minister asemngei}, a former minister) (j:a/semngei) (r:zd:17299/zd:16916) (q:draft)
asemnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (d:<asem> and <nu> written as one word: the woman who works as what is named before it) (j:asem/nu) (r:zd:10662/zd:19707) (q:draft)
asemnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:want to do/willing to work) (d:<a> and <semnuam>, want to do, written as one word: one who wants to do the work; {asemnuam mi} is a person willing to do it) (j:a/semnuam) (r:ts:11162/zd:25919) (q:draft)
asempa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:the one who works as/the man serving as) (d:<a> and <sempa> written as one word after the name of a job or office: the man who does that work, as {Security Guard asempa}, the man working as a security guard) (j:a/sempa) (r:zd:12479/zd:11821/zd:11566) (q:draft)
asempen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:the one who works as/the one serving as) (d:<a>, <sem>, work, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word after a post or a workplace: the one who holds that post is, the ones working there are) (j:a/sem/pen) (r:zd:14646/zd:20250) (q:draft)
asemsa = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:those already working/one who has worked) (d:<a>, <sem> and <sa> written as one word: the ones who already work or have worked somewhere, <sa> here meaning already) (j:a/sem/sa) (r:zd:20639) (q:draft, low confidence)
asemte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:workers/those who work) (d:<a> and <semte> written as one word: those who do the work or hold the post named before it) (j:a/semte) (r:zd:19872/zd:14928) (q:draft)
asep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:do/work/serve) (d:<a> and <sep> written as one word: he does or serves, or what he does; {asep ding} is the work to be done and {asep hunsung} the time he served) (j:a/sep) (r:zd:16777/zd:25243/zd:14839) (q:draft)
asepding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:what one has to do/duty/task) (d:<a> with <sep>, do, and <ding>, will, written as one word: what he or she is to do, the work or duty that falls to someone) (j:a/sep/ding) (r:zd:17112/zd:15084) (q:draft)
asepkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:while working as/while doing) (d:<asep>, he works, with <kawm>, while, written as one word: while working at a job, at the same time as doing something else) (j:asep/kawm) (r:zd:14604/zd:15374) (q:draft)
asepkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:carry out/put into practice) (d:<a> and <sepkhiat> written as one word: he carries out, or the carrying out of what was said) (j:a/sepkhiat) (r:zd:15116/zd:24376) (q:draft)
aseplai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be working/be serving/while serving) (d:<a> and <seplai> written as one word: while he was working or holding an office) (j:a/seplai) (r:zd:25064/zd:19679) (q:draft)
aseplaitak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be serving as/be working as) (d:<a>, <sep> and <laitak> written as one word: who is at present working as, or while he or she was serving as, placed after the name of a post) (j:a/sep/laitak) (r:zd:12715/zd:19818) (q:draft)
aseploh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:not do/leave undone) (d:<a> and <seploh> written as one word: he or she does not do it, or what has not been done; {aseploh phamawh} is what must be done) (j:a/seploh) (r:zd:22989/zd:12279) (q:draft)
asepma = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work/time) (w:before serving as/before working as) (d:<a>, <sep>, work, and <ma>, before, written as one word and followed by <in>, after the name of the work or office: before he or she held it) (j:a/sep/ma) (r:zd:20902/zd:21649) (q:draft)
asepna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:his work/their work) (d:<a> and <sepna> written as one word: the work he or they do, what he does, the post he serves in) (j:a/sepna) (r:zd:24673/zd:17120) (q:draft)
aseppih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:colleague/fellow worker/co-worker) (d:<a> and <seppih> written as one word: the one he works with, his fellow worker; {aseppih uh} is their colleague) (j:a/seppih) (r:zd:21379/zd:21421) (q:draft)
aseppihte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:his co-workers/his colleagues) (d:<a> and <seppihte> written as one word: those who work with him, his fellow workers) (j:a/seppihte) (r:zd:15259/zd:18231) (q:draft)
asepsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:make work/employ as/have serve) (d:<a> and <sepsak> written as one word: he has someone work or serve in a post; also one who works for someone) (j:a/sepsak) (r:zd:16817/zd:20358) (q:draft)
asepsep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:keep working/have been working) (d:<a> and <sepsep> written as one word: he, she or they keep on working, the work that goes on and on) (j:a/sepsep) (r:zd:11755/zd:19095) (q:draft)
asepsung = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work/politics) (w:while in office/while serving as) (d:<a>, <sep> and <sung> written as one word: during the time he or she held a post or did a work) (j:a/sep/sung) (r:zd:15095/zd:19614) (q:draft)
aseptheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:be able to do/can do/be able to work) (d:<a> and <septheih> written as one word: what one can do, that one can work; {aseptheih bangin} is as far as one is able, {na aseptheih nadingin} is so that one can work) (j:a/septheih) (r:zd:25915/zd:20912) (q:draft)
asepzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work/time) (w:since taking up work/since serving as) (d:<a>, <sep>, work, and <zawh>, here after, written as one word: since he or she began the work or the office, followed by a length of time) (j:a/sep/zawh) (r:zd:17703/zd:19215/zd:11545) (q:draft)
asepzawh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be able to do/can accomplish) (d:<a> and <sepzawh> written as one word: what he or she is able to do; {asepzawh zah} is as much as he can do) (j:a/sepzawh) (r:zd:24544) (q:draft, low confidence)
asepzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:way of working/manner of work) (d:<a> and <sepzia> written as one word: his, her or their way of doing the work) (j:a/sepzia) (r:zd:19302/zd:19631) (q:draft)
aset = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:engine/machine/machinery) (d:<a>, its, joined to <set>, machine or engine, a Burmese loan: the engine or machinery of a vehicle, aircraft or device; compare <setvan>) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:23036/zd:19054/zd:17483) (q:draft)
asetsia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:have engine trouble/break down) (d:<a> with {setsia}, from <set>, machine or engine, a Burmese loan word, and <sia>, bad, written as one word: of an aircraft or vehicle, have an engine or mechanical fault) (r:zd:16247/zd:11326) (q:draft)
Asho = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social/politics) (w:Asho/Asho Chin) (d:a Chin people living in the plains of Myanmar) (r:zd:19612) (q:draft)
asi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:die/the dead) (d:<a> and <si> written as one word: he died, or the one who died; <asi aliam> is the dead and the injured) (j:a/si) (r:zd:17794/zd:14895) (q:draft)
asi aliam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/health) (w:casualties/the dead and injured) (d:<asi>, the one who died, and <aliam>, the injured, set side by side without <leh>: the dead and the injured of an accident, a fight or a disaster taken together; in news it is often followed by <omlo>, there were no casualties) (r:zd:14895/zd:14547) (q:draft)
asia apha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:good and bad/right and wrong/pros and cons) (d:<asia>, the bad, and <apha>, the good, said as a pair: the good and the bad of something, right and wrong, or good and bad results alike; {asia apha khen} is tell good from bad) (r:zd:21219/zd:15953) (q:draft)
asiacip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be wrecked/break down/be ruined) (d:<a> and <siacip> written as one word: it is completely ruined or out of order, or the one that is wrecked, said of vehicles, machines and services) (j:a/siacip) (r:zd:19054/zd:21025/zd:15176) (q:draft)
asial = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:food) (w:raw/uncooked) (d:not cooked, said of food; {asial in ne} is eat it raw) (r:zd:12192/zd:11167/zd:11020) (q:draft)
asialam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:the bad side/the worse/evil) (d:<a> and <sialam> written as one word: the bad side of a matter; {asialam in} is in a bad sense or for the worse, against <ahoihlam>, the good side) (j:a/sialam) (r:zd:25914) (q:draft)
asialo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:undamaged/unspoiled) (d:<a> and <sialo> written as one word: what is not spoiled or ruined) (j:a/sialo) (r:zd:24532) (q:draft)
asiam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/education) (w:skilled/expert/good at) (d:<a> and <siam> written as one word: one who is skilled, or that someone is good at the thing named before it, as in {laigelh asiam}, good at writing) (j:a/siam) (r:zd:21042/zd:25919) (q:draft)
asiamkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:expert/skilled person) (d:<a>, <siam> and <khat> written as one word: one who is skilled at what is named before it) (j:a/siam/khat) (r:zd:12512/zd:23977) (q:draft)
asiamlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/education) (w:unskilled/not good at) (d:<a> and <siamlo> written as one word: the one who is not skilled, those who are not good at something) (j:a/siamlo) (r:zd:24381/zd:25919) (q:draft)
asiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/education) (w:his skill/their skill) (d:<a> and <siamna> written as one word: the skill or ability of someone; often paired as {apilna, asiamna}, his knowledge and skill) (j:a/siamna) (r:zd:16126/zd:24014) (q:draft)
asiampen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:the best/most skilled) (d:<a> and <siampen> written as one word: the most skilled one, the best) (j:a/siampen) (r:zd:21302/zd:19118) (q:draft)
asiamtawp = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:to the best of one's ability/as well as one can) (d:<a> and <siamtawp> written as one word, followed by <in>: with all the skill one has) (j:a/siamtawp) (r:zd:17213) (q:draft, low confidence)
asiamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/education) (w:experts/the skilled) (d:<a> and <siamte> written as one word: those who are skilled at something; {apil asiamte} are the learned and skilled) (j:a/siamte) (r:zd:15556/zd:15239) (q:draft)
asiamzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/education) (w:more skilled/better at) (d:<a> and <siamzaw> written as one word: one who is more skilled, or is more skilled than another named with <sang>) (j:a/siamzaw) (r:zd:17965/zd:25089) (q:draft)
Asian = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social/politics) (w:Asian) (d:a person of Asia, or belonging to Asia; {Asian te} and {Asian mite} are Asians) (o:English) (r:zd:23815/zd:24279/zd:19695) (q:draft)
asiang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:clear/clean/settled) (d:<a> and <siang> written as one word: what is clean or clear; of a matter, cleared up, made plain, as in {asiang takin}, clearly) (j:a/siang) (r:zd:12269/zd:12274) (q:draft)
asianglo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/health) (w:unclean/dirty/impure) (d:<a> and <sianglo> written as one word: what is not clean, or an unclean thing) (j:a/sianglo) (r:zd:17834/zd:11915) (q:draft)
asiangtho = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:religion/everyday) (w:holy/clean/pure) (d:<a> and <siangtho> written as one word: what is holy or clean, the one that is holy) (j:a/siangtho) (r:zd:23843/zd:21013/zd:25225) (q:draft)
asiangtholo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health/food) (w:unclean/dirty/unhygienic) (d:<a>, <siangtho> and <lo> written as one word: one that is not clean, said in the news of eating places, food and medicine) (j:a/siangtho/lo) (r:zd:20008/zd:19289) (q:draft)
asianma = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:before it is cleared up/before it is settled) (d:<a>, <sian>, be clean or clear, and <ma>, before, written as one word and followed by <in>: before a matter is cleared up or settled) (j:a/sian/ma) (r:zd:17538/zd:19095) (q:draft, low confidence)
asiansuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/work/religion) (w:clean up/clear away/purify) (d:<a> and <siansuah> written as one word: he cleans or they clean; in news reports of cleaning a house or tank and of clearing a road or a site after an accident, in religious writing of making holy) (j:a/siansuah) (r:zd:14521/zd:15928/zd:22159) (q:draft)
asiansuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:cleaning/refining/place of cleaning) (d:<a> and <siansuahna> written as one word: the cleaning of the thing named before it or the place where it is made clean; {namgimtui asiansuahna} is an oil refinery) (j:a/siansuahna) (r:zd:15575) (q:draft, low confidence)
asiansuahsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:try to clear out/try to get rid of) (d:<asiansuah>, he or they clean up, with <sawm>, intend or try, written as one word: set out to clear people away or get rid of someone) (j:asiansuah/sawm) (r:zd:14611) (q:draft)
asiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:his teacher/their teacher/coach) (d:<a>, his, her or their, and <siapa>, male teacher, written as one word: the teacher, instructor or coach of the person spoken of) (j:a/siapa) (r:zd:20289/zd:20387) (q:draft)
asiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be ruined/break down/go bad) (d:<a> and <siat> written as one word: its being ruined, spoiled or out of order; {asiat leh} is if it is ruined and {asiat ma-in} before it goes bad) (j:a/siat) (r:zd:12357/zd:12121/zd:22658) (q:draft)
asiate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:bad ones/bad things/evil things) (d:<asia>, that which is bad, with the plural <te>: the bad ones, what is evil, the opposite of <ahoihte>) (a:ahoihte) (b:asia) (r:zd:25473/zd:23554) (q:draft)
asiatgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:turn very bad/be badly damaged) (d:<a> and <siatgawp> written as one word: it has gone thoroughly bad, of weather, or is badly damaged) (j:a/siatgawp) (r:zd:20384) (q:draft)
asiatloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be ruined/not decay/not go bad) (d:<a> and <siatloh> written as one word, before <nadingin>: so that it does not decay or come to ruin) (j:a/siatloh) (r:zd:19191/zd:15606) (q:draft)
asiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:damage/breakdown/fault/bad side) (d:<a> and <siatna> written as one word: its being broken or out of order, the damage or fault of a thing; paired with <ahoihna>, the bad side of something) (j:a/siatna) (r:zd:11922/zd:25275/zd:15031) (q:draft)
asiau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/education) (w:applied/who applied) (d:<a> and <siau> written as one word: applied for something, and the one who applied) (j:a/siau) (r:zd:24296/zd:25107) (q:draft)
asiauh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/travel) (w:apply/apply for) (d:<a> and <siauh>, apply, written as one word: he applies, the one who applies, the applying) (j:a/siauh) (r:zd:17841/zd:24736) (q:draft)
asidek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:be dying/be about to die) (d:<a> and <sidek> written as one word: he or she is about to die, or before a noun the one who is dying) (j:a/sidek) (r:zd:16360/zd:11335) (q:draft)
asiding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/health) (w:about to die/going to die) (d:<a>, <si>, die, and <ding>, will, written as one word: the one who is going to die; {asiding in} is expecting him to die, or so that he will die) (j:a/si/ding) (r:zd:18110/zd:22087/zd:25616) (q:draft)
asih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:die) (d:<a> and <sih> written as one word: he or she died, his or her death, the one who died; {asih ciangin} is when he died and {asih khit ciang} is after his death) (j:a/sih) (r:zd:11283/zd:15943/zd:23639) (q:draft)
asihdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:manner of death/how he died) (d:<a> and <sihdan> written as one word: the way he or she died) (j:a/sihdan) (r:zd:12007) (q:draft)
asihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:will die/dying/death) (d:<a> and <sihding> written as one word: that he will die, his dying) (j:a/sihding) (r:zd:11124/zd:20440) (q:draft)
asihdong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:until death/to the death) (d:<a> and <sihdong> written as one word: until he or she dies or died) (j:a/sihdong) (r:zd:24250) (q:draft)
asihhun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/health) (w:time of death/hour of death) (d:<asih>, he or she died, and <hun>, time, written as one word: the time at which someone died or will die) (j:asih/hun) (r:zd:15647/zd:12061) (q:draft)
asihin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:when he died/at his death) (d:<a> and <sihin>, at dying, written as one word: at the time he or she died, at death) (j:a/sihin) (r:zd:19733) (q:draft, low confidence)
asihkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:have died/after the death of) (d:<a> and <sihkhit> written as one word; {asihkhit ciangin} is after he or she died) (j:a/sihkhit) (r:zd:13024/zd:19191) (q:draft)
asihkhitzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/family) (w:after he died/after her death) (d:<asih> and <khitzawh> written as one word: after he or she had died, after the death of the one named before it) (j:asih/khitzawh) (r:zd:19191) (q:draft)
asihlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:the fact of his death/that he had died) (d:<asih>, he or she died, and <lam>, here the fact that, written as one word: that the person has died, with verbs of knowing and noticing) (j:asih/lam) (r:zd:10842/zd:15266) (q:draft)
asihlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/health) (w:die as a result/lose one's life) (d:<a> and <sihlawh>, die because of something, written as one word: he, she or they died as a result, or the one who died as a result) (j:a/sihlawh) (r:zd:13236/zd:19127) (q:draft)
asihlawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/health) (w:death/loss of life) (d:<asihlawh>, die as a result, with the noun ending {-na}: their dying because of something, the deaths that followed) (b:asihlawh) (r:zd:14595) (q:draft)
asihloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not die/survive) (d:<a>, <sih> and <loh> written as one word: his or her not dying; {asihloh hangin} is although he or she did not die) (j:a/sih/loh) (r:zd:17952/zd:14699/zd:18005) (q:draft)
asihma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:before dying/before death) (d:<a>, <sih> and <ma> written as one word, mostly with <in>: before he or she died) (j:a/sih/ma) (r:zd:16867/zd:17083) (q:draft)
asihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:death/his death/her death) (d:<a> and <sihna>, death, written as one word: the death of the person spoken of; {asihna ahang} is the cause of death) (j:a/sihna) (r:zd:21332/zd:23404) (q:draft)
asihni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/family) (w:day of his death/the day he died) (d:<a> and <sihni> written as one word: the day on which he or she died) (j:a/sihni) (r:zd:21174/zd:12002) (q:draft)
asihpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/health) (w:his death/her death) (d:<asih> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: as for his or her death, the dying being what is spoken about) (j:asih/pen) (r:zd:17402) (q:draft)
asihsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:die leaving/die) (d:<a> and <sihsan> written as one word: he or she died leaving others behind, died) (j:a/sihsan) (r:zd:16294/zd:11532) (q:draft)
asihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:may die/can die) (d:<a> and <sihtheih> written as one word, mostly as {asihtheih nading}: so that he or she could die, such as to cause death) (j:a/sihtheih) (r:zd:11553) (q:draft)
asihzawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:after his death/since he died) (d:<a> and <sihzawh> written as one word: after he or she died; followed by a length of time, that long since the death) (j:a/sihzawh) (r:zd:11736/zd:11700) (q:draft)
asik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:step on/tread/press with the foot) (d:<a> and <sik>, step on, written as one word: he steps on something; of a brake, press it, and of a bicycle, pedal it) (j:a/sik) (r:zd:17200/ts:3369) (q:draft)
asikgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:trample/walk all over) (d:<a> and <sikgawp>, trample, written as one word: they tread all over something) (j:a/sikgawp) (r:zd:17605) (q:draft)
asikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/media) (w:already dead/have died) (d:<a> and <sikhin> written as one word: he has already died, or the one who is already dead) (j:a/sikhin) (r:zd:18046/zd:16849) (q:draft)
asikkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:step on/tread on by accident) (d:<a> and <sikkha> written as one word: he or she stepped on something without meaning to; before a noun, the one who stepped on it) (j:a/sikkha) (r:zd:20562/zd:15228) (q:draft)
asilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/everyday) (w:wear/wearing/what one wears) (d:<a> and <silh> written as one word: he or she wears, the one wearing, or the clothes one has on; {asilh leh ateen} is one's clothing) (j:a/silh) (r:zd:15537/zd:25926) (q:draft)
asilhkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:one wearing/a person dressed in) (d:<asilh> and <khat> written as one word, placed after the name of a garment: one who is wearing it; {puansan asilhkhat} is one dressed in red) (j:asilh/khat) (r:zd:17884/zd:14778) (q:draft)
asilhlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/everyday) (w:not wear/not wearing) (d:<a> and <silhlo> written as one word: he or she does not wear it; before a noun, one who is not wearing it) (j:a/silhlo) (r:zd:19667/zd:11943) (q:draft)
asilhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:wearing/what one wears) (d:<a> and <silhna> written as one word: his or her wearing of a garment, or the garment he or she has on) (j:a/silhna) (r:zd:16232/zd:12331) (q:draft)
asilhpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home/everyday) (w:the one wearing/what one wears) (d:<asilh>, wearing, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the one who is wearing it, or the thing worn, as the topic of the sentence) (j:asilh/pen) (r:zd:17983) (q:draft)
asilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:survive/not die) (d:<a>, <si> and <lo> written as one word: who did not die, the survivor of an accident or attack) (j:a/si/lo) (r:zd:17472/zd:14528) (q:draft)
asim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:read/who reads) (d:<a> and <sim>, read, written as one word: he or she reads, or before a noun the one who reads; {asim mi te} are those who read) (j:a/sim) (r:zd:22557/zd:21130/zd:11571) (q:draft)
asimding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:to study/to read) (d:<a> and <simding> written as one word: that he or she should read or study, with <lai>) (j:a/simding) (r:zd:18244) (q:draft)
asimding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:to attack/to raid) (d:<a> and <sim>, attack, and <ding> written as one word: in order to attack a place) (j:a/simding) (r:zd:15412/zd:12136) (q:draft)
asimding = (i:3) (t:v) (f:social) (w:to attend) (d:<a> and <simding> written as one word: in order to attend a feast such as a wedding) (j:a/simding) (r:zd:12021) (q:draft, low confidence)
asimkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/education) (w:happen to read/who reads) (d:<a> and <simkha> written as one word: the one who comes to read something; {asimkha te} are those who read it) (j:a/simkha) (r:zd:17332/zd:11553) (q:draft)
asimlutsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:try to sneak in/who tried to slip in) (d:<a>, <simlut>, enter secretly, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: he tries to get in secretly, or before a noun the one who tried to; found in one headline only) (j:a/simlut/sawm) (r:zd:11044) (q:draft, low confidence)
asimtham = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:secretly/in secret) (d:<a> and <simtham> written as one word, usually followed by <in>: in secret, without others knowing) (j:a/simtham) (r:zd:21603/zd:12487) (q:draft)
asin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:learn/study) (d:<a> and <sin.1> written as one word: he or she learns, the one who learns, what is learned; {asin ding} is what there is to learn) (j:a/sin) (r:zd:16313/zd:19174/zd:24381) (q:draft)
asinailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:not yet dead/still alive) (d:<asi> and <nailo> written as one word: has not died yet, or the one who has not yet died) (j:asi/nailo) (r:zd:16490/zd:17949) (q:draft)
