asuahcil = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:family/health) (w:at birth/when newly born) (d:<a> <suah> <cil> written as one word: when he or she was just born; {asuahcil akipan} is from birth) (j:a/suah/cil) (r:zd:18248/zd:13117/zd:15435) (q:draft)
asuahding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:to become/will become) (d:<a> and <suahding> written as one word: that he or she will become, to become what is named before it) (j:a/suahding) (r:zd:12715/zd:14787) (q:draft)
asuahding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:to be born/be due) (d:<a> and <suahding> written as one word, said of a baby: that is to be born, the birth that is due) (j:a/suahding) (r:zd:14776) (q:draft)
asuahdong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/health/time) (w:until she gives birth/until the birth) (d:<asuah> and <dong>, until, written as one word: until the child is born) (j:asuah/dong) (r:zd:14599/zd:12567) (q:draft)
asuahkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/everyday) (w:take off/strip off) (d:<a> and <suahkhia> written as one word: he or she takes off clothes) (j:a/suahkhia) (r:zd:19707/zd:17145) (q:draft)
asuahkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:media) (w:post/publish/release) (d:<a> and <suahkhia> written as one word: he or she makes a photo or a report public) (j:a/suahkhia) (r:zd:10929) (q:draft)
asuahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:be born/come out) (d:<a> and <suahkhiat> written as one word, before <laitak>, <khitciangin> and similar words: when or after it is born or comes out) (j:a/suahkhiat) (r:zd:13179/zd:14959) (q:draft)
asuahkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:after being born/after giving birth) (d:<a> and <suahkhit> written as one word: once he or she has been born, or once she has given birth; mostly before <ciangin>) (j:a/suahkhit) (r:zd:16093/zd:12942/zd:17899) (q:draft)
asuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/health) (w:birth/birthplace) (d:<a> and <suahna> written as one word: his or her birth, the place where a child is born) (j:a/suahna) (r:zd:21739/zd:11729/zd:16376) (q:draft)
asuahni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/family) (w:his birthday/her birthday/date of birth) (d:<a>, his or her, and <suahni> written as one word: the day on which he or she was born, or its yearly return) (j:a/suahni) (r:zd:16767/zd:15007) (q:draft)
asuahpawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/time) (w:his birthday/her birthday/birthday celebration) (d:<a>, <suah> and <pawi> written as one word: the feast of his or her birth, a birthday celebration) (j:a/suah/pawi) (r:zd:21328) (q:draft)
asuahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:publish/bring out/produce) (d:<a> and <suahsak> written as one word: he or they brought out, published or posted something, or produced it; also of bringing a child into the world) (j:a/suahsak) (r:zd:12392/zd:20796/zd:12600) (q:draft)
asuahsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:release/publication/statement) (d:<a> and <suahsakna> written as one word: what someone has put out or published, as on a website; {asuahsakna ah} is in what they published) (j:a/suahsakna) (r:zd:11438/zd:17733) (q:draft)
asuahtak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:be released/get free/escape) (d:<a> and <suahtak> written as one word: his or her getting free; {asuahtak ciangin} is when he was released) (j:a/suahtak) (r:zd:10722/zd:21929) (q:draft)
asuahtaktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to escape/be able to go free) (d:<a>, <suahtak>, escape, and <theih>, be able, written as one word; mostly in {asuahtaktheih nadingin}, so that he or they could escape or be set free) (j:a/suahtak/theih) (r:zd:15851/zd:20625) (q:draft)
asuahzawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/family) (w:after birth/since being born) (d:<a> and <suahzawh> written as one word, with <suah> in the sense of be born: after he, she or it was born; a length of time follows, as {asuahzawh ni 6}, six days after birth) (j:a/suahzawh) (r:zd:12996/zd:14642/zd:16976) (q:draft)
asuai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:draw/have drawn) (d:<a> and <suai> written as one word: who draws or has it drawn, said of a tattoo) (j:a/suai) (r:zd:12364) (q:draft, low confidence)
asuaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/education) (w:draw/paint/draw up) (d:<a> and <suaih> written as one word: he or she draws or paints, and what is drawn; also said of drawing up a budget or a project) (j:a/suaih) (r:zd:19917/zd:15933/zd:16078) (q:draft)
asuaihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/body) (w:have drawn/draw for someone) (d:<a>, <suaih>, draw, and <sak> written as one word: he or she had it drawn or drew it for someone, said of a portrait or a tattoo) (j:a/suaih/sak) (r:zd:12510/zd:12980) (q:draft)
asuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become/be born) (d:<a> and <suak> written as one word: he becomes or the one who has become something; of birth, he was born or the one born in a place) (j:a/suak) (r:zd:21690/zd:23554/zd:17672) (q:draft)
asuakcil = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family) (w:newborn/just born) (d:<a>, <suak>, be born, and <cil>, at first, written as one word, placed after the noun: {naungek asuakcil} is a newborn baby) (j:a/suak/cil) (r:zd:12014/zd:16767) (q:draft)
asuakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:be born/come out) (d:<a> and <suakkhia> written as one word: he or she is born; before a noun, the one that was born, as in {asuakkhia naungek}, the newborn baby) (j:a/suakkhia) (r:zd:15286/zd:13228) (q:draft)
asuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:publish/put out) (d:<a> and <suaksak> written as one word: they published it, put it out in a paper) (j:a/suaksak) (r:zd:12707) (q:draft)
asuaksak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:make become/cause) (d:<a> and <suaksak> written as one word: make something come to be; {aheh asuaksak} is make it angry) (j:a/suaksak) (r:zd:11627) (q:draft, low confidence)
asuakta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:survive/escape/be free) (d:<a> and <suakta> written as one word: the one who survived or got away; before a noun, free) (j:a/suakta) (r:zd:18911/zd:12166) (q:draft)
asuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/family) (w:those who become/those born) (d:<asuak> and the plural <te> written as one word: those who have become something, or those who are born) (j:asuak/te) (r:zd:16376/zd:13165) (q:draft)
asuamlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:murder/assassinate/kill) (d:<a> and <suamlum> written as one word: he or they attack and kill, the one who killed) (j:a/suamlum) (r:zd:11366/zd:16786) (q:draft)
asuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/work) (w:plant) (d:<a> and <suan>, plant, written as one word: he planted, the one who plants) (j:a/suan) (r:zd:11885/zd:16797) (q:draft)
asuan = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his descendants/their descendants) (d:<a>, his or their, and <suan>, descendant, written as one word; mostly in the pair {asuan leh khak}, their descendants) (j:a/suan) (r:zd:25273) (q:draft)
asuang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:inside/in it) (d:<a> with <suang>, inside, written as one word; {asuang ah} is inside it, said of people in a vehicle) (j:a/suang) (r:zd:11646) (q:draft, low confidence)
asuhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:snatch/rob of/take by force) (d:<a> with <suh>, take by force, and <sak>, written as one word: take a thing from a person by force, said of a purse, a phone or a car; also the one who does so) (j:a/suh/sak) (r:zd:14731/zd:14997) (q:draft)
asuhsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:try to rob/try to snatch) (d:<a> and <suhsawm> written as one word: he tried to snatch, or the one who tried to rob) (j:a/suhsawm) (r:zd:20629) (q:draft)
asuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/nature) (w:go downhill/descend) (d:<a> and <suk>, downward, written as one word: it goes down, of a road or stretch of land that slopes downhill, set against <to>, upward) (j:a/suk) (r:zd:11110) (q:draft, low confidence)
asukha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:affect/harm/that affects) (d:<a> and <sukha> written as one word: it affects or harms, or the thing that affects or harms) (j:a/sukha) (r:zd:12845/zd:12274) (q:draft)
asukham = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:blow up/set off/smash) (d:<a> and <sukham>, break to pieces, written as one word; in the articles mostly of a bomb, {Bomb asukham}, the one who set off the bomb or the bombing itself, also of breaking up a group) (j:a/sukham) (r:zd:13089/zd:24731) (q:draft)
asukhamding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:to blow up/to set off) (d:<asukham> and <ding> written as one word: the one who is to set off a bomb, or in order to blow something up) (j:asukham/ding) (r:zd:15232/zd:15828) (q:draft)
asukhampa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:bomber/one who set off the bomb) (d:<asukham>, set off, with <pa>, man, written as one word: the man who set off a bomb) (j:asukham/pa) (r:zd:12639) (q:draft)
asukkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:be affected/be harmed/be hit) (d:<a> and <sukkhak> written as one word: the ones touched or harmed by an accident, fire or disaster; {asukkhak omlo} is no one was affected) (j:a/sukkhak) (r:zd:17999/zd:19109) (q:draft)
asukkhak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:touch) (d:<a> and <sukkhak> written as one word: he or it touches something) (j:a/sukkhak) (r:zd:17854) (q:draft, low confidence)
asukkhap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:blow up/detonate/break open) (d:<a> and <sukkhap> written as one word: break a thing open by force; in news said of setting off a bomb) (j:a/sukkhap) (r:zd:14711/zd:21961) (q:draft)
asukkhapsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:plan to blow up/attempt to destroy) (d:<a>, <sukkhap>, smash, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: who planned or tried to blow up or destroy something) (j:a/sukkhap/sawm) (r:zd:14711/zd:16932) (q:draft)
asuksiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:destroy/damage) (d:<a> and <suksiat>, destroy, written as one word: that he destroyed, what they damaged, his destroying) (j:a/suksiat) (r:zd:14656/zd:22782) (q:draft)
asuksiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:destroy/damage/wreck) (d:<a> and <suksiatsak> written as one word: he or they destroy or damage something, or those who do so) (j:a/suksiatsak) (r:zd:19530/zd:19247) (q:draft)
asum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:the money/his money) (d:<a> and <sum> written as one word: the money, his, her or their money; {asum in akituat ciangin} is when it is reckoned in money) (j:a/sum) (r:zd:25919/zd:15443/zd:19863) (q:draft)
asumbawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:his purse/her purse/handbag) (d:<a> and <sumbawm> written as one word: his or her purse, wallet or handbag) (j:a/sumbawm) (r:zd:17741/zd:12261) (q:draft)
asumbei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:its cost/the expense) (d:<a> and <sumbei> written as one word: the cost of it, the money spent on it) (j:a/sumbei) (r:zd:12959/zd:12746) (q:draft)
asumin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:work) (w:in money/in value/in terms of money) (d:<asum>, its money, and <in> written as one word: counted in money, its value being) (j:asum/in) (r:zd:12817/zd:15939) (q:draft)
asumlut = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:his income/the revenue/the proceeds) (d:<a> and <sumlut> written as one word: his, her or their income, the money that comes in from something) (j:a/sumlut) (r:zd:20912/zd:19563) (q:draft)
asumneih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:the money he has/his money/his savings) (d:<a>, <sum> and <neih> written as one word: the money that he, she or they have) (j:a/sum/neih) (r:zd:18044/zd:18144) (q:draft)
asumte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:the money/his money/their money) (d:<asum>, the money, with the plural <te> written as one word: the sums of money, his or their money) (j:asum/te) (r:zd:23301/zd:21400) (q:draft)
asun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:by day/daytime) (d:<a> and <sun>, day, written as one word; {asun azan} is day and night, all the time) (j:a/sun) (r:zd:25148/zd:24948/zd:21843) (q:draft)
asun = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be injected/be vaccinated) (d:<a> written together with <sun>, pierce or inject: one who has had an injection; {vaccine asun nai lo} is one who is not yet vaccinated) (j:a/sun) (r:zd:25042) (q:draft)
asung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:its inside/inside it/the inside) (d:<a> and <sung> written as one word: the inside of the thing spoken of; {asung ah} is inside it) (j:a/sung) (r:zd:22658/zd:12337/zd:11409) (q:draft)
asunga = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in it/inside it) (d:<a> and <sunga> written as one word: that is in it, inside it; {asunga om} is what is in it) (j:a/sunga) (r:zd:19577/zd:15662) (q:draft)
asungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:inside it/in it) (d:<a>, its, and <sungah>, inside, written as one word: inside it, in the thing or place just named) (j:a/sungah) (r:zd:12733/zd:15274/zd:15602) (q:draft)
asungkua = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:its entrails/its internal organs) (d:<a> and <sungkua>, internal organs, written as one word: the entrails of a fish, an animal or a body) (j:a/sungkua) (r:zd:12561) (q:draft)
asunglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (w:inside/inner part/interior) (d:<a> and <sunglam> written as one word: its inside, the inner side or inner part of something) (j:a/sunglam) (r:zd:15059/zd:15255/zd:23016) (q:draft)
asungnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his mother-in-law) (d:<a> and <sungnu> written as one word: the mother of his wife) (j:a/sungnu) (r:zd:20540/zd:11872) (q:draft)
asungpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:from inside it/out of it) (d:<a>, its, with <sungpan>, from within, written as one word: from the inside of the thing named; {amau ii asungpan apiang} is born of themselves, their own child) (j:a/sungpan) (r:zd:12901/zd:14523) (q:draft)
asungtawng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:innermost part/heart) (d:<a> and <sungtawng> written as one word: its or their innermost part, deep inside them) (j:a/sungtawng) (r:zd:24155/zd:25628) (q:draft)
asungten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:underwear/undergarment) (d:<a> and <sungten>, underwear, written as one word: the underwear of the persons spoken of) (j:a/sungten) (r:zd:17884) (q:draft)
asunmang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:his dream/her dream/aspiration) (d:<a> and <sunmang> written as one word: his, her or their dream for the future) (j:a/sunmang) (r:zd:12769/zd:16308) (q:draft)
asuplawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:lose/forfeit) (d:<a> and <suplawh> written as one word: he or she loses something, or the loss of it, as a hand or a life) (j:a/suplawh) (r:zd:20056/zd:25572) (q:draft)
asut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:inject/be injected) (d:<a> and <sut> written as one word; in the articles said of a vaccine or other medicine: he injects, the one that is injected) (j:a/sut) (r:zd:25042) (q:draft, low confidence)
asuuk = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:worse/lower/inferior) (d:<a> and <suuk>, go down, written as one word: the one that is lower or worse, often with <zaw> or <mahmah>) (j:a/suuk) (r:zd:21509) (q:draft, low confidence)
Asylum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:asylum) (d:protection that a country gives to a person who has fled another country; {Asylum ngen} is ask for asylum) (o:English) (r:zd:24029/zd:15080) (q:draft)
at = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:cut) (d:cut with a blade. {At khia} is cut off) (q:draft)
at = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:reap/harvest) (d:cut grain at harvest; {buh at} is to reap the grain, and {at} is set against <vawh>, sow) (s:anla) (a:vawh/tuh) (q:draft)
ata = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his child/her child/their child) (d:<a>, his, her or their, and <ta>, child, written as one word) (j:a/ta) (r:zd:17945/zd:20244/zd:12402) (q:draft)
ataai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:run/run off) (d:<a> and <taai>, run, written as one word; {ataai pih} is run off with it, hurry away taking it along) (j:a/taai) (r:zd:21458) (q:draft, low confidence)
ataalkaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:drag/drag away) (d:<a> and <taalkaih> written as one word: he, she or it drags someone along) (j:a/taalkaih) (r:zd:19468) (q:draft)
ataang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:frame/joints) (d:<a>, his or her, written together with the second word of <guhletang>: in the pair {aguh ataang}, his bones and frame; in other writing {ataang in} is in place of, see <taangin>) (r:zd:16332) (q:draft, low confidence)
ataangko = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:announce/declare/proclaim) (d:<a> and <taangko>, announce, written as one word: he or they announce, or the one that is announced; mostly with <khia>) (j:a/taangko) (r:zd:23756/zd:24144) (q:draft)
ataangpi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/everyday) (w:general/common/overall) (d:of the whole or of most of a group, not of one part; {ataangpi-in} after a noun is in general, as a whole, for the most part) (r:zd:21079/zd:17860/zd:17901) (q:draft)
ataangtun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:be accomplished/come to fulfilment) (d:<a> and <taangtun>, accomplish, written as one word; {ataangtun'loh} is that it is not accomplished) (j:a/taangtun) (r:zd:16833) (q:draft, low confidence)
atai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:run/flee) (d:<a> and <tai>, run, written as one word: he runs or flees, the one who flees; of a bus, train or lorry, that runs in a place) (j:a/tai) (r:zd:16323/zd:25203) (q:draft)
ataiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:will run/will operate) (d:<a>, <tai>, run, and <ding>, will, written as one word: that is to run, said of a boat, bus or train on its route) (j:a/tai/ding) (r:zd:17822/zd:12420) (q:draft)
ataih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:hit/strike/attack) (d:<a> with <taih>, strike against or attack: that hits, the one that hit; <damiah ataih> is one who commits a robbery, or a robbery was committed) (j:a/taih) (r:zd:12113/zd:14917) (q:draft, low confidence)
ataihgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:ram/crash into/run down) (d:<ataih>, it hit, with <gawp>, violently, written as one word: of a vehicle, ram into people or cars with great force) (j:ataih/gawp) (r:zd:20225/zd:20129) (q:draft)
ataihkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:hit/crash into/collide with) (d:<a> and <taihkha> written as one word: said of a vehicle that runs into a person, a tree or another vehicle; before a noun, the one that hit) (j:a/taihkha) (r:zd:17299/zd:17104/zd:15836) (q:draft)
ataihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:hit/run into/knock down) (d:the prefix <a> with <taihkhak>, the form of <taihkha> used before a noun, <laitak> or <ciangin>: the one that a vehicle hit, or when it hit; said of a car, bus or ship running into a person or thing) (r:zd:17104/zd:11710/zd:19063) (q:draft)
ataihlaitak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:while hitting/at the moment of striking) (d:<ataih> and <laitak>, at the very time, written as one word: at the moment when something hits, or with <damiah>, while committing a robbery) (j:ataih/laitak) (r:zd:20322/zd:16400) (q:draft)
ataihlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:run over and kill/hit and kill) (d:<a> and <taihlum> written as one word: it hit and killed, said of a vehicle that runs into a person) (j:a/taihlum) (r:zd:15836) (q:draft)
ataihlumkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:ran over and killed/hit and killed) (d:<a> and <taihlumkha>, happen to run over and kill, written as one word) (j:a/taihlumkha) (r:zd:17952) (q:draft)
ataihlup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:run over and kill/hit and kill) (d:<a> with a form of <taihlum> written as one word: hit and killed, said of a vehicle or its driver) (j:a/taihlum) (r:zd:16463/zd:11368) (q:draft)
ataihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:robber/attacker) (d:<ataih> and <pa> written as one word: the man who struck; in the articles always {damiah ataihpa}, the man who committed the robbery) (j:ataih/pa) (r:zd:17661) (q:draft)
ataihpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/media) (d:<a>, <taih>, here carry out a robbery, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: after <damiah>, the one or ones who committed the robbery) (j:a/taih/pen) (r:zd:17385/zd:17661) (q:draft, low confidence)
ataihsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:try to rob/attempt to attack) (d:<ataih> and <sawm>, intend, written as one word; found after <damiah>: the one who tried to commit a robbery) (j:ataih/sawm) (r:zd:19667) (q:draft, low confidence)
ataihsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:crash into/ram/run into) (d:<a> and <taihsuk> written as one word: it ran into or crashed into something, said of vehicles) (j:a/taihsuk) (r:zd:12974/zd:14899) (q:draft)
ataihte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:those who hit/attackers/robbers) (d:<ataih> and <te> written as one word: the ones who struck; {damiah ataihte} is the people who committed the robbery) (b:ataih) (j:ataih/te) (r:zd:17647) (q:draft)
ataikawikawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:run about/run to and fro) (d:<a>, <tai> and <kawikawi> written as one word: that runs about, said of buses and boats on their routes and of people fleeing from place to place) (j:a/tai/kawikawi) (r:zd:12029/zd:18104) (q:draft)
ataikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:flee/run away/escape) (d:<a> and <taikhia> written as one word: he or they fled, or the ones who fled) (j:a/taikhia) (r:zd:15043/zd:15214/zd:15795) (q:draft)
ataikhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:run away/flee/escape) (d:<a> and <taikhiat> written as one word: his or their running away, used before words such as <ciangin> and <khitciangin>) (j:a/taikhiat) (r:zd:16389/zd:11978) (q:draft)
ataikhiatma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:before fleeing/before running away) (d:<a>, <taikhiat> and <ma> written as one word, followed by <in> or <un>: before he, she or they ran away) (j:a/taikhiat/ma) (r:zd:21057) (q:draft)
ataikhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:fleeing/running away/departure) (d:<a> and <taikhiatna> written as one word: his or their running off from a place, fleeing; of a train, its setting off) (j:a/taikhiatna) (r:zd:17419/zd:16229) (q:draft)
ataikhiatsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:try to flee/try to escape) (d:<a> and <taikhiatsawm> written as one word: he or they try to run away) (j:a/taikhiatsawm) (r:zd:21554) (q:draft)
atailai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:travel) (w:moving/running) (d:<a> and <tailai> written as one word before the name of a vehicle: that is running, a bus or train on its way) (j:a/tailai) (r:zd:12304/zd:19234) (q:draft)
atailaitak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:while running/while travelling) (d:<a>, <tai> and <laitak> written as one word: at the very time it was running, said mostly of a vehicle on its way) (j:a/tai/laitak) (r:zd:16346/zd:17239) (q:draft)
ataimang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:flee/run away/escape) (d:<a> and <taimang> written as one word: he fled, or the one who fled) (j:a/taimang) (r:zd:24297/zd:15641) (q:draft)
ataina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:course/track/route) (d:<a> and <taina> written as one word: where it runs, as {ataina lampi}, the road it runs on, and {ataina Runway}, the runway an aircraft runs along; also a place to flee to) (j:a/taina) (r:zd:16851/zd:19807/zd:21509) (q:draft)
atainading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:for it to run on/where it is to run) (d:<ataina> and <ding> written as one word: for it to run on or along, said of the road a vehicle takes and of the runway of an aircraft) (j:ataina/ding) (r:zd:15405/zd:12733) (q:draft)
ataiphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:run across/run toward/run off) (d:<a> and <taiphei> written as one word: he, she or it runs across or runs along toward a place) (j:a/taiphei) (r:zd:12468/zd:19468) (q:draft)
ataisan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:flee from/run away from/abandon) (d:<a> and <taisan> written as one word: he or they run away from or desert someone or something; before a noun, the one who fled or was deserted) (j:a/taisan) (r:zd:21667/zd:17133) (q:draft)
ataisim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:run away/flee/escape/desert) (d:<a> and <taisim>, slip away, written as one word: who has run away or is fleeing, as a prisoner, a soldier who deserts or a person who leaves home) (j:a/taisim) (r:zd:14785/zd:16325/zd:22072) (q:draft)
ataisimsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to flee/attempt to run away) (d:<a> and <taisimsawm> written as one word: he, she or it tries to run away, or the one that tried to flee) (j:a/taisimsawm) (r:zd:20767/zd:10722) (q:draft)
ataisuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:run off/flee/run on through) (d:<a> and <taisuak> written as one word: he or it runs off without stopping, as a driver after an accident, or runs right on through to a place) (j:a/taisuak) (r:zd:15836/zd:25301) (q:draft)
ataitai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:keep running/run on) (d:<a> and <taitai>, keep running, written as one word: he, she or it keeps running or fleeing; also of a car that is running) (j:a/taitai) (r:zd:18063/zd:24068) (q:draft)
ataite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:those that run/those who flee) (d:<a> and <taite> written as one word: the ones that run; of buses, those that run between two places) (j:a/taite) (r:zd:16598/zd:19127) (q:draft)
ataivalval = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:speed along/race along) (d:<atai>, it runs, and <valval>, intensely, written as one word: said of a vehicle or rider that is travelling fast) (j:atai/valval) (r:zd:12823/zd:14699) (q:draft)
atak = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:body) (w:dry/parched) (d:<tak>, dry, with the prefix <a>: after <dang>, throat, {na dang atak} is your throat is dry, you are thirsty, as in <dangtak>) (r:zd:14708/zd:22775) (q:draft)
ataklam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:body) (w:right/right side) (d:<a> and <taklam> written as one word: the right one, his or her right; {akhut ataklam} is his right hand) (j:a/taklam) (r:zd:12490/zd:12623/zd:18063) (q:draft)
atakpi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:true/real/genuine) (d:<a> and <takpi> written as one word: what is true or real, the real thing; {atakpi himawk} is it is indeed true, and {atakpi in} is in reality) (j:a/takpi) (r:zd:16630/zd:14728/zd:12913) (q:draft)
