ataksuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:it comes true/it becomes real) (d:<a> and <taksuah> written as one word: it comes true, or what makes something real) (j:a/taksuah) (r:zd:25515) (q:draft, low confidence)
ataktak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:really/actually/real/in reality) (d:<a> and <taktak> written as one word: the real thing, what is truly so; {ataktak in} is in reality, actually, and {ataktak hilo} is not real, not true) (j:a/taktak) (r:zd:21703/zd:12500/zd:22557) (q:draft)
ataktakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in fact/actually/truly) (d:<a> and <taktakin> written as one word: in fact, the truth is, at the opening of a statement) (j:a/taktakin) (r:zd:22802/zd:15274) (q:draft)
atal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:his forehead/her forehead) (d:<a> and <tal>, forehead, written as one word) (j:a/tal) (r:zd:12736/zd:12980) (q:draft)
atalbo = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:forehead/his forehead) (d:<a> with {talbo}, forehead, written as one word: his or her forehead; compare <tal> and <taltang>) (r:zd:12980) (q:draft, low confidence)
atam = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:many/much/numerous) (d:<tam>, many, with the prefix <a> written together, describing what is many rather than naming an amount; {atam zaw} is most or the greater part, {atam pen} is the most, and {atam mahmah} is very many) (r:zd:23756/zd:12161/zd:20780) (q:draft)
atamdiak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:most numerous/especially many) (d:<atam> and <diak> written as one word: more numerous than at other times or than the rest) (j:atam/diak) (r:zd:13149/zd:15454) (q:draft)
