atamluat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be too much/be too many) (d:<a> and <tamluat> written as one word before <ciangin>: when there is too much of something) (j:a/tamluat) (r:zd:17416/zd:24276) (q:draft)
atamluatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:its excess/there being too much) (d:<a> and <tamluatna> written as one word: the fact that there is too much of the thing named, mostly before <hangin>, because of) (j:a/tamluatna) (r:zd:20155/zd:16715) (q:draft)
atammahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very many/very much/very heavy) (d:<a> and <tammahmah> written as one word before or after a noun: of which there are very many, where there is very much) (j:a/tammahmah) (r:zd:19164/zd:13007) (q:draft)
atamman = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/everyday) (w:expensive/costly/high-priced) (d:<a>, <tam>, much, and <man>, price, written as one word: of high price; {atamman mahmah} is very expensive) (s:manpha) (j:a/tam/man) (r:zd:12132/zd:16408/zd:25919) (q:draft)
atamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:great number/large amount/abundance) (d:<a> and <tamna> written as one word: the great number or amount of something, how much there is of it, or the place where it is most numerous) (j:a/tamna) (r:zd:24226/zd:17649) (q:draft)
