atanu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his daughter/her daughter/their daughter) (d:<a> and <tanu> written as one word) (j:a/tanu) (r:zd:12585/zd:17709/zd:12196) (q:draft)
atanumei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his daughter/her daughter/their daughter) (d:<a> and <tanumei> written as one word) (j:a/tanumei) (r:zd:14597/zd:19644) (q:draft)
atapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his son/her son/their son) (d:<a> and <tapa> written as one word: his, her or their son) (j:a/tapa) (r:zd:11373/zd:16073/zd:19063) (q:draft)
atat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:keep writing/write regularly) (d:<at>, write, doubled and written as one word, mostly with <lai>: write again and again, go on writing) (b:at) (r:zd:21529/zd:16254) (q:draft, low confidence)
atate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:his children/her children/their children) (d:<a> and <tate> written as one word: the children of the person spoken about) (j:a/tate) (r:zd:17936/zd:14954/zd:19571) (q:draft)
