athatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:the one to kill/the supposed killer) (d:<a> and <thatding> written as one word: the one who is to kill, or who is thought to have killed; {athatding in aki ummawh} is suspected of being the killer) (j:a/thatding) (r:zd:13032) (q:draft)
athatlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:kill/he killed) (d:<a> and <thatlum> written as one word: he killed, the one who killed) (j:a/thatlum) (r:zd:15004/zd:17357) (q:draft)
athatlumpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/everyday) (w:killer/the man who killed) (d:<athatlum> and <pa>, man, written as one word: the man who killed the person or animal named before it) (j:athatlum/pa) (r:zd:15004/zd:19439) (q:draft)
athatpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:killer/murderer) (d:<athat> and <pa> written as one word: the man who killed, the killer) (j:athat/pa) (r:zd:11364/zd:23437) (q:draft)
athatte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:killers/those who killed) (d:<athat>, the one who killed, with the plural <te>, written as one word: the persons who killed someone) (b:athat) (j:athat/te) (r:zd:20239) (q:draft)
athau = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:gun/his gun) (d:<thau>, gun, written together with <a>, his or their: the gun someone carries; the words around it show this, as <thautawipa>, gunman, <laksak>, take away, and <kap>, shoot, not the fat of the first sense) (b:thau) (r:zd:11932/zd:14585/zd:18030) (q:draft)
athau = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:body) (w:fat) (d:<thau>, be fat, with <a> before it: the fat one, said of people and paired with <agol>, the big one) (b:thau) (r:zd:19021) (q:draft, low confidence)
athaulua = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:body/health/food) (w:too fat/very fat/fatty) (d:<a> and <thaulua> written as one word: one that is very fat, also of food that is too fatty) (j:a/thaulua) (r:zd:25932/zd:11269) (q:draft)
athaupuak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:the gun he carries/his gun) (d:<a>, his or her, with {thau puak}, gun carried, written as one word: the gun a person has on him) (r:zd:19667) (q:draft)
athautawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:the gun he carried/his weapon in hand) (d:<a>, <thau>, gun, and <tawi>, hold, written as one word: the gun that the person was holding) (j:a/thau/tawi) (r:zd:17750) (q:draft)
athauvallua = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:body/health) (w:overweight/obese/too fat) (d:<athau>, the fat one, and <vallua>, excessive, written as one word: those who are too fat) (j:athau/vallua) (r:zd:16259/zd:11269) (q:draft)
athauzat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:the gun he used/gun used) (d:<athau>, his gun, and <zat>, use, written as one word: the gun that someone used in a shooting) (j:athau/zat) (r:zd:20531/zd:19478) (q:draft)
athawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:he rises/he gets up) (d:<a> and <thawh> written as one word: he or she gets up, his rising; {athawh ciangin} is when he got up) (j:a/thawh) (r:zd:15756/zd:22683/zd:23943) (q:draft)
athawhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (w:he rises again/he gets up again) (d:<a> and <thawhkik> written as one word: he gets up again, he rises from death) (j:a/thawhkik) (r:zd:12214) (q:draft)
athawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/everyday) (w:the bottle/its bottle) (d:<a> and <thawl>, bottle, written as one word: the bottle of a drink or other liquid; {athawl tawh zuak} is sell by the bottle) (j:a/thawl) (r:zd:21067/zd:25479) (q:draft, low confidence)
athei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:know/the one who knows) (d:<a> and <thei> written as one word: the one who knows, those who know; {athei nailo te} is those who do not yet know) (j:a/thei) (r:zd:19676/zd:20440/zd:21262) (q:draft)
atheician = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:one who knows well/one who knows for certain) (d:<a>, <thei>, know, and <cian>, clearly, written as one word: the one who knows a matter well or exactly; with <te> those who know) (j:a/thei/cian) (r:zd:17353/zd:16919) (q:draft)
atheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:know/come to know) (d:<a> and <theih>, know, written as one word: {atheih ciangin} is when he or she learned of it, and {atheih huai thu} is a thing worth knowing) (j:a/theih) (r:zd:14622/zd:25042) (q:draft)
atheihcian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:know clearly/know for certain/understand) (d:<a> and <theihcian> written as one word: he, she or they know it clearly; {atheihcian nadingin} is so that they may know it well) (j:a/theihcian) (r:zd:20764/zd:12959) (q:draft)
atheihciang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:when he found out/on learning) (d:<atheih>, he or she knows, and <ciang>, when, written as one word: when he or she came to know of it) (j:atheih/ciang) (r:zd:14613) (q:draft)
atheihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:to know/should know) (d:<a> and <theihding> written as one word: that he, she or they should know, so that they may know) (j:a/theihding) (r:zd:20008/zd:11440) (q:draft)
atheihhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:media/everyday) (w:worth knowing/good to know) (d:<a> and <theihhuai> written as one word: that which is worth knowing, common in headlines) (j:a/theihhuai) (r:zd:26208/zd:13078) (q:draft)
atheihkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:came to know/found out) (d:<a> and <theihkhak>, come to know, written as one word: he, she or they came to know of it) (j:a/theihkhak) (r:zd:20193/zd:15922) (q:draft)
atheihkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:found out/discovered) (d:<a> and <theihkhiat> written as one word: he, she or they found out, what was found out) (j:a/theihkhiat) (r:zd:14738/zd:12841/zd:16932) (q:draft)
atheihloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not know/be unaware) (d:<a>, <theih> and <loh> written as one word: that he does not know, what is not known; {atheihloh kaalin} is while one is unaware) (j:a/theih/loh) (r:zd:20193/zd:16803) (q:draft)
atheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:knowledge/knowing) (d:<a> and <theihna> written as one word: his or their knowledge, what he knows; {atheihna ding} is so that they may know) (j:a/theihna) (r:zd:22159/zd:20999) (q:draft)
atheihnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to know/wish to know) (d:<a> and <theihnop> written as one word: that he, she or they want to know; {atheihnop dotna} is a question they want answered) (j:a/theihnop) (r:zd:12636) (q:draft)
atheihphet = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:as soon as he knew/the moment they learned) (d:<atheih>, he knows, with <phet>, as soon as, written as one word and followed by <in> or <un>: the moment he or they came to know of it) (j:atheih/phet) (r:zd:15684/zd:16966) (q:draft)
atheihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:witness/acknowledge/know of) (d:<a> and <theihpih>, know together with, written as one word: he or she knows of and acknowledges a matter, the one who is witness to it) (j:a/theihpih) (r:zd:26097/zd:16809) (q:draft)
atheihsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:already know/know already) (d:<a> and <theihsa> written as one word: what he or they already know, already known to them) (j:a/theihsa) (r:zd:24236/zd:13218) (q:draft)
atheikha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:one who knows/witness) (d:<a> and <theikha> written as one word: one who happens to know of it, anyone who knows) (j:a/theikha) (r:zd:12669/zd:18161) (q:draft)
atheikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:already know/the one who already knows) (d:<a> and <theikhin> written as one word: he or they already know, or the one who already knows) (j:a/theikhin) (r:zd:25919/zd:10687) (q:draft)
atheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not know/be unaware) (d:<a>, <thei>, know, and <lo>, not, written as one word: does not know, or one who does not know) (j:a/thei/lo) (r:zd:20970/zd:11206/zd:11548) (q:draft)
atheilote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who do not know) (d:<atheilo>, one who does not know, with the plural <te>: the people who do not know something) (b:atheilo) (r:zd:24381/zd:22964) (q:draft)
atheinuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:want to know/wish to know) (d:<a> and <theinuam> written as one word: the one who wants to know; {atheinuam te} is those who want to know) (j:a/theinuam) (r:zd:16383/zd:16216) (q:draft)
atheipeuh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:whoever knows/anyone who knows) (d:<athei>, the one who knows, with <peuh>, any, written as one word: anyone at all who knows) (j:athei/peuh) (r:zd:18129/zd:12598) (q:draft)
atheite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:those who know) (d:<athei>, the one who knows, with the plural <te>, written as one word: those who know about a matter, mostly as {atheite'n}, asked to tell or write what they know) (j:athei/te) (r:zd:13341/zd:22728) (q:draft)
athem = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:piece/fragment/bit) (d:<a> and <them> written as one word: its pieces, the small broken bits of something) (j:a/them) (r:zd:17713/zd:17591) (q:draft)
athemnen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:debris/small fragments/splinters) (d:<athem>, its pieces, and <nen>, small or fine, written as one word: the small broken bits of something that has been smashed or blown up) (j:athem/nen) (r:zd:20668/zd:15253) (q:draft)
athemneng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:fragments/debris/wreckage/scraps) (d:<a>, <them> and <neng> written as one word: the small broken pieces of something, as the wreckage of an aeroplane or the splinters of a blast) (j:a/them/neng) (r:zd:12888/zd:11588/zd:17164) (q:draft)
Athens = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (j:Athen) (r:zd:22650) (q:draft)
atho = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:he rises/the risen) (d:<a> and <tho> written as one word: he rises, he gets up, the one who has risen) (j:a/tho) (r:zd:12166/zd:23943) (q:draft)
athoh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:withdraw/issue/take out) (d:<a> with <thoh>, a Burmese loan, take out or issue: withdraw money from a bank, or issue an order, a warrant or a curfew) (j:a/thoh) (r:zd:12437/zd:24947/zd:25068) (q:draft, low confidence)
athong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:his prison term/her prison term) (d:<a> and <thong>, prison, written as one word: the prison sentence of the one spoken of, as in {athong kiatding}, the term he is to serve) (j:a/thong) (r:zd:16666) (q:draft, low confidence)
athongkiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:be imprisoned/serve a prison term) (d:<a> and <thongkiat> written as one word: his or her being in prison; {athongkiat zahding} is the length of the prison term) (j:a/thongkiat) (r:zd:19906) (q:draft)
athongkiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:be imprisoned/serve a prison term) (d:<a>, <thongkiat> and <ding> written as one word: that he or she is to be in prison; {athongkiatding akum} is the years to be served) (j:a/thongkiat/ding) (r:zd:17526) (q:draft)
athu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:the matter/the facts) (d:<a> and <thu> written as one word: the matter in question, its facts or content) (j:a/thu) (r:zd:21251/zd:21357/zd:20579) (q:draft)
athu akician = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:the exact facts/the details/the particulars) (d:<athu>, the matter, and <akician>, exact: the exact facts or full details of a matter; mostly followed by <in>, {athu akician in}, in detail, exactly, before a verb of telling, announcing or finding out) (r:zd:20717/zd:12874/zd:19635) (q:draft)
athu ala = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:the details/the facts of the matter/the particulars) (d:<athu>, the matter, and {a la}, its song, written as one word and not the exclamation: the pair {thu leh la}, word and song, means the whole of a matter, so {athu ala} is all the details of what happened; in news reports the object of <kancian>, investigate) (r:zd:15019/zd:19745) (q:draft)
athuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:wear/put on) (d:<a> and <thuah>, put on over or in addition, written as one word: he wears or the one wearing, said of a mask and other things put on the body) (j:a/thuah) (r:zd:24333/zd:24219/zd:17661) (q:draft)
athuah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do together/add) (d:<a> and <thuah>, in addition, written as one word: do one thing along with another, add one thing to another) (j:a/thuah) (r:zd:24750) (q:draft, low confidence)
athuahdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:way of wearing/way of fitting) (d:<athuah> and <dan> written as one word: how a thing is put on or fitted, the way of wearing or installing it) (j:athuah/dan) (r:zd:12068/zd:14985) (q:draft)
athuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:suffer/undergo/endure) (d:<a> and <thuak> written as one word: who suffers or bears something; after a verb form it names the person to whom the thing was done, as <mat athuak>, the one arrested, and {zuak athuak}, the one who was sold) (j:a/thuak) (r:zd:22556/zd:18009) (q:draft)
athuakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:will suffer/will undergo) (d:<a>, <thuak>, undergo, and <ding>, will, written as one word: that he or she will undergo, the punishment or trial that awaits someone) (j:a/thuak/ding) (r:zd:12085/zd:12817/zd:16131) (q:draft)
athuakkha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:victim/the one affected) (d:<a> and <thuakkha> written as one word: the one who has suffered something, a victim; with <te>, the victims) (j:a/thuakkha) (r:zd:11360/zd:15469/zd:11837) (q:draft)
athuaklah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:suffer badly/be hard hit/find hard to bear) (d:<a> and <thuaklah> written as one word: who suffers much from something, or what is hard to bear) (j:a/thuaklah) (r:zd:15067/zd:14519) (q:draft)
athuaklawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:suffer/incur/bear the brunt) (d:<a> and <thuaklawh> written as one word: he or they had to suffer it, the one who was hit by the harm) (j:a/thuaklawh) (r:zd:18042/zd:26124/zd:15301) (q:draft)
athuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:suffering/what one suffers/experience) (d:<a> and <thuakna> written as one word: what he or they suffer or go through, the suffering borne) (j:a/thuakna) (r:zd:12487/zd:21426) (q:draft)
athuakngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have suffered/have undergone) (d:<athuak> and <ngei> written as one word: who has at some time suffered or undergone something) (j:athuak/ngei) (r:zd:17252/zd:24604) (q:draft)
athuaknu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:female victim/the woman who suffered it) (d:<a>, <thuak>, suffer, and <nu>, woman, written as one word: the woman to whom the thing named before it was done) (j:a/thuak/nu) (r:zd:12429/zd:11990) (q:draft)
athuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:victim/the one who suffered) (d:<a> and <thuakpa> written as one word, placed after the word for what was done: the man to whom it was done, as in {mat athuakpa}, the man who was arrested) (j:a/thuakpa) (r:zd:21030/zd:19868/zd:20492) (q:draft)
athuakpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/media) (w:the victim/the one who suffered) (d:<a>, <thuak>, undergo, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, placed after the word for what was done: the one to whom it was done, as the topic of the sentence) (j:a/thuak/pen) (r:zd:12598/zd:19213) (q:draft)
athuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:made suffer/inflicted/imposed) (d:<a> and <thuaksak> written as one word: made someone undergo something, such as a punishment named before it) (j:a/thuaksak) (r:zd:19318/zd:11598) (q:draft)
athuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:victims/those who suffer/sufferers) (d:<a> and <thuakte> written as one word, placed after what was suffered: those who underwent it, as in {kapliam athuakte}, those wounded by shooting, and {hih natna athuakte}, those who have this disease) (j:a/thuakte) (r:zd:24014/zd:15000) (q:draft)
athuakzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:after suffering/after undergoing) (d:<a> and <thuak>, suffer, with <zawh>, after, written as one word: after he or she has suffered it, often followed by a length of time) (j:a/thuak/zawh) (r:zd:18020) (q:draft)
athuakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:endure/be able to bear) (d:<a> and <thuakzo> written as one word: he or she endures, the one who is able to bear it) (j:a/thuakzo) (r:zd:26026/zd:19427) (q:draft)
athugen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:what he says/his speech/his words) (d:<a>, his or her, and <thugen>, written as one word: what a person says or said, a speech or sermon; {athugen ding} is what he is going to speak about) (j:a/thugen) (r:zd:22550/zd:17305) (q:draft)
athugenna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:his speech/his address/what he said) (d:<a>, his or her, and <thugenna>, speech, written as one word) (j:a/thugenna) (r:zd:19302/zd:15933) (q:draft)
athugente = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:his words/what he said) (d:<a>, <thugen> and the plural <te> written as one word: the things that he said) (j:a/thugen/te) (r:zd:20673/zd:25342) (q:draft)
athuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:sign/he signs) (d:<a> and <thuh>, sign, written as one word: he or she signs, as in {min athuh}, signs his name) (j:a/thuh) (r:zd:22922) (q:draft, low confidence)
athuhilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/religion) (w:teach/preach/instruct) (d:<a> and <thuhilh> written as one word: he teaches or preaches, what he teaches; also said of correcting children) (j:a/thuhilh) (r:zd:17883/zd:22778) (q:draft)
athuk = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/nature) (w:deep) (d:<a> and <thuk>, deep, written as one word: deep, that is deep; after a measure it says how deep, as {pi 20 athuk}, twenty feet deep) (j:a/thuk) (r:zd:12355/zd:12450/zd:17673) (q:draft)
athuk = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:food) (w:sour) (d:<a> and <thuk>, sour, written as one word: sour, that which is sour) (j:a/thuk) (r:zd:22775) (q:draft, low confidence)
athukhual = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:considerate/civilised/thoughtful) (d:<a> and <thukhual> written as one word: one who has regard for others, considerate and well-mannered) (j:a/thukhual) (r:zd:23761) (q:draft)
athukhun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:rule/regulation/law) (d:<a> and <thukhun>, rule, written as one word: its or their rules) (j:a/thukhun) (r:zd:24481/zd:19318) (q:draft)
athukim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:agree/one who agrees) (d:<a> and <thukim> written as one word: he or they agree, or those who agree) (j:a/thukim) (r:zd:21050/zd:23982/zd:17291) (q:draft)
athukimlo = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:those who disagree/those against) (d:<a> and <thukimlo> written as one word: the one or ones who do not agree, the votes against) (j:a/thukimlo) (r:zd:19949/zd:24390) (q:draft)
athukkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:retaliate/pay back/respond) (d:<a> and <thukkik> written as one word: he or she pays back or does something in return) (j:a/thukkik) (r:zd:15606) (q:draft, low confidence)
athukna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/everyday) (w:depth/deep part/the deep) (d:<a> and <thukna>, depth, written as one word: its depth, the deep part; before a measure it says how deep, as {athukna Pi 14}, at a depth of 14 feet) (j:a/thukna) (r:zd:22557/zd:22821) (q:draft)
athuksuk = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/nature) (w:deep/deep down) (d:<athuk>, deep, with <suk>, downward, written as one word: after a measure it says how far down a drop or a pit goes) (j:athuk/suk) (r:zd:19277) (q:draft)
athulu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/education) (w:its title/the title/the topic) (d:<a> and <thulu> written as one word: the title or topic of a writing or talk) (j:a/thulu) (r:zd:17305/zd:15874) (q:draft)
athum = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:the three/all three/third) (d:<a> and <thum>, three, written as one word: {athum un} is all three of them, {athum veina} is the third time) (j:a/thum) (r:zd:12311/zd:25351) (q:draft)
