baihmahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very easy) (d:<baih>, easy, and <mahmah>, very, written as one word) (j:baih/mahmah) (r:zd:16317/zd:12752) (q:draft)
baihno = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:easy) (d:<baih>, easy, with a second syllable as in <olno>; found as {baihno takin}, easily, and paired as {olno tak leh baihno takin}, easily and without effort) (s:olno) (a:haksa) (b:baih) (r:zd:16779/zd:20560) (q:draft)
baihpak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:easy/quick and easy) (d:<baih>, easy, with <pak>, quickly, written as one word: easily and soon done, mostly denied, as in {baihpak hetlo}, not easy at all) (j:baih/pak) (r:zd:14601/zd:24165) (q:draft, low confidence)
baihpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:easiest) (d:<baih>, easy, with <pen>, most, written as one word: the easiest; {a baihpen} is the easiest one or the easiest way) (j:baih/pen) (r:zd:25919/zd:21083) (q:draft)
baihsa = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find easy/think easy) (d:<baih>, easy, with <sa>, feel or consider, placed after a verb: find the action easy to do; without the <a> and <in> of {a baihsa-in}, in readiness) (r:zd:8668/zd:25115/zd:16385) (q:draft)
baihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:make easy/make likely/bring on easily) (d:<baih>, easy, with <sak>, cause: make a thing easy or quick to happen; with <lo>, not treat a thing as easy, not do it lightly) (j:baih/sak) (r:zd:20761/zd:21168) (q:draft)
baihtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:easily/readily/without difficulty) (d:<baih> and <tak> written as one word, mostly as {baihtak in}: easily, without trouble or delay) (j:baih/tak) (r:zd:24047/zd:21259/zd:23655) (q:draft)
baihtuak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:easy/simple) (d:<baih>, easy, with <tuak>: easy to do or to live with; mostly used with a negative, not easy) (j:baih/tuak) (r:zd:11360/zd:12389) (q:draft)
baihtuam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:easier/all the easier) (d:<baih.2>, easy, and <tuam.3>, all the more, written as one word: become easier as a result) (j:baih/tuam) (r:zd:17304/zd:20477) (q:draft)
bail = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:bail) (d:money or a pledge on which an arrested person is set free until the trial; {bail tawh khahkhia} is release on bail) (o:English) (r:zd:15499/zd:13209/zd:12546) (q:draft)
bailawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:suffer hardship/suffer loss) (d:said together with <suplawh>, lose, as {suplawh bailawh}: bear trouble or loss as a result of what one does) (r:zd:25015/zd:21845) (q:draft, low confidence)
baina = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:loss/damage/harm) (d:paired with <supna>, loss, as {supna baina} or {ih sup ih baina}: the loss and damage that comes from war, quarrels or a decision, with no thought of bodily laming) (r:zd:20454/zd:16404/zd:21080) (q:draft)
bakbak = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:hastily/abruptly/rashly) (d:of a sudden, unrestrained reaction rather than of eating: {lung tom bakbak} is quick-tempered, and after a verb of answering or anger it means bursting out without thinking) (r:zd:24313/zd:23489) (q:draft, low confidence)
bal = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (w:taro/yam) (d:a root crop with an edible tuber, listed with maize, potato and beans as field food; a noun, not the verb {bal} tear) (r:zd:24176/ts:3375) (q:draft)
Balai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:police station) (d:Malay word for a hall or station, used by Zomi in Malaysia for a police station, in full {Balai Polis}, usually with the name of the place) (o:Malay) (r:zd:23629) (q:draft, low confidence)
Balakong = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Balakong) (d:a township in Selangor, Malaysia, near Kajang, where Zomi live and work) (r:zd:14692) (q:draft)
Balam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (j:Balaam) (r:zd:16488) (q:draft)
balance = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:balance) (d:a state in which things are of equal weight or in the right proportion; also used as a verb, be or keep in balance) (o:English) (r:zd:23780) (q:draft, low confidence)
Balcony = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:balcony) (d:a platform with a railing on the outside of an upper floor of a building) (o:English) (r:zd:12240/zd:16673) (q:draft)
Bali = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Bali) (d:island of Indonesia) (r:zd:15382/zd:20369) (q:draft)
Balloon = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:balloon) (d:a balloon, the toy or the large one that carries people through the air) (o:English) (r:zd:15592/zd:17664) (q:draft, low confidence)
Baltimore = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Baltimore) (d:city in the state of Maryland in the United States) (r:zd:11899) (q:draft)
Bamar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/social) (w:Bamar/Burman) (d:the majority people of Myanmar, in Zolai also called {Kawl}) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:20348) (q:draft)
Bamaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Bhamo) (d:town in Kachin State, Myanmar, on the Irrawaddy river) (r:ts:12506/ts:8689) (q:draft)
banban = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:one after another/in turn/in order/successively) (d:usually as {a banban in}: one after the other, each in its turn) (r:zd:23129/ts:6835/zd:23394) (q:draft)
Band = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:band/music group) (d:a group of musicians who play together) (o:English) (r:zd:16337/zd:21550) (q:draft)
Bandage = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:bandage) (d:a strip of cloth wrapped round a wound; {Bandage tawh kituam} is be wrapped in a bandage) (o:English) (r:zd:11938/zd:12364) (q:draft)
Bandung = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Bandung) (d:city in West Java, Indonesia) (r:zd:16702/zd:17450) (q:draft)
bang = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:what) (d:Question word, what; it also begins the phrases {bang hangin}, why, and {bang ci}, how.) (r:44.21.22)
bang = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:about/approximately/or so) (d:placed after a number or an amount, often after <val>, to show that it is not exact: {100 val bang} is something over 100) (r:ts:3284/ts:1428/ts:479) (q:draft)
bang ahia = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what is it/what is) (d:<bang>, what, and <ahia>, the sentence-final question word: closes a question that asks what the thing named before it is or means; after a quoted word with <cih> or <acih> it asks what that word means) (r:zd:24068/zd:16777/zd:16897) (q:draft)
bang hang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:why) (d:asks the reason, often as {bang hang hiam}) (r:zai:why) (q:draft)
bang hanga = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why/for what reason) (d:<bang>, what, and <hanga>, because of: opens a question about the reason, which usually ends in <hiam>; also the reason why, before a clause closed by <cih>) (s:banghangin/bang hang) (r:zd:16210/zd:9448) (q:draft)
bang phading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:about/approximately/an estimated) (d:<bang>, here about or as much as and not the question word what, and <phading>, will come to: placed after a number or a measure when the amount is an estimate, it comes to about so many; <cihi> or {kici hi}, it is said, often follows) (r:zd:12519/zd:12307) (q:draft)
bangaa = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like/as/according to) (d:<bang>, like, and the linking <aa>, written as one word after a noun or clause: in the way of, of the kind of; {tua bangaa} is such, in that way) (j:bang/aa) (r:zd:21796/zd:19683/zd:21869) (q:draft)
bangah = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in for example/in such as) (d:after the name of a place or thing and not after a number: in that one taken as an example, as {America bangah}, in America for instance; <bang>, like, with the place marker <ah>) (r:zd:19775/zd:21848/zd:23603) (q:draft)
Bangalore = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Bangalore/Bengaluru) (d:city in the state of Karnataka in southern India, where many Zomi study theology) (r:zd:10812/zd:15803) (q:draft)
bangbang hileh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:anyway/in any case/whatever the case) (d:<bangbang>, whatever, and <hileh>, if it is: whatever it may be; stands at the head of a sentence and sets aside what was said before, in any case, anyway) (r:zd:23037/zd:22784) (q:draft)
bangbanga = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:just as/according to/however) (d:<bangbang>, just as, with the linking ending <a> before a verb: in whatever way; {ut bangbanga} is just as one pleases) (b:bangbang) (r:zd:9429/zd:9434) (q:draft)
bangbangah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in whatever/in anything) (d:<bangbang>, whatever, with the marker <ah> written as one word: in whatever it may be) (j:bangbang/ah) (r:zd:24253/zd:24804) (q:draft)
bangbawl = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:do what/make what) (d:<bang> and <bawl> written as one word: do what, what to do, mostly in a question or beside <bangsem>) (j:bang/bawl) (r:zd:24593) (q:draft)
bangbek = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only about/just about/no more than) (d:after a number or an amount, <bang> in its meaning about, with <bek>, only: only about that many and no more, as in {mi 2 bangbek}, only about two people) (r:zd:21388/zd:17694/zd:11548) (q:draft)
bangci = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how) (d:Question word, how, in what way; also with the ending <in>, {bangci-in}.) (s:koici)
bangci = (i:3) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:what kind of/what sort of) (d:before a noun, asking about its nature and not about a way of doing: {bangci mi}, what kind of person; before a verb the word means how) (r:zd:22487) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangci bangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way/by what means) (d:<bangci>, how, and <bangin>, in the manner of: a fuller form of the question word how, asking for the way or the means; it opens a direct question or stands before the verb of an indirect one that ends in <cih>) (s:bangci) (r:zd:25711/zd:13171/zd:15243) (q:draft)
bangcia = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why) for what reason or purpose
bangciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how far/to what extent/how much) (d:<bang> and <ciang> written as one word, a question word: up to what point, how far, to what extent) (j:bang/ciang) (r:zd:16442/zd:21456) (q:draft)
bangciangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:by about/at around/after about) (d:<bang>, about, and <ciangin>, when, written as one word after a time or an amount: when it comes to about that, by around that time) (j:bang/ciangin) (r:zd:24049/zd:21869) (q:draft)
bangcibang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way/what kind of) (d:<bangci> and <bang> written as one word: how, in what way, of what kind; often {bangcibang in}) (j:bangci/bang) (r:zd:12567/zd:18183/zd:11148) (q:draft)
bangcibangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way) (d:<bangci>, how, and <bangin>, like, written as one word: in what way, by what means) (j:bangci/bangin) (r:zd:21135/zd:10793) (q:draft)
bangciciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how far/to what extent/to what outcome) (d:<bangci>, how, and <ciang>, as far as, written as one word: a question about how far a matter has gone or how it will turn out) (j:bangci/ciang) (r:zd:15425/zd:16580/zd:11551) (q:draft)
bangcidan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way/what kind of) (d:<bangci>, how, and <dan>, manner, written as one word: in what manner; before a noun, what kind of) (j:bangci/dan) (r:zd:19111/zd:15541/zd:16216) (q:draft)
bangcihding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what to do/how to do) (d:<bangcih>, how, and <ding> written as one word: what is to be done, how one should act) (j:bangcih/ding) (r:zd:18110/zd:11729/zd:12217) (q:draft)
bangcihiam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:how is it) (d:<bangci>, how, and the question particle <hiam> written as one word: how is it, how is someone or something doing) (j:bangci/hiam) (r:zd:17818/zd:12992) (q:draft)
bangcileng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/by doing what) (d:<bangci>, how, and <leng>, if, written as one word in a question: by doing what, how can it be) (j:bangci/leng) (r:zd:21502/zd:12264) (q:draft)
bangcimuh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:how one sees/what view) (d:<bangci>, how, and <muh>, see, written as one word: how someone sees or regards a person or thing) (j:bangci/muh) (r:zd:11256/zd:11074) (q:draft)
bangdan = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:like/as/in the manner of) (d:<bang>, like, and <dan>, manner, written as one word after a noun or a clause and mostly followed by <in>: in the way of, like; {tua bangdan} is that kind of thing) (j:bang/dan) (r:zd:11642/zd:18893/zd:22116) (q:draft)
bangdan = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way) (d:question word, <bang>, what, and <dan>, manner, written as one word and mostly followed by <in>: in what way) (s:bangci) (j:bang/dan) (r:zd:22643/zd:15727) (q:draft)
bangdang = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:anything else/something else/any other) (d:<bang>, what, and <dang>, other, written as one word: anything else; with a negative, nothing else, no other) (j:bang/dang) (r:zd:21989/zd:12074) (q:draft)
bangdanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like/as/in the manner of) (d:<bang>, like, and <danin>, in the way, written as one word after a noun: in the same way as, as if it were) (j:bang/danin) (r:zd:12240/zd:19355/zd:19902) (q:draft)
bangdanin = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:how/in what way) (d:<bang>, what, and <danin>, in the way, written as one word in a question: in what way, how) (j:bang/danin) (r:zd:19579) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangdankhat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as if/in the manner of) (d:<bang>, like, and <dankhat>, a kind of, written as one word, followed by <in>: as if it were so, in a way that looks like the thing named) (j:bang/dankhat) (r:zd:11587/zd:13278) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangdanlian = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:just like/exactly as) (d:<bangdan>, like, with <lian> used as an emphatic word, exactly, written as one word after a noun and followed by <in>: in just the manner of, exactly as) (j:bangdan/lian) (r:zd:16130/zd:19962) (q:draft)
bangdante = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:such ones/the likes of/things like) (d:<bangdan>, like, with the plural <te>: those of that kind, people or things like the one named before) (b:bangdan) (r:zd:23089) (q:draft)
bangdia = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why/what for) (d:question word, why, for what purpose; <bang>, what, with {ding a}, shortened and written as one word) (r:zd:16037/zd:23773) (q:draft)
bangding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why/what for) (d:<bang>, what, and <ding> written as one word, mostly followed by <in> or <a>: for what purpose, why; the same spelling also stands for {bang ding}, will be like) (j:bang/ding) (r:zd:24058/zd:17437) (q:draft)
bangh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (j:bang) (r:zd:23860/zd:15600) (q:draft)
banghang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (j:bang hang) (r:zd:24028/zd:13217/zd:23943) (q:draft)
banghanga = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why) (d:<bang>, what, and <hanga>, because of, written as one word: why, for what reason) (j:bang/hanga) (r:zd:15377/zd:22646) (q:draft)
banghanghiam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why) (d:<bang hang> and <hiam> written as one word: why; {banghanghiam cih leh}, literally if one asks why, means because) (j:bang hang/hiam) (r:zd:21011/zd:20892) (q:draft)
banghanghiam cih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the reason why/because/why it is so) (d:<banghanghiam>, why is it, and <cih>, saying: the question why as a thing that is known, asked or examined; followed by <leh> as {banghanghiam cih leh}, literally if one asks why, it opens a sentence that gives the reason, and means because or the reason is that) (r:zd:20892/zd:16728) (q:draft)
banghanghiamcihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/for) (d:{bang hang hiam cih leh} written as one word, literally if one asks why: begins a sentence that gives the reason for what was just said) (j:bang/hang/hiam/cih/leh) (r:zd:21989/zd:20871) (q:draft)
banghangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why/for what reason) (d:<bang>, what, and <hangin>, because of, written as one word: why, usually with <hiam> at the end of the question; also written <bang hang>) (j:bang/hangin) (r:zd:16438/zd:11548) (q:draft)
banghi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what is) (d:<bang>, what, and <hi>, is, written as one word: what is it, is what) (j:bang/hi) (r:zd:15926/zd:16337) (q:draft)
banghiam = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:what is it/what) (d:<bang>, what, and the question particle <hiam> written as one word: what is it, often after <acih> or {i cih} to ask what a thing means) (j:bang/hiam) (r:zd:21633/zd:22451) (q:draft)
banghih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:do what/what is being done) (d:<bang>, what, and <hih>, do, written as one word in a question: {banghih nahiam} is what are you doing) (j:bang/hih) (r:zd:19631/zd:12085) (q:draft)
banghileh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:in the case of/for instance in) (d:<bang>, like, and <hileh>, if it is, written as one word after the name of a place: if it is a place like that one, there for instance) (j:bang/hileh) (r:zd:24116/zd:23784) (q:draft, low confidence)
banghong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<bang>, what, and <hong> written as one word, before a verb: what does it do to us or for us) (j:bang/hong) (r:zd:24374) (q:draft)
banghun = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:when/at what time) (d:<bang> and <hun> written as one word: what time, when, in a question; {banghun in} is at what time, and {banghun peuhin} is at any time) (s:cikciang) (j:bang/hun) (r:zd:21739/zd:21715/zd:9434) (q:draft)
Bangi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Bangi) (d:town in the state of Selangor in Malaysia, south of Kuala Lumpur) (r:zd:21476) (q:draft)
bangin kingaihsun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be regarded as/be thought of as/consider oneself) (d:<bangin>, like or as, and <kingaihsun>, be thought or think of oneself: placed after a noun or a clause, to be regarded as that, or to regard oneself as that) (r:zd:15527/zd:21013/zd:23729) (q:draft)
bangkek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as if/just like/pretending) (d:placed after a noun or clause, mostly with <in>: exactly like it, as though it were so, said of pretence or of a false appearance; from <bang>, like) (b:bang) (r:zd:16688/zd:16717/zd:11677) (q:draft)
bangkim = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:everything/all kinds/all sorts) (d:<bang>, what, with <kim>, all: every kind of thing; after a noun, that and everything that goes with it, and {bangkim ah} is in everything) (r:zd:8668/zd:17824) (q:draft)
bangkim = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be all alike/be equal) (d:after the prefix <ki>, {ki bangkim}: be the same in every respect; in the sentences always negated with <lo>, not all alike) (r:zd:16498) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangkimat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics) (d:<bang>, like, and <kimat>, being arrested, written as one word in {hih bangkimat kihen nate}, arrests and detentions like these; the usual spelling is {hih bang kimat}) (j:bang/kimat) (r:zd:22019) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bangkok = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Bangkok) (d:the capital city of <Thailand>) (r:zd:13285/zd:14579) (q:draft)
bangkua = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:household/family circle) (d:the household with its circle of kin, which in Zo custom has set roles in the affairs of the house; {bangkua sung} is within the family; one writer uses it for the leading role in that circle) (r:zd:23990/zd:23590/zd:23551) (q:draft, low confidence)
bangkum = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time/everyday) (w:what year/which year) (d:<bang>, what, and <kum>, year, written as one word in a question: in what year) (j:bang/kum) (r:zd:16337/zd:16442) (q:draft)
bangla = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what song) (d:<bang>, what, and <la>, song, written as one word: what song; in the pair {bangthu bangla} it only echoes <bangthu>: whatever matter, whatever happens) (j:bang/la) (r:zd:12031/zd:12504/zd:16216) (q:draft, low confidence)
