bawldan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:way of making/method/procedure) (d:<bawl> and <dan> written as one word: the way something is made, done or held) (j:bawl/dan) (r:zd:24276/zd:19683/zd:15407) (q:draft)
bawlden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always do/keep doing/do regularly) (d:<bawl>, do or make, with <den>, always, written as one word: do again and again or as a custom) (j:bawl/den) (r:zd:23129/zd:12217/zd:16302) (q:draft)
bawldending = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:do regularly/keep carrying out) (d:<bawl>, do, and <dending>, always, written as one word: carry out again and again, do as a regular practice) (j:bawl/dending) (r:zd:15592/zd:16009) (q:draft)
bawlding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:to make/will make/to do) (d:<bawl> and <ding> written as one word: will make or do, to be made or done, for making) (j:bawl/ding) (r:zd:16442/zd:16735) (q:draft)
bawldingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:in order to do/in order to make/to hold) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <dingin>, in order to, written as one word: in order to make, carry out or hold something) (j:bawl/dingin) (r:zd:22618/zd:19788/zd:21520) (q:draft)
bawldingpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/work) (w:what is to be made/what is to be done) (d:<bawlding> with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: the making or doing of something, as the topic of the sentence) (j:bawlding/pen) (r:zd:17450/zd:18042) (q:draft)
bawldingvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:matter of holding/plan to make) (d:<bawlding>, to make or hold, and <vai>, matter, written as one word: the business of making, building or holding something, common in headlines) (j:bawlding/vai) (r:zd:17864/zd:11340) (q:draft)
bawlhi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:make/build/do) (d:<bawl>, make, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: makes, has made or built) (j:bawl/hi) (r:zd:11211/zd:19816) (q:draft)
bawlhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:worth doing/that ought to be done/worth making) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <huai>, worthy of, written as one word: that should be done or made; paired with <sephuai>) (j:bawl/huai) (r:zd:15942/zd:22223) (q:draft)
bawlhun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:time for making/time for holding/period for applying) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <hun>, time, written as one word: the time or period in which something is made, done or held) (j:bawl/hun) (r:zd:21141/zd:13218) (q:draft)
bawlhunding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/work) (w:time for making/period for applying) (d:<bawl>, make, <hun>, time, and <ding>, for, written as one word: the time allowed for making or getting something, such as a card or a registration) (j:bawl/hun/ding) (r:zd:13215/zd:14549/zd:19143) (q:draft)
bawlkawikawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:carry out here and there/make in many places) (d:<bawl> and <kawikawi> written as one word: make, set up or carry out something in one place after another) (j:bawl/kawikawi) (r:zd:12689/zd:15073/zd:13323) (q:draft)
bawlkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:while making/while doing) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <kawm>, while, written as one word: while making or doing something, often followed by <in>) (j:bawl/kawm) (r:zd:23394/zd:13293) (q:draft)
bawlkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:hold together/do jointly/make together) (d:<bawl> and <khawm> written as one word: make, hold or carry out something together with others, such as an exercise or a celebration) (j:bawl/khawm) (r:zd:15093/zd:17377/zd:16830) (q:draft)
bawlkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:produce/create/invent/bring out) (d:<bawl>, make, with <khia>, out: make something and bring it out, produce or invent) (b:bawl) (r:zd:22983/zd:24574/zd:22643) (q:draft)
bawlkhial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do wrongly/botch/make a mistake) (d:<bawl> and <khial> written as one word: make or do something the wrong way) (j:bawl/khial) (r:zd:15547) (q:draft)
bawlkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:produce/make/create/manufacture) (d:<bawl>, make, with <khiat>, out: make and bring out, produce, invent or found; the form used before words such as <ding> and <zawh> and after the maker, as {Sente bawlkhiat}, made by the Chinese) (j:bawl/khiat) (r:zd:19858/zd:11373/zd:24049) (q:draft)
bawlkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:production/manufacture/making) (d:<bawl>, make, with <khiat>, out, and the noun suffix <na>: the producing of goods, as in a factory) (r:ts:2277/zd:18086) (q:draft)
bawlkhiatzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be able to produce/get made) (d:<bawlkhiat> and <zawh> written as one word: be able to make or complete something, mostly before <nading>) (j:bawlkhiat/zawh) (r:zd:12957/zd:16381) (q:draft)
bawlkhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have made/have done) (d:<bawl> and <khinta> written as one word: has already made or done) (j:bawl/khinta) (r:zd:12217/zd:19460) (q:draft)
bawlkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:do together/make together) (d:<bawl> and <khop> written as one word: make or carry out something jointly with others) (j:bawl/khop) (r:zd:24319/zd:16037) (q:draft)
bawlkhopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:doing together/joint undertaking/cooperation) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <khopna>, the doing of it together: making, holding or carrying out something jointly, often paired with <sepkhop>) (j:bawl/khopna) (r:zd:24605/zd:24230) (q:draft)
bawlkhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:permission to do/permission to hold) (d:<bawl>, make or hold, with <khuan>, permission: leave given by an authority to carry out or hold something) (j:bawl/khuan) (r:zd:15159/zd:11463) (q:draft)
bawlkikding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will do again/will make again) (d:<bawlkik> and <ding> written as one word: will make or do again, or to be done again) (j:bawlkik/ding) (r:zd:15180/zd:19563) (q:draft)
bawlkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:repair/restoration/rebuilding) (d:<bawlkik>, repair or make again, with the noun suffix <na>: the repairing or remaking of a thing) (b:bawlkik) (r:zd:11685/zd:11251) (q:draft)
bawlkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:need to do/must be made/have to undergo) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <kul>, be necessary, written as one word: it is necessary to make or do it; {Surgery bawlkul} is an operation is needed) (j:bawl/kul) (r:zd:12208/zd:18046/zd:11182) (q:draft)
bawlkulding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:will need to do/will have to undergo) (d:<bawlkul> and <ding> written as one word: it will be necessary to do or to have the thing named, as in {Surgery bawlkulding}, will need an operation) (j:bawlkul/ding) (r:zd:15260/zd:19373) (q:draft)
bawllai = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:when making/at the time of doing) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <lai> in its sense of the time when, before <in> or <leh>: at the time something was made or held, not still doing it) (r:zd:16871/zd:25562/zd:22350) (q:draft)
bawllaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:will still make/will go on to carry out) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <laiding>, will still, written as one word: will yet carry out, as an investigation or a report) (j:bawl/laiding) (r:zd:16741/zd:11126) (q:draft)
bawllaitak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:while doing/while holding/in the middle of making) (d:<bawl>, do or make, and <laitak>, at the very time, written as one word: while something is being done, made or held, as a wedding or an operation) (j:bawl/laitak) (r:zd:17794/zd:17899/zd:24116) (q:draft)
bawlleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one makes/if one does) (d:<bawl> and the conditional <leh> written as one word: if someone makes or does it) (j:bawl/leh) (r:zd:23487) (q:draft)
bawllo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not do/not make) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <lo>, not, written as one word: does not do, without doing) (j:bawl/lo) (r:zd:23935/zd:17450/zd:11463) (q:draft)
bawlloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not do/not make/leave undone) (d:<bawl> do or make and the negative <loh> written as one word: not doing a thing, before <ding>, <hangin> and <in>) (j:bawl/loh) (r:zd:23394/zd:24276) (q:draft)
bawllung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:football/ball/soccer) (d:a ball, and the game of football; {bawllung sui} is play football) (o:Burmese, baw-lone) (r:zd:20906/zd:15622) (q:draft)
bawlman = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:finish making/get done/manage to make) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <man>, finish: have a thing made or done, or manage to do it in time; {bawlman nailo} is not yet done) (j:bawl/man) (r:zd:13067/zd:12869) (q:draft)
bawlman = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work) (w:fee for making/charge) (d:<bawl>, make, with <man>, price: the fee charged for making something, such as a card) (j:bawl/man) (r:zd:20343) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlnading = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:for making/in order to do/to hold) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <nading>, for, written as one word, mostly followed by <in> or <ah>: for making a thing, or in order to carry out or hold something) (j:bawl/nading) (r:zd:15232/zd:11560/zd:13293) (q:draft)
bawlnadingin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/work) (w:in order to make/in order to do) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <nadingin>, in order to, written as one word: for making or carrying out the thing named before it) (j:bawl/nadingin) (r:zd:12630/zd:15134) (q:draft)
bawlngeikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have already made/have done before) (d:<bawl>, make, and <ngeikhin>, already before, written as one word; {Police Report bawlngeikhin} is have already filed a police report before) (j:bawl/ngeikhin) (r:zd:17884) (q:draft)
bawlngeilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:never do/never make) (d:<bawl>, do or make, and <ngeilo>, never, written as one word: never do, never cause) (j:bawl/ngeilo) (r:zd:15071/zd:11269) (q:draft)
bawlni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:day of making/day of holding/date of issue) (d:<bawl>, make or hold, and <ni>, day, written as one word: the day on which something is made, done or held; {pawi bawlni} is the day a feast is held) (j:bawl/ni) (r:zd:12695/zd:15622/ts:3201) (q:draft)
bawlnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:want to do/want to make) (d:<bawl>, do or make, and <nop>, want, written as one word: wish to do or make something; {na bawlnop khat} is something you want to do; often paired with <sepnop>) (j:bawl/nop) (r:zd:21377/zd:19898/zd:16037) (q:draft)
bawlnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to make/want to do/wish to hold) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <nuam>, want, written as one word; {a bawlnuam} is anyone who wishes to do it) (j:bawl/nuam) (r:zd:17327/zd:12504/zd:20576) (q:draft)
bawlpan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:start by making/begin to make) (d:<bawl>, make, with a short form of <kipan>, begin: begin by making or doing a thing) (b:bawl) (r:zd:25909) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the making or doing of something, as the topic of the sentence; not the superlative) (j:bawl/pen) (r:zd:12389) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlsakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will make for/will have done/to be done for) (d:<bawlsak>, make or do for someone, and <ding> written as one word: will make or carry out something for someone, or is to have it done) (j:bawlsak/ding) (r:zd:17822/zd:15007) (q:draft)
bawlsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:make for/do for) (d:<bawlsak>, make or do for someone, with <in> written as one word: making it for someone and going on; also the request make it for me) (b:bawlsak) (j:bawlsak/in) (r:zd:23037) (q:draft)
bawlsakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:repair for/redo for/do again for) (d:<bawlsak> and <kik> written as one word: make or do something again for someone, put it right for them) (j:bawlsak/kik) (r:zd:19398/zd:17510) (q:draft)
bawlsaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:not do for/not arrange for) (d:<bawlsak>, do or make for someone, with <lo>, not) (j:bawlsak/lo) (r:zd:13241/zd:13186) (q:draft)
bawlsakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:do for at once/carry out immediately) (d:<bawlsak>, do or make for someone, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: carry out at once for someone, as an operation, a check-up or a report) (j:bawlsak/pah) (r:zd:11825/zd:16767/zd:21588) (q:draft)
bawlsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be making/be carrying out) (d:from <bawl>, make or do: go on with making or holding something; mostly as {bawlsan laitak}, while it is being made, held or carried out) (b:bawl) (r:zd:16895/zd:11600) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:plan to make/intend to make/try to make) (d:<bawl>, make, with <sawm>, intend: plan or set about making something) (j:bawl/sawm) (r:zd:23365/zd:20576) (q:draft)
bawlsawmlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not intend to make/not try to do) (d:<bawlsawm>, intend to make, with <lo>, not, written as one word; {bangmah thu bawlsawmlo} is not mean to make any issue of it) (j:bawlsawm/lo) (r:zd:12910) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlsiagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:abuse badly/mistreat severely) (d:<bawlsia>, mistreat, with <gawp>, severely, written as one word: ill-treat or abuse someone badly) (j:bawlsia/gawp) (r:zd:19465/zd:10722) (q:draft)
bawlsiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:make well/be skilled at making/treat skilfully) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <siam>, skilled, written as one word: know how to make, repair or treat something and do it well) (j:bawl/siam) (r:zd:19676/zd:19798) (q:draft)
bawlsiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:can harm/be able to mistreat) (d:<bawlsia>, mistreat or harm, and <thei>, able, written as one word) (j:bawlsia/thei) (r:zd:13059) (q:draft)
bawlsiatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:damage/vandalise/cause damage to) (d:<bawlsiat>, harm or spoil, and the causative <sak> written as one word: damage or wreck a thing such as a car or a website; with <ki> before it, be damaged) (j:bawlsiat/sak) (r:zd:14897/zd:12472) (q:draft)
bawlsuakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:make straight away/file at once) (d:<bawl>, make, and <suakpah>, straight away, written as one word: do or make it right then, in the articles of a police report) (j:bawl/suakpah) (r:zd:12669/zd:15451) (q:draft)
bawltheihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:to be able to make/be able to do) (d:<bawltheih>, can make or do, and <ding> written as one word: so as to be able to make or do; in the articles mostly of applying for a card or registering) (j:bawltheih/ding) (r:zd:14720/zd:13186) (q:draft)
bawltheihhun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/politics) (w:application period/period for making) (d:<bawltheih>, can make, and <hun>, time, written as one word: the period during which something can be made or applied for, in the articles the Malaysian E-card for foreign workers) (j:bawltheih/hun) (r:zd:14549/zd:15397) (q:draft)
bawltheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:ability to do/power to make/being able to hold) (d:<bawltheih>, be able to make or do, with the noun suffix <na>: the ability or the power to make or do something; with <dinga>, so that it can be held or done) (b:bawltheih) (r:zd:12369/zd:21282) (q:draft)
bawlto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:keep making/go on doing/carry on) (d:<bawl> and <to>, onward, written as one word: go on making or doing something step by step) (j:bawl/to) (r:zd:16442/zd:23066) (q:draft)
bawluh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:make/do/carry out) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and the plural marker <uh> written as one word: they make, they do) (j:bawl/uh) (r:zd:20545/zd:19166) (q:draft)
bawlung = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:football/soccer) (d:the game of football rather than the ball itself, as in {bawlung suih}, play football, {bawlung siam}, a skilled footballer, and {bawlung kidemna}, a football tournament; another spelling of <bawhlung>) (s:bawhlung) (r:zd:24119/zd:26660/zd:20486) (q:draft)
bawlveve = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do anyway/make all the same/go ahead with) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <veve>, all the same, written as one word: do or hold something in spite of what has happened) (j:bawl/veve) (r:zd:11990/zd:21518) (q:draft)
bawlzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:complete/finish making/manage to do) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <zawh>, form of <zo>, be able or finish, written as one word: get something made or done; {bawlzawh nading} is in order to complete) (j:bawl/zawh) (r:zd:11101/zd:17060) (q:draft)
bawlzel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do repeatedly/keep doing/hold regularly) (d:<bawl>, do or make, and <zel>, again and again, written as one word) (j:bawl/zel) (r:zd:11477) (q:draft)
bawlzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:way of making/way of doing/method) (d:<bawl>, make or do, with <zia>, manner: the way something is made, done or held) (s:bawldan) (b:bawl) (r:zd:19816/zd:12630/zd:23466) (q:draft)
bawlziau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:make at once/do right away/just do) (d:<bawl>, make or do, and <ziau>, swiftly, written as one word: do or make something straight away and without fuss; {Report bawlziau} is promptly file a report) (j:bawl/ziau) (r:zd:15216/zd:11110) (q:draft)
bawlziauziau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:make readily/make with ease) (d:<bawl>, make, and <ziauziau>, readily, written as one word: make or produce a thing easily and without scruple) (j:bawl/ziauziau) (r:zd:15358/zd:20234) (q:draft)
bawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:basket/cage) (d:a container made to hold things, such as a basket of fruit or a cage for birds and animals) (s:seeng) (r:26.19.9) (q:draft)
bawm = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:surround/beset/swarm over) (d:as a verb, close in on or cover someone from all sides, said of sickness, hardship or insects; the thing that surrounds takes <in>) (r:zd:25227/zd:25162) (q:draft)
bawmpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:beset at once/quickly surround) (d:<bawm>, surround or beset, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: of sickness, come over people straight away) (j:bawm/pah) (r:zd:22685) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawmpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:large box/crate/large cage) (d:<bawm>, box or cage, with the ending <pi>, big: a large box, crate or cage) (b:bawm) (j:bawm/pi) (r:zd:16389/ts:10733) (q:draft)
bawmsung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:inside of a box/inside of a cage) (d:<bawm> and <sung> written as one word: the inside of a box, cage or cabin, mostly with <ah> or <panin>) (j:bawm/sung) (r:zd:16389/zd:12502) (q:draft)
bawmta = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:helper/go-between/aid) (d:one who lends a hand or acts between two sides, or a thing that assists; {bawmta sem} is act as a helper or go-between) (r:zd:16651) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawng = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature/food) (w:cow/ox/cattle) (d:cow or ox, the general word for cattle of either sex; <bawngpi> is the female, <bawngtal> the male and <bawngno> the young)
bawngbawng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social/family) (w:in groups/group by group) (d:in the phrase {a beh a bawngbawng} or after a doubled noun: each clan or group by itself, group by group) (r:zd:22758/zd:18086) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bawngkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:nature/social) (w:one cow/a cow) (d:<bawng>, cow, and <khat>, one, written as one word, in a list of gifts given by churches and persons: one head of cattle) (j:bawng/khat) (r:zd:14579) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawngkuang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/nature) (w:manger/feeding trough) (d:<bawng> and <kuang> written as one word: the trough from which cattle eat, the manger of the birth of Jesus) (j:bawng/kuang) (r:zd:9242/zd:26385) (q:draft)
bawngnawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:milk) (d:the milk of a cow) (s:nawi) (q:draft)
bawngnawivui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:milk powder/powdered milk) (d:<bawngnawi>, milk, with a word for powder: dried milk, such as formula for babies) (b:bawngnawi) (r:zd:16073/zd:16684) (q:draft)
bawtui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:semen/sperm) (d:the fluid of a man or male animal that carries the seed) (r:zd:14535) (q:draft)
bazaar = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:market/bazaar) (d:a market where goods are bought and sold; {bazaar pai} is go to the market) (s:sumbuk) (o:English) (r:zd:23249) (q:draft)
bazar = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:market/bazaar) (d:a market where goods are sold, also in the names of markets and market towns) (s:sumbuk) (o:Hindi, bazar) (r:zd:22686/ts:4569) (q:draft)
BBC = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:BBC/British Broadcasting Corporation) (d:the British public broadcaster, named in news reports as the source of a story) (r:zd:13098/zd:12785) (q:draft)
bebek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:alone/only/just) (d:placed after a noun: that thing alone, taken or counted by itself; an emphatic form of <bek>) (r:zd:24535/zd:20324/zd:15855) (q:draft)
Bedford = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Bedford) (d:a town in England) (r:zd:9260) (q:draft)
Bedok = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Bedok) (d:a town in the east of Singapore) (r:zd:16287/zd:24595) (q:draft)
Bedroom = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:bedroom) (d:English word set beside the Zolai {lupna inndei} or <lupna> in news reports: the room where someone sleeps) (o:English) (r:zd:16673/zd:12329) (q:draft, low confidence)
bee = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (w:bean/pea) (d:beans and other pulses as a crop or food; {mongphal bee} is the groundnut or peanut) (r:zd:22334/zd:20902) (q:draft, low confidence)
beekin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even/at least) (d:<beek> and <in> written as one word: even, at least; with a negative, not even) (j:beek/in) (r:zd:16655) (q:draft, low confidence)
beeklo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not even/not at all) (d:<beek> and <lo> written as one word, placed after a verb: not even that, not at all) (j:beek/lo) (r:zd:23386/zd:23932) (q:draft)
beel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/food) (w:pot/jar/vessel) (d:container of clay, metal, wood or stone used for cooking, for storing things or for carrying water; {beel kitam} is a broken pot, a potsherd) (r:24.19.10) (q:draft)
beel = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:rely on/take refuge in/cling to/depend on) (d:spelling with a long vowel of <bel.1>: attach oneself to a person, a group or God for shelter and support; {sunghte beel} is living with and depending on the in-laws; not the cooking pot) (r:zd:23754/zd:25203/zd:25137) (q:draft)
beelpawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:ally/associate/partner) (d:one who sides and works together with another, of countries an ally and of a ruler his associates; {kumpi beelpawl te} are the people of a government) (r:zd:25866/zd:15037) (q:draft)
Beelpawlgam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics) (w:the Union/Union of Burma) (d:<beelpawl>, ally, with <gam>, country: a union of states, used as the name of the Union of Burma that became independent in 1948; without a capital also a state that belongs to a union) (j:beelpawl/gam) (r:zd:23597/zd:25866) (q:draft)
beem = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:round/circular) (d:having the shape of a circle or ball, as in {sabuai beem}, a round table; also said of the figure zero; not the grain measure) (r:zd:21221) (q:draft)
beeng = (i:3) (t:n) (f:nature/politics) (w:opium poppy/poppy/opium) (d:the poppy plant grown in hill fields and the opium got from it, as in {beeng cinna}, the growing of poppy; not the verb slap or clap) (r:ts:3907/ts:3969) (q:draft)
beetroot = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (w:beetroot/beet) (d:the red root vegetable, grown in gardens and eaten for health) (o:English) (r:zd:19875) (q:draft)
beh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:clan/family) (d:group of related families within a tribe) (s:phung) (r:15.10.38) (q:draft)
behding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will do further/to add) (d:written as one word after a verb, with <ding>: will do more of it, to do it in addition; the first part means in addition, as in <behlap>, and is not <beh>, clan) (j:beh/ding) (r:zd:11506) (q:draft, low confidence)
Behiang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Behiang) (d:village in Manipur, India, on the border with Myanmar) (r:zd:21421/zd:15637) (q:draft)
behlai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:further/in addition/still more/as well) (d:placed after a verb: the action comes on top of what went before; {kihel behlai} is is included as well, {cih behlai} is said further, and {behlai ding kul} is more of it is still needed) (r:zd:15188/zd:21590/zd:22650) (q:draft)
behlapding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will add/will increase) (d:<behlap> and <ding> written as one word: will add, is to be added; common in headlines about more staff, jobs or places) (j:behlap/ding) (r:zd:11441/zd:16178/zd:16421) (q:draft)
behlapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:addition/increase/supplement) (d:<behlap>, add, with the noun suffix <na>: the adding of something more, or what is added) (b:behlap) (r:zd:23902/zd:25106) (q:draft)
behlapte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:those added/additions) (d:<behlap>, add, and the plural <te> written as one word: the persons or things that have been added) (j:behlap/te) (r:zd:17572) (q:draft)
behlapthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can be added/may increase) (d:<behlap>, add, and <thei>, can, written as one word: can add or be added; {ki behlapthei} of a number, may rise further) (j:behlap/thei) (r:zd:20668/zd:24276) (q:draft)
behlapzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:add more/increase further) (d:<behlap> and <zaw> written as one word: add still more, more is added than before or than expected) (j:behlap/zaw) (r:zd:23984/zd:13295) (q:draft)
behlehphung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:clan/kindred/relatives) (d:<beh>, clan, <leh>, and, and <phung>, lineage, written as one word: clan and kindred, one's own relatives by descent) (j:beh/leh/phung) (r:zd:11648/zd:21037) (q:draft)
behmin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:clan name/family name/surname) (d:<beh>, clan, with <min>, name: the name of the clan a person belongs to, used as a family name) (r:zd:23144/zd:12314) (q:draft)
behna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:addition/further) (d:the verb of adding, as in {gen beh}, say in addition, with the noun suffix <na>, placed after a verb: what is done in addition; {gen behna} is a further statement, {bawl behna} a further building) (r:zd:13076/zd:19676) (q:draft)
behnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to add/wish to ask further) (d:the verb of adding, as in {gen beh}, say in addition, with <nop>, want: wishing to add something more; {dot behnop} is a further question one wishes to ask) (r:zd:25118/zd:19527) (q:draft)
behsung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:within the clan/clan circle) (d:<beh>, clan, and <sung>, inside, written as one word: the clan as a circle of relatives, often paired as {behsung phungsung}, clan and kindred) (j:beh/sung) (r:zd:25712/zd:11648) (q:draft)
behthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can add/can do more) (d:a first part that means add or do in addition, as in <behlap>, with <thei>, able, after a verb: be able to do or get more; {kinei behthei lo} is one cannot get more of it) (r:zd:25919/zd:20387) (q:draft, low confidence)
beiciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:at the end of/by the end of) (d:<bei>, come to an end, and <ciang>, when, written as one word after a word of time or a verb: when it is over, at the end of) (j:bei/ciang) (r:zd:24144) (q:draft)
beiciangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time/everyday) (w:when it is over/when finished/when used up) (d:<bei> and <ciangin> written as one word: when something has come to an end or is used up) (j:bei/ciangin) (r:zd:20092/zd:19679) (q:draft)
beiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:will end/will be over) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with <ding> written as one word: will come to an end, is going to be over) (j:bei/ding) (r:zd:16844/zd:15294) (q:draft)
beiding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work) (w:will cost/will be spent) (d:<bei>, be used up, with <ding> written as one word, said of money: the amount that will be spent, what it will cost) (j:bei/ding) (r:zd:22774/zd:17806) (q:draft)
beidong = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:desperate/distressed/helpless/at a loss) (d:at the end of one's means and not knowing what to do; {beidong kisa} is feel desperate, and it is often paired with <cimawh>) (r:zd:15709/zd:26626) (q:draft)
beidong = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:until the end/until it is gone) (d:<bei>, come to an end, and <dong>, until, written as one word: until something is finished or used up, as {a beidong in}) (j:bei/dong) (r:zd:21918) (q:draft, low confidence)
Beijing = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Beijing) (d:the capital city of China) (r:zd:14814/zd:13030) (q:draft)
beikik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:go away again/come to an end again/disappear) (d:<bei> and <kik> written as one word: of something that had come, end or be gone again) (j:bei/kik) (r:zd:24276/zd:21918) (q:draft)
beikuan = (i:2) (t:n) (f:time) (w:end/close/latter part) (d:the last part of a year, a month or a period, after <kum>, <kha> or a year number and often followed by <lam> or <pawl>: {kum beikuan lam} is towards the end of the year) (r:zd:22595/zd:22992/zd:19662) (q:draft)
beilawhliang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:even lose/go so far as to lose) (d:<beilawh>, lose, and <liang>, even, written as one word, said of life: {nuntakna beilawhliang} is even lose one's life) (j:beilawh/liang) (r:zd:19303/zd:19134) (q:draft)
beileh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if it runs out/when it is gone) (d:<bei>, come to an end, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if or when something is used up or lost) (j:bei/leh) (r:zd:23729) (q:draft)
beilian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be completely gone/run out entirely) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with <lian>, here exactly or completely, written as one word: be finished or used up altogether) (j:bei/lian) (r:zd:17291/zd:25346) (q:draft, low confidence)
beiliang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:spend as much as/cost as much as) (d:<bei> and <liang> written as one word after a sum of money, with <in>: spending even so much, at so great a cost) (j:bei/liang) (r:zd:11668) (q:draft)
beilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not be used up/not come to an end) (d:<bei> and <lo> written as one word: not come to an end, not die out; of money, not be spent, so that {sum beilo in} is without cost, free of charge) (j:bei/lo) (r:zd:24199/zd:22459/zd:24641) (q:draft)
beipah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:end at once/be used up quickly/be over soon) (d:<bei>, come to an end, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: be over or used up straight away) (j:bei/pah) (r:zd:22992/zd:23836/zd:22577) (q:draft)
Beirut = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Beirut) (d:the capital city of <Lebanon>) (r:zd:24685/zd:24532) (q:draft)
beisan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:pass away/die/come to an end) (d:<bei>, come to an end, with the ending {-san}, leaving behind: pass away and leave those who remain, a gentle word for the death of a person, usually as {hong beisan}; also of an event that has come to its end) (r:zd:25477/ts:479/zd:10665) (q:draft)
beisate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:the past/past times/former things) (d:<beisa>, past, with the plural <te>: the things or times that have gone by; {hun beisate} is times past) (b:beisa) (r:zd:20958/zd:21081) (q:draft)
beitading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:will now end/be about to end) (d:<bei>, come to an end, and <tading> written as one word: will now come to an end, is about to be over) (j:bei/tading) (r:zd:11382/zd:19945) (q:draft)
beite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those that are finished/what is spent) (d:<bei>, come to an end or be used up, and the plural <te> written as one word: the ones that have ended or are gone; {lamet beite} are those who have lost hope and {sum beite} the money spent) (j:bei/te) (r:zd:24244/zd:12231) (q:draft)
beithei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can be used up/can run out/can end) (d:<bei>, come to an end or be spent, and <thei>, can, written as one word: of money or time, can be used up; with <lo>, never ending) (j:bei/thei) (r:zd:17607/zd:19427) (q:draft)
beitheiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:may cost/could be spent) (d:<bei>, be used up, and <theiding> written as one word, said after a sum of money: that much may be spent, it may cost so much) (j:bei/theiding) (r:zd:15956/zd:13030) (q:draft)
beithuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:cost extra/cost in addition) (d:<bei>, be spent, with <thuah>, in addition: of money, be spent on top of what is already paid) (j:bei/thuah) (r:zd:13165/zd:20095) (q:draft)
beizah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:expense/cost/amount spent) (d:<bei>, be used up, and <zah>, amount, written as one word: the amount of money or time that is spent, as in {sum beizah}, expenses) (j:bei/zah) (r:zd:25109/zd:20922) (q:draft)
beiziau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be gone at once/end suddenly/be used up quickly) (d:<bei>, come to an end, and <ziau>, swiftly, written as one word: be over or gone all at once) (j:bei/ziau) (r:zd:11391/zd:26664) (q:draft)
beizo = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be spent/cost/be used up) (d:of money or a supply: be spent or used up; after an amount of money {beizo} says how much something has cost) (r:zd:21843/zd:21458/zd:23198) (q:draft)
bek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only/alone) (d:placed after the word it limits: that one and no other, that much and no more) (s:lel) (q:draft)
bek hilo = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:not only) (d:<bek>, only, and <hilo>, is not: placed after a word or clause and mostly followed by <in>, not only that; the next clause often has <zong>, also) (r:zd:22775/zd:16022/zd:21850) (q:draft)
bek hiloin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:not only/not just) (d:<bek>, only, and <hiloin>, not being: placed after a word or clause, not only that; what follows adds something more, often with <zong> or <nangawn>, also or even) (r:zd:24392/zd:25464/zd:24320) (q:draft)
bek thamloh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:not only/besides) (d:<bek>, only, and <thamloh>, not so much: placed after a word or phrase, with or without <in>, not only that but more besides; {tua bek thamloh} opens a sentence as not only that, and the next phrase often has <zong>, also) (s:bekthamlo) (r:zd:17883/zd:24545/zd:22785) (q:draft)
bek thamloin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:not only/moreover/besides) (d:<bek>, only, and <thamloin>, not stopping at: not only that; mostly as {tua bek thamloin} at the head of a sentence that adds a further point, not only that but also) (r:zd:20172/zd:22336) (q:draft)
Bekan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Bekan) (d:name of a village, named with Suahlim; written {bekan} the word is also the soya bean) (r:ts:11942) (q:draft, low confidence)
Bekasi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Bekasi) (d:city and regency in West Java, Indonesia, next to Jakarta) (r:zd:16107) (q:draft)
bekbek aphapan = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/media) (w:only just/barely) (d:<bekbek>, only, and <aphapan>, having just reached: placed after an age or a length of time given with <kum>, <kha> or <ni>, it says that someone is only that old, and it stresses how young; common in news reports) (r:zd:14642/zd:21793) (q:draft)
bekbek inzong = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/media) (w:alone/even just) (d:<bekbek>, only, with <inzong>, also: placed after a time, a place or a cause, in that one alone, even counting nothing else; it leads to a statement of a large number or amount) (r:zd:17607/zd:11579) (q:draft)
bekbekah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only in/in that alone) (d:<bekbek> and <ah> written as one word: only in, in that place alone) (j:bekbek/ah) (r:zd:25158/zd:9236) (q:draft)
bekbekmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only/nothing but/just) (d:<bekbek> and <mah> written as one word after the word it limits: that and nothing else, with strong emphasis) (j:bekbek/mah) (r:zd:19311/zd:18067/zd:11253) (q:draft)
bekbekpen = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:alone/by itself/just) (d:<bekbek>, only, and the topic marker <pen>, written as one word after a noun, before a number: counting that one alone) (j:bekbek/pen) (r:zd:12307/zd:20562) (q:draft)
bekbekzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:alone already/even only) (d:<bekbek> and <zong> written as one word, placed after a noun and before a number: counting only these, they alone already come to so many) (j:bekbek/zong) (r:zd:12115/zd:19151/zd:16367) (q:draft)
bekhilo = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:not only) (d:<bek>, only, and <hilo>, is not, written as one word: not only, placed after the first of two things, often followed by <in> and with <zong>, also, in what follows) (j:bek/hilo) (r:zd:22740/zd:24276/zd:21869) (q:draft)
beklo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not only) (d:<bek>, only, and <lo>, not, written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: not only that, with something more added after it) (j:bek/lo) (r:zd:21866/zd:23977/zd:16442) (q:draft)
bekmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only/alone/none but) (d:<bek> and <mah> written as one word, placed after the word it limits: that one only, with emphasis) (j:bek/mah) (r:zd:26049/zd:15905/zd:11782) (q:draft)
bektawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:with only/merely by/alone) (d:<bek> and <tawh.2> written as one word, placed after a noun: with that alone, by nothing more than that) (j:bek/tawh) (r:zd:23843/zd:11748) (q:draft)
bekte = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the only ones/only those) (d:<bek> and the plural <te> written as one word: those and no others, the only ones) (j:bek/te) (r:zd:11213) (q:draft)
bektham = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not only) (d:<bek>, only, with <tham>, written as one word and always followed by a negative: {bektham loin} or {bektham lo-in} is not only, and at the start of a sentence not only that, moreover) (j:bek/tham) (r:zd:23554/zd:24502) (q:draft)
bekthamlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not only) (d:<bek>, only, and <thamlo>, not so much, written as one word: placed after a word or phrase, not only that but more besides; the next phrase often has <zong>, also) (j:bek/thamlo) (r:zd:13165/zd:14301/zd:19593) (q:draft)
bekthamloh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not only) (d:<bektham> and <loh> written as one word, placed after a phrase: not only that, but more besides) (j:bektham/loh) (r:zd:17152/zd:24089) (q:draft)
bekthamloin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:not only/besides/moreover) (d:<bek> and <thamloin> written as one word: not only that, and more besides; {tua bekthamloin} opens a sentence as moreover) (s:bekthamlo) (j:bek/thamloin) (r:zd:15422/zd:20033) (q:draft)
bekuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only) (d:<bek> and the plural marker <uh> written as one word; with <hilo> or <hikei> after it: they do not only do this, but more) (j:bek/uh) (r:zd:21862/zd:24234) (q:draft)
bekzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even just/not only) (d:<bek> and <zong> written as one word: even that alone; before a negative such as <hilo> or <hituankei>, it is not only that) (j:bek/zong) (r:zd:12746/zd:12538) (q:draft)
bel = (i:3) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:as for/though/however) (d:placed after a noun, pronoun or clause to set it off as the topic or in contrast with what was just said, as in {amau bel}, as for them; not {bel}, take refuge, and not the {bel} of {a masa bel}, the very first) (r:ts:6573/ts:9564/ts:4162) (q:draft)
belah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as for in/in turn) (d:<bel>, as for, and <ah>, in or at, written as one word after a noun: as for that one, in that one however) (j:bel/ah) (r:zd:21279/ts:9163) (q:draft, low confidence)
