buainapi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:great trouble/major problem/serious conflict) (d:<buaina>, trouble, with <pi>, great, written as one word) (b:buaina) (j:buaina/pi) (r:zd:25148/zd:11394) (q:draft)
buainate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:troubles/problems/conflicts) (d:plural of <buaina>: troubles and difficulties in life, and unrest or conflicts in a country) (b:buaina) (r:zd:23975/zd:17055) (q:draft)
buainavai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:incident/trouble/dispute) (d:<buaina> and <vai> written as one word: a matter of trouble, an incident or dispute that is reported or looked into) (j:buaina/vai) (r:zd:18145/zd:16026) (q:draft)
buaingeingai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:be in an uproar/be in commotion) (d:<buai>, be in turmoil, with the expressive <ngeingai>, written as one word: many people are in a noisy stir and confusion) (j:buai/ngeingai) (r:zd:16811/zd:15456) (q:draft)
buaipih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:attend to/deal with/be busy with) (d:<buai>, be occupied, with <pih>, together with or for: take trouble over a matter or over a person in need, as a sick person or a prisoner) (b:buai) (r:zd:14615/zd:16216) (q:draft)
buaipihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:concern/trouble taken/matter dealt with) (d:<buaipih>, be busy with, with the noun suffix <na>: what one is occupied with or takes trouble over, a problem that has to be dealt with) (b:buaipih) (r:zd:24168/zd:23201) (q:draft)
buakgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:douse/pour all over/drench) (d:<buak>, pour on, with <gawp>, thoroughly, written as one word: pour a liquid all over someone or something) (j:buak/gawp) (r:zd:15425/zd:14758) (q:draft)
buakhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:flock to/swarm/throng) (d:come or go in great numbers and with force toward a person, a place or a cause, of a crowd that rushes to support or to attack) (r:zd:12487/zd:25580) (q:draft, low confidence)
bualpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:pool/large pool/lake) (d:<bual>, pool, with <pi>, great: a large pool or lake; also used of a field of activity that people enter) (b:bual) (r:zd:17620) (q:draft, low confidence)
buan = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:rape) (d:a verb, not the word for mud: force a person to have sex, often with <zawhthawh thutawh>, by force; {buan thuak} is be raped) (r:zd:26838/zd:12979) (q:draft)
buan = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:wrestle/grapple) (d:take hold of someone and struggle with him body to body, as Jacob with God; {ki buan} is wrestle with each other, also of two wills that are in conflict) (r:zd:10963/zd:23022) (q:draft, low confidence)
buan athuak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/media) (w:raped/sexually assaulted) (d:<buan>, here a verb, seize and force, rape, not the noun for mud, and <athuak>, the one who suffers it: placed before the word for the person, as {buan athuak numeino}, the girl who was raped; a term of crime reports) (r:zd:12979/zd:11484) (q:draft)
buanciim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:mud/slush/mire) (d:thin wet mud, as left by a flood or on a road in the rainy season; also said of flowing lava) (r:zd:16724/zd:20456) (q:draft)
buanden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:rape repeatedly/keep raping) (d:<buan>, here in the sense seize and violate a person sexually, and <den>, continually, written as one word) (j:buan/den) (r:zd:15082) (q:draft, low confidence)
buangawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:rape/assault/maul) (d:a verb spelled like <buan>, mud, but meaning seize and force, with <gawp>, violently: assault brutally; with <zawhthawh thutawh>, by force, rape; of an animal, maul) (r:zd:19536/zd:25043) (q:draft, low confidence)
buangding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:at least/of all things/for such a one) (d:the emphatic particle <buang> and <ding> written as one word: after a verb, surely at least; after a noun phrase and followed by <in>, for something that is supposed to be such a one) (j:buang/ding) (r:zd:15851/zd:11110) (q:draft, low confidence)
buangleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:unless/except if) (d:<buang> and <leh>, if, written as one word after a negative, as in {ahih kei buangleh}: unless it is, except in the case of) (j:buang/leh) (r:ts:301/zd:16523) (q:draft)
buangnai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:rubber/elastic) (d:rubber, the stretchy material of tyres, erasers and elastic bands; {buangnai thautang} is a rubber bullet) (r:ts:9171/zd:22451) (q:draft)
buanhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:rape/gang-rape) (d:force a person to have sex; in news reports mostly of several men together or one after another; built on a verb for rape that is spelled like <buan>, mud, but is a different word) (r:zd:19540/zd:22813) (q:draft, low confidence)
buanin = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:mud) (d:<buan.1>, mud, with the marker <in>, by: by mud or with mud, as of houses that a mudslide buries, {buanin vukcip}; not the verb of forcing a person) (r:zd:12042) (q:draft, low confidence)
buanlak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:mud/quagmire/muddy ground) (d:<buan>, mud, with <lak>, the midst: a stretch of soft wet mud, a place where one sinks in) (r:zd:15405/zd:22557) (q:draft)
Buanman = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Buanman) (d:one of the Sihzang villages near Thuklai in Chin State) (r:ts:11788) (q:draft)
buanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:struggle/grappling/tussle) (d:a grappling or wrestling with someone or something, also a clash or trouble between people; {ki buanna} is a struggle of two sides with each other) (r:zd:23022/zd:15639) (q:draft, low confidence)
Buannel = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Buannel) (d:the name used by the Falam people for the area that the Tedim people call Lennupa, with forest around it, on the border of the Tedim and Falam regions) (r:zd:24223) (q:draft)
buansak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:make rape/cause to rape) (d:<buan>, rape, and the causative <sak> written as one word: make someone rape another person; {ki buansak} is also found for wrestle) (j:buan/sak) (r:zd:20482) (q:draft, low confidence)
buansawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:try to rape/attempt to rape) (d:<buan>, force a person sexually, with <sawm>, intend: try to rape; in news of arrests and court cases) (j:buan/sawm) (r:zd:15236/zd:12085) (q:draft)
buanthuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:be raped/suffer rape) (d:the verb of <kibuan>, be raped, with <thuak>, suffer: be the victim of rape; {buanthuak numeinu} is the woman who was raped) (s:kibuan) (r:zd:12733/zd:12542) (q:draft)
buanzel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:rape repeatedly/assault repeatedly) (d:<buan>, here the verb wrestle with or rape, and <zel>, repeatedly, written as one word: rape or sexually assault again and again; found in crime reports) (j:buan/zel) (r:zd:21892) (q:draft)
buanzelzel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:rape repeatedly/rape again and again) (d:<buan>, rape, and <zelzel>, again and again, written as one word; found in crime reports) (j:buan/zelzel) (r:zd:11484) (q:draft)
buatbuat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:hastily/rashly/abruptly) (d:placed after a verb: doing it at once and without thought or restraint, as ordering, accepting, marrying or eating in a rush) (r:zd:12544/zd:14861/zd:26097) (q:draft)
Bucharest = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Bucharest) (d:capital city of <Romania>) (r:zd:25918/zd:11145) (q:draft)
bucing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:complete/perfect/whole/full) (d:lacking nothing, complete in every part; {mi bucing} is a perfect person) (s:kicing) (r:zd:26660/zd:25139/zd:9433) (q:draft)
Buckingham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:politics/travel) (w:Buckingham) (d:in Buckingham Palace, the house of the British king or queen in London) (r:zd:25908/zd:24134) (q:draft)
Budda = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (j:Buddha) (r:zd:22565) (q:draft)
Buddha = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Buddha) (d:the Buddha, the teacher from whom Buddhism comes; {Buddha biakna} is Buddhism) (r:ts:3503/zd:19269/zd:19282) (q:draft)
Buddhism = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Buddhism) (d:the religion that follows the teaching of the Buddha, the religion of most Burmese) (o:English) (r:zd:24595/zd:9135/zd:25275) (q:draft)
Buddhist = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:religion) (w:Buddhist) (d:a follower of Buddhism, and of or belonging to Buddhism; {Buddhist biakna} is the Buddhist religion) (o:English) (r:zd:19282/zd:14937/zd:23014) (q:draft)
budget = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:budget) (d:the money that a government or organisation sets aside to spend in a period, and the plan for it) (o:English) (r:zd:22584/zd:24376) (q:draft)
Budhist = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:religion) (j:Buddhist) (r:zd:12405/zd:19662) (q:draft)
buh = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food) (w:rice) (d:rice as a plant and as grain) (r:zai:rice) (q:draft)
