Bulletin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:bulletin/newsletter) (d:printed paper of news and notices put out by a church or an association) (o:English) (r:zd:21717/zd:19657) (q:draft, low confidence)
bullying = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:bullying) (d:the repeated ill-treatment of a weaker person, especially among school pupils; the articles explain the English word with {gitlohna, gualheuna}) (o:English) (r:zd:21690/zd:20060) (q:draft, low confidence)
bulphuhlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not based on/without relying on) (d:<bulphuh> and <lo> written as one word: not taking something as the foundation) (j:bulphuh/lo) (r:zd:24314/zd:10732) (q:draft)
bulphuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:basis/foundation/focus) (d:<bulphuh>, base on, with the noun suffix <na>: what something rests on or is centred on) (b:bulphuh) (r:zd:25043/zd:23780/ts:9859) (q:draft)
bulpi = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:main/chief/principal/basic) (d:placed after a noun: the chief one of its kind or the root from which the rest comes, not a base of stone; <deihna bulpi> is the main aim, {ahang bulpi} the main reason, and <gennop bulpi> the main point one wants to make) (r:zd:21063/zd:11548/zd:15942) (q:draft)
bulpite = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:social/politics) (w:main/basic/fundamental/principal) (d:placed after a noun, as in {ngimna bulpite}, the main aims of an organisation, and {kisap bulpite}, basic needs: the chief or basic ones, not the base of a building) (r:ts:5729/zd:12276/zd:11274) (q:draft)
bulpuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:bulphuh) (r:zd:13076) (q:draft)
buluah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:seize/usurp/take over/occupy) (d:take power or territory by force, as an army does in a coup or an invasion, with <ukna> or <thuneihna> for the power seized; not the plundering of goods) (r:zd:25053/zd:16310/zd:25109) (q:draft)
buluak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:seize/capture/overrun) (d:attack and take a town, a camp or the rule of a country by force; {galkap ukna buluak} is the military seizure of power) (r:ts:8023/zd:25182) (q:draft)
buluh = (i:3) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:seize/usurp) (d:take the power of government by force, with <ukna>; <ukna buluh> before SAC or SAM is the usual name for the military that seized power in Myanmar) (r:ts:6004/ts:5564) (q:draft)
buluhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:raid/attack/seize by force) (d:<buluh>, raid, and <in> written as one word: raiding a place or seizing power by force, and then doing what follows) (j:buluh/in) (r:ts:301/zd:25015) (q:draft)
buluhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:raid/break into) (d:<buluh> and <khia> written as one word: force a way into a place, of police raiding a house or of robbers breaking into a store) (j:buluh/khia) (r:zd:22298) (q:draft)
buluhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:robbery/raid/attack/invasion) (d:<buluh>, raid, with the noun suffix <na>: a robbery or break-in; in news of war also an attack on a camp, an invasion, or a seizure of power) (b:buluh) (r:zd:22550/zd:25698/zd:19837) (q:draft)
buluhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:seize/take by force/raid) (d:<buluh>, seize or raid, and <sak> written as one word: take power or property from someone by force) (j:buluh/sak) (r:zd:23476) (q:draft, low confidence)
