bumh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (j:bum) (r:zd:24731) (q:draft, low confidence)
bun = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hit home/sink in/make an impression) (d:of words, a speech or a piece of writing, reach the mind or heart so that it is felt or understood, as in {lungsim hong bun}; often with <zaw> or <taktak>, and not said of a weapon or of rust) (r:zd:21925/zd:23828) (q:draft)
bung = (i:3) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:cylinder/tin/container/box) (d:a closed container of metal or the like, named by what it holds: <gas bung> is a gas cylinder, <oxygen bung> an oxygen cylinder; also a box or tin into which things are put, not the Bible measure) (r:zd:25184/zd:14523/zd:12819) (q:draft)
bungbusa = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:upside down/head down) (d:<bungbu>, head first, with <sa>: in a head-down position) (b:bungbu) (r:zd:19476) (q:draft, low confidence)
bunghawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:empty can/empty tin/empty jar) (d:a can, tin or jar with nothing in it, often named with <thawlhawm>, empty bottle, as something collected and sold) (r:zd:24502/zd:24029/zd:23367) (q:draft)
bungkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:one box/one can/one pack/one container) (d:<bung>, here a box, can, pack or cylinder, and <khat>, one, written as one word after the thing counted) (j:bung/khat) (r:zd:14539/zd:17501) (q:draft)
