citazen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:actually say/even say) (d:<ci> and <tazen> written as one word after the words reported: it is actually said, they even call it so) (j:ci/tazen) (r:zd:23761/zd:17510) (q:draft, low confidence)
citciat = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as it happens/in fact/actually) (d:placed after a verb, often after <kha>, to say that something happens to be so, usually unexpected or not planned; {kizaihkha citciat} is it happened to be recorded) (r:zd:12089/zd:20224/zd:22116) (q:draft)
citciatse = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as it happens/in fact) (d:<citciat>, as it happens, with the emphatic <se>, written as one word and placed after a verb, before <hi> or <uh>) (j:citciat/se) (r:zd:12654) (q:draft, low confidence)
citek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:each say/all say) (d:<ci>, say, and <tek>, each, written as one word: each of them says, they all say) (j:ci/tek) (r:zd:15790/zd:19051) (q:draft)
cithei = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can say/may say/can call) (d:<ci>, say, with <thei>, can, written as one word: be able to say a thing or to call something so, often in a question such as {i cithei diam}, can we say; the words said come before it, and nothing is meant about being well off) (r:zd:21221/zd:22350/zd:17221) (q:draft)
