daan = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:way/manner/method) (d:the way in which something is done or is, a spelling of <dan>, after a verb or a clause; {zat daan} is the way of using) (s:dan) (r:zd:24324/zd:22802/zd:25390) (q:draft)
daanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:danin) (r:zd:23079) (q:draft)
daante = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:ways/kinds/such things) (d:plural of <daan> in the meaning way or kind, after <cih> or <tua>: {cih daante} is things of that kind; not penalties) (r:zd:22433/zd:24503) (q:draft)
dada = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:expressive word placed after a verb of sound or speech, most often <ging>: the sound goes on loud and without a break, droning or blaring) (r:zd:22046) (q:draft, low confidence)
dah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:mourn/grieve/be sad) (d:feel sorrow, above all over a death or a loss; the opposite of <lungdam>, be glad) (a:lungdam/kipak) (r:1.27.41)
dah akap = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/religion) (w:the bereaved/those who mourn and weep) (d:<dah>, grieve, and {a kap}, who weeps, written as one word: with <a> before it, as {a dah akap}, those who grieve and weep, the bereaved family; a formula of condolence notices, followed by <khempeuh>, all, or <te>) (r:zd:23471/zd:20263) (q:draft)
dahlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not be sad/not grieve) (d:<dah>, be sad, and <lo>, not, written as one word) (j:dah/lo) (r:zd:19150) (q:draft, low confidence)
dahmahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be very sad/grieve deeply) (d:<dah>, be sad, and <mahmah>, very, written as one word) (j:dah/mahmah) (r:zd:17461/zd:15114) (q:draft)
dahna kahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:mourning/grief/sorrow and weeping) (d:<dahna>, sorrow, and <kahna>, weeping, said as a pair: grief and mourning, above all over a death or a disaster; {dahna kahna hun} is a time of mourning) (r:zd:16071/zd:24176) (q:draft)
dahni = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:let us not) (d:<dah>, the word of refusal after a verb, and <ni>, let us, written as one word: let us not do it, I had better not) (j:dah/ni) (r:zd:24427/zd:14585) (q:draft)
dahni = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/time) (w:day of sorrow/time of mourning) (d:<dah>, grieve, and <ni>, day, written as one word; paired with {nopni}, a day of joy) (j:dah/ni) (r:zd:9448/zd:24167) (q:draft)
Dahpa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:social) (w:Dahpa) (d:main character of well-known Zomi folk tales, told as {Dahpa tangthu}; {Dahpa khuang}, the drum of Dahpa, is used as a saying) (r:ts:4831/zd:19501) (q:draft, low confidence)
dahpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:condolence/sympathy) (d:<dahpih>, mourn with, with the noun suffix <na>: sympathy shown to the family of someone who has died; {dahpihna pulak} is express condolence) (b:dahpih) (r:ts:1343/zd:21462/zd:18234) (q:draft)
dahpihna ipulak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/media) (w:we express our condolences) (d:<dahpihna>, condolence, and <ipulak>, we make known: the closing formula of a death notice issued by a group, followed by <hi>; the group is named before it with <mintawh>, in the name of) (r:zd:25872) (q:draft)
DAHPIHNA LAI = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:condolence letter/letter of condolence/message of sympathy) (d:<dahpihna>, condolence, and <lai>, letter: a letter of sympathy that a person or an association sends or publishes for the family of someone who has died; it is used as the heading of such a letter, with the sender before it and <pan>, from) (r:zd:12629/zd:19657) (q:draft)
Dahpihna Lianpitawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:with deep sympathy/with deepest condolences) (d:<dahpihna>, condolence, and <Lianpitawh>, with great: the closing formula of a message of condolence, written before the name of the sender) (r:zd:21591) (q:draft)
dai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:quiet/calm/silent/still) (d:without noise or movement, of people, wind or sea; also as a verb, be quiet, fall silent, die down; {dai takin} is quietly, <dai dide> utterly still) (s:daii/gamdai/daicip) (r:19.107.29) (q:draft)
dai dide = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be utterly silent/fall silent/keep still) (d:<dai>, quiet, and <dide>, the adverb of stillness that goes with it: be completely silent, say nothing at all; with <in> and <om> it means stay silent) (r:zd:22059/zd:22683/zd:23162) (q:draft)
daidai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:hastily/in a rush) (d:placed after a verb: do it at once and eagerly, without waiting or thinking, as someone who fears to lose something) (r:zd:12541/zd:20581) (q:draft, low confidence)
daidam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature/time) (w:cold/chilly) (d:cold and still, said of the winter season in {phalbi daidam}, the cold of winter) (r:zd:17215/zd:22962) (q:draft, low confidence)
daidide = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:dai dide) (r:zd:25908/zd:15082) (q:draft)
daih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:last/be enough/go far) (d:be enough for a need or hold out for a length of time, mostly negated as {daih lo} or {daih zo lo}; said of time, money or a state, not of noise) (r:zd:25915/zd:11163/zd:23893) (q:draft)
daihlaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/home) (w:get an electric shock/be electrocuted) (d:be struck by an electric current; {daihlaih in si} is die of an electric shock) (o:Burmese, dat laik) (r:zd:14856/zd:14662) (q:draft)
dailen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:go to the toilet/relieve oneself/defecate) (d:polite word for emptying the bowels; {dailen buk} is a toilet) (r:zd:25478/zd:23727) (q:draft)
dailenbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/body) (w:toilet/restroom/lavatory) (d:a toilet, the room or the seat; a polite word, from <dailen>, relieve oneself, and <buk>, hut) (s:ekbuk) (r:zd:12337/zd:12181/zd:17301) (q:draft)
dailengbuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/body) (j:dailenbuk) (r:zd:13288/zd:17694) (q:draft)
dailengding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:to relieve oneself/to go to the toilet) (d:{daileng}, go out to relieve oneself, with <ding> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: in order to go to the toilet) (r:zd:16617/zd:21793) (q:draft)
dailing = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/home) (w:barbed wire fence/barbed wire) (d:<daai>, fence, with <ling>, thorn: a fence of thorns; {sik dailing} is a barbed wire fence, as along a border) (r:ts:5871) (q:draft)
daipam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:the lowly/the destitute/outcast) (d:a person of the lowest standing who lives at the margin of the community, named together with the poor, widows and orphans, as in {mizawng daipam}; apparently from the edge outside the village fence) (r:zd:14552/zd:13354) (q:draft, low confidence)
daipamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:the lowly/the marginalised/the needy) (d:people at the edge of society, with the plural <te>; named after <mizawng>, the poor, or <meigong>, widows, as in {mizawng daipamte}, the poor and lowly) (r:zd:21978/zd:21761) (q:draft)
daisakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:belittling/ridicule/putting down) (d:<daisak>, dishonor, with the noun ending <na>: words or acts that make a person look small) (b:daisak) (r:zd:10823) (q:draft, low confidence)
daitansakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/social) (w:committal service/burial service) (d:a part of a funeral named beside or in place of <vuina>, burial, held at the cemetery; it seems to be the service by which the dead is laid to rest) (r:zd:11080/zd:24029) (q:draft, low confidence)
dakdak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:stare/gaze about) (d:after <khua>, the verb <dak>, look, said twice: sit looking about blankly, not knowing what to do or say; not the strengthening word that follows a descriptive word) (s:khuadak) (r:zd:16148/zd:14530) (q:draft, low confidence)
Dakdung = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Dakdung) (d:a place name of the Tedim area, used of a village and of a town quarter; {Dakdung mi} is a person from Dakdung) (r:zd:22136) (q:draft, low confidence)
daklam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:gong dance) (d:a traditional Zomi dance, from <dak>, gong, and <laam>, dance, as in {Zomi ngeina daklam}) (r:zd:15865) (q:draft, low confidence)
Dakota = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Dakota) (d:in {South Dakota} and {North Dakota}, two states of the United States) (r:zd:25189/zd:20334) (q:draft)
daktal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:gong/small gong) (d:a metal instrument that is sounded with <tum>, carried with the drum and the gun in festival processions and beaten by the village crier when he calls out a notice; the exact kind of gong is not confirmed) (r:zd:25393/zd:15996) (q:draft, low confidence)
dal = (i:4) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:prevent/block/hinder/stop) (d:stand in the way of a person or of a thing that is coming and keep it from going on, as in {natna dal}, prevent a disease; here what is named before {dal} is the one stopped, not the one protected) (r:zd:24253/zd:24918/zd:23659) (q:draft)
dalan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:informer/spy) (d:a person who secretly passes information to the army or the authorities; explained in the articles as {thupuak sim}) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:25357/zd:25314) (q:draft)
dalcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:block off/cordon off/shut in) (d:<dal>, block, with <cip>, tightly: block the way completely so that nobody gets through, as police do with a crowd or a ravine does round a camp) (j:dal/cip) (r:zd:16637) (q:draft)
Dalkhai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Dalkhai) (d:village in the Tonzang area of Chin State, near the border with India) (r:zd:15743/zd:19516) (q:draft)
dalkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/work) (w:one sheet/one note) (d:<dal>, counting word for flat things, and <khat>, one, written as one word: one sheet of paper or one banknote) (j:dal/khat) (r:zd:20287/zd:20911) (q:draft)
dalkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:prevent/ward off in advance) (d:<dal>, shield, with <khol>, beforehand: keep something bad, such as illness or damage, from happening by acting before it comes) (b:dal) (r:zd:22364/zd:12121) (q:draft)
dalkholhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/everyday) (w:precaution/prevention) (d:<dal> and <kholhna> written as one word: a guarding against harm beforehand; mostly {ki dalkholhna}, and {dalkholhna in} is as a precaution) (j:dal/kholhna) (r:zd:16061/zd:19927) (q:draft)
Dallas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Dallas) (d:city in the state of Texas in the United States, where a Zomi community lives) (r:zd:11899/zd:19271) (q:draft)
dalna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health/everyday) (w:prevention/protection/defence) (d:the act of keeping something harmful off, not a thing that screens: <natna dalna> is the prevention of disease, <dalna zatui> a vaccine, and {thautang dalna} bulletproof) (s:kidalna) (r:zd:24918/zd:20640/zd:25191) (q:draft)
dalna zatui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:vaccine/vaccination) (d:<dalna>, barrier or prevention, and <zatui>, medicine: medicine that prevents a disease; in full {natna dalna zatui}, and to give it by injection is {dalna zatui sut}) (r:zd:24918/zd:24276) (q:draft)
dalnih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:two sheets/two layers/two slices) (d:<dal.3>, the counting word for flat things, and <nih> written as one word: two sheets, layers or slices) (j:dal/nih) (r:zd:21633/zd:19423) (q:draft)
dalthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:can prevent/be able to prevent/protect from) (d:<dal> and <thei> written as one word: able to prevent or keep off something) (j:dal/thei) (r:zd:16259/zd:21048) (q:draft)
daltheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to prevent/can block) (d:<dal> and <theih> written as one word: be able to prevent or block, before <nadingin> and <zia>) (j:dal/theih) (r:zd:13184/zd:20349) (q:draft)
dalzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:be able to prevent/ward off/hold back) (d:<dal>, shield or block, and <zo>, manage to, written as one word: be able to keep off a danger such as illness, storm or fire) (j:dal/zo) (r:zd:19915/zd:21119) (q:draft)
dam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:be well/be healed/recover) (d:be in good health or get well again; of a sickness, wound or sorrow, heal; {na dam hiam}, are you well, is a greeting) (a:nat) (r:24.8.18) (q:draft)
dam = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:nature) (w:cold/cool) (d:of the weather, with <khua>: {khua dam} is it is cold, as in <khuadam>; not the sense of health) (r:zd:25454) (q:draft, low confidence)
damaih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:robbery/robber) (d:robbery with force or a weapon, and also the robber; {damaih taih} is to rob someone and {damaih te} are robbers) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:19237/zd:11410) (q:draft)
Damansara = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Damansara) (d:an area near Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia where Zomi live; {Kota Damansara} is one part of it) (r:zd:21282) (q:draft)
Damascus = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/religion) (j:Damaskas) (r:zd:21027/zd:10890) (q:draft)
damdam = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:slowly/gradually/gently) (d:before <in> or <a>, at a slow pace or little by little, as {damdam in pai}, go slowly; the same word as <damdamin> written apart, and not the rumbling of sense 1) (s:damdamin) (r:zd:22775/zd:14824/zd:22658) (q:draft)
damdawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:cure/remedy) (d:what heals a sickness or a trouble, its remedy; from <dam>, be healed) (r:zd:12436/zd:25670) (q:draft, low confidence)
damhawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:drive slowly/slow down) (d:drive a vehicle slowly or more slowly; <dam> here is the word of <damdam>, slowly, not be well, with <hawl>, drive) (r:zd:17455/zd:12904) (q:draft)
damiah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:robber/armed robber/robbery) (d:a person who robs by force or threat, and the robbery itself; often paired with <guta>, thief, and {damiah taih} is to commit a robbery) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:15056/zd:19320/zd:17030) (q:draft)
damiah ataih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:rob/commit robbery/hold up) (d:<damiah>, robbery, and <ataih>, hit, the form of <taih> with <a>: commit a robbery, hold someone up; the place or the victim stands before it, and before a noun it means who robbed) (r:zd:14917/zd:20191) (q:draft)
damiah kitaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:be robbed/be held up) (d:<damiah>, robber, and <kitaih.2>, from Burmese: an armed robbery takes place; the place or person robbed stands before it, and with a plural subject it means to carry out a robbery) (r:zd:15913/zd:12063) (q:draft)
damiah lut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:be robbed/robbers break in/armed robbery) (d:<damiah>, robber, as the subject of <lut>, enter: robbers break into a place, a robbery takes place there; the place stands before it, with <ah> or without a marker, as in {Bank khat damiah lut}, a bank is robbed) (r:zd:17661/zd:17260/zd:11868) (q:draft)
damiah lutin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:rob/hold up/break in and rob) (d:<damiah>, robber, and <lutin>, entering: robbers break into a place and rob it; in news headlines it stands after the place with <ah> or <sungah> and before what was taken) (r:zd:11352/zd:15084) (q:draft)
damiah taihin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:commit robbery/rob/hold up) (d:<damiah>, robber, and <taihin>, from the Burmese expression for committing robbery: robbing by force; the place or person robbed stands before it and the main verb of the sentence follows) (r:zd:11130/zd:15178) (q:draft)
damiahpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:robber/armed robber) (d:<damiah>, robber or robbery, with <pa>, the man who: a man who robs by force) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:20522/zd:17260) (q:draft)
damkikthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:can recover/can get well again) (d:<damkik> and <thei> written as one word: be able to become healthy again) (j:damkik/thei) (r:zd:24276/zd:18093) (q:draft)
damkim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:all be well/be wholly well) (d:<dam> and <kim>, all or fully, written as one word: all are in good health, or well in every part; used in greetings and wishes) (j:dam/kim) (r:zd:19168/zd:20102) (q:draft)
damlai = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday/family) (w:still alive/alive/living) (d:<dam> in the sense of being alive, with <lai>, still: still living; {a damlai in} is while he is alive, in his lifetime; the other sense is of being unhurt) (r:zd:17309/zd:25909/zd:24126) (q:draft)
damlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:sick/ill/unwell) (d:<dam> and <lo> written as one word: not well, sick; {damlo te} are the sick, patients) (s:cina) (j:dam/lo) (r:zd:23528/zd:23538/zd:19846) (q:draft)
damloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be unwell/be sick/be ill) (d:<dam> and <loh> written as one word: not be well, the form of {dam lo} used before words such as <hun>, <lai> and <ciangin>; {damloh hun} is a time of sickness) (j:dam/loh) (r:zd:12292/zd:20162/zd:22469) (q:draft)
damlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:illness/sickness/ill health) (d:<dam> and <lohna> written as one word: the state of not being well, an illness or disorder) (s:natna) (j:dam/lohna) (r:zd:23799/zd:23266) (q:draft)
damlote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:the sick/patients/sick people) (d:<damlo>, sick, with the plural <te>: those who are sick, patients; {lungsim damlote} are the mentally ill) (b:damlo) (r:zd:11206/zd:22928/zd:10743) (q:draft)
damlua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be very glad/be very pleased) (d:<dam>, be glad, and <lua>, very, written as one word, said of the heart, <lung>, and often followed by <mahmah>) (j:dam/lua) (r:zd:19166/zd:20289) (q:draft)
dammahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be very glad/be very well) (d:<dam> with <mahmah>, very, written as one word: after <lung>, heart, as in {kalung dammahmah}, I am very glad or thankful; of the body, be in very good health) (j:dam/mahmah) (r:zd:19619/zd:16676) (q:draft)
Dammaw = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday/social) (w:hello/how are you) (d:<dam>, be well, and the question word <maw>, written as one word: are you well, the usual Zolai greeting) (j:dam/maw) (r:zd:16031/zd:12196) (q:draft)
dammawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:sick/ill/unwell) (d:not well, from <dam>, be well; also the sick and sickness, as in {dammawh puakna motor}, a vehicle that carries the sick, an ambulance) (r:zd:11648/zd:15748) (q:draft, low confidence)
dammawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:sickness/ill health/illness) (d:<dammawh>, sick, with the noun ending <na>: the state of being unwell) (s:cidamlohna/natna) (b:dammawh) (r:zd:12112/zd:11648) (q:draft)
dampak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:recover quickly/get well soon) (d:<dam>, get well, with <pak>, quickly, written as one word; mostly negative, {a dampak kei leh}, if it does not get better soon) (j:dam/pak) (r:zd:24276/zd:21306) (q:draft)
Dampi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Dampi) (d:a Zomi village, written {Dampi khua} in the articles) (r:zd:14751) (q:draft, low confidence)
dampih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:still be alive with/live on with) (d:<dam>, be well, and <pih>, together with, written as one word: remain alive and well with others; with <hong> said of parents or elders who are still living among their family) (j:dam/pih) (r:zd:24119/zd:14910) (q:draft)
damsawt = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:live long) (d:<dam> and <sawt> written as one word: be well for a long time, live long; {damsawt hen} is the wish long live) (j:dam/sawt) (r:zd:15493/zd:19260) (q:draft)
damsung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:lifetime/whole life) (d:<dam>, be well and so be alive, and <sung>, during, written as one word: the time that one lives, as long as one lives) (j:dam/sung) (r:zd:20716/zd:24636) (q:draft)
damte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/everyday) (w:the healthy/the living/those who are well) (d:<dam>, be well, with the plural <te>, usually after <a>: those who are well, or those who are alive; {kum sawtpi a damte} are those who live long) (b:dam) (r:zd:25178/ts:7513) (q:draft)
damtui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:water of well-being/healing water) (d:<dam>, be well, with <tui>, water; a word of songs and fine speech: {nunnop damtui luang} is that a good life flows like water) (r:zd:16588) (q:draft, low confidence)
dan siam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:know how to/be good at) (d:<dan>, way, and <siam>, skilled: after a verb, know the way to do it, be good at doing it, as in {lai-at dan siam}, be good at writing; {dan siam kei} is not know how to) (r:zd:21626/zd:21340/zd:18952) (q:draft)
dana = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as if/like/in the manner of) (d:<dan>, manner, with the ending <a>, written as one word and placed after a verb or noun: in the way of, as though) (j:dan/a) (r:zd:20172/zd:20060/zd:11135) (q:draft)
danah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in the way/on how) (d:<dan> and <ah> written as one word after a verb: in or on the way something is done, as in {i makaih danah kinga}, it depends on how we lead) (j:dan/ah) (r:zd:10938/zd:25139) (q:draft)
danbel = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:as for the way) (d:<dan>, manner, and the topic particle <bel> written as one word after a verb: as for the way or extent of it) (j:dan/bel) (r:zd:11775/zd:16337) (q:draft)
dandan = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just as/according to/however) (d:<dan>, manner, doubled: in whatever way, exactly in keeping with what the verb before it says, as in {amau ut dandan in}, just as they please, and {ngaihsut dandan}, just as one thinks; not the trail of something that passes) (s:bangbang) (r:zd:23896/zd:20403/zd:12341) (q:draft)
dandanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just as/according to/in whatever way) (d:<dan>, manner, said twice with <in>: after a verb, just in the way that, exactly according to; {i ut dandanin} is just as we please; compare <danin>) (b:dan) (r:zd:9433/zd:24236/zd:15697) (q:draft)
danding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:way to/how to) (d:<dan>, way, and <ding> written as one word after a verb: the way something is to be done, how to do it; common in headings) (j:dan/ding) (r:zd:25923/zd:25180/zd:25924) (q:draft)
dangdang = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:other/various other) (d:<dang> other said twice for several things, placed after a noun, often with <te> after it, or as {a dangdang}, the others: the other ones, not the one spoken of) (s:dang) (r:zd:12264/zd:20586/zd:20534) (q:draft)
dangin = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in another/in other/otherwise) (d:<dang>, other, with {-in} after a noun other than <ni>: by another one or in another one, as {kammal dangin}, in other words, and {a lam dangin}, in another way) (r:zd:23432/zd:19968/zd:12925) (q:draft)
dangkhat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:another/a different one) (d:<dang>, other, and <khat>, one, written as one word after a noun: another; {a dangkhat} is the other one) (j:dang/khat) (r:zd:23394/zd:21796/zd:23943) (q:draft)
dangkhatpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the other one) (d:<dangkhat> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, after <a>: as for the other one) (j:dangkhat/pen) (r:zd:22019) (q:draft)
danglai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:former times/old days/days gone by) (d:time long past, mostly after <ni>, day: {ni danglai in} is in the old days, in former times) (r:zd:25054/zd:11697/zd:18952) (q:draft)
dangnal = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:eloquent/fluent/smooth-tongued) (d:fluent and ready in speech, said of a person who speaks well and boldly before others) (r:zd:16897) (q:draft)
dangpan = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:from another/from other) (d:<dang>, other, and <pan>, from, written as one word after a noun: from another one) (j:dang/pan) (r:zd:12460/zd:21876) (q:draft)
dangtaak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/food/body) (j:dangtak) (r:zd:22643/zd:22650) (q:draft)
dangtak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/food/body) (w:thirsty) (d:be thirsty, often paired with <gilkial>, hungry; also thirst) (s:tuiduh/duh) (r:20.25.25) (q:draft)
dangtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:with another/with other) (d:<dang>, other, and <tawh>, with, written as one word after a noun: with another one, with other ones) (j:dang/tawh) (r:zd:24276/zd:17618) (q:draft)
dangten = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:others/the others) (d:<dangte>, others, with the subject marker <in> written as one word, short for {dangte in}: the others, as the ones who act) (j:dangte/in) (r:zd:22065/zd:24035) (q:draft)
dangtuamtuam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:various other/other different) (d:<dang>, other, and <tuamtuam>, of various kinds, written as one word after a noun or after <a>: various others, other kinds) (j:dang/tuamtuam) (r:zd:20657/zd:25790/zd:24289) (q:draft)
Dangwangi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:politics/travel) (w:Dang Wangi) (d:Dang Wangi, a district of Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia with a police station and lockup, named in notices about Zomi who are detained there) (r:zd:16799/zd:22825) (q:draft)
Danial = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (j:Daniel) (r:zd:23386/zd:23286) (q:draft)
Danielte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Daniel and his companions/Daniel and the like) (d:the name <Daniel> with the plural <te>: Daniel and those with him, or at the end of a list of names, people such as Daniel) (b:Daniel) (j:Daniel/te) (r:zd:24199/zd:9445) (q:draft)
dankhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:a kind of/as if) (d:<dan>, way, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a sort of, something like; with <in>, as if, in the manner of) (j:dan/khat) (r:zd:22782/zd:11945) (q:draft)
danlian = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just as/exactly the way) (d:<dan>, way or like, with <lian>, here exactly and not large, written as one word after a verb: in exactly the way that, just as) (r:zd:12630/zd:24731) (q:draft, low confidence)
danmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just like/in the very way) (d:<dan>, manner, with the emphatic <mah>, written as one word and followed by <in>: in just the way, exactly like; {kei danmah in} is just like me) (j:dan/mah) (r:zd:19205/zd:24124) (q:draft)
dann = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/education) (w:punishment/penalty) (d:what is laid on someone for a wrong, by a court or a school; {dann tuak} is be punished and {dann pia} is punish) (s:gawtna) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:23616/zd:19318) (q:draft)
danpen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:the way/the manner) (d:<dan>, way or manner, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: as for the way of it) (j:dan/pen) (r:zd:25223/zd:22758) (q:draft)
danpiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:punishment/penalty) (d:<dan>, here punishment, with <piakna>, giving: the giving of a punishment, a penalty) (r:zd:11553/zd:19108) (q:draft)
danteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:the whole manner/all the ways) (d:<dan> and <teng> written as one word: all of how something goes or is done, the whole course of it) (j:dan/teng) (r:zd:22122) (q:draft)
DaNu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/social) (w:Danu) (d:the Danu, a people of Shan State in Burma; mostly written {Danu}) (r:zd:25105/zd:23014) (q:draft)
danuh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:their way/the way they do) (d:<dan>, way or manner, and the plural marker <uh> written as one word after a verb or verbal noun: the way they do it) (j:dan/uh) (r:zd:20176) (q:draft)
danzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the way also/ways too) (d:<dan>, way or manner, with <zong>, also, written as one word after a verbal noun: the way of doing it too, as in {danzong atuamtuam}, the ways too are various) (j:dan/zong) (r:zd:18056/zd:11729) (q:draft)
dapdap = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/body) (d:placed after a verb to describe a heavy sound made again and again, as of snoring, {naksiat dapdap}, or of sobbing, {kapkhia dapdap}) (r:zd:16340) (q:draft, low confidence)
Dashcam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it/travel) (w:dashcam/dashboard camera) (d:video camera fitted in a vehicle that records the road) (o:English) (r:zd:19530/zd:12982/zd:18116) (q:draft)
dat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/food/nature) (w:substance/element/nutrient) (d:a substance that something contains, placed after its name: {Potassium dat} is potassium and {Vitamin C dat} is vitamin C; also a chemical, and in {dat-line} electric power) (o:Burmese, dat) (r:zd:20004/zd:21168/zd:22499) (q:draft)
data = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it/education) (w:data/information/figures) (d:collected facts and figures, also the internet data of a mobile phone) (o:English) (r:zd:22802/zd:24321/zd:17607) (q:draft)
datdat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:one after another/in a stream/steadily) (d:placed after a verb: the action goes on in an unbroken row, one after another, said of tears that fall drop after drop and of people who follow each other) (r:zd:23240/zd:12928/zd:17939) (q:draft, low confidence)
datlaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/home) (w:be electrocuted/get an electric shock) (d:be struck by electric current; also as a noun, electric shock or electrocution) (o:Burmese, dat laik) (r:zd:16249/zd:11362) (q:draft)
datmei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:torch/flashlight) (d:a hand lamp that works with batteries; {datmei de} is shine a torch) (o:Burmese, dat mi) (r:zd:15996/zd:11924/zd:17428) (q:draft)
datsa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/food) (w:mineral salt/mineral/electrolyte) (d:the salts and minerals that the body needs and that come from rock and water; {datsa tui} is a drink of rehydration salts) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:25148/zd:23729) (q:draft, low confidence)
datsi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:petrol/gasoline/fuel) (d:fuel for motor vehicles; {datsi sai} is a filling station) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:20668/zd:18943) (q:draft)
Datsian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:film/movie/cinema) (d:a moving picture, and the film business; {datsian zung} is a cinema, the hall where films are shown) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:25589) (q:draft)
datsisai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:petrol station/filling station) (d:a place where fuel for vehicles is sold, from Burmese <datsi>, petrol, and <sai>, shop) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:15366/zd:16826) (q:draft)
datsithawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/travel) (w:petrol bottle/bottle of petrol) (d:<datsi>, petrol, and <thawl>, bottle, written as one word: a bottle filled with petrol) (j:datsi/thawl) (r:zd:15029) (q:draft)
datt = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/food) (j:dat) (r:zd:14826) (q:draft)
Datuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:Datuk) (d:Malaysian title of honour, placed before the name of the man who holds it) (o:Malay) (r:zd:16205/zd:17605) (q:draft)
dau = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be faint/be dim/fade/weaken) (d:be faint, dull or weak, or grow so, said of colours and letters that are hard to see and of love, concern or a movement that is fading; without <pai>, and often followed by <mahmah> or <lua>) (r:zd:22356/zd:24862/zd:22713) (q:draft)
daudau = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:one after another/in a steady stream/on and on) (d:placed after a verb: the action goes on steadily or things come one after another without a break, as thoughts that keep rising or words read straight through) (r:zd:22595/zd:25773) (q:draft, low confidence)
daupailoh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:not prosper/not succeed) (d:<daupai>, prosper, and the negative <loh> written as one word: not doing well; {daupailoh man-a} is because of not prospering) (j:daupai/loh) (r:zd:22034) (q:draft)
Davao = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Davao/Davao City) (d:the largest city of the southern Philippines) (r:zd:16952) (q:draft)
Davuih = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (j:David) (r:zd:23138) (q:draft)
Daw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:Mrs/Madam/Ms) (d:Burmese title of respect placed before the name of a grown woman) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:15122/zd:20627) (q:draft)
Dawangi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/politics) (w:Dang Wangi) (d:an area of Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia with a police station; {Dawangi lockup} is the police lockup there) (r:zd:22413) (q:draft, low confidence)
Dawbon = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Dawbon) (d:a township of <Yangon> in Myanmar) (r:zd:11110) (q:draft)
Dawei = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Dawei) (d:city in the far south of Myanmar, capital of Tanintharyi Region; also the people of that area) (r:zd:14726/zd:12888) (q:draft)
dawhna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:receiving/holding out to receive) (d:<dawh>, hold out to receive, with the noun ending <na>: the act of receiving what is given, as in {thupha dawhna}, the receiving of blessing, and {dawhna hai}, the cup held out to receive) (r:zd:21148/zd:25115) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawihang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:demon/evil spirit) (d:<dawi>, demon, in the pair {dawihang kauhang}, the demons and harmful spirits that are driven out of house and village at the <Khuado> festival) (r:zd:15996) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawinupi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:she-devil/wicked woman) (d:<dawi>, demon, and <nupi>, woman, written as one word: a demon woman, said in news reports of a woman who has done something cruel) (j:dawi/nupi) (r:zd:15994) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawl = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home) (w:floor) (d:a floor or storey of a building)
dawl = (i:4) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:stage/level/phase/tier) (d:a step or rank in a process or an order, not in a building: a stage of a plan or of a trial, as {dawl masa}, the first stage, or a level of government, as {gambup dawl}, the national level) (r:zd:21803/zd:25078/zd:24417) (q:draft)
dawldawl = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:level by level/in stages/step by step) (d:<dawl>, level, said twice: at each level, one level after another; usually {a dawldawl in}) (b:dawl) (r:zd:22910/zd:25790) (q:draft)
dawlkhatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:first floor) (d:<dawl>, floor, and <khatna>, first, written as one word: the first floor of a building) (j:dawl/khatna) (r:zd:17385/zd:17017) (q:draft)
dawlnih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:home/travel) (w:two-storey/double-decker) (d:<dawl> and <nih> written as one word: with two floors, said of a house or a bus; {dawlnih a pha} is that has two storeys) (j:dawl/nih) (r:zd:17677/zd:24029/zd:19445) (q:draft)
dawlnihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:second floor/second storey) (d:<dawl>, floor, and <nihna>, second, written as one word) (j:dawl/nihna) (r:zd:20425/zd:17164) (q:draft)
dawlthum = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home/everyday) (w:three storeys/three levels) (d:<dawl>, floor or level, and <thum>, three, written as one word: of a building, three storeys high; also three levels or classes of people) (j:dawl/thum) (r:zd:17794/zd:15514) (q:draft)
dawlthumna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:third floor/third storey) (d:<dawl>, floor, and <thumna>, third, written as one word) (j:dawl/thumna) (r:zd:16876) (q:draft)
dawm = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be careful/take care/be sparing with) (d:after <ki>, written as two words for <kidawm>: watch oneself, take care, and with a thing named before it be careful or sparing with it, as in {zu leh za ki dawm}, be careful with drink and tobacco) (s:kidawm) (r:zd:24276/zd:24742/zd:19525) (q:draft)
dawn = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:meet/welcome/go to meet) (d:go out to meet someone who is coming) (s:dawntuah/kimu) (q:draft)
dawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:drink) (d:take a drink; {tui dawn} is to drink water and {zu dawn} to drink wine or beer) (q:draft)
dawn = (i:4) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:answer/reply/respond) (d:give an answer, the form of <dawng> used before <kik>, back: {dawn kik} is answer back, and {dawn kikna} is a reply) (r:ts:5635/zd:22652/zd:13217) (q:draft)
dawna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:answer/reply) (d:a spelling of <dawnna>, what is said in reply, set beside <dotna>, question, as in {dotna dawna}, questions and answers; not the top of a hill) (s:dawnna) (r:zd:21063/zd:23780) (q:draft)
dawnbang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (d:word of songs and elevated speech used before <tuah>, meet: {dawnbang tuah} is to meet one another or come together again; its own sense apart from that phrase is not clear) (r:zd:11110/zd:14507) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawndan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:way of answering/answer/response) (d:<dawn>, here the form of <dawng>, answer, with <dan>, manner, written as one word: the way in which someone answers a question or responds) (j:dawn/dan) (r:zd:9447/zd:12196) (q:draft)
dawnden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:always welcome/keep welcoming) (d:<dawn>, go to meet or welcome, and <den>, always, written as one word: welcome someone every time he comes) (j:dawn/den) (r:zd:23888) (q:draft)
