dawnding = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:food) (w:for drinking/to drink) (d:<dawn>, drink, and <ding> written as one word: that is to be drunk, for drinking; {dawnding tui} is drinking water, and beside <nekding> it means things to eat and to drink) (j:dawn/ding) (r:zd:12042/zd:17120/zd:17575) (q:draft)
dawng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:answer/reply) (d:give an answer to a person or to a question) (s:dawngkik) (a:dong/dot) (r:24.21.3) (q:draft)
dawnga = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:answer/reply) (d:<dawng>, answer, with the linking <a> written as one word: answered and) (j:dawng/a) (r:zd:9219/zd:17391) (q:draft)
dawngkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/media) (w:one song/one verse/one piece) (d:a counting word for songs and stanzas and <khat>, one, written as one word after <la>: {la dawngkhat} is one song or one verse of a song; the first part is spelled like <dawng>, answer, but is not that verb) (j:dawng/khat) (r:zd:14507/zd:19843) (q:draft)
dawnglo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not answer/not reply) (d:<dawng> and <lo> written as one word: does not answer) (j:dawng/lo) (r:zd:22159/zd:19805) (q:draft)
dawnhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:food) (w:good to drink/fit to drink) (d:<dawn>, drink, with the suffix <huai>: worth drinking, right to drink; {dawnhuai lo} is should not be drunk) (r:zd:22019/zd:17152) (q:draft)
dawnkik = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:reply/answer/answer back/respond) (d:<dawn.4>, the form of <dawng>, answer, with <kik>, back: give an answer in return to a question, a letter or a prayer; not {dawnkik}, drink again) (s:dawngkik) (r:zd:15234/zd:22415/zd:19442) (q:draft)
dawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:not drink) (d:<dawn>, drink, and <lo>, not, written as one word) (j:dawn/lo) (r:zd:24036/zd:22019/zd:19749) (q:draft)
dawnloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:not drink/not drinking) (d:<dawn>, drink, and <loh>, not, written as one word: not drinking, the form used before a following word, as in {zu dawnloh}, not drinking alcohol) (j:dawn/loh) (r:zd:9423/zd:24276) (q:draft)
dawnna = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:answer/reply/response) (d:what is said or written in reply, from <dawng>, answer; paired with <dotna>, question, as {dotna leh dawnna}, questions and answers; not drinking and not a meeting) (r:zd:25111/zd:24966/zd:20160) (q:draft)
dawnnate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:answers/replies) (d:plural of <dawnna>, answer; {dotna leh dawnnate} is questions and answers) (b:dawnna) (r:zd:15794/zd:24563) (q:draft)
dawnpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:from the top/from the tip) (d:<dawn>, top or tip, and <pan>, from, written as one word and placed after the thing named: from the top of it) (j:dawn/pan) (r:zd:10945/zd:16101) (q:draft)
dawnpan = (i:2) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:drink only then/start to drink) (d:<dawn>, drink, with <pan>, here only then, begin to: drink only after the time named, as in an instruction to drink an hour after eating) (r:zd:16665) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawntheih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:drink/beverage) (d:<dawn>, drink, and <theih>, can, written as one word: something that can be drunk, a drink; often paired with <nektheih>, food) (j:dawn/theih) (r:zd:16776/zd:17897) (q:draft)
dawnzel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:drink regularly/drink now and then) (d:<dawn>, drink, and <zel> written as one word: drink again and again) (j:dawn/zel) (r:zd:21032/zd:13121) (q:draft)
dawnzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:way of drinking/drinking habits) (d:<dawn>, drink, with <zia>, way, written as one word, often paired with <nekzia>: how one drinks) (j:dawn/zia) (r:zd:19676/zd:24276) (q:draft)
dawnzia = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (w:way of answering/manner of reply) (d:<dawn>, a form of <dawng>, answer, with <zia>, way, written as one word: how someone answers a question) (j:dawn/zia) (r:zd:25339) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:contact/inquire/approach) (d:get in touch with a person or an office about a matter, to ask or to report; {vai dawp} is bring a matter to an office) (r:zd:23538/zd:24119/zd:23543) (q:draft)
dawptheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:can contact/can inquire) (d:<dawp>, contact or inquire, with <theih>, be able, written as one word; {dawptheih ni} is the days on which an office may be approached) (j:dawp/theih) (r:zd:10892) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawtgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:stab repeatedly/stab severely) (d:<dawt>, stab, with <gawp>, severely, written as one word: stab again and again or stab badly) (j:dawt/gawp) (r:zd:15531/zd:21030) (q:draft)
dawtkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:pierce/prick/stab) (d:<dawt>, pierce, with <kha>, happen to: of a sharp thing, come to pierce or prick a part of the body, often by accident) (j:dawt/kha) (r:zd:21954/zd:17085) (q:draft)
dawtliam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/health) (w:stab and wound/wound by stabbing) (d:<dawt> and <liam> written as one word: stab a person so that he is wounded, beside <dawtlum>, stab to death) (j:dawt/liam) (r:zd:15537/zd:17641) (q:draft)
dawtliamgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/media) (w:stab and wound badly/stab severely) (d:<dawt>, stab, and <liamgawp>, be badly wounded, written as one word: stab someone so that he is badly wounded) (j:dawt/liamgawp) (r:zd:20472) (q:draft)
dawtlum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:stab to death) (d:<dawt>, stab, with <lum>: stab a person so that he dies) (b:dawt) (r:zd:15537/zd:21352) (q:draft)
dawtlumsa = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/media) (w:stabbed to death) (d:<dawtlum> with <sa>, already done, written as one word; {aki dawtlumsa in} is having been stabbed to death, said of how a body is found) (r:zd:12201/zd:11825) (q:draft)
dawtlup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:stab/stab down) (d:<dawt>, stab, with <lup>, lie down: stab a person so that the person falls; {dawtlup thuak} is be stabbed) (r:zd:11814) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawtlupna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:stabbing) (d:<dawtlup> with the noun ending {-na}: the act or place of stabbing a person down; usually after <ki>, as in {ki dawtlupna}, the stabbing) (b:dawtlup) (r:zd:13253/zd:22030) (q:draft)
dawtsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:stab) (d:<dawt>, stab, with <sak> written as one word: stab a person in a named part of the body with a knife) (j:dawt/sak) (r:zd:18244/zd:20055) (q:draft)
dawtsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:stab/stab down into) (d:<dawt>, stab, and <suk>, down into, written as one word: drive a knife down into the body) (j:dawt/suk) (r:zd:16826) (q:draft)
