deihbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:wish/wish well/favour) (d:<deih>, want, with <bawl>: wish that something may be so for someone, as in greetings, or be well disposed to someone) (s:deihsak) (r:zd:16813/zd:15187) (q:draft)
deihbek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:only want/want only) (d:<deih>, want, and <bek>, only, written as one word: only want, want nothing but) (j:deih/bek) (r:zd:25919/zd:16906) (q:draft)
deihdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:wish/preference/will/taste) (d:<deih> and <dan> written as one word: the way someone wants a thing to be, what one wishes or prefers; {Pasian deihdan} is the will of God) (j:deih/dan) (r:zd:25923/zd:24217/zd:23655) (q:draft)
deihkaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be biased/slant/take one's own way) (d:<deih>, want, with <kaih>, pull: draw a matter toward what one wants, take or tell it in a one-sided way; in {deihkaih ing} a writer says what he wishes and urges) (r:zd:15859/zd:25569) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihkaihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:bias/partiality/self-will) (d:<deihkaih> with the noun suffix {-na}: pulling a matter toward what one wants, bias or one's own will) (b:deihkaih) (r:zd:24804/zd:25567) (q:draft)
deihkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not want/dislike/refuse) (d:<deih>, want, and the negative <kei>, written as one word: do not want) (s:deihlo) (j:deih/kei) (r:zd:23479/zd:19257) (q:draft)
deihkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:something wanted/what one wants) (d:<deih> and <khat> written as one word: a thing that one wants; {na deihkhat} is what you want) (j:deih/khat) (r:zd:19983/zd:23706) (q:draft)
deihkhempeuh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:all that one wants/everything one wants) (d:<deih>, want, and <khempeuh>, all, written as one word after <na>, <i> or <a>: everything that you, we or they want) (j:deih/khempeuh) (r:zd:20932/zd:21110) (q:draft)
deihleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one wants/if you want) (d:<deih> and <leh> written as one word: if someone wants or wishes for something) (j:deih/leh) (r:zd:21044/zd:13340) (q:draft)
deihlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not want/dislike/reject) (d:<deih> and <lo> written as one word: not want, not like) (j:deih/lo) (r:zd:24064/zd:26700) (q:draft)
deihloh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unwanted/not wanted/disliked) (d:<deih> and <loh> written as one word: not wanting, or what someone does not want; {a deihloh thu} is a thing he does not want, and {deihloh pen in} introduces something one hopes will not happen) (j:deih/loh) (r:zd:24751/zd:20410/zd:20646) (q:draft)
deihlohna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:opposition/rejection/disapproval) (d:the attitude of not wanting a person, a government or an act, which is named just before {deihlohna}; with <lungphona> it is a protest against that person or thing) (r:zd:19662/ts:6531/zd:20315) (q:draft)
deihlohpen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:worst case/the thing least wanted) (d:<deih>, want, <loh>, not, and <pen>, here most, written as one word: what is wanted least; {deihlohpen in} opens a clause about something bad that may happen, if the worst comes) (j:deih/loh/pen) (r:zd:13030/zd:25516) (q:draft)
deihlohte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:unwanted things/those who do not want) (d:<deihloh> and the plural <te> written as one word: the things one does not want, or the people who do not want someone) (b:deihloh) (j:deihloh/te) (r:zd:24072/zd:24064/zd:25110) (q:draft)
deihlote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:those who do not want/opponents) (d:<deihlo>, not want, with the plural <te>: the people who do not want or do not like someone or something) (b:deihlo) (r:zd:25110/zd:24059) (q:draft)
deihmahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want very much/like very much/be very fond of) (d:<deih>, want or like, with <mahmah>, very, written as one word) (j:deih/mahmah) (r:zd:10901/zd:21074) (q:draft)
deihman = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:because of wanting) (d:<deih>, want, and <man>, because, written as one word, followed by <in>: because one wants the thing named before it) (j:deih/man) (r:zd:11852/zd:13127) (q:draft)
deihna bangin = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:according to the will of/as one wishes/as desired) (d:<deihna>, wish or will, and <bangin>, like or accordingly: placed after the person whose wish it is, in the way that person wants) (r:zd:22861/zd:23792/zd:20525) (q:draft)
deihna bulpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:main aim/chief purpose/basic intention) (d:<deihna>, wish or purpose, and <bulpi>, base or main: the main purpose or underlying aim of a person, a group or an action; a possessor stands before it, as in {a deihna bulpi}) (r:zd:21063/zd:12688/zd:23298) (q:draft)
deihnawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:no longer want/not want any more) (d:<deih> and <nawnlo> written as one word: not want someone or something any longer) (j:deih/nawnlo) (r:zd:17372/zd:11477) (q:draft)
deihngetna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:demand/request/petition) (d:<deih>, want, and <ngetna>, request, written as one word: what a group wants and asks for from those in authority) (j:deih/ngetna) (r:zd:11101/zd:23252) (q:draft)
deihpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:rush to at once/flock to) (d:in the articles with <ngeingai>, of neighbours or reporters who come crowding to a place at once; the last part is <pah>, immediately, and the first part is not confirmed) (r:zd:11736/zd:11885) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:favourite/most wanted/most liked) (d:<deih>, like or want, with <pen>, most: what someone likes or wants most) (b:deih) (r:zd:9215/zd:25016/zd:9432) (q:draft)
deihpeuhpeuh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:whatever one wants/anything one wishes) (d:<deih>, want, and <peuhpeuh>, whatever, written as one word, after <na>, <ka> or <a>: whatever you, I or they want) (j:deih/peuhpeuh) (r:zd:20803/zd:20781) (q:draft)
deihsakdiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:care especially for/favour particularly) (d:<deihsak>, care for, and <diak>, especially, written as one word: show special care or goodwill toward someone, with <tungah>) (j:deihsak/diak) (r:zd:20263) (q:draft)
deihsaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:not wish well/not care for/begrudge) (d:<deihsak> and <lo> written as one word: not want good for someone, not care for) (j:deihsak/lo) (r:zd:17285/zd:17264) (q:draft)
deihsakna lianpi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:best wishes/kind regards) (d:<deihsakna>, goodwill, and <lianpi>, great: with <tawh>, with, it is the closing formula of a letter or notice, {deihsakna lianpi tawh}, with great goodwill, followed by the name of the writer) (r:zd:24131/zd:25019) (q:draft)
deihsakna tawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:with best wishes/with goodwill/kind regards) (d:<deihsakna>, goodwill, and <tawh>, with: with goodwill; a formula that closes a letter, notice or column before the name of the writer, and that goes with an invitation or request, {deihsakna tawh kong zawn uh hi}, we kindly invite you) (r:zd:17674/zd:23832) (q:draft)
deihsakte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:loved ones/those one cares for/well-wishers) (d:persons and not wishes: <deihsak>, care for, with the plural <te>; {na deihsakte} are the people you care about, often beside {na itte}, those you love, and {hong deihsakte} are those who care for us) (r:zd:21001/zd:26306/zd:21943) (q:draft)
deihtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:earnestly/intensely/hard/firmly) (d:<deih> with <tak>, placed before a verb: with full will or force; {deihtak thungen} is pray earnestly) (s:deihtakin) (r:zd:25046/zd:12487/zd:26097) (q:draft)
deihteel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:choose/pick/choose freely) (d:<deih>, want, with <teel>, choose: pick what one likes from among others; {deihteel thei} is be able to choose; also as a noun, {ama deihteel}, his own choice) (r:zd:25139/zd:24542) (q:draft)
deihteelna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:choice/free choice/free will) (d:<deihteel>, choose freely, with the noun ending <na>: what a person chooses for himself, his own free choice) (b:deihteel) (r:zd:23604/zd:25139) (q:draft)
deihtel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:choose/choose freely) (d:choose what one wants, from <deih>, want, with <teel>, choose; {deihtel theihna} is the power or freedom to choose, and the noun is <deihtelna>) (r:zd:21989/zd:9142/zd:9429) (q:draft)
deihtelna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:free choice/choice/free will) (d:<deih>, want, with <teelna>, choosing: the choosing of what one wants, one's own free choice; {mipi deihtelna} is the choice of the people) (r:zd:19600/zd:24673/zd:23893) (q:draft)
deihtheih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:desirable/likeable) (d:<deih>, want or like, and <theih>, able, written as one word: that can be wanted or liked, a thing one may desire) (j:deih/theih) (r:zd:21568) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihzah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:amount wanted/as much as one wants) (d:<deih>, want, and <zah>, amount, written as one word: the amount or number that someone wants) (j:deih/zah) (r:zd:23904/zd:16799) (q:draft)
deihzahzah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as much as one wants/as many as one wants) (d:<deih>, want, and <zahzah>, as much as, written as one word: whatever amount a person wishes) (j:deih/zahzah) (r:zd:21876/zd:12070) (q:draft)
dek = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:abstain from/avoid/refrain) (d:after <ki>, {ki dek}: hold oneself back from a food, a drink or a habit; a verb of its own, not the particle that follows a verb) (r:zd:21557/zd:24276/zd:22019) (q:draft)
DeKalb = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/politics) (w:DeKalb) (d:county in the state of Georgia in the United States, with the city of Clarkston, where Zomi families live) (r:zd:17782/zd:15836) (q:draft)
dekdekta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly/about to) (d:<dekdek>, almost, and <ta>, the marker of a change, written as one word after a verb: is now on the point of, has almost) (j:dekdek/ta) (r:zd:11172/zd:21369/zd:21348) (q:draft)
dekin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly) (d:<dek> and <in> written as one word after a describing word or verb: being almost so, as in {aguaktang dekin}, almost naked) (j:dek/in) (r:zd:15264) (q:draft, low confidence)
dekliang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly/very nearly) (d:<dek>, almost, and <liang>, even, written as one word after a verb: so much that it very nearly happens) (j:dek/liang) (r:zd:12289/zd:15019) (q:draft)
dekphial = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly) (d:<dek> and <phial> written as one word, after a verb or an amount: almost, very nearly) (s:dektak) (j:dek/phial) (r:zd:14877/zd:16063/zd:13250) (q:draft)
deksuai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:nowhere near/not at all) (d:stronger form of <dek>, nearly, used after a verb and followed by a negative such as <lo> or <kei>: far from it, not at all, by no means) (r:zd:24199/zd:23311/zd:12370) (q:draft)
dekta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly/about to) (d:<dek>, nearly, and <ta>, now or already, written as one word after a verb: the action is now about to happen or has nearly happened) (j:dek/ta) (r:zd:22586/zd:18943/zd:15331) (q:draft)
dektakbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:nearly/almost/close to) (d:<dektak>, almost, and <bang>, about, written as one word after a number or an amount) (j:dektak/bang) (r:zd:12194/zd:12427) (q:draft)
Delaware = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Delaware) (d:a state in the east of the United States) (r:zd:25610) (q:draft)
deldal = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:sprawled/in full view/spread out) (d:placed after a verb for lie or stand, as in {lum deldal} and {din deldal}: lying or standing spread out in the open where everyone sees it, often of something unseemly) (r:zd:16148/zd:25927) (q:draft, low confidence)
delegate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:delegate/representative) (d:a person sent to a meeting to speak for a group or a village) (s:taangmi/palai) (o:English) (r:zd:23311/zd:25915) (q:draft)
delete = (i:1) (t:v) (f:it) (w:delete/remove) (d:remove a post, picture or message from a phone, computer or website; with <ki>, be deleted) (s:phiat) (o:English) (r:zd:14728/zd:20501) (q:draft)
delhdelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep chasing/pursue on and on) (d:<delh>, chase, said twice: go on chasing or following without stopping) (b:delh) (r:zd:22785/zd:17195) (q:draft)
delhhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:chase after/give chase/go after) (d:<delh>, chase, formed in the same way as <bawhhuan>, rush at: set off after someone in order to catch or reach him) (b:delh) (r:zd:19554/zd:23773) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhhuanpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:chase at once/give chase immediately) (d:<delhhuan> and <pah>, at once, written as one word: set off after someone or something straight away) (j:delhhuan/pah) (r:zd:12869) (q:draft)
Delhi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Delhi/New Delhi) (d:the capital city of India, where a Zomi community lives) (r:zd:26565/zd:17274) (q:draft)
delhkhiapah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:rush out at once/set out after at once) (d:<delhkhia> and <pah> written as one word: go out after something or someone immediately, said of firefighters hurrying to a fire and of people running out after someone) (j:delhkhia/pah) (r:zd:15507/zd:15953/zd:16815) (q:draft)
delhpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:rush to/hurry after/go at once) (d:<delh> and <pah> written as one word: go after someone or hurry to a place at once, as police and firefighters to the scene) (j:delh/pah) (r:zd:20721/zd:15631) (q:draft)
delhpha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:catch up with/reach in time/rush to) (d:<delh>, go after, and <pha>, reach, written as one word: reach what one goes after, keep up with the time, or hurry to a place and get there) (j:delh/pha) (r:zd:22944/zd:11354) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:rush over/run to/chase after) (d:<delh>, go after or hurry to, with <phei>, here across or over to: hurry over to a person or place, to help, to catch or to stop someone) (b:delh) (r:zd:17455/zd:17023/zd:18122) (q:draft)
delhpheipah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:rush over at once/run after at once) (d:<delhphei>, rush over to or run after, and <pah>, at once, written as one word) (j:delhphei/pah) (r:zd:12479/zd:19468/zd:15368) (q:draft)
delhsakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:dispatch at once/send immediately) (d:<delhsak>, send after, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: send firefighters, police or medical teams to a place straight away) (j:delhsak/pah) (r:zd:15773/zd:13300) (q:draft)
delhsuk = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:hurry down/rush down) (d:go down to a place in haste so as to be in time, with the place named before it and nobody being chased, as in {meileng khawlna delhsuk}, hurry down to the railway station) (r:zd:19826) (q:draft, low confidence)
delhto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:follow after/go after/follow up) (d:<delh>, go after, and <to>, up, written as one word: follow someone who has gone ahead, travel after them to the place where they are) (j:delh/to) (r:zd:16148/zd:11259) (q:draft)
deliver = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:deliver) (d:bring goods to the buyer; seen only in one repeated job notice) (o:English) (r:zd:11587) (q:draft, low confidence)
delivery = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:delivery) (d:the work of carrying goods or food to the buyer; in Zolai {van puak}) (o:English) (r:zd:12108/zd:15790) (q:draft)
dem = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:compete/contest/run for) (d:take part in a competition, or stand as a candidate in an election, in order to win; no defiance is meant, and {a dem ding} is one who will compete, {President dem} is run for president) (s:kidem) (r:zd:25474/zd:23389/zd:24468) (q:draft)
demand = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:demand) (d:what a group demands from others; also the demand of buyers for goods or a service) (s:ngetna) (o:English) (r:zd:21105/zd:20095) (q:draft, low confidence)
dembawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:rival/compete against/set oneself against) (d:<dem>, contend with, and <bawl>, do: treat someone as a rival and set oneself against him, where helping would be better) (b:dem) (r:zd:22171) (q:draft, low confidence)
demdem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:keep competing/vie) (d:<dem>, contend with, doubled; with the prefix <ki>, {ki demdem}, keep competing with one another, as rival companies do) (b:dem) (r:zd:19449/zd:11662) (q:draft)
demding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:will compete/to contest) (d:<dem> and <ding> written as one word: going to compete; {a demding} is whoever is to compete) (j:dem/ding) (r:zd:14887) (q:draft, low confidence)
dementia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:dementia) (d:illness of old age in which memory and thinking fail; mostly as {dementia natna}) (o:English) (r:zd:17402) (q:draft)
Democracy = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:democracy) (o:English) (r:zd:25110/zd:20256/zd:22746) (q:draft)
Democrat = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:Democrat/Democratic Party) (d:the Democratic Party of the United States or one of its members; {Democrat te} is the Democrats) (o:English) (r:zd:23479/zd:24831) (q:draft)
Democrats = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:Democrats/Democratic Party) (d:the members of the Democratic Party of the United States, one of the two main parties there) (r:zd:10906/zd:24909) (q:draft)
demsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:try to compete with/try to rival) (d:<dem>, compete, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: set out to match or outdo someone) (j:dem/sawm) (r:zd:21656/zd:22581) (q:draft)
den = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:always/continually/constantly) (d:placed after a verb: keep on doing, or remain so without change) (s:niloh/ngitnget/gige) (r:19.7.11) (q:draft)
dena = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:always and/continually and) (d:<den>, always, and the linking <a> written as one word at the end of a clause: it keeps on being so, and the sentence goes on) (j:den/a) (r:zd:9244/zd:9215/zd:9212) (q:draft)
denciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:later/afterwards/in the future) (d:later on, in time to come, or next in order; the same as <aden> followed by <ciang>, here written without the first <a>) (r:zd:17332/zd:20763) (q:draft)
denden = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:continually/again and again/all the time) (d:<den> said twice for emphasis, placed after a verb: keep on doing, without stopping) (b:den) (r:zd:25109/zd:20829/zd:23745) (q:draft)
dending = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:always/continually) (d:<den>, always, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will or must keep on doing it) (j:den/ding) (r:zd:25927/zd:15617/zd:23872) (q:draft)
dengkhalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not hit/miss) (d:<dengkha>, hit, and <lo>, not, written as one word: a falling or thrown thing does not hit a person) (j:dengkha/lo) (r:zd:16645/zd:11755) (q:draft)
Dengkil = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Dengkil) (d:a town in Selangor, Malaysia; in the articles in the name of a Zomi church fellowship there) (r:zd:15379) (q:draft, low confidence)
denglumkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/media) (w:strike dead/hit and kill) (d:<denglum>, strike dead, with <kha>, showing that it happened without intention, written as one word: a falling or flying thing hits a person and kills him) (j:denglum/kha) (r:zd:12287/zd:11133) (q:draft)
dengsia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:fall on and damage/hit and wreck/smash) (d:<deng> and <sia> written as one word: of a falling or thrown thing, strike something and ruin it) (j:deng/sia) (r:zd:15403/zd:12287) (q:draft)
dengsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:crash down on/fall onto/strike from above) (d:<deng>, strike, with <suk>, down: fall and hit what is below) (j:deng/suk) (r:zd:14547/zd:20738) (q:draft)
dengsukkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:fall on and hit/crash down onto/strike from above) (d:<deng>, strike, <suk>, down, and <kha>, happen to, written as one word: of a falling thing or person, come down on and hit what is below) (j:deng/suk/kha) (r:zd:20170/zd:11532/zd:19692) (q:draft)
Dengue = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:dengue/dengue fever) (d:a fever carried by mosquitoes, often written Dengue Fever) (o:English) (r:zd:14650/zd:16177) (q:draft)
denhi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:always) (d:<den>, always, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word, after a verb: {om denhi} is always is) (j:den/hi) (r:zd:22652) (q:draft)
denkeei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:always/constantly/all the time) (d:<den>, always, and the emphatic <keei> written as one word after a verb: keep on doing, do nothing but) (j:den/keei) (r:zd:16035/zd:12341) (q:draft)
denkei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:always/all the time/constantly) (d:placed after a verb like <den>: all the time, without change; it is not a negative, and {denkei lo} is not always) (r:zd:12564/zd:24164) (q:draft, low confidence)
denkeii = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:always/constantly) (d:<den>, always, and the emphatic <keii> written as one word, placed after a verb: all the time, without ever stopping) (j:den/keii) (r:zd:9253/zd:9239) (q:draft, low confidence)
denkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be hit/be struck) (d:<den>, a form of <deng>, with <khak>, happen to: be hit by a thing that falls; {denkhak neilo} is nothing or nobody was hit) (j:den/khak) (r:zd:11704/zd:17913) (q:draft)
denkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:one who always) (d:<den>, always, and <khat>, one, written as one word after a verb: a person who always does so) (j:den/khat) (r:zd:18924/zd:16308) (q:draft)
denleng = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if always/if regularly) (d:<den>, always, with <leng>, if, written as one word after a verb: if one keeps doing it, followed by a judgement such as {hoih hi}, it is good) (j:den/leng) (r:zd:24276/zd:12093) (q:draft)
denlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not always/not for good) (d:<den>, always, and <lo>, not, written as one word after a verb: not always, not permanently) (j:den/lo) (r:zd:12364/zd:10732) (q:draft)
denmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:just now/a moment ago/in a moment) (d:a very short time from now, mostly a short time ago; {denmah in kiza hi} is it has just been heard) (r:zd:12105/zd:11422) (q:draft, low confidence)
Denmark = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Denmark) (d:a country in northern Europe) (r:zd:11329/zd:20145/zd:10908) (q:draft)
denna = (i:4) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:constant doing/always being) (d:<den>, always, with <na> after a verb: the fact of always doing or always being so, as {ngaihsut denna}, always thinking, and {hoih denna mun}, a place where it is always good; not the {denna} of throwing) (r:zd:23767/zd:24224/zd:24276) (q:draft)
denomination = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:denomination) (d:a branch of the Christian church with its own name and order, in Zolai {biakna pawl} or <pawlpi>; often added in brackets after the Zolai word) (o:English) (r:zd:22390) (q:draft, low confidence)
