dongtuak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:victim/person in distress/sufferer) (d:one who has met with misfortune such as flood, fire, war or sickness and needs help, mostly as <cimawh dongtuak>; also a verb, meet with misfortune) (r:zd:20155/zd:15679/zd:19968) (q:draft)
dongtuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:hardship/distress/misfortune) (d:<dongtuak> with the noun suffix <na>: trouble or disaster that a person meets, often after <genthei> or <hamsat>) (b:dongtuak) (r:zd:23486/zd:15942) (q:draft)
