endik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media/health) (w:check/examine/proofread/edit) (d:<en>, look, with <dik>, correct: look over carefully to see that something is right, as a doctor checks health or an editor checks a text) (j:en/dik) (r:zd:20572) (q:draft)
ending = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to look at/to see/to visit) (d:<en>, look, and <ding>, will, written as one word: in order to look at, see or visit, mostly as {ending in} before a verb of going) (j:en/ding) (r:zd:12267/zd:21028/zd:14523) (q:draft)
endingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:in order to see/to look at) (d:<en>, look, and <dingin>, in order to, written as one word: so as to see or visit) (j:en/dingin) (r:zd:17645/zd:21848) (q:draft)
eng = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:yellow) (d:yellow in colour; {mul eng} is yellow hair) (q:draft)
