galkapkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:a soldier/one soldier) (d:<galkap> and <khat> written as one word: a soldier, one soldier) (j:galkap/khat) (r:zd:16325/zd:15537) (q:draft)
galkaplui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:former soldier/veteran/ex-serviceman) (d:<galkap>, soldier, with <lui>, old, written as one word: one who used to be a soldier) (j:galkap/lui) (r:zd:19763/zd:11555) (q:draft)
galkappuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/politics) (w:military uniform/army clothes) (d:<galkap>, soldier, and <puan>, clothes, written as one word: the uniform of a soldier) (j:galkap/puan) (r:zd:23773/zd:16956) (q:draft)
galkapten = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics) (w:soldiers/troops) (d:<galkapte>, soldiers, with the marker <in> shortened and joined, elsewhere written {galkapte'n}: the soldiers as the doers of the action) (j:galkapte/in) (r:zd:22785/zd:22926) (q:draft)
galkapzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:military skills/soldiering/military drill) (d:<galkap>, soldier, and <zia>, way, written as one word: the ways and skills of a soldier; {galkapzia sinna} is military training) (j:galkap/zia) (r:ts:10698/ts:10291) (q:draft)
galkikap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:fighting/armed clash/exchange of fire) (d:<gal> and <kikap> written as one word: fighting in which the two sides shoot at each other) (j:gal/kikap) (r:zd:16956/ts:5147) (q:draft)
galkuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:go to war/march out/go on campaign) (d:<gal>, war, with <kuan>, set out: go out to fight; also said of the troops that are on the march) (j:gal/kuan) (r:ts:4005/ts:11537/ts:5921) (q:draft)
gallelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:lose a war/be defeated in battle) (d:<gal>, war, and <lelh>, be overcome, written as one word: be losing or be defeated in a fight or war) (j:gal/lelh) (r:zd:11862/zd:24280) (q:draft, low confidence)
