gallu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:enemy head) (d:the head of an enemy taken in war, from <gal>, enemy, and <lu>, head; in former times brought home as a trophy) (r:ts:301/zd:24072) (q:draft)
galmai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:battlefront/front line/battlefield) (d:<gal>, war, with <mai>, face: the front in a war; {galmai nawk} is to advance at the front, to carry out an offensive) (r:ts:11537/zd:20241/ts:11444) (q:draft)
galmuang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/everyday) (w:secure/at peace/safe) (d:safe from enemies and trouble, from <gal>, enemy, and <muang>, trust; paired with <lungmuang>, at ease) (r:zd:25505) (q:draft, low confidence)
galmuhthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be visible from afar/can be seen from a distance) (d:<galmuh> and <thei> written as one word, usually after <ki>: it can be seen from far away) (j:galmuh/thei) (r:zd:13324/zd:20668) (q:draft)
galna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:condolence/condolence gift/compensation) (d:what is given to the family of a dead person in sympathy, mostly money, as {galna sum}, condolence money, and {galna pia}, give condolence; not the visit itself) (r:zd:22085/zd:25194/zd:23441) (q:draft)
galneih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:be enemies/be at enmity/be hostile) (d:<gal>, enemy, with <neih>, have, written as one word: have someone as an enemy; with <ki>, be enemies of each other) (j:gal/neih) (r:zd:12345/zd:19449) (q:draft)
