galphualpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:main base/military base/headquarters) (d:<galphual>, place of battle, with <pi>, great: a large or main military base or camp) (b:galphual) (r:ts:12413/ts:4005) (q:draft)
galphualte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:military camps/bases/battle positions) (d:plural of <galphual>: in news the camps and positions held by an army) (b:galphual) (r:ts:4941/ts:7364) (q:draft)
galpi khatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:First World War/World War I) (d:<galpi>, great war, and <khatna>, first: the First World War, also written {Leitung galpi khatna}; the Second World War is <galpi nihna>) (r:zd:17990/zd:21829) (q:draft)
galpi nihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:Second World War/World War II) (d:<galpi>, great war, and <nihna>, second: the Second World War, 1939 to 1945, often written with capitals; {galpi nihna lai in} is during the Second World War, and the First World War is <galpi khatna>) (r:zd:21085/zd:19379) (q:draft)
galpinih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:Second World War/World War II) (d:<galpi>, great war, with <nih>, two, written as one word: the Second World War; {galpinih hunlai in} is at the time of the Second World War) (j:galpi/nih) (r:zd:17707) (q:draft)
galpinihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/time) (w:Second World War/World War II) (d:<galpi>, great war, and <nihna>, second, written as one word: the Second World War, often as {leitung galpinihna} or {leitungbup galpinihna}) (j:galpi/nihna) (r:zd:16114/zd:17351) (q:draft)
galsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:turn into a fight/become enmity) (d:<gal> and <suak.2> written as one word: become war or enmity; the saying {ciamnuih galsuak} is a joke turns into a fight) (j:gal/suak) (r:zd:14498) (q:draft)
galtai = (i:3) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:flee/take refuge) (d:used as a verb, often before <uh> or <hi>: flee from fighting or persecution, where the other senses name the person who flees) (r:ts:7016/zd:8375) (q:draft)
galtaikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:flee/flee from war/take refuge) (d:<galtai>, flee from fighting, and <khia>, out, written as one word: flee out of a place because of war; also those who have fled) (j:galtai/khia) (r:zd:17616/zd:14937) (q:draft)
galtaimi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:refugee) (d:<galtai> and <mi> written as one word: a person who has fled from war, a refugee) (s:galtai) (j:galtai/mi) (r:zd:22438/zd:12119) (q:draft)
galvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:military affairs/warfare/war matters) (d:<gal>, war, with <vai>, affair: all that has to do with war and armed forces; {galvai tawh kisai} is concerning military matters, and it is paired with <gamvai> in the news sense of political affairs) (r:ts:3110/ts:9489/ts:4298) (q:draft)
galvanleng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:warplane/military aircraft/fighter plane) (d:<gal>, war, with <vanleng>, aircraft: an aircraft of an armed force) (r:zd:25109/zd:24195/ts:9285) (q:draft)
galvanlengte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:warplanes/military aircraft) (d:plural of <galvanleng>) (b:galvanleng) (r:zd:25109/ts:3482) (q:draft)
galven = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:be at peace/fighting dies down/war is over) (d:<gal>, war, and <ven>, cease, written as one word: the war or the fighting is over or has died down; {galven hun} is a time of peace) (j:gal/ven) (r:zd:17521/ts:2027) (q:draft)
galveng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:stand guard/be on guard/be on the alert) (d:keep watch against an enemy, said of armed forces holding a position) (r:ts:8276/ts:1343) (q:draft, low confidence)
galveng = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:the fighting ends/the quarrel is over) (d:<gal>, war or strife, and <veng>, cease, written as one word: a war or a quarrel comes to an end) (j:gal/veng) (r:zd:22159) (q:draft, low confidence)
galvil = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:keep watch/stand guard/guard) (d:used as a verb: keep watch against an enemy or over a place, with verb endings such as <sak> or {zel ni} after it, where the other sense names the watchman) (s:vil) (r:zd:20800/ts:5921) (q:draft)
galzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:win the war/be victorious in war) (d:<gal>, war, with <zo>, win, written as one word; also said of the side that has won) (a:guallel) (j:gal/zo) (r:zd:14696/zd:10746) (q:draft)
gam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:country) (d:A country or region with its people; {mualtung gam} is hill country.)
gambeel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:refugee/asylum seeker/asylum) (d:<gam>, country, with <bel>, take refuge in: a person who seeks shelter in another country, and the status of such a person; named beside <galtai>, one who flees from war; also written <gambel>) (r:zd:23427/zd:22620/zd:20458) (q:draft)
gambeelte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:refugees/asylum seekers/immigrants) (d:people who take refuge in a country that is not their own, said of refugees and of immigrants; <gambeel> with the plural <te>) (b:gambeel) (r:zd:22620/zd:11055/zd:11246) (q:draft)
gambek = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/politics) (w:only the country) (d:<gam>, country, and <bek>, only, written as one word; {gambek hilo} after a name is not only that country) (j:gam/bek) (r:zd:11693/zd:15253) (q:draft)
gambel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:refugee/asylum seeker) (d:<gam>, country, with <bel>, take refuge in: a person who has fled to another country and shelters there; often {gambel mi}) (s:galtai) (r:zd:23528/zd:20119/zd:23317) (q:draft)
gambelding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:to seek asylum/to take refuge) (d:<gambel> and <ding> written as one word: in order to take refuge in another country, to be a refugee there) (j:gambel/ding) (r:zd:15465/zd:11011) (q:draft)
gambelmi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:refugee/asylum seeker) (d:a person who takes refuge in another country; <gambel> with <mi>, person) (s:galtai) (r:zd:21574) (q:draft)
gambelte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:refugees/asylum seekers) (d:<gambel>, refugee, with the plural <te>, written as one word) (b:gambel) (j:gambel/te) (r:zd:23005/zd:22897) (q:draft)
Gambia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics) (w:Gambia/The Gambia) (d:country in West Africa) (r:zd:11007) (q:draft)
gambiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/politics) (w:state religion/religion of the country) (d:<gam>, country, and <biakna>, religion, written as one word: the religion of a country; with <te>, those who hold to it) (j:gam/biakna) (r:zd:12707) (q:draft, low confidence)
gambitna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:national security/defence) (d:<gam>, country, and <bitna>, security, written as one word: the security or defence of a country) (j:gam/bitna) (r:zd:25191) (q:draft)
gambuai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:national unrest/turmoil in the country/upheaval) (d:<gam>, country, and <buai>, be troubled, written as one word: a time when the country is in turmoil, through war or political crisis) (j:gam/buai) (r:zd:25233/zd:20845) (q:draft)
gambuaina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:national crisis/political turmoil/unrest) (d:<gam>, country, with <buaina>, trouble: the turmoil or crisis of a country) (j:gam/buaina) (r:zd:25288/zd:25301) (q:draft)
gambup = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:national/nationwide/union) (d:before a noun, of or for the country as a whole and not one state or town, as in <gambup thukhunpi>, the national constitution, and {gambup dawl}, the national level) (r:zd:25110/zd:24417/zd:22849) (q:draft)
gambup innpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:parliament/union assembly/national assembly) (d:<gambup>, the whole land, and <innpi>, great house: the parliament of the whole country, in Myanmar the Union Assembly, as distinct from the assembly of a state; often written with capitals) (r:zd:22782/zd:23485) (q:draft)
gambup kilemna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:nationwide peace/union peace/nationwide ceasefire) (d:<gambup>, the whole country, and <kilemna>, peace: the peace of the whole union, the term for the peace process and the nationwide ceasefire agreement in Myanmar; often followed by <maban>, process, or <khawmpi>, conference) (r:zd:24966/zd:23485) (q:draft)
gambup kiteelpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:general election/nationwide election) (d:<gambup>, the whole country, and <kiteelpi>, a great election: the general election of a country; the year often stands before it) (r:zd:23485/zd:24731) (q:draft)
gambup thukhunpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:national constitution/constitution of the state) (d:<gambup>, the whole country, and <thukhunpi>, constitution: the constitution of a state, as against the constitution of an organisation; a year before or after it names one, {2008 gambup thukhunpi}) (r:zd:25110/zd:19697/zd:22475) (q:draft)
gambupah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/travel) (w:throughout the country/nationwide) (d:<gambup> and <ah> written as one word: in the whole country) (j:gambup/ah) (r:zd:19275/zd:24677) (q:draft)
gamciat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:each country/own country/respective country) (d:<gam>, country, and <ciat>, each, written as one word: each one his own country, as in {amau gamciat}, their respective countries) (j:gam/ciat) (r:zd:12229/zd:15956) (q:draft)
gamdaihna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:silence/quiet/calm) (d:the state of being quiet and not a place: the silence between people who do not speak, as in {gamdaihna sukham}, break the silence, or calm in a country, beside <lungmuanna>) (r:zd:22683/zd:20322) (q:draft)
gamdaitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social) (w:quietly/peacefully/silently) (d:<gamdai> and <tak> written as one word, mostly with <in>: in a quiet and orderly way) (j:gamdai/tak) (r:zd:11664/zd:20257) (q:draft)
gamdanga = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/social) (w:abroad/in a foreign country) (d:<gamdang>, foreign country, with the ending <a>, in: in another country, abroad) (j:gamdang/a) (r:zd:9447) (q:draft)
gamdangmi khualzin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:foreign tourist/foreign visitor) (d:<gamdangmi>, foreigner, and <khualzin>, travel: a foreigner who travels in the country, a foreign tourist) (r:zd:17349/zd:11401) (q:draft)
gamdangmi nasem = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:foreign worker/migrant worker) (d:<gamdangmi>, foreigner, and <nasem>, worker: a person from another country who works in the land, the term of the news for migrant labour in Malaysia) (r:zd:13218/zd:14704) (q:draft)
gamdangmi nasemte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:foreign workers/migrant workers) (d:<gamdangmi>, foreigner, and <nasemte>, here workers and not servants: people from another country who work in a country, the term of the news for migrant labour) (r:zd:15886/zd:13201/zd:14570) (q:draft)
gamdangmi phalna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:immigration permit/residence permit/foreigner's papers) (d:<gamdangmi>, foreigner, and <phalna>, permission: the official document that allows a foreigner to stay or work in a country; often with <neilo>, without valid papers) (r:zd:14611/zd:19966) (q:draft)
gamdangmite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:foreigners/strangers) (d:plural of <gamdangmi>: people from another country) (b:gamdangmi) (r:zd:24276/zd:22334) (q:draft)
gamdangpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel) (w:from abroad/from another country) (d:<gamdang> and <pan> written as one word: from a foreign country) (j:gamdang/pan) (r:zd:15296/zd:11427) (q:draft)
gamdangsum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:foreign currency/foreign money) (d:<gamdang> and <sum> written as one word: the money of another country) (j:gamdang/sum) (r:zd:15296/zd:16157) (q:draft)
gamdangtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel/politics) (w:with foreign countries/with abroad) (d:<gamdang> and <tawh> written as one word: with another country, with foreign lands) (j:gamdang/tawh) (r:zd:17713) (q:draft)
Game = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it) (w:game/video game) (d:a game that is played, mostly a video game or a match in sport; {Game kimawl} is to play a game) (s:kimawlna) (o:English) (r:zd:15720/zd:17694) (q:draft)
gamgam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/social) (w:each country/various lands/respective countries) (d:<gam>, country, repeated: each in its own land, the various countries, often beside <munmun>) (r:zd:26411/zd:21941) (q:draft)
gamgam = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:vehemently/forcefully/violently) (d:placed after a verb: doing it with great force or heat, as {kiko gamgam}, shout loudly) (r:zd:25393/zd:22171) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamgicing = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:border guard/border guarding) (d:<gamgi>, border, with <cing>, guard, written as one word: guarding the border; {gamgicing galkap} is border guard troops and {gamgicing in om} is be stationed guarding the border) (j:gamgi/cing) (r:zd:17377/zd:16406/zd:10767) (q:draft)
gamgidung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:border area/borderland) (d:<gamgi>, border, and <dung>, length, written as one word: the land along a border, along the border) (j:gamgi/dung) (r:zd:15937/zd:11654/zd:16559) (q:draft)
gamgua = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:wild bamboo/forest bamboo) (d:bamboo, <gua>, that grows in the forest, set against <inngua>, the bamboo by the house; the saying {inngua hah lo gamgua hah}, clearing the wild bamboo and not the house bamboo, blames one who sees to others before his own) (r:zd:25165/zd:11138) (q:draft)
gamhau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:rich country/wealthy country) (d:<gam>, country, with <hau>, rich, written as one word: a wealthy country) (j:gam/hau) (r:zd:22604/zd:24955) (q:draft)
gamhaute = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:rich countries/wealthy countries) (d:plural of <gamhau>: the wealthy countries, set against <gamzawngte>, the poor countries) (b:gamhau) (j:gamhau/te) (r:zd:22604/zd:23975) (q:draft)
gamhtat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:act violently/behave lawlessly/be unruly) (d:treat others roughly and without respect; named together with {pheengtat} and with <totbawl>, provoke) (r:zd:23138/zd:22171) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamhtatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:violence/aggression/lawless conduct) (d:violent or lawless behaviour; probably a spelling of <gamtatna>, conduct, used of bad conduct) (r:zd:16565/zd:15859) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamhuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:territory/area/district) (d:<gam>, land, with <huam>, the area taken in: the area that belongs to a town or a ruler; {Tedim gamhuam} is the Tedim area) (j:gam/huam) (r:zd:19293/zd:8668/zd:19118) (q:draft)
gamhuang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:territory/domain) (d:<gam>, country, with <huang>, enclosure: the bounded area of a country or state) (r:zd:20899/zd:20412) (q:draft)
gamkatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/media) (w:wildfire/forest fire/bushfire) (d:<gam>, wild land or forest, with <katna>, burning: a fire that burns over forest or open country) (s:gammeikang) (r:zd:24602/zd:24515) (q:draft)
gamke = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:state/province/region/division) (d:<gam>, country, with <ke>, part: one of the large parts into which a country is divided, such as a state of the United States or India or a region of Myanmar) (r:zd:25616/zd:15681/zd:14301) (q:draft)
gamkee = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:state/province) (d:one of the parts into which a country is divided, with a government of its own: a state of a union or a province) (b:gam) (r:zd:16457/zd:21327/zd:12563) (q:draft)
gamkeek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:colonialist/colonizer/colonial) (d:<gam>, land, with <keek>, push out a border: one who seizes the land of others; placed before the name of a colonial power, as in {gamkeek Mikang kumpi}, the colonial British government) (r:zd:23667/zd:22746/zd:11400) (q:draft)
gamkeek = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:colonize/annex) (d:take the land of another people and rule it) (r:zd:11007) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamkeekte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:colonizers/colonialists/colonial rulers) (d:those who take the land of other peoples and rule it, from <gam>, land, and <keek>, enlarge a border, with the plural <te>; {Mikang gamkeekte} are the British colonial rulers) (r:ts:301/zd:19316/zd:16457) (q:draft)
gamkek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:colonialist/colonizer/colonialism) (d:a power that takes and rules the land of others, from <gam>, land; also the taking itself; {gamkek hun} is the colonial period and {gamkek kumpi} a colonial government) (r:zd:16210/zd:23198/zd:22371) (q:draft)
gamkekte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:colonialists/colonizers) (d:<gamkek> with the plural <te>: the colonial powers or rulers) (b:gamkek) (r:zd:22371/zd:13354) (q:draft)
gamkete = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:states/provinces/regions) (d:<gamke>, state, with the plural <te>) (b:gamke) (r:ts:4831/zd:25007) (q:draft)
gamkeu = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature/time) (w:be dry/be parched) (d:said of the country in the hot season, when everything is dry and fire spreads easily; {gamkeu} is then the predicate, before <in> or <mahmah>, and not the name of a kind of land) (r:zd:19410/zd:17530) (q:draft)
gamkeuna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:desert/dry land/arid land) (d:<gam> and <keuna> written as one word: dry country, mostly before <mun>, as {sehnel gamkeuna mun}, a sandy desert place) (j:gam/keuna) (r:zd:22450/zd:24933) (q:draft)
gamkhangto = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:developed country) (d:<gam>, country, and <khangto>, grow or develop, written as one word: a developed country; {gamkhangto te} are the developed countries) (j:gam/khangto) (r:zd:15237/zd:12267/zd:15274) (q:draft)
gamkhangtote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:developed countries) (d:<gamkhangto>, developed country, with the plural <te>: the developed countries) (b:gamkhangto) (r:zd:21121/zd:21455) (q:draft)
gamkhatin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/everyday) (w:as a country/as one country) (d:<gamkhat>, a country or one country, and <in> written as one word: as a country of some kind, or together as one country) (j:gamkhat/in) (r:zd:14810/zd:11917) (q:draft)
gamkhatpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/everyday) (w:from one country) (d:<gamkhat>, one country, and <pan>, from, written as one word; {gamkhatpan gamkhat} is from one country to another) (j:gamkhat/pan) (r:zd:21400/zd:15296) (q:draft)
gamkhatpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/travel) (w:one country/a country) (d:<gamkhat>, one country, and the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: one country, as the thing spoken about) (j:gamkhat/pen) (r:zd:19820) (q:draft)
gamkhatpeuh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:any country/whichever country) (d:<gamkhat>, a country, with <peuh>, any) (j:gamkhat/peuh) (r:zd:14904/zd:13218) (q:draft)
gamkhempeuh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/travel) (w:all countries/every country) (d:<gam>, country, and <khempeuh>, all, written as one word) (j:gam/khempeuh) (r:zd:19648/zd:24116/zd:12876) (q:draft)
gamkhen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:state/province/region) (d:<gam>, country, with <khen>, divide: one of the parts into which a country is divided, such as a state of India) (r:zd:15290/zd:19662) (q:draft)
gamkuam = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:region/area/territory) (d:a stretch of country in general, not only a valley, as in {tenna gamkuam}, the area where a people lives, and {gamkuam golpi}, a great region) (r:zd:16342) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamkuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:expedition/field trip/field operation) (d:<gam>, country, with <kuan>, set out: a going out into the country, said of a hunting party, of soldiers on operation and of a group on a trip; {gamkuan te} are those who went out) (r:zd:21117/zd:20889) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamkumpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:national government/government of a country) (d:<gam>, country, and <kumpi>, government, written as one word) (j:gam/kumpi) (r:zd:25279/zd:14620) (q:draft)
gamla = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/travel) (w:far/distant/far away) (d:far in place; with <a> before it and <panin> or <ah> after it, it is used as a noun: {a gamla panin} is from a distance, {a gamla-ah} is at a distance) (a:kinai) (r:41.5.6) (q:draft)
gamlakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (j:gamlatna) (r:zd:20215/zd:20120) (q:draft)
gamlalo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/travel) (w:not far/near/nearby) (d:<gamla>, far, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not far away; {tawh ki gamlalo} is not far from) (j:gamla/lo) (r:zd:22683/zd:11839/zd:12398) (q:draft)
gamlalualo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:travel/everyday) (w:not very far/not far) (d:<gamla>, far, and <lualo>, not very, written as one word; {tawh aki gamlalualo} is not far from) (j:gamla/lualo) (r:zd:11803/zd:13332/zd:17713) (q:draft)
gamlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:region/part of the world/direction of a country) (d:<gam>, country, with <lam>, direction, written as one word: the lands lying in a direction, as {nitumna gamlam}, the West, or the direction of a named country) (j:gam/lam) (r:zd:15253/zd:21908) (q:draft)
gamlapi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:national anthem) (d:<gam>, country, with <la>, song, and <pi>, great: the anthem of a country, named after the country; a different word from {gamlapi}, far away) (r:zd:15165) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamlapipi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:travel/everyday) (w:very far/far away/very distant) (d:<gamla> and the intensifier <pipi> written as one word: very far away) (j:gamla/pipi) (r:zd:15276/zd:14648) (q:draft)
gamleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/social) (w:country and) (d:<gam>, country, and <leh>, and, written as one word; mostly in {gamleh minam}, country and people) (j:gam/leh) (r:zd:24234/zd:14912/zd:14751) (q:draft)
gamlei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/nature) (w:land/territory/homeland) (d:<gam>, country, with <lei>, land: the land of a country or a people, one's own land) (r:zd:17309/zd:22986) (q:draft)
gamlianpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:great country/great power/large country) (d:<gam>, country, and <lianpi>, great, written as one word: a large and powerful country or territory) (j:gam/lianpi) (r:ts:7051/zd:16757) (q:draft)
gamliante = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:great nations/great powers/big countries) (d:plural of <gamlian>: the large and powerful countries of the world) (b:gamlian) (j:gamlian/te) (r:zd:24965/zd:25893) (q:draft)
gamlim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/travel) (w:map/chart) (d:<gam> land with <lim> picture: a map of a country or of the world) (r:zd:20513/zd:20742) (q:draft)
gamlumlua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:be too noisy/be very noisy) (d:<gamlum>, be noisy, and <lua>, too much, written as one word) (j:gamlum/lua) (r:zd:17058/zd:16362) (q:draft)
gammaang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:forest/wild forest/jungle) (d:wild land covered with trees, often said together with <tulak> as {gammaang tulak}) (s:gamlak/tulak) (r:zd:22746) (q:draft)
gammakai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:national leader/head of government/prime minister) (d:<gam>, country, with <makai>, leader: the leader of a country, said of a prime minister, a president or another head of government) (r:zd:20971/zd:19631) (q:draft)
gammakailui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:former national leader/former prime minister) (d:<gammakai>, leader of a country, and <lui>, old, written as one word: a former prime minister or head of state) (j:gammakai/lui) (r:zd:20363/zd:19602) (q:draft)
gammakaipi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:national leader/head of government/prime minister) (d:<gam>, country, with <makaipi>, chief leader, written as one word: the foremost leader of a country) (s:gammakai) (j:gam/makaipi) (r:zd:19619/zd:19820) (q:draft)
gammakaipipa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:prime minister/head of government/national leader) (d:<gammakaipi>, the foremost leader of a country, with <pa> for a man, written as one word) (s:gammakaipi) (j:gammakaipi/pa) (r:zd:11850/zd:20236) (q:draft)
gammang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:wilderness/wild forest/jungle) (d:wild country where no one lives, used as a noun before <lakah>, in the midst of, and in {gammang tulak}, the deep wilderness; not the act of going astray) (r:zd:24574/zd:22305/ts:4005) (q:draft)
gammangtulak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:wild forest/jungle/wilderness) (d:<gammang> and <tulak> written as one word: wild forest country far from where people live) (j:gammang/tulak) (r:zd:22557/zd:11862) (q:draft)
gammei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:wildfire/forest fire/bushfire) (d:a fire burning in forest or open land, from <gam>, land, and <mei>, fire) (r:zd:13092/zd:14871) (q:draft)
gammeikang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:wildfire/forest fire/bushfire) (d:<gam>, wild land, <mei>, fire, and <kang>, burn: a fire that burns over forest or open country) (r:zd:13092/zd:11236/zd:14871) (q:draft)
gammi hihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:citizenship/nationality) (d:<gammi>, citizen, and <hihna>, the fact of being: citizenship or nationality; the name of the country stands before it, and {gammi hihna ngah} is obtain citizenship) (r:zd:19302/zd:25918) (q:draft)
gammial = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:mission field/mission) (d:<gam>, land, with <mial>, dark: a land or people the gospel has not reached, and the mission work done there; {gammial nasep} is mission work and {gammial vei} is have a burden for mission) (r:zd:17060/zd:21547/zd:25078) (q:draft)
gammikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:a citizen/a national) (d:<gammi> and <khat> written as one word: a citizen of the country named before it, as in {Myanmar gammikhat}, a Myanmar national) (j:gammi/khat) (r:zd:19468/zd:20468) (q:draft)
gamminthang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:famous country/renowned country) (d:<gam>, country, and <minthang>, famous, written as one word: a country that is well known or of great name) (j:gam/minthang) (r:zd:11658/zd:17309) (q:draft)
gammipa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:citizen/national/man) (d:<gammi>, citizen, with <pa> marking a man: after the name of a country, a man of that country) (b:gammi) (r:zd:16126) (q:draft)
gammipih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:fellow countryman/compatriot/fellow citizen) (d:a person of the same country as oneself: <gam>, country, with <mipih>, one of the same people) (r:zd:17945/zd:11366) (q:draft)
gammual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:wilds/forest and hills/hill country) (d:<gam>, land or wild country, with <mual>, hill: the wild hill country away from the towns, mostly as {singnuai gammual} and in songs) (r:zd:25473/ts:3369) (q:draft, low confidence)
Gamngai = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel/social) (w:Gamngai) (d:village in the <Tedim> area of Chin State; written after a personal name it tells where the person is from) (r:zd:19430) (q:draft)
gamnih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:two countries/both countries) (d:<gam> and <nih> written as one word: the two countries, placed after their names) (j:gam/nih) (r:zd:15820/zd:11642/zd:14505) (q:draft)
gamnihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:second country) (d:<gam> and <nihna> written as one word: for refugees, the second country, the country of refuge where one waits before resettlement in the <gamthumna>) (j:gam/nihna) (r:zd:20326/zd:20936) (q:draft)
gamnuai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:underground/insurgency) (d:<gam>, land, with <nuai>, under: the underground, armed groups that operate in hiding; {gamnuai mite} are insurgents or militants) (r:ts:3234/zd:16032) (q:draft)
gamnuaimi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:militant/insurgent/rebel) (d:<gam>, country, <nuai>, under, and <mi>, person, an underground person: a member of an armed group that fights a government) (r:zd:11043/zd:11046) (q:draft)
gamnuaimite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:militants/insurgents/rebels) (d:{gam nuai}, underground, with <mite>, people: the members of an armed underground group) (r:zd:11043/zd:11046) (q:draft)
gampanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/politics) (w:from the country of/from the land) (d:<gam>, country, and <panin>, from, written as one word, placed after the name of the country) (j:gam/panin) (r:zd:19314/zd:19130) (q:draft)
gampawlkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:some countries) (d:<gam> and <pawlkhat> written as one word: some countries) (j:gam/pawlkhat) (r:zd:23784/zd:23591) (q:draft)
gampen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/travel) (w:the country/as for the country) (d:<gam> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the country, as the thing spoken about; stands after the name of a country) (j:gam/pen) (r:zd:19786/zd:12161) (q:draft)
gampi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:state/union/nation/country) (d:<gam>, country, with <pi>, great: a whole country or union as a political body, as {federal gampi}, a federal union; not the boundary of a land) (r:zd:25026/zd:25020/zd:25063) (q:draft)
gampua = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:abroad/overseas/foreign country) (d:<gam>, country, with <pua>, outside: the world outside one's own country; often paired with <gamsung>, as in <gamsung gampua>, at home and abroad) (s:gamdang) (r:zd:23492/zd:12039/zd:11415) (q:draft)
gampualam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:abroad/overseas/foreign countries) (d:<gam>, country, and <pualam>, outside, written as one word: outside the country, abroad) (s:gamdang) (j:gam/pualam) (r:zd:12581/zd:17643/zd:19130) (q:draft)
gamsung gampua = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social/politics) (w:at home and abroad/inside and outside the country) (d:<gamsung>, inside the country, and <gampua>, abroad, set side by side without <leh>: at home and abroad, everywhere that the people live; followed by <ah>, in, or <pan>, from) (r:zd:12039/zd:11415) (q:draft)
gamsung meikang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/media) (w:wildfire/bushfire/forest fire) (d:<gamsung>, here the open country or forest, and <meikang>, a burning: a wildfire or bushfire; a place name often stands before it) (r:zd:15820/zd:15795/zd:14681) (q:draft)
gamsung meikatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/media) (w:wildfire/forest fire/bushfire) (d:<gamsung>, the wild open country, and <meikatna>, a fire: a fire that burns through forest and open land, as against a fire in a house or a town; often followed by <hangin>, because of) (r:zd:15820/zd:15679) (q:draft)
gamsungbek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/politics) (w:only in the country/only within) (d:<gamsung>, inside a country, and <bek>, only, written as one word after the name of a land; with <hilo> it means not only in that country) (j:gamsung/bek) (r:zd:13350/zd:12422) (q:draft)
gamsungmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/politics) (w:right in the country/within the country) (d:<gam> and <sungmah> written as one word: in that very country, inside the country just named) (j:gam/sungmah) (r:zd:17713/zd:11327) (q:draft)
gamsungpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel/politics) (w:from the country/out of the country) (d:<gamsung>, the land, and <pan>, from, written as one word and placed after the name of a country: from that country, out of it) (j:gamsung/pan) (r:zd:11265/zd:21968) (q:draft)
gamsungpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/travel) (w:as for the country) (d:<gamsung>, the country, and the topic marker <pen>, written as one word after the name of a country: the country, as the thing spoken about) (j:gamsung/pen) (r:zd:11752/zd:19820) (q:draft)
gamsungteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/nature) (w:whole region/entire country/all the area) (d:<gamsung> and <teng>, here meaning all of, written as one word, placed after the name of a land or region: the whole of its territory, throughout it) (j:gamsung/teng) (r:zd:17622/zd:12210) (q:draft)
gamsungzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/travel) (w:also in the country/the country too) (d:<gamsung>, the land or country, with <zong>, also, written as one word, usually after the name of the country) (j:gamsung/zong) (r:zd:12845/zd:18152) (q:draft)
gamtaampi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:dense forest/jungle) (d:<gam> and <taampi> written as one word: thickly forested country) (j:gam/taampi) (r:zd:20734) (q:draft)
gamtampi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/travel) (w:many countries) (d:<gam> and <tampi> written as one word: many countries, as in {leitung gamtampi}, many countries of the world) (j:gam/tampi) (r:zd:18154/zd:15212) (q:draft)
gamtang = (i:5) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:move/act/be active) (d:used as a verb, with <thei>, <zolo> or <uh> after it: move the body, or of a person or a government take action, act in a certain way) (r:zd:17634/zd:19332/zd:24236) (q:draft)
gamtangsak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:exercise/make move/set in motion) (d:<gamtang>, move, with the causative <sak>, said of the body or of a machine: {pumpi gamtangsak} is exercise the body, and of an engine it is make the car run; not the settling of people on the land) (r:zd:22151/zd:20399) (q:draft)
gamtat = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:conduct/behaviour/manner) (d:used as a noun before words such as <hoih>, <zia>, <dan> and <luhek>: the way a person behaves, conduct) (s:gamtatna) (r:zd:22550/zd:23989/zd:17152) (q:draft)
gamtat luhek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:conduct/behaviour/character) (d:<gamtat>, behave, and <luhek>, manners: a pair that names a person's conduct as a whole, often beside words for speech such as <kampau>) (r:zd:19900/zd:17896) (q:draft)
gamtatdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:behaviour/conduct/manner) (d:<gamtat>, behave, with <dan>, way: the way a person behaves or acts) (s:gamtatna) (j:gamtat/dan) (r:zd:22282/zd:21817) (q:draft)
gamtatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:to behave/to act/how to act) (d:<gamtat>, behave, and <ding>, will, written as one word: to behave or act in a certain way, how one should act) (j:gamtat/ding) (r:zd:14646/zd:12042/zd:15216) (q:draft)
gamtathoih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:good conduct/good behaviour/decorum) (d:<gamtat>, behave, with <hoih>, good, written as one word: good behaviour, and also to behave well) (j:gamtat/hoih) (r:zd:16254/zd:16433) (q:draft)
gamtatlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:not acting/failure to act) (d:<gamtat> and <lohna> written as one word: the fact of not behaving in a certain way; {thuman thutak tawh gamtatlohna}, not acting with truth and honesty, is used for corruption) (j:gamtat/lohna) (r:zd:23358) (q:draft)
gamtatpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:doer/perpetrator) (d:<gamtat>, behave or act, with <pa>, the man who, written as one word: the man who acted so; {agitloh gamtatpa} is the man who did the wicked deed) (j:gamtat/pa) (r:zd:15779/zd:19530) (q:draft)
gamtatsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:attempt/intend to commit) (d:<gamtat> and <sawm> written as one word: set out or plan to do a deed, mostly a bad one; also the attempted deed itself) (j:gamtat/sawm) (r:zd:15327/zd:16080) (q:draft)
gamtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/travel) (w:with the country) (d:<gam> and <tawh> written as one word after the name of a country: with that country) (j:gam/tawh) (r:zd:12011/zd:15372) (q:draft)
gamteelna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:choice of country/country selection) (d:<gam> and <teelna> written as one word: the choosing of the country where a refugee is to be resettled) (j:gam/teelna) (r:zd:22850/zd:22877) (q:draft)
gamtek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:each country/respective country) (d:<gam>, country, and <tek>, each, written as one word: the country of each one; {hongpaikhiatna gamtek} is the country each of them came from) (j:gam/tek) (r:zd:14549/zd:15163) (q:draft)
gamthak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/travel/politics) (w:new country/new land) (d:<gam> and <thak> written as one word: a new land to settle in, or a newly founded country) (j:gam/thak) (r:zd:25918/zd:17309/zd:15527) (q:draft)
gamthu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:national affairs/affairs of the country/politics) (d:<gam>, country, with <thu>, matter: the affairs of a country or region, its public and political matters) (r:zd:24604/zd:16157) (q:draft)
gamthu = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education/nature) (w:geography) (d:the study of lands and of the earth as a school subject; {Zolai Gamthu bu} is the Zolai geography book) (r:zd:25390) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamthum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:three countries) (d:<gam>, country, and <thum>, three, written as one word: three countries, placed after their names) (j:gam/thum) (r:zd:25893/zd:14983) (q:draft)
gamthum = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:third country) (d:for refugees, the third country, where one is resettled after the country of refuge; short for {gam thumna}) (j:gam/thum) (r:zd:19626) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamthumna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:third country) (d:<gam> and <thumna> written as one word: the third country, the country in which refugees are resettled after their own country and the country of first refuge) (j:gam/thumna) (r:zd:22897/zd:20936) (q:draft)
gamthupi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:great country/advanced country/developed country) (d:<gam>, country, with <thupi>, great: a country of high standing, rich and developed) (r:zd:15433/zd:22728) (q:draft)
gamtuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:another country/separate country/foreign land) (d:<gam>, country, and <tuam>, separate, written as one word: a different or separate country; {muntuam gamtuam} is various places and lands) (j:gam/tuam) (r:zd:24215/zd:23635) (q:draft)
gamtuamtuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:various countries/different countries) (d:<gam>, country, and <tuamtuam>, various, written as one word: several different countries, countries of many kinds) (j:gam/tuamtuam) (r:zd:11588/zd:15307/zd:16259) (q:draft)
gamuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:government/rule of a country/state administration) (d:<gam> country with <uk> rule: the governing of a country and those who govern it, mostly before <kumpi> or <makai>, as in {gamuk kumpi}, the ruling government, and {gamuk makai}, national leaders) (r:zd:25060/zd:16210/zd:16782) (q:draft)
gamukpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:ruler/head of state/king) (d:<gam>, country, with <ukpa>, ruler: the man who rules a country, a king, president or chief) (s:kumpipa) (j:gam/ukpa) (r:ts:301) (q:draft)
gamvaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (j:gamvak) (r:zd:23754) (q:draft)
gamvai = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:politics/national affairs) (d:<gam>, country, with <vai>, affair: the affairs of a country, politics; {gamvai ah lut} is go into politics, and it has nothing to do with the breadth of the land) (r:zd:18086/ts:6880/zd:16254) (q:draft)
gamvak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:travel/go about/tour) (d:after <khualzin>, as <khualzin gamvak>: travel about from place to place, also used as a noun for travel and tourism, with no thought of hunting) (s:khualzin) (r:zd:17649/zd:11401/ts:10375) (q:draft)
gamvakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:travel/going about/outing) (d:<gamvak>, go about the country, with the noun suffix <na>: going about away from home; mostly in the pair {khualzin gamvakna}, travel and journeys) (b:gamvak) (r:zd:24283/zd:22426) (q:draft)
gamvakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:travelers/those away from home) (d:<gamvak>, go about away from home, with plural <te>; found in {khualzin gamvakte}, those who are away travelling) (b:gamvak) (j:gamvak/te) (r:zd:16500/zd:25393) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamvan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/travel) (w:patrol) (d:go about an area to watch over it, said of soldiers and officials; {gamvan in pai} is go on patrol) (r:ts:1822/ts:2913) (q:draft, low confidence)
gamveng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:neighbouring country/neighbour) (d:<gam>, country, with <veng>, neighbour: a country that borders another) (r:zd:12210/zd:18952) (q:draft)
gamzawng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:poor country) (d:<gam>, country, and <zawng>, poor, written as one word: a poor country) (j:gam/zawng) (r:zd:17355/zd:12387) (q:draft)
gamzawngte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:poor countries/developing countries) (d:plural of <gamzawng>: the poor countries, set against <gamhaute>, the rich countries) (b:gamzawng) (r:zd:22604) (q:draft)
gamzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/travel) (w:the country also) (d:<gam>, country, and <zong>, also, written as one word, after the name of a country: that country too) (j:gam/zong) (r:zd:20394/zd:17192) (q:draft)
ganan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:arithmetic/mathematics/number) (d:numbers and reckoning with them; {ganan tuat} is do sums) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:22830) (q:draft)
gang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:uncle) (d:kinship term for the husband of a father's sister, also used as a title before his name; the English word gang occurs in the articles only in English phrases) (r:zd:24678) (q:draft, low confidence)
Gangaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Gangaw) (d:town and district in Myanmar on the road between Kalay and the central plain, bordering the Chin hills) (r:zd:22802/ts:10251/zd:10860) (q:draft)
Gangnam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/media) (w:Gangnam) (d:district of Seoul in South Korea; also in the title of the song Gangnam Style) (r:zd:25208) (q:draft, low confidence)
Gangster = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:gangster/gang) (d:a member of a criminal gang, and also the gang itself, as in {Gangster ah lut}, join a gang) (o:English) (r:zd:11389/zd:15398) (q:draft)
ganhing khawina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/work) (w:zoo/animal park/animal farm) (d:<ganhing>, animal, and <khawina>, keeping: a place where animals are kept, a zoo, wildlife park or farm) (r:zd:19468) (q:draft)
ganhingpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:food/nature) (w:from animals) (d:<ganhing> and <pan> written as one word: from an animal or from animals) (j:ganhing/pan) (r:zd:21651) (q:draft)
gankhawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/work) (w:livestock/domestic animal) (d:<gan>, animal, with <khawi>, keep and rear: an animal that people keep, such as mithun, goats, pigs and chickens) (r:zd:21136/ts:3375) (q:draft)
gankhawi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work) (w:animal husbandry/livestock rearing) (d:the work of keeping and rearing animals, often named together with <lokhawh>, farming) (r:zd:22941/zd:24471) (q:draft)
ganno = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home/nature) (w:domestic animal/pet/livestock) (d:any small animal kept at home or on a farm, a pet or farm animal and not only the young of one; brought out by <khawi>, keep or rear, as in {ganno khawi}, and by the pair {ganta ganno}) (r:zd:21013/zd:17958/zd:22713) (q:draft)
gap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/nature) (w:ear/cob/pod) (d:one fruit of a plant counted as a unit, as in {vaimim gap}, an ear of maize, and {nahtang gap}, a banana) (r:zd:22185/zd:24276) (q:draft, low confidence)
gapkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:one piece/one ear) (d:<gap>, one fruit counted as a unit, and <khat>, one, written as one word: one ear, one banana) (j:gap/khat) (r:zd:22448) (q:draft)
Garage = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:garage) (d:a building where vehicles are kept or repaired; {mawtaw koihna} in Zolai) (o:English) (r:zd:15260/zd:22162) (q:draft)
Garuda = (i:1) (t:name) (f:travel) (w:Garuda Indonesia/Garuda) (d:the national airline of Indonesia) (r:zd:11081/zd:17628) (q:draft)
Gas = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:gas/cooking gas) (d:gas burned as fuel, above all for cooking; {Gas bung} is a gas cylinder) (o:English) (r:zd:22584/zd:21259/zd:15354) (q:draft)
gas bung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/food) (w:gas cylinder/gas bottle) (d:{gas}, the English word for cooking gas, and <bung>, a vessel of measure: the metal cylinder that holds cooking gas; in news most often with <puakkham>, explode) (r:zd:14616/zd:21419) (q:draft)
gataam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:fermented beans) (d:a strong-smelling Zomi food named beside ngapi, fish paste, which those who like it find fragrant and others find stinking; apparently fermented soya beans) (r:zd:19447/zd:23075) (q:draft, low confidence)
Gate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:gate/checkpoint/toll gate) (d:a gate on a road or at a border where travellers are stopped, checked or made to pay) (o:English) (r:zd:23997/ts:5480/zd:11308) (q:draft, low confidence)
gau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body) (w:swell/be distended/open wide) (d:be swollen or stand out: {nawi gau} is said of a breast full of milk and {mit gau} of eyes opened wide; the articles also have {vaimim gau}, of maize, and the pair {gu leh gau}, whose meaning is not determined) (r:zd:24117/zd:26097) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/social) (w:slaughter/kill) (d:<gawh>, kill an animal, and <in> written as one word: killing an animal, mostly a pig, for a feast or for guests, and then doing what follows) (j:gawh/in) (r:ts:9389/zd:11400) (q:draft)
gawikha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/health) (w:run over/crush) (d:<gawi>, grind, crush, and <kha>, happen to, written as one word: of a vehicle or machine, run over or crush a person or a part of the body by accident) (j:gawi/kha) (r:zd:17455/zd:11683/zd:20615) (q:draft)
gawikhalodeuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:narrowly miss/just not run over) (d:<gawikha>, run over, with <lo>, not, and <deuh>, written as one word: a wheel just fails to run over someone; seen in one headline only) (j:gawikha/lo/deuh) (r:zd:14799) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawilum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/health) (w:crush to death/run over and kill) (d:<gawi>, grind or crush, with <lum>, dead, written as one word: crush to death, as a train does) (j:gawi/lum) (r:zd:19300) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawina = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:digestion) (d:the breaking down of food in the stomach, in {an gawina} after <gilpi>, stomach; not the grinding of grain with a stone) (r:zd:24276/zd:11167) (q:draft)
gawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:sore throat/throat pain) (d:pain in the throat, named among the signs of illness; from <gawl>, throat, and a word for pain) (r:zd:20547/ts:11223) (q:draft)
gawlpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:body) (w:by the neck/at the neck) (d:<gawl>, neck, and <pan>, from, written as one word) (j:gawl/pan) (r:zd:22932) (q:draft)
gawlsung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:throat/inside of the throat) (d:<gawl>, throat, and <sung>, inside, written as one word: the inside of the throat) (j:gawl/sung) (r:zd:24054/zd:19392) (q:draft)
gawmkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:join together/combine/unite/mix) (d:<gawm>, join, and <khawm>, together, written as one word: put or bring together into one) (j:gawm/khawm) (r:zd:23394/zd:22228/zd:15671) (q:draft)
gawmkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:combine/join together/put together) (d:<gawm>, join, with <khop>, together: bring several things together into one) (s:gawmkhawm) (j:gawm/khop) (r:zd:24199/zd:24605) (q:draft)
gawmkhopding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:to merge/to join together) (d:<gawm>, join, <khop>, together, and <ding>, will, written as one word: to be joined together, a planned merger; with <ki>, to unite with each other) (j:gawm/khop/ding) (r:zd:17630/zd:11329) (q:draft)
gawmkhopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:combination/union/joining together) (d:the bringing together of several things or groups into one, or what results from it) (b:gawmkhop) (r:zd:16442) (q:draft)
gawmna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (w:addition/joining/combining) (d:<gawm>, join or add, with the noun suffix <na>: the adding of numbers, the plus of arithmetic, and the joining of things into one; after <aki> the place where things run together) (b:gawm) (r:zd:25390/zd:11278) (q:draft)
gawmtuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:combine/put together/unite/compile) (d:<gawm> and <tuah> written as one word: bring separate things or people together into one) (j:gawm/tuah) (r:zd:25461/zd:15035/ts:3160) (q:draft)
gawmtuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:combining/joining together/combination) (d:<gawmtuah>, combine, with the noun ending {-na}: the act of bringing things or people together into one) (b:gawmtuah) (r:zd:12544/zd:19453) (q:draft)
Gawmual = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/nature) (w:Gawmual) (d:a hill and locality at Tedim town, named for its viewpoint and its water source) (r:zd:17527/zd:15590) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawmzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be able to unite/manage to join together) (d:<gawm>, join, with <zo>, be able to: succeed in bringing separate people or groups together into one) (j:gawm/zo) (r:ts:7133/ts:7051) (q:draft)
Gawngmual = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Gawngmual) (d:a village near Tedim town; {Gawngmual khuami} is a person of that village) (r:zd:20883/zd:21182) (q:draft)
gawpding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<gawp> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: to do the thing severely, recklessly or to the point of ruin) (j:gawp/ding) (r:zd:19340/zd:12405) (q:draft)
gawpmawk = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/media) (d:<gawp>, severely, with <mawk>, written as one word after a verb: the action is done violently and without restraint, and the writer finds it shocking) (j:gawp/mawk) (r:zd:14839/zd:15779) (q:draft)
gawppah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at once and thoroughly/straight away) (d:<gawp>, severely or all over, and <pah>, at once, written as one word after a verb: the action happens at once and with full force, as in {ki thehzak gawppah}, spread everywhere at once) (j:gawp/pah) (r:zd:13233/zd:13078) (q:draft)
gawtbawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:mistreatment/torture/cruelty/abuse) (d:<gawtbawl>, mistreat, with the noun ending {-na}: harsh treatment of a person or an animal, also as punishment or revenge) (b:gawtbawl) (r:zd:19725/zd:13080) (q:draft)
gawtna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:sanction/sanctions) (d:a penalty that one country lays on another country, its leaders or its citizens, with <bawl> or <pia> and often {gam tungah}, where the first sense is the punishment of a person) (r:zd:24945/zd:15172/zd:20394) (q:draft)
gear = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:gear) (d:the gear of a car or bicycle, and the lever that changes it) (o:English) (r:zd:17450/zd:12021) (q:draft)
geelkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:plan together) (d:<geel> and <khawm> written as one word: plan or think out a thing jointly with others) (j:geel/khawm) (r:zd:21018/zd:25473) (q:draft)
geelkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:plan/devise/draw up) (d:<geel> plan and <khia> out written as one word: work out a plan for something; {a geelkhia} is the one who planned it) (j:geel/khia) (r:zd:24649/zd:24453) (q:draft)
geelkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:plan ahead/plan in advance/prearrange) (d:<geel>, plan, with <khol>, here beforehand: think out and settle in advance what is to be done) (j:geel/khol) (r:zd:24089/zd:25678/zd:22272) (q:draft)
geelkholhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:plan/advance planning/preparation) (d:<geelkholh>, plan beforehand, with the noun ending <na>: a plan made in advance, planning ahead) (b:geelkholh) (r:zd:16150/zd:12099/zd:23022) (q:draft)
geelna kinei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:be planned/there is a plan) (d:<geelna>, plan, and <kinei>, here be held or be had: a plan has been made, it is planned; what is planned stands before it, often with <ding> or <dingin>) (r:ts:9739/zd:21408) (q:draft)
geelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:plan for/arrange for/prepare for) (d:<geel>, plan, with <sak>: plan or arrange something for someone else, on his behalf) (b:geel) (r:zd:26626/zd:23191/zd:23386) (q:draft)
geelsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:arrangement/planning/provision) (d:<geelsak>, plan or arrange for someone, with the noun ending <na>: what is planned or arranged for others) (b:geelsak) (r:zd:13005/zd:16337) (q:draft)
geelsiam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:plan well/plan skilfully/manage well) (d:<geel>, plan, with <siam>, be skilled: plan or arrange a matter wisely, said of leaders and of anyone handling money, work or family affairs; not the craft of a designer) (r:zd:22157/zd:21066/zd:25178) (q:draft)
geelsiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:planning skill/strategy/tactics) (d:<geelsiam>, skilled in planning, with the noun ending {-na}: the skill of planning well; in war, tactics) (b:geelsiam) (r:zd:19676/zd:19410) (q:draft)
Geeltui = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:social) (w:Geeltui) (d:an old Zomi settlement in the Tedim area, named after <Ciimnuai> in the tradition of how the people spread) (r:zd:24227/zd:24072) (q:draft)
geen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:gen) (r:zd:24153) (q:draft)
gega = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:plainly/clearly/right there) (d:placed after a verb other than one of looking, such as <om>, be there, <thei>, know, or <ding>, stand: plainly and fixedly so, in full view; {thei gega} is knowing full well) (r:zd:22429/zd:21095) (q:draft, low confidence)
gegen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep saying/discuss/talk over) (d:<gen>, say, with its first syllable doubled: say at length or more than once; {i gegen sa} is what we have been saying) (b:gen) (r:zd:21989/zd:20888) (q:draft, low confidence)
gegu = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:indeed/plainly/as a matter of fact) (d:placed after a verb to stress that something is plainly or already the case, often before <napi>, although: even though it really is so) (r:zd:21864/zd:9445) (q:draft, low confidence)
geia = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:beside/at the side of/by) (d:<gei>, side, and <a> written as one word after a noun: at the side of, as {mei geia}, by the fire) (j:gei/a) (r:zd:17958) (q:draft)
geigai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:clinging/hanging on) (d:placed after a verb: holding on or staying attached without letting go, as in {len geigai}, keep hold of, and {om geigai}, stay on) (r:zd:9261/zd:21864) (q:draft)
geigei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:placed after a verb of holding, leaning or depending such as <khai> and <kisan>, for a state that goes on: still holding, still hanging on) (r:zd:23476) (q:draft, low confidence)
geikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:place near/place beside) (d:<gei>, side, and <khat>, one, written as one word after the name of a place: a spot near or beside it; {sanginn geikhat ah} is at a place near a school) (j:gei/khat) (r:zd:19923/zd:19180/zd:17628) (q:draft, low confidence)
geikhawng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:vicinity/around the side) (d:<gei>, side, and <khawng>, about, written as one word and followed by <ah>: somewhere beside or near) (j:gei/khawng) (r:zd:15471) (q:draft)
geilian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:right beside/just next to) (d:<gei>, side, with <lian>, exactly, written as one word: the spot directly beside something, usually with <ah>) (j:gei/lian) (r:zd:12913/zd:15669) (q:draft)
geinaiteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:whole surrounding area/vicinity) (d:{geinai teng} written as one word, <geinai>, close by, followed by a word for all of: everywhere close around a place) (b:geinai) (r:zd:18161/zd:12057) (q:draft)
geipan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:from beside/from near) (d:<gei>, side, and <pan>, from, written as one word: from the side of a place, starting from close by it) (j:gei/pan) (r:zd:11590) (q:draft)
geiteng = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:vicinity/surroundings/area around) (d:<gei>, side, with <teng>, all: the whole area beside a place, after a place name or a noun and mostly before <ah>, near or around that place; not only of a shore) (r:zd:14628/zd:14692/zd:13100) (q:draft)
geiteng ah = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:travel/everyday) (w:near/around/in the vicinity of/close by) (d:<geiteng>, the whole edge, from <gei>, side, with the place marker <ah>: placed after the name of a place, in the area round it, near it) (s:geiah) (r:zd:15101/zd:13133) (q:draft)
gel = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:plan/arrange) (d:think out beforehand what is to be done, a shorter spelling of <geel>; {gel khol} is plan ahead, and {a gen le a gel} is the saying and the planning) (s:geel) (r:zd:20587/zd:23899/zd:20004) (q:draft)
gelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:write) (d:put words down in letters. With <lai>, writing, it means write a letter or a document) (s:at/laigelh) (a:phiat) (q:draft)
gelha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:write/write and) (d:<gelh> and the linking <a> written as one word: wrote, and then) (j:gelh/a) (r:zd:20833/zd:9248) (q:draft)
gelhciangin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:when writing) (d:<gelh>, write, and <ciangin>, when, written as one word: when someone writes or when something is written) (j:gelh/ciangin) (r:zd:23929/zd:12353) (q:draft)
gelhdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:spelling/way of writing) (d:<gelh>, write, with <dan>, way: how a word or a language is written, its spelling or style of writing) (r:zd:23929/zd:9449/zd:15693) (q:draft)
gelhding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:to write/to be written) (d:<gelh> and <ding> written as one word: what is to be written, should write, the writing of something that is still to be done) (j:gelh/ding) (r:zd:20574/zd:12336) (q:draft)
gelhgelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:keep writing/write on/write down) (d:<gelh>, write, doubled: write on and on, or be in the course of writing) (b:gelh) (r:zd:21529/zd:9228/zd:22849) (q:draft)
gelhhi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:write/wrote) (d:<gelh>, write, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word) (j:gelh/hi) (r:zd:23432/zd:22203) (q:draft)
gelhin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:write/write down) (d:command form of <gelh> with the imperative ending <in>: write it; ends the clause or stands before <la>, where the linking form of the other sense goes on to a following verb) (r:zd:19453) (q:draft, low confidence)
gelhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:write/write out/write down) (d:<gelh>, write, and <khia>, out, written as one word: put something into writing and make it known, as a post, an article or a document) (j:gelh/khia) (r:zd:21392/zd:12763/zd:22365) (q:draft)
gelhkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/education) (w:written account/writing/post) (d:<gelhkhiat>, write out, with the noun suffix <na>: what someone has written and made known, as a post, a report or a statement; also the act of writing it) (b:gelhkhiat) (r:zd:19788/zd:16438/zd:15547) (q:draft)
gelhkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:have written/have already written) (d:<gelh>, write, and <khin>, already, written as one word: has written, the writing is done) (j:gelh/khin) (r:zd:15584/zd:23929) (q:draft)
gelhngamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:dare not write/not venture to write) (d:<gelh> and <ngamlo> written as one word) (j:gelh/ngamlo) (r:zd:14611) (q:draft)
gelhpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:rush out at once/hurry to the scene) (d:<gelh>, used here for set out in haste and not for write, with <pah>, at once: of firefighters and rescue teams, set out for the place of an accident straight away) (r:zd:14818/zd:19112) (q:draft, low confidence)
gelhphat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/education) (w:rewrite/write anew/redraft) (d:<gelh>, write, with <phat>, here anew: write a text again from the beginning, set beside <puah>, amend, when a constitution is spoken of) (r:zd:23476/zd:22475) (q:draft)
gelhsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:intend to write/plan to write/try to write) (d:<gelh>, write, with <sawm>, intend, written as one word: plan or set about writing something) (j:gelh/sawm) (r:zd:20576/zd:23929) (q:draft)
gelhsiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:write well/be good at writing) (d:<gelh>, write, with <siam>, skilled: write skilfully, or before a noun one who is skilled at writing) (j:gelh/siam) (r:zd:23929/zd:17860) (q:draft)
gelhsuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:write down/set down in writing) (d:<gelh> and <suk> written as one word: put something down in writing) (j:gelh/suk) (r:zd:15425/zd:18063) (q:draft)
gelhthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:can write/be able to write) (d:<gelh>, write, and <thei>, able, written as one word: be able to write, and also may write) (j:gelh/thei) (r:zd:21219/zd:24731) (q:draft)
gelhzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:way of writing/spelling/writing style) (d:<gelh>, write, and <zia>, way, written as one word: how something is written or spelled; {lai gelhzia} is the way of writing) (j:gelh/zia) (r:zd:17168/zd:9449/zd:19201) (q:draft)
gelhzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:be able to write/manage to write) (d:<gelh>, write, and <zo>, be able or finish, written as one word) (j:gelh/zo) (r:zd:25233/zd:24490) (q:draft)
gelin = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:both/the two) (d:<gel> and <in> written as one word: both of them, as the doers of the action) (j:gel/in) (r:ts:9524/zd:19166) (q:draft)
gelin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:plan/planning) (d:<geel>, plan, spelled short and written as one word with <in>: planning, having planned) (j:geel/in) (r:zd:17915) (q:draft, low confidence)
gelkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:plan/design/devise/draw up) (d:<gel>, plan, with <khia>, out: work out a plan for something to be built or set up, often as {gelkhia ding} in a list of aims; not slip away) (r:zd:23528/zd:24649) (q:draft, low confidence)
gelkhol = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:plan ahead/plan in advance/prepare beforehand) (d:<geel>, plan, in a shorter spelling, with <khol>, beforehand: think out and arrange something before the time comes) (r:zd:20647/zd:21456/zd:15933) (q:draft)
gelkholh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:geelkholh) (r:zd:23443/zd:18234) (q:draft)
gelkholhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:advance planning/plan/forethought) (d:noun from <geelkholh>, plan beforehand, written here with a short vowel: a plan made ahead of time; {gelkholhna nei} is plan ahead) (b:geelkholh) (r:zd:22742/zd:18026/zd:24358) (q:draft)
gelkholhsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:planned in advance/prearranged) (d:<gel>, plan, and <kholhsa>, already beforehand, written as one word: what has been planned ahead; the opposite is {gelkholhloh}, unplanned) (j:gel/kholhsa) (r:zd:15905) (q:draft)
gelnate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:plans/intentions) (d:plural of <gelna>, plan: plans, what someone intends to do) (b:gelna) (j:gelna/te) (r:zd:24947/zd:19600) (q:draft)
gelsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (j:geelsa) (r:zd:23422/zd:23777/zd:25932) (q:draft)
gelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:plan for/arrange for) (d:<geel>, plan, in a shorter spelling, with <sak>, for someone: plan or arrange something for another person, often said of what God plans for people; also written <geelsak>) (j:geel/sak) (r:zd:24231/zd:21252) (q:draft)
gelsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/everyday) (w:plan/arrangement/provision) (d:<gelsak>, plan for someone, with the noun suffix <na>: what someone, most often God, has planned or arranged for a person) (b:gelsak) (r:zd:20818/zd:21510) (q:draft)
gelsiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:plan well/plan wisely/be prudent) (d:a shorter spelling of <geel>, plan, with <siam>, skilled: think ahead and plan skilfully; often paired with {vaihawm siam}, manage well) (j:geel/siam) (r:zd:25919/zd:10731) (q:draft)
gelsiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:prudence/wise planning/good judgment) (d:<gelsiam>, plan wisely, with the noun suffix <na>: the skill of thinking ahead and arranging things well) (b:gelsiam) (j:gelsiam/na) (r:zd:20358/zd:12998) (q:draft)
gem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:lie in wait for/aim at/stalk) (d:watch someone closely so as to strike, as a hunter aims at his prey) (r:zd:15572) (q:draft, low confidence)
Gemas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Gemas) (d:a town in the state of Negeri Sembilan in Malaysia, a railway junction) (r:zd:16815) (q:draft)
gemgam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:placed after a describing word to stress a solid, heavy, stark or imposing look: {gum gemgam}, grim; {tul gemgam}, standing stiff and bare; {vom gemgam}, pitch black; {khauh gemgam}, stiff and hard) (r:zd:20874/zd:21121/ts:4569) (q:draft, low confidence)
gen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:tell/say/speak) (d:say or tell something in words; the basic verb of speaking, as in {thu gen}, speak a word) (s:ci)
gen lehang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:to put it/so to speak/if we say) (d:<gen>, say, and <lehang>, if we: if we say it, to put it; follows a word of manner and introduces a restatement, as in {lam khatin gen lehang}, in other words, and {thu dang khatin gen lehang}, to put it another way) (r:zd:11262/zd:23129) (q:draft)
gen siang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:tell plainly/say outright) (d:<gen>, say, and <siang>, clean: say a thing clearly and completely, holding nothing back; with <ngam> and <kei>, not dare to tell it plainly) (r:zd:23734) (q:draft, low confidence)
gena = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say/tell/preach) (d:<gen>, say, with the linking ending {-a} written on to it: saying, said and, before another verb; the Bible text writes {gen a}) (b:gen) (r:zd:9234/zd:9238) (q:draft)
genbang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:as said/what is said) (d:<gen>, say, and <bang>, like, written as one word after the one who speaks: as he says, according to what they said; {genbang mang} is do as told) (j:gen/bang) (r:zd:24276/zd:15249) (q:draft)
genbangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:as said/according to) (d:<gen> and <bangin> written as one word after the speaker: as that person said, according to what was said; {i genbangin} is as we said) (j:gen/bangin) (r:zd:20829) (q:draft)
genbehna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:further statement/additional remark/further explanation) (d:<genbeh>, say in addition, with the noun suffix <na>: what is said in addition; {a genbehna ah} is in his further remarks) (b:genbeh) (r:zd:11635/zd:12347/zd:24303) (q:draft)
genbehnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:want to add/wish to say further) (d:<genbeh>, say in addition, with <nop>, want, written as one word: what one wishes to say in addition) (j:genbeh/nop) (r:zd:20263/zd:24064) (q:draft)
genbek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:only say/merely say) (d:<gen>, say, with <bek>, only, written as one word: only say it, say it and no more) (j:gen/bek) (r:zd:20545) (q:draft, low confidence)
gencian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:explain clearly/state exactly/make clear) (d:<gen>, say, with <cian>, clearly, written as one word: say exactly how a thing is, explain it so that it is clear) (j:gen/cian) (r:zd:23281/zd:24217/zd:21900) (q:draft)
genciang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:when one says/when speaking) (d:<gen>, say, and <ciang>, when, written as one word: when someone says or tells something) (j:gen/ciang) (r:zd:12544/zd:21083) (q:draft)
genciangin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:when speaking/when one says) (d:<gen>, speak, and <ciangin>, when, written as one word: when someone speaks or says something) (j:gen/ciangin) (r:zd:20697/zd:21083/zd:21876) (q:draft)
gencianna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/politics) (w:clarification/explanation/statement) (d:<gencian>, explain clearly, with the noun ending {-na}: a statement that makes a matter clear; <gencianna nei> is give an explanation) (b:gencian) (r:ts:10582/zd:16790) (q:draft)
gencianna nei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:give a statement/give an explanation/clarify) (d:<gencianna>, a clarification, and <nei>, have: make a statement that explains a matter; the matter stands before it, often ending in {ci'n} or <zong>, and the one who speaks takes <in>) (r:ts:11378/zd:20839/zd:17830) (q:draft)
gencianthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:can say for certain/can state clearly) (d:<gen>, say, <cian>, clearly, and <thei>, can, written as one word: be able to say definitely; mostly negative, as in {ki gencianthei nailo}, it cannot yet be said for certain) (j:gen/cian/thei) (r:zd:12099/zd:13324/zd:19392) (q:draft)
genciantheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:can say clearly/can say for certain) (d:<gencian>, say clearly, and <theih>, be able, written as one word; mostly with a negative, as {bangmah genciantheih omnailo}, nothing can yet be said for certain) (j:gencian/theih) (r:zd:13220/zd:14949/zd:19385) (q:draft)
gendan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:way of saying/account/telling) (d:<gen>, say, with <dan>, manner, written as one word: the way something is said or told, and what someone says about a matter) (j:gen/dan) (r:zd:10797/zd:21357/zd:16924) (q:draft)
genden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep saying/always say/say repeatedly) (d:<gen>, say, and <den>, always, written as one word: say something again and again or all the time) (j:gen/den) (r:zd:15951/zd:19174) (q:draft)
Gender = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:gender/sex) (d:the state of being male or female; mostly in English phrases such as {Gender Equality}) (o:English) (r:zd:14577/zd:11668) (q:draft, low confidence)
gending = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will say/to say) (d:<gen>, say, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will say, or what is to be said) (j:gen/ding) (r:zd:21085/zd:21796/zd:21155) (q:draft)
Generator = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:generator) (d:a machine that produces electric power) (o:English) (r:zd:22584/zd:25357/zd:23993) (q:draft)
Geneva = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics) (w:Geneva) (d:city in Switzerland where offices of the United Nations are; {Geneva thukimna} is the Geneva Convention) (r:zd:9124) (q:draft)
gengenloh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:let alone/not to mention) (d:<gengen> and <loh> written as one word, placed after a noun or clause: not to speak of that, let alone that; what follows is the stronger case, often with <nangawn>, even) (j:gengen/loh) (r:zd:21862/zd:25390) (q:draft)
gengensa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:already said/said before) (d:<gengen> with the ending {-sa}, already done: what has been said, or said more than once, earlier; {i gengensa mah bangin} is as we have already said) (b:gengen) (r:zd:16336/zd:20276) (q:draft)
gengente = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:those who keep saying/those who talk of) (d:<gengen>, say again and again, with the plural <te>, written as one word: the people who keep saying something, or the things that are said) (b:gengen) (j:gengen/te) (r:zd:9439/zd:16256) (q:draft)
genhak = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:hard to say/hard to explain) (d:said of a matter and not of a person: difficult to put into words or to explain, as in {gen taktak ni ci lehang genhak}, when one really tries to say it, it is hard to say) (r:zd:21925) (q:draft, low confidence)
genhi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:said/say/tell) (d:<gen>, say, and the sentence-final <hi> written as one word: closes a statement of what someone said) (j:gen/hi) (r:zd:19577/zd:21003) (q:draft)
genhthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social) (j:genthei) (r:zd:17060/zd:22827) (q:draft)
genhtheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (j:gentheihna) (r:zd:20627) (q:draft)
genhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:worth saying/fit to be said) (d:<gen>, say, with <huai>: that ought to be said or is proper to say; {genhuai lo} is what should not be said) (j:gen/huai) (r:zd:20808/zd:20979) (q:draft)
genkawmkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep saying/say while) (d:<gen>, say, and <kawmkawm>, all the while, written as one word: go on saying, or say while doing something else) (j:gen/kawmkawm) (r:zd:13151/zd:15456) (q:draft)
genkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not say/not tell) (d:<gen>, say, and the negative <kei> written as one word: do not say, did not say) (j:gen/kei) (r:zd:14728/zd:18924) (q:draft)
genkhiakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:have stated/have declared) (d:<genkhia>, declare, and <khin>, already, written as one word: has already said or announced) (j:genkhia/khin) (r:zd:20013/zd:19478) (q:draft)
genkhialh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:misstatement/slip of the tongue) (d:<gen> and <khialh> written as one word: something said wrongly, a mistake in what one has said or written) (j:gen/khialh) (r:zd:16651/zd:17213) (q:draft)
genkhialo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:not disclose/not say) (d:<genkhia>, speak out, and <lo>, not, written as one word: did not say or make known) (j:genkhia/lo) (r:zd:11560/zd:14701) (q:draft)
genkhianailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:not yet disclosed/not yet announced) (d:<genkhia> and <nailo> written as one word, mostly after <ki>: has not yet been stated or made public) (j:genkhia/nailo) (r:zd:20335/zd:12848) (q:draft)
genkhianuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:want to disclose/be willing to state) (d:<genkhia> and <nuam> written as one word: be willing to make something known; {genkhianuam nailo} is not yet willing to say) (j:genkhia/nuam) (r:zd:12658/zd:17461) (q:draft)
genkhiapah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:tell at once/announce immediately) (d:<genkhia> and <pah> written as one word: speak out or make known right away) (j:genkhia/pah) (r:zd:12128/zd:20466) (q:draft)
genkhiata = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:have announced/has stated) (d:<genkhia>, speak out, and <ta> written as one word: has now announced, has stated) (j:genkhia/ta) (r:zd:11011/zd:12639) (q:draft)
genkhiatbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:state further/add/also announce) (d:<genkhiat>, speak out, with <beh>, in addition, written as one word: say something more in a statement; usual in news after {ci'n}, saying) (j:genkhiat/beh) (r:zd:19234/zd:15602) (q:draft)
genkhiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:to announce/to state/will tell) (d:<genkhiat> and the future marker <ding> written as one word: to say something out, to make it known) (j:genkhiat/ding) (r:zd:13352/zd:11376) (q:draft)
genkhiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:be able to say/can state/can tell) (d:<genkhia>, state or declare, and <thei>, can, written as one word: be able to say or state something, mostly with a negative, cannot yet be said) (j:genkhia/thei) (r:zd:12628/zd:19277) (q:draft)
genkhiatkhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/politics) (w:permission to disclose/leave to make public) (d:<genkhiat>, speak out, with <khuan>, permission, written as one word: the right or permission to make something public; {genkhiatkhuan omlo} is it may not be disclosed) (j:genkhiat/khuan) (r:zd:11782/zd:12290) (q:draft)
genkhiattheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:be able to state/can be told) (d:<genkhiat>, state or announce, with <theih>, be able, written as one word; {genkhiattheih omnailo} is there is nothing yet that can be stated) (j:genkhiat/theih) (r:zd:17969/zd:12974) (q:draft)
genkhiaziau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:say briefly/state shortly) (d:<genkhia> and <ziau> written as one word: say something out briefly and leave it at that, often closing a report of what someone said) (j:genkhia/ziau) (r:zd:12002/zd:14738) (q:draft)
genkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:discuss together/talk over/talk about together) (d:<gen>, speak, and <khop>, together, written as one word: talk something over with one another) (s:genkhawm) (j:gen/khop) (r:zd:23552/ts:838) (q:draft)
genkhopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:discussion/talks/conference) (d:<gen>, speak, and <khopna>, doing together, written as one word: a talking over of a matter together; {thuthak genkhopna} is a press conference) (j:gen/khopna) (r:ts:11032/zd:25415) (q:draft)
genkhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:permission to speak/right to speak/opportunity to speak) (d:<gen>, speak, and <khuan>, permission, written as one word: the right or the chance to say something) (j:gen/khuan) (r:zd:11409/zd:20850) (q:draft)
genkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:reply/response/retelling) (d:<genkik>, say again or report back, with the noun suffix <na>: what is said in reply, or a telling again of what was said) (b:genkik) (r:ts:2288/zd:24172) (q:draft)
genkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:need to say/need to mention) (d:<gen>, say, with <kul>, be necessary; {genkul lo in} is without needing to be told, it goes without saying) (j:gen/kul) (r:zd:10725/zd:21369) (q:draft)
genlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:say further/go on to tell) (d:<gen>, say, with <lai>, still or more, written as one word: say in addition, still tell; {ka genlai in} is while I was speaking) (b:gen) (r:zd:25322/zd:21876) (q:draft, low confidence)
genleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one says/when one speaks) (d:<gen> and <leh> written as one word: if or when someone says or tells) (j:gen/leh) (r:zd:13154/zd:21075) (q:draft)
genleng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if I say/to put it) (d:<gen>, say, and <leng>, if I, written as one word: if I say it, to put it; introduces a statement after a word of manner, as in {a tomin genleng}, to put it briefly) (j:gen/leng) (r:zd:19971/zd:17333/zd:15600) (q:draft)
genloh = (i:2) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:let alone/not to mention/much less) (d:placed after a noun or clause and before a second, stronger case, often with <zong> or <nangawn> following: without even speaking of the first, the second holds too) (r:zd:25130/zd:23361/zd:21095) (q:draft)
genma = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:before saying/before speaking of) (d:<gen>, say, and <ma>, before, written as one word: before telling or speaking of something) (j:gen/ma) (r:zd:12044/zd:19139) (q:draft)
genmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just as said/the very thing said) (d:<gen>, say, and the emphatic <mah> written as one word: in {a genmah bang in}, exactly as it says) (j:gen/mah) (r:zd:16428) (q:draft, low confidence)
genna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:reference/meaning) (d:what a word or an expression refers to, in an explanation that ends in {genna hi} or {genna ahi hi}: it means, it speaks of; not a statement made by a person) (r:zd:23394/zd:23780) (q:draft)
gennawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say any more/speak further) (d:<gen>, say, and <nawn>, any more, written as one word; used with a negative: not say any more) (j:gen/nawn) (r:zd:21869) (q:draft, low confidence)
genngam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:dare to say/speak boldly) (d:<gen>, say, and <ngam>, dare, written as one word: have the courage to say something) (j:gen/ngam) (r:zd:12564/zd:21075) (q:draft)
genngamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:dare not say/not dare to speak) (d:<gen>, say, <ngam>, dare, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not have the courage to say something) (j:gen/ngam/lo) (r:zd:16606/zd:17426) (q:draft)
genngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have said before/have told) (d:<gen> and <ngei> written as one word: have said or told something at an earlier time) (j:gen/ngei) (r:zd:13181/zd:23322/zd:15416) (q:draft)
genni = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:let us say) (d:<gen>, say, with the ending {-ni}, let us, written as one word; {a tomin genni cileng} is to put it briefly) (j:gen/ni) (r:zd:23432/zd:25919/zd:17161) (q:draft)
gennop bulpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:main point/chief point/gist) (d:<gennop>, what one wants to say, and <bulpi>, the base or chief part: the main point that a speaker or writer wants to make; usually after <i>, <ih> or <na> and followed by <in>, <ah> or {ahih leh} to introduce that point) (r:zd:25123/zd:21063) (q:draft)
gennuam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:mean/refer to) (d:with <a> before it and <hi>, {i hi} or <hiam> after: what a word or statement is meant to say, or whom it refers to, not a wish to speak) (r:zd:22293/zd:22116/zd:21607) (q:draft)
gennuamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:not want to tell/be unwilling to say) (d:<gen>, tell, and <nuamlo>, not want, written as one word: not want to tell or name something; {a min gennuamlo} is who did not want to give his name) (j:gen/nuamlo) (r:ts:3227/zd:12752) (q:draft)
genpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:tell at once/say immediately) (d:<gen> and <pah> written as one word: tell or report something right away) (j:gen/pah) (r:zd:20039/zd:21035) (q:draft)
genpak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:say briefly/mention/tell in short) (d:<gen>, say, and <pak>, for a short while, written as one word: say something briefly; {atom in genpak leng} is to put it briefly) (j:gen/pak) (r:zd:21305/zd:19679/zd:22116) (q:draft)
genpan = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:from what was said/from the words of) (d:<gen>, say, and <pan>, from, written as one word after the name of a speaker: from what that person said; a different use is begin to say) (j:gen/pan) (r:zd:23832) (q:draft, low confidence)
genpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what is said/what someone says) (d:<gen> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, after a possessor: what that person says or said, as the topic of the sentence) (j:gen/pen) (r:zd:20549/zd:23616) (q:draft)
genphapha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:say again and again/stress/urge) (d:<genpha> with its last part doubled: tell something repeatedly or with emphasis, to warn or to reassure) (b:genpha) (r:zd:25932/zd:13233) (q:draft)
genphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:tell/say to/pass on) (d:<gen> and <phei> written as one word: say a thing across to another person, tell it to someone else) (j:gen/phei) (r:zd:23556/zd:15724) (q:draft)
genpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:main theme/main message/chief topic) (d:<gen>, speak, with <pi>, chief: what someone chiefly speaks about; {genpi in nei} is make something the main theme of one's speaking) (r:zd:10793/zd:15274) (q:draft)
genpihden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:always tell/keep telling) (d:<genpih> and <den> written as one word: tell someone again and again) (j:genpih/den) (r:zd:11508/zd:12715) (q:draft)
genpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:discussion/talks/advocacy) (d:<genpih>, talk a matter over with someone, with the noun suffix <na>: talks held with others, or speaking up to them for a cause) (b:genpih) (r:ts:9370) (q:draft)
gensa mah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:as already said/as mentioned) (d:<gensa>, already said, and <mah>, the very: always followed by <bangin>, {gensa mah bangin}, just as was said before; a pronoun such as <ih> or <ka> or the words {a tung a}, above, stand before it) (r:zd:24029/zd:24607) (q:draft)
gensateng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:all that was said/everything said) (d:<gen>, say, and <sateng>, all that, written as one word: all that has been said) (j:gen/sateng) (r:zd:26658/zd:17613) (q:draft)
gensawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:intend to say/be about to say/mean to tell) (d:<gen>, say, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word) (j:gen/sawm) (r:zd:11761/zd:21066) (q:draft)
gensawnding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:to pass on/to tell others) (d:<gensawn>, pass on, and <ding>, to, written as one word: that one should tell it on to others) (j:gensawn/ding) (r:zd:13209/zd:14654) (q:draft)
gensiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:tell plainly/state clearly/tell fully) (d:<gen>, tell, with <siang>, clean, written as one word: tell a matter clearly and completely, leaving nothing hidden) (j:gen/siang) (r:zd:23935/zd:16227/zd:10910) (q:draft)
