guanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:putting in/loading/insertion) (d:<guan>, put into, with the noun ending <na>: the putting in of a thing, what is laid down, or what a thing is put into, as {aki guanna box}, the box they were packed in) (b:guan) (r:zd:19529/zd:24313) (q:draft)
guansa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:loaded/packed/laden) (d:<guan>, put into, with the ending for what is already done: already put in or loaded; {van guansa} is packed goods) (b:guan) (r:zd:24310/zd:19197) (q:draft)
guansak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:pack for/load/put in for) (d:<guan>, put into, and <sak>, written as one word: put things into a bag or onto a vehicle for someone, pack provisions for a traveller) (j:guan/sak) (r:zd:23616/zd:22550) (q:draft)
guansawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to put into) (d:<guan>, put into, and <sawm>, intend or try, written as one word: try to put someone or something into a place) (j:guan/sawm) (r:zd:18102) (q:draft, low confidence)
guapguap = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/food) (w:crunchingly/with a grating noise) (d:word that imitates a crunching or grating sound, as of chewing or of a machine, placed after the verb or after <ging>, sound) (r:zd:23037/zd:15103) (q:draft)
