Gurkha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social/politics) (w:Gurkha/Nepali) (d:the Nepali people, many of whom came to Myanmar and India as soldiers of the British) (r:ts:617) (q:draft)
guta damiah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:thieves and robbers/robbers/criminals) (d:<guta>, thief, and <damiah>, robber, said together as one word for those who steal and rob, and for theft and robbery as a danger; {guta damiah te} are the robbers) (r:zd:15056/zd:15477) (q:draft)
gutabuluh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:thieves and robbers/thief and robber) (d:<guta> and <buluh> written as one word: thieves and robbers as one class of wrongdoers) (j:guta/buluh) (r:zd:20131) (q:draft)
