Hallpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:large hall/main hall) (d:the English word hall with the ending {-pi}, big: a large hall for meetings and gatherings) (o:English, hall) (r:zd:26660/zd:10743) (q:draft)
halmawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:set on fire/burn recklessly) (d:<hal>, burn, and <mawk>, thoughtlessly, written as one word: set a thing on fire rashly or to the surprise of others) (j:hal/mawk) (r:zd:11495) (q:draft)
halsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/home) (w:lit/burning/alight) (d:<hal>, burn, with <sa> marking the action as done, written as one word: already set alight, said of charcoal or a cigarette) (j:hal/sa) (r:zd:17355/zd:19431) (q:draft)
halsim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/travel) (w:every/at intervals of) (d:placed after a length of time and followed by <in>: at each such interval, as {Minute 20 halsim in}, every 20 minutes) (r:zd:16229/zd:12420) (q:draft)
halta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:every/at intervals of) (d:placed after a number with a unit of time or count: once in every so many, at intervals of that length; {kha 6 halta} is every six months) (r:zd:21025/zd:18893/ts:301) (q:draft)
ham = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:speak/talk/utter) (d:of people, speak; mostly paired with <pau> in {pau leh ham}, a person's speech and way of talking) (s:pau) (r:zd:19900/zd:11891) (q:draft)
