hamphate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:fortunate people/the blessed) (d:<hampha>, fortunate, with the plural <te>; mostly as {mi hamphate}, people who are fortunate or blessed) (b:hampha) (r:zd:25106/zd:11831/zd:17599) (q:draft)
hamphathuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:fortunate/blessed/beneficial) (d:<hamphat>, benefit, with <huai>, worthy of: a matter to count as good fortune; {hamphathuai sa} is consider oneself fortunate) (j:hamphat/huai) (r:zd:15527/zd:21845) (q:draft)
hampi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/food) (w:coarse/crude/raw/unrefined) (d:rough and not worked fine; of food coarse, of goods raw and unprocessed, of a piece of writing only a rough outline) (r:zd:21119/zd:22157) (q:draft)
