hamsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (j:haksa) (r:ts:6447/zd:12600/zd:14903) (q:draft)
hamsa sa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find difficult/find hard) (d:<hamsa>, difficult, and <sa>, here the verb feel or consider, not hot: to find something hard; the thing found hard stands before it, usually a verb with <ding>) (r:zd:22171/zd:15681/zd:22757) (q:draft)
hamsalai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:still difficult/still hard) (d:<hamsa>, difficult, and <lai>, still, written as one word) (j:hamsa/lai) (r:zd:13352/zd:20167) (q:draft)
hamsapi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very difficult/very hard) (d:<hamsa>, difficult, with the augmentative <pi>: very hard or troublesome; {hamsapi in} is with great difficulty) (b:hamsa) (r:zd:23428/zd:20418) (q:draft)
hamsasak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:find difficult/make difficult) (d:<hamsa>, difficult, with <sak>, written as one word: find something hard to do, or make it hard for someone) (j:hamsa/sak) (r:zd:15276/zd:18911) (q:draft)
hamsat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:hard/difficult/hardship) (d:form of <hamsa>, hard or in difficulty, used before a noun and in dependent clauses; also as a noun, hardship) (s:haksat) (r:zd:25253/zd:21130/zd:16254) (q:draft)
hamsatak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:with difficulty/in hardship) (d:<hamsa>, hard, and <tak> written as one word, followed by <in>: with difficulty, in hard conditions) (j:hamsa/tak) (r:zd:15816/zd:11972) (q:draft)
hamsatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:hardship/difficulty/trouble) (d:<hamsat>, a form of <hamsa>, hard, with the noun ending <na>: what is hard to bear or to do) (s:haksatna) (b:hamsa) (r:ts:3125/zd:23067/zd:14942) (q:draft)
hamsatnate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:hardships/difficulties/troubles) (d:<hamsatna> and the plural <te> written as one word: hardships, difficulties) (b:hamsatna) (j:hamsatna/te) (r:zd:22755/zd:10725) (q:draft)
hamsatzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:hardship/how hard it is) (d:<hamsat>, hard, and <zia>, way, written as one word: the way in which people have it hard, the extent of their hardship) (j:hamsat/zia) (r:zd:22377/zd:17437) (q:draft)
hamsia = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:unfortunate/unlucky/wretched) (d:of a person, without good fortune or badly off, the opposite of <hampha>; used as a predicate, as in {hamsia mahmah uh hi}, they are very unfortunate, and {hamsia kisa}, count oneself unfortunate) (a:hampha) (r:zd:17961/zd:24320/zd:22812) (q:draft)
hamtangding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:must without fail/be sure to) (d:<hamtang>, without fail, and the particle <ding> written as one word after a verb: it must be done without fail, said of a rule or firm advice) (j:hamtang/ding) (r:zd:11759/zd:11590/zd:20343) (q:draft)
hamtangh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:without fail/surely/necessarily) (d:another spelling of <hamtang>; placed after a verb in present-day writing it says that the thing surely happens or must be done without fail) (j:hamtang) (r:zd:19166/zd:22412) (q:draft)
hamtangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:without fail/be sure to) (d:<hamtang>, without fail, with the <in> that ends a command, written as one word at the end of an instruction: be sure to do it; after <kei>, on no account do it) (j:hamtang/in) (r:zd:21664/zd:23538) (q:draft)
hamte = (i:3) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:elders/the aged/older ones) (d:<ham.2>, old, with the plural <te>: people advanced in age, as {u hamte}, the older brothers and sisters, {a tek a hamte}, the old and aged, and {numei hamte}, older unmarried women) (r:zd:25687/zd:21701) (q:draft)
hamte = (i:4) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:language/speech/tongue) (d:<ham.3>, speak, in the pair {ih pau ih hamte}, our speech and language, the mother tongue of a people; not the cries of animals) (s:pau) (r:zd:22136) (q:draft, low confidence)
hanawt = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:brush teeth) (d:<ha>, teeth, with <nawt>, rub: brush or clean the teeth) (r:zd:16878/zd:14587) (q:draft)
hanawtna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/health) (w:toothbrush) (d:<ha>, tooth, with <nawt>, rub or scrub, and the ending {-na}: the brush with which the teeth are cleaned) (r:zd:16878/zd:21826) (q:draft)
hanciam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try/strive/make an effort) (d:make an effort to do or reach something; it often follows a purpose clause with <dingin> or <nadingin>) (s:hahkat/hamciam) (r:20.2.2) (q:draft)
hanciamding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will try/will strive) (d:<hanciam> and <ding> written as one word: will make an effort, is to strive) (j:hanciam/ding) (r:zd:20263/zd:23443/zd:19868) (q:draft)
hanciamhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:worth striving for/deserving effort) (d:<hanciam> and <huai> written as one word: that ought to be striven for, worth making an effort to do) (j:hanciam/huai) (r:zd:25169/zd:17055) (q:draft)
hanciamkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:strive together/work together/make a joint effort) (d:<hanciam> and <khawm> written as one word: make an effort together with others) (j:hanciam/khawm) (r:zd:10952/zd:20746) (q:draft)
hanciamkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:try again/strive again) (d:<hanciam>, try, and <kik>, again, written as one word: make an effort once more) (j:hanciam/kik) (r:zd:21991/zd:24343) (q:draft)
hanciamnopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:willingness to strive/eagerness/drive) (d:<hanciam> and <nopna> written as one word: the wish to make an effort) (j:hanciam/nopna) (r:zd:24244/zd:20805) (q:draft)
hanciampah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try at once/set about trying) (d:<hanciam>, try, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: begin at once to make an effort) (j:hanciam/pah) (r:zd:26566/zd:14787) (q:draft)
hanciampih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:help to achieve/work hard for/strive with) (d:<hanciam>, strive, with <pih>, together with or for: make an effort for someone or for a cause, help someone to reach something) (b:hanciam) (r:zd:19593/zd:12470/zd:10742) (q:draft)
hanciampihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:effort/support/help) (d:<hanciampih> with the noun suffix <na>: the effort someone makes for another or for a cause; {hanciampihna tawh} is through the efforts of) (b:hanciampih) (r:ts:6943/zd:23797) (q:draft)
hanciamsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:strive for/work hard at/press on with) (d:<hanciam> with an ending of direction: put great effort into a set aim, often after <nading>; {ki hanciamsan} is efforts are being made) (b:hanciam) (r:zd:20629/ts:7399) (q:draft)
hanciamtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:diligently/with effort/earnestly) (d:<hanciam>, strive, with <tak>, which makes an adverb of manner, mostly as {hanciamtak in}: with real effort, trying hard) (j:hanciam/tak) (r:zd:20860/zd:24276) (q:draft)
hanciamtek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:each strive/all try hard) (d:<hanciam>, make an effort, and <tek>, each one, written as one word: every one of them tries hard) (j:hanciam/tek) (r:zd:16031/zd:19667) (q:draft)
hancian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:hanciam) (r:zd:25137/zd:13238) (q:draft)
Handbag = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:handbag) (d:a woman's bag for money and small things, in the articles usually written with a capital) (s:sumbawm) (o:English) (r:zd:12901/zd:16676) (q:draft)
handgel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:hand gel/hand sanitizer) (d:a gel for cleaning the hands without water) (o:English, hand gel) (r:zd:25199/zd:23812) (q:draft)
Handgun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:handgun/pistol) (d:a small gun held in one hand, named in reports of shootings, often together with <thau>, gun) (o:English) (r:zd:20531/zd:17439) (q:draft, low confidence)
Handphone = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:mobile phone/cell phone/handphone) (d:a mobile telephone, the word used in Malaysian and Singaporean English) (o:English) (r:zd:11874/zd:20227) (q:draft)
hang = (i:4) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:we) (d:sentence-final marker of the first person plural including the hearer, placed after a verb or after <hi>: {hi hang} is we are, and {lamen hang} is we hope; not the noun reason) (r:zd:24963/ts:3503/zd:25928) (q:draft)
hang = (i:5) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/even though/though) (d:after a verb, without <in>, shows that what follows happens in spite of it, the short form of <hangin>; {ahih hang} is even so) (s:hangin) (r:zd:24119/ts:6447) (q:draft)
hangaa = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:because of/due to) (d:<hang>, reason, and <aa> written as one word, placed after a noun or clause: because of it, the same as <hangin> after a noun) (j:hang/aa) (r:zd:23787/zd:23988) (q:draft)
hangbek = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:only because of/only for) (d:<hang>, reason, and <bek>, only, written as one word after a noun: only because of it, for that alone) (j:hang/bek) (r:zd:25916/zd:22203) (q:draft)
hangh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:we) (d:sentence-final marker for a first person plural subject that includes the hearer, used in place of <i> before the verb and <hi> after it, as {hi hangh}, we are; also written <hang>; compare <ung>) (r:zd:19147/zd:23731/zd:14755) (q:draft)
hanghi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:is because of/is due to) (d:<hang> and <hi> written as one word, after a noun or clause: it is because of that) (j:hang/hi) (r:zd:21876/zd:12990) (q:draft)
hanghiam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:why/for what reason) (d:<hang> and <hiam> written as one word, after <bang>, what: {bang hanghiam} asks why, and {bang hanghiam cih leh} introduces the reason, because) (j:hang/hiam) (r:zd:18241/zd:20763) (q:draft)
hangin = (i:2) (t:ppm) (f:everyday/media) (w:because of/due to/on account of) (d:placed after a noun or a noun in {-na}, gives the cause of what follows: {gal hangin} is because of the war, {tua hangin} because of that; after a verb the same word means although) (r:ts:12490/ts:3284/ts:12074) (q:draft)
hanginzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even though/even because of) (d:<hangin> and <zong> written as one word: after a verb, even though; after a noun, even because of it, or because of it too) (j:hangin/zong) (r:zd:17547/zd:19109/zd:15300) (q:draft)
hangleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:because of and) (d:<hang>, reason, and <leh>, and, written as one word: {A hangleh B hangin} is because of A and because of B) (j:hang/leh) (r:zd:12436/zd:17824) (q:draft)
hangmah = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:because of/precisely because of) (d:<hang> reason and the emphatic <mah> written as one word after a noun or <tua>: for that very reason; {tua hangmah in} is for that very reason) (j:hang/mah) (r:zd:24531/zd:25224) (q:draft)
hangmaw = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:is it because of) (d:<hang>, reason, with the question word <maw>, written as one word after a noun: is it because of this, said of the first of two possible causes, the second following) (j:hang/maw) (r:zd:14642/zd:21876) (q:draft)
hangpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the reason is) (d:<hang>, reason, and the topic marker <pen>, written as one word; {a hangpen} introduces the reason for what was just said) (j:hang/pen) (r:zd:24320) (q:draft)
hangsandan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:boldness/how daring) (d:<hangsan>, bold, and <dan>, manner, written as one word: the way someone is bold, how daring they are) (j:hangsan/dan) (r:zd:11130) (q:draft, low confidence)
hangsanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:courage/bravery/boldness) (d:<hangsan>, brave, with the noun suffix <na>) (s:hanna/ngamna) (b:hangsan) (r:zd:17958/zd:25165/zd:16441) (q:draft)
hangsansak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:embolden/make brave/give courage) (d:<hangsan>, brave, with the causative <sak>: make someone bold; with <ki> before it, make oneself bold, act the brave one) (b:hangsan) (r:zd:25106) (q:draft)
hangsantak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:bravely/boldly/courageously) (d:<hangsan> and <tak> written as one word, mostly followed by <in>: bravely, with courage) (j:hangsan/tak) (r:zd:21085/zd:11619/zd:25678) (q:draft)
hangsantakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:bravely/boldly/courageously) (d:<hangsantak> and <in> written as one word: in a brave manner, with courage) (j:hangsantak/in) (r:zd:23444/zd:23733) (q:draft)
hangtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:bravely/boldly) (d:<hang>, brave, and <tak> written as one word, followed by <in> or {-a}: bravely, without fear, said of deciding and of speaking out) (j:hang/tak) (r:zd:24638/zd:19676) (q:draft)
hangtawh = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday/media) (w:because of/on account of/due to) (d:<hang> and <tawh> written as one word after a noun: because of it, on account of it; frequent in news reports for the reason of an arrest or a charge) (j:hang/tawh) (r:zd:17731/zd:15431/zd:12708) (q:draft)
hangte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:reasons/causes) (d:<hang> in the sense reason with the plural <te>, not the brave: the reasons for something, as in {a hangte}, its reasons, or after a list of nouns that name the causes) (r:zd:20560/zd:12436) (q:draft)
hanguh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:because they/their reason) (d:<hang>, reason, and the plural <uh> written as one word, after a verb or <man>: it is because they do so) (j:hang/uh) (r:zd:21119) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hangzhou = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/media) (w:Hangzhou) (d:a city in the east of China) (r:zd:14812) (q:draft)
hangzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:also because of/even though) (d:<hang>, reason, and <zong>, also, written as one word: after a noun, also because of it; after a verb with <loh>, even if not) (j:hang/zong) (r:zd:24490/zd:17651) (q:draft, low confidence)
hani = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:gum/gums) (d:the flesh around the roots of the teeth; <ha> is tooth) (r:zd:20814/zd:16878) (q:draft)
hanla = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:victory song/triumph chant) (d:a song of triumph sung, with the firing of guns, over big game or an enemy that has been killed, and at the funeral of a man of renown; {hanla sa} is sing it) (r:zd:23129/zd:24227) (q:draft)
hanlam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social/travel) (w:to the graveyard/toward the grave) (d:<han>, grave, and <lam>, direction, written as one word: toward the burial place) (j:han/lam) (r:zd:11382) (q:draft, low confidence)
hanlung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:zeal/spirit/determination) (d:used with <ciam> as {hanlung ciam}, take heart, be zealous and determined in a common effort) (r:zd:16438/zd:15586) (q:draft, low confidence)
hanlungciam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:strive/make an effort) (d:poetic word, apparently a fuller form of <hanciam>, strive; known from the Zomi motto {Zomi te lung kituak, hanlungciam khangto diam}) (r:zd:16087) (q:draft, low confidence)
hanmual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:cemetery/graveyard/burial ground) (d:<han>, grave, with <mual>, hill: the place where the dead of a community are buried) (r:zd:17375/ts:2009) (q:draft)
