hansanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:courage/bravery/boldness/daring) (d:courage, also in the bad sense of rash daring; <hansan> is another spelling of <hangsan>, brave, here with the noun suffix <na>) (b:hangsan) (r:zd:21876/zd:19783/zd:17271) (q:draft)
hansuang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:gravestone/tombstone/headstone) (d:<han>, grave, with <suang>, stone: the stone set on a grave, on which words are written) (r:zd:9264/zd:9216) (q:draft)
hansung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:inside of the tomb/graveyard/cemetery) (d:<han>, tomb, and <sung>, in, written as one word: the inside of a tomb, or the grounds of a cemetery) (j:han/sung) (r:zd:12196/zd:17779) (q:draft)
