hehnepsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/family) (w:comfort/console) (d:<hehnep> and <sak> written as one word: give comfort to those who mourn, mostly in a wish that God may do so) (j:hehnep/sak) (r:zd:15714/zd:12371) (q:draft)
hehpihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:to pity/to have mercy on) (d:<hehpih>, have mercy on, and <ding> written as one word: to pity, one who is to be pitied) (j:hehpih/ding) (r:zd:16869) (q:draft)
hehpihlua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:pity greatly/have great compassion on) (d:<hehpih>, pity, and <lua>, very much, written as one word) (j:hehpih/lua) (r:zd:11138/zd:24220) (q:draft)
hehsemsem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:grow angrier/become more angry) (d:<heh> and <semsem> written as one word: become more and more angry) (j:heh/semsem) (r:zd:19609/zd:20461) (q:draft)
hehsuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:provoke/anger/enrage) (d:<heh>, angry, with <suah>, bring out: make someone angry; with <ki>, be angry with each other, fall out; {hehsuah huai} is provoking) (s:hehsak) (b:heh) (j:heh/suah) (r:zd:19033/zd:21110/zd:20624) (q:draft)
hehthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be angry/be outraged) (d:<heh>, angry, and <thei> written as one word: become angry at something seen or heard, mostly {hehthei mahmah}, be very angry, said of the public) (j:heh/thei) (r:zd:19932/zd:19939) (q:draft)
heih = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday) (w:hey) (d:a call to get attention or to express surprise or annoyance at the start of what is said) (r:zd:16321) (q:draft, low confidence)
Heilei = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Heilei) (d:a Zomi village in Chin State, Myanmar, listed among the villages where the Teizang dialect is spoken) (r:zd:19952) (q:draft)
HeileiKhua = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Heilei village) (d:<Heilei> and <khua> written as one word: the village of Heilei) (j:Heilei/khua) (r:zd:19952) (q:draft)
Heilongjiang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Heilongjiang) (d:province in the north-east of China, with the city of Harbin) (r:zd:20225/zd:17003) (q:draft)
heisa = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:flower) (d:a flowering tree or plant of the Zo hills, named among its flowers; in song language also used in comparisons) (r:ts:3375) (q:draft, low confidence)
hek = (i:2) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:turn/steer/move) (d:turn something this way or that, as the neck turns the head; {mit hek} is a movement of the eyes as a signal, and {hek leh tat} is all that one does, one's conduct) (r:zd:20798/zd:12373) (q:draft)
hekna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:accusation/charge) (d:<hek>, accuse, with the noun ending <na>: a charge brought against someone; {hekna thuak} is the one accused) (b:hek) (r:zd:9124) (q:draft, low confidence)
heksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:turn aside/divert/steer away) (d:<hek>, turn, with the causative <sak>, written as one word: make a thing turn another way; {thukawng heksak} is change the subject of the talk) (j:hek/sak) (r:zd:23985) (q:draft, low confidence)
hekzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:conduct/behaviour/manner) (d:<hek>, turn or move, with <zia>, way: the way a person or people carry themselves; paired with <tatzia>) (s:tatzia) (r:zd:17212/zd:21848) (q:draft, low confidence)
hel = (i:3) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:court/woo) (d:of a young man, visit and seek the love of a girl, with <nungak> or <zawl> before it) (r:zd:24160) (q:draft, low confidence)
helh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:intersperse/mix in/insert) (d:put something in among other things, as a story or a remark into what is said; {ki helh} is be mixed in, be among) (r:zd:18204/zd:17444/zd:16951) (q:draft)
helhuai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:be worth including/should be mixed in) (d:<hel>, mix in or include, with <huai>, worthy of: it is good or proper to add or include it) (j:hel/huai) (r:zd:24276/zd:21908) (q:draft)
Helicopter = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:helicopter) (o:English) (r:zd:11621/zd:25346) (q:draft)
helicopters = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:helicopter) (d:the English plural of helicopter, used in Zolai sentences for helicopters of the police, of rescue teams and of armies) (o:English) (r:zd:11691/zd:17983) (q:draft, low confidence)
helin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:mixing in/including/together with) (d:<hel>, mix in or include, with the linking <in>, written as one word: mixing it in, including it along with something else) (j:hel/in) (r:zd:21826/zd:21815) (q:draft)
helkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be included/be mixed in/be involved) (d:<hel>, mix in, and <kha>, happen to, written as one word; nearly always after <ki>: come to be included in a group, or get mixed into something) (j:hel/kha) (r:zd:19239/zd:19550/zd:14720) (q:draft)
helkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:get involved/be mixed up in) (d:<hel>, mix in, with <khak>, happen to, used after <ki>: happen to be drawn into or mixed up in something) (j:hel/khak) (r:zd:15814) (q:draft, low confidence)
helkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/everyday) (w:mix together/mingle/blend) (d:<hel>, mix, and <khawm>, together, written as one word: mix things into one) (s:gawmkhawm) (j:hel/khawm) (r:zd:24276/zd:18893) (q:draft)
hellkhuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:hell/pit of hell) (d:<hell> with <khuk>, pit, written as one word: the pit of hell, set against {Vangam}, heaven) (s:hell) (b:hell) (r:zd:19709/zd:14563) (q:draft)
hello = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday/social) (w:hello) (d:word of greeting at the start of a conversation, a letter or a phone call) (o:English) (r:zd:16337/zd:12342) (q:draft)
hello = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be included/be left out) (d:<hel>, include, with <lo>, not, written as one word; mostly as {ki hello}, is not included) (j:hel/lo) (r:zd:21931/zd:21706) (q:draft)
Helmet = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/home) (w:helmet/crash helmet) (d:a hard protective hat, in the news mostly that of a motorcycle rider; often written with a capital and beside <lukhu>) (s:lukhu) (o:English) (r:zd:15913/zd:19353/zd:12994) (q:draft)
helna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:inclusion/joining/mixing in) (d:<hel>, mix in or include, with the noun suffix {-na}: the mixing of one thing into another, or the including of someone in a group or list; with <ki> before it, the joining of a group) (b:hel) (r:zd:25392/zd:20961) (q:draft)
helna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:courtship/courting) (d:the courting of a girl, in {nungak helna}) (r:zd:24160) (q:draft, low confidence)
helna = (i:3) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:revolt/rebellion/revolution) (d:a rising against those who rule; in one article glossed with the English word revolution) (r:zd:23893) (q:draft, low confidence)
helthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be able to take part/can join in) (d:written after a separate <ki>: <kihel>, take part, with <thei>, can; {ki helthei} is be able to take part, and in news often simply took part) (r:zd:22565/zd:18076) (q:draft)
helzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:manage to join in/be able to take part/fit in) (d:<hel>, include, and <zo>, be able, written as one word, mostly after <ki>: manage to be among others or to take part) (j:hel/zo) (r:zd:20281) (q:draft, low confidence)
hem = (i:4) (t:adv) (f:everyday/body) (w:sideways/indirectly) (d:to one side and not straight: {hem et} and {mit hem} are look out of the corner of the eye, and {hem gen} is say a thing by hints; not {hem}, deformed or diminished) (r:zd:22683/zd:25585/zd:23113) (q:draft, low confidence)
hemkhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:will remove/to evacuate/to deport/to clear away) (d:<hemkhia>, remove, and the future marker <ding> written as one word; of people, with <ki>: be evacuated or sent out of a place) (j:hemkhia/ding) (r:zd:12422/zd:11623) (q:draft)
hemkhiaman = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:get out in time/be moved out in time/be evacuated in time) (d:<hemkhia>, move away, and <man>, here manage in time, written as one word and used after <ki>: be taken out or get clear before harm comes) (j:hemkhia/man) (r:zd:20153/zd:14865) (q:draft)
hemkhiapah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:remove at once/evacuate immediately) (d:<hemkhia>, move away or remove, and <pah>, at once, written as one word) (j:hemkhia/pah) (r:zd:15101/zd:16947/zd:15924) (q:draft)
hemkhiasak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/travel) (w:evacuate/move out/remove) (d:<hemkhia>, remove, with the causative ending {-sak}: make people leave a place; {ki hemkhiasak} is be evacuated, be moved out) (b:hemkhia) (r:zd:12040/zd:17777/zd:19514) (q:draft)
hemkhiata = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:be removed/be moved out/be dismissed) (d:<hemkhia>, remove, and the particle <ta> written as one word, used after <ki>: have now been removed from a place, a post or a programme) (j:hemkhia/ta) (r:zd:19674/zd:15023) (q:draft)
hemkhiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be able to remove/be able to take out) (d:<hemkhia>, remove, and <thei>, be able, written as one word: manage to take out or bring away a person or a thing, as people from a burning vehicle or a bomb from a building) (j:hemkhia/thei) (r:zd:17800/zd:11081) (q:draft)
hemna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/religion) (w:defect/blemish/deformity) (d:noun from <hem>: a bodily defect or disfigurement; mostly paired as {poina hemna}, defect and blemish) (s:poina) (b:hem) (r:zd:17988/zd:23297) (q:draft)
hen = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:bind/tie up/detain) (d:tie or bind a person and so hold him in custody; in the news mostly in the pair {mat leh hen}, arrest and detention, and not at the end of the sentence like {hen} of a wish) (r:ts:4411/zd:15622) (q:draft)
hen aw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:religion/social) (w:may it be/oh may) (d:<hen>, let or may, and <aw>, the calling word oh: closes a sentence as a heartfelt wish, oh may it be so; used in traditional songs, blessings and prayers, after the verb and often after <ta>) (r:zd:12023/zd:16038) (q:draft)
Henan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Henan) (d:a province in central China) (r:zd:17701/zd:12355) (q:draft)
hencipgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:tie up tight/cram in/pack tightly) (d:<hencip>, bind fast, with <gawp>, severely, written as one word: tie someone up hard; of people or animals in a small space, be crammed in) (j:hencip/gawp) (r:zd:19529/zd:12752) (q:draft)
hencipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:tie up/bind fast/muzzle) (d:<hencip>, bind fast, and <sak> written as one word: tie a thing fast, have it bound) (j:hencip/sak) (r:zd:18007/zd:23297) (q:draft)
heng = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health/body) (w:decayed/worm-eaten) (d:of a tooth: decayed, eaten hollow; {ha heng} is a decayed tooth and {lung heng} is worm-eaten) (r:zd:21120/zd:9133) (q:draft, low confidence)
henkol = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:shackles/bonds/chains/bondage) (d:<hen>, here bind, with <kol>, shackles: the bonds that hold a prisoner; in the articles a picture for what holds people captive, as sin or fear) (s:kol) (r:zd:22815/zd:24963) (q:draft)
henna = (i:3) (t:n) (f:body) (w:henna/henna dye) (d:loanword from English: the dye made from the henna plant and painted on the skin as a temporary tattoo, as in {Black Henna} and {Henna Tattoo}; not the shrub itself) (o:English, henna) (r:zd:12364) (q:draft)
hennunuai = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:food/health) (w:spinach) (d:a leaf vegetable, glossed in the article as spinach) (r:zd:21417/zd:21119) (q:draft, low confidence)
hento = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:push up into/thrust in/insert) (d:push or stick something up into an opening or a narrow space; the ending is <to>, upward) (r:zd:17402/zd:14748) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hepatitis = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:hepatitis) (d:the liver disease hepatitis, named with its type as in {Hepatitis B}) (o:English) (r:zd:17834) (q:draft)
hepkhiatdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:way of removing/manner of removal) (d:<hepkhiat> and <dan> written as one word: the way in which a thing is taken away) (j:hepkhiat/dan) (r:zd:15920) (q:draft, low confidence)
hepkhiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be removed/to remove) (d:<hepkhiat>, remove, and the future marker <ding> written as one word: to be removed, will remove or clear away) (j:hepkhiat/ding) (r:zd:13155/zd:12442) (q:draft)
hepkhiatloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not remove/not be removed) (d:<hepkhiat>, remove or move out, and the negative <loh> written as one word: not removed; {ki hepkhiatloh phamawh} is they must be moved out) (j:hepkhiat/loh) (r:zd:12442/zd:19514) (q:draft)
hepkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:removal/taking away/clearing out) (d:<hepkhiat>, remove, with the noun suffix {-na}: the removing of a thing or the sending away of people) (b:hepkhiat) (r:zd:21142/zd:12422) (q:draft)
hepkhiattheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can be removed/can be evacuated) (d:<hepkhiat> and <theih> written as one word, used before <nading>: so that people can be moved out or a thing can be taken away) (j:hepkhiat/theih) (r:zd:15507/zd:16373) (q:draft)
Hero = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:hero) (d:a person who is admired and looked up to) (s:galhang) (o:English) (r:zd:24739) (q:draft, low confidence)
Heroin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/politics) (w:heroin) (d:the illegal drug heroin, in reports of drug seizures) (o:English) (r:zd:14748/zd:11348) (q:draft)
Herzegovina = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics) (w:Herzegovina) (d:part of the country Bosnia and Herzegovina in south-eastern Europe, formerly in Yugoslavia) (r:zd:19662) (q:draft)
hetchei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:sneeze) (r:zd:23727/zd:24014) (q:draft)
hethet = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at all/in the least) (d:<het> said twice for force: before a negative, not at all; after a verb of change without a negative it appears to mean steadily, more and more) (b:het) (r:zd:11882/zd:21178) (q:draft)
hetkeng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/never) (d:<het>, at all, with the first person negative ending, a short form of {kei ing}, I do not, written as one word after a verb: I do not at all) (b:het) (r:zd:12701/zd:11776) (q:draft)
hetloding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will not at all/must never) (d:<hetlo>, not at all, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will certainly not, and of a duty, must on no account) (j:hetlo/ding) (r:zd:11251/zd:23943/zd:19562) (q:draft)
hetlohding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:must never/should not at all) (d:<hetloh>, not at all, with <ding>, written as one word after a verb: the action must not happen at all; {koihkhak hetlohding} is must never be left) (j:hetloh/ding) (r:zd:15317/zd:20440/zd:11590) (q:draft)
hetlohpi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/without at all) (d:<het>, at all, and <lohpi>, without doing, written as one word after a verb: {lamet hetlohpi} is quite unexpectedly, without expecting it at all) (j:het/lohpi) (r:zd:17741) (q:draft)
hetlopi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:without at all/although not at all) (d:<het>, at all, and <lopi>, without, written as one word after a verb: without it being so in the least; {lamet hetlopi in} is quite unexpectedly) (j:het/lopi) (r:zd:26411/zd:19878) (q:draft)
hetlote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (d:<hetlo>, not at all, with the plural <te>, after a verb: those who do not at all, those who never) (j:hetlo/te) (r:zd:21262/zd:10742) (q:draft)
heuh = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:rather/instead/of all things) (d:placed after a noun or noun phrase in informal writing to single it out, often against what was expected: that one rather than another) (r:zd:21626/zd:21590) (q:draft, low confidence)
heuhau = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:gaping/wide open) (d:expressive adverb after <vang> hole or {vangsuak}, of a hole that gapes wide open, not of light that glows) (r:zd:17281/zd:15958) (q:draft)
hey = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday) (w:hey) (d:call used to get the attention of someone, mostly in quoted speech) (o:English) (r:zd:21174/zd:25333) (q:draft)
Hezbollah = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:Hezbollah) (d:armed group and political party in Lebanon) (r:ts:3234/ts:4775) (q:draft)
hi mah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:yes) (d:it is so, said in agreement) (r:zai:yes) (q:draft)
hia = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:question particle) (d:sentence-final question word of spoken style, used like <hiam.1> after the verb and its subject marker: {na thei uh hia}, do you know; it does not point to anything) (r:zd:20920/zd:17786/zd:17444) (q:draft)
hiaa = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:being/and so) (d:<hi> and the linking <a> written as one word: is and, being; {tua hiaa} is that being so, therefore, and {na hiaa} is whether you are) (j:hi/a) (r:zd:20747/zd:21502/zd:23972) (q:draft)
hiah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:here) (d:in or at this place; {Hiah om ing}, here I am, is the answer of someone who is called) (s:hihlai-ah) (a:tuasan)
hiai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:after a verb, usually doubled as {hiai-hiai}: steadily, more and more, of something that goes on little by little) (r:zd:21626/zd:12313) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiai = (i:2) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this) (d:this, in writing close to Paite, where Tedim Zolai has <hih>; {hiai hun} is this time or this programme) (r:zd:12074) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiaihiai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:gradually/steadily/more and more) (d:placed after a verb to show that a change goes on step by step: {kiam hiaihiai} is keep decreasing) (s:semsem) (r:zd:23765/ts:3369/zd:15274) (q:draft)
hiaihun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/social) (w:this time/this occasion) (d:<hiai>, this, and <hun>, time, written as one word in writing close to Paite: this time, this event or programme; Tedim Zolai has {hih hun}) (j:hiai/hun) (r:zd:12074/zd:10973) (q:draft, low confidence)
hial = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:conclude/wrap up/close) (d:bring a talk or a writing to its end, not roll up cloth; with <thu> before it or <bawl> after it, as in {thu hial} and {hial bawl}) (r:zd:22686/zd:24542/zd:23086) (q:draft)
hial = (i:3) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:at all/even) (d:after a verb or an adjective it stresses how far a thing goes: {baih hial lo} is not easy at all, and {thong hial} is even so far as that) (r:zd:21027) (q:draft, low confidence)
hialbawl = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:conclude/close/wind up/bring to an end) (d:bring a meeting, a programme or a planned activity to its end, as in {meeting ki hialbawl}, the meeting was closed; the thing is finished, not put off for a later day as in the first sense; often followed by <ta>) (r:zd:22935/zd:19320) (q:draft)
hialhial = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:leisurely/at ease) (d:expressive adverb after a verb of going about such as <vak>, <vakkhawm> or <paikhawm>: moving along in an easy, unhurried way, often said of people strolling together) (r:zd:11955/zd:13144/zd:15114) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiam = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday/home) (w:sharp) (d:having a keen edge, of a knife or blade; the opposite of <mawl>, blunt) (r:zai:bluntness) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiam cihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/the reason is/namely) (d:<hiam>, the word that ends a question, and <cihleh>, if one says: closes a question that the speaker then answers; {banghang hiam cihleh}, if one asks why, is because, for, and the answer often ends in {ahih man hi}; after another question word it means as for what or how, it is this) (r:zd:14927/zd:23297) (q:draft)
hiam cihpen = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/media) (w:as to whether/the question of) (d:the question word <hiam>, whether or which, with <cihpen>, as for what is said: closes an indirect question and makes it the topic, as to whether or what or who; a verb of knowing, saying or inquiring follows, often negated) (r:zd:15425/zd:12099/zd:19303) (q:draft)
hiamcih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:whether/what/why) (d:the question particle <hiam> with <cih>, saying, written as one word: closes a question that is reported or thought about, what, why or whether something is; {banghang hiamcih leh}, if one asks why, means because) (j:hiam/cih) (r:zd:21706/zd:19915/zd:18924) (q:draft)
hiamcihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because) (d:the question particle <hiam> and <cihleh>, if one asks, written as one word after <banghang>, why: if one asks why, that is, because) (j:hiam/cihleh) (r:zd:13076/zd:21037) (q:draft)
hiamgam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:violence/cruelty/brutality) (d:cruel and violent treatment of people; {hiamgam takin} is violently, {innsung hiamgam} is domestic violence) (r:zd:16910/zd:24804) (q:draft)
hiamkhat = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:some or other/something or other/some) (d:the question particle <hiam> with <khat>, one, written as one word after a question word or a describing phrase: an amount or thing that is not known exactly, as {bangzah hiamkhat}, some number of) (j:hiam/khat) (r:zd:9242/zd:18102) (q:draft)
hiammahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/home) (w:very sharp) (d:<hiam> and <mahmah> written as one word: very sharp, of a blade or teeth) (j:hiam/mahmah) (r:zd:15245/zd:15278) (q:draft)
hiamtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:with a blade/with a sharp weapon) (d:<hiam>, here a blade or sharp weapon, and <tawh>, with, written as one word) (j:hiam/tawh) (r:zd:17123) (q:draft)
hiamtawina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:armed force/bearing arms/use of weapons) (d:noun of <hiamtawi>: the carrying or use of weapons, armed means as opposed to words) (b:hiamtawi) (r:zd:25673/zd:25678) (q:draft)
hiamvan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:weapon/arms) (d:<hiam>, sharp, with <van>, goods: a weapon, any tool for wounding or killing; often named together with <galvan>) (s:galvan) (r:zd:15374/zd:17069/zd:12257) (q:draft)
hiang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:branch/division/sect) (d:a part into which a larger whole divides, as a field of knowledge or a group within a religion; a picture taken from the branch of a tree) (r:zd:20400/zd:11394) (q:draft)
Hiangzing = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Hiangzing) (d:village near Taingen on the road between Kalaymyo and Tedim) (r:zd:19358/zd:20972/ts:5513) (q:draft)
hiaulo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:hardly/not really/not at all) (d:<hiau> and <lo> written as one word after a verb: not really, hardly or not at all so) (j:hiau/lo) (r:zd:22396/zd:22448/zd:21866) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiaumawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<hiau> and <mawk> written as one word after a verb, apparently saying that the action goes straight on or turns out so, often to the surprise of the speaker) (j:hiau/mawk) (r:zd:25148/zd:22749) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiauzen = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at once/straight away) (d:<hiau> and <zen> written as one word after a verb: the act is done suddenly and with feeling, at once) (j:hiau/zen) (r:zd:22002) (q:draft, low confidence)
hibang = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:such/like this/this kind of) (d:a short form of <hih>, this, with <bang>, like, written as one word: like this, of this kind; {hibang in} and {hibang dan in} are in this way) (j:hih/bang) (r:zd:16897/zd:21869/zd:23487) (q:draft)
hibangdan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/of this kind/such) (d:<hih>, this, <bang>, like, and <dan>, manner, written as one word in a shortened spelling: in this way, of this kind; before a noun, such) (j:hih/bang/dan) (r:zd:16391/zd:19550) (q:draft)
hibangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way/as follows/thus) (d:<hih>, this, and <bangin>, in the way of, written as one word: in this way; before a verb of saying it introduces the words that follow) (s:hibang) (j:hih/bangin) (r:zd:23670/zd:22122/zd:15384) (q:draft)
hibeka = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be only/be merely) (d:<hi>, be, and <beka> written as one word: is only that and nothing more, linked to the clause that follows) (s:hibek) (j:hi/beka) (r:zd:21018/zd:21309) (q:draft)
hibeklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be not only/be not merely) (d:<hi>, be, and <beklo>, not only, written as one word: it is not only that, with something more added after it) (j:hi/beklo) (r:zd:24464/zd:15178) (q:draft)
hibilbel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to be/be just then) (d:<hi>, be, with <bilbel>, as it happened, written as one word: it just happened to be so, as things turned out) (b:hi) (r:zd:15051/zd:15949/zd:18157) (q:draft, low confidence)
hici bang = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:such/this kind of/like this) (d:<hici>, like this, and <bang>, like: placed before a noun, such a one or this kind of, pointing to what was just described) (r:zd:24814/zd:22623/zd:24356) (q:draft)
hiciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:this far/up to here/to this point) (d:<hi>, here a short form of <hih>, this, with <ciang>, up to: as far as this, to this point or extent; {hiciang tung} is reach this far) (r:zd:19589/zd:19556/zd:22171) (q:draft)
hicibang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:like this/such/of this kind) (d:<hici>, like this, and <bang>, like, written as one word: of this kind; with <in>, in this way) (s:hihbang) (j:hici/bang) (r:zd:16433/zd:13179) (q:draft)
hicibanga = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way/thus) (d:<hici>, like this, and <banga>, in the manner of, written as one word before a verb: in this way, so suddenly as this) (j:hici/banga) (r:zd:21369/zd:13178) (q:draft)
hicih = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the sentence ending <hi> and <cih> written as one word, closing a statement that is reported, known or thought: that it is so; {om hicih phawk in} is remember that there is) (j:hi/cih) (r:zd:21083/zd:25932/zd:21989) (q:draft)
hicih = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way) (d:do or be like this; paired with {huacih}, like that) (s:hici) (r:zd:24130/zd:17675) (q:draft, low confidence)
hidan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/this way/such) (d:{hih dan} written as one word with the final h dropped: this manner, like this; before a noun, such a, and alone, such a thing) (j:hih/dan) (r:zd:25601/zd:17687/zd:24082) (q:draft)
hidanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in this way/like this/thus) (d:<hidan>, this way, and <in> written as one word: in this manner) (j:hidan/in) (r:zd:20973/zd:24121) (q:draft)
hiden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always be/be constantly) (d:<hi>, be, and <den>, always, written as one word: it is always so, it keeps being so) (j:hi/den) (r:zd:14507/zd:10731/zd:10892) (q:draft)
hideuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be mostly/be rather) (d:<hi> and <deuh> written as one word: it is rather so, it is mostly that) (j:hi/deuh) (r:zd:23761/zd:19679) (q:draft)
hidi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:hiding) (r:zd:17442/zd:17341) (q:draft, low confidence)
hidiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be especially/be above all) (d:<hi> and <diak> written as one word: it is so in particular, above the rest) (j:hi/diak) (r:zd:24320/zd:23554) (q:draft)
hiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be/must be/probably is) (d:<hi>, be, and the marker <ding> for what is to come, written as one word: will be, is to be, or is probably) (j:hi/ding) (r:zd:20328/zd:21856/zd:12822) (q:draft)
hiding cihi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:it is said to be likely/is believed to be/reportedly) (d:<hiding>, will be or probably is, and <cihi>, he said or it is said: closes a news sentence and marks what stands before it as the guess of the source, not an established fact) (r:zd:17834/zd:11889) (q:draft)
hiding hiven = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:it must be/presumably/I suppose) (d:<hiding>, it will be, and <hiven>, it is so after all: closes a clause that gives the speaker's guess at the reason or circumstance of what is told next, it must be that, presumably) (r:zd:26097/zd:19779) (q:draft)
hiding kici = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:is said to be/is believed to be/is thought to be) (d:<hiding>, probably is, and <kici>, be said: closes a news statement that reports what people suppose and is not confirmed, it is said that it probably is; <hi> may follow) (r:zd:15435/zd:17375) (q:draft)
hidinga = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be) (d:<hi> and <dinga> written as one word: it will be so, and; closes one clause about what is to be and links it to the next) (j:hi/dinga) (r:zd:23487/zd:20968) (q:draft)
hidingaa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be and) (d:<hi>, be, with <dingaa> written as one word: closes a clause about what will be the case and links it to the next, it will be so and) (j:hi/dingaa) (r:zd:21590) (q:draft, low confidence)
hidinghi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be/must be) (d:<hi>, <ding> and a second <hi> that ends the sentence, written as one word: it will be; in reports, it is probably so, it must be) (j:hi/ding) (r:zd:11062/zd:16772) (q:draft)
hidinghiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:could it be/might be) (d:<hi>, <ding> and <hiam> written as one word: a question or doubt about what may be so, could it be that, whether it might be; often before {cihpen kitheician nailo hi}, it is not yet known) (j:hi/ding/hiam) (r:zd:20302/zd:12208/zd:11283) (q:draft)
hidingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to be/as being) (d:<hi> and <dingin> written as one word: that it is or will be so, mostly before a verb of believing or supposing such as <um> and <ummawh>) (j:hi/dingin) (r:zd:21829/zd:23298) (q:draft)
hiei = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:it is indeed) (d:<hi> and <ei> written as one word at the end of a statement in lively speech: it is so, indeed) (j:hi/ei) (r:ts:3508/zd:16337) (q:draft, low confidence)
Highway = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:highway/expressway) (d:a main road for fast traffic between towns) (s:lamlian) (o:English) (r:zd:13332/zd:20406/zd:19036) (q:draft)
higige = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always be/be constantly) (d:<hi>, be, and <gige>, always, written as one word: it is always so, it remains so) (j:hi/gige) (r:zd:11364/zd:16580) (q:draft)
hih = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this) (d:points to a person or thing near the speaker or just mentioned; before a noun it means this or these, and {hih bangin} is in this way) (a:tua) (r:43.8.4)
hih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do) (r:zai:do) (q:draft)
hihang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we are) (d:<hi>, be, and <hang>, here the verb ending for we including the hearer, written as one word at the end of a sentence: we are; after <ding>, we shall) (j:hi/hang) (r:zd:23057/zd:20860/zd:20329) (q:draft)
hihangh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:hihang) (r:zd:15874/zd:16336) (q:draft)
hihbang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:like this/such/as follows) (d:<hih> and <bang> written as one word: of this kind; before <in>, in this way) (j:hih/bang) (r:zd:22992/zd:16849/zd:14718) (q:draft)
hihbangaa = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way/thus) (d:<hih>, <bang> and <aa> written as one word, where <aa> stands for the adverb ending more often written <in>: in this way, like this) (j:hih/bang/aa) (r:zd:20545/zd:19239) (q:draft)
hihbangdan = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:this kind of/such/like this) (d:<hih>, <bang> and <dan> written as one word: of this kind, in this way; before a noun it means such a) (j:hih/bang/dan) (r:zd:11803/zd:16946/zd:19567) (q:draft)
hihbangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way/thus) (d:<hih> and <bangin> written as one word: in this way, like this; it points to what has just been told or to the words that follow) (j:hih/bangin) (r:zd:23670/zd:17841/zd:24276) (q:draft)
hihbangliang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to such an extent/as badly as this/even like this) (d:<hihbang>, like this, and <liang>, even, written as one word: to such a degree, said with shock at how far something went) (j:hihbang/liang) (r:zd:15123/zd:21067) (q:draft)
hihbangte = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:such things/these) (d:<hihbang>, like this, and the plural <te> written as one word: things of this kind, often before <hangin>, because of) (j:hihbang/te) (r:zd:19453/zd:17060) (q:draft)
hihbangvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:such a matter/a case like this) (d:<hihbang> and <vai> written as one word: a matter or case of this kind) (j:hihbang/vai) (r:zd:19213/zd:16717) (q:draft)
hihbuaina = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media/social) (w:this trouble/this incident) (d:<hih>, this, and <buaina>, trouble, written as one word: this trouble, this incident just reported) (j:hih/buaina) (r:zd:19554/zd:16336) (q:draft)
hihciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:this far/to this point/to this extent) (d:<hih>, this, and <ciang>, as far as, written as one word: up to this point or level, often with <tung>, reach, or followed by <dong>) (j:hih/ciang) (r:zd:11103/zd:20091/zd:21219) (q:draft)
hihcibang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:such/like this/of this kind) (d:<hih>, this, and <cibang>, of that kind, written as one word: such a thing, a thing like this; before a noun it means this kind of) (j:hih/cibang) (r:zd:15886/zd:16890/zd:13179) (q:draft)
hihdan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:like this/in this way/thus) (d:<hih>, this, with <dan>, manner, written as one word: this way, like this; {hihdan in} introduces what is said or done) (j:hih/dan) (r:zd:21607/zd:16216/zd:25223) (q:draft)
hihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to be/to do) (d:<hih> and <ding> written as one word: to be something, or what is to be done; {hihding kisam} is it is necessary to be) (j:hih/ding) (r:zd:21085/zd:21235/zd:11346) (q:draft)
hihen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:let it be/may it be) (d:<hi>, be, and <hen>, let, written as one word: let it be so, may it be) (j:hi/hen) (r:zd:15859/zd:17426) (q:draft)
hihet = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be at all) (d:<hi>, be, and <het>, at all, written as one word and always followed by <lo> or <kei>: {hihet lo hi} is it is not at all so) (j:hi/het) (r:zd:19679) (q:draft)
hihetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be not at all/be by no means) (d:<hi>, be, with <hetlo>, not at all, written as one word: it is not that at all) (j:hi/hetlo) (r:zd:12072/zd:15759/zd:25228) (q:draft)
hihgamsung = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:politics/travel) (w:in this country/this country) (d:<hih>, this, and <gamsung>, land, written as one word, usually before <ah>: in this country) (j:hih/gamsung) (r:zd:21409) (q:draft)
hihhang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because of this/because it is/although it is) (d:<hih> and <hang>, reason, written as one word. {Hihhang in} is because of this; {a hihhang}, with <hih> the form of <hi>, be, is because it is so or although it is so, and alone it opens a sentence as even so) (j:hih/hang) (r:zd:15848/zd:16022/zd:25221) (q:draft)
hihhangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:however/although/even though) (d:the form <hih> of the verb be with <hangin>, written as one word after <a> or <na>: {a hihhangin} is although it is so, however, and {na hihhangin} is although you are) (j:hih/hangin) (r:zd:17883/zd:22988/zd:22171) (q:draft)
hihhi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:hihi) (r:zd:17309) (q:draft)
hihhun = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:this time/this period) (d:<hih>, this, and <hun>, time, written as one word; {hihhun sungah} is during this time) (j:hih/hun) (r:zd:12708/zd:14826) (q:draft)
hihi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is/am/are) (d:<hi>, be, written as one word with the sentence-final <hi> that follows it, after <a>, <ka>, <na> or <i>: {a hihi} is it is, {ka hihi} I am) (r:zd:20892/zd:21417/zd:24064) (q:draft)
hihiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is it/are/is) (d:<hi> and <hiam> written as one word: the verb to be at the end of a question, as in {bang hihiam}, what is it, and {na hihiam}, are you) (j:hi/hiam) (r:zd:10857/zd:21989/zd:24427) (q:draft)
hihiat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:calmly/quietly/just/simply) (d:placed after a verb: do it calmly and without fuss, just do it and nothing more; compare <hithiat> and <hiathiat>) (r:zd:17249/zd:8667) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihin = (i:2) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this) (d:<hih.1>, this, with the marker <in>, at the start of a sentence: this, as the subject, pointing to what has just been said or shown, {hihin a thupi khat ahi hi} this is an important thing; not the verb do) (r:zd:16412/zd:25393/zd:23733) (q:draft)
hihkan = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:than this) (d:<hih> with a following word for than, written as one word and followed by <in>: than this, before a comparison) (s:hihsang) (r:zd:26097/zd:13149) (q:draft)
hihkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be so) (d:<hih> and <kei> written as one word, <hih> being the form of <hi>, be, used before <leh>: {a hihkei leh} is if it is not so, otherwise, or else) (j:hih/kei) (r:zd:20195/zd:21012) (q:draft)
hihkeileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:or/or else/otherwise) (d:<hih>, be so, with <kei>, not, and <leh>, if, written as one word and used after <a> as {a hihkeileh}: if it is not so, and so or, between two things of which one is chosen) (j:hih/kei/leh) (r:zd:21083/zd:21155) (q:draft)
hihkhak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to be/turn out to be/come to be) (d:form of <hikha> used before another word, from <hi>, be, and not from <hih>, do: come to be a certain kind of person, after a noun or <mi> as in {tuabang mi na hihkhak phialleh}, even if you happen to be such a person) (r:zd:21796/zd:17221) (q:draft)
hihkhialh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do wrongly/make a mistake) (d:<hih>, do, and <khialh>, wrongly, written as one word: do something wrongly; also the mistake made) (j:hih/khialh) (r:zd:9451/zd:24248) (q:draft)
hihkhuasung = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:this city/this town) (d:<hih>, this, and <khuasung>, town, written as one word; with <ah>, in this city) (j:hih/khuasung) (r:zd:17017/zd:16952) (q:draft)
hihla = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media/social) (w:this song) (d:<hih>, this, and <la>, song, written as one word) (j:hih/la) (r:zd:16032) (q:draft)
hihlaibu = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:education) (w:this book) (d:<hih> and <laibu> written as one word: this book) (j:hih/laibu) (r:zd:21796/zd:21869) (q:draft)
hihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if it is/as for) (d:<hih>, here the form of <hi> before an ending, with <leh>, written as one word after <a>, <na> or <ih>: if it is, if you are; after a noun or pronoun also as for; the same as <ahihleh>) (j:hih/leh) (r:zd:19969/zd:22742) (q:draft)
hihlohnapi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:though not done/what one did not do) (d:<hihloh> and <napi> written as one word: although one did not do it, said of a thing one is blamed for without having done it) (j:hihloh/napi) (r:zd:20761) (q:draft)
hihmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:indeed be/truly be) (d:<hih>, here the form of <hi>, be, used before a following word, with emphatic <mah>, written as one word; {a hihmah bangin} is just as it really is, in keeping with what it is) (r:zd:17309/zd:17655) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihman = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since) (d:<hih>, here the form of <hi>, be, with <man>, here reason, written as one word; stands after <a>, <i>, <ka> or <na> at the end of a clause, often followed by <in>: because it is, because we are; the same as {ahih manin}) (j:hih/man) (r:zd:23572/zd:21662/zd:11206) (q:draft)
hihmanin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because/since) (d:<hih>, here the form of <hi>, be, with <manin>, because, written as one word; stands after <a>, <i>, <ka> or <na> at the end of a clause: because it is, because I am; the same as {ahih manin}) (j:hih/manin) (r:zd:20892/zd:23212/zd:20896) (q:draft)
hihmawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:worry/anxiety/concern) (d:used after <lung>, heart, as {lung hihmawhna}: worry or concern about what may happen; <hihmawh> with the noun ending <na>) (s:lunghihmawhna) (b:hihmawh) (r:zd:20633/zd:17896/zd:20895) (q:draft)
hihmawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do thoughtlessly/do recklessly) (d:<hih>, do, and <mawk>, without thought or care, written as one word; {bang hihmawk na hiam} is what on earth are you doing) (j:hih/mawk) (r:zd:8375) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihmun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:this place/here) (d:<hih>, this, and <mun>, place, written as one word: this place; {hihmun ah} is here, at this point) (j:hih/mun) (r:zd:24289/zd:20477/zd:24593) (q:draft)
hihna taktak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:true identity/real self/true nature) (d:<hihna>, the fact of being, and <taktak>, real: what a person or a people really is, as against how others see them; it follows a possessor, as in {i hihna taktak}, what we really are) (r:zd:13076/zd:25139/zd:16060) (q:draft)
hihnak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if it is/if indeed) (d:<hih>, be or do, with the first part of <nakleh>, written as one word and followed by <leh>: if indeed it is so, if they do so) (r:zd:22171/zd:17060) (q:draft)
hihnatawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:as being/being) (d:<hihna>, the fact of being, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: as one who is, in view of being what was just named) (j:hihna/tawh) (r:zd:10745) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihnatna = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:health) (w:this disease/this illness) (d:<hih>, this, and <natna>, disease, written as one word) (j:hih/natna) (r:zd:23822/zd:23784) (q:draft)
hihngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have done before/be used to doing) (d:<hih>, do, and <ngei> written as one word: what one has done before or always does, as in {i hihngei dan}, the way we have always done it) (j:hih/ngei) (r:zd:11135) (q:draft)
hihni = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:this day/today) (d:<hih>, this, and <ni>, day, written as one word: this day, the day spoken of) (j:hih/ni) (r:zd:12231/zd:17060) (q:draft)
hihnu = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:she/her/this woman) (d:<hih>, this, with <nu> marking a woman: this woman, she, said of a woman who is present or being spoken about) (s:tuanu)
hihpa = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:he/him/this man) (d:<hih>, this, with <pa> marking a man: this man, he, said of a man who is present or being spoken about) (s:tuapa) (r:1.5.29)
hihpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do at once/do immediately) (d:<hih>, do, and <pah> written as one word: do something right away) (j:hih/pah) (r:zd:22203/ts:3369) (q:draft)
hihpawi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:this festival/this feast) (d:<hih>, this, and <pawi>, festival, written as one word) (j:hih/pawi) (r:zd:15924/zd:23298) (q:draft)
hihpeen = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (j:hihpen) (r:zd:11023/zd:23569) (q:draft)
hihpen = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this) (d:<hih>, this, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: this, as the thing spoken about) (j:hih/pen) (r:zd:21219/zd:20092/zd:16665) (q:draft)
hihphual = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/travel) (w:this place/this site) (d:<hih>, this, and <phual>, site, written as one word: this place, the site that is spoken about) (j:hih/phual) (r:zd:17632/zd:15276) (q:draft)
hihsang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:than this) (d:<hih> and <sang> written as one word, <sang> in the sense than: than this, before a comparison with <zaw>) (j:hih/sang) (r:zd:14941/zd:15543/zd:12434) (q:draft)
hihsangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:than this/more than this) (d:<hih> and <sangin> written as one word: compared with this, usually with <zaw> on the describing word) (j:hih/sangin) (r:zd:11707/zd:20173) (q:draft)
hihsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:aim to be/intend to do) (d:<hih>, do or be, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: set oneself to be or to do what is named before it) (j:hih/sawm) (r:zd:19523) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in this/herein) (d:<hih>, this, and <sung>, inside, written as one word and followed by <ah>: in this, within this) (j:hih/sung) (r:zd:15762/zd:19117) (q:draft)
hihsung = (i:2) (t:n) (f:time) (w:time of being/period as) (d:<hih>, here the form of <hi>, be, and <sung>, during, written as one word after <a>: during the time that someone is or was something, as {kumpi nu a hihsung}, while she was queen) (j:hih/sung) (r:zd:21657) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihtak = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:right here/this very place/this point) (d:<hih>, this, and <tak>, exactly, written as one word and followed by <ah> or <a>: right here, at this very point of what is said or written) (j:hih/tak) (r:zd:11674/zd:21376) (q:draft)
hihtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:with this/including this) (d:<hih> and <tawh> written as one word: with this, counting this one; {hihtawh kisai in} is concerning this) (j:hih/tawh) (r:zd:12645/zd:14606) (q:draft)
hihteh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:since we are/as we are) (d:found as {ih hihteh} after a describing phrase: since we are so, given that we would be so; a form of the verb <hi>, be, with the ending <teh>) (r:zd:15874/zd:21183) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihteng = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:all these/these) (d:<hih>, this, with <teng>, here in its sense of all of, written as one word: all these, the things just named or about to be named) (j:hih/teng) (r:zd:22203/zd:25180/zd:23332) (q:draft)
hihtheihkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot do/be unable to do) (d:<hihtheih>, be able to do, and the negative <kei> written as one word, before <leh>: if one cannot do it) (j:hihtheih/kei) (r:zd:23985/zd:20652) (q:draft)
hihtheihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if possible/if one can) (d:<hihtheih> and <leh> written as one word; {a hihtheihleh} opens advice: if it can be done) (j:hihtheih/leh) (r:zd:21837/zd:23985) (q:draft)
hihtheihnate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:abilities/capabilities/capacities) (d:<hihtheihna>, ability, and the plural <te> written as one word: the things one is able to do) (b:hihtheihna) (j:hihtheihna/te) (r:zd:22450) (q:draft)
hihtheihzah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:as much as one can do/best of one's ability) (d:<hihtheih>, can do, and <zah>, amount, written as one word; {ka hihtheihzah in} is as much as I can, to the best of my ability) (j:hihtheih/zah) (r:zd:21149/zd:23929) (q:draft)
hihthu = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:this matter/this) (d:<hih>, this, and <thu>, matter or word, written as one word: this matter, what has just been told) (j:hih/thu) (r:ts:3366/zd:24314/zd:21869) (q:draft)
hihthupen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:this matter/as for this) (d:<hihthu> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: this matter, as the thing being spoken about) (j:hihthu/pen) (r:zd:21876/zd:17070) (q:draft)
hihthupiang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media/everyday) (w:this incident/this event) (d:<hih> and <thupiang> written as one word: this incident, what has just been reported) (j:hih/thupiang) (r:zd:16647/zd:12285) (q:draft)
hihthute = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:these things/these matters) (d:<hih>, this, and <thute>, matters, written as one word: these things, what has just been told) (j:hih/thute) (r:zd:22116/zd:19679) (q:draft)
hihtuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:seem to be/appear to be/apparently be) (d:a form of <hi>, be, joined with <tuak> and written as one word at the end of a statement: it seems, it appears that; the writer passes on or infers something without stating it as certain) (r:zd:12327/zd:17945/zd:17856) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihtuaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:seem not to be/probably not be) (d:<hihtuak>, seem to be, with <lo>, not, written as one word: it does not seem to be, it is probably not) (j:hihtuak/lo) (r:zd:13072/zd:15732/zd:15788) (q:draft)
hihtuakmawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:seem to be/apparently be) (d:<hihtuak>, seem to be, with <mawk>, written as one word: it appears that it was so, said of something reported with surprise) (j:hihtuak/mawk) (r:zd:15781/zd:14883) (q:draft)
hihvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:this matter/this affair/this case) (d:<hih>, this, and <vai>, matter, written as one word; {hihvai tawh kisai in} is concerning this matter) (j:hih/vai) (r:zd:17547/zd:15951/zd:13243) (q:draft)
hihvaitawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media/everyday) (w:with this matter) (d:<hih>, this, <vai>, matter, and <tawh>, with, written as one word; used in {hihvaitawh kisai in}, concerning this matter) (j:hih/vai/tawh) (r:zd:18244/zd:17188) (q:draft)
hihzahliang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to this extent/as much as this/on this scale) (d:<hihzah>, this much, and <liang>, even, written as one word, usually with <in>: to such a degree as this, often of something never seen before) (j:hihzah/liang) (r:zd:20173/zd:17802) (q:draft)
hihzahzah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:so much/so many/this much) (d:<hih>, this, and <zahzah> written as one word before a noun or verb: as much or as many as this, such a great amount) (j:hih/zahzah) (r:zd:15163/zd:12976) (q:draft)
hihzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:this also/this too) (d:<hih> and <zong> written as one word: this as well) (j:hih/zong) (r:zd:24224) (q:draft)
hihzong = (i:2) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:however/even so) (d:in {a hihzong in}, another way of writing {ahih zongin}: however, even so) (r:zd:25919) (q:draft)
hii = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:hi) (r:zd:24417/zd:21626) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:being/is and) (d:<hi>, be, and <in> written as one word: being so, is this and, closing one clause and linking it to the next) (j:hi/in) (r:zd:20900/zd:21027) (q:draft)
hiing = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I am) (d:<hi>, be, with the first person ending <ing>, written as one word at the end of a sentence: I am) (j:hi/ing) (r:zd:23761) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiing = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:food/everyday) (w:stale/rancid) (d:smelling stale or rancid, of food that has gone off; {vok-hiing} is the stench of pigs) (r:zd:15730) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiithiat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:hithiat) (r:zd:21780/zd:21117) (q:draft)
Hijack = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:hijack) (d:seize a plane or vehicle by force; used with other words, as {ki Hijack}, be hijacked, and {Hijack bawl}, carry out a hijacking) (o:English) (r:zd:11827/zd:12108) (q:draft)
hik = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature/health) (w:louse/head louse/lice) (d:a louse, the small insect that lives in hair and clothing) (r:zd:21690) (q:draft)
hik = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health) (w:germ/virus) (d:the germ or virus that causes a disease; {natna hik} is a disease germ) (r:zd:19858/zd:19846) (q:draft)
hik = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:body/health) (w:numb) (d:without feeling, of the body or a limb; {khe hik} is the feet go numb) (r:zd:16287/zd:12541) (q:draft, low confidence)
hikei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not/be not) (d:<hi>, be, and <kei>, not, written as one word: it is not so; {tua hikei leh} is if not, otherwise) (j:hi/kei) (r:zd:20808/zd:20545/zd:25447) (q:draft)
hikeng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I am not) (d:<hi>, be, and the first person negative ending, short for {kei ing}, written as one word: I am not, it is not that I) (j:hi/keng) (r:zd:22116/zd:19455) (q:draft)
hikhading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:probably be/may be) (d:<hikha>, may be, and <ding>, will, written as one word: it is probably so, it must be; a guess of the writer) (j:hikha/ding) (r:zd:15754/zd:16834) (q:draft)
hikhin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be necessarily/be entirely/be all) (d:before a negative such as <lo>, {khol lo} or {sam lo}: not necessarily so, not the whole of it; here <khin> means wholly and not already) (r:zd:24379/zd:15697/zd:25461) (q:draft)
hikhinlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not all be/not wholly be) (d:<hikhin> and <lo> written as one word: not be so in every case, not all or not wholly so, often after <khempeuh>, all) (j:hikhin/lo) (r:zd:17177/zd:14892/zd:19340) (q:draft)
hikhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:have already been/have become) (d:<hi> and <khinta> written as one word: it already is, it has now come to be, said mostly of a length of time or a number that has been reached) (j:hi/khinta) (r:zd:20050/zd:15924/zd:20562) (q:draft)
hikhollo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be not really/be not very) (d:<hi> and <khollo> written as one word: it is not particularly so, not really) (j:hi/khollo) (r:zd:11081/zd:22662) (q:draft)
hikik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be again/turn out to be) (d:<hi> and <kik> written as one word: it is so again, or it is so in its turn; often followed by <bilbel> or <leuleu>) (j:hi/kik) (r:zd:11401/zd:17814) (q:draft)
hilai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still is/is still) (d:<hi> joined with the word for still, as in {om lai}, still there: is still so, remains) (j:hi/lai) (r:zd:24118/ts:3164) (q:draft)
hilai = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:here/this place) (d:<hih>, this, joined with the word for place or midst, as in {hih lai munah}: here, this place) (j:hih/lai) (r:zd:24310) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilawmlawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, be, and the intensifier <lawmlawm> written as one word at the end of a clause: it really is so, it has gone that far, said with dismay or reproach) (j:hi/lawmlawm) (r:zd:17547/zd:19932) (q:draft, low confidence)
hile = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if/if it were) (d:<hi>, be, and <le>, if, written as one word and followed by the ending for the person, as {hile hang}, if we were, and {hile uh}, if they were) (s:hileh) (j:hi/le) (r:zd:17971/zd:23733) (q:draft)
hilecin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if you are/if you were) (d:<hi>, be, and <lecin>, if you, written as one word: if you are or were, if it were so with you) (j:hi/lecin) (r:zd:14613/zd:19709) (q:draft)
hileeng = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if we were/if it were) (d:<hi>, be, with the conditional ending <leng> spelled with a long vowel, written as one word: if we were, supposing it were so; compare <hileng>) (j:hi/leng) (r:zd:19219/zd:24496) (q:draft, low confidence)
hileh kilawm = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:it seems that/apparently/it looks as if) (d:<hileh>, if it were, and <kilawm>, fitting: closes a statement that the speaker judges likely but does not know for sure, it seems that or presumably; stands after the verb and before the sentence-final <hi>) (r:zd:16897/zd:12998/zd:21945) (q:draft)
hilehang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if we were/if we could) (d:<hi>, be, and <lehang>, if we, written as one word after a verb or adjective: if we were so, if we did so, supposing that we) (j:hi/lehang) (r:zd:22312/zd:17339) (q:draft)
hilehzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/even though) (d:<hileh>, if it is, and <zong>, also, written as one word: even if it is so, even if it be) (j:hileh/zong) (r:zd:13328/zd:24088) (q:draft)
hilelding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:must be just/will only be) (d:<hilel> and <ding> written as one word: it will be nothing more than, it is probably just; often of a first guess that proved wrong) (j:hilel/ding) (r:zd:18211/zd:14952) (q:draft)
hileng = (i:2) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if it were/if we were/if there were) (d:the same form in a supposition about anyone or anything, not only the speaker: if it were so, if we could, if there were; often after <bang>, <thei> or <om>) (r:zd:19058/zd:20587/zd:23528) (q:draft)
hilengh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (j:hileng) (r:zd:16331) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilengzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if I were/even if it were) (d:<hileng>, if I were, and <zong>, also, written as one word: even if it were I, even so) (j:hileng/zong) (r:zd:23664) (q:draft)
hileuleu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, be, with <leuleu>, in turn, written as one word: is in its turn, is again, on the other hand is) (j:hi/leuleu) (r:zd:24282/zd:17854) (q:draft)
hilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:teach/instruct) (d:teach or instruct someone, show how a thing is done) (s:thuhilh/sinsak) (a:sin) (q:draft)
hilhcian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:explain/expound/make clear) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <cian>, clearly: explain a matter fully so that it is understood; of the Bible, expound) (r:zd:19976/zd:25475/zd:21656) (q:draft)
hilhcianna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:explanation/clarification) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <cian>, clearly, and the noun ending {-na}: an explanation that makes a matter clear) (r:zd:23989/zd:11702/zd:22950) (q:draft)
hilhding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:to teach/will instruct) (d:<hilh> and <ding> written as one word: will teach or instruct, in order to teach) (j:hilh/ding) (r:zd:25275/zd:23156) (q:draft)
hilhlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:not teach/not tell) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <lo>, not, written as one word: not teach, without teaching) (j:hilh/lo) (r:zd:20964/zd:19465/zd:20970) (q:draft)
hilhloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:not teach/not tell) (d:<hilh>, teach or tell, and the negative <loh>, written as one word: not teach, not tell someone) (j:hilh/loh) (r:zd:19709/zd:22116) (q:draft)
hilhnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:want to teach/want to tell) (d:<hilh>, teach, and <nop>, want, written as one word: what one wishes to teach or point out to someone) (j:hilh/nop) (r:zd:19168/zd:21945) (q:draft)
hilhnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/religion) (w:want to teach/wish to show) (d:<hilh>, teach, and <nuam>, want, written as one word) (j:hilh/nuam) (r:zd:8667) (q:draft)
hilhzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/religion) (w:teach rather/teach instead) (d:<hilh>, teach, with <zaw>, rather, written as one word: teach this rather than something else) (j:hilh/zaw) (r:zd:21140/zd:23441) (q:draft)
hilhzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/family) (w:be able to teach/manage to teach) (d:<hilh>, teach, and <zawh>, be able, written as one word; with <kei> or <loh>, fail to teach) (j:hilh/zawh) (r:zd:20801) (q:draft)
hilhzel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:keep teaching/teach repeatedly) (d:<hilh> and <zel> written as one word: teach or tell again and again) (j:hilh/zel) (r:zd:20572/zd:12050) (q:draft)
hilian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be exactly/be really) (d:<hi>, be, with <lian> used as an emphatic word, exactly, written as one word: be exactly that, be really so; {hilian lo} is not exactly so) (j:hi/lian) (r:zd:20207/zd:24594) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiliang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is even/amounts to) (d:<hi>, is, with <liang>, even, written as one word: it is as much as that, it even is; said with surprise at a number or degree) (j:hi/liang) (r:zd:19775/zd:20526/zd:11581) (q:draft)
Hillsong = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Hillsong) (d:a church from Australia known over the world for its worship songs and music groups) (r:zd:13240/zd:23025) (q:draft)
hilo = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:not/no) (d:is not, the negative of <hi>, be, written as one word; as a reply it means no, it is not so) (b:hi) (q:draft)
hiloding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:will not be/is probably not) (d:<hilo> and <ding> written as one word: will not be, or in reports, is probably not, is thought not to be) (j:hilo/ding) (r:zd:12761/zd:11545) (q:draft)
hilohi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not/be not) (d:<hilo>, is not, with the sentence ending <hi>, written as one word: it is not, it is not so) (j:hilo/hi) (r:zd:24231/zd:17437/zd:23551) (q:draft)
hilohiam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:is it not/isn't it) (d:<hilo> and <hiam> written as one word at the end of a sentence: a question that expects agreement, is it not so) (j:hilo/hiam) (r:zd:14597/zd:11587) (q:draft)
hiloin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:not being/and not/but) (d:<hilo> and <in> written as one word: it is not that, but; <bek hiloin> is not only) (j:hilo/in) (r:zd:24392/zd:25464/zd:23512) (q:draft)
hilolai = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:is not even/is not either) (d:<hilo> and <lai> written as one word: is still not, is not even that, is not that either) (j:hilo/lai) (r:zd:19831/zd:20444) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilomawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not at all/is not really) (d:<hilo> and <mawk> written as one word at the end of a clause: it is not so, said with regret or surprise; after <ding> it means there is no way that it will, and {gentheih hilomawk} is it cannot be said) (j:hilo/mawk) (r:zd:11057/zd:15547) (q:draft)
hilozaw = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be but rather/rather than being) (d:<hilo>, is not, and <zaw>, rather, written as one word, mostly as {hilozaw in}: it is not this but rather what follows) (j:hilo/zaw) (r:zd:16415/zd:17166) (q:draft)
hilua = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday) (w:exactly/quite so/very much so) (d:<hi>, it is, and <lua>, very much, written as one word: said in agreement, that is quite right; inside a sentence, it is very much so) (j:hi/lua) (r:zd:20545/zd:20999) (q:draft, low confidence)
Himachal = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:politics) (w:Himachal) (d:first word of Himachal Pradesh, a mountain state in northern India) (r:zd:19160/zd:20272) (q:draft)
Himah = (i:2) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/even so/but) (d:{Himah} followed by <leh>, <taleh>, {ta leh} or {tase leh}, at the start of a sentence or after a clause: although that is so, even so; also written as one word, <himahleh>) (r:ts:4831/zd:25572/zd:11917) (q:draft)
himah ta = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/even though/even so) (d:<hi>, be, with the emphatic <mah> and <ta>, here the particle of a reached state and not the noun child: always followed by <leh>, <lehang> or {se leh}, and placed after a clause, although that is so; at the head of a sentence, even so) (s:himahleh) (r:zd:24502/zd:19662) (q:draft)
himah taleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/even so/however) (d:<Himah>, it is indeed so, and <taleh>, even if: although that is so; placed after a clause it means although, and after a comma or at the start of a clause it means even so, however) (s:himahleh/ahizongin) (r:zd:11917/zd:25015/zd:11262) (q:draft)
himahleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:but/although/however) (d:<hi>, <mah> and <leh> written as one word, placed after a clause: although that is so, but) (j:hi/mah/leh) (r:zd:12565/zd:14709) (q:draft)
himai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just is/simply is) (d:<hi>, be, and <mai>, here a particle meaning just or simply and not the noun face, written as one word: it simply is so, there is nothing more to it; often with a tone of resignation or wonder) (r:zd:11259/zd:25477/zd:23037) (q:draft, low confidence)
himaithei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:may well be/might be/could be) (d:<hi>, be, and <maithei>, possibly, written as one word: it may well be so) (j:hi/maithei) (r:zd:25115) (q:draft)
Himalaya = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:nature/travel) (w:Himalaya/Himalayas) (d:the high mountain range north of India; {Himalaya mualsang} is the Himalaya mountains) (r:zd:25115/zd:24215) (q:draft)
himasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be first of all/be primarily/be the main thing) (d:<hi>, be, and <masa>, first, written as one word: be so first of all; mostly with <lo>, as {himasa lo}, it is not mainly that) (j:hi/masa) (r:zd:21140/zd:21305) (q:draft, low confidence)
himasalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be primarily/not really be) (d:<hi>, be, and <masalo> written as one word: it is not in the first place this; usually followed by <hizaw>, it is rather that) (j:hi/masalo) (r:zd:11759/zd:12936) (q:draft)
himawhden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be always worried/keep worrying) (d:<himawh> and <den> written as one word, after <lung>: be anxious all the time) (j:himawh/den) (r:zd:12217/zd:23594) (q:draft)
himawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:anxiety/worry) (d:used after <lung>, heart: {lung himawhna} is worry or anxiety, the same as <lunghimawhna>) (s:lunghimawhna) (b:himawh) (r:zd:24481/zd:10777) (q:draft)
himawk = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be in fact/turn out to be) (d:in a statement, as {himawk hi} or {himawk ahih manin}, says that something is so in fact, often against what was expected or wished; sense 1 is the use in a question) (r:zd:25937/zd:25680/zd:19962) (q:draft, low confidence)
himawkding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:would be/must be) (d:<himawk> and <ding> written as one word: in a question, what or who ever could it be; in a statement, it must surely be) (j:himawk/ding) (r:zd:17830/zd:16511) (q:draft)
himawkleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if indeed/if it should be) (d:<himawk> and <leh>, if, written as one word: if it should really be so, supposing that it were) (j:himawk/leh) (r:zd:14901/zd:18054) (q:draft)
himawklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<himawk> and <lo> written as one word; in a question such as {himawklo ka hiam}, am I not after all, and in {cihtheih himawklo}, it cannot simply be said; exact force not certain) (j:himawk/lo) (r:zd:24139) (q:draft, low confidence)
himhim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at all/whatsoever/in itself) (d:placed after a noun or verb for emphasis: any at all, the thing as such; with a negative, not at all, by no means) (r:zd:23830/zd:25601/zd:22775) (q:draft)
himun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:this place/here/this point) (d:<hih>, this, and <mun>, place, written as one word in a shortened form; {himun ah} is here, at this point) (j:hih/mun) (r:zd:23984/zd:10733) (q:draft)
hin = (i:3) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:surely is/it is indeed) (d:the verb <hi>, be, in the form it takes before <teh> at the end of a sentence: {hin teh} states a thing as the conclusion of the speaker, it surely is so; it is not the shortened <hing>, live) (r:zd:19201/zd:24939) (q:draft, low confidence)
hina = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:first part of <hinapi>, although, when that word is written apart as {hina pi-in} or {hina pi'n}: although it is so, even though being) (r:zd:11197/zd:19577) (q:draft)
hinai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be yet) (d:<hi> be and <nai> yet written as one word; used with a negative, {hinai lo} or {hinai kei}: is not yet) (j:hi/nai) (r:zd:24047/zd:11206) (q:draft)
hinailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be not yet/is not yet) (d:<hi> and <nailo> written as one word: is not yet, has not yet become) (j:hi/nailo) (r:zd:23148/zd:21372) (q:draft)
hinawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be any longer) (d:<hi>, be, and <nawn>, any more, written as one word before <lo>: {hinawn lo} is no longer) (j:hi/nawn) (r:zd:21356/zd:20825/zd:24068) (q:draft)
hinawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be no longer/be not any more) (d:<hi>, be, and <nawnlo>, no longer, written as one word: is no longer what is named before it) (j:hi/nawnlo) (r:zd:19464/zd:20752/zd:23037) (q:draft)
Hindi = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social/education) (w:Hindi) (d:the Hindi language of India; {Hindi te} are the people who speak it) (r:zd:19875/zd:14965/ts:3506) (q:draft)
Hindu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:religion) (w:Hindu) (d:a follower of Hinduism, the main religion of India, or of that religion; {Hindu biakna} is the Hindu religion and {Hindu te} are the Hindus) (r:zd:17577/zd:15884) (q:draft)
Hinduism = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Hinduism) (d:the main religion of India) (o:English) (r:zd:15274/zd:25339) (q:draft)
Hindute = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:religion) (w:Hindus) (d:the Hindus, followers of the Hindu religion) (b:Hindu) (r:zd:10698/zd:10658) (q:draft)
hing = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:I am) (d:<hi> and the first person ending <ing> run together at the end of a sentence, after a noun, <ding> or <lo>: I am, I will, I do not; not the word for alive) (r:zd:25469/zd:20588/zd:24033) (q:draft)
hingei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have been/has ever been) (d:<hi>, be, and <ngei> written as one word: has been so at some time; with <lo>, is never so) (j:hi/ngei) (r:zd:21626/zd:21042/zd:23880) (q:draft)
hingel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:surely be/must be) (d:<hi>, be, and <ngel>, surely, written as one word: it surely is so, said of what the speaker supposes; {hingel ding hi} is it must be so) (j:hi/ngel) (r:zd:17409/zd:25173) (q:draft, low confidence)
hingelngel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:must surely be/most likely be) (d:<hi> and <ngelngel> written as one word, followed by <ding>: it must surely be so, said of what the speaker supposes) (j:hi/ngelngel) (r:zd:12915/zd:24946) (q:draft)
hingh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:I am/I will) (d:<hi> and <ing> written as one word with a final h: sentence-final I am, and after <ding>, I will) (j:hi/ing) (r:zd:24043/zd:16331) (q:draft, low confidence)
hingiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be indeed/truly be) (d:<hi>, is, and <ngiat>, indeed, written as one word: it really is so, nothing else) (j:hi/ngiat) (r:zd:22815/zd:22789) (q:draft)
hingtang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:alive/living) (d:in a living state, not dead; {a hingtang in}, also written <hingtangin>, is alive, while still living, and {hingtang kipiakna} is a living offering of oneself) (b:hing) (r:zd:25749/zd:22650) (q:draft)
hinteh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:it must be/it probably is) (d:<hi>, be, and <inteh> written as one word: sentence-final words for what the speaker supposes, it must be, it is surely) (j:hi/inteh) (r:ts:4885/zd:16216) (q:draft)
hinuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to be/tend to be) (d:<hi> and <nuam> written as one word: want to be something; also said of what is usually the case) (j:hi/nuam) (r:zd:23670/zd:14892) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipa = (i:2) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this man/he/him) (d:spoken form of <hihpa>, this man: used alone, without <a> before it, for a man who has just been mentioned or is pointed at, and not for the one who is something) (s:hihpa) (r:zd:11862/zd:22492/zd:12782) (q:draft)
hipah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be just/be simply/be at once) (d:<hi>, be, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: it is simply that, it follows at once that it is so; {cihna hipah hi} is that is just what it means) (j:hi/pah) (r:zd:22641/zd:24320/zd:22701) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipahding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be/will then be) (d:<hipah> and <ding> written as one word: will at once be, will thereby be, as of the one who will be the first to do something) (j:hipah/ding) (r:zd:11965) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipahlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not necessarily/does not simply mean) (d:<hipah> and <lo> written as one word: it is not simply so, it does not follow at once) (j:hipah/lo) (r:zd:22278/zd:11587) (q:draft)
hipahpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be at once/be simply) (d:<hi> and <pahpah> written as one word: is so at once, is so in each case without more ado) (j:hi/pahpah) (r:zd:11159/zd:22950) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, be, with <pak>, at once or for a moment, written as one word: just happen to be, simply be so) (j:hi/pak) (r:ts:2680) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be only/be just/be so far) (d:<hi>, be, written as one word with <pan>, here just, so far: is only this much as yet; mostly after an age, number or amount with <bek>, only, as in {kum 28 bek hipan hi}, is only 28 years old) (j:hi/pan) (r:zd:11782/zd:14597/zd:12307) (q:draft)
hipanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:would be only/will be the first) (d:<hipan> and <ding> written as one word: is probably only that much, said of an estimated age or amount, or will be the first so far) (j:hipan/ding) (r:zd:11803/zd:19648) (q:draft)
hipanin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:being only/being just) (d:<hipan>, be only so far, with the linking <in>, written as one word: being only this much as yet, after an age or a count, and leading on to the next clause) (j:hipan/in) (r:zd:16162/zd:24457) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipanlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be still only/be only so far) (d:<hipan>, be only so far, with <lai>, still, written as one word: is as yet only this, mostly after <bek>) (j:hipan/lai) (r:zd:12685/zd:19725) (q:draft)
hipen = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:this) (d:<hih>, this, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word at the start of a sentence: this, as for this) (j:hih/pen) (r:zd:16820/zd:21083) (q:draft)
hipen = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, be, with <pen> written as one word at the end of a clause: it is, is it) (j:hi/pen) (r:zd:19441/zd:16442) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipeuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be so/be indeed) (d:<hi>, be, and <peuh> written as one word: {tua hipeuh leh} is if only that is so, in that case, and {hipeuh mah lo} is it is not so at all) (j:hi/peuh) (r:zd:11714/zd:25515/zd:11197) (q:draft)
hipeuhleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if that is so/as long as it is/provided it is) (d:<hi>, be, and <peuhleh> written as one word: if only it is so, as long as it is; {tua hipeuhleh} is if that is the case) (j:hi/peuhleh) (r:zd:21876/zd:17796) (q:draft)
hipeuhmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<hi> and <peuhmah> written as one word, found before <lo>: {hipeuhmah lo hi} is it is not necessarily so, it is by no means so) (j:hi/peuhmah) (r:zd:20315/zd:23554) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipeuhmahlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be not at all/be by no means) (d:<hi>, <peuhmah> and <lo> written as one word: is not at all, is by no means; a strong negative of <hi>, be) (j:hi/peuhmah/lo) (r:zd:19305/zd:11941/zd:15994) (q:draft)
hipha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be mostly/be chiefly) (d:<hi>, be, and <pha> written as one word: be so for the most part, be chiefly or properly so; usually followed by <pen>, <diak> or <deuh>) (j:hi/pha) (r:zd:26444/zd:23901) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiphadiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be mainly/be especially/be chiefly) (d:<hi> and <phadiak> written as one word at the end of a statement: it is mainly, it is above all) (j:hi/phadiak) (r:zd:15465/zd:15089/zd:11997) (q:draft)
hiphial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be indeed/even if it is) (d:<hi>, be, with <phial>, written as one word: before {mah leh}, <taleh> or <zongin> it means even if it is so, and at the end of a sentence it is indeed so) (j:hi/phial) (r:zd:20083/zd:23057/zd:25242) (q:draft)
hiphot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be so for now/be so far) (d:<hi>, the closing word of a statement, and <phot>, for the time being, written as one word at the end of a sentence: that is how it stands for now, so far) (j:hi/phot) (r:ts:5513/ts:8728/zd:16119) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be the main one/be chiefly) (d:<hi>, be, with <pi>, great or chief, mostly as {hipi pen hi}: is the chief one, is mainly that; said of the main cause or the main example) (j:hi/pi) (r:zd:23338/zd:18086) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:seem to be/be rather) (d:<hi>, be, and <pian>, here seemingly, written as one word: it seems to be so, it is rather so) (j:hi/pian) (r:zd:23846/zd:25915) (q:draft, low confidence)
hipipen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be chiefly/be mainly) (d:<hi>, be, and <pipen>, chief, written as one word: is chiefly that, is the main one; {hang hipipen hi} is it is mainly because of) (j:hi/pipen) (r:zd:16259/zd:11117) (q:draft)
hipong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just be/simply be) (d:<hi>, be, and <pong>, anyway, written as one word: it simply is so, it is so regardless) (j:hi/pong) (r:ts:7676/zd:22992) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hiroshima = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Hiroshima) (d:city in Japan, the first city on which a nuclear bomb was dropped, in 1945) (r:zd:12183) (q:draft)
hisa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:think it is so/agree/consider to be) (d:<hi>, be so, with a word for think or feel, elsewhere written {hi sa}: hold that something is so, agree with it, or consider a thing to be what is named before it) (r:zd:19262/zd:20826/zd:10823) (q:draft)
hisam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be really/be exactly) (d:<hi>, be, with a softening particle, written as one word; mostly negative, {hisam lo hi} or {hisam kei}: it is not really so, it is not exactly that) (r:zd:24068/zd:25158/zd:25923) (q:draft)
hisamkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:it is not really/not exactly) (d:<hi>, be, with <samkei>, not really, written as one word: it is not really so, often after {cihzongbel} or <cihbangbel>, not that one would say) (j:hi/samkei) (r:zd:19648/zd:15890) (q:draft)
hisamlo = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:is not really/is not at all) (d:<hi>, be, with <sam> and <lo>, not, written as one word: a stronger <hilo>, it is not really so, it is by no means so; <sam> here strengthens the negative and is not the verb call) (j:hi/sam/lo) (r:zd:22056/zd:15260/zd:16404) (q:draft)
hisawnsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:turn out to be/happen to be) (d:<hi>, be, and <sawnsawn> written as one word: closes a statement in news reports that adds what someone or something proved to be: is in fact, turned out to be) (j:hi/sawnsawn) (r:zd:11731/zd:15456/zd:19562) (q:draft, low confidence)
hise = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, be, with the emphatic particle <se>, written as one word: it is indeed; mostly negative, {hise lo hi}, nor is it, it is not that either) (j:hi/se) (r:zd:11687/zd:20905) (q:draft, low confidence)
hisese = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to be/be just) (d:<hi>, be, with the emphatic <sese>, written as one word: it is just so, it happens to be exactly that) (j:hi/sese) (r:zd:22873) (q:draft, low confidence)
Hispanic = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Hispanic) (d:the Hispanic people of the United States, counted as a group beside Whites, Blacks and Asians) (o:English) (r:zd:25731/zd:22329) (q:draft)
histamine = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:histamine) (d:a substance that the body gives out, as under stress or in an allergy) (o:English) (r:zd:23486) (q:draft, low confidence)
historian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:historian) (d:a person who studies and writes history; used beside the Zolai {tangthukan}) (o:English) (r:zd:23329) (q:draft, low confidence)
hitading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:will now be/will become) (d:<hi>, be, and <tading> written as one word: will be so from now on, is now going to be) (j:hi/tading) (r:zd:12271/zd:12512) (q:draft)
hitakpi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be truly so/really be/be indeed) (d:<hi> and <takpi> written as one word: it truly is so, be really the case) (j:hi/takpi) (r:zd:21670/zd:14750/zd:14805) (q:draft)
hitaktak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really be/truly be) (d:<hi>, be, and <taktak>, truly, written as one word: really is, is in fact) (j:hi/taktak) (r:zd:11289/zd:14751) (q:draft)
hitam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:is it/is it so) (d:<hi>, be, with the question word <tam>, written as one word at the end of a question, often followed by <maw>: is it, could it be; {a takpi mah a hitam} is is it really so) (r:zd:22586/zd:23022) (q:draft, low confidence)
hitamai = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, be, with <tamai>, written as one word at the end of a sentence: it has simply come to be so, that is just how it is) (j:hi/tamai) (r:zd:11642) (q:draft, low confidence)
hitamawk = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:has now become/now is) (d:<hita>, now is, and <mawk>, here a word of surprise or concern, written as one word: it has now come to be so, more than one would expect) (j:hita/mawk) (r:zd:16170/zd:14947) (q:draft)
hitan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:this much/this long/so far) (d:{hih tan} written short and as one word, <hih> this with <tan> as far as: to this extent, for as long or as far as this) (r:zd:20952/zd:24234) (q:draft)
hitawntung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:remain/always be) (d:<hi> and <tawntung> written as one word: be so all the time, stay the same) (j:hi/tawntung) (r:zd:11587) (q:draft)
hiteh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hi> and the second person ending <teh> written as one word, closing a statement about the person spoken to: you are, you will) (j:hi/teh) (r:zd:17271/zd:16245/zd:10746) (q:draft)
hiteng = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:all these/these/all this) (d:{hih teng} shortened and written as one word: these, all of the things or persons just named or about to be named) (r:zd:19654/zd:24276/zd:19953) (q:draft, low confidence)
hitheiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:may be/could be/be likely) (d:<hithei>, can be, and <ding>, will, written as one word: it may be so, it is likely to be; often followed by {kici hi}, it is said) (j:hithei/ding) (r:zd:15836/zd:15732) (q:draft)
hitheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be impossible/cannot be) (d:<hithei> and <lo> written as one word: it cannot be, it is not possible; {a hitheilo ding} is what cannot happen) (j:hithei/lo) (r:zd:19166/zd:23803/zd:14861) (q:draft)
hitheizah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as much as possible/as far as possible) (d:<hithei>, be possible, and <zah>, amount, written as one word; used as {a hitheizah in}, as much as can be) (j:hithei/zah) (r:zd:24276) (q:draft)
hithiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to do at ease/will do in peace) (d:<hithiat>, at ease, and <ding>, to or will, written as one word, after a verb: in order to do it quietly and undisturbed) (j:hithiat/ding) (r:zd:13233/zd:15425) (q:draft)
hithit = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday/food) (w:pleasantly/nicely/cosily) (d:after <lum>, warm: {lum hithit} is a gentle, pleasant warmth, as of a warm drink, warm water or a heated house) (r:zd:24276/zd:22808/zd:19812) (q:draft)
hithong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is indeed/truly is) (d:<hi>, be, with the emphatic ending {-thong} written as one word: is indeed so; {hithong hilo ih hi hiam} asks are we not indeed so) (r:zd:22646) (q:draft, low confidence)
hithu = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:this matter/this) (d:<hih>, this, with <thu>, matter, written as one word: this matter, the thing just spoken of) (j:hih/thu) (r:zd:24230/zd:25678/zd:23363) (q:draft)
hitota = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:has now reached/has come to be/is already) (d:<hi>, be, with <to>, on and on, and <ta>, now, written as one word: has by now come to be, has reached a number or a point in time) (j:hi/to/ta) (r:zd:12941/zd:14869/zd:12715) (q:draft)
hituak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:both be/each be) (d:<hi>, be, and <tuak>, each or both, written as one word: both are, each of them is; before <lo> also it is not fitting that) (j:hi/tuak) (r:zd:12998/zd:17812) (q:draft, low confidence)
hituan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be necessarily/be really) (d:<hi>, be, and the particle <tuan> written as one word, before a negative: {hituan lo hi} is it is not necessarily so, it does not follow that) (j:hi/tuan) (r:zd:12507/zd:26838) (q:draft)
hituankei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not necessarily/is not just) (d:<hi> and <tuankei> written as one word: it is not so for all that; after <bekzong>, it is not only that) (j:hi/tuankei) (r:zd:15639) (q:draft)
hituanlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not necessarily/is not for all that) (d:<hi>, <tuan> and <lo> written as one word: it is not so in spite of what might be expected, it does not follow that it is) (j:hi/tuan/lo) (r:zd:20850/zd:23198/zd:12460) (q:draft)
hiuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be/are) (d:<hi> and the plural <uh> written as one word: they are, you are, mostly in {na hiuh hi} and {ana hiuh hi}) (j:hi/uh) (r:zd:21626) (q:draft)
hiuhiau = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:gently/pleasantly/softly/mildly) (d:placed after <nui> or <maitai>, of a soft, pleasant smile on the face, and after <vot>, <lum> or <san>, of a mild and pleasant degree of cool, warmth or colour; not striking or strong) (r:zd:26385/zd:11323/zd:19812) (q:draft)
hivai = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:this matter/this affair) (d:<hih>, this, and <vai>, matter, written as one word without the final h of <hih>, also written <hihvai>: the matter just spoken of) (j:hih/vai) (r:zd:24495/zd:11623) (q:draft)
hivaw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, the sentence ending, and the exclamation <vaw> written as one word: closes a sentence with feeling, it is so indeed) (j:hi/vaw) (r:zd:11110/zd:8389) (q:draft, low confidence)
hive = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be indeed) (d:<hi> and <ve> written as one word: it is so indeed, an emphatic statement, usually followed by a person ending such as <hang>, <ungh> or <maw>) (j:hi/ve) (r:zd:21590/zd:16457) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiveh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hi> with the exclamatory <veh> written as one word, at the end of a sentence and mostly followed by <aw> or <e>: it surely is, it must be, said with feeling or as a supposition) (j:hi/veh) (r:ts:2963/zd:14498) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiveh aw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hiveh>, it surely is, and the exclamatory <aw>: ends a sentence that the speaker utters with feeling, as an exclamation or a supposition, it really is, it must be, you know) (r:zd:24327/ts:2963) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiven = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:after all/indeed) (d:<hi>, be, with the sentence-final <ven>, written as one word: ends a statement that the speaker treats as plain or as known to the hearer, it is so after all, you see) (j:hi/ven) (r:zd:15883/zd:25686/ts:3446) (q:draft, low confidence)
hiveng = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hi>, <ve> and <ing> written as one word: sentence ending of the first person singular that stresses the statement, I am indeed, I do; {ding hiveng} is I surely will) (j:hi/ve/ing) (r:zd:24132/zd:12998/zd:25562) (q:draft)
hiveve = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still be/be all the same) (d:<hi>, be, and <veve>, all the same, written as one word: it still is so, it is so nevertheless) (j:hi/veve) (r:zd:25928/zd:14599) (q:draft)
hizahin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:this much/so much/to this extent) (d:<hizah>, this much, with <in>, written as one word: to such a degree, as much as this) (j:hizah/in) (r:zd:18005/zd:22334) (q:draft)
hizahliang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:this much/to such an extent/so badly) (d:<hizah>, this much, with <liang>, even, written as one word and followed by <in>: to such a degree as this) (j:hizah/liang) (r:zd:14914/zd:20155/zd:14720) (q:draft)
hizahta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:so much/to this extent/so greatly) (d:<hizah>, this much, with the ending <ta>, compare <zahta>: to such an extent as this; usually followed by <a>, <aa> or <in>) (b:hizah) (r:zd:9445/zd:21066/zd:19295) (q:draft)
hizahtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:so many/so much/this much) (d:<hizah>, this many, and the strengthening <tak> written as one word: as many or as much as this, to such a degree) (j:hizah/tak) (r:zd:19953/zd:24132) (q:draft)
hizahzah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:so many/this many/so much) (d:<hizah>, this many, with <zah> said twice for stress: as many or as much as this, said with wonder at the number) (b:hizah) (r:zd:15221/zd:15943/zd:20503) (q:draft)
hizawden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be mostly/be usually) (d:<hizaw>, be rather, and <den>, always, written as one word: it is more often than not, it is nearly always these) (j:hizaw/den) (r:zd:19367) (q:draft, low confidence)
hizawhi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is rather/is instead) (d:<hizaw>, be rather, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: it is rather this) (j:hizaw/hi) (r:zd:23025/zd:22921) (q:draft)
hizawlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be even more so/be still rather) (d:<hi> and <zawlai> written as one word: it is even more so, it is still rather the case) (j:hi/zawlai) (r:zd:11057/zd:16170) (q:draft, low confidence)
hizawlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is not rather/it is not so much) (d:<hizaw> and <lo> written as one word: it is not this, the first half of a contrast whose second half ends in <hizaw>, it is rather that) (j:hizaw/lo) (r:zd:23113/zd:21288) (q:draft)
hizawpian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be mostly/tend to be/be rather) (d:<hizaw>, be rather, with <pian>, here somewhat: be for the most part, tend to be, often after <vive>, all, only) (b:hizaw) (r:zd:12856/zd:20488/zd:14568) (q:draft, low confidence)
hizawta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:has rather become/is now rather) (d:<hizaw> and the particle <ta> written as one word: it has now come to be rather so; {akiphelhzolam hizawta} is it is now on the way to being put out) (j:hizaw/ta) (r:zd:15795/zd:17301) (q:draft)
Hizbolla = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:Hezbollah) (d:the armed Shia movement and party of Lebanon, allied with Iran, that fights against Israel) (r:ts:3234/ts:5116) (q:draft)
hizeel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still be/be as ever/be always) (d:<hi> and <zeel> written as one word at the end of a statement, often after <mah>: it is still so, it is that again as always) (s:hizel) (j:hi/zeel) (r:zd:20477/zd:25866) (q:draft, low confidence)
hizel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be again/keep being) (d:<hi> and <zel> written as one word at the end of a statement: it is so again, it is always so) (j:hi/zel) (r:zd:21221/zd:15883) (q:draft, low confidence)
hizen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really be/simply be) (d:<hi>, be, and the emphatic <zen> written as one word: it really is so, it is simply that) (j:hi/zen) (r:zd:12998/zd:11409) (q:draft)
hizenleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if it were/if only) (d:<hizen>, really be, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if it really were so, often of something that did not happen or is only wished) (j:hizen/leh) (r:zd:11984/zd:12456) (q:draft)
hizenzen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really be/be exactly) (d:<hi> and <zenzen> written as one word: really be so; mostly with <lo>, as in {hizenzen lo hi}, it is not really so, not exactly, and with <leh>, if it should really be) (j:hi/zenzen) (r:zd:11019/zd:24220/zd:15274) (q:draft)
hizenzenleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if it really is/in the case of/should it be) (d:<hizenzen>, really be, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if it should really be so, in the very case of) (j:hizenzen/leh) (r:zd:17112) (q:draft, low confidence)
hizenzenlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not really be/not necessarily be) (d:<hi>, <zenzen> and <lo> written as one word: is not really so, is not necessarily the case) (j:hi/zenzen/lo) (r:zd:11587/zd:12938) (q:draft)
hiziau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:simply be/just be) (d:<hi>, be, and <ziau> written as one word before the final <hi>: it is simply so, it is just that and nothing more) (j:hi/ziau) (r:zd:17313/zd:19774/zd:20905) (q:draft)
hizong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/whether/however) (d:<hi>, be, and <zong>, also, written as one word: even if it is, whether it is; {a hizong} at the start of a sentence is however, even so) (j:hi/zong) (r:zd:23972/zd:20800) (q:draft)
hizongin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:but/however/whether) (d:<hi>, be, and <zongin>, although, written as one word after <a>: {a hizongin} at the head of a sentence is but or however, after <bangbang> it is whatever the case, and after each of several nouns it is whether this or that) (j:hi/zongin) (r:zd:21869/zd:20142/zd:22584) (q:draft)
Hlaingtharya = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Hlaingtharya/Hlaing Tharyar) (d:a township on the west side of Yangon in Myanmar) (r:zd:16853/zd:19392) (q:draft)
