Hlotdaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:parliament/legislature/assembly) (d:a house of parliament of Myanmar or of one of its states, as in {Chin State Hlotdaw}) (o:Burmese, hluttaw) (r:zd:22586) (q:draft)
Hlutdaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:parliament/assembly/legislature) (d:the parliament of Myanmar or of one of its states, as in {State Hlutdaw}) (o:Burmese, hluttaw) (r:zd:10861/zd:24736) (q:draft)
Hluttaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:parliament/legislature) (d:the parliament of Myanmar or of one of its states and regions; {Pyithu Hluttaw} is the lower house and {Amyotha Hluttaw} the upper house) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:15565/zd:15743) (q:draft)
Hmar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Hmar) (d:a people related to the Zomi and Mizo, living in Mizoram, Manipur and Assam in India) (r:zd:14867) (q:draft)
hmatpongtin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:identity card/national registration card) (d:the citizen identity card of Myanmar, the national registration card; a Burmese word) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:23957/zd:14820) (q:draft)
Hmawbi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Hmawbi) (d:town and township north of Yangon in Myanmar) (r:zd:21925/zd:17409) (q:draft)
Hmm = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday) (w:hmm) (d:sound made while thinking or hesitating before speaking) (r:zd:17860) (q:draft)
Hnahlan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Hnahlan) (d:a village in Mizoram, India, near the border with Myanmar) (r:zd:24544/zd:14867) (q:draft)
hoih = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:good/fine) (d:good in quality or in character, also fine or beautiful; {hoih lo} is not good) (s:pha) (a:gilo/hoihlo/siat) (r:25.3.25)
hoih kisa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:think it good/find it best/be in favour) (d:<hoih>, good, and <kisa>, be felt or considered: it is thought good, used to give an opinion or a recommendation; the thing judged stands before it, often a clause ending in <ding>, it is thought good to do so; of a person it is think oneself good) (r:zd:25212/zd:11076) (q:draft)
hoihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:would be good/will be good) (d:<hoih>, good, and <ding> written as one word: it will or would be good, often after a clause with <leh> or <leng>, if) (j:hoih/ding) (r:zd:12715/zd:21869/zd:25470) (q:draft)
hoihhetlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/health) (w:not good at all/very bad) (d:<hoih> and <hetlo> written as one word: not good at all) (j:hoih/hetlo) (r:zd:20764/zd:16346/zd:14879) (q:draft)
hoihhi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:is good/it is good) (d:<hoih>, good, and <hi.2> written as one word at the end of a sentence: is good; after a verb with <ding> it is good to do so) (j:hoih/hi) (r:zd:11472/zd:17651/zd:16321) (q:draft)
hoihkei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not good/bad) (d:<hoih>, good, and the negative <kei.2>, written as one word: it is not good) (j:hoih/kei) (r:zd:22116) (q:draft)
hoihkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:a good one) (d:<hoih>, good, and <khat>, one, written as one word after a noun: a good one, a good) (j:hoih/khat) (r:zd:20929/zd:25712) (q:draft)
hoihkhin = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:good/all right) (d:<hoih>, good, and <khin> written as one word; in the articles nearly always negated, as {hoihkhin hetlo}, not good at all, and {hoihkhin samlo}, not really good) (j:hoih/khin) (r:zd:13163/zd:14879) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihkhomkhat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:reasonably good/decent/proper) (d:used after <a>: of a fairly good or fitting standard, as well as is suitable; seems to be <hoih>, good, <khom>, be enough, and <khat>, one, written as one word) (j:hoih/khom/khat) (r:zd:23985/zd:24276) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:become good again/recover/be restored) (d:<hoih>, good, and <kik>, again, written as one word) (j:hoih/kik) (r:zd:18054/zd:25620) (q:draft)
hoihkikding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:will be well again/will get better again) (d:<hoih> and <kikding> written as one word: will become good again, will recover) (j:hoih/kikding) (r:zd:19818/zd:17556) (q:draft)
hoihkisa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be considered good/be thought best) (d:<hoih>, good, and <kisa>, be considered, written as one word: people find it good or advisable) (j:hoih/kisa) (r:zd:11076) (q:draft)
hoihlai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:still good/still sound) (d:<hoih>, good, and <lai>, here in its sense of still, written as one word: still good, still in good condition) (j:hoih/lai) (r:zd:12998/zd:16754) (q:draft)
hoihlam = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:good side/positive side/the better) (d:used as a noun, mostly as {a hoihlam}: the good or positive side of a matter, and the direction of improvement; {a hoihlam in mu} is see something positively and {hoihlam manawh} is move toward the better, against <siatlam>) (r:zd:21568/zd:17344/zd:14850) (q:draft)
hoihleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if good/when good) (d:<hoih>, good, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if or when someone or something is good) (j:hoih/leh) (r:zd:21099/zd:16071) (q:draft)
hoihlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:bad/not good) (d:<hoih>, good, with the negative <lo>, written as one word: not good, bad) (s:gilo/siat) (a:hoih) (b:hoih) (q:draft)
hoihloh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not good/bad) (d:<hoih>, good, with the negative <loh> written as one word, the form used before endings such as <na>, <man> and <hangin>; {a hoihloh na} is the bad side of something) (s:hoihlo) (j:hoih/loh) (r:zd:12998/zd:22444) (q:draft)
hoihlohna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:disadvantage/drawback/defect/bad condition) (d:the bad side or poor state of a thing, without any thought of moral evil: paired with <hoihna> it is the disadvantages beside the advantages, and after a thing such as {brake} or <khuahun> it is a fault or a bad condition) (r:zd:22464/zd:20734/zd:24276) (q:draft)
hoihlolam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:bad side/negative side/the wrong way) (d:<hoihlo>, not good, with <lam>, side or direction, written as one word: the bad or negative side; {a hoihlolam ngaihsutna} is negative thinking) (j:hoihlo/lam) (r:zd:21989) (q:draft)
hoihmahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very good/excellent) (d:<hoih>, good, with <mahmah>, very, written as one word) (j:hoih/mahmah) (r:zd:22451/zd:25909) (q:draft)
hoihmaw = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:whether good/is it good) (d:<hoih>, good, with the question particle <maw> written as one word: whether something is good, often followed by <hoihlo>, or not) (j:hoih/maw) (r:zd:19397/zd:23025) (q:draft)
hoihpenpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:the very best/best of all) (d:<hoih> and <penpen> written as one word: the very best) (j:hoih/penpen) (r:zd:22894/zd:21869) (q:draft)
hoihsalua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:like very much/find very good/admire greatly) (d:<hoihsa> and <lua> written as one word: find a person or thing very good or attractive) (j:hoihsa/lua) (r:zd:19357/zd:16817) (q:draft)
hoihsem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:do good/do good work) (d:<hoih>, good, with <sem>, do, written as one word; after <na>, work: {na hoihsem} is do good work) (j:hoih/sem) (r:zd:20337/zd:19257) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihsemsem = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:better and better/ever better) (d:<hoih> and <semsem> written as one word: become better and better) (j:hoih/semsem) (r:zd:11662/zd:12093) (q:draft)
hoihta = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:good now/has become good) (d:<hoih> and <ta> written as one word: it is good now, it has become good) (j:hoih/ta) (r:zd:23014/zd:21259/zd:20736) (q:draft)
hoihtaka = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:well/properly/carefully) (d:<hoih> and <taka> written as one word: well, properly, with care) (s:hoihtakin) (j:hoih/taka) (r:zd:23112/zd:24153) (q:draft)
hoihtakzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not even properly/hardly) (d:<hoihtak> and <zong> written as one word, before a verb with <theilo> or <nawnlo>: not even properly, hardly at all) (j:hoihtak/zong) (r:zd:20668/zd:12996/zd:19894) (q:draft)
hoihtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:with a good/with good) (d:<hoih> and <tawh> written as one word, after a noun: with a good one, as in {mimin hoihtawh}, by a good name) (j:hoih/tawh) (r:zd:22171/zd:22282) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can be good/be good) (d:<hoih>, good, and <thei>, able, written as one word: be able to be good or to do well) (j:hoih/thei) (r:zd:23782/zd:10863) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihtuakzaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:better/more advisable) (d:<hoihtuak>, good and fitting, and <zaw>, more, written as one word: it is better, it would be more advisable) (j:hoihtuak/zaw) (r:zd:12510/zd:15949) (q:draft)
hoihtuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:get better/improve/be the better for it) (d:<hoih>, good, and <tuam>, all the more, written as one word: become better, of health or of a thing) (j:hoih/tuam) (r:zd:21922/zd:11167) (q:draft)
hokhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:finish talking/have talked) (d:<ho>, talk, and <khit>, after, written as one word, mostly as {aki hokhit ciangin}, after they had talked together) (j:ho/khit) (r:zd:15608/zd:18020) (q:draft)
Hokkaido = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Hokkaido) (d:the northernmost of the main islands of Japan, and the region of that name) (r:zd:15781/zd:17551) (q:draft)
holh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:pick/poke into/dig out) (d:push a finger or a thin object into a hole and work it about, as in picking the ear or the nose; {van holh} is poke the sky, said of something very high) (r:zd:24276/zd:12507) (q:draft)
holiday = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/work) (w:holiday/day off) (d:a day or time free from work, a public holiday or a holiday trip; English word used in Zolai sentences) (o:English) (r:zd:23400/zd:16204) (q:draft, low confidence)
holim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:converse/chat/talk together) (d:talk with someone in a friendly, unhurried way; the person talked with is marked by <tawh>, and {ki holim} is talk with one another) (s:kiho) (r:zd:25562/zd:20334/zd:17060) (q:draft)
holimna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:conversation/talk/discussion/chat) (d:a talking together, a conversation or discussion, in news also an interview with someone; {holimna nei} is hold a talk; built on <ho>, talk) (r:zd:20587/zd:22680/ts:5105) (q:draft)
holimnate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:conversations/talks/discussions) (d:plural of <holimna>, conversation) (b:holimna) (r:zd:25562) (q:draft)
holimpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:talk with/converse with/chat with) (d:<holim>, converse, with <pih>, together with: have a talk with someone, who is named without <tawh>) (b:holim) (j:holim/pih) (r:zd:20999/zd:22928) (q:draft)
holimpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/health) (w:counselling/talking with) (d:<holim>, converse, with <pih>, together with, and the noun suffix {-na}: talking with a person to help or comfort, counselling) (b:holim) (r:zd:22928) (q:draft)
Holland = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Holland/Netherlands) (d:the country in western Europe, also called the Netherlands, mostly as {Holland gam}) (s:Netherlands) (r:zd:24230/zd:9237) (q:draft)
Hollywood = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:media) (w:Hollywood) (d:district of Los Angeles in the United States, and the American film industry that has its home there) (r:zd:11796/zd:10722) (q:draft)
Homalin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Homalin) (d:town and township in Sagaing Region, Myanmar) (r:ts:2942/ts:5326) (q:draft)
homecell = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:home cell/cell group/house fellowship) (d:a small group of church members that meets in a home for prayer and worship) (o:English, home cell) (r:zd:10682/zd:13297) (q:draft)
homework = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:homework) (s:innlai) (o:English) (r:zd:20486) (q:draft, low confidence)
hon = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:open) (d:open a door, a gate, a book or the eyes; before <sak> it is written with an apostrophe) (a:khaksak/kalh) (r:20.18.16) (q:draft)
hon hun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/time) (w:opening hours/opening time) (d:<hon>, open, and <hun>, time: the hours when an office, clinic or school is open, or the time when it opens; the place stands before it, as in {zum hon hun}, office hours) (r:zd:20418/zd:24234) (q:draft)
hona = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:talk/conversation/talking) (d:noun form of <ho>, talk: the act of talking with someone, mostly as {ki hona}, a conversation, and {phone hona}, talking on the phone; not the {hona} of {a hon hona}, in groups) (r:zd:23317/zd:20172/zd:19518) (q:draft)
honbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/travel) (w:open more/open further/open another) (d:<hon>, open, with a second part meaning in addition, not <beh>, clan: open a further shop, branch or stretch of line beside those already open) (b:hon) (r:zd:19215/zd:14633) (q:draft)
honbehding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:will open more/will open further) (d:<hon>, open, <beh>, here more or in addition and not the noun clan, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will open more of something, such as shops, service centres or a railway line) (j:hon/beh/ding) (r:zd:14665/zd:11441) (q:draft)
Honda = (i:1) (t:name) (f:travel) (w:Honda) (d:a Japanese make of car and motorcycle) (o:Japanese) (r:zd:17100/zd:15568) (q:draft)
honding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:to open/will open) (d:<hon>, open, and <ding>, written as one word: to open or going to open a door, a shop or a market) (j:hon/ding) (r:zd:19648/zd:24544) (q:draft)
honeymoon = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/travel) (w:honeymoon) (d:the holiday taken by a newly married couple; {honeymoon pai} is go on honeymoon) (o:English) (r:zd:16757/zd:17055) (q:draft)
hong nusiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:pass away/die/leave us) (d:<hong>, towards us, and <nusiat>, a form of <nusia>, leave behind: said of a relative or respected person who has died, he or she has left us; this form stands before words such as <laitakin>, <teh>, <dan> and <dahpihna>) (r:zd:25178/zd:21925) (q:draft)
hong nusiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:passing/death/decease) (d:<hong>, toward us, and <nusiatna>, leaving behind: his or her leaving us, a gentle word for the death of a person in notices of mourning and condolence; the name or kin term of the dead stands before it and <hangin>, because of, usually after it) (r:zd:22938/zd:21550) (q:draft)
hong sihsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:pass away/leave us in death) (d:the prefix <hong>, toward us, and <sihsan>, die leaving behind: to die and leave us; the usual wording of a death notice, and said of a relative who has died) (r:zd:10672/zd:21233) (q:draft)
hong zatsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:use us/use you) (d:<hong>, towards us or you, and <zatsak>, put to use: said of God using a person in his service; in the blessing {Topa'n hong zatsak semsem tahen}, may the Lord use you more and more) (r:zd:23155/zd:15951) (q:draft)
honga = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:open) (d:<hon>, open, with the linking <a> written as one word: opened and; said of opening a parcel, a school or a time for questions) (j:hon/a) (r:zd:9212/zd:22185) (q:draft)
hongbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:make/do) (d:<hong> and <bawl> written as one word: make or do, with the action directed toward the speaker or the person addressed, as when God made us) (j:hong/bawl) (r:zd:20202/zd:17933/zd:21922) (q:draft)
hongbawlpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:our Maker/Creator) (d:<hong> and <bawlpa> written as one word: the one who made us, said of God) (j:hong/bawlpa) (r:zd:15437/zd:15584) (q:draft)
hongbawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:make for us/do for us) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <bawlsak>, make or do for someone, written as one word: made or arranged it for us or for you) (j:hong/bawlsak) (r:zd:17876/zd:20035/zd:25275) (q:draft)
hongbawlsia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:harm us/mistreat you/do harm) (d:<hong> and <bawlsia> written as one word: do harm to us or to you; {hongbawlsia te} are those who harm you) (j:hong/bawlsia) (r:zd:12112) (q:draft)
hongbei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:come to an end/pass/run out) (d:<hong> and <bei> written as one word: come to an end, pass away, be used up) (j:hong/bei) (r:zd:15956/zd:23035/zd:24593) (q:draft)
hongci = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say to me/tell us) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <ci>, say, written as one word after the words quoted: said to me or to us) (j:hong/ci) (r:zd:13190/zd:24029/zd:15662) (q:draft)
hongciah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:come home/come back/return) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <ciah>, go home, written as one word: come back home) (j:hong/ciah) (r:zd:21389/zd:18050/zd:13350) (q:draft)
hongciahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come back/return) (d:the verb prefix <hong> and <ciahkik>, return, written as one word: come back here) (j:hong/ciahkik) (r:zd:19644/zd:11649) (q:draft)
hongcih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say to me/say to us/tell) (d:<hong> and <cih> written as one word: what someone says to the speaker, used before words such as <ciangin>) (j:hong/cih) (r:zd:17187/zd:10874/zd:12329) (q:draft)
hongcing = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/religion) (w:watch over us/guard us/look after us) (d:<hong> and <cing> written as one word: watch over or tend us or me, often beside <hongkem>) (j:hong/cing) (r:zd:24123/zd:22116) (q:draft)
hongcing = (i:2) (t:v) (f:time) (w:be completed/come to the full) (d:<hong> with <cing> in its sense be full, written as one word: of time or a number of years, come to the full; {kum 10 hongcing} is ten years have been completed) (j:hong/cing) (r:zd:21408) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongdal = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:protect us/shield/block) (d:the particle <hong> with <dal>, shield or block, written as one word: it shields or keeps us from something; also it stands in the way) (j:hong/dal) (r:zd:17152/zd:22644) (q:draft)
hongdam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:get cold/ease/be relieved) (d:<hong> and <dam> written as one word: of the weather, turn cold; with <sak>, of tiredness, make it ease) (j:hong/dam) (r:zd:11510/zd:12919) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongdawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:come to meet/come to fetch/welcome) (d:<hong> and <dawn>, meet, written as one word: come to meet or welcome someone, come to fetch someone) (j:hong/dawn) (r:zd:18152/zd:10973) (q:draft)
hongdawn = (i:2) (t:v) (f:food) (w:come to drink) (d:<hong> and <dawn>, drink, written as one word: come and drink) (j:hong/dawn) (r:zd:25915) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongdawng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:answer/reply) (d:<hong> and <dawng>, answer, written as one word: answer the speaker or the person addressed; {hongdawng kik} is answer back) (j:hong/dawng) (r:zd:11170/zd:16216) (q:draft)
hongdeih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want of us/want from you) (d:<hong> and <deih>, want, written as one word: he wants us or you, he wants us or you to do something) (j:hong/deih) (r:zd:22171/zd:16012) (q:draft)
hongdeihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:care for us/wish us well/want for us) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, with <deihsak>, want for, written as one word: wish something good for us or for you, care for us) (j:hong/deihsak) (r:zd:15356) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:will open/be going to open) (d:the verb open, keyword <hon>, here spelled with a final g, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will open a shop, an office, a hospital or an account; before <khia> the same spelling is <hong> <dingkhia>, set out or be founded) (j:hon/ding) (r:zd:11170/zd:12674/zd:19829) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongdo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (w:fight for us/fight) (d:<hong> and <do>, fight, written as one word: fight toward or on behalf of the speaker or the people addressed; {hongdo sak} is fight for someone) (j:hong/do) (r:zd:12801) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongdong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ask/inquire of) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <dong>, ask, written as one word: ask me or us; in a story also ask the person spoken of) (j:hong/dong) (r:zd:23797/zd:10761/zd:21357) (q:draft)
hongdongh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ask me/ask us) (d:<hong> and <dongh>, ask, written as one word: he or she asks me or us) (j:hong/dongh) (r:zd:21876/zd:21869) (q:draft)
hongdot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ask me/ask us) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <dot>, ask, written as one word: someone asks me or us, used before <leh> and <uhteh>, when or if) (j:hong/dot) (r:zd:22707) (q:draft)
honggeel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:plan/arrange) (d:<hong> and <geel> written as one word: plan or arrange something, toward the speaker or for us) (j:hong/geel) (r:zd:12325/zd:13285) (q:draft)
honggelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:write) (d:<hong> and <gelh>, write, written as one word: write to or for the speaker or the reader) (j:hong/gelh) (r:zd:22203/zd:17651) (q:draft)
honggen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:tell/say to) (d:<hong> and <gen> written as one word: tell or say something to the speaker or to us; in a request, tell me) (j:hong/gen) (r:zd:23191/zd:16924/zd:12564) (q:draft)
honggenkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:tell/speak out/declare) (d:<hong> and <genkhia>, speak out, written as one word: speak out or make known to us) (j:hong/genkhia) (r:zd:11204) (q:draft)
honggenna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:what was told to us/statement) (d:<hong> and <genna> written as one word: what someone told the writer; {ama honggenna ah} is in what he told us) (j:hong/genna) (r:zd:11420/zd:11204) (q:draft)
hongguan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:give us/put into/bestow) (d:<hong> and <guan> written as one word: give or put something into us or me, as strength, fear or a wife) (j:hong/guan) (r:zd:19464/zd:20503) (q:draft)
hongguat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:lay on us/provide us with/give us) (d:<hong> and <guat> written as one word: put or lay something on us, or provide us with it) (j:hong/guat) (r:zd:20640/zd:24153) (q:draft, low confidence)
honggum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:side with/favour/save) (d:<hong> and <gum> written as one word: take the side of us or you, or save us) (j:hong/gum) (r:zd:24220) (q:draft, low confidence)
honghal = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:skip over/separate) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <hal>, leave a gap, written as one word: pass over or skip me or us, or lie between and separate us) (j:hong/hal) (r:zd:8668/zd:17428) (q:draft, low confidence)
honghawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/travel) (w:come to visit/visit) (d:<hong> and <hawh>, visit, written as one word: come to see the speaker or the place spoken of) (j:hong/hawh) (r:zd:18071/zd:11401) (q:draft)
honghawhding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/travel) (w:will come to visit/to come and visit) (d:<hong> and <hawhding> written as one word: will come to visit the place or people spoken of) (j:hong/hawhding) (r:zd:13110) (q:draft)
honghawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:share) (d:<hong> and <hawm>, share, written as one word, mostly before <sawn>: share something on with the reader or hearer) (j:hong/hawm) (r:zd:16897/zd:12093) (q:draft)
honghilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:teach us/show us/tell us) (d:<hong> and <hilh> written as one word: teach, show or tell something to the speaker or to us) (j:hong/hilh) (r:zd:22644/zd:25275/zd:21869) (q:draft)
honghopih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:speak to us/speak to me/talk to) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <hopih>, speak to, written as one word: speak to me or to us) (j:hong/hopih) (r:zd:12196/zd:12214) (q:draft)
honghuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:help me/help us/help you) (d:<hong>, the marker of an action toward the speaker or the one spoken to, and <huh>, help, written as one word; {honghuh un} is the cry help us) (j:hong/huh) (r:zd:15243/zd:13022/zd:24604) (q:draft)
hongit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/religion) (w:love you/love me/love us) (d:<hong>, marking an action toward the speaker or the one spoken to, and <it>, love, written as one word: loves you, me or us; {hongit ing} is I love you) (j:hong/it) (r:zd:21011/zd:21355/zd:19518) (q:draft)
hongitkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family) (w:not love us/not love me) (d:<hongit>, love us, with the negative <kei>, written as one word) (j:hongit/kei) (r:zd:17854/zd:19396) (q:draft)
hongkah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/social) (w:come to attend/attend) (d:the verb particle <hong> and the verb for attending, written as one word: come to attend, as in {sang hongkah}, come to school) (r:zd:25916/zd:15584) (q:draft)
hongkan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:come and study/look into) (d:<hong> and <kan> written as one word: come and inquire into or research a matter) (j:hong/kan) (r:zd:21369) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongkem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:look after/protect/keep) (d:<hong> and <kem> written as one word: look after or protect us or me) (j:hong/kem) (r:zd:15422/zd:22287/ts:3366) (q:draft)
hongkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/social) (w:see off/escort/send on the way) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, with <kha>, here send off, written as one word: see travellers off, accompany or send them on their way; said also of God bringing someone safely along) (j:hong/kha) (r:zd:13181/zd:11110/zd:13262) (q:draft)
hongkhaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:send to me/send to us) (d:<hong> and <khaak>, send, written as one word: send here, to the speaker; the same spelling is also found for <hong> with <khaak>, shut, close off) (j:hong/khaak) (r:zd:17860) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:send/send here) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <khak>, send, written as one word: send a letter, a picture or money to me or to us) (j:hong/khak) (r:zd:17120/zd:20896) (q:draft)
hongkhak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:block/hold back/hinder) (d:<hong> and <khak>, shut, written as one word: shut in, block or hold back a person) (j:hong/khak) (r:zd:21989/zd:23784) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongkhakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:will send to you/will send here) (d:<hongkhak>, send to the speaker or hearer, and the future marker <ding> written as one word) (j:hongkhak/ding) (r:zd:12336) (q:draft)
hongkhaktan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:hinder/block/hold back) (d:<hong> and <khaktan> written as one word: stand in our way, stop something that concerns us) (j:hong/khaktan) (r:zd:24673) (q:draft)
hongkhan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:grow/increase/rise) (d:<hong> and <khan>, grow, written as one word: grow, rise or increase, as power or pay) (j:hong/khan) (r:zd:24283/zd:23551) (q:draft)
hongkhang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:grow/increase/rise) (d:<hong> and <khang> written as one word: grow, increase, come up) (j:hong/khang) (r:zd:23066/zd:19969) (q:draft)
hongkhangto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:develop/grow/increase) (d:<hong> and <khangto> written as one word: come to develop or progress, of a country; also of a bad thing, grow and increase) (j:hong/khangto) (r:zd:11078/zd:15913) (q:draft)
hongkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (j:honkhat) (r:zd:17164) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongkhawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:stop/come to rest/land) (d:<hong> and <khawl> written as one word: come to a stop or rest here; of an aircraft, land) (j:hong/khawl) (r:zd:11110/zd:17901) (q:draft)
hongkhen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:judge/give the decision) (d:<hong> and <khen>, decide, written as one word; {thu hongkhen ding} in a programme is the one who will judge) (j:hong/khen) (r:zd:23114) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:open/open up/lay open) (d:<hon>, open, with <khia>, out: open a door or a closed thing, and bring a hidden matter into the open) (r:zd:18020/zd:24414) (q:draft)
hongkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:rescue/deliver) (d:<hon>, save, with <khia>, out: bring someone out of danger or death) (r:zd:9434) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongkhoih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:touch/affect/move) (d:<hong> and <khoih> written as one word: touch or harm you, or touch the heart of the speaker) (j:hong/khoih) (r:zd:12112) (q:draft)
hongki = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hong> and the verb prefix <ki> written as one word and apart from the verb that follows: {hongki zasak} is it was reported to us, {hongki phallo} is we are not allowed) (j:hong/ki) (r:zd:15602/zd:20300/zd:15118) (q:draft)
hongkia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:fall/come down/fall down) (d:<hong> and <kia>, fall, written as one word: fall down toward the speaker or the place spoken of, said of snow and of things from the sky, and of a market that crashes) (j:hong/kia) (r:zd:25919/zd:22658) (q:draft)
hongkiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:decrease/go down/diminish) (d:<hong> and <kiam> written as one word: become less) (j:hong/kiam) (r:zd:24283/zd:15941) (q:draft)
hongkibawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:be made/be lodged) (d:<hong> and <kibawl> written as one word: has been made, said in news of a police report or a complaint that has been lodged) (j:hong/kibawl) (r:zd:15884/zd:19958) (q:draft)
hongkici = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be called/be told) (d:<hong> and <kici> written as one word: I am or we are called so, or we are told so) (j:hong/kici) (r:zd:13089/zd:16893) (q:draft)
hongkidawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be careful/take care) (d:<hong> and <kidawm>, be careful, written as one word: a request to those addressed to be careful about something) (j:hong/kidawm) (r:zd:14606/zd:15283) (q:draft)
hongkigen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be told/be said) (d:<hong> and <kigen> written as one word: be told or said, toward the speaker or hearer) (j:hong/kigen) (r:zd:21035/zd:23977) (q:draft)
hongkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:reopen/open again) (d:<hong>, here the form of <hon>, open, with <kik>, again, written as one word: open again a road, an office or a place that was closed; {ki hongkik} is be reopened) (j:hon/kik) (r:zd:11936/zd:17622/zd:25589) (q:draft)
hongkikhel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:change/come to change) (d:<hong> and <kikhel> written as one word: come to be different, change) (j:hong/kikhel) (r:zd:13314/zd:14587) (q:draft)
hongkilaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:change/be changed) (d:<hong> and <kilaih> written as one word: something comes to be changed, becomes different) (j:hong/kilaih) (r:zd:14587/zd:15274) (q:draft)
hongkilang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:appear/become apparent/show itself) (d:<hong> and <kilang> written as one word: appear to us, come into view) (j:hong/kilang) (r:zd:12196/zd:25917) (q:draft)
hongkipan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:begin/start) (d:<hong> and <kipan> written as one word: something begins, or someone begins to do something) (j:hong/kipan) (r:zd:15775/zd:16257) (q:draft)
hongkipankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:begin/start out/set out from) (d:<hong> and <kipankhia> written as one word: start out or begin from a place, a time or a cause) (j:hong/kipankhia) (r:zd:10768/zd:12472) (q:draft)
hongkipat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:begin/start/come into being) (d:<hong> and <kipat> written as one word: begin, start, said of something that comes into being or into force) (j:hong/kipat) (r:zd:15184/zd:11407) (q:draft)
hongkipia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be given to us/be given to me) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <kipia>, be given, written as one word: be given to me, to us or to you) (j:hong/kipia) (r:zd:12674/zd:16349/zd:14885) (q:draft)
hongkipua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/work) (w:be brought in/be carried here) (d:<hong> and <kipua> written as one word: be carried or transported to this place, be brought into the country) (j:hong/kipua) (r:zd:12140/zd:11433) (q:draft)
hongkipuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be brought/be sent/be taken) (d:<hong> and <kipuak> written as one word: be carried or sent to the place spoken of, as the injured to a hospital) (j:hong/kipuak) (r:zd:14697/zd:16045/zd:17538) (q:draft)
hongkisam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:be called/receive a call) (d:<hong> toward the speaker and <kisam> be called, written as one word: a call came in, we were called or summoned) (j:hong/kisam) (r:zd:17432/zd:13213/zd:12515) (q:draft)
hongkisawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be told to/be sent/be ordered) (d:<hong> and <kisawl> written as one word: I was or we were sent or told to do something) (j:hong/kisawl) (r:zd:14652/zd:20162) (q:draft)
hongkizom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:keep coming/follow one after another/continue) (d:<hong> and <kizom> written as one word: things of one kind keep happening, one after another) (j:hong/kizom) (r:zd:13009/zd:11805) (q:draft)
hongko = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:express to/voice to) (d:<hong> and <ko.2> written as one word: say out to the person addressed; {lungdam hongko} is express thanks to you. In other sentences the same spelling stands for call on or scold) (j:hong/ko) (r:zd:19137) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongkoih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:put/place/leave) (d:<hong> and <koih> written as one word: put, place or leave us or me somewhere or in some state) (j:hong/koih) (r:zd:15941/zd:13268) (q:draft)
Hongkong = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city/land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Hong Kong) (d:city and territory on the south coast of China) (r:zd:17546/zd:10919) (q:draft)
hongkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become necessary/be needed) (d:<hong> and <kul> written as one word, after a verb or verbal noun: it becomes necessary to) (j:hong/kul) (r:zd:16788/zd:23590) (q:draft)
hongkup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:discuss with you/discuss with us) (d:<hong>, toward the hearer or speaker, and <kup>, discuss, written as one word; {hongkup pih nuam ing} is I want to discuss it with you) (j:hong/kup) (r:zd:24289/zd:21369) (q:draft)
hongla = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take/take up) (d:<hong> written as one word with <la>, take, the base form of <lak>: take, said of something that comes toward the speaker or the matter in hand; {pan hongla} is take part and {mun hongla} take a place) (j:hong/la) (r:zd:11228/zd:23992/zd:25616) (q:draft)
honglaang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/health) (w:become widespread/spread/be prevalent) (d:<hong> and <laang> written as one word: come to be found everywhere, said of a disease or a practice) (j:hong/laang) (r:zd:23937/zd:15274) (q:draft)
honglaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:change/replace) (d:<hong> and <laih> written as one word: change or replace something, said of what affects or is done toward the speaker) (j:hong/laih) (r:zd:19427/zd:20725) (q:draft, low confidence)
honglak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:show/point out/reveal) (d:<hong> and <lak>, show, written as one word: shows to us or to you; {lam honglak} is show the way) (j:hong/lak) (r:zd:23554/zd:23843/zd:17120) (q:draft)
honglaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:take away from/seize/capture) (d:<hong> and <laksak> written as one word: come and take something away from someone, or take it from us) (j:hong/laksak) (r:zd:22159) (q:draft, low confidence)
honglei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:buy/come and buy) (d:the verb prefix <hong> and <lei>, buy, written as one word: come and buy, buy) (j:hong/lei) (r:zd:24502) (q:draft)
honglen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:take hold of/hold) (d:<hong> and <len>, hold, written as one word: {nakhut uh honglen in} is taking you by the hand; another article has it after reported speech where the meaning is not clear) (j:hong/len) (r:zd:24696) (q:draft, low confidence)
honglengkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:fly out/take off) (d:<hong> with {leng khia}, fly out, written as one word: fly out from a place, said of an aircraft or a bird, or of a thing flung through the air) (j:hong/lengkhia) (r:zd:11982/zd:16194) (q:draft)
hongluang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/religion) (w:flow out/flow down) (d:<hong> and <luang>, flow, written as one word: flow out or down towards the speaker, said of water and of blessing) (j:hong/luang) (r:zd:22589/zd:19521) (q:draft)
honglut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come in/enter/arrive in) (d:<hong> and <lut> written as one word: enter toward the speaker or the place spoken of) (j:hong/lut) (r:zd:16617/zd:12794/zd:15084) (q:draft)
honglutphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:come in/enter/come across into) (d:<hong> and <lutphei> written as one word: come in across to where the speaker or the scene is) (j:hong/lutphei) (r:zd:15475/zd:19609) (q:draft)
honglutsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:try to come in/attempt to enter) (d:<hong> and <lutsawm>, try to enter, written as one word: try or plan to get into this place or country) (j:hong/lutsawm) (r:zd:13278/zd:15188) (q:draft)
hongmakaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:lead us/guide us) (d:<hong> and <makaih> written as one word: lead us, the one who leads us) (j:hong/makaih) (r:zd:14765/zd:24604) (q:draft)
hongman = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:arrest me/catch us/seize me) (d:<hong> and <man>, catch, written as one word: catch, hold or arrest the speaker or the speaker's group) (j:hong/man) (r:zd:15724/zd:15608) (q:draft)
hongmasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:open first/be the first opened) (d:<hong>, here the verb open, and <masa>, first, written as one word: open or switch on first; {aki hongmasa} is the one opened first) (j:hong/masa) (r:zd:19829/zd:22129) (q:draft)
hongmat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:arrest/catch) (d:<hong> and <mat> written as one word: arrest or catch, said of what is done to the speaker or hearer, or what comes about) (j:hong/mat) (r:zd:17304/zd:14790) (q:draft)
hongmu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:see us/see me/look upon) (d:<hong> and <mu> written as one word: see, with the action directed toward the speaker, see us or me; {hongmu khia} is find out) (j:hong/mu) (r:zd:14709/zd:15362) (q:draft)
hongmuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:come to meet/welcome) (d:<hong> and <muak> written as one word: come out to meet or welcome the speaker or those with the speaker) (j:hong/muak) (r:zd:11110) (q:draft)
hongmukei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not see us/not see me) (d:<hongmu>, see us, with the negative <kei>, written as one word: does not see us) (j:hongmu/kei) (r:zd:17930/zd:16365) (q:draft)
hongna = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/social) (d:<hong>, marking an action toward the speaker, and the preverbal particle <na>, written as one word before a verb, mostly in requests: {hongna maisak in} is please forgive me, {hongna telsiam un} is please understand us) (j:hong/na) (r:zd:15651/zd:24545) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongnawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:strike/hit/attack) (d:<hong> with <nawk>, strike against, written as one word: come upon and strike us, said of a storm, a disease or an army) (j:hong/nawk) (r:zd:19088/zd:23771) (q:draft)
hongnawkding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:will strike/will hit) (d:<hongnawk> and <ding> written as one word: will come and strike, said of a storm) (j:hongnawk/ding) (r:zd:11956/zd:15054) (q:draft)
hongnei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have/hold/give) (d:<hong> and <nei> written as one word: have or hold toward the speaker or the public, as a talk, a meeting or a feeling) (j:hong/nei) (r:zd:11447/zd:12196/zd:16508) (q:draft)
hongneih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:hold/have/come to have) (d:<hong> and <neih> written as one word: hold a prayer or a meeting for or with the speaker's side, as in {thungetna hongneih pih}, or come to have something) (j:hong/neih) (r:zd:15622/zd:14587) (q:draft)
hongneihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:hold for us/conduct for us) (d:<hong> and <neihsak> written as one word: hold a prayer or the like on behalf of the speaker and his side) (j:hong/neihsak) (r:zd:20257) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongneisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give/cause to have) (d:<hong> and <neisak> written as one word: make us or you have a thing, such as a value or a desire) (j:hong/neisak) (r:zd:23977/zd:25914) (q:draft)
hongngah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:get/receive/obtain) (d:<hong> and <ngah> written as one word: come to receive or win something, with the action seen as coming toward the speaker or his people) (j:hong/ngah) (r:zd:15874/zd:8668) (q:draft)
hongngahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:obtain/win/come to hold) (d:<hong> and <ngahkhiat> written as one word: come to obtain or win a thing, such as an office) (j:hong/ngahkhiat) (r:zd:19801) (q:draft)
hongngai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:miss/long for) (d:<hong> and <ngai>, miss, written as one word: miss or long for a person or a place) (j:hong/ngai) (r:zd:15243/zd:26495) (q:draft)
hongngak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wait for/await) (d:<hong> and <ngak> written as one word: wait for you or for us) (j:hong/ngak) (r:zd:19435) (q:draft)
hongngen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:ask for/request) (d:<hong> and <ngen> written as one word: ask for something, toward the speaker or as a plain statement; {thu hongngen} is pray) (j:hong/ngen) (r:zd:17426/zd:12801) (q:draft)
hongnget = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:ask for/request) (d:<hong> and <nget> written as one word: ask us, or come and ask, for something) (j:hong/nget) (r:zd:16617/zd:11652) (q:draft)
hongnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:become glad/become pleasant) (d:the verb prefix <hong> and <nuam>, glad or pleasant, written as one word: become pleasant; {lung hongnuam} is the heart becomes glad) (j:hong/nuam) (r:zd:25909/zd:22171) (q:draft)
hongnusia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:pass away/leave us) (d:<hong> and <nusia> written as one word: has left us, the usual wording of a death notice; {in hongnusia} after a name is has passed away) (j:hong/nusia) (r:zd:17838/zd:12557) (q:draft)
hongnusiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:leave us/pass away) (d:<hong> and <nusiat>, leave, written as one word: left me or us, and of a death, passed away from us) (j:hong/nusiat) (r:zd:22287) (q:draft)
hongom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:come to be/arise/appear/be present) (d:<hong> and <om> written as one word: come into being, arise, come to be there; of people, come and be present) (j:hong/om) (r:zd:15941/zd:19427/zd:14579) (q:draft)
hongpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (j:honpah) (r:zd:21843/zd:16817) (q:draft)
hongpai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <pai>, go, written as one word: come, come here) (j:hong/pai) (r:zd:17325/zd:11953/zd:14899) (q:draft)
hongpaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:will come) (d:<hong>, <pai>, come, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will come, the one who is to come) (j:hong/pai/ding) (r:zd:14954/zd:20289/zd:22416) (q:draft)
hongpaikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:come out/come from/set out) (d:<hong> and <paikhia> written as one word: come out from a place towards here, set out and come) (j:hong/paikhia) (r:zd:15163/zd:14895/zd:14899) (q:draft)
hongpaiphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:come over/come walking across) (d:<hong> and <paiphei> written as one word: come across or along toward the place spoken of) (j:hong/paiphei) (r:zd:20037) (q:draft)
hongpaisuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:come down) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <paisuk>, go down, written as one word: come down or come along down) (j:hong/paisuk) (r:zd:14507/zd:21369) (q:draft)
hongpha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:reach/amount to/come to) (d:<hong> and <pha> written as one word, with <pha> in the sense of reach: come to a number or an amount, or come as far as) (j:hong/pha) (r:zd:19661/zd:19322) (q:draft)
hongphak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:reach/come as far as) (d:<hong> and <phak> written as one word: reach a number of days, or come as far as a place) (j:hong/phak) (r:zd:20831/zd:13285) (q:draft)
hongphal = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:permit/allow/let) (d:<hong> and <phal> written as one word: allow me or us, give us permission) (j:hong/phal) (r:zd:20363/zd:14792) (q:draft)
hongphallo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:not allow/refuse permission) (d:<hong> and <phallo> written as one word: they do not allow, did not permit) (j:hong/phallo) (r:zd:12005/zd:11057) (q:draft)
hongphawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:remember us/remember me/remind) (d:<hong> and <phawk> written as one word: remember me or us, as in a request for prayer; with <sak>, make us remember, remind us) (j:hong/phawk) (r:zd:15805/zd:12378) (q:draft)
hongphawksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:remind/make aware) (d:<hong> and <phawksak> written as one word: it reminds us, makes us aware) (j:hong/phawksak) (r:zd:16961/zd:13026) (q:draft)
hongphukha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:run into/crash into/hit) (d:<hong> and <phukha> written as one word: of a vehicle, come and strike against someone or something) (j:hong/phukha) (r:zd:15667/zd:14899) (q:draft)
hongpia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:give us/give me/grant) (d:<hong> and <pia> written as one word: give to the speaker or to the people addressed, give us, give you; common in blessings, as in <thupha hongpia>, bless us) (j:hong/pia) (r:zd:17022/zd:21085/zd:20035) (q:draft)
hongpiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will give us/will give you) (d:<hongpia>, give to the speaker or hearer, and <ding>, will, written as one word) (j:hongpia/ding) (r:zd:11162/zd:22376) (q:draft)
hongpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:give/gave/given) (d:<hong> and <piak> written as one word: give to the speaker or to us; the form used before a noun, as in {Pasian hongpiak thupha}, the blessing God has given us) (j:hong/piak) (r:zd:19593/zd:16498/zd:11508) (q:draft)
hongpiaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (w:grant/give to us/bestow) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <piaksak> written as one word: give or grant to us or to one of ours; common in blessings, as in {thupha hongpiaksak}) (j:hong/piaksak) (r:zd:11011/zd:23035/zd:13066) (q:draft)
hongpian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:come into being/arise/come about) (d:<hong> and <pian> written as one word: come into existence, arise or happen) (j:hong/pian) (r:zd:24657/zd:15695/zd:22293) (q:draft)
hongpiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen/come about/arise) (d:<hong> and <piang> written as one word: come into being, happen or appear among those spoken of; {hongpiang khia} is come forth) (j:hong/piang) (r:zd:19683/zd:21876/zd:23860) (q:draft)
hongpiangdiam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:will it happen/what will happen) (d:<hongpiang> and the question word <diam.1> written as one word: will it happen; {bangthu hongpiangdiam} is what will happen) (j:hongpiang/diam) (r:zd:15294/zd:19614) (q:draft)
hongpiangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:come about/arise/originate) (d:<hong> and <piangkhia> written as one word: come into being, arise out of something) (j:hong/piangkhia) (r:zd:11972/zd:13309) (q:draft)
hongpiangsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:bring about/cause/create) (d:<hong> and <piangsak> written as one word: make a thing come into being among those spoken of, bring it about; of God, create us) (j:hong/piangsak) (r:zd:15274/zd:20888) (q:draft)
hongpo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:sprout/grow/come up) (d:<hong> and <po> written as one word: of a seed, plant or new growth, come up and grow) (j:hong/po) (r:zd:16194/zd:21837) (q:draft)
hongpua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:carry here/bring/carry) (d:<hong> and <pua> written as one word: carry or bring something toward the speaker, or carry the speaker) (j:hong/pua) (r:zd:23797/zd:17465) (q:draft)
hongpuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:bring here/deliver to us/send here) (d:<hong> and <puak> written as one word: bring or send something or someone to the speaker or to the place spoken of) (j:hong/puak) (r:zd:16073/zd:13078/zd:16455) (q:draft)
hongsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:consider/regard as/find) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker or hearer, and <sa>, here feel or consider, written as one word after a describing word: people find me, us or you so, as in {lamdang hongsa}, be surprised at us) (j:hong/sa) (r:zd:14606/zd:16893) (q:draft)
hongsak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:regard as/consider/find) (d:not opening: the particle <hong>, toward the speaker, written together with <sak>, deem, after a word of quality such as <pil> or <lamdang>: regard me or us as being so) (r:zd:23706/zd:23797) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongsam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:call/invite) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <sam>, call, written as one word: call or invite me or us; also call us by a name) (j:hong/sam) (r:zd:22350/zd:24029) (q:draft)
hongsang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:accept/receive/admit) (d:<hong> and <saang>, accept, written as one word with a short vowel: accept or admit us, as a body admits a member) (j:hong/saang) (r:zd:21161) (q:draft)
hongsang = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:rise/go up) (d:<hong> and <sang>, high, written as one word: become high, rise) (j:hong/sang) (r:zd:25914) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongsap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:call/summon/invite) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <sap>, the form of <sam>, call, written as one word: call or summon me, us or you; of God, call a person to his work) (s:hongsam) (j:hong/sap) (r:zd:25572/zd:17841) (q:draft)
hongsapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:calling/call to us) (d:<hong> and <sapna> written as one word: the call made to us or to you, said of the call of God or Jesus) (j:hong/sapna) (r:zd:19302/zd:23148) (q:draft)
hongsawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:send/command) (d:<hong> and <sawl> written as one word: send here or send to us, and tell us to do something) (j:hong/sawl) (r:zd:19523/zd:25225/zd:17478) (q:draft)
hongsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:intend/plan/set out to) (d:<hong> and <sawm>, intend, written as one word after a verb with <ding>: set about doing, now intend to do) (j:hong/sawm) (r:zd:25916) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongsawm = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:try to open) (d:a verb meaning open, spelled like the particle <hong>, with <sawm>, intend or try, written as one word: try to open a door) (r:zd:12693) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongseem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:blow) (d:<hong> and <seem> written as one word: of wind, blow this way; the same spelling is also written for {hong sem}, come and serve) (j:hong/seem) (r:zd:11110) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongsem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:work/do/come to work) (d:<hong> and <sem> written as one word: do work toward or for the speaker or the person spoken to, set to work) (j:hong/sem) (r:zd:21340/zd:20871/zd:10951) (q:draft)
hongsep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:take office/serve as/come to do) (d:<hong> and <sep> written as one word: come to do a work or hold a post, as in {President hongsep ciangin}, when he became President) (j:hong/sep) (r:zd:20850/zd:19801) (q:draft)
hongsiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:enable/grant/create) (d:<hong> and <siam> written as one word, said of God: enable or grant us to do something, as in the blessing {hongsiam tahen}, may he enable; beside <hongbawl> also made us, created us) (j:hong/siam) (r:zd:14790/zd:17264) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongsik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:provide for us/supply) (d:<hong> and <sikh>, provide, written as one word and without the final h: provide what the speaker or his group needs) (j:hong/sikh) (r:zd:25572/zd:10973) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongsim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:read) (d:<hong> and <sim> written as one word: read, with the action directed toward the speaker or the scene; with <sim> in its other meaning it is also come and attack) (j:hong/sim) (r:zd:10672/zd:12801) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongsu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:touch/affect) (d:<hong> and <su>, touch, written as one word: touch or affect the speaker or his group, usually with <kha>, as in {lungsim hongsu kha}, touch the heart) (j:hong/su) (r:zd:17448/zd:15274) (q:draft)
hongsuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become/turn into/come out/bring out) (d:<hong> and <suah> written as one word: come to be or become something, or come out, appear; with an object, bring out or produce) (j:hong/suah) (r:zd:8667/zd:23848) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become/turn out/come to be) (d:<hong> and <suak> written as one word: become or come to be, said of what comes about for the speaker or the people spoken of, also arise or come out; with <sak>, cause to become) (j:hong/suak) (r:zd:21837/zd:12196/zd:24016) (q:draft)
hongsuakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:come out/emerge/appear) (d:<hong> and <suakkhia>, come out, written as one word: come out or appear toward the one who looks on) (j:hong/suakkhia) (r:zd:11371/zd:17741) (q:draft)
hongsuakta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:has become/has come to be) (d:<hongsuak>, become, and <ta>, the marker of a change now reached, written as one word: has now become) (j:hongsuak/ta) (r:zd:14720/zd:12244) (q:draft)
hongsukha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:touch/move/affect) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <sukha>, touch, written as one word: touch or affect us; with <lungsim> or <lungtang>, heart, move one deeply) (j:hong/sukha) (r:zd:23797/zd:11410) (q:draft)
hongsut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:seize from us/plunder/rob) (d:<hong> and <sut>, take by force, written as one word: take from us or from me by force, plunder what is ours) (j:hong/sut) (r:zd:20200) (q:draft)
hongta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:open/be opened) (d:<hong> in the sense of open, with <ta>, now, written as one word: now open; {ki hongta} is has now been opened) (j:hong/ta) (r:zd:24947/zd:24390) (q:draft)
hongtai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come running/flee here/run to) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <tai>, run or flee, written as one word: come running, or flee to this place) (j:hong/tai) (r:zd:12481/zd:13171) (q:draft)
hongtam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:become many/increase/grow in number) (d:<hong> and <tam>, many, written as one word: become many or more, increase) (j:hong/tam) (r:zd:20531/zd:11510/zd:12051) (q:draft)
hongtan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:ransom me/redeem us/bail out) (d:<hong>, towards the speaker, and <tan>, redeem, written as one word: pay to get me or us released) (j:hong/tan) (r:zd:19320) (q:draft)
hongtan = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature/religion) (w:shine on us/dawn) (d:<hong>, towards the speaker, with <tan>, here shine, which the lexicon writes <taang>: light shines on us or breaks) (j:hong/tan) (r:zd:10793/zd:20670) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongtel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:understand/come to understand) (d:<hong> and <tel> written as one word: understand, said toward the speaker or the group spoken of, as in understand me or understand us) (j:hong/tel) (r:zd:23797/zd:23843) (q:draft)
hongtelsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:make us understand/show us clearly) (d:the verb particle <hong>, towards the speaker, and <telsak>, make understand, written as one word) (j:hong/telsak) (r:zd:23843/zd:19614) (q:draft)
hongthak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:open newly/be newly opened) (d:the verb for open, compare <hon>, with <thak>, new, written as one word: after <ki>, be newly opened, said of a restaurant or hotel) (r:zd:16817) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:know/come to know) (d:<hong> and <thei> written as one word: know or come to know, said toward the speaker or of something learned; {nang pen hongthei lo} is they do not know you) (j:hong/thei) (r:zd:19983/zd:24502) (q:draft)
hongthei = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:can be opened/be able to open) (d:<hong>, here open, a form of <hon>, with <thei>, able: can open or can be opened, said of a lock, a door or a safe) (j:hong/thei) (r:zd:22862/zd:19754) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongtho = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:rise/arise/get up) (d:<hong> and <tho> written as one word: rise, get up; with <kik>, rise again; of a war, break out) (j:hong/tho) (r:zd:18920/zd:21869) (q:draft)
hongthuum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:beg/plead/apologise) (d:<hong> and <thuum>, plead, written as one word: beg or plead with someone; {hongthuum in} is please, I beg you) (j:hong/thuum) (r:zd:17994) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongtuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:cover/enfold) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker or the one addressed, and <tuam>, cover or wrap, written as one word, mostly in blessings: may the Lord cover you or us with his blessing) (j:hong/tuam) (r:zd:16488/zd:11224) (q:draft)
hongtum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:sound at/honk at) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <tum>, sound, written as one word: sound a horn at someone) (j:hong/tum) (r:zd:18303) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongtum = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:hit/strike) (d:<hong> with a verb written like <tum>, sound, but meaning strike with the hand or fist: hit the speaker or the person spoken of) (j:hong/tum) (r:zd:11592) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongtun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:arrive/come/reach) (d:<hong> and <tun> written as one word: arrive here or come to the people spoken of, said of persons, times and events; the form used before <ding>, <ciangin>, <ma> and other endings) (j:hong/tun) (r:zd:22479/zd:24955/zd:23943) (q:draft)
hongtung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:arrive/come/reach here) (d:<hong> and <tung> written as one word: arrive here, come to where the speaker is; also of a feeling or a blessing that comes upon someone) (j:hong/tung) (r:zd:21389/zd:15103/zd:12168) (q:draft)
hongtungding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (w:will come/coming/upcoming) (d:<hong>, <tung> and <ding.1> written as one word: will arrive; before a date or an event, the coming or next one) (j:hong/tung/ding) (r:zd:21334/zd:22377/zd:11209) (q:draft)
hongtungpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:arrive at once/come right away) (d:<hongtung> and <pah> written as one word: arrive here immediately or soon after) (j:hongtung/pah) (r:zd:15216/zd:12304) (q:draft)
hongtungsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/social) (w:bring here/put up/cause to arrive) (d:<hong> and <tungsak>, make arrive or lodge, written as one word: bring us to a place, or of a host put us up) (j:hong/tungsak) (r:zd:15941/zd:22644) (q:draft)
hongtungta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:has arrived/has come) (d:<hong> and <tungta> written as one word: has now arrived here, of a person, a thing or a time) (j:hong/tungta) (r:zd:14931/zd:12093) (q:draft)
hongvaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:feed us/treat to a meal/provide food) (d:<hong> and <vaak>, feed, written as one word: feed or give a meal to us or to you; the same spelling is also found for <vaak>, shine) (j:hong/vaak) (r:zd:24220/zd:14579) (q:draft)
hongvak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:come visiting/come around) (d:<hong>, towards the speaker, and <vak>, go about, written as one word: come here on a visit, come roaming this way) (j:hong/vak) (r:zd:16032/zd:19400) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongveng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:cease/subside/pass) (d:<hong> and <veng>, cease, written as one word: of a disease or a trouble, come to an end) (j:hong/veng) (r:zd:24452/zd:14833) (q:draft)
hongveng = (i:2) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:guard us/protect us) (d:<hong>, here toward us, and <veng>, here guard or watch over, written as one word: guards us, protects us) (j:hong/veng) (r:zd:24123) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongzaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:photograph/film/record) (d:<hong> and <zaih> written as one word: take a picture or record a video, with the action directed toward the speaker or the scene) (j:hong/zaih) (r:zd:18069/zd:16580) (q:draft)
hongzang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:use) (d:<hong> and <zang>, use, written as one word: use towards the speaker or here; in blessings, may the Lord use someone) (j:hong/zang) (r:zd:11587/zd:19455) (q:draft)
hongzangh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:use) (d:<hong> and <zangh>, use, written as one word: use a thing or a word toward the speaker or those spoken of) (j:hong/zangh) (r:zd:13077) (q:draft, low confidence)
hongzasak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:inform us/let us know/report to) (d:<hong>, towards the speaker, and <zasak>, inform, written as one word: let us or me know, report to us; {hongzasak un} is please inform us) (j:hong/zasak) (r:zd:21328/zd:13020/zd:21248) (q:draft)
hongzat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:use/begin to use) (d:<hong> and <zat>, use, written as one word: use me or us, or come to be used) (j:hong/zat) (r:zd:10973/zd:15397) (q:draft)
hongzin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:visit/come on a visit) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker, and <zin>, travel, written as one word: come here on a journey or visit) (j:hong/zin) (r:zd:11401/zd:16488/zd:12919) (q:draft)
hongzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:win/overcome/complete) (d:<hong> and <zo> written as one word: win, get the better of someone, or finish a course of study) (j:hong/zo) (r:zd:22818/zd:17409) (q:draft)
hongzu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:rain/come down) (d:<hong> and <zu>, of rain, fall, written as one word; with <guah>, rain, before it, as {guah hongzu}, the rain comes down) (j:hong/zu) (r:zd:19749/zd:25068) (q:draft)
hongzui = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:follow/come along with) (d:<hong>, toward the speaker or us, and <zui>, follow, written as one word: follow me or us, come after) (j:hong/zui) (r:zd:20997/zd:24593) (q:draft)
honkhat = (i:2) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:some/a number of/several) (d:after a noun, of things as well as people: an unstated number or amount, as in {sum honkhat}, some money; no group or herd is meant) (s:pawlkhat) (r:zd:19754/ts:5913/zd:22464) (q:draft)
honkhatin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:a group of) (d:<honkhat> and <in> written as one word, after a noun: a group of them, as the ones who do the action) (j:honkhat/in) (r:zd:17974/zd:15777/zd:11265) (q:draft)
honkhatmah = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:some/quite a few) (d:<honkhat>, some, with the emphatic <mah>, written as one word: a number of them indeed, quite a few) (j:honkhat/mah) (r:zd:12105/zd:19470) (q:draft)
honkhattawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:with a number of/with a quantity of) (d:<honkhat>, a group or lot, and <tawh>, with, written as one word after a noun: together with a number or quantity of the thing named) (j:honkhat/tawh) (r:zd:17069/zd:16729) (q:draft)
honkhatte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:some people/certain ones) (d:<honkhat>, some, with the plural <te>: some of the people or things spoken of) (b:honkhat) (j:honkhat/te) (r:zd:15382) (q:draft)
honkhatzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:a number also/some as well) (d:<honkhat> and <zong> written as one word, after a noun: a number of them also, a quantity of it as well) (j:honkhat/zong) (r:zd:19318/zd:19289) (q:draft)
honkhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:to rescue/to save) (d:<honkhia>, rescue, and <ding> written as one word: in order to rescue, to get someone out) (j:honkhia/ding) (r:zd:16410/zd:14888) (q:draft)
honkhialo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not rescue/not save) (d:<honkhia>, rescue, and <lo>, not, written as one word: did not rescue; with a following <hikeileh> it means had they not rescued him) (j:honkhia/lo) (r:zd:15385/zd:11927) (q:draft)
honkhiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:to open/will open) (d:<honkhiat>, open, and <ding> written as one word: to open a shop, a safe or a door) (j:honkhiat/ding) (r:zd:19754) (q:draft)
honkhiatding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:to rescue/to get out) (d:<honkhiat>, rescue, and <ding> written as one word: to rescue or free someone who is trapped) (j:honkhiat/ding) (r:zd:17281) (q:draft)
honkhiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:can rescue/be able to save) (d:<honkhia>, rescue, and <thei>, be able, written as one word; with <ki> before it, could be rescued) (j:honkhia/thei) (r:zd:20387/zd:24276) (q:draft)
honkhiatheita = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can now be rescued/have now been rescued) (d:<honkhiathei> and <ta> written as one word; with <ki> before it, have now been able to be rescued) (j:honkhiathei/ta) (r:zd:20387) (q:draft)
honkhiazolo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be unable to save/cannot rescue) (d:<honkhia>, rescue, and <zolo>, cannot, written as one word: not able to save someone) (j:honkhia/zolo) (r:zd:11461) (q:draft)
honkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:reopen/open again) (d:<hon>, open, and <kik>, again, written as one word) (j:hon/kik) (r:zd:25589/zd:24270) (q:draft)
honloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not open) (d:<hon>, open, and <loh>, not, written as one word; {honloh phamawh} is it must be opened, it cannot stay shut) (j:hon/loh) (r:zd:25068/zd:11326) (q:draft)
honmasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:rescue first/save first) (d:<hon.1>, save, and <masa>, first, written as one word: save this one before the others) (j:hon/masa) (r:zd:13114) (q:draft, low confidence)
honna = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social) (w:opening ceremony/inauguration/launch) (d:the event at which a new house, office, memorial stone or book is formally opened or launched, held with <nei> or <kinei>; {thukong honna} is the opening address of a meeting) (r:zd:24594/zd:19858/zd:22948) (q:draft)
honnuamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/everyday) (w:not want to open/refuse to open) (d:<hon>, open, and <nuamlo>, not want, written as one word) (j:hon/nuamlo) (r:zd:12565/zd:14785) (q:draft)
Honolulu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Honolulu) (d:capital city of the state of <Hawaii> in the United States) (r:zd:14559/zd:17763) (q:draft)
honpawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:opening ceremony/inauguration) (d:<hon>, open, with <pawi>, festival: the ceremony at which a building, a school, a shop or an event is opened) (r:zd:15617/zd:14897/zd:12048) (q:draft)
honpi = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:large quantity/great number/lot) (d:of things, not people or animals: a great amount, mostly as {honpi khat} after the noun, as in news of weapons, ammunition or vehicles that were seized) (r:ts:1957/ts:10733) (q:draft)
honpikhat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:a great many/a large amount of/a mass of) (d:<honpi> and <khat> written as one word, placed after a noun: a great quantity or number of it) (j:honpi/khat) (r:zd:11841/zd:17790) (q:draft)
honsa = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday/it) (w:switched on/turned on/running) (d:of an engine, a machine or a camera: switched on and left running, as in {aset honsa in}, with its engine running; not a door or window standing open) (r:zd:15568/zd:14566/zd:19398) (q:draft)
honsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:try to open/be about to open) (d:<hon>, open, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: set out to open a door, a lid or a show) (j:hon/sawm) (r:zd:19495/zd:12487) (q:draft)
Honshu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel/nature) (w:Honshu) (d:the main island of Japan) (r:zd:20384) (q:draft)
hontheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be able to open) (d:<hon>, open, and <theih>, be able, written as one word, mostly before <nading>: so that a school or a shop can be opened) (j:hon/theih) (r:zd:15686/zd:19648) (q:draft)
honzawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:since opening/after being opened) (d:<hon>, open, and <zawh>, after or since, written as one word; after <aki> it means since it was opened) (j:hon/zawh) (r:zd:11887/zd:11182) (q:draft)
hoong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:open) (d:open a school, an office or the like, start it running; a spelling with a long vowel of the verb also written <hon>, which sets it apart from the particle <hong> standing before it) (r:zd:17163/zd:22586) (q:draft, low confidence)
hopihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:greeting/salutation) (d:words spoken to greet someone) (b:hopih) (q:draft)
Hopin = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Hopin) (d:town on the railway between Mandalay and Myitkyina in Kachin State, northern Myanmar) (r:zd:19719/zd:17428) (q:draft)
hopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:distribution/sharing out/donation) (d:<hop>, share out, with the noun ending <na>: the giving out of a thing to people; {sisan hopna} is blood donation) (s:hawmna) (b:hop) (r:zd:24049/zd:10742) (q:draft, low confidence)
hopsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:share/pass on) (d:<hop>, share out, with <sawn>, onward: pass on to others what one has received or learned, as news or an experience) (j:hop/sawn) (r:zd:25148/zd:15180) (q:draft)
