hunkhat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:once/at one time/for a while) (d:<hun> and <khat> written as one word, a time: {hunkhat lai in} is once, at one time in the past, {hunkhat ciangin} is one day, in time, and {hunkhat sung} is for a while) (j:hun/khat) (r:zd:20071/zd:19006/zd:11251) (q:draft)
hunkhatciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:one day/in time/at some time) (d:<hunkhat> and <ciang> written as one word: at some time to come, sooner or later; set against <hunkhatlai>, at one time in the past) (j:hunkhat/ciang) (r:zd:11251/zd:14679) (q:draft)
hunkhatlai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:once/at one time/formerly) (d:<hun>, time, <khat>, one, and <lai>, the time when, written as one word: at one time in the past; {abeisa hunkhatlai in} is some time ago) (j:hun/khat/lai) (r:zd:13089/zd:13059) (q:draft)
hunkhen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work) (w:part-time) (d:<hun>, time, with <khen>, divide: giving part of the working time to a task, set beside <hunbit>, full-time; one article also uses the word for an age or period in a term for post-modernity) (r:zd:9124) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:rescue/save/get out) (d:bring someone out of danger or out of captivity) (s:honkhia) (r:zd:19565/zd:10719/zd:19295) (q:draft)
hunla = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:take time/spend time) (d:<hun>, time, with <la>, take: take one's time, spend time with someone, or of a thing, take a length of time) (r:zd:24248/zd:12544/zd:25132) (q:draft)
hunlai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:time/period/days/era) (d:<hun> and <lai> written as one word: the time when something was so, the days of a person or a rule; {tua hunlai in} is at that time, and after a name or a clause it means in the time of, at the time when) (j:hun/lai) (r:zd:18200/zd:26097/ts:4569) (q:draft)
hunlaipawl = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:about/around the time of) (d:after a stretch of time or a date: at about that time; {abeisa kum 6 hunlaipawl} is about six years ago; from <hun>, time, <lai>, while, and <pawl>, about) (r:zd:20738/zd:11619/zd:16317) (q:draft)
hunlaipek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:ago/back in the time of) (d:<hun> and <laipek> written as one word, after a length of time or a period: that long ago, as far back as that time; often with <akipan>, since) (j:hun/laipek) (r:zd:15417/zd:19875/zd:16849) (q:draft)
hunlaitak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:moment/very time) (d:<hun>, time, with <laitak>, at the very time: the moment or period at which something happens; {hih hunlaitak in} is at this very time) (j:hun/laitak) (r:zd:25292/zd:21869/zd:21876) (q:draft)
hunlaite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:times/days) (d:<hunlai>, time or period, with the plural <te>: those times, the days when something was so) (b:hunlai) (j:hunlai/te) (r:zd:24036/zd:16404) (q:draft)
hunlap = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:in time/on time/timely) (d:<hun>, time, with <lap>, catch up with: in good time, before it is too late, mostly as {a hunlap in}; {hunlap lo} is not in time) (r:zd:15105/zd:17149/zd:17586) (q:draft)
hunlem = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:opportunity/chance/convenient time) (d:<hun>, time, with <lem>, convenient: a suitable time or chance to do something; {hunlem ngah} is get the opportunity) (s:hunpha/hunhoih) (r:zd:15571/zd:12289/zd:10817) (q:draft)
hunlian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:exact time/very moment) (d:<hun>, time, with <lian>, here exactly, written as one word: the very time or moment at which something happens; {tulaitak hunlian} is this very moment, right now) (j:hun/lian) (r:zd:25924/zd:19109/zd:11532) (q:draft)
hunlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/everyday) (w:untimely/premature/before the time) (d:<hun> and <lo> written as one word: not at the proper time, too early, said above all of an early death) (j:hun/lo) (r:zd:22734/zd:17309) (q:draft)
hunma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:before the time/before) (d:<hun>, time, and <ma>, before, written as one word after a noun or a clock time: before the time of what is named; {phalbi hunma in} is before winter) (j:hun/ma) (r:zd:20747/ts:301/zd:25318) (q:draft)
hunmah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:the very time/a time) (d:<hun> and the emphatic <mah> written as one word: a time for something indeed, the very time) (j:hun/mah) (r:zd:19476) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunman = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time) (w:punctual/on time) (d:<hun> and <man> written as one word: keeping the right time, on time; {hunman takin} is punctually) (j:hun/man) (r:zd:21370/zd:19676) (q:draft)
hunman = (i:2) (t:v) (f:time/religion) (w:the time ends/be over) (d:<hun> with <man>, finish, written as one word: the time of a meeting or service comes to its end, as in {hunman ciangin}, when the time was over) (j:hun/man) (r:zd:20016/zd:11110) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunmanpha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:precious time/golden opportunity) (d:<hun>, time, and <manpha>, precious, written as one word: valuable time, a chance that should not be wasted) (j:hun/manpha) (r:zd:22171/zd:17951) (q:draft)
hunmantak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/health) (w:punctually/at regular times/on time) (d:<hunman>, on time, and <tak> written as one word, followed by <in> or <a>: at the proper time, regularly) (j:hunman/tak) (r:zd:20946/zd:20801) (q:draft)
hunnailo = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time/everyday) (w:it is not yet time/too early) (d:<hun> and <nailo> written as one word: the time has not yet come, mostly for saying or doing something) (j:hun/nailo) (r:zd:11376/zd:17556) (q:draft)
hunnei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time) (w:have time) (d:<hun>, time, and <nei>, have, written as one word: have time; {hunnei lo} is have no time) (j:hun/nei) (r:zd:25919/zd:25924) (q:draft)
hunngah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:free time/leisure) (d:<hun>, time, with <ngah>, get: having time to spare, time off) (j:hun/ngah) (r:zd:20892) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunnuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/time) (w:good time/pleasant time/happy time) (d:<hun>, time, and <nuam>, pleasant, written as one word: an enjoyable time spent with others; {hunnuam zang} is have a good time) (j:hun/nuam) (r:zd:12487/zd:23367/zd:21421) (q:draft)
hunpai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/religion) (w:passing of time/course) (d:<hun>, time, and <pai>, go, written as one word: time going on, as in {hunpai tozel in}, as time went on; {hunpai zia} is the order in which a service proceeds) (j:hun/pai) (r:zd:19679/zd:21703) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:from the time/since) (d:<hun>, time, and <pan>, from, written as one word after a clock time or a period: starting from that time) (j:hun/pan) (r:zd:14836/zd:11866) (q:draft)
hunpawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:about the time/around) (d:<hun> and <pawl> written as one word, placed after a clock time: about that time; {9pm hunpawl in} is at around 9 pm) (j:hun/pawl) (r:zd:15521/zd:15651/zd:18947) (q:draft)
hunpawlin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:at about/at around) (d:<hunpawl>, about the time, and <in>, at, written as one word after a clock time: at around that time) (j:hunpawl/in) (r:zd:11729/zd:15002) (q:draft)
hunpek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:as early as/already at/as long ago as) (d:<hun> and <pek> written as one word, placed after a time: stresses how early or how long ago it was; {5am hunpek akipan} is from as early as 5 am) (j:hun/pek) (r:zd:19609/zd:15920) (q:draft)
hunpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:the time) (d:<hun> and <pen> written as one word: the time, as the topic of the sentence; after a verb it is the time when something happened, and what follows tells when that was) (j:hun/pen) (r:zd:18947/zd:16194) (q:draft)
hunpi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:ceremony/service/programme) (d:a formal gathering or its main session, after the word that names the occasion: {Sunday hunpi} is the Sunday service, {khahkhiatna hunpi} a launch ceremony) (r:zd:20784/zd:14579/ts:4661) (q:draft)
hunpia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:give time/take time/devote time) (d:<hun>, time, with <pia>, give, written as one word: set aside time for a person or a task) (j:hun/pia) (r:zd:25924/zd:23977) (q:draft)
hunpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/social) (w:give time/devote time) (d:<hun>, time, and <piak>, give, written as one word: give time to someone or something, also the time that one gives) (j:hun/piak) (r:zd:25924/zd:22988) (q:draft)
hunsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:let it suffice/consider enough) (d:<hun>, here be enough, with <sak>, consider: take something as enough and stop there; {hunsak phot ni} is let that be enough for now) (j:hun/sak) (r:zd:24375) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunsaupi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:long term/long time) (d:<hun> and <saupi> written as one word: a very long time, the long term; {hunsaupi aa ding} is for the long term) (s:hunsau) (j:hun/saupi) (r:zd:16150/zd:12187) (q:draft)
hunsawt = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:long time/long run) (d:<hun>, time, and <sawt>, long, written as one word: a long time, for long; {hunsawt ah} is in the long run) (s:hunsau) (j:hun/sawt) (r:zd:21417/zd:19327/zd:22742) (q:draft)
hunsawtpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:long time/very long time) (d:<hun>, time, and <sawtpi>, for a long time, written as one word: a long time, the long term; {hunsawtpi ading} is for the long term) (s:hunsawt) (j:hun/sawtpi) (r:zd:19917/zd:25918) (q:draft)
hunsim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:all the time/at every moment/constantly) (d:<hun>, time, with the ending {-sim}, every, as in <nisim>, daily: at every time; often said together with <nisim> and <naisim>, every hour) (r:zd:21340/zd:17070) (q:draft)
hunsungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:during/in the time of) (d:<hunsung> and <ah> written as one word: during the time of what is named before it) (j:hunsung/ah) (r:zd:22652) (q:draft)
hunsungin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:during/within the time/in the period) (d:<hunsung>, span of time, with the marker <in>, written as one word: during the time of something, within a period) (j:hunsung/in) (r:zd:21918/zd:14865/ts:301) (q:draft)
hunsungpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:the period/the duration) (d:<hunsung>, period or length of time, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: as for the time during which something happens) (j:hunsung/pen) (r:zd:16026/zd:17802) (q:draft)
hunsungteng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:throughout the time/during the whole period) (d:<hun> and <sungteng> written as one word: through the whole of a period, all the time that something lasts) (j:hun/sungteng) (r:zd:20488/zd:15592/zd:21588) (q:draft)
huntam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:much time/long time) (d:<hun> and <tam> written as one word: a great deal of time, a long time; {huntam kisam} is need much time) (j:hun/tam) (r:zd:25917/zd:17026) (q:draft)
huntampi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:much time/a long time) (d:<hun>, time, and <tampi>, much, written as one word: a great deal of time) (j:hun/tampi) (r:zd:11326/zd:15811/zd:8375) (q:draft)
huntawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time/social) (w:with the times/according to the time) (d:<hun> time and <tawh> with written as one word: {huntawh kituak} is in keeping with the times, up to date, and {huntawh kizui in} is in step with the times) (j:hun/tawh) (r:zd:21586/zd:24765/zd:20964) (q:draft)
hunteh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:at the time/when) (d:<hun>, time, with <teh>, written as one word: {tu hunteh} is at this time, nowadays, {tua hunteh} at that time, and {bang hunteh} at what time, when) (j:hun/teh) (r:zd:22479/zd:14930/zd:22860) (q:draft)
huntehna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:timer/measure of time/time scale) (d:<hun>, time, and <tehna>, measure, written as one word: a means of measuring time, as in {huntehna nai}, a timer) (j:hun/tehna) (r:zd:16878) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:all the time/the whole time/whole period) (d:<hun>, time, and <teng>, all, written as one word: the whole of a time or period) (j:hun/teng) (r:zd:24227) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunthak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/social) (w:modern times/new era/modern) (d:<hun> and <thak> written as one word: the new age, the present time; before a noun, modern) (j:hun/thak) (r:zd:22504/zd:22046/zd:23198) (q:draft)
huntom = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:short time/short term/brief period) (d:<hun> and <tom> written as one word: a short time; {huntom sung} is within a short time, in the short term) (j:hun/tom) (r:zd:24164/zd:20854) (q:draft)
huntomno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:short time/short while/moment) (d:<hun> and <tomno> written as one word: a short time; {huntomno sungin} is within a short time, quickly) (j:hun/tomno) (r:zd:20854/zd:24276/zd:14852) (q:draft)
huntun = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (d:<hun> and <tun> written as one word: the time comes; {a huntun teh} is when its time comes) (j:hun/tun) (r:zd:25678) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:chairperson/master of ceremonies) (d:<hun> and <uk> written as one word: the one who leads the programme of a meeting or service) (j:hun/uk) (r:zd:16210) (q:draft, low confidence)
hunval = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/work) (w:extra time/overtime/spare time) (d:<hun>, time, and <val>, be left over, written as one word: time beyond the set hours, as extra time in a game, overtime at work, or tuition outside school hours) (j:hun/val) (r:zd:20730/zd:20264) (q:draft)
hunzang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/religion) (w:spend time/use the time) (d:<hun> and <zang> written as one word: spend time; at a meeting or service, take a part of the programme, and also the person who takes it) (j:hun/zang) (r:zd:20572/zd:17055) (q:draft)
hunzat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:use of time/time spent/spending time) (d:<hun>, time, with <zat>, use: the way time is used; {hunzat khop} is spend time together) (j:hun/zat) (r:zd:23453/zd:20958/zd:24963) (q:draft)
hunzatkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:spend time together) (d:<hun>, time, <zat>, use, and <khop>, together, written as one word: spend time together; in funeral notices {anunungpen hunzatkhop ding} is the last time to be together with the one who died) (j:hun/zat/khop) (r:zd:22388/zd:25449) (q:draft)
hunzatkhopding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:time to spend together) (d:<hun>, <zat>, <khop> and <ding> written as one word: the time to be spent together; in death notices {a nunungpen hunzatkhopding} is the last time to be together with the dead, the funeral service) (j:hun/zat/khop/ding) (r:zd:10901/zd:11832) (q:draft)
hunzatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion/time) (w:programme/service/use of time) (d:<hun>, time, with <zatna>, using: the spending of time on something, and so a programme, a session or a service held by a group) (r:zd:20792/zd:24036/zd:20172) (q:draft)
hunzawh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:closing/end of the programme) (d:<hun>, time, and <zawh>, after or finished, written as one word: the close of a meeting or programme, as in {hunzawh thungetna}, the closing prayer) (j:hun/zawh) (r:zd:16040/zd:16173) (q:draft)
hunzui = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/everyday) (w:timely/seasonal/up to date/fashionable) (d:<hun>, time, with <zui>, follow: in keeping with the time or season; {a hunzui in} is in due time, as the times require) (j:hun/zui) (r:zd:24276/zd:23156/zd:25333) (q:draft)
hup = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:attract/draw) (d:after <sik>, iron: of a magnet, draw iron to itself, where the other sense is sucking up a liquid; {sik hup} is also the name of a magnet) (r:zd:19803/zd:17501) (q:draft)
hupcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/media) (w:pull in and hold fast/suck in) (d:<hup>, suck or of a magnet draw, and <cip>, fast, written as one word: draw something or someone in and hold it fast, said of the magnet of an MRI machine) (j:hup/cip) (r:zd:17501) (q:draft, low confidence)
