Indo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics/travel) (w:Indo-/Indian) (d:English combining form for India, used before the name of a second country: {Indo-Burma} and {Indo-Myanmar} are India and Myanmar together, mostly of their border and of the Zomi on both sides) (o:English) (r:zd:15743/ts:4823) (q:draft, low confidence)
Indonesia = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Indonesia) (d:island country in Southeast Asia, south of Malaysia) (r:zd:12026/zd:12161) (q:draft)
Indonesian = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics/media) (w:Indonesian) (d:of Indonesia, the English word placed before a noun; {Indonesian gammi} is a citizen of Indonesia) (o:English) (r:zd:18876/zd:12542) (q:draft)
inei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we have) (d:<i> and <nei> written as one word: we have) (j:i/nei) (r:zd:15396/zd:13076/zd:14765) (q:draft)
ineih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we have/what we have) (d:<i> and <neih> written as one word: we have, or that which we have) (j:i/neih) (r:zd:20979/zd:15396/zd:20999) (q:draft)
infection = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:infection) (d:a disease caused by germs entering the body; mostly inside English names of diseases) (o:English) (r:zd:12623) (q:draft, low confidence)
information = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:information) (d:facts and news about a matter that are told, sent or collected) (o:English) (r:zd:22023/zd:20331/zd:11074) (q:draft)
infrastructure = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:infrastructure) (d:the roads, power, water and other basic works of a town or country) (o:English) (r:zd:22830/zd:14755) (q:draft)
ing ei = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:I do indeed) (d:<ing>, the sentence-final ending of the first person singular, and <ei>, here an exclamation, a longer form of <e>, and not the pronoun we: closes a statement about oneself with feeling or emphasis, in speech and in personal writing) (r:zd:24223/zd:11394/zd:16425) (q:draft, low confidence)
ingah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we get/we receive/we obtain) (d:<i>, we, and <ngah>, get, written as one word: we get, or what we have received) (j:i/ngah) (r:zd:14791/ts:3366/zd:15361) (q:draft)
ingaihsut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we think/we consider) (d:<i>, we, and <ngaihsut>, think, written as one word: we think about, our thinking) (j:i/ngaihsut) (r:zd:24019) (q:draft)
ingaihsutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:our thought/our thinking/our view) (d:<i> and <ngaihsutna> written as one word: our thought, our way of thinking) (j:i/ngaihsutna) (r:zd:24068/zd:16343) (q:draft)
inge = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:I am indeed) (d:<ing> and <e> written as one word at the end of a sentence: the first person ending with a warm or emphatic tone, common in songs) (j:ing/e) (r:zd:16300) (q:draft)
ingei = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ing> and <ei> written as one word at the end of a sentence: I am or I do, said with feeling, as in {dam ingei}, I am well indeed) (j:ing/ei) (r:zd:16442) (q:draft)
ingeina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:our culture/our tradition/our custom) (d:<i>, our, and <ngeina>, custom, written as one word: the culture and customs of the speaker and hearers) (j:i/ngeina) (r:zd:16056/zd:19252) (q:draft)
ingh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (j:ing) (r:zd:20920/zd:25223) (q:draft)
ingimna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:our aim/our purpose/our goal) (d:<i> and <ngimna> written as one word) (j:i/ngimna) (r:zd:14791/zd:24068) (q:draft)
ingin = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the first person ending <ing> and the linking <in> written as one word, at the end of a clause that another clause follows: I do so, and; I do so, but) (j:ing/in) (r:zd:25097/zd:23664) (q:draft)
inh = (i:1) (t:ppm) (f:everyday) (j:in) (r:zd:22803/zd:23383) (q:draft, low confidence)
inkuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/home) (j:innkuan) (r:zd:17838) (q:draft)
inkuanpihte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (j:innkuanpihte) (r:zd:25078/zd:23204) (q:draft)
inlah = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the subject marker <in> and the particle <lah> written as one word: as for, for his part; sets one statement beside another that contrasts with it) (j:in/lah) (r:zd:19223/zd:11058) (q:draft)
inleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:and) (d:the marker <in> after a verb or describing word and <leh>, and, written as one word: joins two descriptions or two actions) (j:in/leh) (r:zd:11949) (q:draft, low confidence)
inmaw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/social) (d:the command ending <in> and the sentence-final <maw>, written as one word after a verb: makes a friendly request, please do, will you) (j:in/maw) (r:zd:16124/zd:12231) (q:draft)
inn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:home/house) (s:innsung/teenna)
inn papi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/home) (w:man of the house/head of the household/householder) (d:<inn>, house, and <papi>, grown man: the man of the house, the husband and father as head of a household) (r:zd:15234/zd:15424) (q:draft, low confidence)
Innbuk = (i:1) (t:name) (c:mountain) (f:travel/nature) (w:Innbuk) (d:name of a mountain in Chin State, said as {Innbuk mual}) (r:zd:23444) (q:draft, low confidence)
innbuluh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/home) (w:break into a house/burgle/rob a house) (d:<inn>, house, and <buluh>, raid, written as one word: break into a house to rob it; {innbuluh te} are the people who do so, burglars) (j:inn/buluh) (r:zd:16739/zd:16926) (q:draft)
innbuluhsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/home) (w:attempt to break into a house/attempt burglary) (d:<innbuluh> and <sawm.2> written as one word: try or set out to break into a house; also the people who try) (j:innbuluh/sawm) (r:zd:18073) (q:draft)
innciah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel/home) (w:go home/return home) (d:<inn>, home, and <ciah>, return, written as one word) (j:inn/ciah) (r:zd:17028/zd:21288) (q:draft)
innciat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/family) (w:each home/every house/one's own home) (d:<inn>, house, and <ciat>, each, written as one word: each one's own home; {amau innciat ah} is each in their own homes) (j:inn/ciat) (r:zd:23901/zd:22214/zd:23776) (q:draft)
inncim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/media) (w:building collapse/house collapse) (d:<inn>, house, with <cim>, collapse, written as one word: the collapse of a building) (j:inn/cim) (r:zd:14679/zd:14969) (q:draft)
inncing = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:caretaker) (d:in {inncing kumpi}, a caretaker government: one that keeps the country for a time as a keeper looks after a house, not a guard of a palace) (r:zd:23476/zd:25263) (q:draft)
inndawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:floor/storey) (d:<inn>, house, with <dawl>, floor: a storey of a building, counted with a number, as in {inndawl 5 na}, the 5th floor) (r:zd:22828/zd:13089/zd:14628) (q:draft)
inndawn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:rooftop/top of a building/upper floor) (d:<inn>, house, with <dawn>, top: the top or a high floor of a tall building; with a number it seems to name that floor) (r:zd:19894/zd:14792) (q:draft)
inndei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:room) (d:a room in a house or other building; {lupna inndei} is a bedroom) (s:dei) (r:11.6.30) (q:draft)
inndeisung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:room/inside of a room) (d:<inndei>, room, and <sung>, inside, written as one word: a room of a house, hotel or building, or the inside of it) (j:inndei/sung) (r:zd:16362/zd:12750/zd:19199) (q:draft)
inndong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:home/travel) (w:as far as the house/all the way home) (d:<inn> and <dong>, until, written as one word: up to the house, right to the home) (j:inn/dong) (r:zd:17416/zd:17325) (q:draft)
inngei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:beside the house/near the house) (d:<inn>, house, and <gei>, side, written as one word: the place beside or near a house) (j:inn/gei) (r:zd:23888/zd:14622) (q:draft)
inngolpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/travel) (w:large building/big building) (d:<inn>, house, and <golpi>, large, written as one word: a large building such as a tower, mall or apartment block) (j:inn/golpi) (r:zd:16952/zd:20488/zd:17311) (q:draft)
inngua = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/home) (w:bamboo by the house) (d:<inn>, house, and <gua>, bamboo, written as one word: the bamboo at home, set against <gamgua>, the bamboo of the forest, in a saying about tending what is far off and leaving what is near) (j:inn/gua) (r:zd:11138) (q:draft, low confidence)
innhik = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature/home) (w:house lizard/gecko/lizard) (d:the small lizard that lives on the walls of houses; from <inn>, house) (r:zd:17371) (q:draft)
innhoih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:good house/fine house) (d:<inn> and <hoih> written as one word: a fine, well-built house) (j:inn/hoih) (r:zd:11438/zd:8668) (q:draft)
innhuang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:compound/yard/premises) (d:the enclosed ground on which a house stands, from <inn>, house, and <huang>, enclosure; {innhuang sung} is inside the compound) (r:zd:17540/zd:25156/zd:19699) (q:draft)
innhuangsung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:house compound/yard/grounds) (d:<inn> and <huangsung> written as one word: the space inside the fence of a house; {innhuangsung ah} is in the compound of the house) (j:inn/huangsung) (r:zd:17568/zd:11133) (q:draft)
innka = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:veranda/open platform/deck) (d:the raised open platform at the front of a traditional Zomi house, where people sit, rest and receive visitors) (r:zd:14804/ts:479/zd:26097) (q:draft)
innkaa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (j:innka) (r:zd:11110/ts:3369) (q:draft)
innkang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:house fire/fire) (d:<inn>, house, with <kang>, burn: the burning of a house or building) (r:zd:13009/zd:16739) (q:draft)
Innkangpi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:politics) (w:White House) (d:<inn>, house, <kang>, white, and <pi>, great: the White House, the residence and office of the President of the United States) (j:inn/kang/pi) (r:zd:16340) (q:draft)
innkhan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:room) (d:a room of a house or building; {innkhan sung} is the inside of the room) (s:dei) (r:zd:23972/zd:24014/zd:23590) (q:draft)
innkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:a house/one house) (d:<inn> and <khat> written as one word: a house, one house) (j:inn/khat) (r:zd:15296/zd:11148/zd:19381) (q:draft)
innkhatah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:home) (w:in a house/at a house) (d:<innkhat>, a house, and <ah>, in or at, written as one word) (j:innkhat/ah) (r:zd:16511/zd:12425) (q:draft)
innkhatkhit = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home/everyday) (w:house after house/from house to house) (d:<innkhat> and <khit> written as one word; in {innkhatkhit innkhat}, after one house another, house by house) (j:innkhat/khit) (r:zd:14545/zd:20401) (q:draft)
innkhum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:roof) (d:the top of a house; {innkhum zang} is the flat roof, {innkhum dawn} the rooftop) (s:khum/innkhumzang/tungkhum) (q:draft)
innkhumtung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:rooftop/roof) (d:<innkhum> and <tung> written as one word: the top of the roof, on the roof) (j:innkhum/tung) (r:zd:12188/zd:14904) (q:draft)
innkicim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/media) (w:building collapse/collapsed building) (d:<inn>, house, and <kicim>, collapse, written as one word: the collapse of a building, or the building that has collapsed) (j:inn/kicim) (r:zd:15296/zd:17645/zd:20488) (q:draft)
innkicipna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/media) (w:building collapse/collapse of a house) (d:<inn>, house, and <kicipna>, collapse, written as one word) (j:inn/kicipna) (r:zd:20488/zd:17256) (q:draft)
innkilamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:building under construction/construction site) (d:<inn>, house, and <kilamna>, being built, written as one word: a building that is being built, or the place where it is built) (j:inn/kilamna) (r:zd:18074/zd:16010) (q:draft)
innkim = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home/social) (w:every house/every household/each home) (d:<inn>, house, with <kim>, every: each house or household of a place, as in {innkim ah}, at every house, {innkim ciat}, each household, and {innkim phial}, almost every house; not the area around one house) (r:zd:22444/zd:21099/zd:20131) (q:draft)
innkisia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/nature) (w:damaged house/collapsed building/ruined house) (d:<inn> and <kisia> written as one word: a house or building that has been damaged or destroyed) (j:inn/kisia) (r:zd:19960/zd:20749) (q:draft)
innkong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:house door/front door/door) (d:<inn>, house, and <kong>, door, written as one word: the door of a house or flat) (j:inn/kong) (r:zd:22932/zd:15019) (q:draft)
