kahdingte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:those who will attend) (d:<kahding>, who is to attend, with the plural <te>: those who are going to attend a school or university) (j:kahding/te) (r:zd:20137) (q:draft)
kaheh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:my anger) (d:<ka> and <heh> written as one word: my anger; {kaheh suak} is I get angry) (j:ka/heh) (r:zd:14910/zd:14883) (q:draft)
kahemkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:remove/take away) (d:<ka> and <hemkhia> written as one word: I or we remove, in reported speech) (j:ka/hemkhia) (r:zd:17538) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kahgen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Kahgen) (d:a Zomi village of the Tedim area in Chin State, named together with <Vongmual> and Thenzang) (r:zd:10860/zd:21182) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I am/we are) (d:<ka> and <hi> written as one word: I am; with <uh>, we are) (j:ka/hi) (r:zd:20911/zd:16506) (q:draft)
kahiam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:am I) (d:<ka> and <hiam> written as one word at the end of a question the speaker asks about himself: am I, should I; {kei kua kahiam} is who am I) (j:ka/hiam) (r:zd:19309/zd:9423) (q:draft)
kahih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I am) (d:<ka> and <hih> written as one word, where it is the form of <hi>, be, used before words such as <manin>, <hang> and <pen>: that I am, my being) (j:ka/hih) (r:zd:24165/zd:23797) (q:draft)
kahih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I do) (d:<ka> and <hih>, do, written as one word: I do, what I do) (j:ka/hih) (r:zd:24370) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahihi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I am) (d:<ka> and <hi> followed by the sentence ending, all written as one word: I am, at the end of a sentence in which the speaker says who or what he is) (j:ka/hi) (r:zd:19472/zd:12980) (q:draft)
kahihlam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:that I am) (d:<ka> and <hihlam> written as one word: the fact that I am, followed by a verb of knowing, noticing or forgetting) (j:ka/hihlam) (r:zd:16833/zd:16803) (q:draft)
kahihman = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because I am/since I am) (d:{ka hih man} written as one word: <ka>, I, with <hih>, the form of <hi>, be, as in <ahih>, and <man>, because, as in <manin>; it closes a clause that gives the reason, often followed by <in>) (j:ka/hih/man) (r:zd:22592/zd:22658/zd:10973) (q:draft)
kahihmanin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because I am/since I am) (d:<ka>, I, with <hih>, the form of <hi>, be, and <manin>, because, written as one word: because I am or was) (j:ka/hih/manin) (r:zd:23797/zd:24059) (q:draft)
kahihmanun = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because we are/since we) (d:<kahih> and <manun> written as one word, placed at the end of a clause: because we are or do so, the speaker and others but not the hearer) (j:kahih/manun) (r:zd:17428/zd:17187) (q:draft)
kahihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:my being/that I am) (d:<ka> and <hihna> written as one word: the fact that I am, or with <uh> that we are, what goes before; {Zomi kahihna} is my being a Zomi) (j:ka/hihna) (r:zd:21326/zd:21090) (q:draft)
kahikei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I am not/we are not) (d:<ka>, <hi>, be, and <kei>, not, written as one word: I am not; with <uh>, we are not) (j:ka/hi/kei) (r:zd:19400/zd:16291) (q:draft)
kahimanin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:because I am/since I am) (d:<kahi>, I am, and <manin>, because, written as one word at the end of a clause: because I am, since I do) (j:kahi/manin) (r:zd:24420) (q:draft)
kahin = (i:3) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:attending/going to) (d:<kah>, attend a school, course, training, party or meeting, with the linking ending {-in} before the next verb) (r:ts:301/zd:15788) (q:draft)
kahizaw = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:we rather are/I rather am) (d:<ka> and <hizaw> written as one word, mostly in reported speech: it is rather that I or we) (j:ka/hizaw) (r:zd:19583) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahkah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:keep going up/keep attending/keep rising) (d:<kah> said twice and written as one word: go on climbing, go on attending school, or of prices go on rising) (b:kah) (r:zd:22584/zd:23489) (q:draft)
kahkah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep weeping/weep and weep) (d:<kah>, the form of <kap>, said twice and written as one word: go on crying) (b:kah) (r:zd:22755/zd:24294) (q:draft)
kahkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/education) (w:attend together/go to together) (d:<kah>, attend a meeting or a school, and <khawm>, together, written as one word: attend it together with others) (j:kah/khawm) (r:zd:13181/zd:25624) (q:draft)
kahkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/politics) (w:attend again/return to/reconvene) (d:<kah>, go up or attend, and <kik>, again, written as one word: attend school again, or of a parliament, sit again) (j:kah/kik) (r:zd:24029/zd:15525) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:be still attending/while attending) (d:<kah> in the sense attend a school, with <lai> in the sense still, while, written as one word: be still at school or college, while attending) (j:kah/lai) (r:zd:12470/zd:23443) (q:draft)
kahleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:if one climbs/when one climbs) (d:<kah>, climb, and <leh>, if or when, written as one word: if or when someone or something climbs or goes up) (j:kah/leh) (r:zd:22557/zd:21243) (q:draft)
kahlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/work) (w:not attend/not go to) (d:<kah>, go up to, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not attend a school, an office or a post) (j:kah/lo) (r:zd:21876/zd:22095) (q:draft)
kahloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/social) (w:not attend/not go to) (d:<kah>, attend, and the negative <loh> written as one word: not going to a school or a meeting, used before words such as <ding> and <hun>) (j:kah/loh) (r:zd:11456/zd:21279) (q:draft)
kahna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education) (w:attending/schooling/attendance) (d:<kah>, go to a school or class, with the noun suffix {-na}: attending school or a course, after words such as <sang>, <tuition> and <tentan>; a different word from {kahna}, weeping) (r:zd:20948/zd:20979/zd:21260) (q:draft)
kahnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:want to attend/want to climb) (d:<kah>, attend or climb, with <nop>, want, written as one word: wish to attend a meeting or a school, or to go up something) (j:kah/nop) (r:zd:21266/zd:23386) (q:draft)
kahnopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:wish to attend/desire to attend) (d:<kah>, here attend, with <nopna>, wish: the wish to attend a school or a meeting; before a noun, that one wishes to attend) (j:kah/nopna) (r:zd:21266/zd:24296) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahong = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ka>, I, and the verb prefix <hong> written as one word before a verb: I, towards the hearer or the speaker's side) (j:ka/hong) (r:zd:23127/zd:17860) (q:draft)
kahpau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:speak in tears/sob out) (d:<kah>, weep, with <pau>, speak: speak while weeping, with a voice that breaks into sobs) (j:kah/pau) (r:zd:21626) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:take to/go with/attend with) (d:<kah>, go up to or attend, with <pih>, together with: go with someone to a place or take someone there; {zato kahpih} is take to hospital and {sang kahpih} is attend school together with) (j:kah/pih) (r:zd:23990/zd:25221/zd:19798) (q:draft)
kahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/family) (w:send to school/have attend/enrol) (d:<kah>, go up to or attend, with the causative <sak>: make or let someone attend a school; {sang kahsak} is send a child to school) (b:kah) (r:zd:26097/zd:20979/zd:26310) (q:draft)
kahsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:education/social) (w:while attending/during attendance) (d:<kah>, attend, and <sung>, in or during, written as one word: during the time of attending a school or a meeting, or among those attending) (j:kah/sung) (r:zd:25221/zd:23156) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahtam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:weeping/wailing/lament) (d:crying aloud in grief, from <kah>, weep; {kahtam lo} is to wail, as at a death) (r:zd:24294/zd:25075) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:all who attend/all the attendees) (d:<kah>, attend, and <teng>, all, written as one word: all those who attend a meeting or gathering) (j:kah/teng) (r:zd:16210/zd:14579) (q:draft)
kahthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:be able to attend/can attend) (d:<kah>, here attend a school or a course, and <thei>, able, written as one word: be able to attend, get to study at) (j:kah/thei) (r:zd:21174/zd:19166) (q:draft)
kahtheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:being able to attend/admission/right to attend) (d:<kah>, attend, and <theihna>, ability, written as one word: being able or allowed to attend a school or a meeting; {kahtheihna laihuan} is an entrance examination) (j:kah/theihna) (r:zd:14751/zd:11126) (q:draft)
kahto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go up/ascend/climb/rise) (d:<kah>, climb, with <to>, upward: go or climb up to a higher place, as a mountain, a ship or heaven; also of smoke rising) (s:paito) (a:kahsuk/kumsuk/paisuk) (b:kah) (q:draft)
kahtohding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:to climb up/to go up) (d:<kahtoh> and <ding> written as one word: to go up, going up as something to be done or allowed) (j:kahtoh/ding) (r:zd:14792/zd:16101) (q:draft)
kahtoto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:keep climbing/go up and up) (d:<kah>, climb, and <toto>, onward, written as one word: keep going up, climb higher and higher) (j:kah/toto) (r:zd:22784/zd:8668) (q:draft)
kahuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:I help/we help) (d:<ka>, the first person marker, and <huh>, help, written as one word: I help or we help) (j:ka/huh) (r:zd:15091) (q:draft, low confidence)
kahuh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:they attend/they climb) (d:<kah>, go up or attend, with the plural marker <uh>, written as one word: they go up, they attend school) (j:kah/uh) (r:zd:22827) (q:draft, low confidence)
kai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:pull/draw/drag) (d:draw something toward oneself or along behind) (q:draft)
kaih = (i:3) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:sign) (d:after <suai>, signature: {suai kaih} is put one's signature to an agreement, an order or another document) (r:zd:17760/zd:11025) (q:draft)
kaihkhiatsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to pull out/try to drag out) (d:<kaihkhiat>, pull out, with <sawm>, try or intend, written as one word) (j:kaihkhiat/sawm) (r:zd:15368/zd:14961) (q:draft)
kaihkhopna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media/work/politics) (w:collection/compilation/recruitment) (d:the bringing together of things or people other than a crop: news, data, writings or rubbish that are collected, and with <galkap>, soldiers, recruitment; {ki kaihkhopna} is an assembly of people) (r:zd:10729/zd:15945/zd:18123) (q:draft)
kaihlan = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:food) (w:Chinese kale/kailan) (d:a green leaf vegetable, Chinese kale or kailan; {kaihlan teh} is its leaf) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:21417/zd:24276) (q:draft, low confidence)
kaihna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:signing) (d:after <suai>, signature: {suai kaihna} is the signing of an order, a law or an agreement; {suai kaihna nei} is to sign) (r:ts:12274/zd:11231) (q:draft)
kaihna = (i:3) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:collection/levying) (d:after <siah>, tax: {siah kaihna} is the collecting of tax from the people by a ruler or a government) (r:zd:11400) (q:draft)
kaikhawma = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:collect and/compile and) (d:<kaikhawm>, collect, with the linking ending {-a}, and then: having collected songs, followed by <khenkhiapa> or <khet>, publish) (j:kaikhawm/a) (r:zd:9219/zd:9247) (q:draft)
kaikhawmkik = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:recall/collect back/take back) (d:of a company or the authorities, take back goods already sold because of a fault, said beside the English word <Recall>; goods are collected back, not scattered people as in the first sense) (r:zd:11997/zd:19550/zd:20466) (q:draft)
kaikhiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can pull out/be able to pull out) (d:<kaikhia> and <thei.2> written as one word: able to pull or draw out; with <ki>, could be pulled out, as people from a wreck) (j:kaikhia/thei) (r:zd:14969/zd:13112) (q:draft)
kaikuang = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:food/nature) (w:shrimp/prawn) (r:zd:24276/zd:11860) (q:draft)
kaina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:going up/rising/ascent) (d:<kai>, go up or draw, with the noun suffix <na>: a going up, as of smoke or of going up to heaven; {nawng kaina} is another spelling of <nawngkaina>, hindrance) (r:zd:25224) (q:draft, low confidence)
kaisak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:social) (w:trouble/disturb/hinder) (d:after <nawng>, the two-word spelling of <nawngkaisak>: cause trouble to someone or disturb the mind, with no sense of pulling) (s:nawngkaisak) (r:zd:24089/zd:10725) (q:draft)
kaisuk = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:pull down/drag down) (d:<kai>, pull, with <suk>, downward: pull a thing or drag a person down, as a zip, a garment, or someone dragged under water; with <hong> also bring a person low) (r:zd:17930/zd:12594/zd:18125) (q:draft)
Kajang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Kajang) (d:town in Selangor, Malaysia, south of Kuala Lumpur; its prison and its hospital are often named in notices about Zomi who are held or treated there) (r:zd:23304/zd:21550/zd:22593) (q:draft)
kak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:side by side/in comparison) (d:placed after a verb of looking, measuring or thinking: one against the other, comparing the two; {et kak} and {teh kak} mean compare, as in <enkak> and <tehkak>) (r:zd:8667/zd:23453/zd:22371) (q:draft)
kakah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:I attended/I went to) (d:<ka>, I, and <kah> written as one word; mostly in {sang kakah}, I attended school) (j:ka/kah) (r:zd:16343/zd:17478) (q:draft)
kakem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:I look after/I keep/I take care of) (d:<ka> and <kem> written as one word: I look after, I keep) (j:ka/kem) (r:zd:25572/zd:19987/zd:17372) (q:draft)
kakemding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:I will look after/we will care for) (d:<ka> and <kemding> written as one word: I will look after, and with <uh> or <uhhi> we will look after) (j:ka/kemding) (r:zd:22416/zd:15647) (q:draft)
kakhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I send/I sent) (d:<ka> and <khak> written as one word, with <khak> in the sense send: I send or sent a thing, money or a message to someone) (j:ka/khak) (r:zd:14883/zd:25768) (q:draft)
kakham = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/social) (w:I am drunk/we are drunk) (d:<ka> and <kham> written as one word, after <zu>: I am drunk, or with <uh> we are drunk) (j:ka/kham) (r:zd:16302) (q:draft)
kakhan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/everyday) (w:my lifetime/my life) (d:<ka> and <khan> written as one word: my lifetime; {ka suah kakhan} is in all my life since I was born) (j:ka/khan) (r:zd:24370/zd:25572) (q:draft)
kakhawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:I stop/I quit) (d:<ka>, I, and <khawl>, stop, written as one word: I stop, I have left the work; with <uh> it is we stop) (j:ka/khawl) (r:zd:15199/zd:19801) (q:draft)
kakhe = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:my foot/my leg) (d:<ka> and <khe> written as one word: my foot or leg) (j:ka/khe) (r:zd:21662/zd:22828) (q:draft)
kakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:branch off/split off/diverge) (d:come out of a larger body as a branch, said of a group or organisation that splits off from another; what it comes from stands before <pan>) (r:zd:23767/zd:12550) (q:draft)
kakhial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:I am wrong/I did wrong) (d:<ka> and <khial> written as one word: I have done wrong, I am at fault) (j:ka/khial) (r:zd:16883/zd:15937) (q:draft)
kakhual = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:I care for/I am concerned for) (d:<ka> and <khual> written as one word: I care for, I feel concern for) (j:ka/khual) (r:zd:22990) (q:draft, low confidence)
kakhut = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:my hand) (d:<ka>, my, and <khut>, hand, written as one word) (j:ka/khut) (r:zd:14760/zd:15577) (q:draft)
kaki = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ka>, I, and the verb prefix <ki> written as one word before a verb: I or we, with <uh>, do the thing to myself or to one another, as {kaki ho uhhi}, we talked together) (j:ka/ki) (r:zd:17936/zd:16337/zd:19984) (q:draft)
kakipak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:I am glad/we are glad/I rejoice) (d:<ka>, I, and <kipak>, be glad, written as one word; with <uh> after it, we are glad) (j:ka/kipak) (r:zd:19021/zd:13110) (q:draft)
kakisa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I consider myself/I feel/I thought I) (d:<ka> and <kisa> written as one word: I consider myself to be so, I feel or thought that I was so) (j:ka/kisa) (r:zd:19465/zd:11362) (q:draft)
kakiteen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:I marry/we marry) (d:<ka> and <kiteen> written as one word: I marry, or with <uh>, we marry) (j:ka/kiteen) (r:zd:20363) (q:draft)
kakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:comparison) (d:<kak>, side by side, with the noun ending {-na}, after <et>, look, or <teh>, measure: {et kakna} and {teh kakna} are a comparison of one thing with another) (b:kak) (r:zd:17673/zd:17990) (q:draft)
kakoih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I put/we put/I place) (d:<ka>, I, and <koih>, put, written as one word: I put or keep a thing somewhere, I post it, or I set it as a priority) (j:ka/koih) (r:zd:23797/zd:11783) (q:draft)
kakuaisi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:vaccine) (d:a medicine given by injection to protect against a disease, in the articles the Covid-19 vaccine) (o:Burmese, kakwe hsay) (r:zd:25279) (q:draft)
kakuppih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:I discuss with/we consult with) (d:<ka> and <kuppih> written as one word: I talk a matter over with someone, or with <uh>, we do) (j:ka/kuppih) (r:zd:20263/zd:25319) (q:draft)
kal = (i:5) (t:n) (f:everyday/time) (w:between/interval/while) (d:the space or time between, a short form of <kikal>: after a pair it means between them, as {nupa kal}, between husband and wife, and after a verb with <in> it means while, as {ihmut kal in}, while asleep) (s:kikal) (r:zd:25177/zd:23655/zd:22862) (q:draft)
kal masa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/time) (w:first step/first week) (d:<kal>, a step or a week, and <masa>, first: the first step, mostly in the figurative sense of the first thing done toward an aim; after the name of a month, the first week of that month) (r:zd:21796/zd:26945/zd:21176) (q:draft)
Kaladan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river) (f:travel/nature) (w:Kaladan) (d:a river that flows from Mizoram through Paletwa in Chin State to Sittwe in Rakhine State) (r:zd:20041/zd:17826) (q:draft)
kalah = (i:2) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:between/amid/in the midst of) (d:in the space or time between: after <nupa> or two parties, between them, and {tua kawm kalah}, like <kawmkal>, is meanwhile; not only of a journey as in {lam kalah}) (b:kal) (r:zd:16900/zd:22639) (q:draft)
kalaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I change/I exchange/I replace) (d:<ka>, I, and <laih>, exchange, written as one word: I change one thing for another) (j:ka/laih) (r:zd:19727/zd:21090) (q:draft)
kalak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I took/I got) (d:<ka>, I, and <lak> in the sense take, written as one word: I took or got a thing, often from a source named with <pan>) (j:ka/lak) (r:zd:25319/zd:12765) (q:draft)
kalapau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:Indian language/Hindi) (d:the language of the people of India, with <pau>, language; named beside <Kawlpau> and the English and Chinese languages, and usually written with a capital) (r:zd:24277) (q:draft)
kalate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:Indians/people from India) (d:<kala>, a Burmese word for a person of Indian origin, with the plural <te>; the word can give offence) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:22967) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalate = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:my songs) (d:<ka>, my, and <late>, songs, written as one word) (j:ka/late) (r:zd:16343) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I fear/we are afraid) (d:<ka>, I or we, and <lau>, be afraid, written as one word) (j:ka/lau) (r:zd:13106/zd:22603) (q:draft)
Kalaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Kalaw) (d:hill town in the south of Shan State, Myanmar) (r:zd:19376) (q:draft)
kalawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:my friend) (d:<ka>, my, and <lawm>, friend, written as one word: my friend; {kalawm te} is my friends and {kalawm kagual} my friends and companions) (j:ka/lawm) (r:zd:16241/zd:24574/zd:13314) (q:draft)
kalawmpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:my friend) (d:<ka>, my, and <lawmpa>, male friend, written as one word) (j:ka/lawmpa) (r:zd:15163) (q:draft)
kalawmte = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:my friends) (d:<ka> and <lawmte> written as one word: my friends) (j:ka/lawmte) (r:zd:14792/zd:17450) (q:draft)
kalawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:I am eager/I am excited/we look forward to) (d:<ka> and <lawp> written as one word: I am eager or excited, or with <uh> we are) (j:ka/lawp) (r:zd:16148/zd:24594) (q:draft)
Kalay = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Kalay/Kale/Kalaymyo) (d:town and township in Sagaing Region of Myanmar, in the plain below the Chin Hills, where many Zomi live) (r:zd:25630/zd:11170/zd:16678) (q:draft)
Kalaymyo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Kalaymyo/Kalay) (d:town in Sagaing Region of Myanmar where many Zomi live, in Zolai also called <Kawlpi>) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:12862/zd:20760) (q:draft)
Kale = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua/land) (f:travel) (w:Kale/Kalay) (d:town and valley in Sagaing Region in Myanmar, below the Chin Hills, where many Zomi live; also written Kalay and Kalaymyo) (r:zd:22802) (q:draft)
kalei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:I buy/I bought) (d:<ka> and <lei> written as one word: I buy or bought, and with <uh> we bought) (j:ka/lei) (r:zd:21254/zd:24594) (q:draft)
Kalemyo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Kalemyo/Kalay) (d:town in Sagaing Region of Myanmar, the name in the records of the government for the town the Zomi call <Kawlpi>; also written <Kalaymyo>) (r:ts:4569/zd:24119) (q:draft)
Kalentan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (j:Kelantan) (r:zd:23571) (q:draft)
Kalewa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Kalewa) (d:town and township on the Chindwin river in Sagaing Region, Myanmar, east of Kalaymyo; its Zolai name is given as <Gunkhawm>) (r:ts:7775/zd:21626) (q:draft)
kalhelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:insert in between/put in between/interpose) (d:<kal>, between, with <helh>, mix in: put something in between other things, as a remark into what is being said) (j:kal/helh) (r:zd:24862) (q:draft)
kalhelh = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:interim/by-) (d:coming in between two regular ones: {kalhelh kiteel} is a by-election and {kalhelh kumpi} an interim government) (s:kiallap) (r:zd:24646) (q:draft)
kalhkhumkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/everyday) (w:get locked in/lock in by accident) (d:<kalhkhum>, lock in, with <kha>, happen to: be locked in by accident, said with <kongkhak>, door) (j:kalhkhum/kha) (r:zd:21981/zd:16634) (q:draft)
Kalimantan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Kalimantan) (d:the Indonesian part of the island of Borneo, with provinces such as Central and West Kalimantan) (r:zd:12138/zd:16702) (q:draft)
kalkal = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:in between/at intervals/in spare moments) (d:<kal>, interval, said twice: in the gaps between other things, mostly after {a man hun}, the time one is free, also written {amanhun}, and followed by <in>: whenever one has free time) (b:kal) (r:zd:11461/zd:15681) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:one week/a week) (d:<kal>, week, and <khat>, one, written as one word: one week; {kalkhat in} is in a week, per week, and {nipi kalkhat} is also one week, as <nipikal>) (j:kal/khat) (r:zd:14921/zd:20806/zd:17428) (q:draft)
kalkhat = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:one step/a step) (d:<kal>, step, and <khat>, one, written as one word: one step of the foot; {kalkhat suan} is take one step) (j:kal/khat) (r:zd:20971/zd:21948) (q:draft)
kalkhatsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:for a week/within a week) (d:<kal>, week, <khat>, one, and <sung>, in, written as one word: for one week, during one week) (j:kal/khat/sung) (r:zd:19803/zd:11256/zd:12723) (q:draft)
kalkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:home/everyday) (w:force open/pry open/break open) (d:open by force a door or room that is locked, as police or rescuers do to get in, often with <kongkhak>, door, and a tool) (r:zd:14785/zd:15059/zd:20440) (q:draft)
kallak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:interim/intermediate/in between) (d:what stands in the middle between two sides or two periods; before a noun it means interim, as {kallak kumpi}, interim government) (r:zd:25020) (q:draft, low confidence)
Kallang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Kallang) (d:district of Singapore, in the name of the Kallang-Paya Lebar Expressway) (r:zd:12721) (q:draft)
kalmasa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:first week) (d:<kal>, week, and <masa>, first, written as one word: the first week of a month) (j:kal/masa) (r:zd:20547/ts:8130) (q:draft)
kalmasa = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:first step) (d:<kal>, step, and <masa>, first, written as one word: the first step in something that is undertaken) (j:kal/masa) (r:zd:21568) (q:draft)
kalnatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:kidney disease) (d:<kal>, kidney, with <natna>, disease, written as one word) (j:kal/natna) (r:zd:12557) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalnih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:two weeks/fortnight) (d:<kal>, week, and <nih>, two, written as one word: two weeks; {kalnih sungin} is within two weeks and {kalnih khitciangin} is two weeks later) (j:kal/nih) (r:zd:16045/zd:15816/zd:11700) (q:draft)
kalnihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:second week) (d:<kal>, week, and <nihna>, second, written as one word: the second week of a month) (j:kal/nihna) (r:zd:20547/zd:16799) (q:draft)
kalnihsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:for two weeks/within two weeks) (d:<kalnih>, two weeks, and <sung>, during, written as one word: for or within two weeks) (j:kalnih/sung) (r:zd:13226/zd:13197) (q:draft)
kalo = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home/work) (w:my field/my farm) (d:<ka>, my, and <lo>, field, written as one word; in {ka inn kalo}, my house and my field, it means all that one owns. In another sentence {kalo} follows <min>, name, and seems to be a verb) (j:ka/lo) (r:zd:15679) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:step/big step/stage) (d:a stride, and so a stage on the way to a goal or a large step forward) (r:zd:17213/zd:24457) (q:draft)
kalsim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:weekly/every week) (d:<kal>, week, with <sim>, each: {kalsim in} is every week, and before a noun it means weekly, as in {kalsim thungetna}, the weekly prayer meeting) (r:zd:10892/zd:12822/zd:12647) (q:draft)
kalsuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:walk/step/take a step) (d:move forward on foot, take steps) (r:45.8.1) (q:draft)
kalsuandan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/everyday) (w:way of proceeding/course/approach/gait) (d:<kalsuan> and <dan> written as one word: the way someone walks, and of a people or a government the way it goes about its affairs) (j:kalsuan/dan) (r:zd:25580/zd:9435) (q:draft)
kalsuanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:will walk/will proceed/to go forward) (d:<kalsuan>, step, and <ding> written as one word: to go forward, to proceed in a course of action) (j:kalsuan/ding) (r:zd:25200/zd:11988) (q:draft)
kalsuanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:going forward/proceeding) (d:<kalsuan> and <in> written as one word: walking on, going forward, carrying on in a certain way) (j:kalsuan/in) (r:zd:19688/zd:10854) (q:draft)
kalsuankhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:walk together/go forward together) (d:<kalsuan>, step or walk, with <khop>, together: move forward together as one, mostly before <ding> or <hun>) (j:kalsuan/khop) (r:zd:24035/zd:24733) (q:draft)
kalsuanpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:walk with/lead forward/carry forward) (d:<kalsuan>, step forward, with <pih>, together with: go forward with someone, lead people on, or carry a matter forward) (b:kalsuan) (r:zd:21273/zd:24804) (q:draft)
kalsuanta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:have set out/be now walking/have stepped forward) (d:<kalsuan>, step or walk, and <ta>, which marks that the action has now begun, written as one word: have now started on a road or a course) (j:kalsuan/ta) (r:zd:21869/zd:19997) (q:draft)
kalsuanto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:step forward/advance/progress/go forward) (d:<kalsuan>, step, and <to>, upward or onward, written as one word: go forward step by step, make progress) (j:kalsuan/to) (r:zd:15800/zd:16442) (q:draft)
kalsuanzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:way of proceeding/course/procedure) (d:<kalsuan> and <zia> written as one word: the way one goes forward, how a person, group or office proceeds) (j:kalsuan/zia) (r:zd:12112/zd:22938) (q:draft)
kalsuanziate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:ways of proceeding/courses/practices) (d:<kalsuanzia>, way of proceeding, with the plural <te>: the ways in which a group or church goes about its work) (b:kalsuanzia) (r:zd:11891/zd:25866) (q:draft)
kalsuanzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be able to go forward/manage to carry on) (d:<kalsuan>, step forward, and <zo>, be able, written as one word: manage to keep going or make progress) (j:kalsuan/zo) (r:zd:23629) (q:draft)
kalsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:during the week/in the week) (d:<kal>, week, and <sung>, during, written as one word; {abeisa kalsung in} is last week, in the past week) (j:kal/sung) (r:zd:16916/zd:14664) (q:draft)
kalsungin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:during the week/in the week) (d:<kalsung>, during the week, with <in>, written as one word; {abeisa kalsungin} is last week, in the past week) (j:kalsung/in) (r:zd:16858/zd:12099) (q:draft)
kaltang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:deliberately/insistently) (d:placed after a verb, mostly one with <nuam>, want to: do or want it on purpose and in spite of knowing better) (r:zd:18175) (q:draft, low confidence)
kalthak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:new step) (d:<kal>, step, with <thak>, new, written as one word: a new step; {kalthak suan} is take a new step, go forward into something new) (j:kal/thak) (r:zd:21100/zd:23223) (q:draft)
kalu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:my head) (d:<ka> and <lu> written as one word: my head) (j:ka/lu) (r:zd:11764) (q:draft)
kalung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:my heart/my mind) (d:<ka>, my, and <lung>, heart or mind, written as one word: my heart, the seat of my feeling, as in {kalung nuam lo}, I am not at ease) (j:ka/lung) (r:zd:25173/zd:20565/zd:12217) (q:draft)
kalungdam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:I am glad/I am thankful) (d:<ka>, I, and <lungdam>, glad, written as one word: I am glad, I am thankful) (j:ka/lungdam) (r:zd:25572/zd:19894) (q:draft)
kalungkim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I am satisfied/I am pleased) (d:<ka>, I, and <lungkim>, be satisfied, written as one word) (j:ka/lungkim) (r:zd:24029/zd:12801) (q:draft)
kalungsim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (w:my heart/my mind) (d:<ka> and <lungsim> written as one word: my heart, my mind) (j:ka/lungsim) (r:zd:12093/zd:16038) (q:draft)
kalup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:I lie down/I sleep/I stay in bed) (d:<ka>, I, with <lup>, lie down, written as one word: I lay down or slept; with {zato ah}, I was kept in hospital) (j:ka/lup) (r:zd:25616/zd:13009/zd:23737) (q:draft)
kalut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:I enter/I go in/I join) (d:<ka> and <lut> written as one word: I enter or go into a place, I join a group) (j:ka/lut) (r:zd:24327/zd:24594) (q:draft)
Kalvari = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:religion) (w:Calvary) (d:the hill outside Jerusalem where Jesus was crucified, mostly as {Kalvari mual}; the place the Bible text calls <Golgotha>) (o:Latin, Calvaria) (r:zd:18900) (q:draft)
kama = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education) (w:in the language/in the tongue) (d:<kam>, language, with the ending {-a}, in: placed after the name of a language, as {Tedim kama}, in the Tedim language, and not of something said by mouth) (r:zd:9266/zd:9232) (q:draft)
kamai = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:body/everyday) (w:my face/before me) (d:<ka> and <mai> written as one word: my face; {kamai ah} is in front of me, and {kamai nawt} is I press forward) (j:ka/mai) (r:zd:13328/zd:19783/zd:13072) (q:draft)
kamal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (j:kammal) (r:zd:17883/zd:23928/zd:19606) (q:draft)
kamang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:my dream) (d:<ka>, my, and <mang>, here dream, written as one word; the same spelling also stands for {ka mang} as I obey) (j:ka/mang) (r:zd:26097) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:be guilty/have done wrong) (d:<ka>, I, and <mawh>, be guilty, written as one word: I am guilty; {kamawh kei} is I am not guilty) (j:ka/mawh) (r:zd:11540/zd:15937) (q:draft)
kamawhmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:plead guilty/I am indeed guilty) (d:<kamawh>, I am guilty, with the emphatic <mah>, written as one word: I am indeed guilty, the words of one who pleads guilty in court) (j:kamawh/mah) (r:zd:11941/zd:16162) (q:draft)
kamawhna = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/religion) (w:my fault/my sin/my guilt) (d:<ka>, my, and <mawhna>, sin or wrongdoing, written as one word) (j:ka/mawhna) (r:zd:15724/zd:16883) (q:draft)
Kamayut = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Kamayut) (d:a township of the city of Yangon in Myanmar) (r:zd:14790) (q:draft)
kambek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:words alone/mere speech/speech only) (d:<kam> and <bek> written as one word: the mouth only, words and nothing else; {kambek tawh} is by words alone) (j:kam/bek) (r:zd:20964/zd:17022) (q:draft)
kamciam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:pledge/promise/vow) (d:a promise given by word of mouth; <kam>, mouth, with <ciam>, promise) (s:kamciamna/thuciam/kiciamna) (q:draft)
kamciamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:promises/pledges) (d:<kamciam>, promise, with plural <te>) (b:kamciam) (j:kamciam/te) (r:zd:21461/zd:9244) (q:draft)
Kamhau = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social/politics) (w:Kamhau/Kam Hau) (d:name of a Sukte chief of the Tedim area, and after him of the tract he ruled, its people and their speech; {Kamhau lampi} is a road named after him) (r:zd:22350/zd:19408) (q:draft, low confidence)
kami = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:my people/my person) (d:<ka> and <mi> written as one word: my people, a person who is mine or one of ours) (j:ka/mi) (r:zd:15499/zd:25603/zd:21664) (q:draft)
kamit = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:my eye/my eyes) (d:<ka> and <mit> written as one word: my eye or eyes; {kamit tawh kamuh} is I saw it with my own eyes) (j:ka/mit) (r:zd:15298/zd:23737) (q:draft)
kamkal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:kawmkal) (r:zd:17986/zd:14776) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamkasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:body/everyday) (w:open-mouthed/agape/gaping) (d:<kamka>, open the mouth, with the ending {-sa} of a lasting state: with the mouth left open, also gaping in surprise) (b:kamka) (r:zd:12942/zd:23112) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamkinial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:quarrel/argue/have words) (d:<kam>, mouth, with <kinial>, argue: quarrel with words) (j:kam/kinial) (r:zd:14568/zd:17514) (q:draft)
kamkinialna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:quarrel/argument/dispute) (d:<kam>, mouth, with <kinialna>, dispute: a quarrel in words between people) (s:kinialna) (r:zd:15170/ts:1264) (q:draft)
kamkum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:talk over/discuss/converse) (d:talk a matter over with someone, exchange words; the person talked with is marked by <tawh>, and it is often followed by <khawm>, together) (r:zd:19139/zd:25462/zd:23295) (q:draft)
kamkup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:discuss/converse/talk together) (d:<kam> word with <kup>, talk over: talk with one another about a matter; also as a noun, a discussion, and {kamkup pih} is someone to talk with) (s:kikup) (r:zd:22715/zd:24217/zd:11809) (q:draft)
kamkupna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:discussion/talks/dialogue/consultation) (d:<kam>, word, with <kikupna>, talking a matter over: a discussion or meeting for talks, also talks between opposing sides) (s:kikupna) (r:zd:24217/zd:26620/zd:15011) (q:draft)
kamlet = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:interpreter/translator/interpreting) (d:one who puts the speech of one language into another, and the work of doing so; also used as a verb, interpret) (s:kamphen) (r:zd:24531/zd:13165) (q:draft)
kammal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (w:word/speech) (d:<kam>, mouth, with <mal>, a single unit: a word, a thing said) (s:kamgen) (r:21.12.10) (q:draft)
kammal zat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (w:wording/choice of words/use of words) (d:<kammal>, word, and <zat>, the form of <zang>, use: the words a person uses, wording or choice of words; a possessor may stand before it, and with <ding> or <huai> it is the verb phrase to use a word) (r:zd:24068/zd:22802/zd:25749) (q:draft)
kammalno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:little word/small word) (d:<kammal>, word, with the diminutive {-no}: a single small word) (b:kammal) (r:zd:20751/zd:20224) (q:draft)
kamnam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:food/social) (w:tipsy/having drink on the breath) (d:mostly after <zu>, strong drink: having drunk alcohol so that it shows or can be smelt on the breath, slightly drunk; {zu kamnam te} are people who have been drinking) (r:zd:14992/ts:3125/zd:18175) (q:draft)
kamnial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:argue/dispute/quarrel) (d:<kam>, word, with <nial>, dispute: contradict in words; used with the reciprocal <ki>, as {ki kamnial}, argue with one another) (s:kinial) (r:zd:20622/zd:12272/zd:18067) (q:draft)
kamnialna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:argument/dispute/quarrel) (d:<kamnial>, argue, with the noun suffix {-na}: an argument in words; mostly after <ki>, as in {ki kamnialna}, an argument with one another) (b:kamnial) (r:zd:17491/zd:12869) (q:draft)
kampan = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/body) (w:from the mouth/by word of mouth) (d:<kam>, mouth, with <pan>, from, written as one word: out of the mouth, in what someone says) (j:kam/pan) (r:zd:17976/zd:20874/zd:12607) (q:draft)
Kampar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Kampar) (d:a town and district in the state of Perak in Malaysia) (r:zd:21793) (q:draft)
kampau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:language/speech/words) (d:<kam>, mouth, with <pau>, speak: the language a people speaks, or what a person says) (s:pau/kammal) (r:20.12.25) (q:draft)
kampaute = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:speakers) (d:the people who speak a language, after the name of the language, as {Tedim kampaute} and {Zo kampaute}; not the things that a person says) (r:ts:11162) (q:draft, low confidence)
kampauzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:manner of speaking/way of talking) (d:<kampau>, speech, and <zia>, manner, written as one word: the way a person speaks) (j:kampau/zia) (r:zd:22171) (q:draft)
kampha = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:lucky/fortunate) (d:having good luck, the opposite of <kamsia>; also the noun good luck) (s:hampha) (r:zd:20071/zd:10700/zd:16584) (q:draft)
kamphat = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:lucky/fortunate) (d:form of <kampha>, lucky, used before <na> and in pairs: <kamphatna> is good luck, and <kamsiat> {kamphat} is bad luck and good luck) (b:kampha) (r:zd:25916/zd:9449) (q:draft)
kamphatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:luck/good fortune) (d:good luck; <kamphatna tawh> is by good fortune, fortunately) (a:kamsiatna) (r:zd:20663/zd:12858/zd:23773) (q:draft)
kamphatna tawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:fortunately/luckily/by good fortune) (d:<kamphatna>, good luck, and <tawh>, with: fortunately; it stands at the head of the sentence or before the verb, in news reports mostly of people who escaped harm) (r:zd:20663/zd:13262) (q:draft)
kampheen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (j:kamphen) (r:zd:25105/zd:21079) (q:draft)
kamphente = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:interpreters) (d:plural of <kamphen>: those who put what is said into another language, as at an office) (b:kamphen) (r:zd:18234) (q:draft)
kamsan = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:body/everyday) (w:red-mouthed/betel-stained) (d:<kam>, mouth, with <san>, red: with the mouth stained red from chewing betel, mostly in {kamsan biabua}, the mouth smeared red all over; not {kamsan}, prophesy) (r:zd:22459) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamsang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:prophet) (d:the noun use of {kamsang}: a person who speaks a message from God, before a name as in {kamsang Isaiah}, the prophet Isaiah, and with {-te} for the prophets) (s:prophet) (r:zd:19767/zd:15894/zd:14927) (q:draft)
kamsanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:prophecy/prophesying) (d:<kamsan>, prophesy, with the noun ending {-na}: a message spoken from God about what is to come) (b:kamsan) (r:zd:23740/zd:25484) (q:draft)
kamsiatna tawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:unfortunately/by misfortune/by ill luck) (d:<kamsiatna>, misfortune, and <tawh>, with: by misfortune; stands before the statement of an accident, a death or a loss that nobody intended) (r:zd:23281/zd:16832) (q:draft)
kamsungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:body) (w:in the mouth) (d:<kamsung> and <ah> written as one word: in the mouth, into the mouth) (j:kamsung/ah) (r:zd:21616/zd:20755) (q:draft)
kamtam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:quarrel/argue/have words) (d:after <ki>, exchange many angry words with one another, often beside {ki kamnial} or <kitawng>; a mutual quarrel, not the habit of talking much) (r:zd:16020/zd:14908) (q:draft)
kamtampi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:many words/much talk) (d:<kam>, word, and <tampi>, many, written as one word; {kamtampi pau} is speak a lot) (j:kam/tampi) (r:zd:22474/zd:21434) (q:draft)
kamtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:by mouth/in words/verbally) (d:<kam>, mouth, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: with the mouth, in spoken words, often set against what is done or thought) (j:kam/tawh) (r:zd:23479/zd:20568/zd:20725) (q:draft)
kamtawm = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/everyday) (w:quiet/of few words/reserved) (d:<kam>, mouth or word, with <tawm>, few: speaking little; {a kamtawm mi} is a person of few words) (a:kamtam) (r:zd:19975/zd:22034) (q:draft)
kamu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I see/I saw/I think) (d:<ka>, I, and <mu>, see, written as one word: I see or saw; after a clause with <in> it gives the opinion of the writer, I consider it to be so) (j:ka/mu) (r:zd:11872/zd:12626/zd:12352) (q:draft)
kamuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:I trust/I rely on) (d:<ka> and <muan> written as one word: whom I trust, for me to rely on) (j:ka/muan) (r:zd:16204) (q:draft)
kamuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I see/I saw/what I saw) (d:<ka>, the first person singular, and <muh>, see, written as one word: I see, used before words such as <ciangin> and <hangin>, and what I saw) (j:ka/muh) (r:zd:25572/zd:22658) (q:draft)
kamuhkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I happen to see/what I have seen) (d:<ka>, I, and <muhkhak>, happen to see, written as one word: I come to see, or what I have come to see) (j:ka/muhkhak) (r:zd:14935/zd:20673) (q:draft)
kamuhpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:my seeing/when I saw) (d:<kamuh> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: as for my seeing it, as for the time I saw) (j:kamuh/pen) (r:zd:16294/zd:20721) (q:draft)
kamukha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I saw/I happened to see) (d:<ka>, I, with <mukha>, happen to see, written as one word; with <uh> it is we saw, and {kamukha ngeikei} is I have never seen) (j:ka/mukha) (r:zd:17661/zd:17147) (q:draft)
kamzat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:expression/saying/usage/wording) (d:<kam>, speech, with <zat>, use: the way words are used, an expression or saying that is current; also the speech that a person or people uses) (r:zd:24331/zd:24303/ts:3372) (q:draft)
kanam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:my people/my nation) (d:<ka>, my, and <nam>, people, written as one word) (j:ka/nam) (r:zd:21090/zd:15499) (q:draft)
Kanan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Kanan) (d:village near <Khampat> in Sagaing Region, Myanmar, close to the border with India) (r:zd:23258) (q:draft, low confidence)
kanau = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:my younger sibling/my younger brother/my younger sister) (d:<ka>, my, and <nau>, here a younger brother or sister, written as one word) (j:ka/nau) (r:zd:16442/zd:25768) (q:draft)
kanawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/food) (w:my milk/my breast) (d:<ka>, my, and <nawi>, milk or breast, written as one word) (j:ka/nawi) (r:zd:15485/zd:16259) (q:draft)
Kanbalu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (w:Kanbalu) (d:town and district in Sagaing Region, Myanmar, on the road from Shwebo to Myitkyina) (r:ts:12366) (q:draft)
Kanbawza = (i:1) (t:name) (f:work) (w:Kanbawza) (d:name of a private bank of Myanmar, Kanbawza Bank) (r:zd:15913/zd:17385) (q:draft)
kanbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:research further/inquire further/look into more) (d:<kan>, search or look into, with <beh>, here more, in addition: look further into a matter, find out more about it) (j:kan/beh) (r:zd:20169/zd:24022) (q:draft)
kanbehding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:will investigate further/will look into more) (d:<kanbeh>, inquire further, and <ding> written as one word) (j:kanbeh/ding) (r:zd:20492/zd:13352) (q:draft)
kanbehna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:further research/further inquiry) (d:noun of <kanbeh>, look further into: the looking further into a matter to learn more) (b:kanbeh) (r:zd:20432) (q:draft)
kancian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:investigate/look into/examine closely) (d:<kan>, search, with <cian>, carefully: look into a matter thoroughly to find out what happened) (r:zd:15019/zd:19307) (q:draft)
kancianding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:will investigate thoroughly) (d:<kan>, look into, <cian>, thoroughly, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will investigate fully) (j:kan/cian/ding) (r:zd:21618/zd:19480) (q:draft)
kancianlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:be still investigating/be looking into) (d:<kancian>, investigate, and <lai>, still, written as one word: the inquiry is still going on) (j:kancian/lai) (r:zd:12619/zd:15370) (q:draft)
kancianlaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:will investigate further/will still look into) (d:<kancian>, investigate, and <laiding>, will still, written as one word: the matter is yet to be looked into closely) (j:kancian/laiding) (r:zd:13220/zd:14950) (q:draft)
kancianna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:investigation/inquiry/examination) (d:<kan>, search, with <cian>, thoroughly, and the noun ending {-na}: a thorough looking into a matter, as by the police; {kancianna nei} is carry out an investigation) (r:zd:11389/zd:16131/zd:11229) (q:draft)
kanciansan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate thoroughly/look into) (d:<kan>, look into, with <cian>, clearly, and <san>: examine a matter closely to find out what happened; said of police and authorities, often as {aki kanciansan laitak}, it is being investigated) (r:zd:19054/zd:13135) (q:draft)
kanciantheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:be able to investigate) (d:<kancian>, investigate, and <theih>, be able, written as one word, before <nadingin>: so that it can be looked into thoroughly) (j:kancian/theih) (r:zd:15686) (q:draft)
