kang = (i:4) (t:v) (f:food) (w:fry) (d:cook food in hot oil, said with <sathau>, oil, as in {sathau tawh kikang}, fried in oil; not the burning of a house or the drying up of water) (r:zd:21557) (q:draft, low confidence)
kangah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I get/I receive/I got) (d:<ka>, the first person singular, and <ngah>, get, written as one word: I get or received it) (j:ka/ngah) (r:zd:13148/zd:17971/zd:19779) (q:draft)
kangaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I listen/I hear) (d:<ka>, I, and <ngaih>, listen, written as one word: I listen to; also the first part of {ka ngaihsun}, I think, when it is divided as {kangaih sun} or {kangaih sut}) (j:ka/ngaih) (r:zd:24947) (q:draft, low confidence)
kangaihsun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I think/I consider) (d:<ka> and <ngaihsun> written as one word: I think, I consider) (j:ka/ngaihsun) (r:zd:19676/zd:19302) (q:draft)
