kangtumgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/media) (w:burn up completely/be gutted by fire/burn to ruin) (d:<kangtum>, burn up, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word: of fire, destroy a building, goods or land entirely) (j:kangtum/gawp) (r:zd:18129/zd:15795/zd:11148) (q:draft)
kangtumkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/media) (w:have burnt up/be burnt down) (d:<kangtum>, burn up, and <khin>, already, written as one word: fire has burnt it up completely) (j:kangtum/khin) (r:zd:13213/zd:15820) (q:draft)
kanhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/media) (w:worth looking into/worth finding out) (d:<kan>, look into, and <huai>, worthy of, written as one word: that ought to be inquired about; often together with <theihhuai>, worth knowing) (j:kan/huai) (r:zd:12257/zd:15433) (q:draft)
