kankhiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:to find out/to investigate) (d:<kankhiat> and <ding> written as one word: to find out or investigate the cause or the truth of a matter) (j:kankhiat/ding) (r:zd:17792/zd:18893/zd:15116) (q:draft)
kankhiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:be able to find out/track down/identify) (d:<kankhia>, find out, and <thei>, here be able, written as one word: manage to find out or trace a person or a fact) (j:kankhia/thei) (r:zd:11801/zd:15245/zd:16834) (q:draft)
kankhiattheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:be able to find out/be able to investigate) (d:<kankhiat>, find out, and <theih>, be able, written as one word, used before <nading> and <nadingin>: so that a matter can be found out) (j:kankhiat/theih) (r:zd:13241/zd:12891) (q:draft)
kankhiazo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to find out/manage to trace) (d:<kankhia>, search out, and <zo>, be able, written as one word: manage to find out a matter or trace a person) (j:kankhia/zo) (r:zd:12201/zd:16073) (q:draft)
kankik = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:trace back/investigate again/look into again) (d:<kan>, look into, with <kik>, back or again: go back over a matter, a record or a trail in order to find out what happened, as the police do from camera pictures or a new government with an old case; nothing is brought back) (r:zd:11801/zd:15639/zd:19801) (q:draft)
kankuat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:contest/lay a rival claim to/oppose) (d:strive against others for something that they claim or have obtained, as land, a road project or a decision of the authorities) (r:zd:22586/zd:22334) (q:draft, low confidence)
kankuatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:opposition/objection/protest) (d:the act of opposing or contesting something, from <kankuat>; {kankuatna button} is the button pressed to vote against) (b:kankuat) (r:zd:21117/zd:20545) (q:draft)
kanlai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:look into further/investigate further) (d:<kan>, look into a matter, with <lai>, still, written as one word: the matter is not yet known and will be looked into further; it stands as the verb before <ning> or <ding>, not after another verb as the adverb does) (r:zd:12402/ts:3366) (q:draft, low confidence)
kanlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not look into/not inquire/not study) (d:<kan>, look into or inquire, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not look into a matter, not study or seek out) (j:kan/lo) (r:zd:21815) (q:draft, low confidence)
kanna = (i:3) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:crossing) (d:<kan>, cross over, with the noun suffix <na>: the going across a stream or a border, as in {gamgi kanna}, a border crossing, and {kanna lei}, a bridge for crossing; nothing is broken or looked into) (r:zd:16139) (q:draft, low confidence)
kannop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to ask/want to inquire) (d:<kan> and <nop> written as one word: wanting to inquire into a matter, paired with <dotnop>, wanting to ask) (j:kan/nop) (r:zd:16235) (q:draft, low confidence)
kannop dotnop = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:question/inquiry/enquiry) (d:<kannop>, want to inquire, and <dotnop>, want to ask: a pair of near synonyms used as one noun, anything one wishes to inquire or ask about; often followed by {khat peuhpeuh}, any at all) (r:zd:16235) (q:draft)
kanpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:investigate at once/look into immediately) (d:<kan> and <pah> written as one word: begin to search or investigate right away) (j:kan/pah) (r:zd:15639/zd:11044) (q:draft)
Kanpalet = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel/politics) (w:Kanpetlet) (d:town and township in the south of Chin State, near Mindat) (r:ts:11032/zd:11325) (q:draft)
kansak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:food) (w:fry for/fry) (d:<kang.4>, fry, with <sak> for an act done for someone: fry food for a person, as in {aktui hong kansak}, fried an egg for me; not the drying up of water or the inquiring of the other senses) (r:zd:11735) (q:draft, low confidence)
kansan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:investigate/look into) (d:<kan>, search, with the ending {-san}: follow up a case to find out what happened, said of the police and authorities) (s:kan) (r:zd:15419/zd:20589) (q:draft)
kansanlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:be still investigating/investigate further) (d:<kansan>, investigate, and <lai>, here still, written as one word: the case is still under investigation; with <ki> before it, is still being investigated) (j:kansan/lai) (r:zd:13230/zd:12007) (q:draft)
Kansas = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Kansas) (d:state in the middle of the United States; {Kansas khua} is Kansas City) (r:zd:24691/zd:16308) (q:draft)
kansiam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:researcher/scholar) (d:<kan>, look into, with <siam>, skilled: one who is skilled at research; {tangthu kansiam} is a historian) (j:kan/siam) (r:zd:17745/zd:21739) (q:draft)
kantanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:will cross/in order to cross) (d:<kantan>, cross, and <ding> written as one word: going to cross, or so as to cross a road or a border) (j:kantan/ding) (r:zd:12904/zd:20037) (q:draft)
kantanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:crossing/crossing place) (d:<kantan>, cross, with the noun suffix <na>: the act or place of crossing a road, river or border; {lamzikpi kantanna} is a footbridge over a road) (b:kantan) (r:zd:15043/zd:22046/zd:15362) (q:draft)
kantelna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:research/investigation/inquiry/study) (d:<kantel>, investigate, with the noun suffix <na>: a careful inquiry into a matter, research) (b:kantel) (r:zd:23016/zd:12369) (q:draft)
kanthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:can investigate/be able to study) (d:<kan> and <thei> written as one word: be able to look into, research or study something) (j:kan/thei) (r:zd:24022/zd:22416) (q:draft)
kanu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:my mother) (d:<ka> and <nu> written as one word: my mother; {kanu kapa} is my mother and father, my parents) (j:ka/nu) (r:zd:19556/zd:16020/zd:24542) (q:draft)
kanui = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I laugh/we laugh) (d:<ka> and <nui> written as one word: I laugh, and with a following <uh>, we laugh) (j:ka/nui) (r:zd:24462/zd:15659) (q:draft)
kanung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:behind me/behind us/my back) (d:<ka>, my, and <nung>, the back or the place behind, written as one word; {kanung uhah} is behind us and {kanung panin} is from behind me) (j:ka/nung) (r:zd:14899/zd:20289) (q:draft)
kanusia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I leave/I forsake/I abandon) (d:<ka> and <nusia> written as one word: I leave, I give up) (j:ka/nusia) (r:zd:23025) (q:draft)
kanza = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/politics) (w:cannabis/marijuana/ganja) (d:the hemp plant used as a drug, smoked with <teep>) (o:Hindi, ganja) (r:zd:11675) (q:draft)
kanzek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:look into/study a little) (d:<kan>, search or look into, and <zek>, a little, written as one word: look into a matter somewhat, do some inquiry) (j:kan/zek) (r:zd:21815/zd:23090) (q:draft, low confidence)
kap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:weep/cry/mourn) (d:shed tears: weep, cry or mourn for someone; {nakpi-in kap} is weep bitterly) (s:kah/thuum) (a:nui) (r:43.11.35) (q:draft)
kap ziahziah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:fire heavily/shell/bombard) (d:<kap>, here shoot, and <ziahziah>, freely and without stopping: fire heavily and continuously; the weapon stands before it with <tawh>) (r:ts:4734/ts:5962) (q:draft)
kapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:my father) (d:<ka>, my, and <pa>, father, written as one word) (j:ka/pa) (r:zd:16020/zd:16924) (q:draft)
kapai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:I go/I went) (d:<ka> and <pai> written as one word: I go, I went; {kapai kik} is I go back) (j:ka/pai) (r:zd:17426/zd:25937/zd:25616) (q:draft)
kapaina = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel/everyday) (w:where I go/where I went) (d:<ka> and <paina> written as one word: the place I go to, my going) (j:ka/paina) (r:zd:10973/zd:23014) (q:draft)
kapanpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:I help/I support) (d:<ka> and <panpih> written as one word: I help or support, or we with <uh>) (j:ka/panpih) (r:zd:12919/zd:19302) (q:draft)
Kapar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Kapar) (d:town in the district of Klang in the state of Selangor, Malaysia) (r:zd:15686) (q:draft)
kapasal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:my husband) (d:<ka>, my, and <pasal>, husband, written as one word) (j:ka/pasal) (r:zd:12630/zd:18077) (q:draft)
kapau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:I speak/we speak) (d:<ka>, the first person marker, with <pau>, speak, written as one word: I speak) (j:ka/pau) (r:zd:25174/zd:10973) (q:draft)
kapding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:will shoot/to shoot) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will shoot, is to be shot at; {thautawh kapding} is will shoot with a gun) (j:kap/ding) (r:zd:16869/zd:14783) (q:draft)
kapgawp = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:cry hard/wail/weep bitterly) (d:<kap>, weep, with <gawp>, severely: cry very hard, often beside <awnggawp>, scream; without a gun word such as <thautawh> before it) (r:zd:14824/zd:21793/zd:17818) (q:draft)
kapha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:I reach/we number) (d:<ka> and <pha>, here reach an age or a number, written as one word: I reach an age, or with <uh> we come to a number, as in {mi 20 kiim kapha uh hi}, we were about 20 people) (j:ka/pha) (r:zd:15268/zd:20673) (q:draft)
kaphak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:I reached/I attained) (d:<ka> and <phak> written as one word: I reached, mostly of an age, as in {kum 8 kaphak ciangin}, when I reached eight years) (j:ka/phak) (r:zd:20016/zd:15861) (q:draft)
kaphawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I remember/I realise) (d:<ka>, I, and <phawk>, remember or be aware, written as one word: I remember, I come to realise) (j:ka/phawk) (r:zd:21421/zd:20503) (q:draft)
kaphuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:I compose/I composed) (d:<ka>, I, and <phuah>, compose, written as one word: I compose, or before a noun what I composed, said of songs) (j:ka/phuah) (r:zd:16343/zd:16216) (q:draft)
kaphuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:I compose/I composed) (d:<ka>, I, and <phuak> written as one word: I compose, said of a song; also I give a name) (j:ka/phuak) (r:zd:21326/zd:23666) (q:draft)
kapi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:my grandmother) (d:<ka> and <pi.2> written as one word: my grandmother, named together with <kapu>, my grandfather; the same spelling also occurs once for coffee and as a misspelling of <khapi>, the moon) (j:ka/pi) (r:zd:16772) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I give/I gave) (d:the first person marker <ka> written together with <pia>, give: I give or we give, with the giver as the speaker; usually written as two words, {ka pia}) (r:zd:23037/zd:25165/zd:15323) (q:draft)
kapiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I will give/we will give) (d:<ka> and <piading> written as one word: I will give, and with <uh> after it we will give) (j:ka/piading) (r:zd:15370) (q:draft)
kapiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I give/I gave) (d:<ka> and <piak> written as one word: I give or I gave, and with <uh> we gave) (j:ka/piak) (r:zd:16442/zd:23071/zd:25046) (q:draft)
kapiakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I have given/we have already given) (d:<kapia>, I give, and <khin>, already, written as one word; {thu kapiakhin} is I have given the order) (j:kapia/khin) (r:zd:12217/zd:16490) (q:draft)
kapian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:I was born/my birth) (d:<ka>, I or my, and <pian>, be born, written as one word; {kapian'na} is my birthplace) (j:ka/pian) (r:zd:17448/zd:17325) (q:draft)
kapiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:I was born) (d:<ka> and <piang>, be born, written as one word: I was born) (j:ka/piang) (r:zd:21090) (q:draft)
kapianna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (w:my birth/my origin/my birthplace) (d:<ka>, my, and <pianna>, birth or origin, written as one word: my birth, where or from whom I was born) (j:ka/pianna) (r:zd:21090/zd:12370) (q:draft)
kapin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shooting/firing at) (d:<kap.2>, shoot, with the linking suffix <in>: shooting at someone or something and then doing something else, often after <thautawh>, with a gun, where sense 1 is weeping) (b:kap) (r:zd:17439/zd:11799/ts:9743) (q:draft)
kapkap = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:keep shooting/keep firing) (d:<kap.2>, shoot, said twice: fire guns or shells again and again; neighbouring words such as {thaupi tang}, shells, show that it is not weeping) (r:zd:25109) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:while weeping/in tears) (d:<kap>, weep, and <kawm>, while, written as one word: weeping while doing something else) (j:kap/kawm) (r:zd:17478/zd:19943) (q:draft)
kapkawm = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:while shooting/firing as one goes) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <kawm>, while, written as one word: shooting while doing something else, as while running away) (j:kap/kawm) (r:zd:12845) (q:draft)
kapkawmkawm = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:while weeping/in tears) (d:<kap> and <kawmkawm> written as one word: weeping all the while) (j:kap/kawmkawm) (r:zd:15255/zd:20446) (q:draft)
kapkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:hit/shoot/wound by shooting) (d:<kap>, shoot, with <kha>, happen to reach: hit a person or a part of the body with a shot; also said of the sun striking someone) (b:kap) (r:zd:17439/zd:13131/zd:19478) (q:draft)
kapkhakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/health) (w:being shot/gunshot hit/place hit) (d:<kapkhak>, hit by shooting, with the noun ending <na>: the fact of being hit by a shot, or the place that was hit) (j:kapkhak/na) (r:zd:12854/zd:15447) (q:draft)
kapkhalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:miss/not hit) (d:<kapkha>, hit with a shot, and <lo>, not, written as one word: the shot does not hit) (j:kapkha/lo) (r:zd:16450/zd:19478) (q:draft)
kapkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shoot down/fire/shoot) (d:<kap> in its sense of shoot, with <khia>, out: fire a shot, or bring down an aircraft or a bird by shooting; {vanleng kapkhia} is shoot down a plane) (r:ts:6447/zd:14742/zd:24490) (q:draft)
kapkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shoot down) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <khiat>, out or down, written as one word: bring down an aircraft by shooting, in the form used before words such as <sak> and <khit>) (j:kap/khiat) (r:ts:8273) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:launcher/firing system) (d:<kap>, shoot, with <khiat>, out, and the noun ending {-na}: a weapon or device from which missiles or rockets are fired) (r:zd:10886/zd:17591) (q:draft)
