kapkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:have shot/after shooting) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <khit> written as one word: after shooting or after an exchange of fire; {a kapkhit akipan} is from the time they fired) (j:kap/khit) (r:ts:4005/zd:11495) (q:draft)
kapkhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:permission to shoot/licence to shoot) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <khuan>, permission, written as one word; {thautawh kapkhuan pia} is give leave to shoot with guns) (j:kap/khuan) (r:zd:14783) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:shoot back/return fire) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <kik>, back, written as one word: fire back at those who shot) (j:kap/kik) (r:zd:12437/ts:3254) (q:draft)
kapkik = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cry again/weep again) (d:<kap>, weep, and <kik>, again, written as one word) (j:kap/kik) (r:zd:12319) (q:draft, low confidence)
kapliam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:shoot and wound/wound by shooting) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <liam>, be wounded, written as one word: wound someone with a shot; {kapliam athuak} is one who was shot and wounded) (j:kap/liam) (r:zd:19868/zd:17556) (q:draft)
kapliamkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:be shot and wounded/shoot and wound) (d:<kapliam>, wound by shooting, with <kha>, happen to: hit and wound someone with a shot) (j:kapliam/kha) (r:zd:19991) (q:draft)
kapliamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/health) (w:gunshot wound/being shot and wounded) (d:<kapliam> with the ending {-na}: the wounding of someone by a shot; {aki kapliamna} is his being shot and wounded) (b:kapliam) (r:zd:14859/zd:19597) (q:draft)
kaplo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:not shoot) (d:<kap>, shoot, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not shoot at, not attack with guns; the same spelling can be <kap>, weep, with <lo>, not weep) (j:kap/lo) (r:zd:17709/zd:12803) (q:draft)
kaploh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:not shoot/not fire) (d:<kap>, shoot, and the negative <loh> written as one word: not shooting; {kaploh phamawh} is cannot but shoot, have to shoot) (j:kap/loh) (r:ts:11979/zd:14859) (q:draft)
kaplumkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:shoot dead) (d:<kaplum>, shoot dead, with <kha>, happen to, written as one word: shoot someone dead, also by accident) (j:kaplum/kha) (r:zd:17032) (q:draft)
kaplumpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:man who shot dead/gunman) (d:<kaplum> and <pa> written as one word: the man who shot someone dead; after <aki>, {aki kaplumpa}, the man who was shot dead) (j:kaplum/pa) (r:zd:10813/zd:17766) (q:draft)
kaplumpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:shoot dead at once/shoot dead on the spot) (d:<kaplum>, shoot dead, with <pah>, at once, written as one word) (j:kaplum/pah) (r:zd:13082/zd:15537) (q:draft)
kaplumthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:manage to shoot dead/be able to shoot dead) (d:<kaplum>, shoot dead, and <thei>, able, written as one word: succeed in shooting someone or something dead) (j:kaplum/thei) (r:zd:15537/zd:20310) (q:draft)
