lai tahen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:religion/social) (w:may it go on/may it continue) (d:<lai>, still, yet, and <tahen>, may it be: ends a wish or blessing that something go on, placed after a verb, often after <semsem>, more and more, as in {Topa'n hong zang semsem lai tahen}, may the Lord go on using you more and more) (r:zd:23155/zd:20909) (q:draft)
Laia = (i:2) (t:ppm) (f:time) (w:at the time of/in the days of/during) (d:{laia}, written in lower case, is <lai>, time, with the linking <a>: of or at the time named before it, as {tua hun laia}, of that time, and {nidang laia}, of former days; not the instrument) (r:zd:17168/ts:479/zd:9430) (q:draft)
laiat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:writing/piece of writing/article) (d:<lai>, writing, and <at>, write, written as one word: the act of writing, or what someone has written; {laiat pa} is the writer) (j:lai/at) (r:zd:21869/zd:22116/zd:21989) (q:draft)
laibawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:written agreement/treaty/document) (d:<laibawl>, draw up a document, with the ending <na>: an agreement set down in writing; {kilemna laibawlna} is a peace agreement and {thukimna laibawlna} a memorandum of understanding) (b:laibawl) (r:zd:20902/zd:25461) (q:draft)
laibek = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:education) (w:only writing/letters only/only a letter) (d:<lai>, writing or letter, and <bek>, only, written as one word) (j:lai/bek) (r:zd:20256/ts:3508) (q:draft)
laibupi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:big book/record book/register) (d:<laibu>, book, with <pi>, big, written as one word: a large book, also the main book in which records are kept) (j:laibu/pi) (r:zd:24249/zd:22557) (q:draft)
laibusaal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:library) (d:<laibu>, book, with <saal>, storehouse, written as one word: a library; also used as the title of a collection of writings) (j:laibu/saal) (r:zd:19447/zd:24028) (q:draft)
laidal = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:document/papers/card) (d:an official paper that shows who a person is or what is granted, as {UN laidal}, the refugee document of the UNHCR, and {appointment laidal}; not a blank sheet to write on) (r:zd:19222/zd:20782) (q:draft)
laidalneu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:note/slip of paper/small card) (d:<laidal> and <neu> written as one word: a small sheet of paper or card with something written on it) (j:laidal/neu) (r:zd:11827/zd:18292) (q:draft)
laidalno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (w:note/slip of paper/leaflet/tract) (d:<laidal>, sheet of writing, with the ending {-no}, small: a small written sheet, such as a short note or letter, a receipt slip or a religious tract) (b:laidal) (r:zd:14916/zd:11653/zd:15243) (q:draft)
laidalpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:paper document/sheet of paper/letter) (d:<laidal>, sheet, with <pi>, big: a full sheet of paper; in the news the paper letter that a refugee holds instead of a card) (b:laidal) (r:zd:11289/zd:11908) (q:draft)
laidep = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<lai>, still, and <dep>, indeed, written as one word after the verb and before <hi> or {uh hi}: still doing so, and that is notable) (j:lai/dep) (r:zd:24731) (q:draft, low confidence)
laidiam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<lai>, here still, and <diam> written as one word at the end of a question: will it still be so, I wonder whether it will yet) (j:lai/diam) (r:zd:21168/zd:24091/zd:20263) (q:draft)
laiding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will still/will yet) (d:<lai>, here still, and <ding>, the marker of what is to come, written as one word after a verb: will still, is yet to, will go on; with <maw> or <hiam> it asks whether something is to go on) (j:lai/ding) (r:zd:17132/zd:23896/zd:17657) (q:draft)
laidinghi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will still/is yet to) (d:<laiding>, will still, and the sentence-final <hi> written as one word after a verb or a describing word) (j:laiding/hi) (r:zd:20555/zd:23343) (q:draft)
laigelh = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:writing/piece of writing) (d:the verb used as a noun: the act of writing, or what someone has written, as in {ka laigelh}, my writing; the same as <laigelhna>) (s:laigelhna) (r:zd:11891/zd:16849/zd:19621) (q:draft)
laigelhkhiat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it) (w:what one writes/post/written piece) (d:<lai>, writing, and <gelhkhiat>, write out, written as one word: what someone writes and puts out, as a post on social media) (j:lai/gelhkhiat) (r:zd:14720/zd:16042) (q:draft)
laigelhpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:writer/author) (d:<laigelh>, write, with <pa> for a man: the man who wrote a text; a writer also uses it of himself, the present writer) (b:laigelh) (r:zd:20924/zd:24804) (q:draft)
laigelhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:have a letter written) (d:<lai> and <gelhsak> written as one word: have a letter written for oneself by someone else, here by an office) (j:lai/gelhsak) (r:zd:22685/zd:21664) (q:draft)
laigelhsiam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:writer/author/skilled writer) (d:<laigelh>, write, and <siam>, skilled, written as one word: a person skilled at writing, an author) (j:laigelh/siam) (r:zd:16593/zd:9251) (q:draft)
laigelhzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:way of writing/writing style) (d:<laigelh>, writing, and <zia>, way, written as one word: how a person writes, the conventions followed in writing) (j:laigelh/zia) (r:zd:24395/zd:24394) (q:draft)
laigil = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (w:core/essence/heart/nucleus) (d:the innermost and most important part of something; <thu laigil> is the heart of a matter) (r:zd:20786/zd:25166) (q:draft)
laigilte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/education) (w:essentials/core points/heart) (d:<laigil>, core, with the plural <te>: the central and most important parts of a matter; {Pasian thu laigilte} is the heart of the word of God) (b:laigil) (r:zd:17613/zd:25235) (q:draft)
laigual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:line/sentence/line of writing) (d:<lai>, writing, with <gual>, row: a line of written text, a sentence) (r:zd:25337/zd:11262) (q:draft)
laigualte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:lines/sentences/lines of writing) (d:plural of <laigual>: the lines or sentences of a piece of writing) (b:laigual) (r:zd:21392/zd:21325/zd:24303) (q:draft)
laiguizom = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:full sibling/sibling by birth) (d:<laigui>, umbilical cord, and <zom>, join, written as one word: brothers and sisters born of the same mother, siblings by blood; often after <sanggam> or <unau>) (j:laigui/zom) (r:zd:12192/zd:15941) (q:draft)
laiguizomte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:full siblings/siblings by birth) (d:plural of <laiguizom>: brothers and sisters born of the same mother) (b:laiguizom) (r:zd:22140/zd:21096) (q:draft)
laihanciam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:study hard/work hard at school) (d:<lai>, writing or study, and <hanciam>, strive, written as one word: make an effort in one's studies) (j:lai/hanciam) (r:zd:24502) (q:draft)
laihawl = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:medium/middle/average/intermediate) (d:in the middle between high and low or large and small; {mi laihawl} is the middle class and {sumlut laihawl gam} a middle-income country) (r:zd:22157/zd:21225/zd:18086) (q:draft)
laihawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:newsletter/periodical/bulletin/magazine) (d:a paper or magazine given out at regular times, from <lai>, writing, and <hawm>, distribute) (r:zd:20576/zd:20538/zd:21066) (q:draft)
laihawmte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:newsletters/periodicals/newspapers) (d:plural of <laihawm>: papers and magazines that are given out regularly) (b:laihawm) (r:zd:19953/zd:16385) (q:draft)
laihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will replace/to change/to exchange) (d:<laih>, replace or change, and the future marker <ding> written as one word: will change, in order to change) (j:laih/ding) (r:zd:22736/zd:12336) (q:draft)
laihdingbek = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:only to change/just to replace) (d:<laihding> and <bek>, only, written as one word: for nothing more than changing it) (j:laihding/bek) (r:zd:12336) (q:draft)
laihi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:still/yet) (d:<lai>, still, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word after a verb or describing word: it is still so, it can still be done) (j:lai/hi) (r:zd:20518/zd:15305/zd:19219) (q:draft)
laihiam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:still) (d:<lai>, still, and the question word <hiam> written as one word after a verb or describing word: is it still so, whether it is still so) (j:lai/hiam) (r:zd:17079/zd:21605) (q:draft)
laihilh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:education) (w:teach/give lessons) (d:used as a verb, teach in a school or class, with <ding>, <dingin> or the sentence ending <hi> after it; the noun sense names the teacher or the work) (r:zd:9245/zd:22683/zd:20572) (q:draft)
laihilhsia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:teacher/lecturer/tutor) (d:<laihilh>, teach, and <sia>, teacher, written as one word: a person whose work is teaching, in a school, a university or at home) (j:laihilh/sia) (r:zd:26026/zd:12942) (q:draft)
laihilhzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:teaching method/way of teaching/pedagogy) (d:<laihilh>, teaching, and <zia>, way, written as one word: the way of teaching in school) (j:laihilh/zia) (r:zd:9253/zd:25687) (q:draft)
laihkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:replace/remove/change) (d:<laih>, replace, with <khia>, out: take someone out of an office and put another in, or change a thing for another) (j:laih/khia) (r:ts:4831/zd:23797) (q:draft)
laihkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:change back/change again/replace again) (d:<laih>, replace or exchange, with <kik>, again or back, written as one word: change something again, or change it back to what it was) (j:laih/kik) (r:zd:9249/zd:10733) (q:draft)
laihlaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep changing/change again and again/take turns) (d:doubled form of <laih>, exchange: change one for another again and again; with <ki>, keep changing; after a verb, do it in turns) (b:laih) (r:zd:24072/zd:23734) (q:draft)
laihlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not change/not replace) (d:<laih> and <lo> written as one word: not changing, without replacing) (j:laih/lo) (r:zd:22411/zd:12280) (q:draft)
laihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:replacement/change/amendment/exchange) (d:noun from <laih>: putting one thing in place of another, as changing a phone number, replacing old aircraft or amending a law) (b:laih) (r:zd:25415/zd:22782/zd:11087) (q:draft)
laihnading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/work) (w:to replace/in place of) (d:<laih>, replace, and <nading>, in order to, written as one word: for replacing the thing named before it) (j:laih/nading) (r:zd:13011/zd:11003) (q:draft)
laihsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:change/replace/have changed) (d:<laih>, exchange, with the causative <sak>: change one thing for another, or change it for someone, as clothes, a name or a number) (b:laih) (r:zd:17978/zd:23729/zd:19917) (q:draft)
laihsakin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:changing/having changed) (d:<laihsak>, change one thing for another, with the linking <in>, written as one word: changing it and then) (j:laihsak/in) (r:zd:15547) (q:draft)
laihsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to change/intend to replace) (d:<laih> and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: set out to change one thing for another) (j:laih/sawm) (r:zd:15547/zd:16940) (q:draft, low confidence)
laihtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:can be changed/be replaceable/able to change) (d:<laih>, change or replace, and <theih>, be able, written as one word: able to be changed or replaced, often before <nadingin>) (j:laih/theih) (r:zd:16645/zd:15652) (q:draft)
laihuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:examination/exam) (d:a school examination; {laihuan zo} is pass the examination. A few sentences use the word in other ways that are not clear) (r:zd:24595/zd:2072) (q:draft, low confidence)
laihuanding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:education) (w:to sit the examination/for the examination) (d:<laihuan>, examination, and <ding>, to or for, written as one word: in order to sit the examination; {laihuanding alut} is one who goes in to sit the examination, and {laihuanding pelh} seems to mean stay away from it) (j:laihuan/ding) (r:zd:12403) (q:draft, low confidence)
laihuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:examination/exam) (d:<laihuan>, examination, with the noun ending {-na}: an examination, the sitting of an examination) (b:laihuan) (r:zd:12403/zd:24244) (q:draft)
laiin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time) (w:while/when/at the time of) (d:<lai> in its sense of a period of time and <in> written as one word, placed after a verb or a word of time: while, at the time when; {tua hun laiin} is at that time) (j:lai/in) (r:zd:23212/zd:9426/zd:20944) (q:draft)
laikhak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:letter) (d:a written message sent to someone; {laikhak sim} is read a letter) (s:lai/laikhakna) (r:24.29.29) (q:draft)
laikhaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:have a letter sent/send a letter) (d:<lai>, letter, <khak>, send, and the causative <sak> written as one word: send a letter or have one sent to someone) (j:lai/khak/sak) (r:zd:20181) (q:draft, low confidence)
laikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:a letter/a note/a piece of writing) (d:<lai> and <khat> written as one word: one letter, note or written message) (j:lai/khat) (r:zd:17547/zd:16095/zd:10660) (q:draft)
laikhetna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:printing/print) (d:<lai>, writing, and <khetna>, printing, written as one word: the printing of books and papers; {laikhetna set} is a printing press) (j:lai/khetna) (r:zd:16765/zd:21066) (q:draft)
laikhun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:bed/sickbed) (d:a bed, the place where one lies, in songs and elevated language; the everyday word is <lupna>) (r:zd:23902) (q:draft, low confidence)
laikipia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:be given a paper/be issued a document) (d:<lai> and <kipia> written as one word: be given a letter or written permit) (j:lai/kipia) (r:zd:17530) (q:draft, low confidence)
lailam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:literature/letters/learning) (d:<lai> and <lam> written as one word: the field of writing, books and learning; {lailam nasep} is literary work) (j:lai/lam) (r:zd:21066/zd:20587/zd:25916) (q:draft)
laileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (d:<lai>, here still, and <leh>, here if, written as one word after a verb: if one still does it, if it goes on) (j:lai/leh) (r:zd:21626/zd:19676/zd:15919) (q:draft)
laileng = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if we also/if we go on to) (d:<lai>, here still or further, and <leng>, if, written as one word after a verb: if we do this as well, if we go on doing it; the result follows) (r:zd:19676/zd:23361/zd:17226) (q:draft)
Lailet = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/education) (w:translate/translated by) (d:<lai>, writing, with <let> in the sense of turning into another language: translate a text; placed at the end of an article before the name of the translator, as {lai at} is placed before the name of the writer) (r:zd:17313/zd:23006) (q:draft)
Lailui = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Lailui) (d:village near Tedim in Chin State; written in brackets after a personal name it tells the home village) (r:ts:3160/zd:9266) (q:draft)
lailung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:heart/core/inmost part) (d:the middle or inmost part of a thing or of a person, the heart or mind; {ka lailung ah} is in my heart) (r:zd:25433/zd:24160) (q:draft, low confidence)
laimai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:page) (d:<lai>, writing, with <mai>, face: one side of a leaf of a book) (r:zd:22557/zd:20806/zd:21848) (q:draft)
laimalgawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:spelling) (d:<laimal>, written letter, with <gawm>, join: the way the letters of a word are put together, spelling) (s:malgawm) (r:zd:12353/zd:15489) (q:draft)
laimawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<lai>, still, and <mawk>, a word of surprise or emphasis, written as one word after a verb: still, even now, and more than one would expect) (j:lai/mawk) (r:zd:13100/zd:11736/zd:24594) (q:draft, low confidence)
Laimi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Lai people/Lai) (d:the Lai people of the Hakha and Falam areas of Chin State, one of the names used among the Chin peoples beside Zomi and Mizo) (r:zd:25097/zd:25329/zd:20148) (q:draft)
laimun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:place/spot/point) (d:a place or spot, also a place in a text or talk; {hih laimun ah} is at this place, at this point) (r:zd:25918/zd:25919) (q:draft)
lain = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take/collect/fetch) (d:<la>, take, and <in> written as one word: taking, or as a request with <hong>, come and take) (j:la/in) (r:zd:10892/zd:15800) (q:draft, low confidence)
lainatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:sympathise with/feel pity for/condole with) (d:<lainat>, feel pity, with the suffix <pih>: feel sorrow together with someone who suffers or mourns; {ki lainatpih} is said in messages of condolence) (b:lainat) (r:zd:16313/zd:12311/zd:19271) (q:draft)
lainatpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:sympathy/condolence/compassion) (d:<lainat>, feel compassion, with <pih>, together with, and the noun suffix <na>: feeling the pain of someone together with them; {lainatpihna lahna} is a showing of condolence to the bereaved) (b:lainat) (r:zd:11757) (q:draft)
laingek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/nature) (w:core/pith/heart/essence) (d:the soft inner part of a stem or trunk, and so the core or essential part of a matter) (r:zd:23298) (q:draft, low confidence)
laipai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:writing/written text/letter) (d:written letters or a written text; {laipai khat zong} with a negative is not even a single letter, of one who cannot read or of something done without any writing) (r:ts:7972/zd:22873) (q:draft, low confidence)
laipekin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:back when/long ago when) (d:<lai>, time, and <pekin>, long ago, written as one word after a describing word: back in the time when it was so) (j:lai/pekin) (r:zd:22287) (q:draft, low confidence)
laipen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:education/media) (w:the letter/the writing) (d:<lai>, a letter or piece of writing, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the letter, this writing, as the thing spoken about) (j:lai/pen) (r:zd:19934/zd:12876/zd:23883) (q:draft)
laiphah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:document/letter/paper) (d:a written paper handed in or laid before someone, such as a letter of support or the papers of a case; used by one writer) (r:zd:17860) (q:draft, low confidence)
laiphi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:sit an examination/take an exam) (d:<lai> and <phi> written as one word: sit a school examination; {tan 10 laiphi} is to sit the tenth standard examination) (j:lai/phi) (r:zd:23275/zd:12292) (q:draft)
laiphot = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:still for now/for the time being) (d:<lai>, still, and <phot>, for the time being, written as one word after a verb: the action goes on for now) (j:lai/phot) (r:zd:15397/zd:17213) (q:draft)
laipi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/education/work) (w:certificate/formal letter/official document) (d:<lai>, writing, with <pi>, great: a formal paper given or sent, named by the word before it, as {pahtawina laipi}, a certificate of honour, {ngetna laipi}, an application, {sapna laipi}, an invitation; not the conjunction {laipi}, while still) (r:zd:25268/zd:16686/zd:22948) (q:draft)
Laipian = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Laipian) (d:the religion founded by Pau Cin Hau and the script he made, {Laipian Lai}; also said of its followers and their church) (r:ts:3375/zd:23171) (q:draft)
laipil = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:education) (w:educated/learned/good at studies) (d:<lai>, letters, with <pil>, wise: learned from books, doing well at school; also a person who is so, as in {laipil khat}) (r:zd:21991/zd:22556/zd:24502) (q:draft)
laipilna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/book learning/schooling) (d:<lai>, letters, and <pilna>, knowledge, written as one word: learning gained from books and school) (j:lai/pilna) (r:zd:24963/zd:25115/zd:23112) (q:draft)
laipuak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:letter sent/delivered letter) (d:<lai>, letter, and <puak>, send or deliver, written as one word: a letter that is sent or brought to someone; also the act of delivering it) (j:lai/puak) (r:zd:17060/zd:11805) (q:draft, low confidence)
Laisaingtho = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (j:Laisiangtho) (r:zd:15810) (q:draft)
laisam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<lai>, still, with the particle <sam>, indeed, written as one word after a verb: still does so, to be sure; it grants a point, often before a contrast) (j:lai/sam) (r:zd:17097/zd:26495) (q:draft, low confidence)
laisan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/social) (w:laisan cloth) (d:in {puan laisan}, a traditional woven cloth of the <Zomi>, worn at celebrations and put on a person to honour him) (r:zd:19335) (q:draft, low confidence)
laisiah = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:as long as/as far as) (d:placed after a clause: for as long as, or to the extent that, it is so; {ahih theih laisiah} is as far as possible) (r:zd:24069/zd:23394/zd:16202) (q:draft)
laisiam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:education) (w:educated/learned/good at study) (d:<lai>, writing or study, with <siam>, skilled: learned, well educated or good at school work; also a noun, an educated person) (r:zd:9134/zd:20125/zd:21617) (q:draft)
laisiamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/learning/scholarship) (d:<laisiam>, educated, with the noun suffix <na>: being educated, skill in study) (b:laisiam) (r:zd:23022/zd:21105) (q:draft)
Laisiangtho = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Bible/Scripture/Holy Scripture) (d:<lai>, writing, and <siangtho>, holy, written as one word: the Bible) (j:lai/siangtho) (r:zd:20798/zd:15810/zd:23191) (q:draft)
laisim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:read/study) (d:<lai>, writing, with <sim>, read: read a text; {laisim ngei lo} is never having studied) (s:sim) (q:draft)
laisimbu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:textbook/reader/primer) (d:<laisim>, read, with the word for book as in <laibu>: a book for learning to read or for study at school) (r:zd:25390/ts:3375/zd:22391) (q:draft)
laisimin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:reading/studying) (d:<laisim> and <in> written as one word: reading or studying, and; the action joined to the verb that follows) (b:laisim) (j:laisim/in) (r:zd:16779/zd:24276) (q:draft)
laisimlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:not read/not study) (d:<laisim>, read or study, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not reading, not studying) (j:laisim/lo) (r:zd:22474/zd:11918) (q:draft)
laisimmi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:reader) (d:<laisim>, read, with <mi>, person: a person who reads, one who has the habit of reading) (j:laisim/mi) (r:zd:24244) (q:draft)
laisimna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:reading/study/education) (d:<laisim>, read or study, with the noun suffix <na>: the reading of books, and study or schooling as a whole) (b:laisim) (r:zd:22680/zd:11891/zd:21617) (q:draft)
laisimte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:readers/students) (d:<laisim>, read or study, with the plural <te>, written as one word: those who read, the readers of a text, and also those who study) (b:laisim) (j:laisim/te) (r:zd:19139/zd:12436/zd:16860) (q:draft)
laisin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:study/schooling/learning) (d:<lai>, writing, and <sin>, learn, written as one word: studying, going to school; {laisin kum} is a school year) (j:lai/sin) (r:zd:10717/zd:24429/zd:23198) (q:draft)
Laisingtho = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (j:Laisiangtho) (r:zd:17488) (q:draft)
laisinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/schooling/study/learning) (d:<lai>, letters, with <sinna>, learning: study at school and what is gained by it; {laisinna sang} is a school) (r:zd:21529/zd:16415/zd:21168) (q:draft)
laisinte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:students/learners/pupils) (d:<laisin>, study, with the plural <te>, written as one word: those who study, the learners in a class, set against <laihilhte>, the teachers) (b:laisin) (j:laisin/te) (r:zd:25687) (q:draft)
laisuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:sign/notice/label) (d:writing put up or printed on something to be read, such as a signboard, a banner or the label on a bottle) (r:zd:21067/zd:16947) (q:draft, low confidence)
laisung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:education/media) (w:in the writing/in the document) (d:<lai>, writing, and <sung>, in, written as one word: in this article, letter or report) (j:lai/sung) (r:zd:20181/zd:20649) (q:draft)
laisungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:education) (w:in writing/in the book/in the letter) (d:<lai>, writing, and <sungah>, inside, written as one word: in a book, letter or other writing) (j:lai/sungah) (r:zd:21085/zd:21989/zd:21900) (q:draft)
laita = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday/religion) (w:still/yet) (d:<lai.3>, still, written together with <ta.2> after a verb, not {laita} the middle one: the action goes on; {hong zang semsem laita hen} is a blessing, may he go on using you more and more) (r:zd:20639/zd:22383/zd:12882) (q:draft)
laitaan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (j:laitan) (r:zd:24153/zd:24253) (q:draft)
laitakpen = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time) (w:at the very moment/while) (d:<laitak> and <pen> written as one word: the very moment when something was happening, taken as the topic of the sentence) (j:laitak/pen) (r:zd:11472/zd:16731) (q:draft)
laitaktawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:with the very time of) (d:<laitak> and <tawh> written as one word, before <kituak>: something falls together with the very time when another thing is going on) (j:laitak/tawh) (r:zd:11236/zd:22873) (q:draft)
laitakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:those currently doing) (d:<laitak>, at the very time, with the plural <te>, written as one word after a verb: those who are doing it at present, as {sem laitakte}, those now working or in office) (j:laitak/te) (r:zd:24466/zd:24126) (q:draft)
laitakzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:even while/also at the moment when) (d:<laitak>, at the very time, and <zong>, also, written as one word: the very moment when something happens, as well) (j:laitak/zong) (r:zd:14616/zd:17419) (q:draft)
laitam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:education) (w:much reading matter/many books) (d:<lai> and <tam> written as one word: a lot of writing, much to read; elsewhere the same spelling is <lai>, still, before the particle <tam>) (j:lai/tam) (r:zd:24082) (q:draft, low confidence)
laitan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/level of education/schooling) (d:the level of schooling a person has reached, formal education; {laitan sang} is a high level of education) (r:zd:21991/zd:24471/zd:17971) (q:draft)
laitawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:education/social) (w:in writing/by letter) (d:<lai> and <tawh> written as one word: in writing, by a written document; after the name of a language, in that language or script) (j:lai/tawh) (r:zd:14910/zd:15274/zd:25022) (q:draft)
laithai = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:playing cards/cards) (d:playing cards, in {laithai kap}, play cards; named beside drinking as a bad habit that harms marriage and keeps people from worship) (r:zd:9436/zd:9453) (q:draft, low confidence)
laithei = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:education) (w:educated/literate/learned) (d:of people today, able to read and write or well schooled, not the scribe of the Gospels; often beside <laisiam> or after <khangno>, and also a noun, an educated person) (r:zd:22203/zd:19676/zd:9240) (q:draft)
laithupi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:important document/important paper) (d:<lai> and <thupi> written as one word: an important paper or document, often beside the English word Document) (j:lai/thupi) (r:zd:20320/zd:22162) (q:draft)
laito = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:post/mail/post office) (d:the postal service by which letters and parcels are sent; {laito panin khak} is send by post, and {laito zum} is the post office) (r:zd:23022/zd:11954) (q:draft)
Laituite = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Laitui people) (d:the people of the village <Laitui>) (b:Laitui) (r:zd:23489/zd:20406) (q:draft)
laitung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/everyday) (j:leitung) (r:zd:15839) (q:draft, low confidence)
laiuh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/social) (w:their writing/their script/their language) (d:<lai>, writing, and <uh> written as one word after <a>: {a laiuh} is their own writing or written language) (j:lai/uh) (r:zd:23204/zd:12867) (q:draft)
laiun = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:while they/while you) (d:<lai>, while, and <un>, the plural marker with <in>, written as one word after a verb: while they, or you, several people, are doing it) (j:lai/un) (r:zd:9448/zd:9452) (q:draft, low confidence)
laivuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:examination/exam) (d:<lai>, writing, with <vuan>: a school examination, and to sit one; {Tan 10 laivuan} is the grade ten examination) (r:zd:22683/zd:25666/zd:11748) (q:draft)
laivuanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:sit an examination/take an exam) (d:<laivuan>, sit an examination, and <ding>, will, written as one word: to sit an examination, going to sit an examination; also the examination that is to be held) (j:laivuan/ding) (r:zd:11392/zd:18012/zd:11748) (q:draft)
laivuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:examination/exam) (d:a written examination at school or university; {Tan 10 laivuanna} is the tenth standard, matriculation, examination) (r:zd:15459/zd:25630) (q:draft)
laivuanpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:final examination/final exam) (d:<laivuan>, examination, with {-pi}, great: the main examination at the end of the school year) (b:laivuan) (r:zd:22683/zd:19342) (q:draft)
laizang = (i:4) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:actually/even) (d:after a verb at the end of a clause it shows surprise that someone goes so far as to say or do the thing, as in {ong ci laizang hi}, he actually said to me; not the place word of the other senses) (r:zd:22773/zd:22649/zd:17224) (q:draft, low confidence)
Laizo = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Laizo) (d:name of the Chin people of the Falam area and of their language, also called Falam; {Laizo pau} is the Laizo language) (r:zd:22334/zd:26700) (q:draft)
laizom = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:full sibling/blood brother or sister/kin) (d:a brother or sister born of the same mother, often <sanggam laizom>, {unau laizom} or {pianpih laizom}; in a wider sense fellow members of one people, as {Zomi laizom}) (s:sanggam) (r:zd:12998/zd:23717/zd:25866) (q:draft)
laizomte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:kinsfolk/brothers and sisters/relatives/brethren) (d:plural of <laizom>, one joined by the same navel cord: brothers and sisters, and more widely relatives or fellow members of the people, often said with <sanggam>) (r:zd:25287/ts:1343) (q:draft)
laizomteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:all the brothers and sisters/all the kin) (d:<laizom>, full sibling, with <teng>, all, written as one word: all the brothers and sisters, all who are of one kin; found in songs) (j:laizom/teng) (r:zd:17309) (q:draft, low confidence)
laizong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:education) (w:writing also/letter also) (d:<lai>, writing, letter or studies, and <zong>, also, written as one word) (j:lai/zong) (r:zd:19662/zd:18244) (q:draft)
lak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take) (d:take something into the hand or into one's keeping. The form of <la>, take, used before endings and other words) (a:pia) (q:example wanted)
lak = (i:4) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:show/point out) (d:let someone see or know something, show it; {hong lak} is show us; a different word from {lak}, take, and the same as <lakh>) (r:zd:12112/zd:8667) (q:draft)
laka khat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:one of/one among) (d:<laka>, among, and <khat>, one: placed after a plural noun phrase, usually ending in <te> or {te'}, one of those named; often followed by {ahi hi}, is) (r:zd:9445/zd:13340/zd:23137) (q:draft)
lakaa = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:among/in the midst of) (d:<lak>, midst, with <aa> written for <ah>: another spelling of <lakah>, among) (j:lak/aa) (r:zd:17060/zd:20176) (q:draft)
lakah kihel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be among/be one of/be counted among) (d:<lakah>, among, and <kihel.2>, be included: after a plural noun, be one of that group or be counted in it; with <sak>, {lakah kihel sak}, count someone among) (r:zd:21978/zd:9253/zd:24227) (q:draft)
lakahzong = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:also among/even among) (d:<lakah>, among, and <zong>, also, written as one word: among those people or things too) (j:lakah/zong) (r:zd:12656/zd:19586) (q:draft)
lakam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:poetic word/poetic language/poetic diction) (d:<la>, song, with <kam>, word: the special words and phrases used in Zomi songs and poetry, different from everyday speech) (r:zd:15396/zd:23651) (q:draft)
lakamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/media) (w:poetic words/poetic expressions) (d:plural of <lakam>, the special words of Zomi songs and poetry) (b:lakam) (r:zd:24393) (q:draft)
lakbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:take more/take in addition) (d:<lak>, take, with <beh>, here in addition and not clan: take more besides what was taken before, as hire more workers or capture more ground) (b:lak) (r:zd:11602/zd:10702) (q:draft)
lakdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:way of taking/way of interpreting) (d:<lak>, take, and <dan>, way, written as one word: the way something is taken, and so how a text is understood or how a person is taken on) (j:lak/dan) (r:zd:15274) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to take/to be taken) (d:<lak>, take, and <ding> written as one word: that is to be taken or for taking; {Refugee lakding} is the taking in of refugees) (j:lak/ding) (r:zd:15465/zd:22159/zd:11011) (q:draft)
lakh = (i:1) (t:num) (f:work) (w:hundred thousand/lakh) (d:one hundred thousand, used in counting money and people) (o:Hindi, lakh) (r:zd:17675/zd:16754) (q:draft)
lakh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:show/display) (d:another spelling of <lak>, show, let something be seen; compare <lah> and <kilak>) (r:zd:25025) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media/everyday) (w:one song/a song) (d:<la> and <khat> written as one word: one song; in the pair {thukhat lakhat}, any matter that comes up, something or other) (j:la/khat) (r:zd:17047/zd:12394) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakhia = (i:4) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:capture/seize/take) (d:in war news, take a town, camp or post from the enemy, often with <zo> or <khin>; the object is a place and not a thing lifted out) (r:ts:4892/ts:3921/ts:5105) (q:draft)
lakhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to take out/to collect/will take out) (d:<lakhia>, take out, and <ding>, to or will, written as one word; with <in> after it, in order to take out or fetch) (j:lakhia/ding) (r:zd:12575) (q:draft)
lakhiapah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take out at once/pull out at once) (d:<lakhia>, take out, and <pah>, at once, written as one word) (j:lakhia/pah) (r:zd:19536/zd:12913) (q:draft)
lakhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:capture/seize/take) (d:form of <lakhia>, take out, used before <ding>, <uh> and similar words, also written <lakkhiat>; in war news, take a camp or a town from the enemy) (b:lakhia) (r:ts:8561/ts:5396) (q:draft)
lakhiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to take out/can remove/can retrieve) (d:<lakhia>, take out, and <thei>, able, written as one word: manage to get a person or thing out of where it is) (j:lakhia/thei) (r:zd:19692/zd:13016) (q:draft)
lakhiazo = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:capture/seize/take) (d:in war news, succeed in taking a camp, hill or town from the enemy; the place is named before {lakhiazo}, mostly followed by <uh> or <ta>) (r:ts:4369/ts:9093/ts:10771) (q:draft)
lakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have taken/have received) (d:<la>, take, and <khin>, already, written as one word: have already taken or received; {pension lakhin} is retired, having taken the pension) (j:la/khin) (r:zd:12876/zd:16900/zd:16640) (q:draft)
lakhs = (i:1) (t:num) (f:work) (w:lakh/hundred thousand) (d:a hundred thousand, used in counting Myanmar kyats; the English plural form stands after any number) (s:tengh/tulza) (o:English, lakh) (r:zd:19166/zd:19210) (q:draft)
lakhui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:album/song album) (d:a set of recorded songs released together; often followed by the English word, {lakhui album}) (r:zd:20920/zd:16442/zd:21070) (q:draft)
lakhum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:record a song/make a recording) (d:record songs, as in a studio or on a cassette, from <la>, song, and <khum>, put in; also the recording that is made) (r:zd:9229/ts:9846) (q:draft)
lakhun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/work/time) (w:harvest time/time of gathering) (d:<lak> and <hun> written as one word: the time when a crop is taken in, or when something is received) (j:lak/hun) (r:zd:20747) (q:draft)
lakkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to show/show) (d:<lak>, show, with the verb particle <kha>, written as one word; the sentences do not make clear whether the first part is show or take) (j:lak/kha) (r:zd:12280) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:take together/gather/capture together) (d:<lak>, take, and <khawm> written as one word: take or win something jointly, or bring items together in one collection) (j:lak/khawm) (r:zd:11917/zd:11157) (q:draft)
lakkhiat = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:capture/seize/take) (d:take a camp, base or town from the enemy in war; the object is a place such as <Camp> or <khuapi>, and {lakkhiat kik} is retake) (r:ts:5635/ts:6108/ts:7798) (q:draft)
lakkhiatna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:capture/seizure) (d:the taking of a military camp or base from the enemy in war news, after {camp} or <galphual>, as in {SAC galphual lakkhiatna}; not the taking of a thing out of a place) (r:ts:8880/ts:4528) (q:draft)
lakkhiatsa = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:captured/seized/taken) (d:<lakkhiat.2>, capture, with {-sa}, already done: of a camp, base or town that a force has taken from the enemy in war; the one who took it stands before it, as in {CDNF te' lakkhiatsa}) (r:ts:4162/ts:3687/ts:10491) (q:draft)
lakkhiattheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to take out/can remove) (d:<lakkhiat>, take out, and <theih>, be able, written as one word; {lakkhiattheih nadingin} is so that it can be taken out) (j:lakkhiat/theih) (r:zd:12212/zd:17100) (q:draft)
lakkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:revoke/have taken back/withdraw) (d:<lakkik>, take back, with the causative <sak> written as one word: cause to be taken back; with <ki> before it, of a licence, be revoked) (j:lakkik/sak) (r:zd:15408) (q:draft)
lakkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:need to take/have to take) (d:<lak>, take, and <kul>, must, written as one word: it is necessary to take or get something) (j:lak/kul) (r:zd:17000/zd:12600) (q:draft)
lakkullo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:need not take/without needing) (d:<lak>, take, with <kullo>, need not, written as one word: without having to take or obtain something, as a visa) (j:lak/kullo) (r:zd:12229/zd:11736) (q:draft)
laklak = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:again and again/quickly) (d:descriptive word placed after a verb for a quick, sudden movement or response that comes again and again, as of flames that flash, {tang laklak}, a head that turns, {luhei laklak}, or a person who answers back at once, {dawng laklak}) (r:zd:22658/zd:19676/zd:23489) (q:draft, low confidence)
laklawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unfinished/incomplete/halfway/half-done) (d:left in the middle before it is complete, of work, schooling or talk; of a person, half-taught or half-grown, as in {mipil laklawh}) (r:zd:26565/zd:22773/zd:23591) (q:draft)
laklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not show) (d:<lak>, show, with <lo>, not, written as one word: not show, as an illness that shows no signs or a driver who gives no signal; {serious laklo} is not take seriously) (j:lak/lo) (r:zd:24492/zd:19427) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not take) (d:<lak>, take, and <loh>, not, written as one word: not take, without taking; {summet lakloh in} is without taking interest) (j:lak/loh) (r:zd:24616/zd:19239) (q:draft)
laknopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:desire to take/wish to take on) (d:<laknop>, want to take, with the noun suffix <na>: the wish to take something, to take on a duty or to capture a place) (b:laknop) (r:zd:11206/ts:5635) (q:draft)
lakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:show at once) (d:<lak>, show, and <pah> written as one word: show something or show oneself without delay; {zato ki lakpah} is go to be seen at the hospital at once) (j:lak/pah) (r:zd:20961/zd:12727) (q:draft)
lakpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/nature) (w:the very midst/the middle) (d:<lak>, midst, with the ending {-pi}, great: right in the middle of a thing, as of the dark or of a cliff) (b:lak) (r:zd:14804) (q:draft, low confidence)
laksakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:will be taken away/will seize) (d:<laksak>, take away from, and <ding>, will, written as one word; after <ki> it is passive, will be taken away) (j:laksak/ding) (r:zd:20367) (q:draft)
laksakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:take back/repossess/withdraw) (d:<laksak>, take away from, and <kik>, back, written as one word: take back from someone what was given or granted) (j:laksak/kik) (r:zd:16317) (q:draft)
laksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:plan to take/try to take/be about to take) (d:<lak>, take, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: plan, try or be about to take, take in or capture; in headlines of a country that plans to take in refugees) (j:lak/sawm) (r:zd:15465/zd:15116/zd:11924) (q:draft)
laksawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:take over/adopt/borrow/copy) (d:<lak>, take, with <sawn>, on: take over from another what is then used or passed on, as a custom from another people or lines from a book; the source takes {tung panin}) (j:lak/sawn) (r:zd:23936/zd:20576) (q:draft, low confidence)
laksiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:take wisely/know how to take/receive well) (d:<lak>, take, with <siam>, skilled, written as one word: know how to take or accept something and make good use of it) (j:lak/siam) (r:zd:17221/zd:14885) (q:draft)
laktheihding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/education) (w:that can be taken/to be able to take) (d:<laktheih> and <ding> written as one word: something that can or should be taken, as {Lesson laktheihding}, a lesson to be learned, and leave that may be taken) (j:laktheih/ding) (r:zd:12099/zd:13222) (q:draft)
lakzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:capture/win/obtain) (d:<lak>, take, and <zawh>, be able, written as one word: manage to take, as capture a place, win the hearts of people or obtain a degree) (j:lak/zawh) (r:zd:24116/zd:19676/zd:21085) (q:draft)
lakzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:way of taking/method of taking) (d:<lak>, take, and <zia>, way, written as one word: the way something is taken or obtained; {action lakzia} is the way action is taken) (j:lak/zia) (r:zd:21624/zd:20959) (q:draft)
lala = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:repeatedly/again and again/on and on) (d:placed after a verb: do the action over and over or without restraint; {tai lala} is keep scolding) (r:zd:24072/zd:18023) (q:draft, low confidence)
lala = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep taking/take again and again) (d:the verb for take said twice: take one after another, take up repeatedly) (r:zd:22742) (q:draft, low confidence)
lalna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/social) (w:migration/immigration/moving) (d:<lal>, move to live elsewhere, with the noun ending {-na}: moving from one place or country to live in another) (b:lal) (r:zd:11697/zd:23479) (q:draft)
lalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not take/not charge) (d:the verb take, whose other form is <lak>, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not take, not accept; {sum lalo} is without taking money) (j:la/lo) (r:zd:15453/zd:12487/zd:19939) (q:draft)
Lalta = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel/social) (w:Lalta) (d:a Zomi village, named as the home village of persons and in the name of its village association; said to be in the Tedim area of Chin State) (r:zd:15275) (q:draft, low confidence)
lalui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:old song) (d:<la>, song, and <lui>, old, written as one word: an old song, a song of former times) (a:lathak) (j:la/lui) (r:zd:16939/zd:15652) (q:draft)
lam = (i:4) (t:n) (f:work/education) (w:field/area/side/matter) (d:a field of work or study or one side of a matter, placed after the noun that names it: {upadi lam} is the field of law, {zato lam} medicine, {politic lam} politics; not a direction in space) (r:ts:3164/ts:8105) (q:draft)
lam phawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:realize that/be aware that/bear in mind that) (d:<lam>, way, used here as the fact that, and <phawk>, remember or be aware: realize or keep in mind that something is so; follows a clause that ends in <ahih> or another verb, and is often closed by a hortative, as {lam phawk ni}, let us bear in mind that, or by <tawntung>, always) (r:zd:9445/zd:21340/zd:25891) (q:draft)
lam zuanin = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:travel/everyday) (w:toward/towards/in the direction of/bound for) (d:<lam>, direction, and <zuanin>, heading for: placed after a place name or a noun of place and before a verb of movement, toward that place) (r:zd:26708/zd:20083/zd:9254) (q:draft)
lamaa = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:of the side/on the side of) (d:<lam>, side, and <aa>, belonging to, written as one word: that of a certain side or kind) (j:lam/aa) (r:zd:22922) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamah = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:in the field of/as regards/in terms of) (d:after a noun that names a subject or quality and not a place: in the matter of, as far as that is concerned, as in {music lamah}, in music; no movement and no location is meant) (r:zd:22341/ts:3125/zd:24176) (q:draft)
lamal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:lyrics/words of a song) (d:<la>, song, with <mal>, a single word: the words of a song, as distinct from {la-aw}, its tune) (r:zd:9258/zd:16337/zd:14789) (q:draft)
lamalte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:lyrics/words of a song) (d:<la>, song, and <malte>, words, written as one word: the words of a song or hymn, as distinct from its tune) (j:la/malte) (r:zd:9220/zd:9228) (q:draft)
lamasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take first/put first) (d:<la>, take, with <masa>, first, written as one word: take something before anything else, give it the first place) (j:la/masa) (r:zd:19455/zd:20254) (q:draft)
lambeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/home) (w:build in addition/build more) (d:<lam>, build, with <beh>, in addition: build more of something beside what there is) (r:zd:16619/zd:20315) (q:draft, low confidence)
lambek = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:only the side of/only toward) (d:<lam>, side or direction, with <bek>, only, written as one word after a noun or clause: only on that side, only in that direction or matter) (j:lam/bek) (r:zd:25919) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:around/toward/about the time of) (d:<lam>, side, and <ciang> written as one word after a word of time, often with <in>: at about that time; {a nung lamciang} is later on) (j:lam/ciang) (r:zd:22371/zd:25221) (q:draft)
lamdan = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:differ/be different) (d:short spelling of <lamdang> after the prefix <ki>, written {ki lamdan} for <kilamdang>, differ from one another; with <na>, the difference between things, not wonderful) (r:zd:24641/zd:16994/zd:25680) (q:draft)
lamdan = (i:3) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:way of building/building method) (d:<lam>, build, with <dan>, manner, written as one word after <inn>, house: how a house is built; not the short form of <lamdang>) (r:zd:18136) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamdang = (i:4) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:strange/wonderful/unusual/amazing) (d:placed after a noun, describing a thing that is out of the ordinary: {aksi lamdang}, a strange star, and {na lamdang}, a wonder or miracle; the other senses are the feeling of surprise itself) (r:zd:26385/zd:9235) (q:draft)
lamdang kasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I am amazed/I find it strange/I wonder) (d:<lamdang>, strange or wonderful, and <kasa>, I feel: the expression {lamdang sa}, find something strange or marvellous, in the first person; the thing wondered at stands before it) (r:zd:10973/zd:21034) (q:draft)
lamdang kisa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be astonished/cause amazement/be thought strange) (d:<lamdang>, surprise, and <kisa>, the form with {ki-} of <sa>, feel: people find it strange, there is astonishment; said of an event without naming who is surprised, often closing a headline, while {lamdang sa} names the person who is surprised) (r:zd:25227/zd:21042) (q:draft)
lamdangkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:a strange one/an unusual one) (d:<lamdang> and <khat> written as one word, placed after a noun: a strange or unusual one, as in {ganhing lamdangkhat}, a strange animal) (j:lamdang/khat) (r:zd:15647/zd:21291) (q:draft)
lamdanglo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not strange/not surprising/normal) (d:<lamdang> and <lo> written as one word: not strange, nothing unusual) (j:lamdang/lo) (r:zd:24029/zd:17838) (q:draft)
lamdanglo = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:no different/the same) (d:after <ki>, as in {ki lamdanglo}: does not differ, is no different from) (j:lamdang/lo) (r:zd:11587/zd:15056) (q:draft)
lamdangtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/religion) (w:wonderfully/strangely/amazingly) (d:<lamdang>, be wonderful or strange, and <tak> written as one word: in a wonderful or strange way, usually with <in>; before or after a noun, wonderful, strange) (j:lamdang/tak) (r:zd:21948/zd:20829/zd:24542) (q:draft)
lamdanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:difference/distinctiveness/strangeness) (d:<lamdang> with the noun suffix {-na}: what makes a person or thing different or unusual; {ki lamdanna} is the difference between two) (b:lamdang) (r:zd:25919/zd:11447/zd:20790) (q:draft)
lamdawt = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:shortcut/short cut) (d:a shorter way that cuts across, and so a quick or easy way to get something without the proper effort; {lamdawt tawn} is take a shortcut) (r:zd:26645/zd:23590/zd:26310) (q:draft)
lamenlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not expect/not hope for) (d:<lamen>, expect, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not expect that something will happen) (j:lamen/lo) (r:zd:12998/zd:20252) (q:draft)
lametbei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:hopeless/despairing/without hope) (d:<lamet>, hope, with <bei>, come to an end: having no hope left; also as a noun, hopelessness, despair) (j:lamet/bei) (r:zd:19975/zd:21384) (q:draft)
lametloh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unexpected/unexpectedly) (d:<lamet> and <loh> written as one word: not expected; {lametloh laitak in} is at a moment when no one expects it, {lametloh in} unexpectedly) (j:lamet/loh) (r:zd:14709/zd:22717) (q:draft)
lametlohpi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:unexpectedly/suddenly/by surprise) (d:<lamet>, expect, and <lohpi>, without, written as one word: without its being expected, usually followed by <in>) (j:lamet/lohpi) (r:zd:14776/zd:19197) (q:draft)
lamgui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:line dance/chain of dancers) (d:a line of people dancing together at a feast; {lamgui laam} is dance in such a line and {lamgui kai} is draw the line along; the first part is the word written <laam>, dance) (r:zd:15996) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:property/possessions/belongings) (d:found in the pair {neih leh lamh}, what one has and owns; elsewhere in the articles it is part of personal names) (r:zd:23594) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamhilh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:guide/show the way/direct) (d:the verb beside the noun {lamhilh}, a guide: show someone the way or the right course; before <ding> and <dingin>, as in {lamhilh ding makai}, a leader to guide one) (r:zd:20787/zd:23419) (q:draft)
lamhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (j:lamna) (r:zd:23667/zd:17060) (q:draft)
lamhoih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:good road/good way) (d:<lam> and <hoih> written as one word: a good road, or a good way of doing something) (j:lam/hoih) (r:zd:15586/zd:21717) (q:draft)
lamhon = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/travel) (w:open the way/make a way) (d:<lam> and <hon> written as one word: open a way for someone; {Pasian lamhon sakna} is the way that God opened) (j:lam/hon) (r:zd:13020/zd:21321) (q:draft)
lamhong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/religion) (w:the way for us) (d:<lam>, way, and <hong>, toward the speaker, written as one word before a verb: show us or open for us the way) (j:lam/hong) (r:zd:20092) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamhonsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/travel) (w:opening of a way/opportunity) (d:<lam> way and <honsakna> opening written as one word: the opening of a way for someone, said mostly of God making it possible to go abroad, as in {Pasian lamhonsakna tawh}) (j:lam/honsakna) (r:zd:22664/zd:25060) (q:draft)
lamkaai = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel/politics) (w:on the side of/lying on the side of) (d:placed after the name of a country: the part that lies on that side of the border, as {India lamkaai} and {Kawlgam lamkaai}; the first part is <lam>, side; a dictionary gives the word as leader, which the sentences do not show) (r:zd:16121/zd:21003) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamkaal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (j:lamkal) (r:zd:19435/zd:20545) (q:draft)
lamkabom = (i:2) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:intersection/junction/crossroads) (d:the place where two or more roads cross, with traffic lights and waiting vehicles, rather than an open square where people gather; {meileng lamkabom} is a railway crossing) (r:zd:13318/zd:23957/zd:23556) (q:draft)
lamkan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:cross the road/cross the street) (d:<lam>, road, with <kan>, step over or cross, as in <kantan>, written as one word: go across a road; {khetawh lamkan} is cross on foot) (j:lam/kan) (r:zd:11710/zd:14676/zd:15846) (q:draft)
lamkanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:crossing/road crossing) (d:a place for crossing a road, from <lamkan>, cross the road, with the ending {-na}; {lamkanna lei} is a footbridge over a road) (b:lamkan) (r:zd:15834/zd:14676) (q:draft)
lamkawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:bend in the road/curve/turn) (d:<lam>, road, and <kawi>, bent, written as one word: a place where the road bends) (j:lam/kawi) (r:zd:15693/zd:11265) (q:draft)
lamkhakcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:block the road/obstruct the road) (d:<lam>, road, and <khakcip>, block, written as one word: lie or stand across the road so that nothing can pass) (j:lam/khakcip) (r:zd:18028/zd:14904) (q:draft)
lamkhang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/nature) (w:lower roadside/downhill side of the road) (d:the side of a road that falls away below it, the opposite of the upper side; {lamsak lamkhang} is both sides of the road) (r:zd:14824/zd:17952) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamkhanglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/nature) (w:downhill side of the road/lower roadside) (d:<lamkhang>, the lower side of a road, with <lam>, side or direction, written as one word; with <ah> it says a vehicle went off the road down the slope) (j:lamkhang/lam) (r:zd:21020/zd:17689) (q:draft)
lamkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:one side/one way) (d:<lam> and <khat> written as one word: one side or one point of view; {lamkhat panin} is in one way, on the one hand) (j:lam/khat) (r:zd:20818/zd:22557) (q:draft)
lamkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:dance together) (d:<laam>, dance, here spelled with one a, and <khawm>, together, written as one word: dance together with others) (j:laam/khawm) (r:zd:25624/zd:24594) (q:draft)
lamkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:build/erect/establish) (d:<lam>, build, and <khia>, out, written as one word: build something up so that it stands, a building or a state) (j:lam/khia) (r:zd:15874/zd:16901) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamkhialhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:going astray/wrong course/error) (d:<lamkhial>, take the wrong way, with the noun ending {-na}: a taking of the wrong way, by a person, a people or a system) (b:lamkhial) (r:zd:15919/zd:16245) (q:draft)
lamkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:build/build up/establish) (d:put up a building, or set up a state or a union; the form used before <ding> and <nading> and as a noun, as in {te ii lamkhiat}, what they built) (r:zd:21050/zd:16901) (q:draft)
lamkhopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/work) (w:building together/joint construction) (d:<lam>, build, with <khopna>, doing together, written as one word: the building of something as a shared work; {Biakinn lamkhopna} is the joint building of a church) (j:lam/khopna) (r:zd:13020) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamkikding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:will rebuild/to be rebuilt) (d:<lamkik>, build again, and <ding>, the marker of what is to come, written as one word: will build again, is to be rebuilt) (j:lamkik/ding) (r:zd:19508/zd:11383) (q:draft)
lamkim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:midway/halfway/on the way) (d:the middle of a journey, a point partway along the road; often paired with <lampam> for along the way and by the roadside) (r:zd:15484) (q:draft)
lamkiu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:street corner/road bend/roadside) (d:<lam>, road, with <kiu>, corner: the corner or bend of a road, also the edge of the road where a vehicle stops) (r:zd:17138/zd:14852) (q:draft)
lamlai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:roadway/middle of the road) (d:<lam>, way, with <lai>, middle: the road itself or a point along the way, mostly as {lamlai ah}, on the road, midway) (r:zd:17992/zd:24164) (q:draft)
lamlai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work) (w:under construction/being built) (d:<lam>, here build, and <lai>, here still, written as one word: still being built; {a ki lamlai in} is while it was being built) (r:zd:17005) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamlakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/social) (w:guidance/leading/direction) (d:<lamlak>, guide, with the noun suffix {-na}: the act of showing the way, guidance) (b:lamlak) (r:zd:26565/zd:15810) (q:draft)
lamlam = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:whichever way/wherever) (d:<lam>, way or direction, said twice: whichever way, wherever; after a noun in {-na} and before <ah>, as {i deihna lamlam ah}, in whichever direction is wanted) (r:zd:21246/zd:25919/zd:23086) (q:draft)
lamlam = (i:3) (t:v) (f:social) (w:dance on/keep dancing) (d:<lam>, dance, said twice for dancing that goes on and on; not the word for birds circling) (r:ts:301/zd:15264) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamlamah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:whichever way/wherever/in whatever direction) (d:<lamlam>, whichever way, and <ah>, written as one word after a verb or a noun in {-na}: in whatever direction something goes or someone says) (j:lamlam/ah) (r:zd:19242/zd:14861) (q:draft)
lamlang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:side of the road/roadside) (d:<lam>, road, and <lang>, side, written as one word: one side of the road, or the other side of it; a vehicle swerves or overturns {lamlang ah}) (j:lam/lang) (r:zd:17952/zd:11579) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:side and) (d:<lam>, side, and <leh>, and, written as one word: after a noun, on that side and, linking it to the next) (j:lam/leh) (r:zd:19257) (q:draft, low confidence)
lammah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/politics) (w:that very side/the side of) (d:<lam>, side or direction, and the stressing <mah> written as one word after a name: the side of that one and no other) (j:lam/mah) (r:zd:19239) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamman = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:right way/right path/true course) (d:<lam>, way, and <man>, true or right, written as one word: the right way to go or to live, the proper course) (j:lam/man) (r:zd:20410/zd:12121/zd:26658) (q:draft)
lamnuai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:lower road/lower side of the road) (d:<lam> and <nuai> written as one word: the road or the ground below, set against <lamtung>, the road above, in a town built on a slope) (j:lam/nuai) (r:zd:12765) (q:draft, low confidence)
lampai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:walk/travel) (d:<lam>, road, and <pai>, go, also used as a noun, journey) (s:khualzin) (q:draft)
lampam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:roadside/wayside) (d:<lam>, road, with <pam>, side: the side of the road; {lamkim lampam} is all along the road, and of news, from here and there by hearsay) (j:lam/pam) (r:zd:21869/zd:19626) (q:draft, low confidence)
lampan = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:from the side of/on the part of/from) (d:<lam>, side or direction, and <pan>, from, written as one word: from the side of, on the part of, as regards) (j:lam/pan) (r:zd:15992/zd:21050/zd:16442) (q:draft)
lampanin = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday/politics) (w:from the side of/on the part of) (d:<lam>, side or direction, and <panin>, from, written as one word and placed after a noun: from that side or direction, on the part of that person or body) (j:lam/panin) (r:zd:20676/zd:18112/zd:12938) (q:draft)
lampawl = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/time) (w:about/around/among) (d:<lam> and <pawl> written as one word after a word of time or quality: around that time, or of about that kind, as {zankim lampawl}, around midnight, and {a sau lampawl}, among the longer ones) (j:lam/pawl) (r:zd:12155/zd:24029) (q:draft, low confidence)
lampen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<lam>, way, side or aspect, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: as for the way, the side or the matter of what is named before it) (j:lam/pen) (r:zd:11887/zd:11798) (q:draft)
lampi = (i:3) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:road) (b:lam)
lampi maan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:right path/right way) (d:<lampi>, road, and <maan>, true or right: the right path, said of right conduct in life and not of a road; the object of verbs of walking, leading and teaching, as in {lampi maan tot}, walk the right path, and {lampi maan hilh}, show the right way) (r:zd:23191/zd:26645/zd:23301) (q:draft)
lampialkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:go off the road/derail/veer off) (d:<lampial>, leave the way, and <khia>, out, written as one word: of a car, train or aircraft, leave the road, the rails or the runway) (j:lampial/khia) (r:zd:20272/zd:15405) (q:draft)
lampigei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:roadside/side of the road) (d:<lampi>, road, and <gei>, side, written as one word: the side of the road, beside the road) (j:lampi/gei) (r:zd:17924/zd:20008/zd:19581) (q:draft)
lampikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:a road/one way/one path) (d:<lampi> and <khat> written as one word: a road, or one way to follow) (j:lampi/khat) (r:zd:12187/zd:15272) (q:draft)
lampimaan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:right way/true path) (d:<lampi> and <maan> written as one word: the right or true way, the proper course to take) (j:lampi/maan) (r:zd:17152/zd:20746) (q:draft)
lampinawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:roadside/side of the road) (d:<lampi> and <nawl> written as one word: the edge of a road and the strip beside it) (j:lampi/nawl) (r:zd:16148/zd:17909) (q:draft)
lampithak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:new road/new way/new route) (d:<lampi> and <thak> written as one word: a new road or railway line, or a new way of doing or living) (j:lampi/thak) (r:zd:21898/zd:19975/zd:22540) (q:draft)
lampitung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel) (w:on the road/on the street) (d:<lampi>, road, and <tung>, on, written as one word: on the road, also after the name of a road; {lampitung tuahsiatna} is a road accident) (j:lampi/tung) (r:zd:20641/zd:17735/zd:25047) (q:draft)
lampizik = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:main road/built road) (d:<lampi> and <zik> written as one word: a made-up road, such as the main street of a town, along which houses stand) (j:lampi/zik) (r:zd:20512) (q:draft, low confidence)
lampizong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:the road also/seek a road) (d:<lampi>, road, and <zong> written as one word; <zong> is either also, the road as well, or the verb seek, look for a road) (j:lampi/zong) (r:zd:24249) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamsa = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:property/possessions/belongings) (d:in the pair {neihsa lamsa}, things owned and things built: all that a person owns, house and goods together; the builder is not named before it as with the adjective) (r:zd:22941/zd:8667/zd:19457) (q:draft)
lamsaap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (j:lamsap) (r:zd:12231) (q:draft)
lamsak = (i:2) (t:n) (f:travel/nature) (w:upper roadside/uphill side of the road) (d:<lam>, road, with <sak>, upper: the ground that rises above a road or path, the opposite of <lamkhang>; {lamsak lamkhang} is both sides of the road; not the verb {lamsak}, build for) (a:lamkhang) (r:zd:14824/zd:11110) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be under construction) (d:in {aki lamsan}, which is still being built: build, with the ending {-san}, while it is going on; compare <kilam>, be built) (r:zd:12448/zd:20488) (q:draft)
lamsang = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:lift up/raise up/promote) (d:as a verb, <lam> with <sang>, high: raise a person, a people or a thing to a higher place or standing; the verb inside <kilamsang>, exalt oneself, and unlike the noun it stands at the end of the clause, often after <hong>) (r:zd:23554/zd:21085) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamsap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:fare/travel cost/travel expenses) (d:<lam>, way, with <sap>, hire: the money paid for a journey, as <innsap> is the rent for a house) (r:zd:20639/zd:20587/zd:21717) (q:draft)
lamsau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:long way/long distance) (d:<lam>, way, and <sau>, long, written as one word: a long way, far along the way) (j:lam/sau) (r:zd:21989/zd:24217) (q:draft)
lamsial = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:road building/road clearing/preparing the way) (d:<lam>, way, with <sial>, clear: the work of clearing or making a road; also in the figurative sense, preparing the way for something) (j:lam/sial) (r:zd:23037/zd:20725) (q:draft)
lamsiam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:skilled dancer/good dancer) (d:<laam>, dance, written with a short vowel, and <siam>, skilled, as one word: good at dancing, or a person who is; also used as a title after a name) (j:laam/siam) (r:zd:21282) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamsiau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:take a walk/stroll/walk about) (d:go about on foot for exercise or pleasure, without an errand; of a small child, be able to walk) (r:zd:24276/zd:25115/zd:20841) (q:draft)
lamsiauh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (j:lamsiau) (r:zd:24276/zd:25223) (q:draft)
lamsiauhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:walking/walk) (d:<lamsiauh>, take a walk, with the noun suffix <na>: walking as exercise) (b:lamsiauh) (r:zd:24276/zd:14816) (q:draft)
lamsuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:downhill road/descent/downward slope) (d:a stretch of road that goes down, from <lam>, way, and <suk>, downward) (r:zd:20164) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamtampi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:many ways/many respects) (d:<lam>, way or side, and <tampi>, many, written as one word: many ways or means of doing something) (j:lam/tampi) (r:zd:20092/zd:22116/zd:20997) (q:draft)
lamtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in the area of/by way of) (d:<lam>, side or direction, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: {biakna lamtawh kisai} is concerning religion, and {politic lamtawh} is by way of politics) (j:lam/tawh) (r:zd:24469/zd:20899/zd:22850) (q:draft)
lamtawntung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:travel) (w:all along the way/the whole journey) (d:<lam>, way, and <tawntung>, continuously, written as one word: all the way, throughout the journey; also with <ah>) (j:lam/tawntung) (r:zd:11764/zd:14561) (q:draft)
lamtawp = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:end of the road/journey's end/destination) (d:<lam>, way, with <tawp>, end: the end of a road or of a journey) (r:zd:23443) (q:draft)
lamte = (i:3) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:side/those on the side of/people of) (d:<lam.3>, side, with the plural <te>, after the name of an army, a party, a group or a region: the people of that side, as {SAC lamte}, the SAC side, and {kumpi lamte}, those of the government; not builders) (r:ts:2731/zd:23332/zd:15514) (q:draft)
lamteh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (d:<lam> and <teh> written as one word after a word of time: at about that time, only then; {a nung lamteh} is only afterwards and {tu lamteh} nowadays) (j:lam/teh) (r:ts:2731/zd:12352) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamteh = (i:2) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:cross) (d:second part of {sing lamteh}, the cross, written as one word in <singlamteh>) (r:zd:25947) (q:draft)
lamten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:those of the side/people of) (d:<lam>, side or direction, with the plural <te> and the subject marker <in> written as one word: the people of that side, group or region, as the ones who act) (j:lam/te/in) (r:ts:8304/zd:22350) (q:draft)
lamthak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:new road/new way) (d:<lam>, way, and <thak>, new, written as one word: a newly made road, or a new way of doing things) (j:lam/thak) (r:zd:20176/zd:25569) (q:draft)
