lamzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/home) (w:be able to build/manage to build) (d:<lam>, here build, and <zawh>, be able, written as one word: be able to build a house or building; the form of <lamzo> used before <nading>, <nang> and <ngeiloh>) (b:lamzo) (j:lam/zawh) (r:zd:14867/zd:23978) (q:draft)
lamzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:building style/construction/design) (d:the way something is built or put together, from <lam>, build, with <zia>, manner: {inn lamzia} is the style in which a house is built) (r:zd:9422/zd:15274) (q:draft)
lamziik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/work) (w:build a road/make a road) (d:<lam>, road, with <ziik>, build up: build or widen a road by digging and heaping up earth; also the road so made) (j:lam/ziik) (r:zd:20176/zd:8667) (q:draft)
lamzik = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:road/street) (d:a road for vehicles, in a town or between towns) (s:lampi) (r:zd:11646/zd:20023) (q:draft)
