langbai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/politics) (w:lopsided/lame on one side/unbalanced) (d:<lang>, one side, and <bai>, lame: lame or failing on one side, said of a thing that does not stand evenly and of democracy that goes wrong) (j:lang/bai) (r:zd:23358/zd:22157) (q:draft, low confidence)
langbang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:about half) (d:<lang>, half, and <bang>, about, written as one word, after <a>: about half of what is named before it) (j:lang/bang) (r:zd:23754/zd:21198) (q:draft)
langdo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:oppose/resist/go against) (d:<lang>, side, with <do>, fight: take a stand against a person, a rule or a government; {kumpi langdo te} are those who oppose the government) (s:langpang/langpan) (r:zd:18952/zd:25923/zd:13354) (q:draft)
langdona = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:opposition/rebellion/resistance/insurgency) (d:the act of taking the other side and fighting against someone, from <lang> and <dona>; {kumpi langdona} is rebellion against the government) (r:zd:23670/zd:19316) (q:draft)
