lokhawh = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work/nature) (w:farming/agriculture/cultivation) (d:the working of fields to grow crops, <lo>, field, with <khawh>, till: used as a noun and before <nading> and <dan>, and paired as {lokhawh singpuak}, farm work in general) (s:lokho) (r:zd:23770/ts:3375/zd:21908) (q:draft)
lokhomi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/nature) (w:farmer/cultivator) (d:<lokho>, farm, and <mi>, person, written as one word: one who works the land) (j:lokho/mi) (r:zd:15772/zd:24474) (q:draft)
