mehlim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:tasty dish/delicacy/good curry) (d:<meh>, the dish eaten with the staple, with <lim>, tasty: a tasty dish; often paired with <anlim> as {anlim mehlim}, good food) (r:zd:24276/zd:19355/zd:20516) (q:draft)
mehngah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (j:mehgah) (r:zd:21006) (q:draft)
mehte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:dishes/side dishes) (d:<meh>, cooked dish, with the plural <te>, written as one word; {an leh mehte} is rice and the dishes eaten with it) (b:meh) (r:zd:24276/zd:26588) (q:draft)
mehteh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:vegetable/leaf vegetable/herbs) (d:leaf vegetables eaten as a cooked dish with the staple) (s:anteh) (q:draft)
mehtehmehgah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/health) (w:vegetables/greens) (d:vegetables of every kind, <mehteh>, leaf vegetable, with <mehgah>, vegetable that is a fruit or pod) (r:zd:24276/zd:21298) (q:draft)
mehthuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:tomato) (d:<meh>, cooked dish, with <thuk>, sour: the tomato) (r:zd:23896/zd:24276) (q:draft)
mehtui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:soup/broth) (d:<meh>, a cooked dish, with <tui>, water: the liquid of a stew, broth) (s:satui) (q:draft)
mehtuisa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:hot soup/hot broth) (d:<mehtui>, soup, and <sa>, hot, written as one word: hot soup) (j:mehtui/sa) (r:zd:15425/zd:15521) (q:draft)
mehza = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:seasoning/seasoning powder/spice) (d:a seasoning put into food to give it taste; in the news mostly the white seasoning powder, monosodium glutamate) (r:zd:12210) (q:draft)
mehzaa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:seasoning/spice/condiment) (d:<meh>, cooked dish, with <zaa>: what is put into a dish to give it taste, such as spice or flavouring powder) (r:zd:23729) (q:draft, low confidence)
mei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/nature) (w:fire) (d:fire, the flame that burns; also a lamp or light, and the first part of many words such as <meikuang>, flame, and <meikhu>, smoke) (s:meikuang) (r:3.9.11) (q:draft)
meibung = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home) (w:fire/brazier/hearth) (d:a fire or pan of glowing charcoal kept in the house to warm oneself at, not an oven for baking; {meibung awi} is warm oneself at the fire and {meihol meibung} is a charcoal brazier) (r:zd:22059/zd:21175/zd:16038) (q:draft)
meidet = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/home) (w:torch/torchlight) (d:a burning torch carried for light, from <mei>, fire; {meidet pawi} is the torch festival, a name of the Khuado festival, and the word is also used as a picture, as the torch of revival) (r:zd:16640/zd:21141) (q:draft, low confidence)
meigit = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:match/matchstick) (d:a match for lighting fire; {meigit tang khat} is one matchstick) (r:zd:23828/zd:13340) (q:draft)
meigong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:widow) (d:a woman whose husband has died, also said as {meigong numei}; often named together with {pa nei lote}, the fatherless) (s:meigongnu) (r:42.21.2)
meihal = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:set fire to/set on fire/burn) (d:<mei>, fire, with <hal>, burn, used as a verb: set something on fire on purpose; {meihal te} are those who set the fire, and as a charge it is arson) (r:zd:14783/zd:12736/zd:15301) (q:draft)
meihtu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/education) (w:copy/photocopy) (d:a copy of a document, such as a card or a certificate, kept or handed in beside the original) (s:copy) (o:Burmese, meit-tu) (r:zd:13194/zd:18939) (q:draft)
meiikai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:be cloudy/be overcast/cloud over) (d:<meii>, cloud, and <kai>, gather, written as one word: clouds gather, the sky is overcast; {guah meiikai} is rain and cloud) (j:meii/kai) (r:zd:26097/zd:21097) (q:draft)
meikai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:mist/fog/low cloud) (d:mist or cloud that hangs low and hides the view; {guahzu meikai nuai} is under rain and mist; also said of something too hazy to understand) (r:zd:21991/zd:17733/zd:14824) (q:draft, low confidence)
meikang = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:fire/blaze) (d:an outbreak of fire in a building, a vehicle or a forest, as reported in news; {meikang akipan} is the fire started and <gamsung meikang> is a forest fire, not a wound made by fire) (r:zd:12736/zd:18157/zd:15820) (q:draft)
meikanggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:burn down/be destroyed by fire/be badly burned) (d:<meikang>, here catch fire and burn, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word: be burned down or badly burned; common in news headlines) (j:meikang/gawp) (r:zd:11148/zd:13316/zd:14692) (q:draft)
meikangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:by fire/burning) (d:<meikang>, fire or burn, with <in> written as one word: by fire, being on fire) (j:meikang/in) (r:zd:10945) (q:draft, low confidence)
meikanglak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:midst of a fire/scene of a fire) (d:<meikang>, a fire, and <lak>, the midst, written as one word: the place where a fire is burning or has burned) (j:meikang/lak) (r:zd:12502/zd:11466) (q:draft)
meikanglum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:burn to death/be burnt to death) (d:<mei>, fire, and <kanglum>, burn to death, written as one word: die in a fire) (j:mei/kanglum) (r:zd:12900) (q:draft)
meikangpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media/everyday) (w:the fire) (d:<meikang>, here a fire that burns a building, and the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: the fire, as for the fire) (j:meikang/pen) (r:zd:17917/zd:16739) (q:draft)
meikangthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:can catch fire/be able to burn) (d:<meikang>, burn or be on fire, and <thei>, able, written as one word: be liable to catch fire) (j:meikang/thei) (r:zd:12009/zd:12456) (q:draft)
meikangtum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/home) (w:burn down/be destroyed by fire) (d:<mei>, fire, and <kangtum>, burn up, written as one word: be completely burnt by fire) (j:mei/kangtum) (r:zd:12761/zd:13161/zd:17800) (q:draft)
meikangza = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:health/home) (w:aloe/aloe vera) (d:a plant grown at home whose cut flesh is put on burns and scalds and rubbed on the scalp, probably aloe vera; from <meikang>, burn, and the word for medicine found in <zatui>; found in one article) (r:zd:24276) (q:draft, low confidence)
meikat = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:fire/blaze) (d:used as a noun in news reports: a fire that breaks out in a building or vehicle, after <hih> or <tua> and before <kipatna>, the start, or <buaina>, the trouble) (r:zd:13220/zd:13230/zd:16239) (q:draft)
meikatpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:the fire) (d:<meikat>, fire, with the topic marker <pen> written as one word: as for the fire) (j:meikat/pen) (r:zd:14559/zd:12532) (q:draft)
meikatvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:fire incident/case of fire) (d:<meikat>, burn, and <vai>, matter, written as one word: the matter of a fire, a fire as an event in the news) (j:meikat/vai) (r:zd:13222/zd:22162) (q:draft)
meikhau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/it) (w:electric wire/power line/cable) (d:a wire or cable that carries electricity, from <mei>, fire or light, and <khau>, cord) (r:zd:15677/zd:17175/zd:13264) (q:draft)
meikhuam = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home/travel) (w:lamp post/electric pole/utility pole) (d:a post by the road that carries a street light or the electric wires, from <mei>, here electric light or power, and <khuam>, post; {lampi meikhuam} is a street lamp post) (r:zd:13320/zd:15920/zd:14662) (q:draft)
meikhugim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/nature) (w:smell of smoke/smoke smell) (d:<meikhu>, smoke, and <gim>, here smell, written as one word: the smell of smoke or of burning) (j:meikhu/gim) (r:zd:14736/zd:19392) (q:draft)
Meiktila = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Meiktila) (d:town in Mandalay Region, central Myanmar) (r:zd:17208/zd:15266) (q:draft)
meikuang akipan = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:fire broke out/a fire started) (d:<meikuang>, flame, with {a kipan}, it began, written as one word: a fire broke out, the set wording of a news report; the place stands before it with <ah> or <panin>, and <akipan> is here the verb and not the marker from or since) (r:zd:15461/zd:17729) (q:draft)
meikuanggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:burst into flames/burn up/be burnt out) (d:<meikuang> and <gawp> written as one word: catch fire and burn fiercely, to the point of ruin; said of vehicles and houses) (j:meikuang/gawp) (r:zd:19157/zd:18911/zd:13324) (q:draft)
meikuanglak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:nature/media) (w:amid the flames/in the fire) (d:<meikuang>, flames, and <lak>, midst, written as one word: the midst of a burning fire) (j:meikuang/lak) (r:zd:16739/zd:11236) (q:draft)
meikuangpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:catch fire at once/burst into flames) (d:<meikuang>, blaze, and <pah>, at once, written as one word) (j:meikuang/pah) (r:zd:11938/zd:20668) (q:draft)
meikuangpen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/nature) (w:the fire/the blaze) (d:<meikuang>, fire, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the fire, as the thing spoken about) (j:meikuang/pen) (r:zd:20369/zd:11606/zd:15410) (q:draft)
meikuangsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:burning/alight/on fire) (d:<meikuang>, flame, with the ending {-sa}, already: already set alight, burning) (r:zd:15029) (q:draft)
meikuangteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/media) (w:all the flames/the whole fire) (d:<meikuang>, fire or flame, and <teng>, all, written as one word: the whole of a fire that is burning) (j:meikuang/teng) (r:zd:17289/zd:15276) (q:draft)
meileeng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:train/railway train) (d:<mei>, fire, with <leeng>: a railway train; {meileeng lampi} is a railway) (r:zd:10952/zd:18147/zd:23653) (q:draft)
meileng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:train/railway train) (d:a train that runs on rails; <meileng lampi> is the railway line) (r:zd:23086/zd:11571/zd:15109) (q:draft)
meileng khawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:railway station/train station) (d:<meileng>, train, and <khawlna>, stopping place: the station where trains stop; followed by <ah> for at the station, and often by the name of the station) (r:zd:17861/zd:14694/zd:12040) (q:draft)
meileng lampi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:railway/railway line/railway track) (d:<meileng>, train, and <lampi>, road: the track on which trains run, and a railway line between two places) (r:zd:14888/zd:11901) (q:draft)
meileng station = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:railway station/train station) (d:<meileng>, train, and the English word {station}: a railway station, also of a metro, monorail or light rail line; the name of the place or of the line stands before it) (r:zd:17994/zd:12338) (q:draft)
meilenghawl = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:train driver/engine driver) (d:one who drives a train: <meileng>, train, with <hawl>, drive) (j:meileng/hawl) (r:zd:14726/zd:11296) (q:draft)
meilengkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:a train/one train) (d:<meileng>, train, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a train) (j:meileng/khat) (r:zd:17659/zd:11901) (q:draft)
meilenglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:railway line/railway track) (d:<meileng>, train, and <lam>, way, written as one word: the track on which trains run) (j:meileng/lam) (r:zd:20945) (q:draft)
meilengpen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:the train) (d:<meileng>, train, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the train, as the topic of the sentence) (j:meileng/pen) (r:zd:19300/zd:19141) (q:draft)
meilengsung = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:in the train/inside the train) (d:<meileng> and <sung> written as one word: the inside of a train, in the train) (j:meileng/sung) (r:zd:20492/zd:19790) (q:draft)
meilengthak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:new train) (d:<meileng>, train, with <thak>, new, written as one word) (j:meileng/thak) (r:zd:17822/zd:14555) (q:draft)
meilengtung = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:on the train/aboard a train) (d:<meileng>, train, and <tung>, on, written as one word) (j:meileng/tung) (r:zd:20016/zd:21876) (q:draft)
meilet = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:policy/principle) (d:found after <thu> as {thu meilet}, the same as <thumeilet> written in two words: the policy, principles or rules that a body or a person holds to; as a verb, hold to a position or account) (r:zd:25022/ts:301) (q:draft, low confidence)
meilum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:warmth of a fire/fire heat) (d:<mei>, fire, with <lum>, warm: the warmth of a fire; {meilum awi} is warm oneself at a fire) (r:zd:17355) (q:draft, low confidence)
meilum = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:haze) (d:the haze that hangs over distant hills) (r:zd:22305) (q:draft, low confidence)
meimai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/nature) (w:dimly/hazily/blankly) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: dim, dark or hazy, of cloud, smoke, darkness or a clouded head; of people, as in {om meimai} and {tu meimai}, be or sit there blankly, doing nothing) (r:zd:22658/zd:19676) (q:draft, low confidence)
meimual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:volcano) (d:<mei>, fire, with <mual>, mountain: a mountain that throws out fire; <meimual puakkham> is a volcano erupts) (r:zd:15382/zd:16304/zd:17808) (q:draft)
meimual puakkham = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/media) (w:erupt/volcanic eruption) (d:<meimual>, volcano, as the subject of <puakkham>, burst: a volcano erupts; common in news headlines, with the place before it marked by <ah>) (r:zd:19514/zd:11776) (q:draft)
meingong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (j:meigong) (r:zd:19630/zd:14930) (q:draft)
meiphelh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:firefighting/fire brigade/firefighter) (d:<mei>, fire, with <phelh>, put out: the putting out of fires, and those whose work it is; <meiphelh mawtaw> is a fire engine and {meiphelh zum} a fire station) (r:zd:15851/zd:23281/zd:20297) (q:draft)
meiphelh mawtaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:fire engine/fire truck) (d:<meiphelh>, putting out fire, and <mawtaw>, motor vehicle: a fire engine; a number may follow it) (r:zd:19470/zd:19558/zd:20297) (q:draft)
meiphelhding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:to put out the fire/fight the fire) (d:<mei>, fire, <phelh>, put out, and <ding>, written as one word: in order to put out the fire, mostly as {meiphelhding in}) (j:mei/phelh/ding) (r:zd:17911/zd:14681) (q:draft)
meiphelhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:firefighting/fire extinguishing) (d:<meiphelh>, put out a fire, with the noun suffix <na>: the work of putting out a fire; before the name of a tool, the thing used for it, as a fire extinguisher) (b:meiphelh) (r:zd:14783/zd:12790/zd:20717) (q:draft)
meiphelhpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work/media) (w:the firefighting/putting out the fire) (d:<meiphelh>, putting out fire, with the topic marker <pen> written as one word) (j:meiphelh/pen) (r:zd:13220/zd:15276) (q:draft)
meipi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:cloud) (d:another spelling of <meiipi>, a large cloud that covers a mountain or hides the view, not the big fire of the first sense; verbs such as <tuam>, cover, bring it out) (s:meiipi) (r:zd:18900) (q:draft, low confidence)
meisa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/home) (w:heat of fire/fire heat) (d:<mei>, fire, and <sa>, hot, as one word: the heat that a fire gives off) (r:zd:14692) (q:draft, low confidence)
meisah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:lighter/cigarette lighter) (d:a small device that is struck to make a flame, built on <mei>, fire) (r:zd:22717) (q:draft)
meisah = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:thick fog/dense mist) (d:<mei>, cloud or mist, with <sah>, thick: fog so thick that the road is hard to see) (r:zd:14824) (q:draft, low confidence)
meisan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:red light/red traffic light) (d:<mei>, light, with <san>, red: the red light of a traffic signal; {meisan ngak} is wait at the red light and {meisan kan} is run the red light) (r:zd:14644/zd:11646/zd:13318) (q:draft)
meiset = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:generator/electric generator) (d:an engine that makes electricity) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:15880/zd:24234/zd:25265) (q:draft)
meitang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:lamplight/light/electric light) (d:the light of a lamp or of electric lights, the lights that are on at night; compare <meivak>) (r:zd:22557/zd:21659/ts:4885) (q:draft)
meitawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:with fire) (d:<mei> and <tawh> written as one word: with fire, used with verbs of burning, as {meitawh halsak}, set on fire) (j:mei/tawh) (r:zd:17542/zd:11710) (q:draft)
meite = (i:3) (t:n) (f:home/travel) (w:lights/lamps/electricity) (d:plural of <mei> in the sense light: electric lights and lamps of a room, a street or a vehicle, and with <Electric> or beside <lampi> and <tui> the electricity supply, not open fires and not tails) (r:zd:21981/zd:11472/zd:16061) (q:draft)
Meitei = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social/politics) (w:Meitei/Manipuri) (d:the people of the Manipur valley, called Kathe by the Burmese; {Meitei gun} is the Manipur River) (r:zd:20900/zd:25532) (q:draft)
Meiteigun = (i:1) (t:name) (c:river) (f:travel/nature) (w:Manipur River) (d:the Manipur River, the river of the Meitei, which flows from Manipur through the Tedim area; with <gun>, river) (r:ts:4569/zd:16924) (q:draft)
Meiteite = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Meiteis/Meitei people) (d:<Meitei> with the plural <te>: the Meitei, the people of the Manipur valley) (b:Meitei) (r:zd:24280/ts:1428/ts:301) (q:draft)
meitha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/work) (w:electricity/electric power) (d:<mei>, fire or light, with <tha>, power: electric power) (r:zd:20582/zd:24176/zd:19781) (q:draft)
meitui = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/work/travel) (w:fuel/petrol/oil) (d:fuel for engines and generators, and oil as a product of a country, the present-day use beside lamp oil; {meitui man} is the price or cost of fuel) (r:zd:22085/zd:25128/zd:22203) (q:draft)
meivaak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/social) (j:meivak) (r:zd:15998) (q:draft)
meivakpawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:festival of lights) (d:<meivak> and <pawi> written as one word: the festival of lights kept in Burma, with lamps and fireworks) (j:meivak/pawi) (r:zd:17062) (q:draft)
meivakpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:great light/beacon/torch) (d:<meivak>, light, with the suffix <pi>, great: a great light, a beacon or torch, also in a figurative sense) (j:meivak/pi) (r:zd:24743/zd:24357) (q:draft)
meizom = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:aftermath/consequence/continuation) (d:what follows on from something as its tail: the after-effect of a sickness, the result of a policy, the successor of a state; {tua meizom in} is following on from that) (r:zd:25099/zd:24918) (q:draft)
meizong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home/everyday) (w:electricity also/the power too) (d:<mei>, here electric light or power, and <zong>, also, written as one word) (j:mei/zong) (r:zd:19109/zd:14714) (q:draft)
mekcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:squeeze tight/grip/strangle) (d:<mek>, press with the hand, with <cip>, tightly: grip and hold fast; of the throat, strangle) (r:zd:15456/zd:19231) (q:draft)
mekding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it/health) (w:should press/to be pressed/to squeeze) (d:<meek>, press or squeeze, written with a short vowel and joined to <ding>: is to be pressed) (j:meek/ding) (r:zd:22238/zd:12917) (q:draft)
mekkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:it/everyday) (w:press by mistake/press accidentally) (d:<mek>, press with a finger, with <kha>, happen to: press a key or a trigger without meaning to, or press the wrong thing) (j:mek/kha) (r:zd:18054) (q:draft)
mekmek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:keep pressing/press repeatedly/knead) (d:press with the fingers again and again, as the keys of a phone or dough; from <mek>, press) (r:zd:17618/zd:22002) (q:draft, low confidence)
mekna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:pressing/print/button) (d:the pressing of something with a finger, or the thing pressed, not the kneading of dough: {khutpi mekna}, thumb pressing, is a fingerprint and also the signing of an order, and {datkahlei mekna} is a button of a lift) (r:zd:17295/ts:9570) (q:draft, low confidence)
