mimalkim = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:social/everyday) (w:every individual/each person/everyone) (d:<mimal> individual and <kim> every written as one word: each single person) (s:mikim) (j:mimal/kim) (r:zd:16790/zd:22171/zd:15268) (q:draft)
mimalte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:individuals/individual persons) (d:<mimal>, individual, with the plural <te>: single persons, as against a group, a church or an organisation) (b:mimal) (r:zd:23943/zd:24064/zd:24019) (q:draft)
mimalvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:personal matter/personal interest/private affair) (d:<mimal>, individual, and <vai>, affair, written as one word: what concerns one person only, set against the affairs of the people or the country) (j:mimal/vai) (r:zd:19095/zd:25866) (q:draft)
miman = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:seize people/kidnap/catch men) (d:<mi>, person, and <man>, seize, written as one word: catch or carry off people, as kidnappers do; also of the disciples as fishers of men) (j:mi/man) (r:zd:11600/zd:15259) (q:draft)
mimang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:missing person) (d:<mi>, person, with <mang>, here be lost: someone who has disappeared and is being looked for) (r:zd:20331/zd:12099) (q:draft)
mimangcip = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:missing person/the missing) (d:<mi>, person, and <mangcip>, disappear, written as one word: a person who has gone missing, as after a disaster) (s:mimang) (j:mi/mangcip) (r:zd:15463/zd:15751) (q:draft)
mimasa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:first person/earliest people/former ones) (d:<mi>, person, and <masa>, first, written as one word: the first or earliest person or people, as Adam the first man; before <makaite>, the earlier leaders) (j:mi/masa) (r:zd:15956) (q:draft, low confidence)
mimasate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:forerunners/pioneers/elders) (d:<mi> and <masate> written as one word: the people who came or led before, the earlier leaders) (j:mi/masate) (r:zd:14735) (q:draft)
mimawh = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:simple people/common people) (d:plain, unlearned people of low standing, named beside <mihai>, the foolish, and glossed as grassroots people by one writer; not the sinner of the other sense) (r:zd:23356) (q:draft, low confidence)
mimawkmawk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:ordinary person/commoner/nobody in particular) (d:<mi>, person, with <mawkmawk>, ordinary, written as one word: a person of no special rank or standing) (j:mi/mawkmawk) (r:zd:15315/zd:12512) (q:draft)
mimel = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/social) (w:human face/human appearance/human form) (d:<mi>, person, and <mel>, appearance, written as one word: the face or looks of a person, the form of a human being) (j:mi/mel) (r:zd:24166) (q:draft, low confidence)
mimin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:name of a person/name) (d:<mi> and <min> written as one word: a person's name; {mimin thang} is a famous person, more often written {mi minthang}) (j:mi/min) (r:zd:22171) (q:draft, low confidence)
mimuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:trusted person/confidant/trusted aide) (d:<mi>, person, with <muan>, trust: a person someone relies on, a trusted helper or adviser of a leader) (r:zd:19934/zd:21657) (q:draft)
mimuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:public view/public/sight of others) (d:<mi>, people, and <muhna>, sight, written as one word: where people can see; {mimuhna ah} is in public, in front of people) (j:mi/muhna) (r:zd:12267/zd:24712) (q:draft)
min = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:name)
