muntuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/social) (w:different place/another place/elsewhere) (d:<mun> and <tuam> written as one word: a different place; mostly in the pair {muntuam gamtuam}, different places and different lands, said of people living scattered in many countries) (j:mun/tuam) (r:zd:17120/zd:23645/zd:23635) (q:draft)
