Naga = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social/politics) (w:Naga) (d:the Naga peoples of northeast India and northwest Myanmar; {Naga te} is the Nagas) (r:zd:26163/zd:17212) (q:draft)
Nagaland = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics/travel) (w:Nagaland) (d:state in the north-east of India, north of Manipur) (r:zd:23037/zd:19997) (q:draft)
nagam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/travel) (w:your country) (d:<na>, your, and <gam>, country, written as one word: your country; the same letters also arise when the noun ending {-na} is split from its word, as in {pian nagam} for {pianna gam}, native country) (j:na/gam) (r:zd:14615/zd:20169) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nagasaki = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Nagasaki) (d:city in Japan, the second city on which a nuclear bomb was dropped, on 9 August 1945) (r:zd:22658/zd:12183) (q:draft)
nagawn = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:nangawn) (r:zd:19654/zd:17897/zd:20092) (q:draft)
nagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:hurt badly/ache severely) (d:<na>, here hurt or be in pain, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word: be in great pain, said of a part of the body) (j:na/gawp) (r:zd:12996/zd:11833) (q:draft)
nagelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:you write) (d:<na>, you, and <gelh>, write, written as one word: you write, what you wrote) (j:na/gelh) (r:zd:12336/zd:20148) (q:draft)
nagelhdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/it) (w:the way you wrote it/your way of writing) (d:<na>, you, and <gelhdan>, way of writing, written as one word) (j:na/gelhdan) (r:zd:12336) (q:draft)
nagen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you say/you tell) (d:<na> and <gen> written as one word: you say, what you say) (j:na/gen) (r:ts:9856/zd:22293/zd:16442) (q:draft)
nagennop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you want to say/you wish to tell) (d:<na> and <gennop> written as one word: what you want to say; common in interview questions) (j:na/gennop) (r:zd:12544/zd:16360) (q:draft)
nagual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:your companions/your peers/your friends) (d:<na>, your, and <gual>, here one's peers, written as one word; used after <nalawm> or {na lawm} as {nalawm nagual}, your friends and companions) (j:na/gual) (r:zd:14939/zd:25924/zd:13124) (q:draft)
nahang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:because of/reason) (d:the noun ending {-na} of the verb before it written together with <hang>, reason: {neihloh nahang} is because of not having; with <in>, because) (j:na/hang) (r:zd:15274/zd:22293/zd:19390) (q:draft)
nahangin = (i:1) (t:ppm) (f:everyday) (w:because of/on account of) (d:the noun suffix {-na} written apart from its verb and joined to <hangin>: {kithah nahangin} is {kithahna hangin}, because of the killing) (j:na/hangin) (r:zd:23492/zd:12093) (q:draft, low confidence)
nahau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:have plenty/be rich) (d:<na> and <hau> written as one word: you are rich, you have plenty of something; with the particle <na> and another subject, was rich in it) (j:na/hau) (r:zd:16665/zd:20071) (q:draft)
nahawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/travel) (w:you visit/you go to) (d:<na> and <hawh> written as one word: you visit, you go to see a person or a place) (j:na/hawh) (r:zd:12121/zd:22444) (q:draft)
nahawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:you share/you distribute) (d:<na> and <hawm> written as one word: you divide or give out; with <vai> before it, you plan or arrange) (j:na/hawm) (r:zd:23148/zd:16442) (q:draft)
nahi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you are) (d:<na> and <hi> written as one word: you are; with <uh>, you all are) (j:na/hi) (r:zd:19733/zd:19397/zd:17955) (q:draft)
nahi = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:the noun ending {-na} written apart from its verb and joined to <hi>: it is the doing of what the verb says, as {kitan nahi hi}, it is a break) (j:na/hi) (r:zd:22470) (q:draft, low confidence)
nahi gige = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:in fact is/turns out to be) (d:{na hi}, here not you are but the particle <na> of something found to be so with <hi>, and <gige>, always: placed at the end of a statement, usually before a final <hi>, it says that the thing is in fact so or has turned out so) (r:zd:24393/zd:19667) (q:draft, low confidence)
nahia = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:closes a question put to one person, after a question word such as <bang>: <na>, you, with <hia> as a question word, a form of <hiam>, written as one word; {bang sem nahia} is what do you do) (j:na/hia) (r:zd:16337/zd:19603/zd:15425) (q:draft)
nahiam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:do you/are you) (d:<na> and <hiam> written as one word at the end of a question put to the person addressed: {koi munah om nahiam} is where are you) (j:na/hiam) (r:zd:22380/zd:9429/zd:12187) (q:draft)
nahih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you are) (d:<na>, you, and <hih>, the form of be taken before <leh>, <manin> and <hangin>, written as one word: {Zomi nahih leh} is if you are a Zomi) (j:na/hih) (r:zd:21664/zd:19266/zd:21178) (q:draft)
nahihi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you are) (d:<na> and <hihi> written as one word: you are) (j:na/hihi) (r:zd:24638/zd:16637) (q:draft)
nahihiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:are you/do you/did you) (d:<na> and <hihiam> written as one word at the end of a question put to a person: are you, is it that you; in reported questions also used of a third person) (j:na/hihiam) (r:zd:16772/zd:14883) (q:draft)
nahihlam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:that you are) (d:<na>, you, and <hihlam>, the fact of being, written as one word before <phawk> or <thei>: that you are) (j:na/hihlam) (r:zd:23784/zd:11837) (q:draft)
nahihleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if you are) (d:<na>, you, and <hihleh>, if it is, written as one word: if you are, placed after what the person is) (j:na/hihleh) (r:zd:15286/zd:16360) (q:draft)
nahihman = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:because you are/since you are) (d:<na>, you, and <hihman>, because, written as one word, followed by <in>: because you are, or because you will, after a clause with <ding>) (j:na/hihman) (r:zd:22171) (q:draft)
nahihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:your being) (d:<na> and <hihna> written as one word: the fact that you are; with <tawh>, as one who is, since you are) (j:na/hihna) (r:zd:14992/zd:16442) (q:draft)
nahihtuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:turn out to be/apparently be/seem to be) (d:<na>, here a particle for something found out afterwards, and <hihtuak>, seem to be, written as one word at the end of a statement: it turns out to be, often followed by <mawk>) (j:na/hihtuak) (r:zd:16122/zd:15374/zd:15693) (q:draft)
nahilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:tell/inform) (d:<na>, you, and <hilh>, teach or tell, written as one word; in requests such as {nahilh sawnsak un}, please tell it on to others) (j:na/hilh) (r:zd:23048) (q:draft, low confidence)
nahilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:was not/is not) (d:<na>, the word before a verb for what was found to be so, and <hilo>, is not, written as one word: it was not, it turned out not to be; not you are not) (j:na/hilo) (r:zd:23025/zd:17501) (q:draft)
nahimawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:turn out to be/prove to be) (d:<na>, here a particle of discovery, and <himawk> written as one word: it turned out to be, to the surprise of the one who found it so) (j:na/himawk) (r:zd:12854/zd:13009) (q:draft)
nahitakpi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really be/turn out to be indeed) (d:<na>, already, and <hitakpi>, truly be, written as one word: it proved indeed to be so, mostly before <mawk>) (j:na/hitakpi) (r:zd:15609) (q:draft)
nahizaw = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:turn out to be rather/be in fact) (d:<na> and <hizaw>, be rather, written as one word: it turns out to be this and not what was first thought; <na> here is the particle before a verb for what is found to be so, not the pronoun you) (j:na/hizaw) (r:zd:13250/zd:21328) (q:draft)
nahlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:gain/benefit/be better off) (d:come off well or be rewarded for how one acts, mostly with <pek> or <peek>; known from the saying {Nu le pa thumang a nahlawh peek}; meaning inferred, to be checked) (r:zd:16900) (q:draft, low confidence)
nahoihlo = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:bad thing/evil/wrong) (d:<na>, thing, and <hoihlo>, bad, written as one word: something bad, a wrong deed) (j:na/hoihlo) (r:zd:25919/zd:15588) (q:draft)
nahoihsepna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:good work/good deed) (d:<nahoih>, good thing, and <sepna>, work, written as one word: the doing of good, a good work done for others) (j:nahoih/sepna) (r:zd:19342) (q:draft, low confidence)
nahoihte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:good things/good deeds) (d:<nahoih> with the plural <te>: good things, good works done) (b:nahoih) (r:zd:24313/zd:19607) (q:draft)
nahong = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<na>, you, and <hong>, toward the speaker, written as one word before a verb: you do it to me or to us, as in {nahong ci uh hiam}, do you say of me; more often written <nong>) (j:na/hong) (r:zd:23432/zd:25277) (q:draft, low confidence)
nahonkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:rescue/save/bring out) (d:<na>, the particle for an action already done elsewhere, and <honkhia>, rescue, written as one word: had rescued, got someone out of danger) (j:na/honkhia) (r:zd:19894/zd:14572) (q:draft)
nahtang = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:food/nature) (w:banana) (d:the banana, fruit and plant; {nahtang kung} is a banana plant) (r:zd:17958/zd:24276/zd:24130) (q:draft)
nahun = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:your time) (d:<na>, your, and <hun>, time, written as one word) (j:na/hun) (r:zd:19236/zd:19586) (q:draft)
nahvawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be in contact with/be involved with/be connected with) (d:used after <ki> and with <tawh>, as {tawh ki nahvawh}: have dealings or contact with, be involved in) (r:zd:24381/zd:12231) (q:draft, low confidence)
nai = (i:3) (t:n) (f:time) (w:time/hour/o'clock) (d:an hour, or the hour of the day by the clock; {nai khat} is one hour and {nitak nai thum} is three in the afternoon)
nai = (i:4) (t:adj) (f:everyday/travel) (w:near/close) (d:near in place or time, not far) (r:zai:approach) (q:draft, low confidence)
nai hetlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:not yet at all/still far from) (d:<nai>, here yet, and <hetlo>, not at all: placed after a verb or describing word, not yet at all; {sawt nai hetlo} is not long ago at all) (r:zd:21117/zd:25937) (q:draft)
naibangzah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:how many hours) (d:<nai>, hour, and <bangzah>, how many, written as one word: how many hours) (j:nai/bangzah) (r:zd:19801/zd:12395) (q:draft)
Naiganyee = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (j:nainganzi) (o:Burmese, naingngan-ye) (r:zd:24068) (q:draft, low confidence)
naihetlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:not yet at all/still not) (d:<nai>, yet, and <hetlo>, not at all, written as one word after a verb: it has still not happened at all) (j:nai/hetlo) (r:zd:20892/zd:11534) (q:draft)
naihphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go up to/approach/draw near) (d:<naih>, come near, and <phei>, across, written as one word: go over close to someone) (j:naih/phei) (r:zd:15608/zd:20492) (q:draft)
naii = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (j:nai) (r:zd:22479/zd:22709) (q:draft, low confidence)
naikal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:hour) (d:an hour as a length of time; {naikal nih} is two hours) (r:zd:23086/zd:11279/zd:24375) (q:draft)
naikei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:not yet/never yet) (d:<nai> and the negative <kei> written as one word after a verb: not yet; {naikei in} forbids for the present, do not yet) (s:nailo) (j:nai/kei) (r:zd:21458/zd:17345/zd:23252) (q:draft)
naikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:one hour/an hour) (d:<nai>, hour, and <khat>, one, written as one word; {naikhat in} is per hour and {naikhat sung} for an hour) (j:nai/khat) (r:zd:21358/zd:19578/zd:16665) (q:draft)
naikhatin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/travel) (w:per hour/an hour) (d:<naikhat> and <in> written as one word: in one hour, used in stating speed) (j:naikhat/in) (r:zd:11236/zd:23676) (q:draft)
naikhatsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:in one hour/for one hour/per hour) (d:<naikhat>, one hour, and <sung>, in or during, written as one word: within or during one hour; of speed, per hour) (j:naikhat/sung) (r:zd:15054/zd:11909) (q:draft)
naikhatval = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:more than an hour/over an hour) (d:<naikhat>, one hour, and <val>, exceed, written as one word) (j:naikhat/val) (r:zd:14559/zd:12845) (q:draft)
nailang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:half an hour/half hour) (d:<nai> hour with <lang> half: thirty minutes) (j:nai/lang) (r:zd:12267/zd:20484/zd:24276) (q:draft)
nailoding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will not yet/not yet be going to) (d:<nailo>, not yet, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: it will not yet be so, still will not) (j:nailo/ding) (r:zd:16383/zd:14555) (q:draft)
nailoh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:not yet) (d:<nai>, yet, with <loh>, the form of the negative used before a noun or another word, written as one word after a verb: not yet, as {i theih nailoh thu}, a thing we do not yet know; compare <nailo>) (j:nai/loh) (r:zd:16404/zd:24932) (q:draft)
nailohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/time) (d:<nailoh>, not yet, with the noun ending {-na}: the place where, or the fact that, something has not yet happened or been done; {ka pai ngei nailohna} is where I have never yet gone) (b:nailoh) (r:zd:17786/zd:24814/zd:25094) (q:draft)
nailohte = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:those not yet/things not yet done) (d:<nailoh> and the plural <te> written as one word after a verb: the things or people that have not yet been so, as {theih nailohte}, things not yet known) (j:nailoh/te) (r:zd:23019/zd:11019) (q:draft)
nailopi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:before/while not yet) (d:<nai>, yet, with <lopi>, written as one word after a verb, often with <in>: before doing, while it has not yet happened) (j:nai/lopi) (r:zd:23977/zd:24331) (q:draft)
nailopipi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:not yet at all/before it has) (d:<nai> and <lopipi> written as one word after a verb: while the thing has not yet happened) (j:nai/lopipi) (r:zd:14611) (q:draft)
nailote = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<nailo>, not yet, with the plural <te>, written as one word after a verb: those who have not yet done it, the things that have not yet happened) (j:nailo/te) (r:zd:17634/zd:15758/zd:12563) (q:draft)
nailung = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature/work) (w:silkworm) (d:the worm that is kept for its silk, as in {nailung khawi}, rear silkworms; the tree it feeds on is {nailung kung}, the mulberry) (r:zd:24211/zd:22371) (q:draft)
naimahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/everyday) (w:very near/imminent) (d:<nai>, near, and <mahmah>, very, written as one word: very close in place or time) (j:nai/mahmah) (r:zd:15382) (q:draft, low confidence)
naingangyi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:politics) (d:politics, the public affairs of a country and of its parties; also written with a capital) (s:nainganyii/nainganzi/politics) (o:Burmese, naingngan-ye) (r:zd:24480/zd:17046) (q:draft)
Nainganyee = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:politics) (d:the Burmese word for politics, used in Zolai writing; {nainganyee party} is a political party) (s:gamvai) (o:Burmese, naingngan-yay) (r:zd:24714/zd:24277) (q:draft)
nainganyii = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:politics) (d:politics, the public affairs of a country and of its parties) (o:Burmese, naingnganye) (r:zd:16055/zd:21219/zd:22316) (q:draft)
nainganzi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:politics) (d:politics, the affairs of governing a country; {Kawlgam nainganzi} is the politics of Myanmar) (o:Burmese, naingngan-ye) (r:zd:21050/zd:17971) (q:draft)
nainganzii = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:politics) (d:politics, the Burmese word; {nainganzii makai} is a political leader) (s:politics/gamvai) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:20091/zd:22484) (q:draft)
Naingngaanzee = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:politics/political affairs) (d:politics, the Burmese word in Zolai spelling; often written with a capital letter) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:19239/zd:17060) (q:draft)
nainih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:two hours) (d:<nai>, hour, and <nih>, two, written as one word: two hours; {nainih sung} is for two hours) (j:nai/nih) (r:zd:20661/zd:16511/zd:12450) (q:draft)
naipaak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature/everyday) (w:yellow/orange yellow) (d:the colour yellow to orange, mostly as {naipaak mel}, yellow colour, with <mel>) (r:zd:22238/zd:23597) (q:draft)
naipak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/nature) (w:orange/deep yellow) (d:a colour named beside <eng>, yellow, and <san>, red, and said of pumpkin and carrot: orange or deep yellow; {naipak mel} is that colour) (r:zd:20747/zd:24862) (q:draft, low confidence)
naipi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/home) (w:clock) (d:<nai>, watch or hour, with <pi>, big: a clock, such as one that hangs on a wall or post) (r:zd:21876/zd:22683) (q:draft)
Naipitau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/travel) (w:clock tower) (d:a tower with a large clock set up in a town or village, apparently <nai>, clock, with <pi>, great, and <tau>, a raised platform) (r:zd:20131/zd:22444) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nairobi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Nairobi) (d:the capital city of Kenya) (r:zd:20977) (q:draft)
naisim = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:hourly/every hour) (d:<nai> hour with <sim>, each; mostly paired with <nisim> as {nisim naisim}, every day and every hour, all the time) (r:zd:12167/zd:17070) (q:draft)
naitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at close range/closely) (d:<nai>, near, with <tak>: from very near; other writers join {nai tak}, not yet really, in the same way) (j:nai/tak) (r:ts:11942) (q:draft, low confidence)
naitau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/travel) (w:clock tower/belfry) (d:a tower or monument with a clock, <nai>, standing in a town) (r:zd:11510/zd:11170) (q:draft)
naitha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:hourly wage/hourly pay) (d:<nai>, hour, with <tha>: pay for work reckoned by the hour, beside <nitha>, pay by the day, and <khasum>, pay by the month) (r:zd:18079/zd:22704) (q:draft)
naive = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:sentence-final, said to the person addressed and often followed by <maw>: you surely are, you surely will; apparently {na hi} shortened and joined with <ve>) (r:zd:20149/zd:17181) (q:draft, low confidence)
naivua = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:colloquial ending of a question put to several people, seemingly {na hi uh a} run together: are you, have you) (r:zd:16216/zd:16337) (q:draft, low confidence)
nak = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very/greatly/much) (d:placed before a verb: to a great degree, as {nak liam} be badly hurt and {nak ngaihsut} think hard; the same word as in <nakpi>) (r:ts:9564/zd:15883/zd:21925) (q:draft)
nak = (i:3) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if/as long as/provided that) (d:with a following <leh>, after the verb of a condition: {nak leh} is <nakleh> written as two words, if indeed, as long as) (r:zd:22775/zd:23022) (q:draft)
nakam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:your mouth) (d:<na>, your, and <kam>, mouth, written as one word) (j:na/kam) (r:zd:14706/zd:12267) (q:draft)
Nakan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you inquire/you look into) (d:<na>, you, and <kan>, search or inquire, written as one word: you look into or ask about a matter) (j:na/kan) (r:zd:15951/zd:24064) (q:draft)
nakap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:shoot/fire at/spray) (d:<na>, marker of an event told of, and <kap>, shoot or spray, written as one word: shot at, sprayed) (j:na/kap) (r:zd:12437/zd:24155) (q:draft)
nakbing = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:blocked nose/nasal congestion) (d:<nak>, nose, with <bing>, be stopped up: a stuffed nose as in a cold; also used as a verb, have a blocked nose) (r:zd:24276/zd:23512) (q:draft)
nakem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:had kept/have ready) (d:the particle <na>, beforehand, and <kem>, keep, written as one word: had been keeping something, had it ready) (j:na/kem) (r:zd:14829) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you keep/keep) (d:<na>, you, and <kep>, keep, written as one word: you keep or look after; also the polite command with <na>, please keep) (j:na/kep) (r:zd:19117/zd:8667) (q:draft)
nakepsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:look after for/keep for/take into care) (d:<na> and <kepsak> written as one word: look after a person or thing on behalf of someone; with <un> or <in> a request, please look after for me) (j:na/kepsak) (r:zd:15485/zd:12171) (q:draft)
nakhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:send) (d:<na> and <khak>, here in the sense send, written as one word: you send, said of money, a photo or a message) (j:na/khak) (r:zd:15274/zd:14554) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakhamkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:have had your fill/have had enough) (d:<na>, you, with <khamkhit>, have had one's fill, written as one word: after you have eaten or drunk your fill, also of having drunk enough to be drunk) (j:na/khamkhit) (r:zd:21664) (q:draft)
nakhat = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:something/a thing) (d:<na>, thing, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a thing, something; {nakhat peuhpeuh} is anything at all) (j:na/khat) (r:zd:25923/zd:9253/zd:19676) (q:draft)
nakhawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:stop/wait) (d:<na>, you, and <khawl> in the sense of stop or rest, written as one word: said to someone, stop doing it, or wait a moment) (j:na/khawl) (r:zd:14543/zd:22958) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakhe = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:your foot/your leg/your feet) (d:<na>, your, and <khe>, foot or leg, written as one word) (j:na/khe) (r:zd:16343) (q:draft)
nakhempeuh = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:everything/all things) (d:<na>, thing, and <khempeuh>, all, written as one word) (j:na/khempeuh) (r:zd:21358/zd:19816/zd:23257) (q:draft)
nakhua = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:your village/your home town) (d:<na>, your, and <khua>, village, written as one word: your village or home community) (j:na/khua) (r:zd:22815/zd:21137) (q:draft)
nakhualna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:your regard/your concern) (d:<na>, your, and <khualna>, regard, written as one word; {na tangek nakhualna in} is out of regard for your baby, for the sake of your baby) (j:na/khualna) (r:zd:13112) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakhut = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:your hand/your hands) (d:<na> your and <khut> hand written as one word) (j:na/khut) (r:zd:24054/zd:14706) (q:draft)
naki = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<na>, you, and the prefix <ki> written as one word and apart from the verb: you, with a verb of doing to oneself or to one another, often in requests such as {naki hilhsawn un}, pass it on to one another) (j:na/ki) (r:zd:12457/zd:12009) (q:draft)
naki = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the particle <na>, here already or as it turned out, and the prefix <ki> written as one word before a verb in a report of something found to have happened) (j:na/ki) (r:zd:12517/zd:23554) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakiim = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:around you/your surroundings) (d:<na> and <kiim> written as one word: the area around you; mostly in the pair {nakiim napaam}, all around you, your surroundings and neighbours) (j:na/kiim) (r:zd:14601/zd:10777/zd:21115) (q:draft)
nakipawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:your organisation/your association) (d:<na>, your, and <kipawlna>, organisation, written as one word: the organisation or community group to which you belong) (j:na/kipawlna) (r:zd:11162/zd:20498) (q:draft)
nakisem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:work is done/work) (d:<na>, thing or work, and <kisem>, be done, written as one word: work is done, people work) (j:na/kisem) (r:zd:25919/zd:25097) (q:draft)
nakivial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/everyday) (w:be found coiled/lie coiled) (d:<na>, here the particle for something found to be so, and <kivial>, be coiled, written as one word: turn out to be coiled up there, said of a snake) (j:na/kivial) (r:zd:21022/zd:12181) (q:draft)
naklah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:be short of breath/gasp for breath/suffocate) (d:built on <nak>, nose: have trouble breathing, as from smoke or illness; {naklah liangin gen} is say breathlessly) (r:zd:21476/zd:14783) (q:draft)
naklahgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:gasp for breath/struggle to breathe/suffocate) (d:<naklah>, be short of breath, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word: have great trouble breathing) (j:naklah/gawp) (r:zd:12561/zd:11553) (q:draft)
nakle = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (j:nakleh) (r:zd:22950/zd:22888/zd:24461) (q:draft)
nakliam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be seriously injured/be badly hurt) (d:<liam>, be wounded, with the first part of <nakpi>, greatly: be badly wounded or hurt, as in an accident) (b:liam) (r:zd:20164/zd:18112/zd:15631) (q:draft)
nakliamlua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be very seriously injured/be critically hurt) (d:<nakliam>, be badly hurt, with <lua>, too much, written as one word: be hurt so badly that urgent care is needed) (j:nakliam/lua) (r:zd:11470/zd:17230) (q:draft)
naknak = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:whenever/as long as) (d:doubled <nak> before <leh>, the same as <nakleh> with more weight: whenever, wherever it is so) (r:zd:23022) (q:draft, low confidence)
naknak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:breathe/keep breathing) (d:doubled <nak>, breathe: go on breathing, draw breath after breath) (r:zd:20857) (q:draft, low confidence)
naknawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:no longer breathe/stop breathing) (d:<nak>, here breathe, and <nawnlo>, no longer, written as one word: not breathing any more) (j:nak/nawnlo) (r:zd:16093/zd:15924) (q:draft)
nakoih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:you put/you keep/you deposit) (d:<na> and <koih> written as one word: you put or keep something, or what you have put aside, as money in a bank) (j:na/koih) (r:zd:12908/zd:20089) (q:draft)
nakpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:body/health) (w:through the nose/from the nose) (d:<nak> and <pan> written as one word: out of or through the nose, said of breathing) (j:nak/pan) (r:zd:20195/zd:23906) (q:draft)
nakpitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:greatly/very much/strongly) (d:<nakpi> and <tak.1> written as one word, alone or followed by <in>: to a great degree, with great force) (s:nakpitakin) (j:nakpi/tak) (r:zd:21063/zd:21657) (q:draft)
nakpitakin kidahpih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:deeply condole/mourn deeply with) (d:<nakpitakin>, greatly, and <kidahpih>, grieve with each other: the set words of a message of condolence, by which a society or family declares its sorrow with the bereaved; it stands at the end of the notice, after the name of the body that sends it, and is commonly joined with <kilainatpih>) (r:zd:10688/zd:21699) (q:draft)
naksep = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:work hard/labour intensely) (d:work hard and with great effort, often as {na naksep mahmah}, work very hard) (r:zd:18200/zd:9447) (q:draft)
naksung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:inside of the nose/nasal cavity) (d:<nak>, nose, and <sung>, inside, written as one word: the inside of the nose) (j:nak/sung) (r:zd:24276/zd:12267/zd:24054) (q:draft)
naktam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very many/a great many) (d:<nak>, very, and <tam>, many, written as one word: very many, often followed by <lua> or <mahmah>) (j:nak/tam) (r:zd:12334/zd:26620) (q:draft)
nakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:be able to breathe) (d:taken as a short spelling of <naak>, breathe, with <thei>, able, written as one word: be able to breathe; also said of one who can just get by or is given relief) (r:zd:20215) (q:draft, low confidence)
naktheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:be unable to breathe/cannot breathe) (d:<nakthei>, be able to breathe, with <lo>, not) (j:nakthei/lo) (r:zd:15461/zd:16344) (q:draft)
naktuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:nose cover/face mask) (d:a covering worn over the nose, from <nak>, nose, with <tuam>, cover; named beside <muktuam>, also used as a verb, cover the nose) (s:muktuam) (r:zd:23935/zd:24158) (q:draft)
Nakzang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Nakzang) (d:village in the north of Chin State, Myanmar, in the Tedim and Tonzang area; {Nakzang lei} is the bridge there) (r:zd:25479/zd:16331) (q:draft)
nakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:be able to breathe) (d:<nak>, breathe, and <zo>, be able, written as one word; with <nawnlo> it means can no longer breathe, said of someone who is dying) (j:nak/zo) (r:zd:22894/zd:22097) (q:draft)
nakzolo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:cannot breathe/be unable to breathe) (d:<nak>, here the verb breathe, and <zolo> written as one word: not able to breathe) (j:nak/zolo) (r:zd:15301) (q:draft)
nala = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media/social) (w:your song) (d:<na>, your, and <la>, song, written as one word) (j:na/la) (r:zd:16291) (q:draft)
nala = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take) (d:<na> before the verb <la>, take, written as one word: you take, or took as a past event) (j:na/la) (r:zd:17745) (q:draft, low confidence)
nalai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:your letter/your document/your writing) (d:<na>, your, and <lai>, letter or document, written as one word) (j:na/lai) (r:zd:11011/zd:10892) (q:draft)
nalaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:change/replace/exchange) (d:<na> and <laih>, replace, written as one word: with <na>, already, they changed it, as in {a min nalaih}, changed its name; with <na>, you, change it yourself) (j:na/laih) (r:zd:15501/zd:18893) (q:draft, low confidence)
nalaihnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you want to change) (d:<na>, <laih> and <nop> written as one word, before <leh>: if you want to change or replace something) (j:na/laih/nop) (r:zd:12317) (q:draft)
nalaiteng = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:all your papers/all your documents) (d:<na>, your, <lai>, letter or document, and <teng>, here all, written as one word: all the papers you have) (j:na/lai/teng) (r:zd:11789) (q:draft, low confidence)
nalak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you take/you show) (d:<na> and <lak> written as one word: you take, what you have taken; with <lak> in the sense show, you show) (j:na/lak) (r:zd:21163/zd:25347) (q:draft, low confidence)
nalam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:direction/side) (d:the noun ending {-na} of the preceding word written together with <lam>, direction: {nisuah nalam} is {nisuahna lam}, the direction of sunrise, the east; after a place, toward it) (j:na/lam) (r:zd:25312/zd:12153) (q:draft, low confidence)
nalam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work) (w:build) (d:the particle <na> before <lam> used as the verb build, written as one word: built, was building) (r:zd:24604) (q:draft, low confidence)
nalawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:your friend) (d:<na>, your, and <lawm>, friend, written as one word; {nalawm nagual} is your friends and companions) (j:na/lawm) (r:zd:14939/zd:13112) (q:draft)
nalawmte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:your friends) (d:<na>, your, and <lawmte>, friends, written as one word) (j:na/lawmte) (r:zd:20056/zd:26565) (q:draft)
naleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:and) (d:the noun ending {-na} written apart from its verb and joined to <leh>, and: links a verbal noun to the next noun, as in {lamet naleh lunggulhna}, hope and longing) (j:na/leh) (r:zd:15249/zd:12110/zd:17788) (q:draft)
nalei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:you buy) (d:<na>, you, and <lei>, buy, written as one word: you buy, your buying) (j:na/lei) (r:zd:11854/zd:19775) (q:draft)
nalen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hold/grab/seize) (d:<na> and <len>, hold, written as one word; <na> is either you, as in you hold, or the particle before a verb that tells of something done, as in he grabbed her) (j:na/len) (r:zd:12801/zd:19637) (q:draft, low confidence)
naleng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even) (d:placed after the word or phrase it stresses, marking an extreme or unexpected case) (s:nangawn) (r:zd:25171/zd:24115/zd:19953) (q:draft)
nalian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:great work/great thing/big task) (d:<na>, work or thing, and <lian>, great, written as one word: a great work, an important undertaking; often {nalian pi}) (j:na/lian) (r:zd:25332/zd:15484/zd:15853) (q:draft)
nalianpi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work/everyday) (w:great work/great thing) (d:<na>, thing or work, and <lianpi>, great, written as one word: a great work, a big thing) (j:na/lianpi) (r:zd:20725/zd:19816/zd:21119) (q:draft)
nalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:not hurt/not ache) (d:<na>, hurt or be in pain, and <lo>, not, written as one word: does not hurt; of a plant, not be damaged) (j:na/lo) (r:zd:14826/zd:20004) (q:draft, low confidence)
nalua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:hurt very much/be very painful) (d:<na>, hurt, and <lua>, too much, written as one word: be in great pain, of the stomach or of a treatment) (j:na/lua) (r:zd:21793/zd:12510) (q:draft)
nalung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (w:your heart/your mind) (d:<na.1> and <lung> written as one word: your heart, in expressions of feeling such as {nalung kia}, you lose heart, and {nalung nuam}, you are glad) (j:na/lung) (r:zd:19474/zd:24417/zd:17488) (q:draft)
nalunggulh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you desire/what you long for) (d:<na.1> and <lunggulh> written as one word: you long for, or the thing that you long for) (j:na/lunggulh) (r:zd:16360/zd:25768) (q:draft)
nalup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:you go to bed/you lie down) (d:<na> and <lup> written as one word: you lie down, you go to bed; {nalup ding ciangin} is when you are about to go to bed) (j:na/lup) (r:zd:21918/zd:21529) (q:draft)
nalupna = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home) (w:your bed) (d:<na>, your, and <lupna>, bed, written as one word: your bed, the place where you sleep) (j:na/lupna) (r:zd:22856/zd:12061) (q:draft)
nalut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:you enter/you go in) (d:<na>, you, and <lut>, enter, written as one word: you go in, you log in) (j:na/lut) (r:zd:15445/zd:20263) (q:draft)
nam = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:nation/people/race) (d:a people or nation, as in <minam>; {gam leh nam} is country and people, and {nam it} is love one's people) (r:zd:22495/zd:8667) (q:draft)
namahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:hurt badly/ache greatly) (d:<na>, here hurt or be painful, with <mahmah>, very, written as one word: be very painful; {ka lungtang namahmah hi} is my heart aches) (j:na/mahmah) (r:zd:20721/zd:15435) (q:draft)
namai = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/body) (w:your face/in front of you/ahead of you) (d:<na>, your, and <mai>, face or front, written as one word: your face, or what lies before you, as in {nanung namai}, behind you and in front of you) (j:na/mai) (r:zd:21174/zd:12112) (q:draft)
naman = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:catch/arrest/seize) (d:<man>, catch, with the particle <na> before it, usually written {na man}: caught or arrested someone, or caught fish or a falling thing; follows the doer marked with <in> or {te'n}) (r:zd:15214/zd:12214/zd:12693) (q:draft)
namang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:you obey/obey) (d:<na> and <mang.1> written as one word: you obey, mostly after <thu>, word) (j:na/mang) (r:zd:21826) (q:draft, low confidence)
namanpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:arrest at once/seize immediately) (d:the narrative particle <na> written together with <manpah>: caught or arrested him right away, said of what others did) (j:na/manpah) (r:zd:15427/zd:14758) (q:draft)
namawk = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:you idly/you in vain) (d:<na>, you, and <mawk>, idly or for nothing, written as one word before a verb: {sum namawk beisak} is you waste money for nothing) (j:na/mawk) (r:zd:14921/zd:14887) (q:draft, low confidence)
nambup = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:whole nation/entire people) (d:<nam>, here a people or nation, and <bup>, whole, written as one word: the people as a whole, often paired with <gambup>, the whole country) (j:nam/bup) (r:zd:10742/zd:16342) (q:draft)
namdangten = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/politics) (w:other peoples/foreigners) (d:<namdang>, another people, and <ten>, the plural marker of the doer, written as one word: other peoples, people of other nations, as the doer of the action) (j:namdang/ten) (r:zd:11135/zd:23044) (q:draft)
namek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:it) (w:you click/you press) (d:<na>, you, with <mek>, press, written as one word: you press or click a link or a button on a screen) (j:na/mek) (r:zd:12441/zd:11734/zd:11350) (q:draft)
namel = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:whether/perhaps) (d:placed after a verb or after <ahih> to show that the speaker does not know whether it is so: whether it will be, who knows if) (r:zd:24186/zd:16235) (q:draft, low confidence)
nameltheih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:your acquaintance/someone you know) (d:<na> and <meltheih> written as one word: a person you know; {nameltheih tanau te} is the relatives and people you know) (j:na/meltheih) (r:zd:17355/zd:15286) (q:draft)
namgim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/work) (w:petroleum/oil/fuel oil) (d:oil from the ground and the fuel made from it; {namgim tui} is liquid fuel such as kerosene or petrol, and {namgim khuk} is an oil well) (r:zd:24165/zd:25601/zd:26620) (q:draft)
namgimtui = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature/work/travel) (w:petroleum/oil/petrol/fuel) (d:mineral oil from the ground and the fuel made from it for engines, not oil for a lamp: {namgimtui khuk} is an oil well and {namgimtui zuakna} a place that sells petrol) (r:zd:11548/zd:17692/zd:19383) (q:draft)
namin = (i:3) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:your name) (d:<na>, your, with <min>, name, written as one word: your name; {namin in} is in your name, at the end of a prayer) (r:zd:8667/zd:21130/zd:17945) (q:draft)
namke = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:tribe/ethnic group/sub-tribe) (d:a division of a people, a tribe or ethnic group within a larger <minam>) (r:zd:20850/zd:18077/zd:15946) (q:draft)
namkee = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:tribe/subgroup of a people) (d:one of the groups into which a people is divided, as the tribes of the Zomi) (r:zd:25628/zd:21690) (q:draft)
Namkham = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Namkham) (d:town and township in the north of Shan State in Myanmar) (r:ts:4941/ts:3882) (q:draft)
namkhatmah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:a kind of/one kind of) (d:<namkhat>, one kind, and the emphatic <mah>, written as one word after a noun: it is a kind of that thing) (j:namkhat/mah) (r:zd:12299/zd:14756) (q:draft)
namkhatpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:one kind/a kind of) (d:<namkhat>, one kind, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: a kind of the thing just named, as the topic of the sentence) (j:namkhat/pen) (r:zd:22193/zd:12521) (q:draft)
namkhatzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:also a kind of/one kind too) (d:<namkhat>, one kind, and <zong>, also, written as one word: another kind as well, also one kind of something) (j:namkhat/zong) (r:zd:12996/zd:11723) (q:draft)
namli = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:four kinds/four sorts) (d:<nam>, kind, and <li>, four, written as one word: four kinds; {namli in khen} is divide into four kinds) (j:nam/li) (r:zd:26310/zd:25924) (q:draft)
namlian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:great nation/great people/noble race) (d:<nam>, kind or people, and <lian>, great, written as one word: a great nation or people; of a person, high or noble birth, as in the pair {nampi namlian}) (j:nam/lian) (r:zd:8375/zd:12512) (q:draft, low confidence)
nammahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:smell strongly) (d:<nam> in the sense smell, give off a smell, and <mahmah> written as one word: smell very strongly; {galgim nammahmah} is the smell of war is strong, war is in the air) (j:nam/mahmah) (r:zd:15447) (q:draft, low confidence)
namnam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/education) (w:kind by kind/by kinds) (d:<nam>, kind, said twice: each kind apart; {a namnam in khen} is divide into kinds, classify) (b:nam) (r:zd:22803) (q:draft)
namnam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:family/body) (w:keep sniffing/keep kissing) (d:a verb for smelling or kissing by sniffing, said twice: sniff or kiss again and again, as the cheeks of a baby) (r:zd:12267) (q:draft, low confidence)
namneu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:minority/small people/minority group) (d:<nam>, kind or people, and <neu>, small, written as one word: a people or group that is small in number, set against a large people; before a noun it means of a minority, as in {namneu biakna}, a minority religion) (j:nam/neu) (r:zd:23770/zd:19644/zd:15583) (q:draft)
namneute = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:minorities/small peoples) (d:<namneu> with the plural <te> written as one word: the peoples that are small in number) (b:namneu) (j:namneu/te) (r:zd:25053) (q:draft)
Namni = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/time/politics) (w:national day) (d:<nam>, a people, with <ni>, day: the day of a people; almost always in {Zomi Namni}, Zomi National Day, kept on 20 February) (r:zd:8668/zd:17722/zd:8375) (q:draft)
nampi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:main kind/main type/category) (d:<nam>, kind, with <pi>, main: one of the main kinds into which a thing is divided, before a number, as {nampi nih in khen}, divide into two main kinds) (r:zd:12867/zd:21605/zd:16055) (q:draft)
nampi = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:great people/major people/large nation) (d:<nam>, people, with <pi>, great: a large or major people or race, set against <namneu>, a minority; {nampi lungsim} is the mindset of a great people) (a:namneu) (r:zd:11206/ts:3160/zd:12370) (q:draft)
nampih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:fellow countryman/kindred/one of the same people) (d:<nam>, people, with <pih>, fellow: a person of the same nation or people as oneself) (s:mipih) (j:nam/pih) (r:zd:21090) (q:draft)
nampite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:great nations/major peoples) (d:<nampi>, here a great or large people, with the plural {-te}: the big nations, set against <namneute>, the small peoples) (b:nampi) (j:nampi/te) (r:zd:22470) (q:draft)
nampuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/social) (w:traditional cloth/national dress/ethnic costume) (d:<nam>, people, with <puan>, cloth: the woven cloth or dress that belongs to a people, as {Zomite nampuan}, the traditional cloth of the Zomi) (r:zd:11076/ts:301) (q:draft)
Namsan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (w:Namhsan) (d:town in the north of Shan State, Myanmar) (r:ts:4941) (q:draft)
namsia = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:smelly/stinking/foul-smelling) (d:having a bad smell, smell bad; {gim namsia} is a bad smell) (s:uih) (r:zd:9430/zd:10929/zd:15358) (q:draft)
namsialua = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:very smelly/stinking) (d:<namsia> and <lua> written as one word: smelling very bad, too smelly) (j:namsia/lua) (r:zd:15157/zd:19981) (q:draft)
namtam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:of many kinds/varied) (d:<nam>, kind, and <tam>, many, written as one word: of many kinds, in many kinds) (j:nam/tam) (r:zd:12541/zd:11409) (q:draft)
namtampi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:many kinds/many sorts) (d:<nam> and <tampi> written as one word: many kinds of something) (j:nam/tampi) (r:zd:19816/zd:20461) (q:draft)
namthum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:three kinds/three sorts) (d:<nam> and <thum> written as one word: three kinds, three points) (j:nam/thum) (r:zd:15857/zd:23112/zd:26444) (q:draft)
namtuamtuam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:of various kinds/various/assorted) (d:<nam>, kind, with <tuamtuam>, various, written as one word and placed after a noun: of many different kinds) (j:nam/tuamtuam) (r:zd:11150/zd:15978) (q:draft)
namtuina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/everyday) (w:fragrance/sweet smell/scent) (d:<namtui>, fragrant, with the noun ending {-na}: a pleasant smell) (b:namtui) (r:zd:23729/zd:22749) (q:draft)
namu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you see/you find) (d:<na> and <mu> written as one word: you see, you find; in narration <na> can also be the particle for something done beforehand, and the whole then means saw or noticed) (j:na/mu) (r:zd:17152/zd:25488) (q:draft, low confidence)
namuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you see) (d:<na> and <muh> written as one word: you see, the form used before <leh>, <ciangin> and similar words) (j:na/muh) (r:zd:12181/zd:19929) (q:draft)
namuhkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you happen to see/you notice) (d:<na>, you, and <muhkhak>, happen to see, written as one word; often {namuhkhak uhleh}, if you happen to see) (j:na/muhkhak) (r:zd:20008/zd:21552) (q:draft)
namukha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to see/notice/come upon) (d:the narrative particle <na> and <mukha> written as one word: happened to see, noticed, came upon) (j:na/mukha) (r:zd:19763/zd:17758) (q:draft)
namun = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:place where/place/spot) (d:the noun ending {-na} written together with <mun>, place, and apart from the word before it: the place where something is or happens, as {a kisap namun}, where it is needed, more often spelled {kisapna mun}) (r:zd:23959/zd:19390/zd:19327) (q:draft)
namvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:national affairs/ethnic affairs/national politics) (d:<nam>, people or nation, and <vai>, affair, written as one word: the affairs and the cause of one's own people) (j:nam/vai) (r:zd:21376) (q:draft)
nanawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:you go near/you pass through) (d:<na>, you, and <nawk>, go through, written as one word; in warnings with {kei un} or {khakei un}: do not go near or through a place) (j:na/nawk) (r:zd:12626/zd:12031) (q:draft)
nanei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you have) (d:<na> and <nei> written as one word: you have) (j:na/nei) (r:zd:16216/zd:16235) (q:draft)
naneih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you have) (d:<na> and <neih> written as one word: you have; {naneih leh} is if you have and {naneih kei leh} if you do not have) (j:na/neih) (r:zd:19266/zd:21717/zd:19676) (q:draft)
naneihleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if you have) (d:<naneih>, you have, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if you have) (j:naneih/leh) (r:zd:11253/zd:25824) (q:draft)
nanek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:you eat) (d:<na>, you, and <nek>, eat, written as one word: you eat, what you eat) (j:na/nek) (r:zd:14708) (q:draft)
nang = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:you) (d:second person singular pronoun, used of one person; {nang in} marks the subject, and {nang hong} before a verb marks you as the object) (s:nangmah)
nang = (i:3) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:for/to/in order to) (d:short form of <nading> placed after a verb, mostly after <theih> and <zawh>, to say what something is for: {ngah theih nang lampi} is a way to be able to get; not the pronoun you) (s:nading) (r:zd:22444/zd:21217/zd:16022) (q:draft)
nanga = (i:2) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:yours) (d:<nang> you with the possessive <a>, also written {nang' a}: the thing that belongs to you, said before <hi>; unlike {nanga} before <kipan>) (r:zd:25005/zd:11339) (q:draft)
nangah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you receive/you get) (d:<na>, you, and <ngah>, receive, written as one word: you receive, you get; in some sentences the same letters are the noun ending {-na} of the word before and <ngah>) (j:na/ngah) (r:zd:18107/zd:8375) (q:draft)
nangaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you think/you consider) (d:<na>, you, joined to <ngaih>, the first part of <ngaihsun>, think, while the rest of the verb is written apart: {nangaih sun} is you think, {nangaih sutsut} is you keep thinking) (j:na/ngaih) (r:zd:23131/zd:22856) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wait/wait for/await) (d:<ngak>, wait, written as one word with the particle <na> that stands before a verb: wait for someone or something, be waiting there) (j:na/ngak) (r:zd:25016/zd:13067/zd:12214) (q:draft)
Nangarhar = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics/travel) (w:Nangarhar) (d:province in the east of Afghanistan) (r:zd:12179/zd:26124) (q:draft)
nangawna = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even in/even while) (d:<nangawn>, even, with the ending <a>, placed after the state or time it stresses: even in that state, even then) (j:nangawn/a) (r:zd:9425/zd:19641) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangawng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:nangawn) (r:zd:20116/zd:12763) (q:draft)
nangawngzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even/even ... too) (d:<nangawng> and <zong> written as one word, placed after the word it stresses: even this one too, marking an unexpected case) (j:nangawng/zong) (r:zd:16809/zd:19385) (q:draft)
nangawnzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even/even also) (d:<nangawn>, even, and <zong>, also, written as one word after the word they stress: even that one too) (j:nangawn/zong) (r:zd:19712) (q:draft)
nangbang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what do you) (d:<nang>, you, and <bang>, what, written as one word at the head of a question: you, what, as in {nangbang nasem}, what work do you do) (j:nang/bang) (r:zd:20736/zd:18046) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangbek = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:only you/you alone) (d:<nang> and <bek> written as one word: you and no one else, you by yourself) (j:nang/bek) (r:zd:14992/zd:21436/zd:23676) (q:draft)
nangding = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (j:nading) (r:zd:12871/zd:23446) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:ask for/request/pray) (d:<na> and <ngen> written as one word: asked for, or you ask; {thu nangen} is pray) (j:na/ngen) (r:zd:24199/zd:16360/zd:21257) (q:draft)
nangetnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:you want to ask for/you wish to request) (d:<na> and <ngetnop> written as one word: what you want to ask for, if you wish to request) (j:na/ngetnop) (r:zd:12550/zd:16360) (q:draft)
nangh = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (j:nang) (r:zd:19969/zd:19654) (q:draft)
nangh = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:weak/inferior/lowly) (d:weak, of low standing compared with others; {nangh zaw} is weaker, inferior) (r:zd:21862) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangkia = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:you alone/only you/by yourself) (d:<nang>, you, with the ending {-kia}, alone: you by yourself, you and no one else) (s:nangbek) (r:zd:22046/zd:23554/zd:17152) (q:draft)
nangleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:you and) (d:<nang>, you, and <leh>, and, written as one word: {nangleh kei} is you and I) (j:nang/leh) (r:zd:23943/zd:15584) (q:draft)
nanglehkei = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday/social) (w:you and I/you and me) (d:<nang>, <leh> and <kei> written as one word: you and I, the writer and the reader together) (j:nang/leh/kei) (r:zd:14654/zd:25124) (q:draft)
nanglekei = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:you and I/all of us) (d:<nang>, <le> and <kei> written as one word: you and I, meaning every ordinary one of us) (j:nang/le/kei) (r:zd:22709/zd:23382) (q:draft)
nanglenang = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:yourself) (d:<nang>, <le> and <nang> written as one word, literally you and you: yourself, as the one you act upon) (j:nang/le) (r:zd:21918/zd:20092/zd:21869) (q:draft)
nanglo = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:without you) (d:<nang> and <lo> written as one word: without you, as in {nanglo in}) (j:nang/lo) (r:zd:25222) (q:draft)
nangma = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:your) (d:possessive form of <nang>, placed before a noun; {nangma aa} is yours) (s:nangmah) (b:nang) (r:19.119.60)
nangpen = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:you/as for you) (d:<nang> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: you, as the one the sentence is about) (j:nang/pen) (r:zd:22282/zd:19266) (q:draft)
nangsang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:than you) (d:<nang>, you, with <sang> in the sense than, written as one word and often followed by <in>; compare <sangin>) (j:nang/sang) (r:zd:10929/zd:23487) (q:draft)
nangtawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:with you) (d:<nang>, you, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: together with you) (j:nang/tawh) (r:zd:11308/zd:20200) (q:draft)
nangthu = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:about you/on your own) (d:<nang> and <thu> written as one word: the matter of you, about you; with <in> after it, by your own decision, on your own) (j:nang/thu) (r:zd:19983/zd:14954) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangtung = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:on you/upon you/to you) (d:<nang>, you, and <tung>, upon, written as one word, mostly followed by <ah>: on you, toward you, in you) (j:nang/tung) (r:zd:11789/zd:23823) (q:draft)
nangzong = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:you also/you too) (d:<nang> and <zong> written as one word: you also, you as well) (j:nang/zong) (r:zd:22116/zd:21075/zd:21670) (q:draft)
nangzongh = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (j:nangzong) (r:zd:21989) (q:draft)
Nanjing = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Nanjing) (d:a city in Jiangsu Province in the east of China) (r:zd:14792) (q:draft)
nanu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:your mother) (d:<na>, your, and <nu>, mother, written as one word) (j:na/nu) (r:zd:22815/zd:23386) (q:draft)
naom = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you are/you stay) (d:<na>, you, and <om> written as one word: you are, you stay or live) (j:na/om) (r:zd:24054/zd:8668) (q:draft)
naom = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is/there are) (d:<om>, be there, written together with the particle <na> that stands before a verb in a statement of what is found to be so; it does not mean you here) (j:na/om) (r:zd:23343/zd:10821) (q:draft, low confidence)
napaam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:your surroundings/those around you/your neighbours) (d:<na>, your, and <paam> written as one word, in the pairs {nakiim napaam} and {naveng napaam}: the people and the place around you, your neighbours) (j:na/paam) (r:zd:22380/zd:11994) (q:draft)
napai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:you go) (d:<na>, you, and <pai>, go, written as one word: you go, your going) (j:na/pai) (r:zd:19915/zd:25624/zd:23528) (q:draft)
napaitektek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:go yourself/go in person) (d:<napai>, you go, and <tektek>, own or very, written as one word: you yourself going there in person) (j:napai/tektek) (r:zd:12317/zd:12822) (q:draft, low confidence)
napam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:your surroundings/around you) (d:<na>, your, and <pam>, vicinity, written as one word, used in the pair {na kiim napam}, all around you) (j:na/pam) (r:zd:14601/zd:17374) (q:draft)
napan = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:from) (d:the ending <na> written apart from its word and joined to <pan>, from: {sin napan} is from learning, {inndawl 12 napan} is from the twelfth floor; not <na>, you) (j:na/pan) (r:zd:25919/zd:12565/zd:16952) (q:draft)
napang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:take position/stand ready/wait for) (d:the narrative particle <na> and <pang> written as one word: took up a position, stood waiting for someone or something at a place) (j:na/pang) (r:zd:19763/zd:14758) (q:draft, low confidence)
napate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:your fathers/your father) (d:<na>, your, and <pate>, fathers, written as one word; {nanu napate} is your parents) (j:na/pate) (r:zd:23552/zd:23386) (q:draft)
napen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:the noun ending <na> written apart from its verb and joined to the topic marker <pen>: {lungkham napen} is {lungkhamna pen}, as for the worry) (j:na/pen) (r:zd:19427/zd:22638) (q:draft)
napeuh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:wherever/everywhere that) (d:the noun ending {-na}, place of, written apart from its verb and joined to <peuh>, any: with <ah> after it, in every place where; {apai napeuh ah} is wherever they go) (j:na/peuh) (r:zd:11457/zd:20513) (q:draft)
naphak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:you reach/you number) (d:<na>, you, and <phak>, reach, written as one word: you reach an age, or you come to a number) (j:na/phak) (r:zd:11702/zd:21377) (q:draft)
naphawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:remember/notice/realise) (d:<na> and <phawk> written as one word: remember, be aware of, realise; before <un> it is a command, remember; {khua naphawk} is be conscious) (j:na/phawk) (r:zd:14708/zd:11866/zd:22371) (q:draft)
naphung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:your clan/your lineage) (d:<na> and <phung> written as one word: your clan, mostly paired with {na beh}) (j:na/phung) (r:zd:22380/zd:12912) (q:draft)
naphut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:founded/established) (d:<na>, already, and <phut>, set up, written as one word: set up or founded at an earlier time) (j:na/phut) (r:zd:19273/zd:19381) (q:draft)
napia = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:gave/give) (d:<na> as the particle before a verb for what others did or what was already done, with <pia>, give, written as one word: he or they gave; the giver is not <nang>, you, and <uh> or <uhhi> often follows) (r:zd:15048/zd:16428) (q:draft, low confidence)
napiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you give) (d:<na> and <piak> written as one word: you give, that which you give, in dependent clauses) (j:na/piak) (r:zd:19249/zd:13076/zd:18107) (q:draft)
napiaksa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:that you gave/that you have given) (d:<na>, you, and <piaksa>, given, written as one word, placed before the thing given) (j:na/piaksa) (r:zd:12336) (q:draft)
napii = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (j:napi) (r:zd:20477) (q:draft)
napil = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:you are wise/you become learned) (d:<na> and <pil> written as one word: you are or become wise or educated) (j:na/pil) (r:zd:23680/zd:23386) (q:draft)
napin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/though/even though) (d:<napi> with the ending {-in}, placed after a verb: even though this is so) (b:napi) (r:zd:17204/zd:12214/zd:22544) (q:draft)
napnit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/social) (w:blow one's nose) (d:<nap> and <nit> written as one word: blow the nose; of persons, not even want to blow the nose at them, a way of showing contempt) (j:nap/nit) (r:zd:25343/zd:15583) (q:draft, low confidence)
napsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:kiss/let kiss/let smell) (d:<nap>, kiss or smell, with the <sak> that follows a verb: give a kiss to someone, or let someone kiss or smell something) (j:nap/sak) (r:zd:15816/zd:17495) (q:draft, low confidence)
napuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:had taken/already sent) (d:<na>, already, and <puak>, send or bring, written as one word: someone had already taken or sent a person or thing somewhere) (j:na/puak) (r:zd:21419) (q:draft, low confidence)
napuak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:you bring/you carry) (d:<na>, you, and <puak>, send or bring, written as one word: you bring or carry something to others) (j:na/puak) (r:zd:16428) (q:draft, low confidence)
napuansilh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:your clothes/your clothing) (d:<na>, your, and <puansilh>, clothing, written as one word: the clothes you wear) (j:na/puansilh) (r:zd:19707) (q:draft, low confidence)
napum = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:body) (w:your body/your person) (d:<na>, your, and <pum>, body, written as one word; {napum tungah} is on your person) (j:na/pum) (r:zd:14992) (q:draft, low confidence)
napumpi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:body) (w:your body) (d:<na> and <pumpi> written as one word: your body) (j:na/pumpi) (r:zd:22856/zd:16806) (q:draft)
Narathiwat = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Narathiwat) (d:a province in the far south of Thailand, near the border with Malaysia) (r:zd:17368) (q:draft)
Narcotics = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/politics) (w:narcotics/illegal drugs) (d:forbidden drugs; mostly inside English names of offices, a few times as a word of its own beside <guihtheih khamtheih>) (o:English) (r:zd:13176/zd:17281) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nargis = (i:1) (t:name) (f:nature) (w:Nargis/Cyclone Nargis) (d:the cyclone that struck the Irrawaddy delta of Myanmar in 2008 and killed many thousands) (r:zd:22391/zd:13039) (q:draft)
nasa = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:think/find/regard as) (d:<na> written together with <sa>, feel or regard, after a quality word such as <hoih> or after <bangci>: find something to be so; {bangci nasa hiam} is what do you think of it) (r:zd:19338/zd:21102/zd:15727) (q:draft)
nasa = (i:3) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:hurt/feel pain) (d:<na>, pain, with <sa>, feel: feel pain in the body or be pained in the heart; not the verb ending of the first sense) (r:zd:24276/zd:12264) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasakgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:hurt badly/injure severely) (d:<nasak>, cause pain, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word: do serious harm to a part of the body) (j:nasak/gawp) (r:zd:12996/zd:12264) (q:draft)
nasakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:feel pain with/share the pain of/sympathise) (d:feel the hurt of another as one's own, with the ending <pih>, together with; paired with <thuakpih>, suffer with) (r:ts:4564) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasalua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find too much/feel very keenly) (d:<nasa>, find or feel, with <lua>, too much or very: find something too hard or too costly, or feel hurt very much) (j:nasa/lua) (r:zd:12387/zd:14597) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:call/summon) (d:<na> and <sam> written as one word: you call; also with the <na> that stands before a verb in a report or a command, they called, call) (j:na/sam) (r:zd:19633/zd:14981) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:beat/strike/hit) (d:the verb prefix <na> and <sat>, strike, written as one word: beat or strike someone) (r:zd:18244) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:commanded/told) (d:<na>, the particle for an earlier action, and <sawl>, command, written as one word: had commanded, told someone to do it) (j:na/sawl) (r:zd:23670) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nasdaq = (i:1) (t:name) (f:work) (w:Nasdaq) (d:a stock exchange in the United States on which companies are listed) (o:English) (r:zd:19453) (q:draft)
naseem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (j:nasem) (r:zd:23590/zd:25200/zd:19733) (q:draft)
nasem = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:work/serve) (d:do work, or serve an employer. From <na>, work, with <sem>, do, written as one word) (s:sem) (b:sem) (r:4.8.15) (q:draft)
nasema = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:work/having worked) (d:<nasem>, work, and the linking <a> written as one word: working and, having worked and) (j:nasem/a) (r:zd:20172/zd:9252) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasemding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:to work/in order to work) (d:<nasem> and <ding> written as one word: who will work or in order to work; {nasemding in apai} is went in order to work and {nasemding mi} is people to do the work) (j:nasem/ding) (r:zd:15761/zd:16634/zd:18104) (q:draft)
nasemkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:a worker/an employee) (d:<nasem>, one who works, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a worker, an employee) (j:nasem/khat) (r:zd:20508/zd:15575) (q:draft)
nasemkhawm = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:work together/work with/cooperate) (d:<nasem>, work, with <khawm>, together, used as a verb: work together with someone, usually after <tawh>, with; not the person who works alongside) (r:zd:22171/zd:22217/zd:23569) (q:draft)
nasemlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be still working/be at work) (d:<nasem>, work, and <lai>, still or while, written as one word: be still working or in operation, or be at work at the time) (j:nasem/lai) (r:zd:15471) (q:draft)
nasemlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:not work/be out of work/be out of order) (d:<nasem> and <lo> written as one word: not working, said of a person without work and of an organ or a machine that does not function) (j:nasem/lo) (r:zd:16245/zd:19176/zd:14734) (q:draft)
nasemmi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:worker/employee/labourer) (d:<nasem> with <mi>: a person who works for an employer) (s:nasem) (r:zd:24955/zd:11755) (q:draft)
nasempa = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work) (w:worker/employee/staff member) (d:a man who works in a job, office or shop, named after his workplace or employer as in {kumpi nasempa}, a government employee, and {NGO nasempa}; the woman is <nasemnu>) (r:zd:16900/zd:16137/zd:17501) (q:draft)
nasempen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:workers/staff) (d:<nasem>, worker or work, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the workers, those who work, as the topic of the sentence) (j:nasem/pen) (r:zd:17974/zd:14704) (q:draft)
nasemsem = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:keep working/work on and on) (d:<nasem>, work, with <sem> doubled: go on working without stopping) (b:nasem) (r:zd:15571/zd:25914) (q:draft)
nasemsem = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:hurt more and more/ache increasingly) (d:<na>, hurt, and <semsem>, more and more, written as one word: said of hands and feet that ache more and more in an illness) (j:na/semsem) (r:zd:23832) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasemte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work) (w:workers/employees/staff) (d:plural of <nasem>: people who work for pay in a company, a hospital or another country, where the Bible sense is the servants of a master; <gamdangmi nasemte> are foreign workers) (r:zd:21876/zd:23846/zd:17102) (q:draft)
nasemten = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work/social) (w:workers/servants) (d:<nasemte>, workers or servants, with the subject marker <in> shortened and written as one word: the workers, as the doer of the action) (j:nasemte/in) (r:zd:17485/zd:17398) (q:draft)
nasemteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:all the workers/all the staff) (d:<nasem>, worker, with <teng>, here all of them, written as one word: all the workers, the whole staff) (j:nasem/teng) (r:zd:13190/zd:20013) (q:draft)
nasemthak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:new worker/new staff/new employee) (d:<nasem>, worker, and <thak>, new, written as one word: a worker who has just started) (j:nasem/thak) (r:zd:19932) (q:draft)
nasemthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:can work/be able to work) (d:<nasem>, work, and <thei>, can, written as one word) (j:nasem/thei) (r:zd:17448/zd:11109) (q:draft)
nasemzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be able to work/work well) (d:<nasem>, work, with <zo>, be able, written as one word: be able to work or to get work done; {nasemzo nawnlo} is no longer able to work) (j:nasem/zo) (r:zd:25768) (q:draft)
nasep = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:work/job/service/duty) (d:the work a person does or is given to do: a task, a duty, an occupation; from <na>, work, and <sep>, do) (r:14.34.13)
nasep hun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/time) (w:working hours/work time/working time) (d:<nasep>, work, and <hun>, time: the hours or days of work of a job, a heading in job notices, followed by the hours or the number of days) (r:zd:12695/zd:10892) (q:draft)
nasep khawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:stop work/quit work/leave a job) (d:<nasep>, work, and <khawl>, here stop or rest: to stop working, either for a time or by leaving a job; with <sak> after it, to make somebody stop work, to suspend or dismiss) (r:zd:21939/zd:22704/zd:23138) (q:draft)
nasep khop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:work together/cooperate/collaborate) (d:<nasep>, work, with <khop>, together: do work jointly with others; the form used before <ding>, <theih>, <zia> and <pih>, and the partner stands before it with <tawh>) (r:zd:23317/zd:19335) (q:draft)
nasep kician = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:steady job/regular work/proper employment) (d:<nasep>, work, and <kician>, firm or sound: a steady, proper job; commonly with {nei lo}, to have no regular work; as a statement, {nasep kician hi} says that the work is done soundly) (r:zd:21032/zd:18119) (q:draft)
nasep neilote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:the unemployed/jobless people) (d:<nasep>, work, and <neilote>, those who do not have: people without a job, the unemployed; the group they belong to stands before it) (r:zd:23048) (q:draft)
nasepdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:way of working/working method) (d:<nasep>, work, with <dan>, manner: how a person or body works, how a thing does its work) (s:nasepzia/sepdan) (r:zd:19302/zd:14867/zd:19624) (q:draft)
nasepdang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:other work/another job) (d:<nasep>, work, and <dang>, other, written as one word: a different job, other work) (j:nasep/dang) (r:zd:11961/zd:20197) (q:draft)
nasepding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:work to do/task/job) (d:<nasep>, work, with <ding>: the work that is to be done, a task or a job to take up) (j:nasep/ding) (r:zd:12174/zd:25768) (q:draft)
nasephoih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:good job/good work) (d:<nasep>, work, and <hoih>, good, written as one word: a good job or good employment) (j:nasep/hoih) (r:zd:21918/zd:19342) (q:draft)
nasephun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/time) (w:working time/working hours/time to work) (d:<nasep>, work, and <hun>, time, written as one word) (j:nasep/hun) (r:zd:19464/zd:17152) (q:draft)
nasepkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:a job/a work/a task) (d:<nasep>, work, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a job, one work) (j:nasep/khat) (r:zd:20035) (q:draft)
nasepkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:work together/cooperate) (d:<nasep>, work, and <khop>, together, written as one word: work together, cooperate; also as a noun, cooperation) (s:sepkhop) (j:nasep/khop) (r:zd:17383/ts:8052) (q:draft)
nasepkhopna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:cooperation/joint work/partnership) (d:<nasep>, work, with <khopna>, doing together: working together, or a body in which people work together) (j:nasep/khopna) (r:zd:20181/zd:17814) (q:draft)
nasepkhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:work permit/right to work/permission to work) (d:<nasep>, work, with <khuan.3>, permission: the leave or right to do a job, as given to refugees or held by a person in his post) (s:sepkhuan) (j:nasep/khuan) (r:zd:11109/zd:12792) (q:draft)
nasepkuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:go to work/set out for work) (d:<nasep>, work, and <kuan>, set out, written as one word: go out to one's work) (j:nasep/kuan) (r:zd:12571/zd:14763) (q:draft)
nasepkum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/time) (w:term of office/working year/year of service) (d:<nasep> and <kum> written as one word: the year or the years for which someone holds an office or does a work) (j:nasep/kum) (r:zd:13251/zd:12414) (q:draft)
naseploh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:not working/off duty) (d:<nasep>, work, and <loh>, not, written as one word: being without work or off duty; {naseploh hunsung} is while off duty) (j:nasep/loh) (r:zd:17372/zd:12274) (q:draft)
nasepnei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:employer) (d:<nasep>, work, and <nei>, have, written as one word: one who has work to give, an employer; also said of people who have a job) (j:nasep/nei) (r:zd:17102/zd:12882) (q:draft)
nasepneilo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work) (w:unemployed/jobless/out of work) (d:<nasep>, work, and <neilo>, not have, written as one word: having no work; also the people who have none) (j:nasep/neilo) (r:zd:23487/zd:17572) (q:draft)
naseppen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:the work/the job) (d:<nasep>, work, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the work or job, as the thing spoken about) (j:nasep/pen) (r:zd:17668/zd:12641/zd:16735) (q:draft)
naseppihding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:to be a co-worker/as an employee) (d:<naseppih>, fellow worker, and <ding>, to be, written as one word: for someone to work with, as when an employer calls a worker) (j:naseppih/ding) (r:zd:23569) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasepthak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:new job/new work) (d:<nasep> and <thak> written as one word: a new job, newly created work) (j:nasep/thak) (r:zd:17572/zd:11602) (q:draft)
naseptheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:be able to work/be allowed to work) (d:<nasep> and <theih> written as one word, mostly before <nading>: so as to be able or permitted to work, as with a work permit) (j:nasep/theih) (r:zd:19143/zd:13218/zd:21372) (q:draft)
naseptheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:work permit/permission to work) (d:<nasep>, work, with <theih>, be able, and the noun suffix <na>: the right to work in a country, or the document that gives it) (j:nasep/theih/na) (r:zd:12938/zd:19143) (q:draft)
naseptheihna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work) (w:ability to work) (d:<nasep>, work, with <theih>, be able, and the noun suffix <na>: what one is able to do in work) (j:nasep/theih/na) (r:zd:23037) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasepvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:work matter/business/work affairs) (d:<nasep>, work, with <vai>, matter, written as one word: a matter of work, business; {nasepvai tawh} is on business) (j:nasep/vai) (r:zd:15636/zd:15073/zd:18024) (q:draft)
nasepzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:way of working/working method/procedure) (d:<nasep>, work, with <zia>, manner: how work is done, how something works) (s:sepzia) (r:zd:16862/zd:21856) (q:draft)
nasepzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:work also/the job too) (d:<nasep>, work, and <zong>, also, written as one word: the work too, jobs as well) (j:nasep/zong) (r:zd:14526/zd:14665) (q:draft)
nashia = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:nasia) (r:zd:17011/zd:22412) (q:draft)
Nashville = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Nashville) (d:city in the state of Tennessee in the United States, home of a Zomi community) (r:zd:18026) (q:draft)
nasi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:you die) (d:<na>, you, and <si>, die, written as one word; the same letters are also the Malay word for rice in names of dishes such as Nasi Lemak) (j:na/si) (r:zd:23737) (q:draft, low confidence)
nasia = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:greatly/tremendously/impressively) (d:as an intensifier with no bad meaning, of something done or found on a grand scale: {nasia takin} before a verb is in a big way, and {nasia} before <thupi> is very grand) (r:zd:20920/zd:22203) (q:draft)
nasiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:you are skilled/you are good at) (d:<na>, you, and <siam>, skilled, written as one word: you are skilled, you are good at the thing named before it) (j:na/siam) (r:zd:25512/zd:21083/zd:23386) (q:draft)
nasiatak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:severely/intensely/very hard/greatly) (d:<nasia> and <tak> written as one word, often followed by <in>: to a very great degree, of bad things and also of effort or celebration) (j:nasia/tak) (r:ts:3085/zd:23022/zd:15671) (q:draft)
nasiatakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:greatly/intensely/strongly/vigorously) (d:<nasia>, intense, with <takin>, which makes an adverb, written as one word: to a great degree, with great force or effort) (s:nakpi) (j:nasia/takin) (r:zd:16254/zd:14551/zd:24743) (q:draft)
nasiatleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:if severe/when severe) (d:<nasiat> and <leh> written as one word: if or when an illness is severe) (j:nasiat/leh) (r:zd:24276/zd:21323) (q:draft)
nasim = (i:2) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:you read) (d:not the word for respect: <na>, you, written together with <sim>, read, mostly in a request to the reader such as {nasim un}, read it, and {lai nasim}, you read the text) (r:zd:19397/zd:19591/zd:21918) (q:draft)
nasimbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:you read further/read more) (d:<na>, you, and <simbeh>, read more, written as one word: mostly a request to the reader to read more about a matter, as {nasimbeh in}) (j:na/simbeh) (r:zd:15724/zd:11664) (q:draft)
nasimnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:you want to read) (d:<na>, you, and <simnop>, want to read, written as one word: if or what you want to read) (j:na/simnop) (r:zd:14941) (q:draft)
nasimsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/education) (w:you read on/go on reading) (d:<na>, <sim> and <suak> written as one word: you read on, in the request to the reader {nasimsuak vemaw}, do read on) (j:na/sim/suak) (r:zd:21075) (q:draft)
nasin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:you learn/you study) (d:<na> and <sin> written as one word: you learn or study; also you try something) (j:na/sin) (r:zd:20787/zd:23016) (q:draft)
nasuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you become) (d:<na> and <suah>, become, written as one word: you become, your becoming) (j:na/suah) (r:zd:23554/zd:17672) (q:draft)
nasuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you become) (d:<na>, you, and <suak>, become, written as one word: you become, you turn out to be) (j:na/suak) (r:zd:21991/zd:15972) (q:draft)
nasuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:your descendants/your offspring) (d:<na>, your, and <suan>, descendant, written as one word; mostly in the pair {nasuan nakhak}, your descendants, your children and their children) (j:na/suan) (r:zd:21050/zd:24421/zd:8375) (q:draft)
nasum = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work/everyday) (w:your money) (d:<na>, your, and <sum>, money, written as one word) (j:na/sum) (r:zd:19774/zd:11308) (q:draft)
nasungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/body) (w:inside you/within you) (d:<na>, your, and <sungah>, inside, written as one word: within you) (j:na/sungah) (r:zd:21869/zd:20553) (q:draft)
nasunglam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/everyday) (w:your inside/your inner self) (d:<na> and <sunglam> written as one word: the inside of you, your inner being) (j:na/sunglam) (r:zd:21876/zd:21869) (q:draft)
nata = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:your child/your children) (d:<na>, your, and <ta>, child, written as one word; {nazi nata} is your wife and children and {natu nata} your grandchildren and children, your descendants) (j:na/ta) (r:zd:19330/zd:15772/zd:22159) (q:draft)
natampi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:many things/much work) (d:<na>, thing or work, and <tampi>, many, written as one word: many things, a lot of work) (j:na/tampi) (r:zd:23443) (q:draft, low confidence)
natapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:your son) (d:<na>, your, and <tapa>, son, written as one word) (j:na/tapa) (r:zd:19843/zd:16398) (q:draft)
natate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:your children) (d:<na> and <tate> written as one word: your children) (j:na/tate) (r:zd:24248/zd:19850) (q:draft)
natawh = (i:1) (t:prep) (f:everyday) (w:with/by/through) (d:the noun ending {-na} written apart from its verb and joined to <tawh>: with or by the doing of it; {hanciam natawh} is {hanciamna tawh}, through the effort) (r:zd:19952/zd:16136/zd:23319) (q:draft)
natawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hold/carry) (d:<na> and <tawi> written as one word: you hold, what you carry in the hand, as a card or a weapon) (j:na/tawi) (r:zd:15300/zd:15321) (q:draft)
natawm = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even) (d:placed after the word it stresses, marking an extreme or unexpected case; used like <nangawn>) (s:nangawn) (r:zd:20410/zd:21886) (q:draft)
natel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:you understand) (d:<na> and <tel> written as one word: you understand; {natel kei leh} is if you do not understand) (j:na/tel) (r:zd:17327/zd:11034) (q:draft)
nateng = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:dwell/settle/live) (d:the particle <na> before the verb <teng>, dwell, written as one word: have lived or settled in a place; not {na teng}, all the things) (r:zd:11325/zd:23554) (q:draft)
natgual = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:influenza/flu) (d:a common illness that passes from person to person, such as influenza) (r:zd:23830/zd:25148) (q:draft)
nathak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:new thing/innovation) (d:<na>, thing, and <thak>, new, written as one word: something new, a new idea or invention) (j:na/thak) (r:zd:21989/zd:23191) (q:draft)
nathau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/everyday) (w:your gun) (d:<na>, your, and <thau.1>, gun, written as one word: your gun) (j:na/thau) (r:zd:11799/zd:17556) (q:draft)
nathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you know) (d:<na>, you, and <thei>, know, written as one word; {nathei uhhiam} is do you know, to several people) (j:na/thei) (r:zd:16951/zd:23112) (q:draft)
nathei = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:know already/have known) (d:the preverbal <na>, already or as it turned out, and <thei>, know, written as one word: someone other than the hearer knew it already) (j:na/thei) (r:zd:24594) (q:draft, low confidence)
natheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you know) (d:<na>, you, with <theih>, the form of <thei>, know, written as one word: that you know; {natheih leh} is if you know) (j:na/theih) (r:zd:12028/zd:24289/zd:19834) (q:draft)
natheihnop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:you want to know) (d:<na>, you, and <theihnop>, want to know, written as one word; {natheihnop leh} is if you want to know) (j:na/theihnop) (r:zd:11342) (q:draft)
nathu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/everyday) (w:your word/your matter) (d:<na>, your, and <thu>, word or matter, written as one word; in prayer and scripture it is the word of God. In {lungdam nathu}, good news, the letters are divided differently: it is {lungdamna thu}) (j:na/thu) (r:zd:10794/zd:19850) (q:draft)
nathuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:you suffer/you undergo) (d:<na>, you, and <thuak>, suffer, written as one word) (j:na/thuak) (r:zd:21285) (q:draft)
nathuak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:suffer/undergo/receive) (d:<thuak>, suffer, with the particle <na> before it, as in <ana>, written as one word: had to bear something, as blows, hardship or blame) (j:na/thuak) (r:zd:23432/zd:26444) (q:draft, low confidence)
nathute = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:your things/your matters) (d:<na>, your, and <thute>, matters, written as one word: your matters, what you have to say or settle) (j:na/thute) (r:zd:20263) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nationalism = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:nationalism) (d:devotion to the interests and standing of one's own people or nation; {Zomi Nationalism} is the national feeling of the Zomi) (o:English) (r:zd:15543/ts:11162/ts:3341) (q:draft)
natlehsat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:sickness and injury/medical trouble) (d:<nat>, <leh> and <sat> written as one word: illness and bodily harm, a case of sickness or injury) (j:nat/leh/sat) (r:zd:24022/zd:14867) (q:draft, low confidence)
natna dalna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:disease prevention/immunity/protection against disease) (d:<natna>, disease, and <dalna>, barrier: the warding off of disease; {natna dalna zatui} is a vaccine, {natna dalna tha} is the immunity of the body, and {natna dalna dingin} is in order to prevent a disease; the name of the disease stands before it) (r:zd:25215/zd:20640/zd:24458) (q:draft)
natna lungno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:germ/pathogen/virus/microbe) (d:<natna>, disease, and <lungno>, worm: the tiny living thing that causes a disease, a germ, virus or bacterium; {natna lungno ngah} is to be infected) (r:zd:16949/zd:20961) (q:draft)
natna ngah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health) (w:be infected/catch a disease/fall ill) (d:<natna>, disease, and <ngah>, get: catch a disease, be infected; {natna ngah mi} are the infected persons, the cases counted in a report) (r:zd:24369/zd:25168/zd:24278) (q:draft)
natna satna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:sickness/illness/affliction) (d:<natna>, sickness, with the rhyming <satna>: a paired expression for sickness and bodily suffering of every kind; used like a single noun, often beside <haksatna>, hardship) (r:zd:16254/zd:19681) (q:draft)
natnanei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health) (w:having a disease/diseased/sick) (d:<natna>, disease, and <nei>, have, written as one word; {natnanei mi} is a person who has a disease) (j:natna/nei) (r:zd:22652) (q:draft)
NATO = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:NATO) (d:the North Atlantic Treaty Organization, a military alliance of North American and European states) (r:zd:25601/zd:11014) (q:draft)
natsiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be badly damaged/be wrecked) (d:of a building, a vehicle or a thing: be badly damaged by fire, an accident or an earthquake; mostly as {natsiat mahmah}) (r:zd:15512/zd:15842/zd:16101) (q:draft)
nattunza = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:fever medicine/malaria medicine) (d:medicine against <nattun>, fever, here malaria; the articles use it of quinine and chloroquine) (r:zd:20545/zd:23815) (q:draft)
natu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:your grandchild) (d:<na>, your, and <tu>, grandchild, written as one word; {natu nata} is your grandchildren and children) (j:na/tu) (r:zd:21473) (q:draft, low confidence)
natuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:meet with/encounter) (d:<na>, you, and <tuah>, meet with, written as one word: you meet with, said of trouble such as arrest) (j:na/tuah) (r:zd:19237/zd:20418) (q:draft)
natuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:you meet with/you experience) (d:<na> and <tuak> written as one word: you meet with or go through something, such as trouble or arrest; {natuak leh} is if it happens to you) (j:na/tuak) (r:zd:23538/zd:23487) (q:draft)
natun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:you arrive/you reach) (d:<na>, you, and <tun>, arrive or reach, written as one word: you arrive, you reach, before words such as <ciangin> and <theihna>) (j:na/tun) (r:zd:15424/zd:11775) (q:draft)
natung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:arrive/have arrived) (d:<na>, the verb prefix for something that has already happened, written as one word with <tung>, arrive: arrived, got there) (j:na/tung) (r:zd:16337/zd:25392) (q:draft)
natung = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:you arrive/you reach) (d:<na>, you, and <tung>, arrive, written as one word) (j:na/tung) (r:zd:20158) (q:draft, low confidence)
natuntheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:you can reach/you can arrive) (d:<na>, you, and <tuntheih>, be able to reach, written as one word; mostly before <nadingin>, so that you can reach) (j:na/tuntheih) (r:zd:12280/zd:12504) (q:draft)
natut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:you sit/when you sit) (d:<na.1> and <tut>, the form of <tu>, sit, written as one word before words such as <ciangin> and <leh>: when or if you sit) (j:na/tut) (r:zd:12886/zd:25686) (q:draft)
natveh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/social/religion) (w:visit the sick) (d:<nat> and <veh> written as one word: go to see someone who is ill; also as a noun, a visit to the sick) (j:nat/veh) (r:zd:19536/zd:12827) (q:draft)
natvehna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/health) (w:sick visit/visiting the sick/sympathy gift) (d:<nat>, be ill, with <vehna>, visiting: a visit to a sick person, and the money given to the sick or their family on such a visit) (r:zd:24029/zd:15123) (q:draft)
nau = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:child) (d:a baby or small child, also the child in the womb; {nau paai} is to be pregnant and {nau suak} to give birth) (s:naungek/naungeek)
naubang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:family) (w:like a child/like a baby) (d:<nau>, child, with <bang>, like: in songs and poems said of weeping, as in {naubang kap}, weep like a child) (j:nau/bang) (r:zd:24086) (q:draft, low confidence)
naucin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/education) (w:childcare/child minding) (d:<nau>, child, with the verb look after that is also in <naucing>: the looking after of small children; {naucin sang} is a nursery school) (r:zd:24029/zd:17049/zd:11891) (q:draft)
naudalna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/family) (w:contraception/contraceptive/birth control) (d:<nau>, child, and <dalna>, prevention, written as one word: the prevention of pregnancy, and a device or medicine used for it) (j:nau/dalna) (r:zd:12392/zd:16259) (q:draft)
naudap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/home/health) (w:nappy/diaper/pad) (d:<nau>, baby, with <dap>, pad: an absorbent cloth or pad, as worn by a baby) (r:zd:15984) (q:draft, low confidence)
naugil = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:pregnancy/pregnant belly) (d:the state of carrying a child, or the belly of a woman who is pregnant, not the organ; {naugil tawh} is while pregnant, and a number of weeks or months after {a naugil} says how far the pregnancy is) (r:zd:12128/zd:23540) (q:draft)
nauhalna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/family) (w:contraception/birth control/birth spacing) (d:keeping from becoming pregnant, or leaving years between children; {nauhalna zatui} is a contraceptive medicine) (r:zd:22151/zd:24476) (q:draft)
naukem = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/work) (w:nanny/babysitter/childminder) (d:<nau>, child, with <kem>, look after: a person, usually a woman or girl, who looks after a small child, often as paid work) (s:naucing) (r:zd:16900/zd:12087/zd:21476) (q:draft)
naukemding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/work) (w:to look after a child/as a nanny) (d:<naukem> and <ding> written as one word: someone to be a nanny, or in order to look after a child) (j:naukem/ding) (r:zd:16095/zd:15315) (q:draft, low confidence)
naukemnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/work) (w:nanny/babysitter/childminder) (d:<naukem>, one who looks after a child, with <nu> for a woman, written as one word: a woman or girl who looks after a small child) (s:naukem) (j:naukem/nu) (r:zd:19565/zd:21476) (q:draft)
naukepna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/work) (w:childcare/child minding/nursery) (d:<nau> and <kepna> written as one word: the minding of small children, and the place where children are minded while the parents work) (j:nau/kepna) (r:zd:20721/zd:20508) (q:draft)
naukhak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/family) (w:birth prevention/contraception) (d:<nau>, child, with <khak>, shut: stopping the birth of children; named beside <nauhalna>) (r:zd:24476) (q:draft, low confidence)
nauluai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/home) (w:cradle) (d:a hanging or rocking bed for a baby; {nauluai vei} is rock the cradle) (r:zd:26026/zd:21530) (q:draft)
naumilim = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/family) (w:doll) (d:<nau>, child, and <milim>, image, written as one word: a toy figure of a person for children to play with) (j:nau/milim) (r:zd:22983) (q:draft)
naumin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:baby's name/child's name) (d:<nau>, child, and <min>, name, written as one word: the name given to a baby, also the name entered for a child on a birth certificate) (j:nau/min) (r:zd:25573) (q:draft, low confidence)
naunau = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:eagerly/in a rush) (d:placed after a verb, of many doing the same thing: all hurrying to do it, eagerly and one after another) (r:zd:14563/zd:23676) (q:draft, low confidence)
naunawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/family) (w:breast milk/mother's milk) (d:<nau>, baby, with <nawi>, milk: the milk a mother gives her baby; {naunawi piak} is to breastfeed) (r:zd:14606/zd:12267) (q:draft)
naunei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:have a baby/bear a child) (d:<nau>, baby, with <nei>, have, written as one word: have a baby, become a mother) (j:nau/nei) (r:zd:16582) (q:draft)
nauneih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:have a child/bear a child) (d:<nau>, child, and <neih>, have, written as one word; {nauneih theih nading} is in order to be able to have a child) (j:nau/neih) (r:zd:19593/zd:22499) (q:draft)
naunen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:small child/little one/infant) (d:<nau>, child, with <nen>, small: very young children, named after <naupang> or with <nupi>, women) (r:zd:15307/zd:24270) (q:draft)
Naungcho = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Nawnghkio/Naungcho) (d:town in the north of Shan State, Myanmar, on the road from Mandalay to Lashio) (r:zd:17067/ts:8304) (q:draft)
naungek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:baby/infant) (d:a baby or very young child; {nawi ne naungek} is a baby still at the breast) (s:naungeek) (q:draft)
naungeka = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:family/religion) (w:as a baby) (d:<naungek>, baby, with <a> written on to it, in {naungeka suak}: be born as a baby) (j:naungek/a) (r:zd:21780) (q:draft, low confidence)
naungekin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:family) (w:as a baby/the baby) (d:<naungek> with <in>: as a baby, said of being born; also the baby as the one who acts) (j:naungek/in) (r:zd:21780/zd:22065) (q:draft)
naungekno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:baby/newborn/infant) (d:<naungek>, baby, with <no>, here young or little: a very small baby) (s:naungek) (b:naungek) (r:zd:11924/zd:18872) (q:draft)
naungekpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:the baby) (d:<naungek> and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the baby, as the one spoken about) (j:naungek/pen) (r:zd:20721/zd:17479) (q:draft)
nauno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/health) (w:small child/little one/baby/unborn child) (d:<nau>, child, with the diminutive <no>: a little child or baby, also the child in the womb; {sangkah nauno} is a young school child) (s:naungek) (b:nau) (r:zd:23424/zd:19593) (q:draft)
naupaaikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:be already pregnant) (d:<naupaai>, be pregnant, and <khin>, already, written as one word) (j:naupaai/khin) (r:zd:14648/zd:16332) (q:draft)
naupai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/family) (j:naupaai) (r:zd:14887/zd:16606) (q:draft)
naupaii = (i:3) (t:v) (f:health/family) (w:be pregnant/pregnant) (d:be with child, said of a woman, as in {tua numei naupaii hi}; placed before or after <nupi> or before <te> it describes the women who are pregnant, where the other senses name the state itself) (r:zd:15294/zd:20004/zd:20486) (q:draft)
naupaite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/family) (w:pregnant women/expectant mothers) (d:<naupai>, pregnant, with the plural <te>: those who are pregnant) (b:naupai) (j:naupai/te) (r:zd:25393) (q:draft)
naupan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/time) (w:childhood/child) (d:form of <naupang>, child, used before another word: {naupan lai} is childhood, the time when one was a child, and {naupan vai} is a childish thing) (b:naupang) (r:zd:24069/zd:11135/zd:16340) (q:draft)
naupang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (w:child) (r:1.4.25) of offspring
naupangkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (w:a child) (d:<naupang>, child, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a child, one child) (j:naupang/khat) (r:zd:25926/zd:16170) (q:draft)
naupanglai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/everyday) (w:still a child/still young) (d:<naupang>, child, and <lai>, here still, written as one word: be still a child, be very young) (j:naupang/lai) (r:zd:12311/zd:12763) (q:draft)
naupangluai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/home) (w:child swing/baby swing) (d:<naupang>, child, and <luai>, cradle, written as one word: a hanging seat in which a small child is swung, said of a toddler swing sold by a toy company) (j:naupang/luai) (r:zd:11445) (q:draft, low confidence)
naupangngek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:infant/baby/small child) (d:<naupang>, child, with <ngek>, tiny and tender, written as one word: a very young child, a newborn) (j:naupang/ngek) (r:zd:17062/zd:20440) (q:draft)
naupangnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (w:girl/little girl) (d:<naupang>, child, with the female ending {-nu}: a girl child) (s:numeino) (b:naupang) (r:zd:12618/zd:23431) (q:draft)
naupangpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/everyday) (w:the child) (d:<naupang>, child, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: the child, as the one spoken about) (j:naupang/pen) (r:zd:13179/zd:19894/zd:12788) (q:draft)
naupangtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/everyday) (w:with a child/with children) (d:<naupang>, child, and <tawh>, with, written as one word) (j:naupang/tawh) (r:zd:14535/zd:20056) (q:draft)
naupangvai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (w:childishness/childish matter) (d:<naupang> and <vai> written as one word: a matter of children, what is childish; {naupangvai takin} is in a childish way) (j:naupang/vai) (r:zd:15767/zd:20716) (q:draft)
naupangzong = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (w:children also/child as well) (d:<naupang>, child, and <zong>, also, written as one word: children too, even a child) (j:naupang/zong) (r:zd:14528/zd:13300) (q:draft)
nauphiat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/family) (w:abortion) (d:<nau>, child, with <phiat>, wipe out: the ending of a pregnancy, abortion) (r:zd:25323/zd:13048) (q:draft)
nauphiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/family) (w:abortion) (d:<nauphiat>, abortion, with the noun ending {-na}: the act of ending a pregnancy) (b:nauphiat) (r:zd:24892/zd:24896) (q:draft)
Nauru = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Nauru) (d:small island country in the Pacific Ocean) (r:zd:23198) (q:draft)
nausuak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:health/family) (w:give birth/deliver) (d:{nausuak} used as a verb: bear a child, with the mother as subject and often a place before it, as in {lamzikpi tungah nausuak}, give birth on the road) (r:zd:14931/zd:14776/zd:14965) (q:draft)
nausuakcil = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/health) (w:newborn/newborn baby) (d:<nau>, baby, and <suakcil>, just born, written as one word; before a noun, having just given birth) (j:nau/suakcil) (r:zd:12267) (q:draft)
nausuakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/family) (w:be about to give birth/give birth) (d:<nausuak>, childbirth, and <ding>, will, written as one word: about to give birth, in order to give birth; before a noun, for childbirth, as in {nausuakding Operation}) (j:nausuak/ding) (r:zd:17899/zd:14931) (q:draft)
nausuaklai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:birth certificate) (d:<nausuak>, childbirth, with <lai>, document: the paper that records a birth) (j:nausuak/lai) (r:zd:13165/zd:23571) (q:draft)
nausuakthak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:newborn/newborn child) (d:{nau suak thak}, a child newly born, written as one word; in the articles it stands in membership fee lists for a child added to a family) (j:nau/suak/thak) (r:zd:13069) (q:draft, low confidence)
nausuakthakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:newborn children/newborns) (d:{nausuak thak}, newly born child, with the plural <te>, written as one word: children who have just been born) (j:nausuak/thakte) (r:zd:16813) (q:draft)
nausuaktung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/health) (w:newborn/newborn baby) (d:<nausuak>, birth, with <tung> in the sense just now: a child that has just been born) (j:nausuak/tung) (r:zd:19968) (q:draft, low confidence)
nausuakzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/health) (w:way of giving birth/how the birth happened) (d:<nausuak>, childbirth, with <zia>, way, written as one word: the way in which a woman gave birth) (j:nausuak/zia) (r:zd:11729) (q:draft, low confidence)
nautaang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (j:nautang) (r:zd:24230/zd:24638/zd:16746) (q:draft)
nautaangte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (j:nautangte) (r:ts:9856) (q:draft)
nautangin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:common people/ordinary people) (d:<nautang> and the marker <in> written as one word, after <mipi>: the ordinary people, as the doer or as the manner) (j:nautang/in) (r:ts:12519) (q:draft)
nautawdap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/home) (w:nappy/diaper) (d:<nau> and <tawdap> written as one word: the cloth or pad put under the bottom of a baby) (j:nau/tawdap) (r:zd:12267/zd:11240) (q:draft)
nautawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family) (w:carry a baby/hold a child) (d:<nau>, baby, and <tawi>, hold in the arms, written as one word: have a small child in the arms; {nupi nautawi} is a woman carrying a baby) (j:nau/tawi) (r:zd:14626) (q:draft, low confidence)
naute = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:younger siblings/younger brothers and sisters) (d:<nau> in its meaning of younger sibling, with the plural <te>: the younger brothers and sisters, set against <ute>, the older ones; {u le naute} and <ute naute> address brothers and sisters, also fellow believers) (r:zd:10746/zd:23591/zd:26310) (q:draft)
nauteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:all the younger siblings/all the younger ones) (d:<nau>, younger sibling, and <teng>, all, written as one word; {u le nauteng} is all brothers and sisters, all the relatives) (j:nau/teng) (r:zd:16052/zd:16148) (q:draft)
nauzaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:younger one/younger sibling/the younger) (d:the younger of two children or siblings, opposite of <uzaw> the older) (b:nau) (q:draft)
navaak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (j:navak) (r:zd:24199/zd:15996) (q:draft)
navai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:your matter/your case/your affairs) (d:<na>, your, and <vai>, matter, written as one word: your affair or business, as a case at an office) (j:na/vai) (r:zd:11702/zd:18939) (q:draft)
navan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:your things/your luggage) (d:<na> and <van> written as one word: your goods, your belongings) (j:na/van) (r:zd:14498) (q:draft)
naveina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:your concern/your care) (d:<na>, your, and <veina>, concern, written as one word: the concern or burden that you feel for someone, as for your own people) (j:na/veina) (r:zd:26565) (q:draft)
naven = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:though/although/but) (d:placed at the end of a clause, usually after <sam>: granted that it is so, though; the speaker admits a point and then goes on to something else) (r:zd:15259/zd:24594) (q:draft, low confidence)
navet = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<na> and <vet> written as one word after <gen>: {gen navet om kei} is there is nothing even to say of them, let alone those) (j:na/vet) (r:zd:22412) (q:draft, low confidence)
navuah = (i:1) (t:ppm) (f:everyday) (w:in their/at the place where they) (d:the noun ending {-na} written apart from its verb and joined to <vuah>: {athusuah navuah} is in their publication, {atuntun navuah} wherever they arrive) (r:zd:15274/zd:21543) (q:draft, low confidence)
navun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:your skin) (d:<na>, your, and <vun>, skin, written as one word) (j:na/vun) (r:zd:13314) (q:draft, low confidence)
navyte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:navy/naval forces) (d:the English word navy with the plural <te>: the navy of a country and its men) (o:English) (r:zd:10785/zd:11016) (q:draft)
nawhdeih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:want urgently/need at once) (d:<nawh>, hurry, with <deih>, want: want in a hurry; in job notices <ki nawhdeih> is urgently wanted) (r:zd:20033/zd:19320) (q:draft)
nawhtaigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:run out of control/race away) (d:<nawhtai>, run in great haste, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word: of a machine, run much too fast and do harm; found of an escalator in one report) (j:nawhtai/gawp) (r:zd:21330) (q:draft, low confidence)
nawhzak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:hear often/hear again and again) (d:in {ki nawhzak}, said of news: be heard often, one report soon after another; apparently <nawh>, hurry, with <zak>, hear) (j:nawh/zak) (r:zd:17260/zd:15949) (q:draft, low confidence)
nawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:milk) (d:milk, of a mother or of an animal such as a cow, sheep or goat; {nawi ne} is to drink milk, to nurse) (s:nawitui) (q:draft)
nawimek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/body) (w:breast groping/molestation) (d:the groping of a woman's breasts as a sexual offence, from <nawi>, breast; {nawimek thuak} is to suffer it) (r:zd:12479) (q:draft)
nawipiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:breastfeed/nurse/suckle) (d:<nawi>, milk, and <piak>, give, written as one word: give a baby the breast; {nawipiak hun} is the time of nursing) (j:nawi/piak) (r:zd:11860/zd:21514) (q:draft)
nawituam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/body) (w:brassiere/bra) (d:<nawi>, breast, with <tuam>, cover: a woman's undergarment for the breasts) (r:zd:16817/zd:17967) (q:draft)
nawivui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/family) (w:milk powder/powdered milk/infant formula) (d:<nawi>, milk, and <vui>, powder, written as one word: dried milk that is mixed with water, given to a baby in place of mother's milk) (j:nawi/vui) (r:zd:22913) (q:draft)
nawk = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:face/go through/confront) (d:meet and go through something hard or important that lies ahead, such as a trial, a challenge, an election or a battle front; {nawk zo} is to get through it) (r:zd:24630/zd:16457/zd:18142) (q:draft)
nawkding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/media) (w:will hit/will strike) (d:<nawk> strike or rush against and the future marker <ding> written as one word: will hit, said mostly of a storm reaching a place) (j:nawk/ding) (r:zd:15054/zd:14714/zd:14595) (q:draft)
nawkgawpding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:will batter/will sweep over) (d:<nawkgawp> and <ding> written as one word: of a storm, will strike a place hard) (j:nawkgawp/ding) (r:zd:14714/zd:19960) (q:draft)
nawkgawpna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:battering/lashing/devastation) (d:<nawk> and <gawpna> written as one word: the violent striking of a storm or flood on a place; {nawkgawpna munte} are the places it struck) (j:nawk/gawpna) (r:zd:19960) (q:draft)
nawkin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:striking/sweeping over) (d:<nawk>, strike, with the linking ending <in>: said of a storm, wind or rain that strikes a place, after the subject marker as in {huihpi in nawkin}, not a going through by people) (r:zd:16828/zd:19088) (q:draft)
nawkkha = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:hit/run into/crash into/knock down) (d:of a vehicle, strike a person, animal or thing in its way, the vehicle standing before with <in>, as in {mawtaw in nawkkha}, hit by a car; not a harmless passing by) (r:zd:15619/zd:15562/zd:19414) (q:draft)
nawkkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:run into/hit/encounter/come up against) (d:<nawk>, strike against, with <khak>, happen to, written as one word; the form of <nawkkha> used before other words: collide with or strike something, and so meet with or go through an event or a trouble) (j:nawk/khak) (r:zd:21198/zd:19593/zd:15099) (q:draft)
nawkkhalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:not hit/miss) (d:<nawk>, strike against, and <khalo> written as one word: did not happen to hit, said of a vehicle that just misses someone) (j:nawk/khalo) (r:zd:15114/zd:15454) (q:draft)
nawkkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:press on together/push forward together) (d:<nawk> and <khawm> written as one word: push ahead together, go at a task side by side) (j:nawk/khawm) (r:zd:24951/zd:22758) (q:draft, low confidence)
nawkkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/nature) (w:crash through/sweep away/drive out) (d:<nawk>, rush against, with <khia>, out: strike a thing and go through or off it, as a vehicle that hits a barrier; of water, sweep a place away; of people or troubles, drive them out) (r:zd:14638/zd:16063/zd:11697) (q:draft)
nawkkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:strike again/hit back) (d:<nawk>, rush against or strike, and <kik>, again or back, written as one word: strike once more, or strike back at an attacker) (j:nawk/kik) (r:zd:15751) (q:draft, low confidence)
nawklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:not go through/not face/avoid) (d:<nawk> and <lo> written as one word: not go through or over a road, a hill or a hard thing, mostly as {nawklo in}, without going through) (j:nawk/lo) (r:zd:22569/zd:15909) (q:draft)
nawkna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:nature/politics) (w:onslaught/strike/attack/offensive) (d:<nawk>, rush against, with the noun suffix <na>: the striking of a storm after <huihpi>, an offensive in war after <galmai>, or the ramming of a vehicle; often before <hangin>, because of) (r:zd:19920/ts:11537/zd:15121) (q:draft)
nawkphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:crash into/ram/pass through) (d:<nawk>, rush against, with {-phei}, across: run into a person or thing in one's way, or push on through a place such as a border or a checkpoint) (b:nawk) (r:zd:17661/zd:14781/zd:15103) (q:draft)
nawkpheigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:plough into/ram into/crash through) (d:<nawkphei>, ram, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word: drive violently into people or things in the way) (j:nawkphei/gawp) (r:zd:20129/zd:19351) (q:draft)
nawkpheikha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:crash into/run into/hit) (d:<nawkphei>, crash into, and <kha.4>, happen to, written as one word: run into a person or vehicle by accident) (j:nawkphei/kha) (r:zd:19414) (q:draft)
nawkpheisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:ram/crash into/drive into) (d:<nawkphei> and the causing <sak> written as one word: drive a vehicle into something or someone, ram it) (j:nawkphei/sak) (r:zd:20225/zd:17766) (q:draft)
nawksak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:crash into/ram/run into) (d:of a driver or vehicle, drive into and hit another vehicle or its side, as in {mawtaw nawksak}; here <nawk> is strike against, not pass through) (r:zd:19562/zd:16450) (q:draft)
nawksakgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:ram violently/plough into) (d:<nawksak.2>, drive into, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word: drive a vehicle hard into people or other vehicles, doing great harm) (j:nawksak/gawp) (r:zd:20225/zd:14875) (q:draft)
nawksia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:crash into/ram and damage) (d:<nawk>, collide, and <sia>, here be damaged, written as one word: a vehicle runs into something and damages it) (j:nawk/sia) (r:zd:20767/zd:19554) (q:draft)
nawksiagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/nature) (w:smash up/wreck/be wrecked) (d:<nawk>, strike against, with <siagawp>, be ruined: wreck by hitting, or be wrecked by a collision, a flood or a storm) (j:nawk/siagawp) (r:zd:19351/zd:19554) (q:draft)
nawksuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:crash down through/rush down into) (d:<nawk>, strike or rush against, and <suk>, downward, written as one word: break through or push on downward) (j:nawk/suk) (r:zd:19277) (q:draft)
nawkthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/everyday) (w:can strike/be liable to hit) (d:<nawk>, strike or rush against, and <thei>, able, written as one word: of storms and the like, be apt to strike a place) (j:nawk/thei) (r:zd:21563) (q:draft, low confidence)
nawkto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:advance/push on/press forward) (d:<nawk> and <to> written as one word: push forward or upward with force, as an army advancing or a storm striking; also press on in spite of difficulty) (j:nawk/to) (r:ts:3168/zd:22563) (q:draft)
nawkzel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/everyday) (w:strike again and again/hit repeatedly) (d:<nawk> and <zel> written as one word: of storms, floods and fires, strike a place time after time) (j:nawk/zel) (r:zd:19646/zd:15679) (q:draft)
nawlh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:nolh) (r:zd:11454/zd:23382) (q:draft)
nawlkhiin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (j:nawlkhin) (r:zd:19239/zd:17933) (q:draft)
nawlkhinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:rejection/exclusion) (d:<nawlkhin>, reject, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of pushing a person aside, or the state of being pushed aside by others) (b:nawlkhin) (r:zd:20260/ts:12519/zd:23594) (q:draft)
nawlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:nawnlo) (r:zd:25584/zd:25323) (q:draft)
nawmlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:nawnlo) (r:zd:17722/zd:17860) (q:draft)
nawn ken = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:do not any more/no longer/stop) (d:<nawn>, any more, and <ken>, here not the pronoun but the word that forbids, do not: placed after a verb at the end of a sentence, it tells one person not to do it any longer or not to do it again) (r:zd:22736/zd:19822/zd:21340) (q:draft)
nawn keng = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:no longer/not any more) (d:<nawn>, any more, with <keng>, here not the verb but a short form of <kei>, not, and <ing>, the first person ending: placed after a verb at the end of a sentence, I no longer do it, I do not do it any more) (r:zd:22683/zd:25097/zd:23136) (q:draft)
nawnding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<nawn> and <ding> written as one word, after a verb: will any more, will again; mostly in a negative or doubting statement, will no longer) (j:nawn/ding) (r:zd:24955/zd:15547) (q:draft)
nawng = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:trouble/bother/hindrance) (d:not a marsh: with <kai> it is the two-word spelling of <nawngkai>; {nawng kai} is be troubled, {nawng kaisak} is to trouble or hinder someone) (r:zd:24089/zd:23192/zd:10725) (q:draft)
nawngkaai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/everyday) (w:troublesome/tangled/complicated) (d:in disorder and causing trouble; {nawngkaai sak} is to trouble or disturb someone) (r:zd:20003/zd:22654) (q:draft)
nawngkaigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be badly disrupted/be thrown into turmoil) (d:<nawngkai>, be disturbed, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word: be badly disturbed, or a serious disturbance) (j:nawngkai/gawp) (r:zd:12770/zd:12479) (q:draft)
nawngkaisakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:will trouble/will disturb) (d:<nawngkaisak>, cause trouble to, and <ding> written as one word: will trouble or inconvenience, intending to disturb) (j:nawngkaisak/ding) (r:zd:11175/zd:21554) (q:draft)
nawngkaisakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:harassment/disturbance/molestation/trouble) (d:<nawngkaisak>, trouble or disturb, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of troubling or harassing someone, also used of an offence in law) (b:nawngkaisak) (r:zd:14820/zd:12913) (q:draft)
nawnkai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (j:nawngkai) (r:zd:23350/zd:23663) (q:draft)
nawnkaina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (j:nawngkaina) (r:zd:22685) (q:draft)
nawnkeileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if no longer/if not any more) (d:<nawn>, any more, and <keileh>, if not, written as one word after a verb: if it is no longer so) (j:nawn/keileh) (r:zd:24733/zd:12933) (q:draft)
nawnkeng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I no longer/I cannot any more) (d:<nawn>, any longer, written as one word with <keng>, here the negative ending for I and not the verb carry: after a verb, I do not or cannot any more) (j:nawn/keng) (r:zd:12285) (q:draft)
nawnloding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:will no longer/no more) (d:<nawnlo> and the future marker <ding> written as one word, placed after a verb: will not do or be so any longer) (j:nawnlo/ding) (r:zd:13011/zd:26945) (q:draft)
nawnloh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:no longer/not any more) (d:<nawn>, any more, and <loh>, the form of not taken before <ding>, <ciang>, <hun> and similar words, written as one word after a verb: no longer do or be) (j:nawn/loh) (r:zd:26615/zd:11548/zd:21945) (q:draft)
nawnloh nadingin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:so that no longer/so that not again/lest again) (d:<nawnloh>, no longer, and <nadingin>, so that: placed after a verb, it states the purpose that the thing shall not happen or be done any more; the clause that follows says what is done to prevent it) (r:zd:20490/zd:21869/zd:12767) (q:draft)
nawnlohding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:no longer to/not to any more) (d:<nawnloh>, no longer, and <ding> written as one word after a verb: that the thing is not to be done any more) (j:nawnloh/ding) (r:zd:20263/zd:21372) (q:draft)
nawnlohi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:no longer/not any more) (d:<nawn>, any longer, <lo>, not, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: closes a statement that something no longer is or happens) (j:nawn/lo/hi) (r:zd:23432/zd:22159) (q:draft)
nawnlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:no longer being/ceasing) (d:<nawn> and <lohna> written as one word after a verb: the fact, or the place, of no longer doing or being, as {hat nawnlohna}, being no longer strong) (j:nawn/lohna) (r:zd:25477/zd:24574/zd:15767) (q:draft)
nawnlohte = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:those no longer) (d:<nawnloh>, no longer, with the plural <te>, written as one word after a verb: those who or which no longer do so) (j:nawnloh/te) (r:zd:17672/zd:25489) (q:draft)
nawnlote = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:those who no longer) (d:<nawnlo>, no longer, and the plural <te> written as one word after a verb: those who no longer do or are so) (j:nawnlo/te) (r:zd:20857/zd:25918) (q:draft)
nawnta = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:any more/again/now) (d:<nawn>, again or any more, with the particle <ta> that marks a change of state, written as one word after a verb) (j:nawn/ta) (r:zd:24068/zd:10973) (q:draft, low confidence)
nawnvetlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:no longer at all/not any more) (d:<nawn>, any more, and <vetlo>, not at all, written as one word after a verb: not at all any longer) (j:nawn/vetlo) (r:zd:20263/zd:13011) (q:draft)
nawt = (i:4) (t:v) (f:body/home) (w:brush/scrub/polish) (d:rub a surface to make it clean or bright, as {ha nawt} brush the teeth and {khedap nawt} polish shoes; the same rubbing as in wearing something away, but done to clean) (r:zd:19593/zd:24276/zd:21659) (q:draft)
nawtna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/body) (w:wiper/brush/wiping) (d:<nawt>, rub or wipe, with the noun suffix {-na}: the wiping or brushing of something, or the thing used for it; {ha nawtna} is a toothbrush or brushing the teeth, {puan nawtna} a cloth for wiping) (b:nawt) (r:zd:26097/zd:16878) (q:draft)
nawtna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:pushing ahead/advance) (d:in {mai nawtna}, pressing forward, going on ahead) (b:nawt) (r:zd:21081) (q:draft, low confidence)
nawtsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/health) (w:rub clean/scrub/brush/polish) (d:<nawt>, rub, with <siang>, clean: rub or brush a thing until it is clean; {ha nawtsiang} is brush the teeth) (j:nawt/siang) (r:zd:20814/zd:11020) (q:draft)
Naypitaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (j:Naypyidaw) (r:ts:12498/zd:20545) (q:draft)
Naypyidaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (w:Naypyidaw/Nay Pyi Taw) (d:capital city of Myanmar) (r:zd:15393/zd:19118) (q:draft)
Naypyitaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (w:Naypyitaw/Nay Pyi Taw) (d:the capital city of Myanmar) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:26620/ts:4379) (q:draft)
naza = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have heard/hear) (d:the particle <na> of what is already so and <za>, hear, written as one word: have heard, keep hearing; this <na> is not the pronoun you) (j:na/za) (r:zd:11494/zd:26565) (q:draft, low confidence)
nazah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:as much as/to the extent that) (d:the noun ending <na> written together with <zah>, amount, instead of with the verb before it: {lamet nazah} is {lametna zah}, as much as was hoped) (j:na/zah) (r:zd:22412) (q:draft, low confidence)
nazaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:take a photograph/record/film) (d:<na> and <zaih> written as one word: you take a picture; after another subject the first part marks what was done at that moment, they took a picture or recorded a video) (j:na/zaih) (r:zd:12267/zd:15016) (q:draft)
nazaihkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/it) (w:happen to film/record/capture on camera) (d:the verb prefix <na> written together with <zaihkha>: someone was there and recorded it, mostly with <Video>) (j:na/zaihkha) (r:zd:11044/zd:15606) (q:draft)
nazaihsaksim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:photograph secretly/take a picture in secret) (d:<na>, <zaihsak>, photograph, and <sim>, here secretly, written as one word: took a photo of someone without her knowing) (j:na/zaihsak/sim) (r:zd:14778) (q:draft, low confidence)
nazak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:you hear) (d:<na> and <zak> written as one word: you hear, when you hear) (j:na/zak) (r:zd:11759) (q:draft)
nazang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:use) (d:<na> and <zang> written as one word: you use; also with the <na> that stands before a verb in a report of what someone did, used) (j:na/zang) (r:zd:11854/zd:12727/zd:15274) (q:draft)
nazat = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:you use) (d:the two words {na zat} written as one: <na>, you or your, before <zat>, the form of <zang>, use; not the noun for equipment; {Facebook ah nazat Password} is the password you use on Facebook) (r:zd:18893/zd:16661) (q:draft)
nazatkhakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:your happening to use/your use) (d:<nazat>, you use, and <khakna> written as one word: the fact that you happen to use something, here certain words) (j:nazat/khakna) (r:zd:12138) (q:draft)
nazatleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if you use) (d:<na>, you, <zat>, use, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if you use it, when you use it) (j:na/zat/leh) (r:zd:16398) (q:draft)
nazatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:your use/your using) (d:<na>, your, and <zatna>, use, written as one word: your use of something, the fact that you use it; not the noun <nazat>, equipment) (j:na/zatna) (r:zd:12544/zd:11854) (q:draft)
nazi = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:your wife) (d:<na>, your, and <zi>, wife, written as one word; with a capital letter the same spelling is the German Nazi party) (j:na/zi) (r:zd:19287/zd:13112/zd:15772) (q:draft)
nazin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:you travel) (d:<na>, you, and <zin>, travel, written as one word: you travel, when you are on a journey) (j:na/zin) (r:zd:14826/zd:15296) (q:draft)
Nazis = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:politics) (w:Nazis) (d:the National Socialists who ruled Germany under Hitler from 1933 to 1945) (o:English) (r:zd:18241/zd:25603) (q:draft)
NBC = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:NBC) (d:an American television network and its news service, named as a source of news) (r:zd:15684/zd:11155) (q:draft)
NCA = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:Nationwide Ceasefire Agreement/NCA) (d:the ceasefire agreement between the government of Myanmar and ethnic armed groups, written with its English initials) (r:zd:21509/zd:11463) (q:draft)
ne = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/food) (w:eat) (d:take food; {an ne} is eat a meal; the form <nek> or <neek> is used before <ding>, <theih> and <nading>) (s:anne) (r:1.2.17)
Nebraska = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Nebraska) (d:a state in the Midwest of the United States of America) (r:zd:9227/zd:10952) (q:draft)
nebum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/social) (w:eat alone/eat without sharing) (d:eat everything oneself and share nothing; known from the proverb {hawmsiam nungta, nebum si}, the one who shares lives, the one who eats alone dies) (r:zd:23835/zd:21866) (q:draft, low confidence)
necklace = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:necklace) (d:a chain or string worn round the neck as an ornament) (o:English) (r:zd:12061) (q:draft, low confidence)
necktie = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:necktie/tie) (o:English) (r:zd:16236) (q:draft, low confidence)
neden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:eat regularly/always eat/keep eating) (d:<ne>, eat, and <den>, always, written as one word: eat something all the time or as a habit) (j:ne/den) (r:zd:12192/zd:22740) (q:draft)
neding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:will eat/to eat) (d:<ne> and <ding> written as one word: will eat, should eat; {neding in} is in order to eat) (j:ne/ding) (r:zd:21421/zd:22019) (q:draft)
nee = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (j:ne) (r:zd:19846) (q:draft, low confidence)
neekding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:food/something to eat) (d:<neek> and <ding> written as one word: what is to be eaten, food; also of eating that is to take place) (j:neek/ding) (r:zd:17465/zd:17428) (q:draft)
neekkhawm = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:communion/Lord's Supper/Eucharist) (d:the Christian meal of bread and wine shared in church, from <neek>, eat, and <khawm>, together; {neekkhawm piakna} is the giving of communion) (r:zd:25680/zd:25433) (q:draft)
neekloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:not eat/not take) (d:<neek>, eat, and <loh>, not, written as one word: not eating, not taking food or medicine; {neekloh ding} is should not eat) (j:neek/loh) (r:zd:19846) (q:draft)
neekna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:eating/consumption) (d:<neek>, eat, with the noun suffix <na>: the eating of something; {golhguk neekna} is the taking of bribes) (b:neek) (r:zd:24955/zd:19846) (q:draft)
neekngaih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/family) (w:fondness for food/craving to eat) (d:<neek>, eat, with <ngaih>, love or long for: love of eating, eagerness for food; also of the wish to eat together with others) (j:neek/ngaih) (r:zd:17022) (q:draft, low confidence)
neekpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/social) (w:eat with/share a meal with/dine with) (d:<neek>, eat, with <pih>, together with: eat a meal together with someone) (b:neek) (r:zd:20944) (q:draft)
neektheih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:food/edible thing) (d:<neek>, eat, and <theih>, can, written as one word: what can be eaten, edible; {neektheih dawntheih} is food and drink) (j:neek/theih) (r:zd:21864/zd:19462) (q:draft)
neemna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:weakness/softness/gentleness) (d:<neem>, soft or weak, with the noun suffix <na>; {tha neemna} is weakness, a weak point, set against {tha hatna}, strength) (s:nemna) (b:neem) (r:zd:22833/zd:25067) (q:draft)
neen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/food) (w:fine/minute/in small pieces) (d:very small or fine, of pieces into which something is cut or ground; placed after a verb it says that the action is done finely or thoroughly) (r:ts:479) (q:draft, low confidence)
Negaraku = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics/social) (w:Negaraku) (d:the national anthem of Malaysia; the Malay name means my country) (o:Malay) (r:zd:12678) (q:draft)
negative = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:health/everyday) (w:negative) (d:of a medical test, showing that the illness is not present; also unfavourable or critical; the opposite of <positive>) (o:English) (r:zd:24454/zd:21989/zd:24278) (q:draft)
negotiation = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:negotiation/talks) (d:talks between two sides to reach an agreement; {negotiation bawl} is negotiate; the word is often added in brackets after <kikupna>) (o:English) (r:zd:24500/zd:24489) (q:draft, low confidence)
Negro = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Negro) (d:older English name for black people of African descent, used in accounts of slavery and of the past in America; one writer says that the <mivom>, black people, should not be called so) (o:English) (r:zd:9224/zd:24230) (q:draft)
nehneh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep coming close/edge nearer/press close) (d:<neh>, come near, said twice: come closer and closer, keep close up to someone) (b:neh) (r:zd:12427/zd:13076) (q:draft)
nehno = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:tearful/moved to tears/tender-hearted) (d:easily moved to tears, soft of heart; {nehno in} is with emotion, close to weeping) (r:zd:24601/zd:9251) (q:draft)
nehphei = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:approach/go up to/come up to) (d:move over to a person or thing and come close beside it, often after <gei> or <lam> and before speaking or acting; the body does not lean on anything) (r:zd:17030/zd:15239/zd:16820) (q:draft)
nehpik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:sneer at/scorn/belittle) (d:treat someone with contempt, said along with laughing at and rejecting them; also with <san>, as in <nehpiksan>) (s:nehpiksan) (r:zd:18266/zd:19856) (q:draft, low confidence)
nei = (i:4) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:hold/make/carry out/give) (d:carry out the act named by the noun before it, mostly a noun in {-na}: <kikupna nei> is hold a discussion, <pulakna nei> make an announcement, <thusuahna nei> issue a statement) (r:ts:8105/ts:9579/ts:3179) (q:draft)
neia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have/hold) (d:<nei>, have, with the linking <a> written as one word: having, and) (j:nei/a) (r:zd:23989/zd:24167) (q:draft)
neiaa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:having/have and) (d:<nei>, have or make, with the linking <aa>, and, written as one word: having it, and then) (j:nei/aa) (r:zd:21876/zd:22238) (q:draft)
neiciat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:each have/all have) (d:<nei>, have, and <ciat>, each, written as one word: every one has it, each has his own) (j:nei/ciat) (r:zd:22709/zd:13295/zd:17264) (q:draft)
neiden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always have/hold regularly/keep having) (d:<nei>, have, with <den>, always, written as one word: have or hold something regularly or all the time) (j:nei/den) (r:zd:16210/zd:10892/zd:16216) (q:draft)
neiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will have/will hold) (d:<nei>, have or hold, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will have a thing, or will hold a meeting, an inquiry or an event) (j:nei/ding) (r:zd:10815/zd:19583) (q:draft)
neidingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:in order to have/to hold) (d:<nei>, have or hold, and <dingin>, in order to, written as one word: so as to have something, or to hold an event such as a hearing or a meeting) (j:nei/dingin) (r:zd:20971/zd:15447/zd:11396) (q:draft)
neigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:carry out heavily/hold on a large scale) (d:<nei> and <gawp> written as one word: carry out the act named before it severely or on a large scale) (j:nei/gawp) (r:zd:20912) (q:draft, low confidence)
neigige = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always have/keep having) (d:<nei> and <gige> written as one word: have or hold all the time; {mitsuan in neigige} is keep one's eyes fixed on) (j:nei/gige) (r:zd:25470/zd:16080) (q:draft)
neih = (i:3) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:hold/conduct) (d:form of <nei> used in dependent clauses, said of an event or activity that people carry out together, such as a meeting, a prayer, a tournament or an inspection; nothing is owned) (r:zd:22019/ts:6702) (q:draft)
neihbang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:like what others have) (d:<neih>, what one has, and <bang>, like, written as one word after the owner: the same as that person has, as in {mi neihbang}, like what others have) (j:neih/bang) (r:zd:12436/zd:21989) (q:draft)
neihbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have in addition/have another/do further) (d:<neih>, have or hold, with <beh>, in addition: have one more, as another child, or carry out something further, as a further check or statement) (b:neih) (r:zd:19917/zd:11839) (q:draft)
neihciang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:when having/when getting) (d:<neih> and <ciang> written as one word: when someone has or gets something; {pasal neihciang} is when she married) (j:neih/ciang) (r:zd:21869/zd:21853) (q:draft)
neihciangin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:when one has) (d:<neih>, have, and <ciangin>, when, written as one word: when someone has or gets what is named) (j:neih/ciangin) (r:zd:22740/zd:21869) (q:draft)
neihden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:always have/hold regularly/keep) (d:<neih>, have or hold, and <den>, always, written as one word: have at all times, or hold regularly, as a yearly event) (j:neih/den) (r:zd:17327/zd:20796) (q:draft)
neihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to have/to hold) (d:<neih> and <ding> written as one word: to have, that is to be had or held; {neihding kisam} is it is necessary to have) (j:neih/ding) (r:zd:25932/zd:21529/zd:25212) (q:draft)
neihdingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:in order to have/in order to hold) (d:<neih>, have or hold, and <dingin>, in order to, written as one word; {thusitna neihdingin} is in order to hold an interrogation, for questioning) (j:neih/dingin) (r:zd:20540/zd:25212/zd:14751) (q:draft)
neihetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not have at all/have no) (d:<nei> and <hetlo> written as one word: have none at all; {laumel neihetlo} is show no sign of fear) (j:nei/hetlo) (r:zd:12736/zd:14656) (q:draft)
neihhun = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:time to have/time of having) (d:<neih>, have, and <hun>, time, written as one word: the time when one has a thing, or the time to get it) (j:neih/hun) (r:zd:19599/zd:25914) (q:draft, low confidence)
neihi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have/hold) (d:<nei> and <hi> written as one word at the end of a sentence: has, had, held) (j:nei/hi) (r:zd:16754/zd:20905/zd:19866) (q:draft)
neihiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:does it have/has) (d:<nei>, have, and the question particle <hiam> written as one word, closing a question that begins with <bang> or <bangtan>: what does it have, how much does one have) (j:nei/hiam) (r:zd:12466/zd:24244/zd:14720) (q:draft)
neihkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not have/have no) (d:<neih>, have, and the negative <kei> written as one word, mostly before <leh>: if one does not have) (j:neih/kei) (r:zd:23706/zd:21097/zd:23441) (q:draft)
neihkhempeuh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/work) (w:all that one has/all possessions) (d:<neih>, possession, and <khempeuh>, all, written as one word: everything a person owns) (j:neih/khempeuh) (r:zd:21876/zd:24116) (q:draft)
neihkhit = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have had/have held) (d:<neih> and <khit> written as one word: finish having or holding; {neihkhit ciangin} is after having or after holding something) (j:neih/khit) (r:zd:21529/zd:23172/zd:21989) (q:draft)
neihkhitzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media/time) (w:after being held) (d:<neih>, hold, and <khitzawh>, after, written as one word; {aki neihkhitzawh} is after it has been held) (j:neih/khitzawh) (r:zd:14555) (q:draft)
neihkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:have in common/share/own jointly) (d:form of <neihkhawm>, have together, used before a noun, before <ding> and at the end of a clause; {i neihkhop} is what we have in common) (b:neihkhawm) (r:zd:25461/zd:21095/zd:23717) (q:draft)
Neihkhup = (i:1) (t:name) (c:beh) (f:family/social) (w:Neihkhup) (d:a Zomi clan name) (r:zd:23054) (q:draft)
neihkibang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:same-sex marriage/homosexual) (d:written before the English terms Same Sex Marriage and Homosexual: marriage or pairing of two people of the same sex, and a person of that kind; from <kibang>, the same) (r:zd:14577) (q:draft, low confidence)
neihkikding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:will hold again/to have again/to marry again) (d:<neihkik> and <ding> written as one word: to hold or have again in the future; {zi neihkikding} is to take a wife again) (j:neihkik/ding) (r:zd:19743/zd:14597) (q:draft)
neihkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:need to have/must have) (d:<neih> and <kul> written as one word: it is necessary to have) (j:neih/kul) (r:zd:16640/zd:8668) (q:draft)
neihlawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:gain/come to have/acquire) (d:<neih>, have, with the ending {-lawh}, get as a result: come to have something as the outcome of what was done or happened) (r:zd:25174/zd:19244) (q:draft)
neihleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if have) (d:<neih>, have, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if someone has; {na neihleh} is if you have) (j:neih/leh) (r:zd:23443/zd:21099/zd:21869) (q:draft)
neihlehlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (j:neihlelam) (r:zd:24605/zd:20670) (q:draft)
neihlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not have/be without) (d:<neih>, have, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not having, without) (j:neih/lo) (r:zd:14554/zd:20000) (q:draft)
neihloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not have/lack) (d:<neih>, have, and <loh>, not, written as one word: not having; {neih leh neihloh} is whether one has or has not) (j:neih/loh) (r:zd:25928/zd:24381) (q:draft)
neihlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:lack/not having/absence) (d:<neih> and <lohna> written as one word: the state of not having something, as in {pilna neihlohna}, lack of education, and {nasep neihlohna}, unemployment) (j:neih/lohna) (r:zd:23770/zd:22262/zd:20454) (q:draft)
neihma = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:before having/before holding) (d:<neih>, have or hold, and <ma>, before, written as one word and mostly followed by <in>: before one has, makes or holds the thing named) (j:neih/ma) (r:zd:23156/zd:21159) (q:draft)
neihman = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:because of having) (d:<neih>, have, and <man>, because, written as one word: because one has, on account of having) (j:neih/man) (r:zd:20841/zd:20853/zd:20202) (q:draft)
neihnailoh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not yet have/not have so far) (d:<neih>, have, and <nailoh>, not yet, written as one word, before a noun or <pen>: that one does not yet have) (j:neih/nailoh) (r:zd:20917/zd:26658) (q:draft)
neihnak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one has/as long as one has) (d:<neih>, have, and <nak> of the conditional {nak leh} written as one word; followed by <leh>: if indeed one has) (j:neih/nak) (r:zd:20932) (q:draft)
neihngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have had/have held before) (d:<neih>, have or hold, and <ngei>, ever, written as one word: have had or held before; {ih neihngei sa mah bangin} is just as we have held it before) (j:neih/ngei) (r:zd:23171) (q:draft)
neihngeisa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:held before/had before) (d:<neih>, hold or have, with <ngeisa>, formerly, written as one word: that has been held or had before; {i neihngeisa mah bang in} is just as we have held it before) (j:neih/ngeisa) (r:zd:23205/zd:15859) (q:draft)
neihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:hold with/have with/conduct for) (d:<neih>, have, and <pih>, together with, written as one word: hold a meeting, a talk or a service together with someone or for someone) (j:neih/pih) (r:zd:14734/zd:22159/zd:11107) (q:draft)
neihpihin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:hold with/conduct for) (d:<neihpih> and <in> written as one word: holding a prayer, a meeting or a talk together with or for someone, and so) (j:neihpih/in) (r:zd:14826/zd:12822) (q:draft)
neihsak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:lead/conduct/hold for) (d:<neih> in its meaning hold or conduct, with <sak>, do for others: lead a prayer, a service item or a session for the people present, mostly as {hong neihsak} after <thungetna> or another noun of the programme) (r:zd:20033/zd:10743/zd:12996) (q:draft)
neihsakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:to hold for/to have done) (d:<neihsak>, hold or conduct for someone, and <ding>, will, written as one word: to hold a prayer for someone, or to have an examination carried out) (j:neihsak/ding) (r:zd:11382/zd:17479) (q:draft)
neihsamah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work/everyday) (w:the very property of/owned by) (d:<neihsa>, property, with the emphatic <mah>, written as one word: something that is itself owned by the one named before it) (j:neihsa/mah) (r:zd:15517) (q:draft, low confidence)
neihsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:plan to have/try to have/plan to hold) (d:<neih> and <sawm> written as one word: intend or try to have something, or plan to hold an event) (j:neih/sawm) (r:zd:13077/zd:10783/zd:23985) (q:draft)
neihsunsun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:what little one has/the little one has) (d:<neih>, have, and <sunsun>, what little, written as one word: the little that one has, all that one has though it is not much; follows a possessor or a noun) (j:neih/sunsun) (r:zd:12571/zd:25919/zd:24733) (q:draft)
neihtheihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to be able to have/can hold) (d:<neihtheih> and <ding> written as one word: so as to be able to have or to hold something) (j:neihtheih/ding) (r:zd:20263/zd:16259) (q:draft)
neihtuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have each/have as well) (d:<neih>, have, with <tuak>, each, written as one word: each of them has, or has that too; with <lo> none of them has) (j:neih/tuak) (r:ts:3369/zd:11378) (q:draft, low confidence)
neihuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:that they have/that they hold) (d:<neih>, have, and the plural marker <uh> written as one word: that they have or hold) (j:neih/uh) (r:zd:21876) (q:draft)
neihzawh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:time) (w:since having/have had for) (d:<neih>, have, with <zawh> in its meaning after, before a count of years: the time that has passed since something was got, as {ka pasal neihzawh kum 8}, eight years since I married; not the ability to have) (r:zd:19402/zd:12341) (q:draft)
neihzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:attainment/being able to have) (d:<neihzawh>, manage to have, with the noun suffix <na>; {neihzawhna ding} is in order to come to have) (b:neihzawh) (r:zd:12187/zd:22935) (q:draft)
neiin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:having/with) (d:<nei> and <in> written as one word: having, and with that) (j:nei/in) (r:ts:3375/zd:9429/zd:23989) (q:draft)
neikawikawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:hold in many places/have here and there) (d:<nei> and <kawikawi> written as one word: have or hold something in one place after another, as inspections or protests) (j:nei/kawikawi) (r:zd:11932/zd:16698) (q:draft)
neikei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not have/have no) (d:<nei>, have, and the negative <kei> written as one word: do not have) (j:nei/kei) (r:zd:19603/zd:15584) (q:draft)
neikeng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I do not have/I have none) (d:<nei>, have, with {-keng}, the first person negative ending short for {kei ing}: I do not have) (b:nei) (r:zd:25924/zd:20892/zd:16337) (q:draft)
neikhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:one who has/owner) (d:<nei>, have, and <khat>, one, written as one word and placed after what is had: one who has it, the owner of it) (j:nei/khat) (r:zd:25474/zd:23977) (q:draft)
neikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:issue/give out/make) (d:<nei> and <khia> written as one word: put out or give, as a statement, an explanation or an appeal; of children, come to have) (j:nei/khia) (r:zd:18033/zd:15782/zd:21853) (q:draft)
neikhiata = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:has issued/has given out) (d:<nei>, make, and <khiata>, out now, written as one word: has now issued, as an announcement) (j:nei/khiata) (r:zd:19674) (q:draft, low confidence)
neikhinsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/everyday) (w:already having/who already has) (d:<nei>, have, and <khinsa>, already, written as one word: who already has a wife, a husband or children) (j:nei/khinsa) (r:zd:12409/zd:11333) (q:draft)
neikhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have already/have made) (d:<nei>, have, and <khinta>, already done, written as one word: already have, or have already made or held an agreement, a plan or an oath) (j:nei/khinta) (r:zd:19602/zd:22107/zd:20095) (q:draft)
neikhol = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have in advance/make beforehand) (d:<nei>, have or make, and <khol>, beforehand, written as one word: have or make a thing ahead of time, as a plan or a pledge) (j:nei/khol) (r:zd:16245/zd:19676) (q:draft)
neikikding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:will have again/will hold again) (d:<neikik>, have again, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will have or hold once more, said of a hearing, an inspection, an announcement or a child) (j:neikik/ding) (r:zd:13220/zd:13169/zd:17609) (q:draft)
neikikkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:have again held/have again made) (d:<neikik> and <khin> written as one word after a noun in {-na}: has already carried out that act once more) (j:neikik/khin) (r:zd:11635/zd:19932) (q:draft)
neilaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:will still have/will yet hold/will go on to carry out) (d:<nei>, have or hold, with <laiding>, will still, written as one word: something is yet to be held or done, as {kancianna neilaiding}, will carry out further investigation) (j:nei/laiding) (r:zd:19367/zd:13226) (q:draft)
neileh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one has/seem to have) (d:<nei>, have, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if one has; {neileh kilawm} is seems to have) (j:nei/leh) (r:zd:21003/zd:20170) (q:draft)
neileng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if I had/if we had) (d:<nei>, have, and <leng>, if, written as one word: if I or we had) (j:nei/leng) (r:zd:24502/zd:24480) (q:draft)
neiloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not have/be without/lack) (d:<nei>, have, and the negative <loh> written as one word, the form used before words such as <manin> and <phamawh>; {neiloh phamawh} is cannot do without, must have) (s:neilo) (j:nei/loh) (r:zd:12187/zd:22586) (q:draft)
neiloin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:without/without having) (d:<nei>, have, and <loin>, without, written as one word: without having something, having none) (j:nei/loin) (r:zd:17988/zd:23148) (q:draft)
neilopa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:man who does not have/one without) (d:<neilo>, not have, and <pa>, man, written as one word: the man who lacks the thing named) (j:neilo/pa) (r:zd:22922/zd:22415) (q:draft)
neilopi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:without/without having) (d:<nei>, have, with <lopi>, without, written as one word and usually followed by <in>: without having) (j:nei/lopi) (r:zd:14881/zd:12534/zd:24673) (q:draft)
neimahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:have very much/have greatly) (d:<nei>, have, and <mahmah>, very, written as one word; {thu neimahmah} is have great authority) (j:nei/mahmah) (r:zd:12792/zd:11821) (q:draft)
neimasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have first/hold first) (d:<nei> and <masa> written as one word: have or hold something first, before anything else is done) (j:nei/masa) (r:zd:22742/zd:11138) (q:draft)
neimawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have/happen to have) (d:<nei>, have, and <mawk>, which marks the fact as unexpected, written as one word: have or get, as it turned out) (j:nei/mawk) (r:zd:16976/zd:18077) (q:draft)
neimello = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hardly have/have no real) (d:<nei>, have, with <mello>, hardly, written as one word: have scarcely any, have no proper one) (j:nei/mello) (r:zd:17945) (q:draft, low confidence)
neimi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:one who has/possessor/owner) (d:<nei>, have, and <mi>, person, written as one word after the thing had: a person who has it, as {upna neimi}, a person of faith) (j:nei/mi) (r:zd:23784/zd:24276) (q:draft)
neinai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:placed after a verb or noun, apparently for something that shows in great amount or is made much of, as smoke billowing up thickly in {khuto neinai}; often followed by <sa> or <in>) (r:zd:20428/zd:20641) (q:draft, low confidence)
neinailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not have yet/have not yet) (d:<nei>, have, and <nailo>, not yet, written as one word: not yet have; after a noun of action, as {pulakna neinailo}, have not yet made an announcement) (j:nei/nailo) (r:zd:16332/zd:12985/zd:20717) (q:draft)
neinawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have any longer/still have) (d:<nei>, have, and <nawn>, any longer, written as one word, followed by a negative such as <lo> or <kei>: no longer have) (j:nei/nawn) (r:zd:15724/zd:19783) (q:draft)
neinawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:no longer have) (d:<nei> have and <nawnlo> no longer written as one word) (j:nei/nawnlo) (r:zd:18012/zd:25768) (q:draft)
neingei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have had/have ever had) (d:<nei>, have, and <ngei>, ever, written as one word: have had at some time; with <lo> or <kei>, have never had) (j:nei/ngei) (r:zd:16302/zd:15374) (q:draft)
neingeilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have never had) (d:<neingei> and <lo> written as one word: has not had at any time) (j:neingei/lo) (r:zd:15554/zd:21989) (q:draft)
neingiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really have/truly have) (d:<nei>, have, and <ngiat>, indeed, written as one word: really have, have for certain) (j:nei/ngiat) (r:zd:25919/zd:17262) (q:draft)
neinuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to have/wish to hold) (d:<nei> and <nuam> written as one word: want to have something, or want to hold a talk, a question or a statement) (j:nei/nuam) (r:zd:12932/zd:20428) (q:draft)
neinuamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:not want to have/be unwilling to give) (d:<neinuam> and <lo> written as one word: not want to have or hold something, as a talk or a statement) (j:neinuam/lo) (r:zd:12007/zd:12002) (q:draft)
neipen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the one who has/owner/those who have) (d:<nei>, have, and the marker <pen> written as one word after the thing had: the one who has it, those who have it; after <mawhpuak> also the one who has the most) (j:nei/pen) (r:zd:18248/zd:14728) (q:draft)
neipha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have plenty of/have fully) (d:<nei>, have or hold, and <pha>, here well or fully, written as one word: have much of a quality, or hold something thoroughly) (j:nei/pha) (r:zd:23653/zd:16600) (q:draft, low confidence)
neipih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:hold with/have with) (d:<nei>, hold or have, with <pih>, together with: hold a meeting or have relations together with someone) (j:nei/pih) (r:zd:16038/zd:10880) (q:draft)
neisam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:do have/have indeed) (d:<nei>, have, and the softening particle <sam>, not the verb call, written as one word: do have, have after all, often before a contrast or a reason) (j:nei/sam) (r:zd:14652/zd:15118) (q:draft, low confidence)
Neisok = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (d:a kind of flowering plant of the Zomi hills whose flowers last long and are used in making <zu>; said to be different from <ngeisok>) (r:zd:17081/zd:17162) (q:draft, low confidence)
neisuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:keep as one's own/come to own/own for good) (d:<nei>, have, with <suak>, on: have something as one's own from then on, keep it for good; {salin neisuak} is keep as slaves) (j:nei/suak) (r:ts:4831/zd:23910) (q:draft)
neitading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:will now hold/be about to have) (d:<nei>, have or hold, and <tading> written as one word: is now going to have a child, hold a meeting, make an announcement or take an oath) (j:nei/tading) (r:zd:15190/zd:19583) (q:draft)
neitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:having/with) (d:<nei>, have, with <tak>, written as one word after a noun and mostly before <in>: truly having it, so that {khiatna neitak} is meaningfully and {man neitak} is with worth) (j:nei/tak) (r:zd:23074/zd:17070) (q:draft)
neitek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:each have/all have) (d:<nei> and <tek> written as one word: each one has, every one has its own) (j:nei/tek) (r:zd:24464/zd:19316) (q:draft)
neiten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:those who have/owners) (d:<nei>, have, with the plural <te> and the subject marker <in> written as one word: those who have something, as the subject of the sentence; {sum neiten} is those who have money and {thu neiten} is the authorities) (j:nei/te/in) (r:zd:18213/zd:22691/zd:19520) (q:draft)
neiteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:all who have/everyone who has) (d:<nei>, have, and <teng>, all, written as one word: all those who have the thing named before it, as in {inn neiteng}, all who own a house) (j:nei/teng) (r:zd:19953/zd:22444) (q:draft)
neithei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can have/be able to have/get to have) (d:<nei>, have, and <thei>, able, written as one word: be able to have, or come to have) (j:nei/thei) (r:zd:20553/zd:12567/zd:24542) (q:draft)
neitheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot have/be unable to have) (d:<neithei>, can have, and <lo>, not, written as one word: cannot have, cannot hold or bear) (j:neithei/lo) (r:zd:20657/zd:14957) (q:draft)
neito = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:come to have/go on to hold) (d:<nei>, have or hold, with <to>, on and upward: come to have more and more, or hold something as time goes on) (j:nei/to) (r:zd:23703/zd:22981) (q:draft, low confidence)
neituak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:each have/both have) (d:<nei>, have, with <tuak>, each or both: have something on both sides or each one alike) (j:nei/tuak) (r:zd:13218/zd:21369) (q:draft)
neituam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have as one's own/have the more) (d:<nei>, have, with <tuam> written as one word: have separately, as one's own apart from others; also have all the more as a result) (j:nei/tuam) (r:zd:24257/zd:13110) (q:draft, low confidence)
neituan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have/give) (d:<nei>, have or make, and the particle <tuan> written as one word, used before a negative: not have or not make even so, not yet at all) (j:nei/tuan) (r:zd:13102) (q:draft, low confidence)
neituanlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not have either/not have for all that) (d:<nei>, have, and <tuanlo>, not for all that, written as one word: does not have it in spite of what might be expected) (j:nei/tuanlo) (r:zd:20932/zd:18040) (q:draft)
neiuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have) (d:<nei> and the plural <uh> written as one word: they have, you have, said of several people) (j:nei/uh) (r:zd:20162/zd:21282) (q:draft)
neivetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not have at all/have none) (d:<nei> and <vetlo> written as one word: have nothing of it at all) (j:nei/vetlo) (r:zd:11619/zd:11360/zd:14792) (q:draft)
neizel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:hold regularly/have regularly/keep having) (d:<nei>, have or hold, with <zel>, repeatedly: hold a meeting, a meal or an event time after time or by custom) (j:nei/zel) (r:zd:21155/zd:25680/zd:15772) (q:draft)
neizolo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot have/be unable to have) (d:<nei>, have, with <zolo>, cannot, written as one word: not be able to have or get something) (j:nei/zolo) (r:zd:18104/zd:24604/zd:21989) (q:draft)
nekden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:eat regularly/always eat) (d:<nek> and <den> written as one word, used before <ding>: eat regularly or all the time) (j:nek/den) (r:zd:24276/zd:21298) (q:draft)
nekding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:to eat/for eating) (d:<nek> and <ding> written as one word: to be eaten, that one should eat; as a noun, something to eat, food, as in {nekding omlo}, there is nothing to eat) (j:nek/ding) (r:zd:11617/zd:17120/zd:17632) (q:draft)
nekdingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:to eat/for eating) (d:<nek>, eat, and <dingin>, in order to, written as one word: so as to eat it, as food for someone) (j:nek/dingin) (r:ts:3375/zd:12869) (q:draft)
nekdingzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:food) (w:even food to eat) (d:<nekding> and <zong> written as one word: even anything to eat, also for eating; {nekdingzong neilo} is not even having anything to eat) (j:nekding/zong) (r:zd:18104/zd:15387) (q:draft)
nekei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:not eat/do not eat) (d:<ne> and the negative <kei> written as one word: do not eat, did not eat) (j:ne/kei) (r:zd:23906/zd:22775/zd:11508) (q:draft)
nekguk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:corruption/embezzlement/taking bribes) (d:<nek>, eat, with a second part that means by stealth: take for oneself in secret what belongs to the public or to others; used as a verb and as a noun, and paired with <golhguk>, bribe) (r:zd:24574/zd:25919) (q:draft)
nekgukna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:corruption/embezzlement) (d:{nek guk}, eat in secret, with the noun suffix <na>: taking for oneself money that belongs to the public or to others; {nekgukna leh golhgukna} is corruption and bribery, see <golhguk>) (r:zd:17291/zd:11145) (q:draft)
nekhangin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:even if one eats/though one eats) (d:<nek> and <hangin> written as one word: even though someone eats it) (j:nek/hangin) (r:zd:22019) (q:draft)
nekhetloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:not eat at all/avoid eating) (d:<nek> and <hetloh> written as one word, before <ding>: not eat at all) (j:nek/hetloh) (r:zd:24276) (q:draft)
nekhial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:eat something harmful/get food poisoning) (d:<ne>, eat, with <khial>, wrong, written as one word: eat by mistake something bad or poisonous and fall ill or die; {an nekhial} is food poisoning) (j:ne/khial) (r:zd:17538/zd:17974) (q:draft)
nekhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:food/health) (w:good to eat/worth eating) (d:<nek>, eat, and <huai>, worthy of, written as one word: that should be eaten, good for one to eat) (j:nek/huai) (r:zd:24276/zd:21284/zd:19875) (q:draft)
nekhun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/time) (w:mealtime/time to eat) (d:<nek>, eat, with <hun>, time, written as one word; {sun an nekhun} is lunch time) (j:nek/hun) (r:zd:22019/zd:20946) (q:draft)
nekkhialh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:eat wrongly/take wrongly) (d:<nek> and <khialh> written as one word: eat or take something in the wrong way; {an nekkhialh} is eating food that makes one ill) (j:nek/khialh) (r:zd:20755/zd:17974) (q:draft)
nekkhop = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food/work) (w:enough to eat/livelihood) (d:<nek> eat with <khop> in its sense enough: food enough to live on, as the object of <mu>, find; nobody eats together here) (r:zd:22282/zd:25115) (q:draft)
nekkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:eat again) (d:<nek>, eat, and <kik>, again, written as one word: eat again, eat once more) (j:nek/kik) (r:zd:11949/zd:24276) (q:draft)
nekledawnte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:food and drink/things to eat and drink) (d:<nekledawn>, food and drink, with the plural {-te}: the things one eats and drinks) (b:nekledawn) (r:zd:24276/ts:3125) (q:draft)
nekleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:food) (d:<nek>, eat, and <leh> written as one word: either food and, as in {nekleh taak}, food and clothing, or if one eats, as in {i nekleh}, if we eat) (j:nek/leh) (r:zd:22740/zd:23037) (q:draft, low confidence)
neklehdawn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:food and drink/diet) (d:<nek>, eat, <leh>, and, and <dawn>, drink, written as one word: what one eats and drinks, eating and drinking) (j:nek/leh/dawn) (r:zd:16737/zd:11269) (q:draft)
neklohding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:not to eat/must not be eaten) (d:<nekloh>, not eat, and <ding>, will, written as one word: that one should not eat something, or before a noun a thing that is not to be eaten) (j:nekloh/ding) (r:zd:20254/zd:15237/zd:11508) (q:draft)
nekma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:food/time) (w:before eating) (d:<nek> and <ma> written as one word: before eating, usually followed by <in>) (j:nek/ma) (r:zd:21876/zd:14790) (q:draft)
neknek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food) (w:keep eating/eat regularly) (d:<nek>, eat, said twice: eat again and again or as a habit; whatever one eats or drinks) (b:nek) (r:zd:21510/zd:22650/zd:24653) (q:draft)
nekngaih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/food) (w:see that others eat/care for with food) (d:think of what another person has to eat and provide for it, as for guests, friends or a woman who has given birth) (r:zd:26708/zd:22021) (q:draft, low confidence)
