nemnum = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:vaguely/loosely/imprecisely) (d:placed after a verb: in a vague, inexact or half-and-half way; {hi nemnum} is be unclear, neither one thing nor the other, and {khial nemnum} is be somewhat wrong) (r:zd:21013/zd:17634) (q:draft, low confidence)
nemsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:soften/make gentle/weaken) (d:<nem>, soft, with the causative <sak>: make soft or gentle, as the heart or the voice; of the body or its strength, make weak) (b:nem) (r:zd:21502/zd:19174/zd:21673) (q:draft)
nencip = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:pin down/crush/press down/trap under) (d:press a person or thing down with real weight so that it cannot move, as a vehicle or a load does in an accident; {ki nencip} is be pinned or trapped under, where the other sense is the weight of sin or wickedness) (r:zd:22129/zd:22688/zd:21164) (q:draft)
neng = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:detail/particular) (d:in the pair {a neng a tawng}, the small points of a matter; {a neng a tawngin} is in detail, point by point, with a verb of telling or explaining) (r:zd:19379/zd:16227) (q:draft)
nengcik = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:tiny bit/speck/particle) (d:<neng>, crumb, with the ending {-cik}, tiny: the smallest bit of something; {nengcik khat zong} with a negative verb is not even a little) (r:zd:16803/ts:10275) (q:draft)
