ngahkhakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will happen to get/may get) (d:<ngahkhak>, happen to get, and <ding>, the marker of what is to come, written as one word: will or may come to get something, wanted or unwanted, such as a job or a disease) (j:ngahkhak/ding) (r:zd:20167/zd:16259) (q:draft)
ngahkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:obtain/win/gain/capture) (d:<ngah>, get, with <khia>, out: get something out of an effort or from another, such as a prize, an office, freedom or weapons taken in battle) (b:ngah) (r:zd:14928/zd:11244/ts:4309) (q:draft)
ngahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:obtain/win/capture) (d:form of <ngahkhia> used before words such as <ding>, <nading> and <kuan>) (b:ngahkhia) (r:zd:11076/ts:5309) (q:draft)
ngahkhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have already received/have already got) (d:<ngah>, receive or get, and <khinta>, already done, written as one word; with <ki>, has already been received or is already available) (j:ngah/khinta) (r:zd:11504/zd:15435) (q:draft)
ngahkikthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be able to get back/can recover) (d:<ngahkik>, get back, and <thei>, able, written as one word: able to get back what was lost or stolen; with <ki>, can be recovered) (j:ngahkik/thei) (r:zd:16998/zd:12190) (q:draft)
ngahkiktheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to get back/can regain/can recover) (d:<ngahkik>, get back, and <theih>, be able, written as one word, used before <nading>: {ngahkiktheih nading} is so that it can be got back) (j:ngahkik/theih) (r:zd:12712/zd:15471) (q:draft)
ngahlah = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:long for/wait eagerly/look forward to) (d:another spelling of <ngaklah>: wait for something with longing, after a clause with <ding>, {ding kal} or {hun ding} that names what is awaited; not <ngah>, get) (s:ngaklah) (r:zd:26092/zd:24030) (q:draft)
ngahleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one gets/when one receives) (d:<ngah>, get, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if or when someone gets or receives something) (j:ngah/leh) (r:zd:23902/zd:24276) (q:draft)
ngahlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not get/not receive/be without) (d:<ngah>, get, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not get or not have received) (j:ngah/lo) (r:zd:11548/zd:20979) (q:draft)
ngahloding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will not get/will not receive) (d:<ngah>, get, with <loding>, will not, written as one word: will not get or have something) (j:ngah/loding) (r:zd:16061/zd:12355) (q:draft)
ngahloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not get/not receive) (d:<ngah>, get, and the negative <loh> written as one word: not getting, used before endings such as <nading>, so as not to get) (j:ngah/loh) (r:zd:23873/zd:24082/zd:16331) (q:draft)
ngahlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:not receiving/failure to get/not obtaining) (d:<ngah>, receive, with <lohna>, the not doing: the fact of not getting something; {ngahlohna ahang} is the reason for not getting it) (j:ngah/lohna) (r:zd:21461/zd:22586) (q:draft)
ngahloin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:without getting/not receiving) (d:<ngah>, get, and <loin>, without, written as one word: without getting, as in {contact ngahloin om} be out of reach) (j:ngah/loin) (r:zd:23494) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahlua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:get very much/have plenty of/get too much) (d:<ngah> and <lua> written as one word: get or have a great deal of something, as time or energy) (j:ngah/lua) (r:zd:22827/zd:19991) (q:draft)
ngahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:get/receive/really get) (d:<ngah> and the stressing <mah> written as one word: indeed get; {ngahmah ngahlo} is whether got or not) (j:ngah/mah) (r:zd:21608/zd:19239) (q:draft)
ngahmi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (w:recipient/one who has got) (d:<ngah> and <mi> written as one word: the person who receives or has got something, as a disease, a blessing or a curse) (j:ngah/mi) (r:zd:24276/zd:20997) (q:draft)
ngahnading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:in order to get/for getting) (d:<ngah>, get, and <nading>, in order to, written as one word: for getting, so as to obtain) (j:ngah/nading) (r:zd:11314/zd:15431) (q:draft)
ngahnai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:have yet got/have yet received) (d:<ngah>, get, with <nai>, yet, written as one word and followed by <lo>: {ngahnai lo} is not yet got, not yet received) (j:ngah/nai) (r:zd:11416/zd:12867) (q:draft)
ngahnailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not yet receive/not yet get) (d:<ngah>, get, and <nailo>, not yet, written as one word: have not yet received or obtained) (j:ngah/nailo) (r:zd:13190/zd:12142) (q:draft)
ngahnate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:gains/things received) (d:plural of <ngahna>: the things that are received or obtained) (b:ngahna) (r:ts:838/zd:22774) (q:draft)
ngahnawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:no longer get/no longer receive) (d:<ngah>, get, and <nawnlo>, no longer, written as one word: something is not received any more, said often of electricity and services) (j:ngah/nawnlo) (r:zd:17645/zd:14301) (q:draft)
ngahngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have once received/have won before) (d:<ngah>, get, with <ngei>, ever, written as one word: have received or won something at some time in the past) (j:ngah/ngei) (r:zd:11348) (q:draft)
ngahngeilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have never received/never get) (d:<ngah> and <ngeilo> written as one word: has never received or obtained something) (j:ngah/ngeilo) (r:zd:21876/zd:22116) (q:draft)
ngahnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to get/want to have) (d:<ngah>, get, and <nuam>, want, written as one word) (j:ngah/nuam) (r:zd:21989/zd:11943) (q:draft)
ngahpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:get at once/receive right away) (d:<ngah>, get, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: get something immediately, without delay) (j:ngah/pah) (r:zd:14734/zd:12504/zd:12196) (q:draft)
ngahpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the getting/what is received) (d:<ngah>, get, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the getting of something, or what someone got, as the topic of the sentence) (j:ngah/pen) (r:zd:22282) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahphial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:even if one gets) (d:<ngah> and <phial> written as one word: even if one gets or obtains it, followed by <zongin>) (j:ngah/phial) (r:zd:23737/zd:25917) (q:draft)
ngahpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:obtain for/win for/gain for) (d:<ngah>, get, with <pih>, for or with someone: get something for a person or a group, bring it to them) (b:ngah) (r:zd:20695/zd:16331/zd:21389) (q:draft)
ngahsate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education/everyday) (w:those who have obtained/holders) (d:<ngahsa>, obtained, and the plural <te> written as one word: those who have already got what is named, as a degree or a title) (j:ngahsa/te) (r:zd:20979) (q:draft)
ngahsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to get/seek to obtain/aim to win) (d:<ngah>, get, with <sawm>, intend: set out to get or win something) (j:ngah/sawm) (r:zd:21075/zd:25673) (q:draft)
ngahsim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:whenever one gets/every time one has) (d:<ngah>, get, and <sim>, every time, as in <simin>, written as one word and followed by <in>: each time one gets something, mostly in {hun ngahsim in}, whenever there is time) (j:ngah/sim) (r:zd:22474/zd:22983/zd:21918) (q:draft)
ngahsun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:ngaihsun) (r:zd:10777/zd:25221) (q:draft)
ngahsut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:ngaihsut) (r:zd:8667/zd:24224) (q:draft)
ngahsutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:ngaihsutna) (r:zd:26658/zd:18204) (q:draft)
ngahtading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:will get/will now receive/be available) (d:<ngah>, get, and <tading> written as one word: will now get; with <ki>, will now be obtainable) (j:ngah/tading) (r:zd:11011/zd:16809) (q:draft)
ngahtek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:each get/all receive) (d:<ngah>, get, and <tek>, each, written as one word: every one of them gets or suffers it, as in {liamna ngahtek}, all were injured) (j:ngah/tek) (r:zd:20164/zd:25102) (q:draft)
ngahthak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/work) (w:newly received/newly obtained/newly appointed) (d:<ngah> and <thak> written as one word, placed after a noun: newly got, as a new case of an illness, or a person who has just received a degree or an office) (j:ngah/thak) (r:zd:20300/zd:24458) (q:draft)
ngahtheiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be able to get/can receive) (d:<ngah>, get, with <theiding>, will be able, written as one word: will be able to get; with <ki>, can be obtained) (j:ngah/theiding) (r:zd:11766/zd:11438) (q:draft)
ngahtheihiam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (d:<ngahthei>, can get, and the question particle <hiam> written as one word: how or where could one get it; closes an indirect question) (j:ngahthei/hiam) (r:zd:18183) (q:draft)
ngahto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:go on to get/come to hold/attain) (d:<ngah>, get, and <to>, onward, written as one word: reach or win a place, rank or amount in the course of events) (j:ngah/to) (r:zd:15968/zd:12416) (q:draft)
ngahuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:get/receive/obtain) (d:<ngah> and the plural marker <uh> written as one word: they get, they receive) (j:ngah/uh) (r:zd:21989/zd:24564) (q:draft)
ngahzolo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be unable to get/fail to obtain) (d:<ngah>, get, and <zolo>, cannot, written as one word: not manage to get or reach something) (j:ngah/zolo) (r:zd:19734/zd:16302/zd:24277) (q:draft)
ngai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:listen/pay attention) (d:give ear to what is said and take it to heart; {ngai in} is the command to one person and {ngai un} to several) (s:don/ngaihsak) (q:draft)
ngai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:miss/long for/love) (d:feel the absence of a dear person or be fond of someone, with a person as object and often <mahmah> or <lua> after it; {ki ngai} is to be in love with each other; not the meaning listen, which has speech as object) (r:ts:301/zd:24119/zd:16695) (q:draft)
ngaidam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:forgive/pardon/excuse) (d:forgive a fault or mistake; the closing line {khialhna a om leh ngaidam} asks the reader to pardon any mistakes) (r:zd:21463/zd:14820) (q:draft)
ngaih = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:loud) (d:loud, of a voice or sound, as in {aw ngaih}) (r:zai:loud) (q:draft)
ngaih = (i:4) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:love/long for/miss) (d:form of <ngai> in its meaning love or long for a person, used before words such as <pen> and <mahmah>; {i ngaih pen} is the one we love most; not listening and not loudness) (r:zd:16779) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihbang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/everyday) (w:lovely/attractive/charming) (d:pleasing and lovable in looks, voice or manner) (s:etlawm/ithuai) (r:zd:22203/zd:11425) (q:draft)
ngaihdam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (j:ngaidam) (r:zd:24677/zd:24174) (q:draft)
ngaihdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:opinion/view/way of thinking) (d:a way of thinking about a matter, an opinion; {ngaihdan tuamtuam} is different views. With <dan>, way, after other verbs of the same form it is also the way of listening or the way of loving) (r:zd:17685/zd:12177) (q:draft)
ngaihloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:not love) (d:<ngaih>, love, and <loh>, not, written as one word; {ngaih leh ngaihloh} is loved or not loved) (j:ngaih/loh) (r:zd:16779/zd:15377) (q:draft)
ngaihloh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not listen) (d:<ngaih>, listen, and <loh>, not, written as one word) (j:ngaih/loh) (r:zd:23977) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihmahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very loud) (d:<ngaih>, loud, and <mahmah>, very, written as one word: very loud, of a sound, mostly after <gin>, sound) (j:ngaih/mahmah) (r:zd:17256/zd:15884/zd:15368) (q:draft)
ngaihmahmahkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:a very loud one) (d:<ngaihmahmah>, very loud, and <khat>, one, written as one word, after <agin>: {agin ngaihmahmahkhat} is a very loud sound) (j:ngaihmahmah/khat) (r:zd:11133/zd:20215) (q:draft)
ngaihmuanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:confidence/assurance/trust) (d:the state of being able to rely on something, named beside <lungmuanna>, peace of mind) (r:zd:21458/zd:23670) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihngaih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:keep thinking/ponder/dwell on) (d:after <lung>, mind, as {lung ngaihngaih}: keep turning a thing over in the mind or keep longing, where the other sense is listening with the ears) (r:zd:21461) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihnu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:girlfriend/sweetheart/beloved) (d:<ngaih>, beloved, with <nu> marking a woman: the girl or woman a man loves; mostly {lawm ngaihnu}, girlfriend) (s:ngaihno) (b:ngaih) (r:zd:26947/zd:15416) (q:draft)
ngaihpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:boyfriend/sweetheart/lover) (d:<ngaih>, beloved, with <pa> marking a man; used after <lawm> as {lawm ngaihpa}, the man a woman loves, which is also written <lawmngaihpa>) (r:zd:20092/zd:12512) (q:draft)
ngaihpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/religion) (w:most beloved/dearest/best loved) (d:<ngaih>, lovely or beloved, and <pen>, most, written as one word: the most loved; {la ngaihpen} is the best loved or sweetest song) (j:ngaih/pen) (r:zd:9228/zd:22962/zd:15396) (q:draft)
ngaihpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:love along with/be in love with) (d:<ngaih>, love, with <pih>, together with: love someone as one of one’s own; {ki ngaihpih} is the one a person is in love with) (j:ngaih/pih) (r:zd:10673) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihsak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:raise the voice/make loud) (d:<ngaih.3>, loud, with <sak>: make the voice loud, after <aw>, voice; not the listening of the other sense) (r:zd:21673) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihsun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:think/consider/think about) (d:use the mind: think about something, consider it, or regard a person or thing in a certain way; {ngaihsun un} is the command to several people) (s:lungngai)
ngaihsunkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:think back on/reconsider/recall) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, and <kik>, again or back, written as one word: think something over again, or think back on what is past) (j:ngaihsun/kik) (r:zd:20697/zd:24217) (q:draft)
ngaihsunlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not think/not consider) (d:<ngaihsun> and <lo> written as one word: do not think of something, do not consider or intend it) (j:ngaihsun/lo) (r:zd:25215/zd:23087/zd:12876) (q:draft)
ngaihsunna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:ngaihsutna) (r:zd:25687/ts:11162) (q:draft)
ngaihsunthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can think/can imagine/can regard) (d:<ngaihsun>, think, and <thei>, able, written as one word: be able to think of or imagine something, or to regard it in a certain way) (j:ngaihsun/thei) (r:zd:25221/zd:14885) (q:draft)
ngaihsut phat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:think over/consider carefully/reflect on/ponder) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, and <phat>, which after a verb here means well or thoroughly and not praise: think a matter over with care; very often followed by <huai>, {ngaihsut phat huai}, worth thinking over, or by <ding>) (r:zd:11281/zd:21049/zd:17488) (q:draft)
ngaihsut piakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:suggestion/advice/recommendation) (d:<ngaihsut>, thought, and <piakna>, a giving: a suggestion or piece of advice offered to someone; the person advised stands before it with <tungah> or <adingin>) (r:zd:24011/zd:20200/zd:24418) (q:draft)
ngaihsut theihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/education) (w:ability to think/reasoning/intellect) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with <theihna.2>, the power to understand: the faculty of thinking, the mind's ability to reason; often {thu ngaihsut theihna}) (r:zd:20798/zd:20334/zd:20060) (q:draft)
ngaihsutdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/education) (w:way of thinking/view/opinion) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, and <dan>, way, written as one word: how a person thinks about something) (s:ngaihsutna) (j:ngaihsut/dan) (r:zd:22896/zd:11831) (q:draft)
ngaihsutding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to think about/to consider) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, and <ding> written as one word: to be thought about, something to consider; {ngaihsutding thu} is a matter to think about) (j:ngaihsut/ding) (r:zd:20796/zd:11440/zd:25866) (q:draft)
ngaihsuthuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/education) (w:worth considering/thought-provoking) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, and <huai>, worthy of, written as one word: that deserves to be thought about) (j:ngaihsut/huai) (r:zd:9424/zd:10721/zd:24214) (q:draft)
ngaihsutkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:think again/think back on/reconsider) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with <kik>, again or back, written as one word: think a thing over again, or look back on it) (j:ngaihsut/kik) (r:zd:16343/zd:22650) (q:draft)
ngaihsutlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not consider/not think/disregard) (d:<ngaihsut> and <lo> written as one word, after a describing word: not think it so; {thupi ngaihsutlo} is not consider it important) (j:ngaihsut/lo) (r:zd:20490/zd:12942) (q:draft)
ngaihsutloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not think/not consider) (d:<ngaihsut> and the negative <loh> written as one word: not think of, not consider; {ngaihsutloh kaalin} is while one is not thinking of it, unnoticed) (j:ngaihsut/loh) (r:zd:16803) (q:draft)
ngaihsutpiakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:suggestion/advice/opinion) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, and <piakna>, giving, written as one word: a thought offered to others, a suggestion or piece of advice) (j:ngaihsut/piakna) (r:zd:21159/zd:25132/zd:25354) (q:draft)
ngaihsutpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:think about for someone/consider on behalf of/feel for) (d:<ngaihsut>, think, with <pih>: give thought to the situation or need of someone, think it over with or for that person) (j:ngaihsut/pih) (r:zd:9451/zd:20716/zd:20313) (q:draft)
ngaihsutsut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep thinking/think over/ponder) (d:<ngaihsut> think with the last syllable repeated: go on thinking about something, think it over and over) (b:ngaihsut) (r:zd:20329/zd:19661) (q:draft)
ngaihsutziate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:ways of thinking/attitudes) (d:<ngaihsutzia>, way of thinking, with the plural <te>) (b:ngaihsutzia) (r:zd:22757/zd:23074) (q:draft)
ngaihteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:all the beloved/all the dear ones) (d:<ngaih>, love, and <teng>, all, written as one word: all those who are dear, used in addressing readers or kin, often {it leh ngaihteng}) (j:ngaih/teng) (r:zd:15874) (q:draft)
ngaihtheithei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:as loud as possible/very loud) (d:<ngaih>, loud, with <theithei>, here as much as can be: as loud as possible, said of a sound, {agin ngaihtheithei}) (j:ngaih/theithei) (r:zd:13320/zd:11256) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihzawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/social) (w:since being in love/time as lovers) (d:<ngaih>, love, and <zawh>, since, written as one word after the prefix <ki> or <aki>: {aki ngaihzawh} is the time since two people became lovers, followed by a number of years) (j:ngaih/zawh) (r:zd:13072/zd:12676) (q:draft)
ngaikha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:happen to hear/get to listen) (d:<ngai>, listen, and the particle <kha>, happen to, written as one word; other uses in the articles are unclear) (j:ngai/kha) (r:zd:2072) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not listen/not heed/disregard) (d:<ngai>, listen, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not listen to or heed what is said) (j:ngai/lo) (r:zd:12544/zd:22095) (q:draft)
ngailo = (i:2) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:not love/not care for) (d:<ngai>, here love or long for, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not love or be fond of someone; often paired with <itlo> and <deihlo>) (j:ngai/lo) (r:zd:22059/zd:25768) (q:draft)
ngaina = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:be fond of/like/love) (d:like or be attracted to something or someone; {laibu ngaina mi} is a lover of books) (r:zd:23887) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaina = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (j:ngeina) (r:zd:12341) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaingai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:keep pondering/meditate/think over) (d:after <lung>, heart: {lung ngaingai} is <lungngai>, ponder, with its second part said twice, keep turning a matter over in the heart, not listening with the ears) (r:zd:21461/zd:19108/zd:19683) (q:draft)
Ngaingngaanzee = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:politics) (d:politics, the affairs of state and of parties; {Ngaingngaanzee party} is a political party; one writer spells the Burmese word this way and with a capital) (s:gamvai) (o:Burmese, nainganyay) (r:zd:19239) (q:draft)
ngaisut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:ngaihsut) (r:zd:25919/zd:16035) (q:draft)
ngaisutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:ngaihsutna) (r:zd:21869/zd:12544) (q:draft)
ngait = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:ngiat) (r:zd:18121/zd:18958) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaite = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:those who miss/those who love/loved ones) (d:<ngai.2>, miss or be fond of, with plural {-te}: the people who love someone and feel his absence, in the condolence formula {a it a ngaite}, those who love and miss him; not those who listen) (r:ts:9846) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaitheipah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:fall in love at once/take to at once) (d:<ngai>, love, <thei>, can, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: come to love someone straight away, as at first sight) (j:ngai/thei/pah) (r:zd:11150) (q:draft)
ngaitsut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:ngaihsut) (r:zd:19676/zd:25866) (q:draft)
Ngaizaw = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:love more/hold dearer/be more attached to) (d:<ngai>, here love or long for, and <zaw>, more, written as one word: love someone or something more) (j:ngai/zaw) (r:zd:21886/zd:15105) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wait/wait for/keep watch) (d:wait for someone or something, or stay awake and keep watch) (q:draft)
ngaka = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:waiting for/awaiting) (d:<ngak>, wait for, and the linking <a> written as one word: while waiting for, depending on; {lupna ngaka} is confined to bed) (j:ngak/a) (r:zd:9261/zd:9254) (q:draft)
ngakbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wait for/await) (d:<ngak>, wait, and <bawl> written as one word: wait on purpose for something to happen or to pass) (j:ngak/bawl) (r:zd:17442/zd:16876) (q:draft)
ngakcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wait/keep watch/stand guard) (d:<ngak>, wait, and <cip>, firmly, written as one word: wait without leaving, or stay on guard at a place) (j:ngak/cip) (r:zd:11529/zd:13133/zd:12835) (q:draft)
ngakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:will wait/to wait) (d:<ngak>, wait, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will wait, or having to wait) (j:ngak/ding) (r:zd:23700/zd:17152) (q:draft)
ngakin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health/home) (w:keeping to/staying at) (d:staying in one place without leaving it, said of a sick person or of one who minds the house: {lupna ngakin om} is be bedridden and {inn ngakin om} is stay at home keeping the house) (r:zd:13110/zd:19396/zd:10986) (q:draft)
ngakkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:while waiting/as one waits) (d:<ngak>, wait, and <kawm>, while, written as one word, usually followed by <in>: while waiting for something) (j:ngak/kawm) (r:zd:15861/zd:20302) (q:draft)
ngakkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have to wait/must wait) (d:<ngak> and <kul> written as one word: it is necessary to wait) (j:ngak/kul) (r:zd:11409/zd:21616) (q:draft)
ngakkulding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:will have to wait/must wait) (d:<ngak>, wait, and <kulding>, will have to, written as one word) (j:ngak/kulding) (r:zd:12280/zd:18054) (q:draft)
ngaklahhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:eagerly awaited/worth waiting for) (d:<ngaklah>, wait eagerly, and <huai>, worthy of, written as one word: something one looks forward to or is eager to see) (j:ngaklah/huai) (r:zd:12101/zd:21072) (q:draft)
ngaklahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:longing/eager waiting/impatience) (d:<ngaklah>, wait eagerly, with the noun ending {-na}: eager or impatient waiting for something, also the complaint of one who is tired of waiting) (b:ngaklah) (r:zd:23487) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaklaitak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:be waiting for/be awaiting) (d:<ngak>, wait, with <laitak>, at the very time, written as one word: at present still waiting; after <ki>, is now being awaited) (j:ngak/laitak) (r:zd:16431) (q:draft)
ngaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not wait/not wait for) (d:<ngak>, wait, and <lo>, not, written as one word) (j:ngak/lo) (r:zd:21358/zd:25678) (q:draft)
ngakna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:waiting/waiting place) (d:<ngak>, wait, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of waiting or the place where one waits, as {Bus ngakna}, a bus stop; not {ngakna} a stand on which a thing rests) (r:zd:20966) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngakngak = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:habitually/commonly/over and over) (d:after a verb of speaking such as <kici> or <cih>, with no thought of waiting: the thing is said or done again and again, as a habit) (r:zd:25893/zd:16348) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngakngeungau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wait a long time/wait and wait) (d:<ngak>, wait, with the descriptive word <ngeungau>: keep waiting long and wearily) (j:ngak/ngeungau) (r:zd:19197) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaksak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:make wait/keep waiting) (d:<ngak> in its meaning wait, with the causative <sak>: make someone wait or keep someone waiting, as passengers for a bus or applicants for an office; not lay a hand on) (r:zd:16334/zd:18939) (q:draft)
ngakte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:attendants/keepers/minders) (d:<ngak> in its meaning keep watch over a place, with plural <te>: the people who mind a place, as in {sumbuk ngakte} shop attendants and {inn ngakte} those who stay to mind the house) (r:zd:22686) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngakzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:wait through/manage to wait/have waited) (d:<ngak>, wait, and <zawh>, finish or be able, written as one word; the form of <ngakzo> used before <ding>, <hangin> and <ciangin>: be able to wait, or have waited a length of time) (j:ngak/zawh) (r:zd:22185/zd:19166/zd:21843) (q:draft)
ngakzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:patience/ability to wait) (d:<ngakzo>, be able to wait, with the noun suffix <na>: the ability to wait, patience) (s:lungduaina) (b:ngakzo) (r:zd:13242/zd:10680) (q:draft)
ngakzolo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot wait/be unable to wait) (d:<ngakzo> and <lo> written as one word: not manage to wait) (j:ngakzo/lo) (r:zd:15031) (q:draft)
ngakzote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:those who wait/those who can wait) (d:<ngakzo>, be able to wait, with the plural {-te}: those who manage to wait, as in the saying that good things come to those who wait) (b:ngakzo) (r:zd:23890) (q:draft)
ngal = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:strength/effort/labor) (d:the second half of the pair {tha leh ngal}, strength and effort: the bodily work a person gives, named beside money and skill; not the animal) (r:zd:23554/zd:23993/zd:16340) (q:draft)
ngal = (i:4) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:other than/apart from/except) (d:after <lo> or <loh>, not, as in {cih loh ngal} and {cih ding lo ngal}: apart from that, followed by a statement that there is nothing else or that all the rest is different) (r:zd:16385/zd:22136/zd:10731) (q:draft)
ngalkhaat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/social) (w:lone boar/loner) (d:a wild boar that goes about alone, from <ngal>, wild boar, and {khaat}, single; {ngalkhaat bang} is like a lone boar, said of one who acts alone and does not join with others) (r:zd:23554) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngalliam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:hero/warrior/brave man) (d:a brave man who fights for his people, a word of songs and of praise; {Zomi ngalliam} is a hero of the Zomi) (s:galhang) (r:zd:12352/zd:25268) (q:draft)
ngalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not face/not rest on) (d:<nga> and <lo> written as one word: not turned toward something; {ki ngalo} is not depend on) (j:nga/lo) (r:zd:23394/zd:23006) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaltang = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:big wild boar/lone boar) (d:<ngal>, wild boar, with <tang>: a full-grown boar, bigger game than a deer; known from the saying {sakhi man lo ngaltang tum}, not having caught a deer one aims for a boar, said of reaching for the greater thing before having the lesser) (r:zd:15730) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngalthen = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature/social) (w:hornet/wasp) (d:a kind of wasp or hornet that has grubs and no honey, named beside <ngaltun> and {tuunpi}; its nest is taken at the <Khuado> festival and addressed in the song of the <khuai>) (r:zd:15996/zd:25393) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaltun = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (d:a kind of wild bee or wasp, named together with <ngalthen> and {khuaithuum}; its nest was looked at for omens at the Khuado festival; the exact kind is not determined) (r:zd:15996) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngamding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:dare to/will dare) (d:<ngam>, dare, and <ding> written as one word after a verb: to dare to do it, will dare to do it) (j:ngam/ding) (r:zd:22171/zd:25923) (q:draft)
ngamkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:dare not/not dare) (d:<ngam>, dare, and <kei>, not, written as one word and placed after the main verb) (j:ngam/kei) (r:zd:18071/zd:20545) (q:draft)
ngamlel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:simply dare/just go ahead and) (d:<ngam>, dare, and <lel>, just, written as one word after a verb: do it boldly and without hesitation) (j:ngam/lel) (r:zd:22709/zd:17215) (q:draft)
ngamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:dare not/not dare/be afraid to) (d:<ngam>, dare, and <lo>, not, written as one word after a verb: not dare to do it) (j:ngam/lo) (r:zd:19262/zd:10860/zd:15082) (q:draft)
ngamloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not dare/dare not) (d:<ngam> and <loh> written as one word after a verb: that one does not dare to do, as in {gen ngamloh}, that one dare not say) (j:ngam/loh) (r:zd:12196/zd:24231/zd:16340) (q:draft)
ngamlohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:not daring/lack of courage) (d:<ngam>, dare, with <lohna> written as one word after a verb: the fact of not daring to do it; {pai ngamlohna mun} is a place where one dare not go) (j:ngam/lohna) (r:zd:20780) (q:draft)
ngamlote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who dare not) (d:<ngamlo>, dare not, with the plural <te> after a verb: the people who do not dare to do it) (b:ngamlo) (j:ngamlo/te) (r:zd:15770/zd:21293) (q:draft)
ngammawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:dare/have the nerve) (d:<ngam>, dare, and <mawk> written as one word, after a verb: do a bold or shocking thing without fear or shame, as in broad daylight) (j:ngam/mawk) (r:zd:14981/zd:20629) (q:draft)
ngamta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:now dare/come to dare) (d:<ngam>, dare, and the particle <ta>, now or already, written as one word after a verb: now dare to, have come to dare) (j:ngam/ta) (r:zd:14587/zd:19814) (q:draft)
ngamtat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (j:gamtat) (r:zd:22435/zd:17448) (q:draft)
ngamtatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (j:gamtatna) (r:zd:20092/zd:20959) (q:draft)
nganhing = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (j:ganhing) (r:zd:20202/zd:19683) (q:draft)
Ngapali = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Ngapali) (d:beach and resort on the coast of Rakhine State in Myanmar, near Thandwe) (r:zd:11182) (q:draft)
ngapik = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:fish paste/shrimp paste/ngapi) (d:Burmese fermented paste of fish or shrimp, with a strong smell, eaten as a relish) (o:Burmese, ngapi) (r:zd:19447/zd:23797) (q:draft)
ngaplo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not dare/cannot bear to/not be up to) (d:<ngap>, dare or be up to, and <lo>, not, written as one word after a verb: not have the heart or the strength to do it) (j:ngap/lo) (r:zd:23928/zd:12267) (q:draft)
ngaploh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not be up to/be unable) (d:<ngap> and <loh> written as one word: not having the strength or heart for something; {ngaploh hun} is a time when one is not up to it) (j:ngap/loh) (r:zd:22582/zd:16302) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngapngap = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:daringly/boldly) (d:<ngap>, dare, doubled: keep daring, do something boldly and without holding back) (b:ngap) (r:zd:9435) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngasa = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:food/nature) (w:fish) (d:a fish, as a living creature and as food; {ngasa bengte} are fishermen) (s:nga)
ngate = (i:2) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:the five/five) (d:<nga>, five, with the plural <te>: the five things of a set that is named before it, as in {Solas ngate}, the five Solas, and after {sawm le} the fifteen; not fish) (r:zd:16387/zd:21257) (q:draft)
ngatin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:pointing at/holding at/threatening with) (d:after the name of a weapon, as in {temta ngatin}, with a knife pointed at someone to threaten him while another action follows; not the face or ear turned toward something) (r:zd:12628/zd:13005) (q:draft)
ngau = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:langur) (d:a long-tailed kind of monkey; the proverb {zawng nek ngau in thuak lawh} says that the langur suffers for what the monkey ate) (r:zd:25666/zd:24072) (q:draft)
ngau = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:social) (w:destitute/needy) (d:paired with <zawn>, poor, as {zawn leh ngau}: poor and destitute) (r:zd:16424) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngauna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:destitution/want/poverty) (d:the state of having nothing; nearly always said together with <zawnna>, poverty, as {zawnna ngauna}, poverty and want) (r:zd:16254/zd:20922/zd:21908) (q:draft)
ngaungau = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:earnestly/keenly/deeply) (d:placed after a verb of feeling, asking or saying: with deep and lasting feeling, earnestly and again and again, as in {lunggulh ngaungau}, long for keenly, and {kap ngaungau}, keep whining) (r:zd:25218/zd:17961/zd:24327) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaw = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:at last/finally/just then) (d:written twice, {ngaw ngaw} or {ngaw-ngaw}: at last, only then, after a wait or several attempts) (r:ts:5530/zd:19244) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngawhbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:accuse/blame) (d:<ngawh>, accuse, with <bawl>, do: lay the blame on someone, often for something not proved) (j:ngawh/bawl) (r:zd:12708) (q:draft)
ngawhbawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:accusation/allegation/charge) (d:<ngawh>, accuse, with <bawlna>, doing, written as one word: the act of accusing someone, or the accusation made) (j:ngawh/bawlna) (r:zd:15498) (q:draft)
ngawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:accusation/allegation/charge) (d:a claim that someone has done wrong; {ngawhna nial} is deny an accusation and {ngawhna tuak} is be accused) (s:mawhsakna) (b:ngawh) (r:zd:24000/zd:10924/zd:11475) (q:draft)
ngawhnate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:accusations/charges/allegations) (d:plural of <ngawhna>: the charges laid against someone) (b:ngawhna) (r:zd:11475) (q:draft)
ngawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/food) (w:fish weir/fish trap) (d:a barrier or trap set in a stream to catch fish) (r:ts:3375) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngawlhcip = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:starve/deprive of food) (d:after <an>, food: keep someone wholly without food, from <ngawl>, go without, and <cip>, completely) (r:zd:11941) (q:draft)
ngawlsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:food/health) (w:deprive of/make go without/make abstain) (d:<ngawl>, go without, and the causing <sak> written as one word: make someone go without something; {an ngawlsak} is leave without food, starve, and of a habit, make someone give it up) (j:ngawl/sak) (r:zd:23590/zd:20764) (q:draft)
ngawngaw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:only then/at last) (d:word of emphasis placed after a time or a verb: only at that point, at long last, not before) (r:ts:2320/zd:23137) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngawngkai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (j:nawngkai) (r:ts:5848/zd:11581) (q:draft)
ngawngsau = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature/home) (w:long-necked) (d:<ngawng>, neck, and <sau>, long, written as one word: with a long neck; {sa ngawngsau} is a giraffe and {khedap ngawngsau} a boot) (j:ngawng/sau) (r:zd:20310) (q:draft)
ngawngtan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:behead/decapitate) (d:<ngawng>, neck, and <tan>, cut off, written as one word: cut off the head, behead) (j:ngawng/tan) (r:zd:21040/ts:3168) (q:draft)
ngawngtansak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:behead/have beheaded) (d:<ngawngtan>, behead, and <sak> written as one word: cut off the head of someone, or have someone beheaded) (j:ngawngtan/sak) (r:zd:11501) (q:draft)
ngawnin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even) (d:<ngawn> and <in> written as one word after <na> or {te na}: the second part of {na ngawn in}, the same as <nangawn>, even) (j:ngawn/in) (r:zd:23112/zd:20545) (q:draft)
ngawnzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even/even also) (d:<ngawn> and <zong>, also, written as one word, for {nangawn zong} with its first part written apart: even that, even in that case) (j:ngawn/zong) (r:zd:25919) (q:draft)
ngawp = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is done heavily, thoroughly or all over; close in use to <gawp>) (r:zd:21006/zd:24231) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeekbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:pamper/treat tenderly/dote on) (d:<ngeek>, tender, with <bawl>, treat: handle someone gently and with great care, pamper) (j:ngeek/bawl) (r:zd:22065/zd:24234) (q:draft)
ngeekngeek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:hard/again and again/without letting up) (d:placed after a verb for an action done with force and kept up without a break, as beating, walking on or enduring) (r:zd:19381/zd:20176) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeel = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (j:ngel) (r:zd:24132) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeetngaat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:expressive word placed after a verb of going or lining up, as <kigual>: in a long line, many following one after another) (r:zd:18200) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngei nawn = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:ever again/never again) (d:<ngei>, ever, and <nawn>, any more: placed after a verb and followed by a negative such as <lo> or <kei>, never again) (r:zd:23896/zd:25506) (q:draft)
ngeiding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will ever) (d:<ngei> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: will ever do or happen, will at some time; with <lo> or <kei>, will never) (j:ngei/ding) (r:zd:11346/zd:21918) (q:draft)
ngeihi = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:have ever/once) (d:<ngei> and <hi> written as one word at the end of a sentence: it has happened before, has once done so) (j:ngei/hi) (r:zd:21588/zd:18154/zd:14609) (q:draft)
ngeihiam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:have ever) (d:<ngei>, ever, and the question word <hiam>, written as one word after a verb: has it ever been so, whether one has ever done it) (j:ngei/hiam) (r:zd:10735) (q:draft)
ngeiingaii = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:ngeingai) (r:zd:19581/zd:16291/zd:19381) (q:draft)
ngeikhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:former/one who once) (d:<ngei> and <khat> written as one word after a verb or a noun: one who has done or been so before, a former one) (j:ngei/khat) (r:zd:19332/zd:21649/zd:12477) (q:draft)
ngeikhin = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/time) (w:have already/before) (d:<ngei>, ever, and <khin>, already, written as one word after a verb: the thing has already happened or been done before now) (j:ngei/khin) (r:zd:19495/zd:12963/zd:20234) (q:draft)
ngeikhinsa = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/time) (w:have already/before) (d:<ngei> and <khinsa> written as one word after a verb: the thing has already happened once before now) (j:ngei/khinsa) (r:zd:20703/zd:16109) (q:draft)
ngeikhollo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:hardly ever/seldom/rarely) (d:<ngei> and <khollo> written as one word after a verb: has hardly ever happened or been so) (j:ngei/khollo) (r:zd:13326/zd:15913) (q:draft)
ngeilo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:never) (d:<ngei>, ever, with <lo>, not, placed after a verb: has never done or has never been so) (s:ngeikei/cikmah) (a:den/tawntunga) (b:ngei) (q:draft)
ngeilohte = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:those never before/things never) (d:<ngeiloh>, never, and the plural <te> written as one word, after a verb: the things or people that one has never seen, heard or known) (j:ngeiloh/te) (r:zd:22757/zd:21042) (q:draft)
ngeilote = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ngeilo>, never, with the plural <te>, after a verb: those who never do it, those who have never done so) (j:ngeilo/te) (r:zd:15361/zd:24276) (q:draft)
ngeimawk = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/media) (w:have once/has happened before) (d:<ngei>, have ever, and <mawk>, unexpectedly, written as one word after a verb: such a thing has in fact happened before) (j:ngei/mawk) (r:zd:12115/zd:12691) (q:draft)
ngeina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:culture/tradition/custom/regulation) (d:the customary way of doing things, handed down from the ancestors; {biakna ngeina} is a fixed rule of worship) (b:ngei)
ngeina bangmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social/everyday) (w:as usual/as is the custom) (d:<ngeina>, custom, and <bangmah>, here <bang> and <mah>, just like, not the word for nothing: just as is the custom or practice; followed by <in> and placed after the word or clause that says whose practice or what practice) (r:zd:22019/zd:23533) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeina van = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:traditional articles/cultural items/heritage objects) (d:<ngeina>, custom, and <van>, here goods or things and not heaven: the articles that belong to a tradition, such as dress, tools and instruments shown at a cultural event) (r:zd:15622/zd:22200) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeinai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (j:geinai) (r:zd:20050/zd:22545) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeinai = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:ever yet) (d:<ngei>, ever, and <nai>, yet, written as one word after a verb; with a negative it means never yet) (j:ngei/nai) (r:zd:12972/zd:11150) (q:draft)
ngeinailo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:never yet/never before) (d:<ngei> ever and <nailo> not yet written as one word after a verb: has never yet done or been so) (j:ngei/nailo) (r:zd:21034/zd:12581) (q:draft)
ngeinalaam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:traditional dance/cultural dance) (d:<ngeina>, tradition, and <laam>, dance, written as one word: a dance of the tradition of a people, shown at a festival) (j:ngeina/laam) (r:zd:21232) (q:draft)
ngeingaina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:commotion/stir/bustle) (d:<ngeingai> with the noun ending <na>, placed after a verb: the doing of something in a noisy stir by many people together, as fighting in a brawl or working busily side by side) (j:ngeingai/na) (r:zd:14738/zd:17974) (q:draft)
ngeingei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:surely/certainly/really/definitely) (d:placed after a verb or phrase to stress that it really is so or will surely be so; with <kei>, certainly not) (r:zd:22802/zd:19239/zd:24697) (q:draft)
ngeise = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ngei> and the emphatic <se> written as one word, before a negative: {ngeise lo} is never at all, not even once) (j:ngei/se) (r:zd:23653/zd:25923) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeisok = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:rhododendron) (d:the rhododendron tree and its flower, {ngeisok kung} and {ngeisok paak}; also found in place names) (r:ts:3375/zd:17162) (q:draft)
ngekbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:pamper/cosset/treat tenderly) (d:<ngek>, tender, with <bawl>, make: treat someone very gently, as one treats a small child, and so also spoil) (r:zd:9448/zd:17049) (q:draft)
ngekna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (j:ngetna) (r:zd:12933/zd:19442) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngekngek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:on and on/without a break/again and again) (d:expressive word placed after a verb: the action goes on hard and without a break, or comes again and again one after another, as in {kizom ngekngek}, keep on coming, and {kikap ngekngek}, keep on shooting at each other) (r:zd:11805/zd:15257/ts:3641) (q:draft)
ngelding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:surely/most likely/must) (d:<ngel>, surely, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb, often after <kha>: it must surely be so, a confident guess of the writer) (j:ngel/ding) (r:zd:22331/zd:12754) (q:draft)
ngelh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (j:gelh) (r:zd:25624/zd:24091) (q:draft)
ngelhngelh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:really/actually/in fact) (d:placed after a verb or describing word for emphasis: really and truly so, actually doing it) (r:zd:26385/zd:9220/zd:18918) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngelna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:plan/planning/design) (d:what is planned or arranged in the mind; {ngaihsutna ngelna} is thoughts and plans) (r:zd:21876/zd:22116) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngelngel = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:surely/certainly/most likely) (d:<ngel> said twice, placed after a verb; with <ding> it says that something must surely be so) (b:ngel) (r:zd:23937/zd:14814) (q:draft)
ngelngelding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:surely will/must surely) (d:<ngelngel>, surely, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: it must surely be so) (j:ngelngel/ding) (r:zd:20120/zd:12063) (q:draft)
ngen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ask for/request) (d:ask someone to give something; the form <nget> is used in dependent clauses) (q:draft)
ngending = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to ask for/will ask for/will request) (d:<ngen>, ask for, and <ding>, will, written as one word; {huhna ngending in} is in order to ask for help) (j:ngen/ding) (r:zd:11350/zd:14931) (q:draft)
ngengen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (w:keep praying/keep asking) (d:<ngen> said twice: go on asking; {thu ngengen} is keep on praying) (b:ngen) (r:zd:24029/zd:23022) (q:draft)
ngengngang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/nature) (w:mightily/massively/tremendously) (d:expressive word after a verb for something very great and overwhelming, as smoke billowing up or thunder roaring) (r:zd:11677/zd:11750) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngenhi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ask for/request) (d:<ngen>, ask for, and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: asks for, asked for; {huhna ngenhi} is asked for help) (j:ngen/hi) (r:zd:20215/zd:11283) (q:draft)
ngenkawikawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:ask around/go about asking) (d:<ngen> and <kawikawi> written as one word: ask for something here and there, from one place or person after another) (j:ngen/kawikawi) (r:zd:15647/zd:20257) (q:draft)
ngenkik = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:ask back/reclaim/demand back) (d:<ngen>, ask, with <kik> in the sense of back and not of again: ask for the return of what one gave, deposited or had taken away, such as money or land) (r:zd:15913/zd:23252) (q:draft)
ngenlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not ask for/not request) (d:<ngen> and <lo> written as one word: not ask for; {man ngenlo in} is without asking payment, free of charge) (j:ngen/lo) (r:zd:23245/zd:12550) (q:draft)
ngenloin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/work) (w:without asking/without charging) (d:<ngen>, ask for, and <loin>, without, written as one word: without asking for something; <man ngenloin> is free of charge) (j:ngen/loin) (r:zd:23388/zd:18234) (q:draft)
ngenmasa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:ask first/request beforehand) (d:<ngen> and <masa> written as one word: ask for a thing first, before anything else) (j:ngen/masa) (r:zd:12267) (q:draft)
Ngennung = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Ngennung) (d:village in Tedim Township, Chin State) (r:zd:21559) (q:draft)
ngenta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:ask for/request) (d:<ngen>, ask for, with <ta>, now or already, written as one word: has asked for, now asks for) (j:ngen/ta) (r:zd:14681/zd:19676) (q:draft)
ngenthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:can ask for/can request/can apply) (d:<ngen>, ask for, and <thei>, able, written as one word) (j:ngen/thei) (r:zd:12307/zd:23569) (q:draft)
ngetbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as requested/as asked) (d:<nget>, ask for, and <bang>, like, written as one word: just as was asked, usually {a ngetbang}) (j:nget/bang) (r:zd:20176) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngetbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:ask further/request more/ask for an extension) (d:<nget>, ask for, with the ending {-beh}, in addition, as in <behlap>: ask for something more, or ask again for more time) (r:zd:15084/zd:14549) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngetkikna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:claim/request for return/appeal) (d:<nget>, ask for, and <kikna>, back or again, written as one word: a request to get something back or to have a matter looked at again) (j:nget/kikna) (r:zd:19685) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngetna nei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:make a request/petition/appeal/ask for) (d:<ngetna>, a request, and <nei>, have: to make a request or an appeal; the thing asked for stands before the pair, often as a clause with <ding>, and the one asked takes <tungah> or <kiang>) (r:zd:14543/zd:25622) (q:draft)
ngetngut = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:earnestly/deeply) (d:placed after a verb of feeling or asking: deeply and without ceasing, earnestly, as in {lungdam ngetngut}, be deeply thankful, and {thum ngetngut}, plead earnestly) (r:zd:12144/zd:22560) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngetpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:pray for/pray with) (d:<nget>, ask, with <pih>, together with or for someone: in {thu ngetpih}, pray for someone or pray together with someone) (b:nget) (r:zd:16204/zd:26708/zd:17398) (q:draft)
ngetsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:intend to ask for/try to demand/seek) (d:<nget>, ask for, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: set out to ask for or demand something, as money or rights) (j:nget/sawm) (r:zd:15994/zd:14919) (q:draft)
ngettheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:right to apply/means of requesting) (d:<nget> and <theihna> written as one word: being able to ask or apply for something, the opening for applications) (j:nget/theihna) (r:zd:11118) (q:draft)
ngeu = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:placed after a verb for emphasis, about as plainly, outright or just so: {hi ngeu hi} is it plainly is; also doubled as {ngeu ngau}. In {zawh ngeu} it is part of <zawhngeu>, cat) (r:zd:24977/zd:25470) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngeungeu = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:plaintively/on and on) (d:expressive word after a verb of sound such as <kap>, weep, <tau>, groan, or <khuang>, of a cicada: the sound goes on and on in a drawn-out, moaning way; {kap ngeungeu} is weep bitterly) (r:zd:25616/zd:20026) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngiahsun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:ngaihsun) (r:zd:21605/zd:23129) (q:draft)
ngiahsutna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:ngaihsutna) (r:zd:20520/zd:20568) (q:draft, a frequent misspelling of ngaihsutna with the letters a and i exchanged)
ngial = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:indeed/outright/altogether) (d:emphatic word placed after a verb or noun, close to <ngiat>: really so, to the full extent) (r:zd:25687/zd:23754) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngiat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:indeed/truly/certainly/definitely) (d:placed after a verb or a name to give it emphasis: really and without doubt, on purpose, that very one; with a negative, not at all) (r:zd:10957/zd:20071/zd:21929) (q:draft)
ngiat inzong = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/media) (w:even/himself too/in person) (d:<ngiat>, indeed, with the subject marker <in> and <zong>, also, written together: placed after the subject, most often a person of high office, it says that even this very one did or said the thing) (r:zd:13282/zd:11604/zd:19125) (q:draft)
ngiatding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<ngiat> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: so that it will indeed be done, to do it without fail) (j:ngiat/ding) (r:zd:25768/zd:20595) (q:draft)
ngiatdingin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:in order really to/expressly to) (d:<ngiat>, indeed, and <dingin>, in order to, written as one word after a verb: with the firm purpose of doing it) (j:ngiat/dingin) (r:zd:21321) (q:draft)
ngiatin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:himself/in person/expressly) (d:the emphatic word <ngiat>, the very one or really so, with <in>: after a person, he himself and no other; after a purpose, expressly or on purpose for it) (r:zd:13195/ts:3284/zd:12785) (q:draft)
ngiatlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/certainly not) (d:the emphatic <ngiat> with <lo> written as one word after a verb: not at all, by no means) (j:ngiat/lo) (r:zd:22116/zd:19898/zd:19816) (q:draft)
ngiatmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:indeed/the very/really) (d:<ngiat> and <mah> written as one word after a verb or a name for strong emphasis: really so, that very one and no other) (j:ngiat/mah) (r:zd:11783/zd:15301) (q:draft)
ngiatna = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:indeed/truly) (d:<ngiat>, indeed, written together with the <na> of <nading>: {ngah ngiatna ding in} is so that one may indeed receive) (j:ngiat/na) (r:zd:19779) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngiatngait = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:ngiatngiat) (r:zd:22371/zd:23240) (q:draft)
ngiatngiat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:steadily/without fail/strictly) (d:placed after a verb: doing it each time, one after another and without leaving any out, or in that one way only; {khe tawh pai ngiatngiat} is go on foot the whole way) (r:zd:22046/zd:25616/zd:23830) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngiattawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:with that very/purely by/expressly with) (d:<ngiat> and <tawh> written as one word after a noun: by means of that very thing and nothing else; {khe ngiattawh} is on foot, {ngimna ngiattawh} is on purpose) (j:ngiat/tawh) (r:zd:24847/zd:20293) (q:draft)
ngiatte = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:those who truly) (d:<ngiat> and the plural <te> written as one word after a verb: those who really do it, the ones who actually do so) (j:ngiat/te) (r:zd:11057/zd:26310) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngiatzen = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:truly indeed/really) (d:<ngiat> and <zen> written as one word, placed after a verb for strong emphasis: truly, really and no less) (j:ngiat/zen) (r:zd:21803/zd:21780) (q:draft)
ngiatzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even/himself too) (d:placed after a noun or name: even that very person or thing, he himself as well; the emphatic <ngiat> with <zong> written as one word) (r:zd:19966/zd:17668/zd:11934) (q:draft)
ngiau = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:expressive word placed after a verb; it seems to say that the thing simply or outright happens or is so, just like that; the exact sense is to be confirmed) (r:zd:20334/zd:21908/zd:21509) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngiaumawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<ngiau> and <mawk> written as one word, an expressive word placed after a verb: the thing is said or done outright, just like that, with a note of surprise; the exact sense is to be confirmed) (j:ngiau/mawk) (r:zd:21780/zd:21803) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngiengei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/nature) (w:winding/meandering) (d:descriptive adverb placed after a verb: in a winding, twisting way, as a river or a crooked path) (r:zd:25863) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngiim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:ngim) (r:zd:21567/zd:22571) (q:draft)
ngiimna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:ngimna) (r:zd:22334/zd:21037) (q:draft)
ngiingeii = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:utterly/badly) (d:expressive word placed after a verb, giving it force: to a great degree, thoroughly; perhaps a form of <ngeingai>) (r:zd:21108) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngilh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:forget) (d:forget; mostly the second part of {mang ngilh}, which the lexicon writes <mangngilh>, and in {ngilh mawh}, not to be forgotten) (r:zd:10882/zd:23453) (q:draft)
ngilhmawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unforgettable/not to be forgotten) (d:<ngilh>, forget, with <mawh>: that cannot or must not be forgotten) (j:ngilh/mawh) (r:zd:22691/zd:11387) (q:draft)
ngimbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:target/aim at/single out) (d:<ngim>, aim at, with <bawl>, make: make someone or something the target, of an attack or of a product or plan) (j:ngim/bawl) (r:zd:16970/zd:19667) (q:draft)
ngimin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:aim at/target) (d:<ngim> and <in> written as one word: taking aim at, with someone or something as the target) (j:ngim/in) (r:zd:12803/zd:13061) (q:draft)
ngimna bulpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:main aim/chief objective/basic purpose) (d:<ngimna>, aim, and <bulpi>, foundation, main: the principal aim of a person, plan or organization; used after a possessive, as in {i ngimna bulpi}, our main aim, and in headings that list the aims of a society) (r:zd:24069/zd:25461/zd:16150) (q:draft)
ngimnam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (j:gimnam) (r:zd:19447/zd:20798) (q:draft)
ngimnapi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:main aim/chief goal) (d:<ngimna>, aim, with <pi>, chief: the main aim or goal) (j:ngimna/pi) (r:zd:25109/ts:2349) (q:draft)
ngimngiat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/social) (w:deliberately/on purpose/intentionally) (d:<ngim>, aim at, with <ngiat>, indeed: aiming straight at someone or something, on purpose and not by accident; usually followed by <in>) (r:zd:14687/zd:19369) (q:draft)
ngimngim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep aiming at/aim deliberately) (d:<ngim>, aim at, said twice: keep pointing a thing at a target; {ngimngim in} is on purpose, with intent) (b:ngim) (r:zd:26976) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngimsa = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:aimed at/pointed at/targeted) (d:<ngim>, aim a weapon at, with <sa>, already done: held aimed at a person or place, after <thautawh>, with a gun, and before {in koih}, keep so; differs from the first sense, an intention) (r:zd:13061/zd:13145/zd:12097) (q:draft)
nging = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:sound/ring) (d:make a sound, ring; apparently the same word as <ging>, sound; some sentences have another use that is not clear) (r:zd:20798/zd:21989) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngingkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:ring out/sound aloud) (d:<nging>, sound, and <khia>, out, written as one word: of laughter or a voice, come out loud and clear) (j:nging/khia) (r:zd:20778/zd:21876) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngiungeu = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:steadily/fixedly/unmoved) (d:expressive word after a verb of staying in one state, such as <kip>, be firm, <tu>, sit, or <um>, believe: remaining so without moving or changing, where the sense of waiting is absent) (r:zd:24574/zd:16254/zd:24214) (q:draft)
ngo = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:NGO/non-governmental organisation) (d:the English abbreviation, written in capitals as {NGO}: an aid or welfare organisation that is not part of a government, not the colour word) (o:English) (r:zd:12550/zd:20403/zd:18208) (q:draft)
ngongtat = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:terrorist/extremist/violent group) (d:those who use violence against the public, in the news before <te>, <pawl> or <galkap>: terrorists, an armed violent group; in recent news also a label put before the name of the military council) (r:zd:12829/ts:2097) (q:draft)
ngongtatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:to commit violence/to attack) (d:<ngongtat>, do violence, and <ding> written as one word: in order to commit violence, going to carry out an attack) (j:ngongtat/ding) (r:zd:10767/zd:18231) (q:draft)
ngongtatlua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:be too violent/be very harsh/be cruel) (d:<ngongtat>, be violent, and <lua>, too much, written as one word: act too harshly or cruelly) (j:ngongtat/lua) (r:zd:22178) (q:draft)
ngongtatnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:want to do violence/be bent on violence) (d:<ngongtat> and <nuam> written as one word: want to act with violence; {mi ngongtatnuam} is a person given to violence) (j:ngongtat/nuam) (r:zd:16916/zd:12307) (q:draft)
ngongtatsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:plot an attack/attempt violence) (d:<ngongtat>, do violence, with <sawm>, intend, written as one word: plan or attempt a violent attack; {a ngongtatsawm mi} is a person who plots an attack) (j:ngongtat/sawm) (r:zd:18231/zd:12860) (q:draft)
ngongtatsawmna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:terror plot/planned attack) (d:the noun of <ngongtatsawm>: a plan or attempt to carry out a violent attack) (b:ngongtatsawm) (r:zd:15073) (q:draft)
ngongtatsawmpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:would-be attacker/man who plotted an attack) (d:<ngongtatsawm>, plot an attack, and <pa> written as one word: the man who planned or attempted a violent attack) (j:ngongtatsawm/pa) (r:zd:15188/zd:16932) (q:draft)
ngontat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (j:ngongtat) (r:zd:11735) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngosak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/health) (w:whiten/make white) (d:<ngo>, white, with the causative <sak>: make something white or fair, as the skin) (b:ngo) (r:zd:20131/zd:12611) (q:draft)
ngualzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (j:gualzawh) (r:zd:19783/zd:19731) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngualzawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:gualzawhna) (r:zd:19663/zd:19731) (q:draft)
ngualzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (j:gualzo) (r:zd:19731/zd:20271) (q:draft, low confidence)
nguan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:instil/put into) (d:put a thought or feeling into the mind of someone; probably another form of <guan>) (r:zd:22282) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngumngek = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/family) (w:young/youthful) (d:placed after a word for a young person, as in {tangval ngumngek lai}: still in the bloom of youth) (r:zd:24574) (q:draft, low confidence)
NHK = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:NHK) (d:the public broadcaster of Japan, often quoted as a source of news) (r:zd:17822/zd:19476) (q:draft)
ni = (i:1) (t:num) (f:time) (w:day) (d:a day as a length of time, used with a number to count days) (r:1.1.5) as in counting of days number
ni = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:aunt) (d:the sister of one's father) (r:zai:aunt) (q:draft)
ni = (i:3) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:let us) (d:placed at the end of a sentence after a verb to call on the hearers to do something together with the speaker: let us; {kei ni} is let us not) (r:zd:26956/ts:3280/zd:25136) (q:draft)
niainuai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:hazily/murkily/in a muddle) (d:placed after a verb: thick and unclear, of smoke that fills a place or of a dazed and muddled mind) (r:zd:12856) (q:draft, low confidence)
nialcipden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:keep denying/deny flatly) (d:<nial>, deny, <cip>, firmly, and <den>, always, written as one word: go on denying a thing firmly) (j:nial/cip/den) (r:zd:19801) (q:draft)
nialden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:keep denying/always contradict) (d:<nial>, deny or dispute, with <den>, always, written as one word: go on denying, or argue against something all the time) (j:nial/den) (r:zd:25909) (q:draft)
nialkik = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:deny in reply/rebut/counter) (d:<nial>, deny, with <kik> in its meaning back, in return: answer a charge or a report by denying it, mostly after {ci'n}, saying; it is a first denial given in reply, not a denial made a second time) (r:zd:19671/zd:12302) (q:draft)
niallo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not refuse/not object/accept) (d:<nial> and <lo> written as one word: not refuse or contradict; {niallo in} is without objecting) (j:nial/lo) (r:zd:21028/zd:20829/zd:22873) (q:draft)
nialpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:deny at once/refuse at once/reject immediately) (d:<nial>, deny or refuse, and <pah>, at once, written as one word) (j:nial/pah) (r:zd:20569/zd:23977) (q:draft)
nialthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:can deny/can refuse) (d:<nial> and <thei> written as one word: able to deny or refuse; {nialthei nawnlo} is no longer able to deny) (j:nial/thei) (r:zd:14922/zd:16713) (q:draft)
nialtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:can be denied/can be refused) (d:<nial>, deny or refuse, with <theih>, be able: {nialtheih omlo} is it cannot be denied or refused) (j:nial/theih) (r:zd:20850) (q:draft)
nialzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:refute/be able to deny) (d:<nial> and <zawh> written as one word: be able to deny or argue down; {kuamah a nialzawh ding thu ahi kei} is a thing no one can deny) (j:nial/zawh) (r:zd:19239) (q:draft, low confidence)
nialzo = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:be able to refuse/resist/say no to) (d:<nial> in its meaning refuse, with <zo>, be able: manage to say no to a desire or a pleasure, as in {pumpi deihna nialzo}; not contradicting what someone says) (r:zd:14927/zd:24214) (q:draft)
niamkiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:decline/fall low/sink/be degraded) (d:<niam>, low, with <kiat>, fall: go down in standing, quality or way of life; unlike <kiniamkhiat>, humble oneself, it is a fall that is not chosen) (r:zd:21978/zd:21049/zd:24749) (q:draft)
niamkiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:decline/fall/degradation/low state) (d:<niamkiat>, fall low, with the noun suffix <na>: a fall in standing or condition, distinguished from <kiniamkhiatna>, humility) (b:niamkiat) (r:zd:21049/zd:9426) (q:draft)
niamlam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/body) (w:lower part/lower side/low end) (d:<niam>, low, with <lam>, side, written as one word and used after <a>: the lower part of a thing, the downward direction, or those of low standing) (j:niam/lam) (r:zd:21306/zd:24320) (q:draft)
niangphan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:plain tea/green tea) (d:tea drunk plain, without milk or sugar, the bitter tea served in tea shops; compare <niangtui>, tea) (r:zd:22775/zd:21032) (q:draft, low confidence)
niangteh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:tea/tea leaf) (d:the leaves of the tea plant, fresh or dried, and tea in general; the drink made from them is <niangtui>) (r:zd:23249/zd:22856) (q:draft)
niangtui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:tea) (d:tea as a drink) (r:zai:tea) (q:draft)
niangtuisai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/social) (w:tea shop/teahouse/cafe) (d:<niangtui>, tea, and <sai>, shop, written as one word: a shop where people sit to drink tea and eat) (j:niangtui/sai) (r:zd:25915/zd:11078) (q:draft)
nianua = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/home) (w:in a mess/in a jumble/messily) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: all mixed up, untidy and without order; {kigawm nianua} is mixed in a jumble) (r:zd:21605/zd:25927/zd:20905) (q:draft)
niapnuap = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:shabby/dowdy/run-down) (d:poor and worn in look, said of clothes and of a place or person that has nothing fine) (r:zd:25433) (q:draft, low confidence)
nibang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (d:<ni>, day, and <bang> written as one word: in {nibang zah}, how many days; in songs and blessings <ni> is the sun and the sense is like the sun) (j:ni/bang) (r:zd:22557/zd:15865) (q:draft, low confidence)
nibup = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:whole day/all day) (d:<ni>, day, and <bup>, whole, written as one word; {nibup in} is all day long) (j:ni/bup) (r:zd:25305/zd:22830) (q:draft)
Nicaea = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:religion) (w:Nicaea) (d:ancient city of Asia Minor where the church council of AD 325 was held) (r:zd:9239) (q:draft)
Nice = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Nice) (d:city on the south coast of France; also the name of its football club) (r:zd:11771) (q:draft, low confidence)
niciam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/health/social) (w:appointment/appointed day) (d:<ni>, day, with <ciam>, promise: a day fixed in advance for a meeting or a visit, as with an office or a clinic) (r:zd:25347/zd:25262) (q:draft)
niciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:on the day/until the day) (d:<ni>, day, and <ciang>, up to or when, written as one word after a date or day name: on that day, by or until that day; {nikhat niciang} is some day) (j:ni/ciang) (r:zd:23528/zd:19805/zd:15294) (q:draft)
niciangbek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:only until the day/only up to) (d:<niciang> and <bek> written as one word after a date: until that day and no later) (j:niciang/bek) (r:zd:13270) (q:draft)
niciangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:on the day/when the day comes) (d:<ni> day and <ciangin> when written as one word: on a coming day, as in {Monday niciangin}, on Monday; {nikhat niciangin} is one day, some day) (j:ni/ciangin) (r:zd:24452/zd:20387) (q:draft)
nicileng = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if we were to say/to put it) (d:<ni>, let us, and <cileng>, if we say, written as one word after <gen>: {a tom in gen nicileng} is to put it briefly) (j:ni/cileng) (r:zd:23943/zd:10682) (q:draft)
nickel = (i:1) (t:n) (c:stone) (f:nature/work) (w:nickel) (d:a silver-white metal that is mined) (o:English) (r:zd:22595/zd:20403) (q:draft, low confidence)
Nickname = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:nickname) (d:the English word, used beside or in place of <minneu>) (s:minneu) (o:English) (r:zd:18056/zd:12179) (q:draft, low confidence)
nidang = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:another day/some other day/later) (d:<ni>, day, with <dang>, other: on another day; with <ciangin> it looks forward to a later day, where the other sense looks back to the past) (r:zd:10761/zd:9257) (q:draft, low confidence)
nidang sangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:than before/more than formerly) (d:<nidang>, formerly, and <sangin>, than: than before, than it used to be; it stands before the quality or verb that is compared, which is mostly followed by <zaw>, more) (r:zd:26097/zd:21156) (q:draft)
nidangciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:some other day/later/in the future) (d:<nidang>, another day, and <ciang>, when, written as one word: when another day comes, at a later time) (j:nidang/ciang) (r:zd:25909/zd:20892) (q:draft)
nidanglai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:long ago/in former times/in the old days) (d:<nidang>, formerly, with the ending {-lai}, at the time of: in former times; before a noun, of old) (b:nidang) (r:ts:301/zd:21059/zd:20410) (q:draft)
niding = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time) (w:day/date) (d:<ni> and <ding> written as one word: the day on which something is to be done, the date set for it) (j:ni/ding) (r:zd:11540/zd:19166/zd:15111) (q:draft)
nidong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:until/up to the day) (d:<ni>, day, with <dong>, until, written as one word after a date or a day of the week: until that day) (j:ni/dong) (r:zd:12336/zd:11081) (q:draft)
Nigeria = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Nigeria) (d:a country in West Africa) (r:zd:11062/zd:20145) (q:draft)
Nightclub = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:nightclub) (d:a place open at night for drinking, music and dancing) (o:English) (r:zd:13326/zd:14763) (q:draft)
nihah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in two/at two) (d:<nih>, two, and <ah>, at, written as one word after a noun: in two of them, as {mun nihah}, in two places) (j:nih/ah) (r:zd:22686/zd:21843) (q:draft)
nihlak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:among two/of the two/between two) (d:<nih>, two, and <lak>, among, written as one word; {nihlak ah} is of the two, {nihlak pan} out of the two) (j:nih/lak) (r:zd:21989/zd:21918) (q:draft)
nihleh = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:two and/two or) (d:<nih> and <leh> written as one word: two and, before a further number or thing; {nihleh thum} is two or three) (j:nih/leh) (r:zd:11044/zd:11271) (q:draft)
nihmah = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:both/the two) (d:<nih> and the emphatic <mah> written as one word: the two of them, both) (j:nih/mah) (r:zd:16976/zd:20142) (q:draft)
nihpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:two of them/the two) (d:<nih>, two, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: the two, or two of those just named; {asite lakah nihpen} is two among the dead) (j:nih/pen) (r:zd:11752/zd:15123) (q:draft)
nihtak = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:two/both/as many as two) (d:<nih>, two, and <tak> written as one word after a noun: two of them, with weight on the number; {nihtak in} is the two of them together as doers) (j:nih/tak) (r:zd:11504/zd:17514) (q:draft)
nihtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:with two/by two) (d:<nih>, two, and <tawh>, with, written as one word after a noun: with two of them, by means of two) (j:nih/tawh) (r:zd:12456/zd:11545/zd:14848) (q:draft)
nihtepen = (i:1) (t:num) (f:everyday) (w:the two/both) (d:<nihte>, the two, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word after a noun: the two of them, as what the sentence is about) (j:nihte/pen) (r:zd:14899/zd:16584) (q:draft)
nihtezong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:both also/both of them too) (d:<nihte>, the two, and <zong>, also, written as one word after a noun: both of them, the two as well) (j:nihte/zong) (r:zd:14965/zd:15994) (q:draft)
nihtuak = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:both/both of them) (d:<nih>, two, and <tuak>, each, written as one word: {a nihtuak} is both of the two) (j:nih/tuak) (r:zd:22495/zd:23590/zd:26953) (q:draft)
nihveibang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:about twice/some two times) (d:<nihvei>, twice, and <bang>, about, written as one word) (j:nihvei/bang) (r:zd:12955/zd:15283) (q:draft)
nihveitak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/everyday) (w:twice/as many as two times) (d:<nihvei>, twice, with the emphatic <tak>, written as one word: two whole times, stressing that it happened more than once) (j:nihvei/tak) (r:zd:11285/zd:13260) (q:draft)
nihzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:both/the two also) (d:<nih> and <zong> written as one word, after a noun: both of them, the two as well) (j:nih/zong) (r:zd:11234/zd:15577/zd:15255) (q:draft)
