nui = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:laugh) (d:laugh, with joy or in disbelief; before another word such as <hun>, time, the form is <nuih>) (a:kap) (q:draft)
nuihciam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:joke/jest/fun) (d:joking, what is said in fun and not meant; {nuihciam lel} is only as a joke, the same as <ciamnuih> with its parts in the other order) (s:ciamnuih) (r:zd:22691/zd:19600) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuihmai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:smile/be cheerful) (d:<nuih>, laugh, with <mai>, face: smile, show a glad face; also used as a noun, a smile) (r:zd:21075/zd:22040/zd:20697) (q:draft)
nuihsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:try to laugh/mean to laugh) (d:<nuih>, laugh, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: make a point of laughing) (j:nuih/sawm) (r:zd:20778) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuihza = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find funny/be amused/laugh at) (d:feel like laughing at someone or something, find it laughable; from <nuih>, laugh) (b:nuih) (r:zd:25139/zd:14591/zd:15528) (q:draft)
nuikawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:laughing/while laughing/with a laugh) (d:<nui>, laugh, and <kawm>, while, written as one word: laughing while doing something else) (j:nui/kawm) (r:zd:16245/zd:15491) (q:draft)
nuikhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:laugh together) (d:<nui>, laugh, and <khawm>, together, written as one word: laugh together, share laughter) (j:nui/khawm) (r:zd:19174/zd:20358) (q:draft)
nuikhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/body) (w:laugh out/burst out laughing/smile) (d:<nui>, laugh, with <khia>, out: break into a laugh or a smile) (j:nui/khia) (r:zd:20942/zd:14587) (q:draft)
nuisak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:make laugh/amuse) (d:<nui>, laugh, with the causative <sak>: make someone laugh) (b:nui) (r:zd:25734/zd:25808) (q:draft)
nukibanglo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family) (w:of different mothers) (d:<nu> and <kibanglo> written as one word: not having the same mother, said of half brothers and half sisters, often together with <pakibang>) (j:nu/kibanglo) (r:zd:11366) (q:draft)
nule = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:mother and) (d:<nu> and <le> written as one word: mother and; {nule pa} is mother and father, parents) (j:nu/le) (r:zd:13076/zd:15941) (q:draft)
nuleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:mother and) (d:<nu> and <leh> written as one word, in the pair {nuleh pa}, mother and father, parents) (j:nu/leh) (r:zd:20572/zd:15644) (q:draft)
nulehpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (j:nu leh pa) (r:zd:23616/zd:23888) (q:draft)
nulehpate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:parents) (d:<nulehpa>, mother and father, with the plural <te>: parents) (b:nulehpa) (r:zd:20972/zd:15361/zd:25281) (q:draft)
nulepa = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:parents/mother and father) (d:<nu>, mother, <le>, and, and <pa>, father, written as one word: the parents of a child, the usual meaning in present-day writing, often with <te> or beside <tate>, children) (s:nu leh pa) (r:zd:14652/zd:16508/zd:20039) (q:draft)
nulepate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:parents) (d:<nu>, mother, <le>, and, and <pate>, fathers, written as one word: mother and father, parents) (s:nu leh pa) (j:nu/le/pate) (r:zd:24069/zd:21991/zd:24320) (q:draft)
nulkeu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/body) (w:wipe dry/dry off) (d:<nul>, wipe, and <keu>, dry, written as one word: wipe something until it is dry, as the face after washing) (j:nul/keu) (r:zd:24276/zd:19330) (q:draft)
nulmang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:wipe away/erase/blot out) (d:<nul>, wipe, with <mang>, away: wipe something out so that it is gone, said of past mistakes, old records and tears) (j:nul/mang) (r:zd:17055/zd:24713) (q:draft)
nulna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:wiper/wiping cloth) (d:<nul>, wipe, with the noun ending {-na}: a thing for wiping, named after what is wiped, or the act of wiping) (b:nul) (r:zd:23848/zd:13217) (q:draft)
numai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (j:numei) (r:zd:17468) (q:draft, low confidence)
numbat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/it) (j:nambat) (o:English) (r:zd:23870/zd:19679/zd:16799) (q:draft)
number = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it/everyday) (w:number) (d:a number that identifies something, as in {Phone number}; also a figure used in counting) (s:nambat) (o:English) (r:zd:16660/zd:15772/zd:22975) (q:draft)
numei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:woman) (d:an adult female person) (a:pasal)
numei kizuak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:prostitute/sex worker) (d:<numei>, woman, and <kizuak>, sell oneself: a woman who sells herself, a prostitute; used as a noun, with <khat> or a number after it) (r:zd:17575/zd:23297) (q:draft)
numei kizuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:brothel/prostitution) (d:<numei>, woman, and <kizuakna>, selling: the selling of women, that is prostitution, and the place where it is done, a brothel; with <ah> and a verb of sending, into prostitution or to a brothel) (r:zd:19145/zd:12470) (q:draft)
numei naupang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:women and children) (d:<numei>, woman, and <naupang>, child, set side by side without <leh>: women and children, named together as those who are weak and to be protected; in other sentences the same two words are a female child, a girl) (r:zd:16157/ts:1885) (q:draft, low confidence)
numei pasal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:women and men/both sexes/male and female) (d:<numei>, woman, and <pasal>, man, set side by side without <leh>, and: women and men together, people of either sex; {numei pasal cih omlo} is without regard to sex) (r:zd:20930/zd:24948) (q:draft)
numeibuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:rape) (d:<numei>, woman, and <buan>, rape, written as one word: the rape of a woman, named as a crime) (j:numei/buan) (r:zd:14756) (q:draft)
numeidang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/family) (w:another woman/other women) (d:<numei> and <dang> written as one word: a woman other than the one spoken of) (j:numei/dang) (r:zd:16504/zd:16085) (q:draft)
numeikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:a woman/one woman) (d:<numei> and <khat> written as one word: a woman, a certain woman) (j:numei/khat) (r:zd:21015/zd:17536) (q:draft)
numeinih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:two women) (d:<numei> and <nih> written as one word: two women or two girls) (j:numei/nih) (r:zd:11769/zd:11283) (q:draft)
numeino = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:girl/little girl/young girl) (d:<numei>, female, with <no>, young or small: a girl) (b:numei) (r:42.8.54) (q:draft)
numeinote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:girls/young girls) (d:<numeino>, girl, with the plural <te>) (b:numeino) (r:ts:3137/zd:22446) (q:draft)
numeipen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:the woman) (d:<numei>, woman, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the woman, as the one spoken about) (j:numei/pen) (r:zd:16365/zd:22422) (q:draft)
numeisan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:mere woman) (d:a woman of no special standing, in {numeisan khat}, a mere woman; meaning inferred from two sentences) (r:zd:24411/zd:25609) (q:draft, low confidence)
numeiten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:women/the women) (d:<numei>, woman, with <ten>, the plural marker joined with the marker of the doer: the women, as those who do or say something) (b:numei) (j:numei/ten) (r:zd:25110/zd:18920) (q:draft)
numeivan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:female genitals/female organ/vagina) (d:<numei>, woman, with <van>, thing, written as one word: a polite word for the female sexual organ) (j:numei/van) (r:zd:12392) (q:draft, low confidence)
numeizong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/everyday) (w:women also/women too) (d:<numei>, woman, and <zong>, also, written as one word: women as well, also women) (j:numei/zong) (r:zd:19906/zd:15745) (q:draft)
Numin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/everyday) (w:mother's name) (d:<nu>, mother, and <min>, name, written as one word: the name of the mother, as asked for on a form) (j:nu/min) (r:zd:16928) (q:draft, low confidence)
nun = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:life/living) (d:the first part of <nuntak>, live, written as a separate word: life or living, in {nun zia}, way of life, which is also written <nunzia>, in {nun nuam}, live happily, and in {nun tak}) (r:zd:21013/zd:23989) (q:draft)
nung = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:time) (w:last/previous) (d:before a word of time such as <kum> or the name of a weekday: the one just past, as in {nung kum}, last year, and {nung Monday}, last Monday) (r:zd:10783/zd:12869) (q:draft)
nungak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:young woman/girl/maiden) (d:a young unmarried woman, a virgin) (a:tangval) (r:19.148.12) (q:draft)
nungak siangtho = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:virgin) (d:<nungak>, young woman, and <siangtho>, holy: a virgin, a woman who has not been with a man, said above all of Mary the mother of Jesus; among Roman Catholics also a nun, a religious sister) (r:zd:23792/zd:21978) (q:draft)
nungak tangval = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:young people/young women and men/unmarried youth) (d:<nungak>, a young woman, and <tangval>, a young man, set side by side without a conjunction: the unmarried young people of a community taken together, or a girl and a boy as a couple) (r:zd:17023/zd:20794) (q:draft)
nungaklai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/time) (w:maidenhood/girlhood) (d:<nungak> and <lai> written as one word: the time when a woman is still young and unmarried) (j:nungak/lai) (r:zd:19593/zd:20725) (q:draft)
nungciang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:afterwards/later/hereafter) (d:<nung> and <ciang> written as one word: afterwards, later on; before a noun, the time to come, also the life after death) (j:nung/ciang) (r:zd:24542/zd:21898/zd:15894) (q:draft)
nungciangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:afterward/later/then) (d:<nung>, after, with <ciangin>, when; {tua nungciangin} is after that, {a nungciangin} is afterward or in turn) (s:nungcianga) (q:draft)
nungdeuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:recently/lately/a little later) (d:<nung>, after or behind, with <deuh>, somewhat: a little while back, as in {nungdeuh mahmah in}, very recently; also a little further on in a text or in time) (j:nung/deuh) (r:zd:11924/zd:23784/zd:15784) (q:draft)
nungdiak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:recently/lately/not long ago) (d:<nung>, after, with <diak>: a short time ago, mostly as {nungdiak in}; before a noun it means recent, as in {nungdiak thupiangte}, the recent events) (r:zd:11150/zd:18067/zd:12033) (q:draft)
nungdiakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:recently/lately) (d:<nungdiak> and <in> written as one word: a short time ago) (j:nungdiak/in) (r:zd:11175/zd:11679) (q:draft)
nunggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:blow hard/blow violently) (d:of wind or a storm: <nung>, here blow as in <nungsuk>, with <gawp>, violently) (j:nung/gawp) (r:zd:14547/zd:19960) (q:draft)
nungin = (i:2) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:after) (d:<nung>, back or behind, with {-in}: after an event or a length of time, mostly as {khit nungin} after a verb; not the blowing of the wind) (s:khitciangin) (r:zd:11279/zd:16245/zd:19577) (q:draft)
nungkal = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last week) (d:<nung>, back, with <kal>, week: in the week before this one; before the name of a day it means that day of last week, as {nungkal Thursday ni in}, last Thursday) (r:zd:17175/zd:15535/zd:19385) (q:draft)
nungkalsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/media) (w:last week/in the past week) (d:<nung> behind, <kal> week and <sung> during written as one word, mostly as {nungkalsung in}: during the week that has passed) (j:nung/kal/sung) (r:zd:12309/zd:19860/zd:15374) (q:draft)
nungkha = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last month) (d:<nung>, behind, and <kha>, month, written as one word: the month before this one, last month) (j:nung/kha) (r:zd:11864/zd:18058/zd:12807) (q:draft)
nungkhasung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last month) (d:<nung>, behind or past, <kha>, month, and <sung>, during, written as one word: during last month; usually followed by <in>) (j:nung/kha/sung) (r:zd:18110/zd:14648/zd:15679) (q:draft)
nungkum = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last year) (d:<nung>, behind or after, with <kum>, year: the year before this one) (s:nikum) (r:zd:12259/zd:22046/zd:16239) (q:draft)
nungkumsung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:last year/during last year) (d:<nung>, back, <kum>, year, and <sung>, during, written as one word: in the course of last year) (j:nung/kum/sung) (r:zd:21563/zd:18028) (q:draft)
nunglam = (i:2) (t:n) (f:time) (w:past/the past) (d:the time that lies behind, what has already happened, set against <mailam>, the time ahead; {nunglam thu} is matters of the past) (a:mailam) (r:zd:21081/zd:23045/zd:17055) (q:draft)
nunglam = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:afterwards/later) (d:in {a nunglam ciangin} and {a nunglam ah}: at a time after the event just told, later on) (r:zd:9216/zd:20010) (q:draft, low confidence)
nunglamdeuh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:some time ago/a while back/earlier) (d:<nunglam>, the past, and <deuh>, somewhat, written as one word: a little while back, at some earlier time) (j:nunglam/deuh) (r:zd:19182/zd:15272) (q:draft)
nunglamdiak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:earlier/some time ago/previously) (d:<nunglam>, the past, and <diak> written as one word, often followed by <in>: at an earlier time, of something that has happened before) (j:nunglam/diak) (r:zd:20234/zd:11099) (q:draft)
nungleh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:backward/back/turning back) (d:<nung>, back, with a second part meaning turn over: turned toward the back; {nungleh pai} is go backward and {a nungleh ding} are those who will turn back) (s:nungkik) (r:zd:22695) (q:draft, low confidence)
nungngatsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:turn one's back on/forsake/abandon) (d:<nungngat> with the ending {-san}, away from: turn the back on someone and leave them) (b:nungngat) (r:zd:9251/zd:21803) (q:draft)
nungnung = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:time) (w:last/latest) (d:another spelling of <nunung>, last, not the blowing of the wind; {a nungnung pen in} after a date is at the latest) (s:nunung) (r:zd:14921) (q:draft, low confidence)
nungpan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:from behind/from the back) (d:<nung> and <pan> written as one word: from behind something, often followed by <in>) (j:nung/pan) (r:zd:21876/zd:12974) (q:draft)
nungsang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:time) (w:afterwards/later time/what comes after) (d:with <a> or <tua> before it and often <ciangin> or <lam> after it: the time after something, so that {a nungsang ciangin} is afterwards, later on; not placed at the end of a clause like the conjunction) (r:zd:22807/zd:24176/zd:21044) (q:draft)
nungsangah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:afterwards/later/in the end) (d:<nungsang> with <ah>, written as one word: {a nungsangah} is afterwards, later on, and after a person, after that person is gone) (j:nungsang/ah) (r:zd:20646/zd:23882) (q:draft)
nungsungteng = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time/media) (w:recently/lately/in recent days) (d:<nung>, behind, past, with <sungteng>, throughout: during the time just past, in recent days or weeks) (r:zd:17628/zd:14566/zd:11652) (q:draft)
nungta = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:alive/live/be alive) (d:live, be alive; {a nungta lai} is still living) (a:si/sih) (r:27.6.21)
nungta pasian = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:the living God) (d:<nungta>, alive, and <Pasian>, God: the living God, a fixed term of Christian speech, nearly always with <a> before it as {a nungta Pasian}, the God who lives, set against idols and the gods of the forefathers) (r:zd:23394/zd:20786) (q:draft)
nungtaakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:nuntakna) (r:zd:25414/zd:25394) (q:draft)
nungtak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:nuntak) (r:zd:16254/zd:19783) (q:draft)
nungtakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:nuntakna) (r:zd:23367/zd:24336) (q:draft)
nungtalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not live/not be alive) (d:<nungta> and <lo> written as one word: not live in a certain way, or not be alive) (j:nungta/lo) (r:zd:14965/zd:23394) (q:draft)
nungtathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:can live/be able to live/survive) (d:<nungta>, live, and <thei>, able, written as one word) (j:nungta/thei) (r:zd:12571/zd:15505) (q:draft)
nungtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:learn afterwards/find out later) (d:<nung>, after, and <theih>, know, written as one word: come to know a thing only after it has happened; with <ki> before it, it became known afterwards) (j:nung/theih) (r:zd:17060/zd:25322) (q:draft, low confidence)
nungthu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:background/back story) (d:<nung>, behind, with <thu>, matter: the story behind something, as the circumstances in which a song was written; also what follows from an act, its consequences) (j:nung/thu) (r:zd:9258/zd:9221) (q:draft)
nungthuap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:back up/support/reinforce) (d:<nung>, behind, with <thuap>, add a layer: stand behind someone as support or reserve, or be what gives backing to a work) (r:zd:20999/zd:20649) (q:draft)
nungthup = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:defender/back) (d:in football, a player of the back line who defends; named in a list of awards between <kungpang>, goalkeeper, and <maikah>, striker; from <nung>, back) (r:zd:15622) (q:draft, low confidence)
nungtolh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:go backward/fall back/regress/backslide) (d:move back instead of forward: draw back from an undertaking, decline instead of progressing, fall away in faith) (s:nungkik) (r:zd:25056/zd:25273/zd:19662) (q:draft)
nungun = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time) (w:after) (d:<nung>, after, and the plural marker <un>, written as one word after a verb whose subject is more than one: after they had done it) (j:nung/un) (r:ts:3369/zd:11153) (q:draft)
nungzui = (i:2) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:conductor/bus conductor) (d:the helper on a bus or other vehicle who collects the fares and assists the driver, after <mawtaw> as {mawtaw nungzui}) (s:conductor) (r:zd:14797) (q:draft, low confidence)
nungzuihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:discipleship/following) (d:<nungzuih>, follow after, with the noun ending {-na}: the following of someone, especially of Christ) (b:nungzuih) (r:zd:23936/zd:17329/zd:23928) (q:draft)
nungzuipi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:apostle/chief disciple) (d:<nungzui>, disciple, with <pi>, chief: one of the twelve disciples of Jesus) (s:sawltak) (b:nungzui) (r:zd:21939/zd:16765) (q:draft)
nungzuipite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:apostles/disciples) (d:<nungzui>, disciple, with {-pi}, chief, and the plural <te>: the apostles, the first disciples of Jesus) (b:nungzui) (r:zd:25751/zd:21530) (q:draft)
nunna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:life/living/way of life) (d:<nun>, live, with the noun suffix <na>: a person's life or way of living, the same as <nuntakna>; it follows a person or a possessive, as in {mihing nunna}, human life, and not <huih>, wind) (s:nuntakna) (r:zd:15324/zd:17535/zd:22557) (q:draft)
nunneem = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/everyday) (j:nunnem) (r:zd:19166/zd:25397) (q:draft)
nunnem = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/everyday) (w:gentle/mild/meek) (d:of a person, soft and gentle in manner, not harsh) (r:zd:23887/zd:21013) (q:draft)
nuno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:aunt/mother's sister) (d:<nu>, mother, with <no>, young: the younger sister of one's mother) (b:nu) (q:draft)
nunote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:aunts/mother's sisters) (d:<nuno>, the younger sister of one's mother, with the plural <te>; also said of the women of the neighbourhood of that standing) (b:nuno) (r:zd:23865) (q:draft, low confidence)
nunta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:nungta) (r:zd:11994/zd:17271/zd:15528) (q:draft)
nuntaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:nuntak) (r:zd:25414/zd:23770) (q:draft)
nuntaakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (j:nuntakna) (r:zd:23148/zd:25414/zd:16428) (q:draft)
nuntaakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (j:nuntakpih) (r:zd:16428) (q:draft)
nuntaaksung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/time) (w:during life/in one's lifetime) (d:<nuntaak> and <sung> written as one word: while a person lives, in the course of life) (j:nuntaak/sung) (r:zd:25893) (q:draft)
nuntaakzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (j:nuntakzia) (r:zd:21498/zd:23770) (q:draft)
nuntak khuasak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:live one's life/lead a life/make a living) (d:<nuntak>, live, and {khuasak}, the second form of <khuasa>, lead one's daily life: the two verbs together mean live and get along from day to day; {nuntak khuasak zia} is a way of life, and the noun is <nuntak khuasakna>; not the village name Khuasak) (r:zd:22944/zd:25749) (q:draft)
nuntak khuasakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:living/livelihood/living conditions/standard of living) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <khuasakna>, way of life, a pair of two words of like meaning: the daily life and living of people, how well they live; followed by a describing word such as <niam>, low, or <haksa>, hard) (r:zd:21717/zd:22262) (q:draft)
nuntak khuasakzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:way of life/living conditions/standard of living) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <khuasakzia>, way of life: a pair of near synonyms used as one noun for how people live and what their living conditions are; the people concerned stand before it) (s:khuasakzia) (r:zd:15720/zd:15234/zd:19462) (q:draft)
nuntak nading = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:livelihood/means of living/for living) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <nading>, for the purpose of: what one needs in order to live, a living or livelihood, as the object of verbs of seeking and gathering; also plainly in order to live) (r:zd:20800/zd:17313) (q:draft)
nuntak sungin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:in one's lifetime/during one's life/as long as one lives) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <sungin>, within: during the whole time that someone is alive; a subject marker such as <a> or <na> stands before it) (r:zd:21978/zd:25222) (q:draft)
nuntak tawntungna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:eternal life/everlasting life) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <tawntungna>, everlastingness: living for ever, the eternal life of Christian teaching; used as a noun, as object of verbs such as <ngah>, receive, and <pia>, give) (r:zd:23806/zd:23394/zd:20848) (q:draft)
nuntakkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:live together) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <khop>, together, written as one word: live together with someone, who is named with <tawh>) (j:nuntak/khop) (r:zd:17437) (q:draft)
nuntakna bei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media/health) (w:lose one's life/die) (d:<nuntakna>, life, and <bei>, come to an end: the life ends, a respectful way to say that a person died; mostly as {nuntakna bei lawh}, lose one's life as a result of something) (r:ts:7296/zd:17990) (q:draft)
nuntakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (w:live by/live out/practise) (d:<nuntak>, live, with <pih>, together with: live with something as part of one's life, live according to a teaching or a value) (b:nuntak) (r:zd:15894/zd:21097/zd:21607) (q:draft)
nuntakpihding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (w:to live by/to live with) (d:<nuntakpih>, live by, and <ding>, to, written as one word: what one is to live by or live with) (j:nuntakpih/ding) (r:zd:17087) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuntakpihte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/everyday) (w:those who live by/those who live out) (d:<nuntakpih>, live by, with the plural <te>: the people who live according to a belief or a truth they know) (b:nuntakpih) (r:zd:24396/zd:24055) (q:draft)
nuntakzonna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/social) (w:livelihood/making a living/economic life) (d:<nuntak>, live, and <zonna>, seeking, written as one word: the work of finding a living, the economic side of life) (s:nekzonna) (j:nuntak/zonna) (r:zd:11758) (q:draft)
nunun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:put last/do later/leave till later) (d:do or place something after other things, the opposite of <masak>, do first; verb form of <nunung>, last) (b:nunung) (r:zd:25467/zd:19222/zd:23725) (q:draft)
nunzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:way of life/lifestyle/conduct) (d:short form of <nuntakzia>: the way a person or a people live) (s:nuntakzia/nuntakdan) (r:zd:20972/zd:11571/zd:12121) (q:draft)
nunziate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:ways of life/conduct) (d:plural of <nunzia>, way of life) (b:nunzia) (r:zd:21948) (q:draft)
nupa kaal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:between husband and wife/married life/marital relationship) (d:<nupa>, husband and wife, and <kaal.2>, the space between: what is between a husband and wife, their life together as a couple; it stands before a noun such as <kizopna>, relationship, or before <sung> and <sungah>, within) (r:zd:21673/zd:19287/zd:24087) (q:draft)
nupakal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:marital relations/between husband and wife) (d:<nupa>, husband and wife, with <kal>, the space between: what is between a married couple; {nupakal buaina} is a marital quarrel) (b:nupa) (r:zd:20492/zd:16047) (q:draft)
nupakop = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:couple/married couple) (d:<nupa>, husband and wife, and <kop>, pair, written as one word: a man and a woman as a pair, usually a married couple) (j:nupa/kop) (r:zd:12091/zd:12567/zd:22312) (q:draft)
nupen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the woman/she) (d:<nu>, the woman, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word: the woman just spoken of, as the topic of the sentence) (j:nu/pen) (r:zd:12555/zd:12701) (q:draft)
nuphal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:in-law) (d:a group of relatives by marriage named beside <sungh>, the wife's family, and also a role in the household kinship order; which relatives exactly is not clear from the sentences) (r:zd:24119) (q:draft, low confidence)
nupi naupaai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/family) (w:pregnant woman/expectant mother) (d:<nupi>, woman, and <naupaai>, be pregnant: a pregnant woman; the verb follows the noun without a relative marker and the pair is used as one noun, with <te> for the plural or <khat> for one) (r:zd:11337/zd:16853) (q:draft)
nupikhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/family) (w:a woman/a married woman) (d:<nupi>, woman, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a certain woman) (j:nupi/khat) (r:zd:19871/zd:15048/zd:19676) (q:draft)
nupinu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:woman/married woman/lady) (d:<nupi>, woman, with <nu>, the female one: a grown or married woman, in news reports the woman who is spoken of; the male word is <papipa>) (r:zd:16600/zd:13024/zd:15943) (q:draft)
nupisa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:married woman/wife) (d:<nupi>, married woman, with <sa>, already: a woman who is already married, as against a girl) (b:nupi) (r:zd:13072/zd:15485) (q:draft)
Nurse = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/work) (w:nurse) (d:a nurse; {Nurse nu} is a female nurse and {Nurse pa} a male nurse) (o:English) (r:zd:12466/zd:15724) (q:draft)
nusiakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:have already left/have passed away) (d:<nusia>, leave, and <khin>, already, written as one word: has already left a place; {hong nusiakhin} is has left us, has died) (j:nusia/khin) (r:zd:12290/zd:12674) (q:draft)
nusialo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:not leave/not forsake/not abandon) (d:<nusia>, leave, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not leave or give up a person, a faith or a place) (j:nusia/lo) (r:zd:24673/zd:19619) (q:draft)
nusiasa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/family) (w:late/deceased/departed) (d:<nusia>, leave, and the ending {-sa}, already done, written as one word; {hong nusiasa} before a name is the late, the one who has left us) (j:nusia/sa) (r:zd:23301/ts:11162/zd:9217) (q:draft)
nusiata = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:have left/pass away) (d:<nusia>, leave, and <ta>, now or already, written as one word: has now left; of a person, {hong nusiata} is has left us, has died) (j:nusia/ta) (r:zd:22540/zd:19098) (q:draft)
nusiatma = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/time) (w:before leaving/before departing from) (d:<nusiat>, leave, and <ma>, before, written as one word: before someone leaves a person, a place or an office; of a parent, before dying) (j:nusiat/ma) (r:zd:10970/zd:19098) (q:draft)
nusiatna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:passing/death/departure) (d:the death of a person, spoken of gently as leaving those who remain; nearly always <hong nusiatna> or <ong nusiatna>, his or her leaving us, in messages of condolence) (r:zd:23709/zd:25258/zd:22590) (q:draft)
nusiatna hangin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:on the passing of/because of the death of) (d:<nusiatna>, leaving behind, and <hangin>, here because of: with <hong> before it, {hong nusiatna hangin}, because he or she has left us, the usual wording of a condolence notice for a death; the person stands before it) (r:zd:21550/zd:22685) (q:draft)
nusiatsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:abandoned/left behind/forsaken) (d:<nusiat>, leave, with the ending {-sa}, already done: that has been left or given up, said of a place, a house or a body one belonged to, with the one who left named before it) (b:nusiat) (r:zd:24899/zd:17264) (q:draft)
nusiatsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:leave behind/leave/abandon) (d:<nusiat>, leave, with <san>, away from: go away from a place, a job or this world and leave it behind) (s:nusia) (j:nusiat/san) (r:zd:11157/zd:11279) (q:draft)
nusiaziau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:leave at once/just abandon/walk away from) (d:<nusia> and <ziau> written as one word: leave a person or a thing behind quickly and lightly, without more ado) (j:nusia/ziau) (r:zd:14931/zd:14523) (q:draft)
nutakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (j:nuntakna) (r:zd:26974/zd:20304) (q:draft)
nutawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/social) (w:with the woman/with her) (d:the feminine ending {-nu} of the noun before, a woman or girl, with <tawh>, with, written as one word: with that woman or girl) (j:nu/tawh) (r:zd:13336/zd:11492) (q:draft)
nute pate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:parents/mothers and fathers) (d:<nute>, mothers, and <pate>, fathers, set side by side without <leh>: parents as a group, used as subject or possessor when speaking of parents in general) (r:zd:22140/zd:23803) (q:draft)
nuteek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:old woman/aged mother) (d:<nu>, mother or woman, with <teek>, old: an aged woman; paired with {pateek}, old man, for old people) (r:zd:11159) (q:draft)
nuteh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:sentence-final word after a verb, said to several people: you will, you surely; {kisik kei nuteh} is you will not regret it) (r:zd:12289/zd:20956) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuten = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:the mothers) (d:<nu>, mother, and <ten>, the plural with the marker of the doer, written as one word: the mothers, as the ones who act; after a name, the mother of that person and those with her) (j:nu/ten) (r:zd:21013/zd:22683) (q:draft)
nuthawi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:divorced woman/woman married before) (d:a woman who has had a husband before, apparently a divorced woman; the male counterpart is {pathawi}; in a list of rules for priests after Leviticus 21 the priest must not marry one) (r:zd:23297/zd:23382) (q:draft, low confidence)
nutsiat = (i:2) (t:v) (f:family/social) (w:pass away/die) (d:after <hong>: a gentle way to say that someone has died and so left the family, as <nusia.2>; usual in notices of death and condolence) (r:zd:25178) (q:draft)
nutsiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:leaving/departure/passing) (d:<nutsiat>, leave behind, with the noun suffix {-na}: the leaving of someone or something; {hong nutsiatna hangin} is because he has left us, said of a death) (s:nusiatna) (b:nutsiat) (r:zd:18955/zd:12013) (q:draft)
nuu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (j:nu) (r:zd:24079) (q:draft, low confidence)
NUUPAA = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (j:nupa) (r:zd:19396) (q:draft)
Nyipitaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (j:Naypyitaw) (r:zd:23077) (q:draft)
Nyipyidaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (j:Naypyidaw) (r:ts:6954/zd:24595) (q:draft)
Nyipyitaw = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (j:Naypyitaw) (r:zd:20959/zd:11418) (q:draft)
nylon = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:asphalt/tarmac) (d:in road building, the tar or asphalt surface of a road, as in {nylon kattaya} and {nylon kultal}; the English word, used as in Burmese, also names the fibre nylon) (s:kattaya) (o:English) (r:zd:24271/zd:19345) (q:draft)
nzong = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:also/too) (d:the doer marker <n> and <zong>, also, written as one word after an apostrophe, as in {te'nzong} for {te in zong}: they also, even they) (j:n/zong) (r:zd:12727/zd:13100/zd:20225) (q:draft)
O = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:please/do) (d:written {o} at the end of a request or command, often after <dih> or <kei>: a friendly, coaxing tone, as in {na dawng mai o}, do just answer; not the {O} of address before a name) (r:zd:25357/zd:24116/zd:17181) (q:draft)
Oaxaca = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Oaxaca) (d:state in the south of Mexico) (r:zd:15089) (q:draft)
objection = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:objection) (d:a formal statement against a decision or result; {objection bawl} is raise an objection) (o:English) (r:zd:24800) (q:draft, low confidence)
Odisha = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Odisha) (d:state on the east coast of India) (r:zd:19536/zd:15958) (q:draft)
off = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:day off/time off) (d:time free from work; job notices tell with it how many days off there are, and {off ni} is a day off) (o:English) (r:zd:11011/zd:17327/zd:10794) (q:draft)
Offday = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:day off/rest day) (d:the day of the week on which a worker does not work; a heading in job advertisements in Malaysia) (o:English) (r:zd:16799/zd:17978) (q:draft, low confidence)
Office = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:office) (d:an office: the place where the work of a company, an organisation or a government body is done, and that body itself) (s:zum) (o:English) (r:zd:17327/zd:12437/ts:7051) (q:draft)
Officer = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:officer/official) (d:a person holding rank or office in the police, the army or a government department; {Police Officer} is a police officer) (o:English) (r:zd:19745/zd:14814/zd:15952) (q:draft)
Officers = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:officer/official) (d:officers of the police or of a government office; the English plural form is used as the word, often after Police and followed by the plural <te>) (o:English) (r:zd:20252/zd:15012) (q:draft)
official = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:official/officer) (d:a person who holds a post in a government or other public body) (o:English) (r:zd:20252/zd:15803) (q:draft)
official = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:politics) (w:official/officially) (d:said or done with the authority of a government or other body; {official in} is officially) (o:English) (r:zd:24414/zd:15237/ts:2513) (q:draft)
officially = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/social) (w:officially/formally) (d:the English adverb used in Zolai sentences, mostly as {officially in}: in an official way, with public authority) (o:English) (r:zd:17675/zd:13268/zd:24058) (q:draft)
Officials = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:officials/official) (d:the English plural, used for the people who hold office in a government or a body, mostly after its English name and followed by <te>) (o:English) (r:zd:15101/zd:11725) (q:draft)
offline = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:it) (w:offline) (d:not connected to the internet, set against <online>; with <in> or <ah> it is used as an adverb) (o:English) (r:zd:23680/zd:20565) (q:draft)
Ohio = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Ohio) (d:state of the United States of America) (o:English) (r:zd:9227/zd:15101) (q:draft)
Ohkathah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:chairman/speaker) (d:the chairman of a council or administrative body, and the speaker of a parliament; {Hluttaw Ohkathah} is the Speaker of Parliament and {Ohkathah pa} the chairman as a man) (o:Burmese, okkahta) (r:zd:19166/zd:24236) (q:draft)
ohsuh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:village tract) (d:an administrative unit below the township, made up of a group of villages) (o:Burmese, oksu) (r:zd:24736/zd:24124) (q:draft)
Oi = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:everyday) (w:oh/hey) (d:a cry of delight or surprise, or a call to get attention) (r:ts:4885) (q:draft, low confidence)
Okkathah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:chairman) (d:Burmese title of the chairman of a council or committee, in the articles the chairman of a government council of a township or of the country; followed by <pa> for the man who holds the office) (s:Chairman) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:20176) (q:draft)
Oklahoma = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Oklahoma) (d:a state of the United States; many Zomi live in its city of Tulsa) (r:zd:22004/zd:24453) (q:draft)
ollo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not easy/difficult) (d:<ol> and <lo> written as one word: not easy) (j:ol/lo) (r:ts:3160/zd:21369) (q:draft)
olmawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:take seriously/regard as important/heed) (d:treat a matter as something that counts; {olmawh lo} is neglect, take lightly) (r:zd:24279/zd:16799) (q:draft)
olmawhlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:unconcerned/heedless/indifferent) (d:paying no attention to something, not caring about it; {olmawhlo in} is without taking any notice) (r:zd:19536/zd:19939) (q:draft)
olnotak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:easily/with ease) (d:<olno>, easy, and <tak> written as one word, followed by <in> or <a>: easily, without difficulty) (j:olno/tak) (r:zd:19166/zd:12093) (q:draft)
olsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find easy/feel easy) (d:<ol>, easy, and <sa>, feel, written as one word: find something easy to do) (j:ol/sa) (r:zd:21918/zd:21032) (q:draft)
Olympic = (i:1) (t:name) (f:social/media) (w:Olympics/Olympic Games) (d:the Olympic Games, the international sports competition) (o:English) (r:zd:23780/zd:19578) (q:draft)
om = (i:5) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:abide) (d:stay or live in a person or a place, remain there)
om hithiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:be still/stay quiet/keep calm/rest) (d:<om>, stay, and <hithiat>, at ease: stay still and quiet, doing nothing and not stirring; often a piece of advice, with <in> or <ding> after it, and with <daitak>, quietly, before it) (r:zd:22563/zd:20329/zd:25932) (q:draft)
oma = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is and/exist) (d:<om>, be or there is, and the linking <a> written as one word: there is, and; it ends a clause and joins it to the next) (j:om/a) (r:zd:14751/zd:9251/zd:17911) (q:draft)
omaa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is and/be and) (d:<om>, be, and the linking <aa>, and, written as one word: there is or there are, and) (j:om/aa) (r:zd:20829/zd:24242) (q:draft)
Oman = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:politics) (w:Oman) (d:a country on the Arabian Peninsula) (r:zd:14785) (q:draft, low confidence)
ombang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/everyday) (w:according to/as it stands) (d:<om> and <bang> written as one word: as there is, in keeping with what exists; {thukhun ombang in} is according to the law in force) (j:om/bang) (r:zd:25111/zd:14797) (q:draft)
ombangin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/politics) (w:according to/in accordance with) (d:<om> and <bangin> written as one word: as there is, in keeping with what exists; {thukhun ombangin} is according to the law in force) (j:om/bangin) (r:zd:22813/zd:19805) (q:draft)
ombeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there are more/be in addition/be added) (d:<om>, be, with <beh>, here in addition, written as one word: there is more of something besides what there was; {ombeh lai} is there are still more) (j:om/beh) (r:zd:25488/zd:24595) (q:draft)
omciang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:when there is/when one is) (d:<om>, be, and <ciang>, when, written as one word: when there is, when one is in a place; {ih omciang} is when we are) (j:om/ciang) (r:zd:21745/zd:12596/zd:19676) (q:draft)
omcih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media/everyday) (w:that there is) (d:<om>, be, and <cih>, that, written as one word: that there is or that it is so, before a verb of saying) (j:om/cih) (r:zd:19912) (q:draft)
omcipden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:stay continually/remain constantly) (d:<omcip>, stay in place, and <den>, always, written as one word: stay there or remain so all the time) (j:omcip/den) (r:zd:20518/zd:11623) (q:draft)
omcipna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:staying put/staying in/remaining) (d:<omcip>, stay without moving, with the noun suffix: a staying in one place, as staying indoors, or the place where one always stays) (b:omcip) (r:zd:24452/zd:17097) (q:draft)
omcipsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:keep inside/confine/make stay put) (d:<omcip>, stay still, with the causative <sak>: make people stay where they are and not leave, as in a lockdown) (j:omcip/sak) (r:zd:15833/zd:11970) (q:draft)
omcitciat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there really is/be right there) (d:<om>, be, with the emphatic <citciat> written as one word: it is plainly there, there is indeed) (j:om/citciat) (r:zd:11943/zd:15647) (q:draft, low confidence)
omdaan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/health) (j:omdan) (r:zd:20926/zd:21308) (q:draft)
omdan khawldan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:conduct/manners/way of life) (d:<omdan>, way of being, and <khawldan>, way of staying: a pair that names as one thing how a person lives and behaves among others) (r:zd:19990/zd:22138) (q:draft)
omdante = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:ways/conditions/behaviour) (d:plural of <omdan>: how things are, or how a person lives and behaves) (b:omdan) (r:zd:17152) (q:draft)
omding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:will be/will take place) (d:<om> and <ding> written as one word: there will be, will be held; also is to stay) (j:om/ding) (r:zd:12862/zd:12168/zd:24024) (q:draft)
omdinga = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be/there will be) (d:<omding> with the linking <a> written as one word: there will be, and; before a noun, that is to be) (j:om/ding/a) (r:zd:24604/zd:25431) (q:draft, low confidence)
omdinghi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there will be/there must be) (d:<om> and <dinghi> written as one word: there will be; after a number, there are thought to be about that many) (j:om/dinghi) (r:zd:17897/zd:22171) (q:draft)
omdingin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:to be/that there will be) (d:<om> and <dingin> written as one word: so as to be, or as likely to be; with <ki ummawh>, be suspected to be, and with <um>, believe that there will be) (j:om/dingin) (r:zd:20468/zd:13020) (q:draft)
omgige = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be always there/always exist) (d:<om> and <gige> written as one word: is there all the time, there always is) (j:om/gige) (r:zd:20287/zd:20430) (q:draft)
omhang = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:because there is/though being) (d:<om> and <hang> written as one word: on account of there being, or although one is; at the end of a sentence also there are, said of us) (j:om/hang) (r:zd:24955) (q:draft, low confidence)
omhetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none at all/not be at all) (d:<om>, be, and <hetlo>, not at all, written as one word: there is none at all, be not there at all) (j:om/hetlo) (r:zd:13186/zd:13203/zd:14751) (q:draft)
omhi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is/there are/exist) (d:<om>, be there, and the sentence-final <hi> written as one word: closes a statement that something or someone is there) (j:om/hi) (r:zd:20720/zd:22203/zd:17919) (q:draft)
omhiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is there/are there) (d:<om>, be, with the question particle <hiam>, written as one word: is there, what is there, how is it) (j:om/hiam) (r:zd:20860/zd:21085/zd:20574) (q:draft)
omhiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there probably is/there must be) (d:<om> and <hiding> written as one word: there must be or there probably is, said of what is supposed and not known for sure) (j:om/hiding) (r:zd:19445/zd:12285) (q:draft)
omhithiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:stay at ease/sit still/stay calm) (d:<om> and <hithiat> written as one word: stay quietly and undisturbed, without care or concern) (j:om/hithiat) (r:zd:14952/zd:19465) (q:draft)
omhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:ought to exist/fit to be) (d:<om>, be, and <huai>, worthy of, written as one word: that ought to be there, that deserves to exist or to stay) (j:om/huai) (r:zd:16365/zd:20041) (q:draft)
omkawikawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be here and there/occur in many places) (d:<om>, be, and <kawikawi>, here and there, written as one word: be found in many places, be all around) (j:om/kawikawi) (r:zd:14650/zd:16926/zd:20012) (q:draft)
omkei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is not/not be/not exist) (d:<om> and the negative <kei> written as one word: there is none, is not there; <omkei leh> is if there is none, without) (j:om/kei) (r:zd:25173/zd:20971/zd:19556) (q:draft)
omkei leh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:without/if there is no/were it not for) (d:<omkei>, there is not, and <leh>, here if: placed after a noun, if there is none of it, without it; the result follows) (r:zd:20971/zd:19556) (q:draft)
omkeileh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if there is no/if there were not/without) (d:<om> and <keileh> written as one word: if there is not, if someone or something does not exist) (j:om/keileh) (r:zd:20481/zd:11980/zd:15305) (q:draft)
omkhading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there may be/there will probably be) (d:<omkha>, happen to be, with <ding>, will, written as one word: there may well be, there are likely to be) (j:omkha/ding) (r:zd:14581/zd:13266/zd:15245) (q:draft)
omkhahiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:is there by any chance/are there perhaps) (d:<om>, be, with <khahiam>, by any chance, written as one word: a question whether someone or something happens to be there) (j:om/khahiam) (r:zd:15054/zd:16649) (q:draft)
omkhaleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if there happens to be/if there should be) (d:<omkha>, happen to be, and <leh>, here if, written as one word: if there should be any) (j:omkha/leh) (r:zd:10743/zd:12304) (q:draft)
omkhalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none/not be there) (d:<omkha> and <lo> written as one word: there happened to be none, no one was there, often of people killed or hurt) (j:omkha/lo) (r:zd:14545/zd:13140) (q:draft)
omkhathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there may be/may occur) (d:<om>, be, and <khathei>, perhaps, written as one word: there may well be, it could happen) (j:om/khathei) (r:zd:15205/zd:16782) (q:draft)
omkhawmthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/family) (w:can live together/be able to stay together) (d:<omkhawm> and <thei> written as one word: be able to be or live together) (j:omkhawm/thei) (r:zd:12571/zd:12645) (q:draft)
omkhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:already exist/be there already) (d:<om> and <khinta> written as one word: there is already, has already come to be in a place or state) (j:om/khinta) (r:zd:19648/zd:12845/zd:14531) (q:draft)
omkhinzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have already been/there have already been) (d:<om> and <khinzo> written as one word: has already come to be, there has already been) (j:om/khinzo) (r:zd:25470/zd:25712) (q:draft)
omkhollo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:hardly exist/be scarce) (d:<om> and <khollo> written as one word: there is hardly any, there are not many) (j:om/khollo) (r:zd:20142/zd:14704/zd:12281) (q:draft)
omkhop = (i:2) (t:v) (f:family/health) (w:have sexual intercourse/sleep together) (d:polite word for sexual intercourse, mostly of husband and wife, as in {nupa omkhop}; the plain sense is only being in one place together) (r:zd:22614/zd:24476) (q:draft)
omkhopding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family) (w:to sleep together/to live together) (d:<omkhop> and <ding> written as one word: to be together as husband and wife, to sleep together) (j:omkhop/ding) (r:zd:15689) (q:draft)
omkhopna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family/health) (w:sexual intercourse/sex/sexual union) (d:a polite word for sexual intercourse, after <nupa>, husband and wife, or <numei pasal>, woman and man; after <mipi> or <mihon>, crowd, it stays the plain being together of sense 1) (r:zd:22614/zd:21293) (q:draft)
omkhuan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:permission to stay/right to remain/leave to stay) (d:<om>, stay, and <khuan>, permission, written as one word: leave given by an authority to stay in a place or country; {omkhuan pia} is allow to stay) (j:om/khuan) (r:zd:19953/zd:15054/zd:19143) (q:draft)
omkiaukiau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there are some/occur now and then) (d:<om> and <kiaukiau> written as one word: there are some here and there, it happens now and then) (j:om/kiaukiau) (r:zd:13127/zd:18286) (q:draft)
omkikding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:will be again/will be held again) (d:<omkik>, be again, and <ding> written as one word: there will again be, it will take place again) (j:omkik/ding) (r:zd:19624/zd:19805) (q:draft)
omlaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will still be/there are probably still) (d:<omlai>, still be there, with <ding>, will, written as one word: there will still be, there are thought to be more) (j:omlai/ding) (r:zd:15828/zd:19543) (q:draft)
omlaimawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still be there/still remain) (d:<omlai>, still be there, with <mawk>, a word of surprise or emphasis, written as one word: there still are, more than one would expect) (j:omlai/mawk) (r:zd:20401/zd:10821) (q:draft)
omlaitak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:be staying/while being) (d:<om> and <laitak> written as one word: while being or staying, be in a place or busy with something at that moment) (j:om/laitak) (r:zd:17256/zd:11759) (q:draft)
omlak = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:among those that exist/among the ones there are) (d:<om> and <lak> written as one word, after <a> and before <pan> or <ah>: from among the things that there are) (j:om/lak) (r:zd:20035/zd:21370) (q:draft)
omle = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if there is/if there are) (d:<om> with <le>, here the short form of <leh>, if, written as one word: if there is, if there are; {i omle} is if we are, if any of us) (j:om/le) (r:zd:20795/zd:25248/zd:15726) (q:draft)
omleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if there is) (d:<om>, be, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if there is, if someone is in a place) (j:om/leh) (r:zd:22773/zd:20004/zd:11759) (q:draft)
omlel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just be there/simply exist) (d:<om> and <lel>, merely, written as one word: there simply is, just be or stay there) (j:om/lel) (r:zd:10821/zd:25573) (q:draft)
omleng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one stays/if there were) (d:<om>, be or stay, and <leng>, if, written as one word: if I or we stay, if we had) (j:om/leng) (r:zd:23935/zd:12715) (q:draft)
omleuleu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:there is again/there is also) (d:<om> and <leuleu> written as one word: there is once more, or there is on the other hand; closes a report of another event of the same kind) (j:om/leuleu) (r:zd:17252/zd:15629/zd:15274) (q:draft)
omlian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be exactly/be definite) (d:<om>, be, with <lian>, here exactly, written as one word: be exactly there, exist for certain; {omlian nailo} is there is not yet a definite one) (j:om/lian) (r:ts:2549/zd:12917/zd:15539) (q:draft)
omlianlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is no definite/not exactly exist) (d:<omlian>, be definite, and <lo>, not, written as one word: there is nothing definite or exact) (j:omlian/lo) (r:zd:12280) (q:draft)
omlo = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:there is no/not exist/be absent) (d:<om>, be, with <lo>, not, written as one word and used as the verb of the sentence, mostly before <hi>: there is none, it does not exist; with <kuamah> it is there is nobody) (r:zd:17132/ts:11162/ts:9829) (q:draft)
omloding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there will not be/will not be) (d:<om>, be, <lo>, not, and <ding>, will, written as one word: there will be none, will not be; as an instruction, must not stay) (j:om/lo/ding) (r:zd:21032/zd:11371/zd:11956) (q:draft)
omloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not be/be absent/be without) (d:<om> and <loh> written as one word: form of <omlo> used before <ding>, <nading>, <laitak> and <man>; {a omloh nadingin} is so that there may not be, and {a omloh laitak} is while there is none) (j:om/loh) (r:zd:22654/zd:24276/zd:14734) (q:draft)
omlohiam = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:is there not/is there none) (d:<omlo>, there is not, with the question particle <hiam>, written as one word: is there not, is there none; {omhiam, omlohiam} is whether there is or not) (j:omlo/hiam) (r:zd:14941/zd:18069) (q:draft)
omloin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:without/there being no) (d:<om>, be there, and <loin>, without, written as one word: without there being any, with none) (j:om/loin) (r:zd:23130/zd:23670) (q:draft)
omlomawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none/turn out not to be there) (d:<omlo>, not being there, with <mawk>, here marking what is unexpected or simply so, written as one word: there is simply none, or someone is found not to be there) (j:omlo/mawk) (r:zd:12645/zd:19357) (q:draft)
omlopah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none/not exist) (d:<omlo>, there is not, and <pah> written as one word: there is none either, said as the plain result of what was stated before) (j:omlo/pah) (r:zd:13316/zd:12042) (q:draft, low confidence)
omlote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who are not there/those not in) (d:<om>, be, and <lote>, those who are not, written as one word: the people or things that are not in a place, a list or a state) (j:om/lote) (r:zd:24420/zd:16813) (q:draft)
omlozaw = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be less/rather not be) (d:<omlo>, there is not, and the comparative <zaw> written as one word: there is less of it, or someone is mostly not there; {khialh omlozaw} is there is less mistake) (j:omlo/zaw) (r:zd:11378/zd:11314) (q:draft)
omlua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there are very many/abound) (d:<om> and <lua> written as one word: there is very much or very many of something; with a negative, there is not so very much) (j:om/lua) (r:zd:20297/zd:14941/zd:26017) (q:draft)
omma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:before there was/before the existence of) (d:<om>, be, and <ma>, before, written as one word: before something existed or took place) (j:om/ma) (r:zd:17565/zd:16765) (q:draft)
ommai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just be/simply stay) (d:<om>, be or stay, and the particle <mai>, just, written as one word: there simply are, just stay around) (j:om/mai) (r:zd:17022/zd:13320) (q:draft, low confidence)
omman = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be there for a time/happen to occur) (d:<om> and <man> written as one word: there has been, something was there or came about for a time) (j:om/man) (r:zd:14728/zd:19927) (q:draft, low confidence)
omman = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:boarding fee/charge for staying) (d:<om>, stay, with <man>, price: the fee paid for staying, as by a boarder at a school) (j:om/man) (r:zd:16799) (q:draft, low confidence)
ommawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family/social) (w:naughty/restless/unruly) (d:not staying still or behaving properly, said mostly of a child; {khut ommawh} is said of a man who cannot keep his hands to himself) (r:zd:19465/zd:9451/zd:21168) (q:draft)
ommawk = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there are/exist/happen to be) (d:<om>, be or exist, with <mawk>, which marks a fact as unexpected or regrettable: there are, there turn out to be, closing a report after a number or after <pawlkhat> or <tampi>; not the sense be idle) (r:zd:14652/zd:15639/zd:14879) (q:draft)
ommello = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there seems to be none/hardly exist) (d:<om>, be, <mel>, appearance, and <lo>, not, written as one word: there is no sign of it, there seems to be none) (j:om/mel/lo) (r:zd:12159/zd:12099/zd:17094) (q:draft)
ommuan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:idly/at ease/casually) (d:<om>, stay, with <muan>: just staying as one is, without effort or special purpose; {ommuan in} is idly, casually, from where one happens to be) (r:zd:23332/zd:22639) (q:draft, low confidence)
ommuanin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:idly/while just sitting/at leisure) (d:<ommuan> and <in> written as one word: while one is just sitting or staying with nothing else to do) (j:ommuan/in) (r:zd:21458) (q:draft, low confidence)
omna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:place to stay/dwelling/location) (d:used alone as a noun for a place to live or the place where a thing is, as in {omna neilo}, having no place to stay; the listed sense is the same word after a subject, the place where someone is) (r:zd:19320) (q:draft, low confidence)
omna ciat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:each one's place/wherever each is) (d:<omna>, the place where one is, and <ciat>, each: the place where each one is; mostly as {i omna ciat ah}, wherever each of us is, in blessings and exhortations to people who live scattered) (r:zd:24382/zd:12122/zd:25042) (q:draft)
omna inn = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:residence/dwelling/home) (d:<omna>, the place where one is, and <inn>, house: the house where a person lives or stays, a residence; a possessive such as <a> or <ka> stands before it) (r:zd:22451/zd:14650/zd:8667) (q:draft)
omna mun = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:location/whereabouts/place of residence) (d:<omna>, being or staying, and <mun>, place: the place where someone or something is or lives; stands after a possessor, as {i omna mun}, the place where we live, or after the thing located) (r:zd:12196/zd:23928/zd:11215) (q:draft)
omna pia = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:accommodation provided/lodging given) (d:<omna>, place to stay, and <pia>, give: a formula of job notices, the employer gives a place to stay; it stands beside {an vak} or {an pia}, food is provided, and {an pialo}, no food) (r:zd:12695/zd:12024) (q:draft)
omnading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/home) (w:place to stay/for staying/so that there may be) (d:<om> and <nading> written as one word: for living in, a place to stay; also so that something may exist) (j:om/nading) (r:zd:18104/zd:18012) (q:draft)
omnailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is not yet/not exist yet) (d:<om> and <nailo> written as one word: there is none so far, has not yet come about) (j:om/nailo) (r:zd:11553/zd:21032) (q:draft)
omnalam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:direction of/toward where someone is) (d:<omna>, the place where someone or something is, and <lam>, direction, written as one word: the side on which it is, usually followed by <ah>) (j:omna/lam) (r:zd:15454/zd:12579) (q:draft)
omnapi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:although there is/though being) (d:<om> and <napi> written as one word: although there is, or although someone is there, often followed by <in>) (j:om/napi) (r:zd:10793/zd:22586) (q:draft)
omnateng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:whole place/every place) (d:<omna>, the place where someone or something is, with <teng>, all, written as one word: the whole place, or all the places, where it is) (j:omna/teng) (r:zd:15103/zd:11801) (q:draft)
omnawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is no longer/be no more/no longer exist) (d:<om> and <nawnlo> written as one word: there is no longer, is not there any more; {bangmah omnawnlo} is there is nothing left) (j:om/nawnlo) (r:zd:13222/zd:22584/zd:11485) (q:draft)
omnawnloding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will no longer be/will be no more) (d:<om>, be, and <nawnloding> written as one word: there will no longer be, will not exist any more) (j:om/nawnloding) (r:zd:20084/zd:19721) (q:draft)
omngeikhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have already been/have happened before) (d:<omngei> and <khin> written as one word: there has already been such a thing before) (j:omngei/khin) (r:zd:20014/zd:17729) (q:draft)
omngeilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have never been/have never happened) (d:<omngei>, have once been, with <lo>, not, written as one word: there has never been, it has never happened before) (j:omngei/lo) (r:zd:15751/zd:15609) (q:draft)
omngeina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:former residence/place where one has been) (d:<omngei>, have been, with the noun suffix <na>: the place where someone once lived or stayed; also where or how something has always been) (b:omngei) (r:zd:16463/zd:24731) (q:draft, low confidence)
omngeingai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be in a stir/be astir) (d:<om>, be, with the expressive <ngeingai>, written as one word: many people are there in a stir or commotion) (j:om/ngeingai) (r:zd:20663/zd:15851) (q:draft, low confidence)
omnuam = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:tend to occur/be liable to happen/be common) (d:of a thing or event, not a person: it tends to be there or to happen, often before <phadiak> or <phadeuh>, as {tuahsiatna omnuam}, accidents are liable to happen) (r:zd:16584/zd:17999/zd:19088) (q:draft)
omomna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:wherever one is/each one's place) (d:<omom> with the noun suffix <na>, after a person marker: the place where each one is living; {i omomna ah} is wherever we are) (j:omom/na) (r:zd:15529/zd:25686/zd:23893) (q:draft)
ompak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be there/exist) (d:<om> in its meaning exist, with <pak>, used with a negative, {ompak kei}, {ompak nai}, {ompak nawn kei}: there is not even one, there is none yet or none any more; not staying somewhere) (r:zd:13243/zd:12933) (q:draft)
ompakpaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:rarely occur/hardly ever happen/be rare) (d:<om>, be, and <pakpaklo>, hardly ever, written as one word) (j:om/pakpaklo) (r:zd:14954/zd:14942) (q:draft)
ompan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is only/there is just) (d:<om>, be there, with <pan>, here only just, written as one word and used with <bek>, only: there is no more than that so far) (r:zd:24420) (q:draft, low confidence)
ompen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:the one that is/being) (d:<om>, be or stay, and <pen> written as one word: with the topic marker, being so or that which is; after a word of quality, the one that is most so, as in {a naii ompen}, the nearest one) (j:om/pen) (r:zd:20647/zd:22709) (q:draft, low confidence)
ompeuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<om> and <peuh> written as one word: with <leh>, whenever there is, if only there is; as a command, just stay as it is) (j:om/peuh) (r:zd:16442/zd:25687) (q:draft)
omphial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there even is/happen to be) (d:<om>, be, and <phial>, even, written as one word: there even is such a one, it goes so far that there is) (j:om/phial) (r:zd:11177/zd:22391) (q:draft, low confidence)
omphot = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:stay for now/be so far) (d:<om>, be or stay, and <phot>, for the time being, written as one word: stay there for now; also there is so far) (j:om/phot) (r:zd:11219/zd:12283) (q:draft)
omsak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:cause/bring about/give rise to/create) (d:make something exist or arise, not put it in a place: the object is a state or an event, as {buaina omsak}, cause trouble, and {kimuanna omsak lo}, create no trust) (r:zd:20116/zd:21908/zd:20466) (q:draft)
omsaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not allow/not let there be/not cause) (d:<omsak>, cause to be, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not let something be or happen, leave no room for it) (j:omsak/lo) (r:zd:22151/zd:23138/zd:18157) (q:draft)
omsam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there are indeed/there certainly are) (d:<om>, be, with the particle <sam>, indeed, to be sure: there certainly is or are, often granting a point before a contrast) (b:om) (r:zd:24955/zd:25923/zd:19464) (q:draft, low confidence)
omsamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:there is none/not be at all) (d:<om>, be, with <samlo>, not at all, written as one word: there is none after all, there was not any) (j:om/samlo) (r:zd:20966/zd:12982/zd:17104) (q:draft)
omsan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:stay unmoved/take no notice/let be) (d:<om>, stay, with <san>, here leaving something aside: stay as one is and do nothing about a matter; {a thei lo bangin omsan} is carry on as if one did not know) (b:om) (r:zd:25025/zd:19790) (q:draft, low confidence)
omsawnsawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there are also/keep being) (d:<om>, be, and <sawnsawn> written as one word: there is, with the sense that this too is the case or goes on being so) (j:om/sawnsawn) (r:zd:16083/zd:11617) (q:draft, low confidence)
omselo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is not much/without any) (d:<om> and <selo> written as one word: there is none to speak of, without there being any such thing) (j:om/selo) (r:zd:21817/zd:15671) (q:draft)
omseselo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none at all/not be at all) (d:<om>, be, and <seselo>, not at all, written as one word: there is no such thing at all, or it is not in that place at all) (j:om/seselo) (r:zd:21588/zd:13155) (q:draft)
omsuaksuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:stay on and on/overstay/keep staying) (d:<omsuak>, stay on, with <suak> said twice, written as one word: go on staying, as in a country after the visa has run out) (j:omsuak/suak) (r:zd:20012) (q:draft)
omsun = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:only/sole/the only existing) (d:the only one or the little that there is, like <neihsun> for what one has; {omsun teng} is all that there is) (r:zd:16665/zd:20537) (q:draft, low confidence)
omsunsun = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:what little there is/the few there are) (d:<om>, be, and <sunsun>, what little, written as one word: the little that exists, the few who are there) (j:om/sunsun) (r:zd:12174/zd:24168) (q:draft)
omtakpi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really exist/there really is) (d:<om>, be, and <takpi>, truly, written as one word: there really is, really take place) (j:om/takpi) (r:zd:11099/zd:23485/zd:20046) (q:draft)
omtaktak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:really exist/truly be) (d:<om> and <taktak> written as one word: there really is, it really happened) (j:om/taktak) (r:zd:17868/zd:11278) (q:draft)
omtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the same as being) (d:<om>, be, and <tawh>, with, written as one word after <a> and before <kibang>: {a omtawh kibang} is it is like being in the place or state named) (j:om/tawh) (r:zd:23488/zd:20801) (q:draft)
omteh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:when there is) (d:<om> and <teh> written as one word, after <a>: when or whenever there is; compare <takteh>) (j:om/teh) (r:zd:24234/zd:24339) (q:draft)
omtei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is indeed/exist to be sure) (d:<om>, be, with the emphatic <tei> written as one word, used before <hang> or <hangin>: although there indeed is) (j:om/tei) (r:zd:22922/zd:20979) (q:draft, low confidence)
omtek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:each be there/all exist) (d:<om> and <tek> written as one word: each of those named is there, each one has it) (j:om/tek) (r:zd:25923/zd:22581) (q:draft)
omtheiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:may be/may happen/will be able to be) (d:<omthei>, can be, and <ding>, will, written as one word: there may be, it may happen, one will be able to be so) (j:omthei/ding) (r:zd:20345/zd:15811) (q:draft)
omtheihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/travel) (w:right to stay/permission to stay/residence) (d:<omtheih>, be able to be, with {-na}: being allowed to stay in a country, as in {omtheihna permit}; also a place where something can be) (b:omtheih) (r:zd:20850/zd:15037) (q:draft)
omtheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot be/cannot be present/cannot exist) (d:<om>, be, with <theilo>, unable, written as one word: cannot be there, cannot take place, there cannot be) (j:om/theilo) (r:zd:22818/zd:17450/zd:24604) (q:draft)
omtheimawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can even be/may well be/happen to be) (d:<omthei> and <mawk> written as one word: there can indeed be, said with surprise or disapproval of something that does occur) (j:omthei/mawk) (r:zd:12257/zd:18033) (q:draft)
omtheinawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can no longer be/be no longer possible) (d:<omthei>, can be, and <nawnlo>, no longer, written as one word: there can no longer be, it can no longer exist) (j:omthei/nawnlo) (r:zd:12888/zd:19964) (q:draft)
omtheizel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen now and then/tend to occur/there are often) (d:<omthei>, can be, and <zel>, repeatedly, written as one word: it happens from time to time, there tend to be) (j:omthei/zel) (r:zd:17062/zd:15221) (q:draft)
omthu = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what is there) (d:<om>, be, and <thu>, matter, written as one word after <a>: {sunglam a omthu} is what is inside a person, the state of the inner life) (j:om/thu) (r:zd:20932) (q:draft, low confidence)
omtuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:seem to be/there probably is) (d:<om>, be there, with <tuak>, here showing what the writer supposes, written as one word: there seems to be, there surely is) (j:om/tuak) (r:zd:11924/zd:15968) (q:draft)
omtuak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:both be/each be) (d:<om>, be or live, with <tuak>, each or both, written as one word: both are, each of them is) (j:om/tuak) (r:zd:21369) (q:draft, low confidence)
omtuaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:seem not to be/there is apparently no) (d:<omtuak>, there seems to be, and <lo>, not, written as one word: as far as can be seen there is none, there is no sign of it) (j:omtuak/lo) (r:zd:15417/zd:15065) (q:draft)
omtuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is/exist) (d:<om>, be there, and <tuan> written as one word, nearly always before a negative or in a question: there is not really any, there is no such thing after all) (j:om/tuan) (r:zd:11761/zd:13149/zd:15184) (q:draft)
omtuanlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none/not be at all) (d:<om> be, <tuan> and the negative <lo> written as one word: there is none after all, nothing of the kind exists) (j:om/tuan/lo) (r:zd:12349/zd:14611/zd:15023) (q:draft)
omuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be/stay/remain) (d:<om>, be, and the plural marker <uh> written as one word: they are, they stay or remain so) (j:om/uh) (r:zd:17060/zd:21279) (q:draft)
omvet = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be at all/exist at all) (d:<om>, be, and the emphatic <vet> written as one word before a negative: there is none at all, not be there at all) (j:om/vet) (r:zd:22953/zd:21458) (q:draft)
omvetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:there is none at all/not exist at all) (d:<om>, be, with the emphatic <vet> and <lo>, not, written as one word: there is nothing at all, not a single one) (j:om/vet/lo) (r:zd:11617/zd:11587) (q:draft)
omveve = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still exist/there is nevertheless) (d:<om>, be there, with <veve>, all the same: there still is, there is such a thing in spite of what was said) (j:om/veve) (r:zd:17655/zd:11251/zd:14686) (q:draft)
omzeel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:omzel) (r:zd:25394/zd:21853) (q:draft)
omzel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep happening/be there often) (d:<om>, be or happen, and <zel>, repeatedly, written as one word: there is again and again, be somewhere often) (j:om/zel) (r:zd:12723/zd:11283) (q:draft)
omzelzel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:keep happening/occur again and again/often be) (d:<om>, be, with <zelzel>, repeatedly, written as one word: there is again and again, it keeps occurring) (j:om/zelzel) (r:zd:13094) (q:draft)
omzihziah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be there in great numbers/be all over) (d:<om>, be, and <zihziah> written as one word: be present in great numbers, be found all over a place) (j:om/zihziah) (r:zd:13303/zd:19197) (q:draft)
omzo = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:already exist/have already been) (d:<om> be with <zo> marking what is already done: have existed or been there before the time spoken of, often followed by <pek>, long ago; ability is not meant here) (r:zd:25390/zd:19166) (q:draft)
omzolo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot be/cannot stay/be unable to exist) (d:<om> and <zolo> written as one word: not able to be or stay, there cannot be) (j:om/zolo) (r:zd:24731/zd:17637/zd:24054) (q:draft)
ong nusiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:passing/death/decease) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, toward us, and <nusiatna>, a leaving behind: the leaving of us, a respectful word for the death of a person; stands after the name of the dead and before words such as <hangin> or {tawh kisai}) (r:zd:22595/zd:13178) (q:draft)
ongbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:hongbawl) (r:zd:16031/zd:26444) (q:draft)
ongci = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say to me/tell us) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, and <ci>, say, written as one word after the words quoted: he or she said to me or to us) (j:hong/ci) (r:zd:25768/zd:15192) (q:draft)
ongcih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say to me/tell me) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, with <cih>, written as one word: what someone says to the speaker; {ongcih bang} is as I was told, {ongcih teh} when she said to me) (j:hong/cih) (r:zd:17181) (q:draft)
onggen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:tell/say to) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, and <gen>, written as one word: tell or say something to us or to the hearer) (j:hong/gen) (r:zd:24354/zd:26444) (q:draft)
ongkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:send to/send here) (d:{ong}, another spelling of <hong>, toward the speaker or hearer, written as one word with <khak>, send: send a message, money or a document to me, to us or to you) (j:hong/khak) (r:zd:16813/zd:12371/zd:11797) (q:draft)
ongki = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<hong> in the spelling {ong} written together with the prefix <ki>, before a verb: toward the speaker or to us, with a passive or reflexive verb; {ongki ze-et} is we are tempted) (j:hong/ki) (r:zd:17955) (q:draft, low confidence)
onglak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:show us/reveal to us) (d:{ong}, another spelling of the verb particle <hong>, and the verb for showing, of which <lah> is a form, written as one word: it shows us, makes known to us) (r:zd:19900/zd:24026) (q:draft)
onglo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:fail/not pass) (d:{ong}, pass an examination or test, a Burmese loan, written as one word with <lo>, not: fail, not pass) (r:zd:16900/zd:16152/zd:19983) (q:draft)
ongneih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:hold/give/have) (d:{ong}, a spoken form of <hong>, and <neih>, have, written as one word; in announcements {hanthotna ongneih ding} is will give the exhortation) (j:hong/neih) (r:zd:21139) (q:draft, low confidence)
ongnusia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:leave us/pass away) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, toward the speaker, and <nusia>, leave, written as one word: has left us, used in condolence notices of a person who has died) (r:zd:21699/zd:22703) (q:draft)
ongpai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:come/come here) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, with <pai>, written as one word: come toward the speaker) (j:hong/pai) (r:zd:15933/zd:17723) (q:draft)
ongpia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:give us/give to me/grant) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, toward the speaker, and <pia>, give, written as one word: give to us or to me; {thupha ongpia} is bless us) (r:zd:17181/zd:25768/zd:20016) (q:draft)
ongpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:give/given to us) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, with <piak>, give, written as one word: that is given to us or to you) (j:hong/piak) (r:zd:19257/zd:23872) (q:draft)
ongpuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:bring/send/take to) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, and <puak> written as one word: bring or send something or someone, toward the speaker or the person spoken of) (j:hong/puak) (r:zd:25275/zd:23737) (q:draft)
ongsa = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find/consider/feel) (d:{ong}, another spelling of <hong>, and <sa>, feel or consider, written as one word after a describing word: {lamdang ongsa} is found it strange) (j:hong/sa) (r:zd:19779/zd:16376) (q:draft)
ongsuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (j:hongsuak) (r:zd:23782/zd:19834) (q:draft)
ongte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:those who come) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong> used as a verb, come, with the plural <te>, written as one word: {a ongte} is those who come) (j:hong/te) (r:zd:23014) (q:draft, low confidence)
ongtun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:arrive/come/reach) (d:{ong}, another spelling of <hong>, and <tun> written as one word: come to the people spoken of, said of a day or an event that comes round; the form used before endings such as <sialin>, every time) (j:hong/tun) (r:zd:17786/zd:12432) (q:draft)
ongtung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:arrive/come to) (d:{ong}, another spelling of <hong>, and <tung> written as one word: arrive here, come to a place) (j:hong/tung) (r:zd:22664/zd:10688) (q:draft)
ongtungding = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time) (w:coming/upcoming/next) (d:{ong}, a spelling of <hong>, with <tung>, arrive, and <ding>, written as one word: that will arrive, the coming; placed before a date) (j:hong/tung/ding) (r:zd:15190/zd:11832) (q:draft)
online = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:it) (w:online/on the internet) (d:on the internet; {online pan} is from the internet, by way of the internet, and {online ah} is on the internet) (o:English) (r:zd:21042/zd:24393/zd:26411) (q:draft)
Ontario = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Ontario) (d:province of Canada; Lake Ontario is the lake on its southern border) (r:zd:21583) (q:draft)
Ooredoo = (i:1) (t:name) (f:it) (w:Ooredoo) (d:a mobile phone company, one of the telecoms operators of Myanmar) (r:zd:17607/zd:25332) (q:draft)
Oparasi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:raid/immigration raid/operation) (d:an operation of the Malaysian police or immigration officers in which people without documents are checked and arrested; {Oparasi tawh kiman} is arrested in a raid) (o:Malay, operasi) (r:zd:13291/zd:23629) (q:draft)
oparasi lut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:raid/carry out a raid) (d:{oparasi}, an immigration raid, and <lut>, enter: of the authorities, come into a place to check papers and arrest people without them; the place stands before with <ah>) (r:zd:23629) (q:draft)
Operasi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:raid/operation/crackdown) (d:in Malaysia, an operation of the police or immigration officers to check and arrest foreigners without papers; {Operasi lut} is a raid comes in) (o:Malay, operasi) (r:zd:14836/zd:21552/zd:15739) (q:draft)
operasi lut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:raid/carry out a raid) (d:{operasi}, raid, and <lut>, enter: the authorities carry out a raid on a place, above all an immigration raid in Malaysia; the place stands before it with <ah> and the number of people arrested follows) (r:zd:15745/zd:12464) (q:draft)
operasi lutin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics) (w:in a raid/in a crackdown) (d:<Operasi>, a raid of the Malaysian police or immigration officers, and <lutin>, entering: a raid having come in, that is in a raid; the place stands before it with <ah> or <sungah>, and the number of people arrested follows with <kiman>) (r:zd:15187/zd:16197) (q:draft)
Operation = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:operation/surgery) (d:a surgical operation; {operation bawl} is to operate on someone or to have an operation) (o:English) (r:zd:24029/zd:12285) (q:draft)
Operation = (i:2) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:operation) (d:an organised action of soldiers, police or rescuers) (o:English) (r:zd:11043/zd:13082) (q:draft, low confidence)
Operator = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:operator) (d:a person who works a machine such as a crane or a lift, or a company that runs a service such as buses or telephones) (o:English) (r:zd:15639/zd:17607) (q:draft)
