pasal = (i:3) (t:n) (f:family) (w:husband) (d:a married man in relation to his wife) (r:zai:husband) (q:draft)
pasaldang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:another man/other man) (d:<pasal>, man, and <dang>, other, written as one word) (j:pasal/dang) (r:zd:19854/zd:11938) (q:draft)
pasalhon = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:group of men/band of men) (d:<pasal>, man, and <hon>, group, written as one word: a group of men) (j:pasal/hon) (r:zd:18056/zd:20611) (q:draft)
pasalna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:manliness/manhood/bravery) (d:<pasal>, man, with the noun suffix {-na}: the quality of being a man, manly courage) (b:pasal) (r:zd:21251) (q:draft)
pasalna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (d:in the pair {numei-pasalna}, woman and man: relations between the sexes, love affairs and sexual pleasure, named beside drink and money as worldly pursuits) (b:pasal) (r:zd:9429/zd:9425) (q:draft, low confidence)
pasalneih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:marriage/taking a husband) (d:<pasal>, husband, and <neih>, having, written as one word: a woman's marrying; paired with <zineih>, taking a wife, for marriage in general) (j:pasal/neih) (r:zd:11150/zd:12630) (q:draft)
pasalnih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:two men) (d:<pasal> and <nih> written as one word: two men) (j:pasal/nih) (r:zd:12748/zd:12634) (q:draft)
pasalno = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:boy/male child) (d:<pasal>, male, with <no>, young) (s:naupangpa) (a:numeino) (b:pasal) (q:draft)
pasalnokhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/social) (w:a boy/one boy) (d:<pasalno>, boy, and <khat>, one, written as one word) (j:pasalno/khat) (r:zd:17426/zd:16321) (q:draft)
pasian bawlsa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:creation/God's creation/created things) (d:<Pasian>, God, with <bawlsa>, what is made: what God has made, the created world; also placed before a noun, as in {Pasian bawlsa nate}, the things God made) (r:zd:23896/zd:23877) (q:draft)
pasian deihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:will of God/God's will) (d:<Pasian>, God, and <deihna>, what one wants: the will of God, a fixed term of church speech; one follows it, {Pasian deihna zuih}, and it is set against {ci leh sa deihna}, the desire of the flesh) (r:zd:23394/zd:23629) (q:draft)
pasian hehpihna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:grace of God/God's mercy) (d:<Pasian>, God, and <hehpihna>, grace: the grace of God; most often in the formula {Pasian hehpihna tawh}, by the grace of God, said of health, success or anything received) (r:zd:16442/zd:20699) (q:draft)
pasian kammal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:word of God/God's word) (d:<Pasian>, God, and <kammal>, word: the word of God, said of the Bible and its teaching; written {Pasian kammal} with a capital) (r:zd:23394/zd:24064) (q:draft)
pasian nasem = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:servant of God/minister/church worker) (d:<Pasian>, God, and <nasem>, work or serve: one who serves God, a minister or church worker; also used as a verb, serve God, as in {hunbit Pasian nasem}, serve God full time) (r:zd:23057/zd:20971) (q:draft)
pasian nasemte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:ministers/clergy/church workers/servants of God) (d:<Pasian>, God, and <nasemte>, those who work or serve: the people who serve God as their calling, the pastors, evangelists and other workers of the churches taken together; one of them is {Pasian nasem}) (r:zd:25291/ts:4564/zd:25464) (q:draft)
pasian phatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:praise of God/worship/praise) (d:<pasian>, God, and <phatna>, praise: the praising of God in song and prayer; before <la> or <labu> it names a hymn of praise or a hymn book) (r:zd:23556/zd:9249/zd:15572) (q:draft)
pasian thuthuk = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/education) (w:theology/deep things of God) (d:<Pasian>, God, and <thuthuk>, deep matter: the deep truths about God, and so theology as a subject of study; {Pasian thuthuk sinna} is the study of theology or a theological school, and {Pasian thuthuk hilh} is one who teaches it) (r:zd:19093/zd:25891/zd:10966) (q:draft)
pasian zahtak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:fear God/revere God/be God-fearing) (d:<Pasian>, God, and <zahtak>, respect: revere God, the usual expression for the fear of God; before <mi> or <te> it describes people, {Pasian zahtak mi}, a God-fearing person) (r:zd:23551/zd:8667/zd:24480) (q:draft)
pasian zahtakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:fear of God/reverence for God/godliness) (d:<Pasian>, God, and <zahtakna>, respect: the reverence a person has for God, the term used where the English Bible says the fear of the Lord; God is the one revered, not the one who reveres) (r:zd:9434/zd:17639/zd:11409) (q:draft)
Pasianin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:religion) (w:God) (d:<Pasian> and the subject marker <in> written as one word: God, as the one who acts) (j:Pasian/in) (r:zd:22415/zd:19850/zd:12134) (q:draft)
