paukam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:language/speech) (d:<pau>, speech, with <kam>, mouth: a language, the tongue of a people; a term some writers use and gloss as language) (r:zd:20787/zd:24569) (q:draft)
paulam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:use as a pretext/invoke/cite) (d:put something forward as the reason for what one does, used as a verb where {paulam} the noun is the excuse itself; mostly as {paulam in} after the thing named, in the name of or on the pretext of, and not always with blame) (r:zd:21761/zd:23717/zd:22159) (q:draft)
paulap = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:use as an excuse/use as a pretext) (d:as a verb after a noun, give that thing as the reason for what one does or fails to do, as in {biakna paulap in}, using religion as a pretext) (r:zd:25186/zd:20667) (q:draft)
paulapin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social/politics) (w:as a pretext/on the pretext of) (d:<paulap>, pretext, and <in> written as one word: using the thing named before it as an excuse; {cih paulapin} is on the pretext that) (j:paulap/in) (r:zd:19316/zd:23476) (q:draft)
paulapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:pretext/excuse/justification) (d:what someone gives as the reason for an action or a claim, often a reason that does not hold) (s:paulap) (b:paulap) (r:zd:10984) (q:draft)
paulo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not speak/say nothing) (d:<pau>, speak, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not speak, without speaking; one who does not speak a language) (j:pau/lo) (r:zd:22683/zd:25573) (q:draft)
