paunakin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social/everyday) (w:as the proverb says/in the proverb) (d:<paunak>, proverb, and <in> written as one word: in the words of the proverb, placed before the saying that is quoted) (j:paunak/in) (r:zd:14804/zd:23761) (q:draft)
paunuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:want to speak/like to talk) (d:<pau>, speak, and <nuam>, want, written as one word: be willing or eager to speak) (j:pau/nuam) (r:zd:21085) (q:draft, low confidence)
paupih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:reprove/rebuke/tell off) (d:speak to someone in blame about what he has done or how he looks, where <paupih.1> is only saying something to someone; the anger or silence that follows in the sentence brings it out) (r:zd:20116/zd:19707/zd:16900) (q:draft, low confidence)
pautang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:common language/lingua franca) (d:the language that people of different speech use with one another, or the main language of a country) (r:zd:22789/zd:24157) (q:draft)
