phakdong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:time) (w:until reaching/up to) (d:<phak>, reach, and <dong>, until, written as one word: until an age or a number is reached, as in {kum 60 a phakdong}, until he reached sixty) (j:phak/dong) (r:zd:21817/zd:23616) (q:draft)
phakei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not quite/not very/hardly) (d:<pha>, reach, and the negative <kei> written as one word after a verb or describing word: not to any great degree, hardly) (j:pha/kei) (r:zd:24749/zd:14730) (q:draft, low confidence)
phakhinding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:will have reached/probably amount to) (d:<phakhin>, have reached a number, and <ding>, will, written as one word: the number is thought to have reached so many already; mostly after a number with <bang>, about) (j:phakhin/ding) (r:zd:12553/zd:14859) (q:draft)
phakhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have reached/have already reached) (d:<phakhin>, have already reached, with <ta>, written as one word after a number: an age or a count has now reached that number) (j:phakhin/ta) (r:zd:17049/zd:12618/zd:14770) (q:draft)
phakin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:time) (w:reach/attain) (d:<phak>, reach an age, with the linking ending <in>: on reaching, after <kum> and a number, as in {kum 43 a phakin}, at the age of 43; not the word for leprosy) (r:zd:9222/zd:23138/zd:11279) (q:draft)
phakleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:when one reaches/if one reaches) (d:<phak>, reach, and <leh>, if or when, written as one word, said of reaching an age) (j:phak/leh) (r:zd:23972/zd:24248) (q:draft)
phakloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not reach/be beyond) (d:<phak>, reach, and the negative <loh>, written as one word: not reaching, out of reach; {theih phakloh} is beyond what one can know) (j:phak/loh) (r:zd:22713/zd:24963) (q:draft, low confidence)
phakma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:before reaching) (d:<phak>, reach, and <ma>, before, written as one word and followed by <in>: before reaching an age or a place; {kum 40 a phakma in} is before he reached the age of 40) (j:phak/ma) (r:zd:20736/zd:22159) (q:draft)
Phalaam = (i:1) (t:name) (f:travel/politics) (j:Falam) (r:zd:20176/zd:19166) (q:draft)
phalai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still number/amount to) (d:<pha>, here reach a number, and <lai>, still, written as one word after a count: still amount to, number as many as) (j:pha/lai) (r:zd:20401/zd:14740) (q:draft, low confidence)
phalaiding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday/media) (w:will still/will yet/will go on to) (d:written after a verb in reports of what officials are yet to do: {encian phalaiding uh} is they will still examine it; it ends in <laiding>, will still, and the force of the first part <pha> is not clear) (j:pha/laiding) (r:zd:14628/zd:20466) (q:draft, low confidence)
Phalam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (j:Falam) (r:zd:20176) (q:draft)
phalbi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:time/nature) (w:winter/cold season) (d:the cold season of the year, winter, set against <khuakhal>, summer; {phalbi lai} is in winter) (s:phabi/phaibi) (a:khuakhal/khualkhal) (r:22.2.11) (q:draft)
phallo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:not allow/forbid/refuse permission) (d:<phal>, permit, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not allow; {ki phallo} is it is not allowed) (s:khaam) (j:phal/lo) (r:zd:12487/zd:19455/zd:14767) (q:draft)
phalloh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/politics) (w:not permitted/unauthorised/forbidden) (d:<phal> and <loh> written as one word: not permitting, without the permission of; {kumpi phalloh} is not permitted by the government, illegal) (j:phal/loh) (r:zd:20930/zd:23784/zd:19427) (q:draft)
phallohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:prohibition/ban) (d:<phal> and <lohna> written as one word: the not allowing of something, a prohibition, the opposite of <phalna>, permission) (j:phal/lohna) (r:zd:23008) (q:draft)
phalna kician = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/work) (w:valid permit/legal documents/proper authorisation) (d:<phalna>, permission, and <kician>, firm or sound: an official permit that is valid, above all the papers that allow a foreigner to stay or work in a country; {phalna kician neilo} is without valid documents, undocumented) (r:zd:13255/zd:20912/zd:24297) (q:draft)
phalna omlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/work) (w:without permission/without a licence/illegally) (d:<phalna>, permission, and <omlo>, there not being: followed by <in>, without permission or licence, said of what is done unlawfully; the one whose permission is lacking stands before it in the possessive, {kumpi' phalna omlo in}) (r:zd:20909/zd:18952) (q:draft)
phalna omlopi = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/social) (w:without permission/without a permit/illegally) (d:<phalna>, permission, with <omlopi>, there being none: without permission or a licence, followed by <in> and a verb for what is done unlawfully) (r:zd:11649/zd:11594) (q:draft)
phalnailo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:not yet permit/not yet allow) (d:<phal>, permit, and <nailo>, not yet, written as one word: have not yet given leave) (j:phal/nailo) (r:zd:11698/zd:19614) (q:draft)
phalnawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:no longer allow/no longer permit) (d:<phal>, allow, and <nawnlo>, no longer, written as one word; with <ki> before it, be no longer allowed) (j:phal/nawnlo) (r:zd:11833/zd:11854) (q:draft)
phalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not reach/not amount to) (d:<pha>, here reach or amount to, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not reaching a number or level, not much, not quite) (j:pha/lo) (r:zd:22278/zd:17634) (q:draft, low confidence)
phaltak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social) (w:generously/willingly/freely) (d:<phal>, generous or willing, and <tak> written as one word, mostly with <in>: giving or lending without holding back) (j:phal/tak) (r:zd:11159/zd:21559) (q:draft)
phaltakin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:social/religion) (w:generously/willingly/freely) (d:<phal>, willing, with <takin>, written as one word: giving or allowing gladly, without holding back) (j:phal/takin) (r:zd:17685/zd:22938) (q:draft)
Phaltang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Phaltang) (d:a village near the border of India and Myanmar; {Phaltang khuathak} is New Phaltang, also called Bulphek) (r:zd:20315) (q:draft, low confidence)
phalvetlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not allow at all/forbid/refuse to let) (d:<phal>, allow, and <vetlo>, not at all, written as one word: not allow in any way) (j:phal/vetlo) (r:zd:13151/zd:12676) (q:draft)
pham = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/family) (w:pass away/die) (d:die, a gentle and poetic word used with respect of people; {pham sate} are those who have passed away) (s:si) (r:zd:24086/zd:9421/zd:15809) (q:draft)
phamahmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:very much/greatly/indeed) (d:<pha> and <mahmah> written as one word and placed after a verb or describing word: very much, to a great degree; the first part strengthens the second and does not mean good) (j:pha/mahmah) (r:zd:25866/zd:15274/zd:12688) (q:draft)
phamawhlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:all right/not a problem/not matter) (d:<phamawh> and <lo> written as one word: it does not matter, there is no harm in it) (j:phamawh/lo) (r:zd:11487/zd:17841) (q:draft)
phamawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:necessity/compulsion) (d:<phamawh> with the noun suffix {-na}; after a verb with <loh>, the fact that it must be done: {khawl loh a phamawhna mun} is a place where one has to rest) (b:phamawh) (r:zd:25288/zd:24733) (q:draft)
phamawhsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:regard as important/mind/take seriously) (d:<phamawh>, of concern, and <sak>, consider, written as one word: count something as mattering, be bothered by it) (j:phamawh/sak) (r:zd:9451) (q:draft, low confidence)
phamawhta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have to/must) (d:<phamawh>, necessary, and <ta>, the marker of a change, written as one word: after a verb with <loh>, not doing it was no longer possible, had to) (j:phamawh/ta) (r:zd:12998/zd:15280) (q:draft)
phamawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:amount to/reach/number) (d:<pha>, here reach, with <mawk>, written as one word after a number or a measure: come to that much, be as many or as high as that) (j:pha/mawk) (r:zd:12567/zd:12854) (q:draft)
phamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/family) (w:death/passing) (d:<pham>, pass away, with the noun suffix <na>: death, a gentle and poetic word) (s:sihna) (b:pham) (r:zd:25277/ts:301) (q:draft)
phamsa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:the deceased/the departed/the dead) (d:poetic and respectful word for those who have died; {phamsa te phawkna} is a remembrance of the departed) (s:misi) (r:zd:12024/zd:23388) (q:draft)
phan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/work) (w:weave/plait/knit) (d:make a thing by interlacing strips or threads by hand, such as a basket, a mat or knitted clothing) (r:ts:3375) (q:draft, low confidence)
phangphang = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:one after another/in a rush) (d:after a verb, of many people or things doing the same thing suddenly and in quick succession, as leaving, arriving or going astray; it carries no blame of rashness) (r:zd:15941/zd:21908/zd:25181) (q:draft, low confidence)
phanuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:want to reach/wish to get to) (d:apparently <pha.5>, reach, and <nuam>, want, written as one word: wish to reach a place) (j:pha/nuam) (r:zd:12112) (q:draft, low confidence)
phapan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:time/everyday) (w:have just reached/be only just) (d:<pha>, here reach an amount, with <pan>, here only just, written as one word: have only now reached an age or a length of time, as in {kum 15 bek phapan}, only just 15 years old) (j:pha/pan) (r:zd:16713/zd:12087/zd:11484) (q:draft)
phapha = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:social/media) (w:earnestly/sincerely/kindly) (d:after a verb of inviting, informing or thanking in a notice or letter, as {kong zawn phapha uh hi}, we earnestly invite you, and {kizasak phapha}, it is hereby made known: a polite strengthening of the request, not care in doing something) (r:zd:22539/zd:22590/zd:21510) (q:draft)
Pharaoh = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (w:Pharaoh) (d:title of the king of ancient Egypt, in its English spelling; the Bible text writes <Faro>) (s:Faro) (o:English) (r:zd:16897/zd:22275) (q:draft)
Pharisee = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:religion) (w:Pharisee) (d:member of the Pharisees, a Jewish religious party strict in keeping the law, in the English spelling; the Bible text writes <Farisai>) (s:Farisai) (o:English) (r:zd:17883/zd:11256) (q:draft)
Pharoah = (i:1) (t:name) (c:male) (f:religion) (j:Faro) (r:zd:21137) (q:draft)
phasak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:amount to/total/make up) (d:after a number or quantity, bring the count to that number, or reckon it at that number, <pha>, reach, with the causative <sak>; {nam 8 bang phasak} is make eight kinds in all) (r:zd:11769/zd:16302/ts:3375) (q:draft)
phasakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:will make up/will total) (d:<phasak.3>, bring the count to a number, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a number: there will be that many made or built) (j:phasak/ding) (r:zd:11846/zd:12420) (q:draft)
phasan = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:greatly/considerably) (d:placed after a verb: to a marked degree) (r:zd:25176/zd:9220) (q:draft, low confidence)
phasem = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:even more/all the more) (d:placed after a verb or a describing word: to a still greater degree, as {lauhuai phasem}, even more dangerous; compare <semsem>, more and more) (r:zd:13026/zd:22238) (q:draft, low confidence)
phat = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:carefully/thoroughly/well) (d:after a verb of thinking or examining, such as <ngaihsut>, <kikup>, <kisit> and <et>: do it with care, go over it well; not {phat}, praise, and often followed by <huai> or <ding>) (r:zd:25136/zd:21049) (q:draft)
phata = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:reach/amount to/number) (d:<pha>, here reach or amount to, and <ta>, now, written as one word after a number: has now reached that number, amount or age) (j:pha/ta) (r:zd:21690/zd:11619/zd:19080) (q:draft)
phatak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:well/properly/thoroughly) (d:<pha>, good, with <tak>, written as one word: well, properly, with care; mostly as the second half of a pair, {hoihtak phatak in}, well and properly) (j:pha/tak) (r:zd:19371/zd:22334/zd:11670) (q:draft)
phatbawl = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:praise/compliment/commend) (d:<phat>, praise, and <bawl>, make, written as one word: speak well of someone, treat with praise) (j:phat/bawl) (r:zd:12436/zd:15496) (q:draft, low confidence)
phatdiak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:especially/particularly/most of all) (d:form of <phadiak> used before a noun or before words such as <uh> and <ding>: {atam phatdiak hun} is the time when there are most) (b:phadiak) (r:zd:15822/zd:11253/zd:20877) (q:draft)
phatding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:should carefully/to do thoroughly) (d:<phat>, carefully, and <ding>, to or should, written as one word after a verb of thinking, asking or examining: it is to be done with care) (j:phat/ding) (r:zd:24446/zd:17677) (q:draft)
phathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can reach/may amount to) (d:<pha>, reach a number or amount, and <thei>, can, written as one word after a number: may come to that many or that much) (j:pha/thei) (r:zd:11342/zd:20747) (q:draft)
phatkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion) (w:praise together/worship together) (d:<phat>, praise, and <khop>, together, written as one word: praise God together with others) (j:phat/khop) (r:zd:15407/zd:11135) (q:draft)
phatloh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not quite/not really/not fully) (d:<phat> and <loh> written as one word after a verb: not fully so, not really; the form used before a noun or <ciangin>) (j:phat/loh) (r:zd:21869/zd:20790) (q:draft, low confidence)
phatmahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:praise highly) (d:<phat>, praise, and <mahmah>, very, written as one word) (j:phat/mahmah) (r:zd:12029/zd:16817) (q:draft)
phatmawh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (j:phamawh) (r:zd:25891/zd:25126) (q:draft)
phatnate = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:good qualities/merits/virtues) (d:<phatna.2>, goodness, with the plural <te>: the good and praiseworthy qualities of a person, mostly paired with <hoihna> as {hoihna phatnate}, and not words or songs of praise) (r:zd:19269/zd:21898) (q:draft)
phatota = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have reached/have risen to) (d:<phato>, reach up to, with <ta>, now: a growing number has now reached this figure, common in headlines that count the dead) (j:phato/ta) (r:zd:12194/zd:14858/zd:20023) (q:draft)
phatphat = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:carefully/closely/thoroughly) (d:placed after a verb such as <et>, <sim> or <ngaih>: doing it with care and attention, as in {et phatphat}, look closely; not the doubled <phat>, praise) (r:zd:10672/zd:13302/zd:20176) (q:draft)
phatsak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be proud/boast) (d:after <ki>, written apart, it is the verb <kiphatsak>, be proud or boast, not let praise; {ki phatsak pih} is be proud of something) (s:kiphatsak) (r:zd:15794/zd:17521/zd:16442) (q:draft)
phatsakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:self-praise/pride/conceit) (d:found after <ki> as {ki phatsakna}, the same as <kiphatsakna> written in two words: a high opinion of oneself, pride) (b:phatsak) (r:zd:19124) (q:draft)
phatsakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:boast of/take pride in) (d:written after a separate <ki> or {ki-}, the two together being <kiphatsakpih>: be proud on account of something) (r:zd:23301/zd:20728) (q:draft)
phatsiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:be good at praising/praise readily) (d:<phat>, praise, with <siam>, skilled, written as one word: know how to praise others, be ready with praise) (j:phat/siam) (r:zd:20697/zd:21340) (q:draft)
phattuam nading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:social) (w:for the benefit of/for the good of/benefit) (d:<phattuam>, benefit, and <nading.2>, for: placed after the one who gains, for the benefit or good of that person or group; {mipi phattuam nading} is the public good, and with <in> after it the phrase gives a purpose) (r:zd:21876/zd:21224) (q:draft)
phatuam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:be saved/be spared/be eased) (d:said of a cost or a burden, as <sumbei>, expense, <hunbei>, time spent, <sing>, firewood, or a fire: become less, be saved or eased, where sense 1 is said of the thing that does good) (r:zd:21259/zd:11658) (q:draft, low confidence)
phatuamding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will save/will benefit/will help) (d:<phatuam>, be of use, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will be of benefit; of cost or time, will be saved or reduced) (j:phatuam/ding) (r:zd:11308/zd:15067/zd:20104) (q:draft)
phatuamlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be of no use/not help/be useless) (d:<phatuam> and <lo>, not, written as one word: it does no good, brings no relief) (j:phatuam/lo) (r:zd:10722/zd:16433/zd:12359) (q:draft)
phatuamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:benefit/advantage/profit/use) (d:<phatuam>, be of use, with the noun ending <na>: the good or gain that comes from something; {aituam phatuamna} is personal gain) (s:hamphatna) (b:phatuam) (r:zd:23332/zd:16588) (q:draft)
phatuamsak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health) (w:relieve/ease/be good for) (d:with an illness or complaint before it, as {natna phatuamsak}: make the complaint better, said of a food, a medicine or an exercise) (r:zd:11167/zd:14816/zd:21239) (q:draft)
phawk = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:remember) (d:keep or bring back in mind, the opposite of <mangngilh>, forget) (s:phawkkik/phawkkha) (a:mangngilh)
phawka = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:remember and/be aware and) (d:<phawk>, remember or be aware, and the linking <a> written as one word) (j:phawk/a) (r:zd:24238) (q:draft, low confidence)
phawkciat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:each remember/all keep in mind) (d:<phawk> and <ciat> written as one word: remember, every one of us or of you, as in a request for prayer) (j:phawk/ciat) (r:zd:15565/zd:14967) (q:draft)
phawkciatni = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:let us each remember) (d:<phawk>, remember, and <ciatni>, let us each, written as one word; {thungetna ah phawkciatni} is let us each remember them in prayer) (j:phawk/ciatni) (r:zd:11259/zd:12290) (q:draft)
phawkden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always remember/keep in mind) (d:<phawk>, remember, and <den>, always, written as one word: never forget, keep in mind at all times) (j:phawk/den) (r:zd:10687/zd:23602) (q:draft)
phawkdenleng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if we always remember) (d:<phawkden>, always remember, and <leng>, if, written as one word: if we keep it in mind) (j:phawkden/leng) (r:zd:16365/zd:14709) (q:draft)
phawkdet = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep in mind/bear in mind/remember firmly) (d:<phawk>, remember, and <det>, steadily, written as one word, nearly always before <huai>: something that ought to be kept firmly in mind) (s:phawkden) (j:phawk/det) (r:zd:15300/zd:14581) (q:draft)
phawkding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to remember/to bear in mind/to note) (d:<phawk> and <ding> written as one word: to be remembered, something one should keep in mind; {phawkding thu} is a point to note) (j:phawk/ding) (r:zd:17355/zd:22019/zd:19092) (q:draft)
phawkhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:worth remembering/notable/to be kept in mind) (d:<phawk>, remember, with <huai>, worthy of: that ought to be remembered or noticed; at the end of a sentence, it should be remembered that) (j:phawk/huai) (r:zd:23394/zd:24375/zd:22754) (q:draft)
phawkkawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:while remembering/bearing in mind) (d:<phawk> and <kawm> written as one word, followed by <in>: while remembering, keeping something in mind as one acts) (j:phawk/kawm) (r:zd:16442/zd:21134) (q:draft)
phawkkhalo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not notice/be unaware) (d:<phawkkha> and <lo> written as one word: not notice, not realise that something is happening) (j:phawkkha/lo) (r:zd:12304/zd:11780/zd:19871) (q:draft)
phawkkik = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:regain consciousness/come to/come round) (d:after <khua>, or alone of someone who had fainted: become conscious again, where the other sense is recalling a thing to mind) (r:zd:14824/zd:12304/zd:17547) (q:draft)
phawklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:not notice/be unaware) (d:<phawk> and <lo> written as one word: not notice, not be aware of; {khua phawklo} is to be unconscious) (j:phawk/lo) (r:zd:12290/zd:16302) (q:draft)
phawkloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not remember/be unaware/not notice) (d:<phawk> and <loh> written as one word: not remember, not be aware of; {i phawkloh kal in} is while we are not aware, without our noticing) (j:phawk/loh) (r:zd:12784/zd:20568/zd:24370) (q:draft)
phawknawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:lose consciousness/be unconscious) (d:<phawk> and <nawnlo> written as one word; with <khua>, {khua phawknawnlo}, no longer aware of anything, unconscious) (j:phawk/nawnlo) (r:zd:12733/zd:14635/zd:12304) (q:draft)
phawkni = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:let us remember/let us keep in mind) (d:<phawk>, remember, and the ending <ni>, here let us, written as one word; {thungetna ah phawkni} is let us remember it in prayer) (j:phawk/ni) (r:zd:19080/zd:11827) (q:draft)
phawkpak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:recall offhand/remember for the moment) (d:<phawk>, remember, with <pak>, quickly or for a short while, written as one word: remember offhand, what comes to mind at the moment) (j:phawk/pak) (r:zd:15834/zd:14579) (q:draft)
phawkpan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:only then notice/realize only then) (d:<phawk>, be aware, with <pan>, begin: notice or realize something only at that moment, not before) (j:phawk/pan) (r:zd:12669/zd:18128) (q:draft)
phawktawntung = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:always remember/keep in mind) (d:<phawk> and <tawntung> written as one word: remember at all times, never forget) (j:phawk/tawntung) (r:zd:20917/zd:14722) (q:draft)
phawkthak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be reminded/remember afresh) (d:<phawk>, remember or be aware, and <thak>, new, written as one word: call to mind again, be reminded; with <huai>, worth being reminded of) (j:phawk/thak) (r:zd:14709/zd:12596) (q:draft)
phawkthakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:reminder/renewed awareness) (d:<phawkthak>, be reminded, with the noun suffix <na>: a reminder, becoming aware again) (b:phawkthak) (r:zd:12746/zd:14720) (q:draft)
phawng = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:stir/move/prompt/awaken) (d:with <lungsim> or <ngaihsutna>, mostly after <hong>: stir the heart or the thoughts, of words, a question or a memory that will not leave someone at rest) (r:zd:16315/zd:25265/zd:15767) (q:draft)
phawt = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (j:phot) (r:zd:15069) (q:draft, low confidence)
phazo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:enough/sufficient) (d:said of what is sufficient; {phazo hi} means that is enough, often said to stop someone)
phazolo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not reach/fall short of/cannot keep up) (d:<pha>, reach, <zo>, be able, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not come up to a number or amount, or be unable to reach or keep up with someone) (j:pha/zo/lo) (r:zd:12337/zd:22873) (q:draft)
pheek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:mat) (d:mat for lying on, in {lupna pheek}, sleeping mat) (q:draft)
phei = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday/travel) (w:across/over) (d:placed after a verb of going, coming or giving, as in {pai phei}, {hawh phei} and {pia phei}: the action goes across to a person or place on the same level, not up or down; not the noun {phei}, thigh) (r:zd:16243/zd:22040/zd:9228) (q:draft)
pheiphei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:on and on/one after another/continually) (d:placed after a verb: the action goes on and on or passes from one to the next, as in {en pheiphei}, keep looking on, and {ci pheiphei}, keep on saying) (r:zd:21218/zd:19826) (q:draft, low confidence)
pheiphung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:legs/feet) (d:word of songs and elevated speech for the legs or feet with which one walks, from <phei>, leg; {pheiphung suankhawm} is step forward together) (r:zd:13043) (q:draft, low confidence)
phek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (j:pheek) (r:zd:15286) (q:draft, low confidence)
phek = (i:2) (t:v) (f:body/home) (w:plait/braid) (d:weave strands together, as hair into plaits; the word also counts the plaits, as {phek thum}, three plaits) (r:ts:3375) (q:draft, low confidence)
phekap = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:card playing/gambling at cards) (d:playing cards, especially for money; named with drink and drugs as a harmful habit) (r:zd:15329) (q:draft, low confidence)
Phekong = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:politics/travel) (w:Pekon/Phekon) (d:town in the south of Shan State in Myanmar, near Moebye) (r:ts:4418/ts:4298) (q:draft)
phelhhuan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:fight a fire/work to put out) (d:<phelh>, put out a fire, with a second part that is not explained: work at putting out a fire, said in the articles of firefighters and others who do so in numbers; {phelhhuan ngeingai} is fight the fire hard) (b:phelh) (r:zd:13092/zd:12736) (q:draft, low confidence, the part huan is not explained)
phelhkhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have put out/have extinguished) (d:<phelh>, put out a fire, and <khinta>, already done, written as one word: have already put the fire out) (j:phelh/khinta) (r:zd:19125/zd:13352) (q:draft)
phelhkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:put out again/extinguish) (d:<phelh>, put out a fire, and <kik>, back or again, written as one word: bring a fire that has broken out back under control; mostly passive, {ki phelhkik}) (j:phelh/kik) (r:zd:12750/zd:15669) (q:draft)
phelhpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:put out at once/extinguish immediately) (d:<phelh>, put out a fire, and <pah>, at once, written as one word) (j:phelh/pah) (r:zd:15461/zd:19394) (q:draft)
phelhsiang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:extinguish completely/put out) (d:<phelh>, put out a fire, with <siang>, clean: put a fire out completely) (b:phelh) (r:zd:17289/zd:16239/zd:15686) (q:draft)
phelhsiangthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:be able to put out/manage to extinguish) (d:<phelhsiang> and <thei> written as one word: be able to put a fire out completely) (j:phelhsiang/thei) (r:zd:14865/zd:14575) (q:draft)
phelhsiangzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:put out completely/manage to extinguish) (d:<phelh>, put out a fire, <siang>, clean, and <zo>, be able, written as one word: succeed in putting a fire out completely; {ki phelhsiangzo} is the fire was fully put out) (j:phelh/siang/zo) (r:zd:17729/zd:17917/zd:20335) (q:draft)
phelhsiangzopan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:finally put out/manage to extinguish) (d:<phelhsiang> and <zopan> written as one word: only then manage to put a fire out completely) (j:phelhsiang/zopan) (r:zd:14545/zd:21164) (q:draft)
phelkhat = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food/everyday) (w:piece/slice) (d:one piece or slice cut from something, not necessarily a half, as {sing phelkhat}, a piece of ginger) (r:zd:24276) (q:draft, low confidence)
phelkhiading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:will tear down/to be demolished/will pull down) (d:<phelkhia>, tear down, and <ding> written as one word: will pull a building down, or after <ki> is to be demolished) (j:phelkhia/ding) (r:zd:19508) (q:draft)
phelkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/home) (w:tear down/demolish/break off) (d:form of <phelkhia> used in relative clauses and before <khitciangin> and similar words: take a building apart, or break pieces off rock) (b:phelkhia) (r:zd:17097/zd:24280) (q:draft)
phen = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:interpret/translate) (d:put what someone says into another language, a figure of opening the speech; with <sak> for the person served, {hong phen sak}, interpret for you, and with <kam> in {kam phen}, the work of the <kamphen>, interpreter) (r:zd:18159) (q:draft, low confidence)
phenghawlgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:drive recklessly/drive wildly) (d:<pheng>, rashly, and <hawlgawp>, drive wildly, written as one word: drive a vehicle fast and without any care) (j:pheng/hawlgawp) (r:zd:15953/zd:15201) (q:draft)
phengzatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:squandering/misuse/misappropriation) (d:<phengzat>, squander, with the noun ending {-na}: the reckless or wrongful spending of money, as of the funds of a church) (b:phengzat) (r:zd:17526) (q:draft)
pheta = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:time) (w:as soon as/the moment) (d:<phet> with the linking <a> written as one word, placed after a verb: as soon as, the moment that) (j:phet/a) (r:zd:23989) (q:draft, low confidence)
phi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/work) (w:sit/take/answer) (d:take an interview or a test and answer its questions; {interview phi} is to go through an interview) (r:zd:21664/zd:22074) (q:draft, low confidence)
phia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:dart about/rush about/scurry) (d:of people or children, move quickly here and there, not of lightning; followed by a sound word such as <ziazua> or {kheokho}) (r:zd:15107/zd:17060) (q:draft, low confidence)
phial = (i:4) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly/practically) (d:after a word of totality or frequency such as <khempeuh>, <gambup> or <nisim>, shows that the statement holds for nearly the whole: {mi khempeuh phial}, almost everyone, <nisim phial>, almost every day) (r:zd:20919/zd:17162/ts:6697) (q:draft)
phiala = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly/practically) (d:<phial> with the ending <a>, after a word of amount, extent or totality: nearly so, to the point of) (j:phial) (r:zd:21326) (q:draft, low confidence)
phialah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in almost/in nearly) (d:<phial>, almost, and the place marker <ah> written as one word, after a word of totality: {khempeuh phialah} is in almost all) (j:phial/ah) (r:zd:14498) (q:draft, low confidence)
phialbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:about/as many as/nearly) (d:<phial> and <bang> written as one word after a number: about that many, as many as) (j:phial/bang) (r:zd:20850/zd:20369/zd:13188) (q:draft)
phialding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:would even/might almost) (d:<phial> and <ding> written as one word after a verb, mostly followed by <in>: it would even go as far as that, said of what is feared, thought or supposed) (j:phial/ding) (r:zd:12105/zd:25188) (q:draft, low confidence)
phialkapgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:shoot at random/fire wildly at) (d:<phial> and <kapgawp>, shoot severely, written as one word: open fire on people without choosing a target; the sense of <phial> here is taken from the sentences) (j:phial/kapgawp) (r:zd:12803/zd:17461) (q:draft)
phialleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/as if) (d:<phial> and <leh>, if, written as one word after a verb: even if it should be so; before <kilawm> it means it almost seems that, it is as though) (j:phial/leh) (r:zd:21796/zd:12693) (q:draft)
phialmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:practically/almost/even) (d:<phial> and <mah> written as one word: stresses that something is as good as so, practically, all but; with <leh> <zong>, even if) (j:phial/mah) (r:zd:9231/zd:21458) (q:draft, low confidence)
phialmawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:practically/almost/one might even say) (d:<phial> and <mawk> written as one word after a verb or describing word: stresses that the statement goes that far, it is practically so) (j:phial/mawk) (r:zd:17208/zd:11130) (q:draft, low confidence)
phialphial = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly/just about) (d:placed after a describing word: so close to it that one could almost say so; {kikim phialphial} is just about equal) (s:dektak) (r:zd:25165/zd:14804) (q:draft, low confidence)
phialta = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:almost/nearly/even if) (d:<phial> and <ta> written as one word, placed after a verb: almost or nearly so, and before <zongin> even if it really were so) (j:phial/ta) (r:zd:22272/zd:23653) (q:draft)
phialzong = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/even though) (d:<phial> and <zong> written as one word, placed after the verb and often followed by <in>: even if it should be so) (j:phial/zong) (r:zd:14709/zd:24641/zd:25790) (q:draft)
phialzongin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if/even though) (d:<phial> and <zongin> written as one word after a verb: even if that is so) (j:phial/zongin) (r:zd:20725/zd:20162) (q:draft)
phiat = (i:4) (t:v) (f:body/home) (w:wash/wipe clean) (d:after <mai>, face: {mai phiat} is wash the face, as on getting up in the morning) (r:zd:24276/zd:21918/zd:23036) (q:draft)
phiat = (i:5) (t:v) (f:health) (w:abort) (d:after <nau>, child: {nau phiat} is end a pregnancy, and also the noun abortion) (r:zd:25323) (q:draft, low confidence)
phiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will erase/to be removed/to be struck out) (d:<phiat>, erase, and <ding> written as one word: to be erased or removed, as a name from a list or a tattoo from the skin) (j:phiat/ding) (r:zd:21309/zd:21876) (q:draft)
phiatkhia = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:delete/remove/abolish) (d:take a thing away so that it is no longer there: delete a video, remove a tattoo, do away with a custom or a division; often passive with <ki>) (r:zd:16580/ts:4831/zd:25078) (q:draft)
phiatkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/it) (w:delete/remove/erase) (d:<phiat>, erase, and <kik>, back, written as one word: take away again something that was written, posted or made) (j:phiat/kik) (r:zd:20287/zd:23008/zd:20697) (q:draft)
phiatmaiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:will abolish/will cancel/will remove) (d:<phiatmai>, wipe out, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will do away with it altogether, said of a tax or a rule) (j:phiatmai/ding) (r:zd:19674/zd:19685) (q:draft)
phiatna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health/social) (w:removal/getting rid of/abolition) (d:<phiat>, wipe out, with the noun suffix {-na}: the getting rid of something unwanted, as a smell, a job or a law; {nau phiatna} is abortion; not {phiatna} the flashing of lightning) (r:zd:25323/zd:9124/zd:19843) (q:draft)
phiatsak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:wipe off/erase/remove) (d:<phiat> wipe with <sak>: wipe or clean something away, as dirt from the face, a name written on the skin or bad things from inside a person; not said of a vow) (r:zd:21826/zd:21796/zd:19917) (q:draft)
phiatsak = (i:4) (t:v) (f:health) (w:abort/have aborted) (d:after <nau>, child: {nau phiatsak} is end a pregnancy or make a woman end it) (r:zd:14597) (q:draft, low confidence)
phiauphiau = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:freely/without restraint/carelessly) (d:placed after a verb: doing it freely and without holding back or thinking twice) (r:zd:17649/zd:25064) (q:draft, low confidence)
phih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work) (w:fill in/fill out/complete) (d:write what is asked into a form, after the English word <form>: {form phih} is fill in a form; a present-day use apart from the meaning spit) (r:zd:25248/zd:23973/zd:24006) (q:draft)
phiit = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (j:phit) (r:zd:15495) (q:draft)
