Philtun = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Philtun) (d:place of a bridge over the Tuithang or Manipur river in the Tedim and Tonzang area; {Philtun gunlei} is the Philtun bridge) (r:zd:17675/zd:15642) (q:draft, low confidence)
phin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:drizzle/rain lightly) (d:of rain, fall lightly in fine drops, after <guah> and often followed by <seuhseuh> or {nelhnelh}; not the sense provoke) (r:zd:14824/zd:25630) (q:draft)
phinphian = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:body) (w:shrivelled/wasted) (d:describes something dried up or wasted away: after <gawng>, thin, it means thin to the bone) (r:zd:25918) (q:draft, low confidence)
phisian = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:clear away/get rid of/wipe out) (d:remove a trouble or a wrong completely, said of problems and hardships) (r:zd:21869/zd:17976) (q:draft, low confidence)
phit = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:whistle/pipe) (d:a small instrument blown to give a shrill sound, the whistle of a conductor or policeman and a traditional pipe named among the Zomi instruments, not the hissing itself; {phit mutsan} is blow a whistle at someone) (r:zd:13328/zd:18125/ts:3375) (q:draft)
phitkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/everyday) (w:spurt out/spout/shoot out/burst out) (d:<phit> with <khia>, out: be forced out under pressure, as lava and ash from a volcano or air that has built up; also of anger held in for long that bursts out) (r:zd:23113/zd:17411) (q:draft)
phitkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:spurt out/squirt out/spew out) (d:of a liquid, shoot out in a jet; written after a separate <ki>, as of lava thrown out by a volcano) (r:zd:19514) (q:draft, low confidence)
phitphet = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:to the brim/chock-full/tightly) (d:after <dim>, full, and verbs of loading such as <pua> and <tuang>, not of time: filled or packed completely, with no room left) (r:zd:11375/zd:12790/zd:17375) (q:draft)
phiupheu = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/nature) (d:descriptive word after <kang>, white, and <puang>, pale: white all over, as ground or clothes covered with snow) (r:zd:19826/zd:17527) (q:draft, low confidence)
Phoenix = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Phoenix) (d:city in the state of Arizona in the United States, home of a Zomi community; the name also occurs in the names of other places and organisations) (r:zd:15805) (q:draft)
phok = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature/travel) (w:bumpy/rough/uneven) (d:of a surface or a road, uneven, full of bumps and holes) (r:zd:21421) (q:draft, low confidence)
pholaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (j:pholak) (r:zd:11415/zd:23670) (q:draft)
pholakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:expose/disclose/bring to light) (d:<pholak>, expose, and <khia>, out, written as one word: bring out into the open what was hidden) (j:pholak/khia) (r:zd:10859/zd:10975) (q:draft)
pholakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:expose/reveal/disclose) (d:<pholak>, expose, with <khiat>, out, written as one word: bring something hidden out into the open; the form used before words such as <manin> and <laitak>) (j:pholak/khiat) (r:zd:10859/zd:19958) (q:draft)
pholh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:bring out/reveal/disclose) (d:seen only with <khia>, out, as {pholh khia}, bring out what is hidden, such as sins or thoughts; mostly written as one word, <pholhkhia>) (r:zd:22815/zd:15758) (q:draft, low confidence)
pholhkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:bring out/reveal/disclose/dig out) (d:take out what is hidden or buried; of a matter, lay it open and make it known) (r:ts:11162/zd:23670) (q:draft, low confidence)
pholhkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/media) (w:bringing out/disclosure/exposition) (d:noun of <pholhkhia>, bring out or reveal: the act of bringing out and making known) (b:pholhkhia) (r:zd:19206) (q:draft, low confidence)
phone = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:phone/telephone) (o:English) (r:zd:20822/zd:12441) (q:draft)
phong = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wake/awaken/rouse) (d:wake someone from sleep) (s:khanglosak/phawng) (q:draft)
phonggyi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Buddhist monk/monk) (d:a Buddhist monk of Myanmar; {phonggyi sang} is a monastery school) (o:Burmese, hpongyi) (r:zd:23869/zd:20834) (q:draft)
phongkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:wake up/rouse) (d:wake a person out of sleep, <phong> with <khia>; of a sleeper, not of anger) (r:zd:19338) (q:draft, low confidence)
phongkhia = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:lift out/pull out/raise up) (d:lift something up and out of where it lies, as a child out of a heap of rubbish) (r:zd:12277) (q:draft, low confidence)
phonglo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:rouse/revive/stir up) (d:wake something up again: stir the heart of people, bring back strength or a custom, or bring up again what is past; often followed by <kik>, again) (r:zd:17877/zd:22116) (q:draft)
phongzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to wake/be able to lift up) (d:<phong>, wake someone or lift up, with <zo>, manage to, written as one word: manage to wake a person, or manage to raise the head) (j:phong/zo) (r:zd:19338/zd:10893) (q:draft, low confidence)
phosphate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/work) (w:phosphate) (d:phosphate rock, mined and used as fertilizer) (o:English) (r:zd:22550/zd:23198) (q:draft)
photding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will first/for the time being) (d:<phot>, first or for now, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will do it first, will do it for the time being) (j:phot/ding) (r:zd:16786/zd:20295) (q:draft)
photni = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:let us first) (d:<phot>, first or for now, written as one word with the ending <ni>, let us, placed after a verb: let us do this first, let us do it for the time being) (j:phot/ni) (r:zd:19108/zd:20845) (q:draft)
Photo = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it) (w:photo/photograph/picture) (d:a picture taken with a camera; {photo zaih} is to take a photo) (o:English) (r:zd:21365/zd:17983/zd:26163) (q:draft)
Photographer = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/work) (w:photographer) (d:a person who takes photographs; the Zolai word beside it in the articles is <manzaih>) (o:English) (r:zd:11780/zd:13293) (q:draft)
Photote = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it) (w:photos/photographs/pictures) (d:<Photo> with the plural marker <te>: photos) (b:Photo) (o:English) (r:ts:5326/ts:2438) (q:draft)
photphot = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:just/first/for now) (d:<phot> said twice, after a verb and mostly in a request: just do it, go ahead and do it for now) (b:phot) (r:zd:22474/zd:21598/zd:22473) (q:draft)
phuahbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/media) (w:compose in addition/add) (d:<phuah>, compose, with <beh>, here in addition and not clan, written as one word: write a further verse or part for a song) (j:phuah/beh) (r:zd:9226/zd:9240) (q:draft)
phuahna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:composing/composition/making up) (d:<phuah>, compose or make up, with the noun ending <na>: the composing of a song or poem; {zuau phuahna} is the making up of lies, fabrication) (b:phuah) (r:zd:9254/zd:12269) (q:draft)
phuahphat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (j:puahphat) (r:zd:25620) (q:draft, low confidence)
phuahsa = (i:2) (t:v) (f:media/religion) (w:composed/written) (d:<phuah>, compose a song or poem, with <sa>, already done: placed before <la>, song, as {ama' phuahsa la}, the song he composed, where the other sense is of a name that was given) (r:zd:9240/zd:9238/zd:9221) (q:draft)
phuahsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:compose for/name/give a name to) (d:<phuah> with <sak>, do for another: compose a tune or words for someone or for a song, or give a name to someone or something) (j:phuah/sak) (r:zd:9220/zd:17446/zd:9261) (q:draft)
phuahte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media) (w:compositions/songs composed/works) (d:<phuah.2>, compose, with plural <te>, after <la>, song, or a word such as poem: the songs or poems that someone composed, not persons who were given a name) (r:zd:9214/zd:9220/zd:9231) (q:draft)
phuaigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:maul/tear at/claw) (d:an attack on the body that leaves wounds, with <gawp>, severely: said of a bear, of stray dogs beside <pet>, bite, and of people beside <benggawp>; the exact act, clawing, tearing or pulling about, is not certain) (r:zd:19536/zd:15385) (q:draft, low confidence)
phuailum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/media) (w:maul to death) (d:of a wild animal such as a bear, attack and tear a person so that he dies; the second part is <lum>, to death) (r:zd:19536) (q:draft, low confidence)
Phuaizang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:social) (w:Phuaizang) (d:a village of the <Guite> clan in the <Tedim> area, named in the history of the Sukte chiefs) (r:ts:301/zd:20584) (q:draft)
phuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:name/call/give a name) (d:give a name to a child, a place or a thing, with <min>, name) (s:phuah)
phuaka = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/religion) (w:compose) (d:<phuak>, compose a song, and the linking <a> written as one word: composed, and then) (j:phuak/a) (r:zd:9224/zd:9255/zd:9257) (q:draft)
phuakin = (i:2) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:composing/making up) (d:<phuak>, here compose or make up, with the linking ending <in>: composing a song after <la>, or making up a lie after <zuau>, and then going on to the next action) (r:zd:23556/zd:19255/zd:9219) (q:draft)
phuaknu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:composer/author/writer) (d:<phuak>, compose, with <nu>, woman: the woman who composed a song or its words; {la phuaknu} is the woman who wrote a song) (b:phuak) (r:zd:9260/zd:9220) (q:draft)
phuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:composer/author/writer) (d:<phuak>, compose, with <pa>, man: the man who composed a song, its words or its tune; {la phuakpa} is the writer of a song) (b:phuak) (r:zd:9245/zd:9244) (q:draft)
phuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:compose for/make up for) (d:<phuak>, compose or name, and <sak>, do for someone, written as one word: compose a song, a tune or words for another person, or give a name to someone) (j:phuak/sak) (r:zd:9224/zd:24852) (q:draft)
phuaksiam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:skilled composer/gifted writer) (d:<phuak>, compose, and <siam>, skilled, written as one word: a person good at composing songs or tunes, as in {la phuaksiam}) (j:phuak/siam) (r:zd:9223/zd:9241) (q:draft)
phuakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:composers/authors/makers) (d:<phuak>, compose or make up, and the plural <te> written as one word: those who compose a song or coin a word, or who make up a story; {la phuakte} is the writer or writers of a song) (j:phuak/te) (r:zd:25475/zd:25580) (q:draft)
phual = (i:3) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:lump/bump/pimple) (d:a small raised spot or lump that comes out on the skin or in the flesh, said with <po>, come out, as in {a phual hong po}) (r:zd:20926) (q:draft, low confidence)
phualsatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:camp/encampment/military camp/base) (d:<phualsat>, set up camp, with the noun suffix <na>: the place where troops are stationed, a military camp or post) (b:phualsat) (r:ts:3446/ts:4653/ts:9033) (q:draft)
phualteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:site/scene/place) (d:<phual>, site, and <teng>, all, written as one word: the whole place where something is or happened, usually followed by <ah>) (j:phual/teng) (r:zd:16942/zd:12293) (q:draft, low confidence)
Phualva = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:hornbill) (d:the hornbill, a large forest bird taken as an emblem of the Zomi; in most articles part of the name Phualva Lungtuak Media) (r:zd:20800) (q:draft)
Phualva Lungtuak = (i:1) (t:name) (f:media) (w:Phualva Lungtuak) (d:<Phualva>, hornbill, and <lungtuak>, be of one mind: name of a Zomi news group, mostly as {Phualva Lungtuak Media}, given as the source or the translator at the head or foot of an article) (r:zd:20078/zd:20464) (q:draft)
phuangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:initiate/set up/launch/bring forth) (d:<phuang>, start, with <khia>, out: set something new going, such as a committee, a plan or a teaching) (s:phuankhia) (b:phuang) (r:zd:21040/zd:17060) (q:draft)
phuangkhiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:founder/initiator/pioneer) (d:<phuangkhia>, start something new, and <pa>, man, written as one word: the man who first set something going) (j:phuangkhia/pa) (r:zd:9253) (q:draft)
phuanin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:found/set up/establish) (d:<phuan>, set up, and <in> written as one word: setting up a committee, school or organisation, and then doing what follows) (j:phuan/in) (r:zd:24595/ts:6945) (q:draft)
phuankhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:found/establish/set up) (d:<phuan>, set up, with <khia>, out: start an organisation, a company or a church; {a phuankhia pa} is the founder) (r:zd:21720/zd:14531/zd:25447) (q:draft)
phuankhiapa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:founder) (d:<phuankhia>, found or set up, with <pa> for a male person: the man who founded an organisation, a company or a movement) (r:zd:9257/zd:24957/zd:17577) (q:draft)
phuanpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:set up at once/form immediately) (d:<phuan>, set up, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: set up a commission or committee straight away) (j:phuan/pah) (r:zd:19860) (q:draft)
phuat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:found/establish/set up) (d:found an organisation such as a church, a party or an armed group) (b:phuan) (r:zd:12337/zd:25562) (q:draft)
phuba = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:revenge/vengeance) (d:a wrong that is to be paid back; {phuba la} is take revenge) (s:phu) (r:zd:20116/zd:9124) (q:draft)
phuhkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:establish/found/set up) (d:<phuh>, found, with <khiat>, out: bring an organisation, a committee or a state into being; the form used before <ding> and <uh>) (r:ts:4823/ts:7820/zd:25020) (q:draft)
phuhkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:establishment/founding/setting up) (d:the bringing into being of a state, a country or an organisation) (b:phuhkhiat) (r:ts:3307/zd:25026) (q:draft)
phuisam = (i:2) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:chant an invocation/invoke/intone a ritual prayer) (d:in the old Zomi religion, of a <siampi> or an elder: chant the ritual words over an offering, often while spraying <zu>, to ask the spirits for a favour; a request for blessing, not a curse on someone) (r:ts:3375/zd:23394/zd:21141) (q:draft)
phuisamna = (i:3) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:incantation/spell/chant) (d:words recited by a priest in the old spirit worship, or in another religion, to drive out spirits or to dedicate something; a ritual formula, not a curse spoken against a person) (r:zd:15772/zd:19166/zd:22873) (q:draft)
phuitong = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:cherry/cherry tree) (d:a tree of the Chin hills that blossoms in December, and its fruit; {phuitong pak} is cherry blossom and {phuitong gah} is the cherry fruit; Phuitong is also the name of a village) (r:zd:11400/zd:24276) (q:draft)
Phuket = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Phuket) (d:island and province in the south of Thailand, visited by many tourists) (r:zd:17239/zd:14869) (q:draft)
phukhagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:crash badly/smash into/pile up) (d:<phukha> and <gawp> written as one word: strike against with great damage; {ki phukhagawp}, of vehicles, is crash into one another) (j:phukha/gawp) (r:zd:15613/zd:12967/zd:20353) (q:draft)
phul = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:brave/face/push through) (d:go straight at a hardship or an obstacle and force a way through it, as in {haksatna phul}; {phul khak} is run into, come up against) (r:zd:22736/zd:23835) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:ram into/plough into) (d:drive a vehicle with force into a crowd of people; the second part is <gawp>, violently) (r:zd:11470/zd:13061) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulkhagawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:crash into/plough into/smash into) (d:<phul>, push straight into, with <khagawp>, hit hard, written as one word: of a vehicle, run hard into other vehicles or people) (j:phul/khagawp) (r:zd:17100/zd:17560/zd:14781) (q:draft)
phulkhia = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:well up/spring up/pour out) (d:of thoughts, words, wisdom or joy, come up freely from within a person as water gushes from the ground, often after {lungsim tawng pan} or {sung pan}, from within) (r:zd:21037/zd:16415/zd:24119) (q:draft)
phulna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/health) (w:outbreak/springing up) (d:<phul>, gush out or spring up, with the noun suffix <na>: the springing up or breaking out of something; {phulna mun} is the place where a disease breaks out) (b:phul) (r:zd:24609/zd:24453) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:plough through/ram through) (d:of a vehicle, drive into and across a crowd or a place; from one headline that is repeated) (r:zd:11691) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulpheigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:plough into/ram into/run down) (d:of a vehicle or its driver, drive straight into and through people who are in the way; the ending <gawp> shows that the act is violent and does great harm) (r:zd:12955/zd:12559) (q:draft)
phulum = (i:1) (t:n) (c:animal) (f:nature) (w:winged termite/flying termite) (d:an insect that swarms up out of the ground and flies high; the proverb {phulum phulna dingin leikha in petlet} says that it bursts out only because the <leikha> under the ground bites it; which insect is meant is not certain) (r:zd:11024/zd:24688) (q:draft, low confidence)
phulum = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:ram to death/run down and kill) (d:<phu>, drive straight into, with <lum>, lie down, here to death, written as one word: kill by driving into) (r:zd:10855) (q:draft, low confidence)
phumna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:burial/burying/immersion) (d:<phum>, bury or immerse, with the noun suffix <na>: the putting of a body or a thing into the ground, {suang phumna} the setting of a stone, or immersion in water) (b:phum) (r:zd:25908/ts:3179) (q:draft)
phumzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:after burying/be able to bury) (d:<phum>, bury, and <zawh> written as one word: with a time after it, after being buried; before <kei>, not be able to bury) (j:phum/zawh) (r:zd:12277/zd:17335) (q:draft)
phung = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/family) (w:clan/family/lineage) (d:the family line a person belongs to) (s:beh) (q:draft)
phung = (i:3) (t:n) (f:everyday/religion) (w:foot/base) (d:the lower end on which an upright thing stands, as in {singlamteh phung}, the foot of the cross; not the clan and not a wall) (s:bul) (r:zd:23936) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:dare to face/dare to take on) (d:<phu>, press against, and <ngam>, dare, written as one word: have the courage to meet a hard thing head on) (j:phu/ngam) (r:zd:9451/zd:21908) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungcing = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/family) (w:well established/flourishing/thriving) (d:of a family line, a church or an organisation: strong, firmly rooted and with many members) (r:zd:26310/zd:19676) (q:draft, low confidence)
phungpha = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature/social) (w:flourishing/thriving/prolific) (d:of a plant, growing in a full clump with many shoots; of a family, a people or an organisation, growing in number and doing well) (r:zd:24176/zd:12166/zd:23343) (q:draft)
phungpi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:centre/root/main body/heart) (d:the main stem from which the rest grows: the home or centre of a people or an empire, the parent body of several organizations, the root of a trouble; paired with <bulpi> in {a phungpi leh a bulpi}) (r:zd:25573/zd:25094/zd:20125) (q:draft)
phungvuh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:nurture/foster/support/build up) (d:care for a person, a group or a gift so that it grows and stands firm; said of a church, a party, a people or a talent. The literal sense, heaping earth around the foot of a plant, is not attested in the articles) (r:zd:25172/zd:24003/zd:24381) (q:draft, literal sense to be confirmed)
phungvuhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/work) (w:nurturing/fostering/building up/support) (d:<phungvuh>, nurture, with the noun suffix {-na}: the act of caring for a people, a group or a heritage so that it grows; writers gloss it as investment and capacity building) (b:phungvuh) (r:zd:25628/zd:21544) (q:draft)
phungzi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:Buddhist monk/monk) (d:a Buddhist monk; {phungzi sang} is a monastery, and the word is also used for a Christian monk) (o:Burmese, hpongyi) (r:zd:23113/ts:2189/ts:1657) (q:draft)
phungzipa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:monk/Buddhist monk) (d:<phungzi>, monk, with {-pa}, the male person: the monk, one particular monk) (b:phungzi) (r:ts:9564/zd:10743) (q:draft)
phungzite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:monks/Buddhist monks) (d:plural of <phungzi>, monk; {lutol phungzite} are the shaven-headed monks) (b:phungzi) (r:zd:21258/zd:15859) (q:draft)
phunlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:not grumble/not complain/without complaining) (d:<phun>, grumble, and <lo>, not, written as one word; {phunlo in} is without grumbling, and {phunlo paulo in} is without complaint or a word) (j:phun/lo) (r:zd:24673/zd:20941/zd:15384) (q:draft)
phunpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:complain at once/protest at once) (d:<phun>, grumble, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: react at once with complaints, often followed by <ngeingai>) (j:phun/pah) (r:zd:12151/zd:15362) (q:draft)
phunphunthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:tend to grumble/may complain) (d:<phunphun>, grumble, and <thei>, able or apt, written as one word: be apt to grumble or complain) (j:phunphun/thei) (r:zd:14941) (q:draft)
phuphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:crash into/ram/run into) (d:of a vehicle or a person: drive or rush straight into something or someone and hit it, as a car hits a tree or a road divider) (r:zd:11472/zd:12974) (q:draft)
phupheigawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:ram/smash into/crash into) (d:<phuphei>, crash into, with <gawp>, violently, written as one word: drive straight into something with force) (j:phuphei/gawp) (r:zd:20767/zd:15531) (q:draft)
phupheikha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/media) (w:crash into/hit/run into) (d:<phuphei>, run into, and the particle <kha>, happen to, written as one word: happen to crash into something or someone) (j:phuphei/kha) (r:zd:13159/zd:11201) (q:draft)
phuphu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/work) (w:press for/urge persistently/push for) (d:keep pressing a person or pushing a matter until it is done, also by repeated requests to someone in authority) (r:zd:23767/zd:19166) (q:draft, low confidence)
phut = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:encounter/meet with/run into) (d:come upon a person or a difficulty without planning it, not set something up; in this meaning {phut} stands before <khak>, as in {phut khak}, happen to meet) (r:zd:21462/zd:23791) (q:draft, low confidence)
phutding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:to establish/will found/to set up) (d:<phut> and <ding> written as one word: will set up or found, in order to establish a state, a province or an organisation) (j:phut/ding) (r:zd:22293/zd:15824) (q:draft)
phutkhak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:collide/crash/run into) (d:of vehicles, after <ki> or <aki> and often with <tawh>, strike against each other in a road accident, not merely meet on the way) (r:zd:20589/zd:16731) (q:draft)
phutkhakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:collision/crash/encounter) (d:<phutkhak>, come up against, with the noun suffix <na>: a running into something, mostly of vehicles; also a meeting with hardship) (b:phutkhak) (r:zd:12569/zd:11666) (q:draft)
phutkhakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:collide with/run into) (d:<phutkhak> and <pih> written as one word: meet or strike together with something; {aki phutkhakpih mawtaw} is the car that it collided with) (j:phutkhak/pih) (r:zd:15429/zd:12105) (q:draft)
phutkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:establish/found/set up) (d:<phut>, set up, with <khia>, out, written as one word: found an organisation, a government or a country) (j:phut/khia) (r:zd:20673/ts:3289) (q:draft)
phutkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:establish/found/set up) (d:form of <phutkhia>, found or set up, used when a word such as <ding> follows; {gam phutkhiat} is to found a country) (b:phutkhia) (j:phut/khiat) (r:zd:23994/zd:25105) (q:draft)
phutphut = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:motorcycle) (d:a name once given to the motorcycle, after the sound of its engine) (r:ts:3168) (q:draft, low confidence)
phutsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to ram/try to confront) (d:<phut>, run into, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: try to run into a thing, as a gate with a car, or set out to face a hard matter) (j:phut/sawm) (r:zd:17748) (q:draft, low confidence)
phutukkha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:knock over/knock down by accident) (d:<phu>, push against, with <tuk>, fall, and <kha>, happen to: bump into something so that it falls, without meaning to) (j:phu/tuk/kha) (r:zd:14601) (q:draft, low confidence)
phuum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (j:phum) (r:zd:23754/zd:22470) (q:draft)
phuut = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:encounter/run into/face) (d:meet with something hard, come up against it; {i phuut khop} is what we face together, said beside {i thuak khop}, what we bear together) (r:zd:21517/zd:22334) (q:draft, low confidence)
Physics = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:physics) (d:the science of matter and energy, as a subject of study) (o:English) (r:zd:15845/zd:22556) (q:draft)
Phyu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Phyu) (d:town in Bago Region of Myanmar; the same word, Burmese for white, is also part of Burmese personal and place names) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:17202) (q:draft, low confidence)
pi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:grandmother) (d:grandmother, the mother of one's father or mother) (q:draft)
pi = (i:4) (t:n) (f:social) (w:Mrs/Madam) (d:title of respect written before the name of a married or older woman, the same word as grandmother used as a title) (r:ts:3168/zd:24806) (q:draft)
pi = (i:5) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:while/although/without) (d:after <lo>, not, and followed by <in>: while or although something is not so, without it; the same {pi} as in <napi>, although) (r:zd:22019/zd:22495) (q:draft)
pia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give/grant) (d:hand something over to someone or grant it; {thu pia} is give an order and <thupha pia> is bless) (a:ngah/lak)
piaciat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:each give/all give) (d:<pia> and <ciat> written as one word: every one gives, each for his part; {tha piaciat ni} is let us each give support) (j:pia/ciat) (r:zd:11064/zd:20007/zd:20446) (q:draft)
piaden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep giving/always give) (d:<pia> and <den> written as one word: give again and again, give all the time) (j:pia/den) (r:zd:21826/zd:22774) (q:draft)
piading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will give/to give) (d:<pia>, give, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will give, in order to give, to be given) (j:pia/ding) (r:zd:19249/zd:22704/zd:24331) (q:draft)
piadingin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:in order to give/to give) (d:<pia>, give, and <dingin>, in order to, written as one word: for the purpose of giving) (j:pia/dingin) (r:zd:15571/zd:17609) (q:draft)
piagiap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:give outright/grant firmly) (d:<pia> and <giap> written as one word: give something outright, without holding back; {thu piagiap} is give a firm order) (j:pia/giap) (r:zd:14812) (q:draft, low confidence)
piahi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give/grant) (d:<pia> and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: gives, gave) (j:pia/hi) (r:zd:23602/zd:21409) (q:draft)
piakbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:give more/give in addition/pay extra) (d:<piak>, give, with the ending {-beh}, in addition: give or pay something more on top of what was given) (b:piak) (r:zd:12327/zd:22448/zd:20670) (q:draft)
piakciang = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:when given/when one gives) (d:<piak>, give, and <ciang>, when, written as one word and followed by <in>: at the time when something is given) (j:piak/ciang) (r:zd:22376/zd:23590) (q:draft)
piakdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:way of giving/manner of giving) (d:<piak> and <dan> written as one word: the way something is given; {min piakdan} is the way of naming) (j:piak/dan) (r:zd:15637/zd:20576) (q:draft)
piakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to give/to be given) (d:<piak> and <ding> written as one word: will give, to be given, or what is to be given; {sum piakding} is money to be paid) (j:piak/ding) (r:zd:15571/zd:24370) (q:draft)
piakei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not give/do not give) (d:<pia>, give, and the negative <kei>, written as one word: {piakei in} and {piakei un} are do not give, {piakei ning} is I would not give) (j:pia/kei) (r:zd:20263/zd:23733) (q:draft)
piakeining = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I would not give/I will not give) (d:<piakei>, not give, and <ning>, the ending for I will, written as one word) (j:piakei/ning) (r:zd:23664) (q:draft)
piakhiakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:have given out/already hand over) (d:<piakhia> and <khin> written as one word: have already given out or handed over) (j:piakhia/khin) (r:zd:11441) (q:draft)
piakhiate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:those who give/things given) (d:<piakhia>, give out, with plural <te>: the people who give something away, or the things that are given) (b:piakhia) (j:piakhia/te) (r:zd:25572/zd:22408) (q:draft)
piakhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:donation/contribution/giving) (d:<pia>, give, with <khiatna>, the act of doing outward, written as one word: what is given out for a cause, a donation; {piakhiatna nei} is make a donation) (j:pia/khiatna) (r:zd:23439/zd:20839) (q:draft)
piakhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have given/have already given) (d:<pia> and <khinta> written as one word: has already given; with <thu>, has given an order or instruction) (j:pia/khinta) (r:zd:19018/zd:21330) (q:draft)
piakhuai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/everyday) (w:worth giving/deserving to be given) (d:<piak> and <huai> written as one word: that ought to be given, as honour or praise that someone deserves) (j:piak/huai) (r:zd:22463/zd:19523) (q:draft)
piakikding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:will give again/will give back) (d:<piakik>, give back or give again, and <ding>, will, written as one word) (j:piakik/ding) (r:zd:17504/zd:11289) (q:draft)
piakim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:give to all/give to each/give in full) (d:<pia>, give, and <kim>, every or fully, written as one word: give to every one without exception; {hong piakim ciat tahen} is may he give to each of us) (j:pia/kim) (r:zd:12134/zd:21228) (q:draft)
piakkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:happen to give/get to give) (d:<piak>, give, with <khak.2>, happen to, written as one word: come to give or have the chance to give; {piakkhak loh} is not having given) (j:piak/khak) (r:zd:20558/zd:12708) (q:draft)
piakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:give out/hand over/give away) (d:<piak>, give, and <khia>, out, written as one word: give something out or hand it over) (s:piakhia) (j:piak/khia) (r:zd:25206/zd:15902) (q:draft)
piakkhiatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:to give out/to hand over/to give up) (d:<piakkhiat>, give out, and <ding>, to, written as one word: to give away or hand over, the giving of something) (j:piakkhiat/ding) (r:zd:19400/zd:14740) (q:draft)
piakkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/social) (w:giving/generosity/donation/dedication) (d:<piakkhiat>, give out, with the noun suffix <na>: the giving away of money, goods or oneself for others or for God) (b:piakkhiat) (r:zd:24119/zd:21561/zd:18107) (q:draft)
piakkhiatte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:gifts/donations/what was given) (d:<piakkhiat>, give out, with the plural <te>: the things that have been given away, such as gifts and donations) (b:piakkhiat) (j:piakkhiat/te) (r:zd:22090/zd:25176) (q:draft)
piakkhiattheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to give out/can hand over/can release) (d:<piakkhiat>, give out, and <theih>, be able, written as one word before <ding> and <nadingin>: that can be given away or handed over) (j:piakkhiat/theih) (r:zd:24132/zd:11397) (q:draft)
piakkholh = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/social) (w:pay in advance/prepay) (d:of money, with <sum>: give it ahead of time, before the need comes, as a contribution paid beforehand to a funeral fund; not a word or command given beforehand) (r:zd:21843) (q:draft, low confidence)
piakkim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:give to all/give in full/pay in full) (d:<piak>, give, and <kim.2>, all or fully, written as one word: give to every one, or give or pay the whole of it) (j:piak/kim) (r:zd:15275/zd:25165) (q:draft)
piakkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:must give/have to pay) (d:<piak> and <kul> written as one word: it is necessary to give or to pay; with <lo>, need not pay) (j:piak/kul) (r:zd:23863/zd:25824/zd:22581) (q:draft)
piakkulding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:will have to pay/will have to give) (d:<piakkul> and <ding> written as one word: it will be necessary to pay or give) (j:piakkul/ding) (r:zd:11308/zd:19373) (q:draft)
piakkullo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:need not pay/need not give) (d:<piakkul> and <lo> written as one word: there is no need to give or to pay) (a:piakkul) (j:piakkul/lo) (r:zd:19563/zd:20197) (q:draft)
piaklai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:still give/be giving) (d:<piak>, give, and <lai>, still or while, written as one word: still to be given; before <tak>, at the very time of giving) (j:piak/lai) (r:zd:17017/zd:20035) (q:draft, low confidence)
piakleh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:if one gives/when one gives) (d:<piak>, give, with <leh>, if or when, written as one word: if or when someone gives; {thupha na piakleh} is if you bless) (j:piak/leh) (r:zd:21044/zd:17481) (q:draft)
piakloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not give) (d:<piak> and <loh> written as one word: not giving, not given; {piakloh phamawh} is must be given, and {piakloh omlo} is there is none who is not given) (j:piak/loh) (r:zd:23437/zd:21370) (q:draft)
piaklohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:not giving/failure to give) (d:<piak>, give, and <lohna>, the fact of not doing, written as one word: the fact that something is not given) (j:piak/lohna) (r:zd:23591) (q:draft)
piakna = (i:3) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:giving/presentation) (d:the act of giving, after the word for what is given: {letsong piakna} is the giving of gifts, {sisan piakna} giving blood, <thupha piakna> the giving of a blessing; not the thing that is given) (r:zd:17634/zd:24361/zd:19249) (q:draft)
piaknate = (i:2) (t:n) (f:social) (w:things given/givings) (d:plural of <piakna.3>, after the word for what is given and not an offering to God: {ngaihsut piaknate} is the suggestions or advice that people give, {niciam piaknate} the appointments that are given) (r:zd:19174/zd:22464/zd:25347) (q:draft)
piaknazong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:also the giving of) (d:<piakna> and <zong> written as one word: a giving, as of a warning, as well; {Warning piaknazong nei} is also issue a warning) (j:piakna/zong) (r:zd:20384) (q:draft)
piakngiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:give indeed/give specially) (d:<piak>, give, and <ngiat>, indeed, written as one word: what someone has truly or specially given) (j:piak/ngiat) (r:zd:11325/zd:23311) (q:draft)
piakpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep giving/give again and again) (d:doubled form of <piak>, give: go on giving, give repeatedly) (b:piak) (r:zd:23676/zd:11674) (q:draft)
piaksak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:grant/bestow/give) (d:give something to a person as a favour, where <sak> marks that the giving is for the good of the receiver and no third person is involved; mostly after <hong> in the wish {Topa'n thupha hong piaksak tahen}, may the Lord grant you blessing) (r:zd:17409/zd:15379/zd:10892) (q:draft)
piaksakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/politics) (w:will provide/to be paid/will have given) (d:<piaksak> and <ding> written as one word: will give or pay for someone, or is to be made to pay) (j:piaksak/ding) (r:zd:20543/zd:11427) (q:draft)
piaksakin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:granting/bestowing) (d:<piaksak> and the linking <in> written as one word: granting, and; mostly in the wish {Topa'n thupha hong piaksakin}, may the Lord bless you and) (j:piaksak/in) (r:zd:19430) (q:draft)
piaksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:giving/presentation/giving on behalf of) (d:<piaksak>, give for or to someone, with the noun suffix <na>: the act of handing something over, as a vote cast or a book presented) (j:piaksak/na) (r:zd:16797/zd:19552) (q:draft)
piaksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to give/offer/intend to give) (d:<piak>, give, with <sawm>, intend, written as one word: be about to give, offer or attempt to give) (j:piak/sawm) (r:zd:14701/zd:19814) (q:draft)
piaksawmlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:refuse to give/not intend to give/not be willing to give) (d:<piaksawm>, intend to give, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not mean to give or pay, withhold) (j:piaksawm/lo) (r:zd:15579/zd:13260) (q:draft)
piaksawn = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:pass on/give onward/hand on) (d:<piak> and <sawn> written as one word: give on to others what one has received) (s:gensawn) (j:piak/sawn) (r:zd:21943/zd:9435) (q:draft)
piaktak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:deserve to be given/be due/ought to give) (d:<piak>, give, with <tak> in the sense of worthy: fit or right to be given, as credit, a blessing or a price) (j:piak/tak) (r:zd:26444/zd:22159) (q:draft)
pial = (i:2) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:go out/step outside/go beyond) (d:after <pua>, outside, as in {kong pua pial}, go out of the door, and {gam pua pial}, go out of the country: go out past a boundary, with no thought of going wrong) (r:zd:21117/ts:7876) (q:draft, low confidence)
pialai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:give more/give in addition/also give) (d:<pia>, give, with the ending {-lai}, still or further: give something more, give as well) (b:pia) (r:zd:23136/zd:21590/zd:20587) (q:draft)
pialo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:not give/not provide/withhold) (d:<pia> and <lo> written as one word: does not give; in job notices {an pialo} means that food is not provided) (j:pia/lo) (r:zd:20577/zd:12336) (q:draft)
pialphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:swerve across/veer over/cut across) (d:<pial.1>, turn aside, and <phei>, across, written as one word: of a vehicle, leave its line and go across to the side or in front of another) (j:pial/phei) (r:zd:14899/zd:17952) (q:draft)
pian = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:somewhat/rather/a little/seemingly) (d:after a verb or adjective, softens the statement: it is so to some degree or seems to be so, as in {hi zaw pian hi}, it is rather so; not birth and not a likeness of a thing) (r:zd:18927/zd:15474/zd:25222) (q:draft)
pianawnlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:no longer give/not give any more) (d:<pia>, give, and <nawnlo>, no longer, written as one word: stop giving or issuing something; after <ki> be no longer given) (j:pia/nawnlo) (r:zd:11587/zd:17097) (q:draft)
pianawnloding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will no longer give/will not be given any more) (d:<pianawnlo>, no longer give, and <ding> written as one word: will stop giving; after <ki>, will no longer be given) (j:pianawnlo/ding) (r:zd:19191/zd:11587) (q:draft)
piancil = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:first come into being/originate/begin) (d:used as a verb, mostly after <hong>: come into being for the first time, said of a country, a group or an event; sense 1 is the noun for that time) (r:zd:25020/zd:23057) (q:draft, low confidence)
Piancit = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:France) (d:France, in a name taken from Burmese; {Piancit pai} is the going of Zomi men to France in 1917, remembered at its hundredth year in 2017) (o:Burmese, pyinthit) (r:zd:11549/zd:18086) (q:draft)
piandang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:unusual/strange/peculiar/different) (d:<pian>, form or appearance, with <dang>, other: of another kind than the usual, out of the ordinary) (r:zd:23298/zd:25094) (q:draft)
pianga = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:arise and/come about and/be born and) (d:<piang> and the linking <a> written as one word: something comes about or is born, and the sentence goes on) (j:piang/a) (r:zd:19193/zd:21605/zd:11135) (q:draft)
piangam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:dare to give/be willing to give) (d:<pia>, give, and <ngam>, dare, written as one word) (j:pia/ngam) (r:zd:25203/zd:20964) (q:draft, low confidence)
piangden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep happening/happen all the time) (d:<piang>, happen, and <den>, always, written as one word) (j:piang/den) (r:zd:12264/zd:17110) (q:draft)
piangding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will happen/will come about) (d:<piang>, happen or come into being, and <ding>, will, written as one word) (j:piang/ding) (r:zd:20355/zd:23832) (q:draft)
pianggawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (w:break out/erupt/happen violently) (d:<piang> happen with <gawp>, which shows that the action is severe, written as one word: of trouble, a fight or an accident, break out) (j:piang/gawp) (r:zd:15937/zd:16225/zd:13330) (q:draft)
pianghen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (w:let there be/let it come into being) (d:<piang>, come into being, and <hen.1>, let, written as one word: the word of command by which God creates) (j:piang/hen) (r:zd:19816) (q:draft)
pianghi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen/occur/arise) (d:<piang> and the sentence ending <hi> written as one word: it happens or happened, it comes about) (j:piang/hi) (r:zd:17848/zd:19562/zd:21323) (q:draft)
pianghiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:happen) (d:<piang> and the question particle <hiam> written as one word, at the end of a question: did it happen; {banghang in pianghiam} is why it happened) (j:piang/hiam) (r:zd:14738/zd:15535) (q:draft)
piangkhawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:family/everyday) (w:be born together/arise together/coincide) (d:<piang>, be born or come about, and <khawm>, together, written as one word: be born of the same parents or at the same time, come into being together) (j:piang/khawm) (r:zd:21096/zd:21458) (q:draft)
piangkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:emergence/origin/coming into being) (d:<piangkhia>, arise, with the noun suffix {-na}: the coming into being of a person, a group or a thing; with <ding>, so that it may arise) (b:piangkhia) (r:ts:11162/zd:16593) (q:draft)
piangkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/time) (w:have happened/have already occurred) (d:<piang>, happen, and <khin>, already, written as one word: have already happened or come about, often after a count of cases) (j:piang/khin) (r:zd:19662/zd:11715/zd:20682) (q:draft)
piangkhinsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/everyday) (w:already happened/past) (d:<piang>, happen, and <khinsa>, already, written as one word, mostly as {a piangkhinsa} before <thu>: what has already taken place) (j:piang/khinsa) (r:zd:21869/zd:21876) (q:draft)
piangleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if it happens/if it comes about) (d:<piang>, happen, and <leh>, if, written as one word, mostly after <hong>: if it happens, if it comes into being) (j:piang/leh) (r:zd:19943/zd:20195) (q:draft)
piangleuleu = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:happen again/occur again) (d:<piang>, happen, and <leuleu>, again, written as one word) (j:piang/leuleu) (r:zd:15292/zd:20023) (q:draft)
pianglo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not happen/not come about/not arise) (d:<piang>, come into being or happen, with <lo>, not, written as one word) (j:piang/lo) (r:zd:12337/zd:22140/zd:21050) (q:draft)
