piangta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have come about/have arisen/have happened) (d:<piang>, come into being, and <ta>, now or already, written as one word: has now come about) (j:piang/ta) (r:zd:21974) (q:draft)
piangte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:events/happenings/occurrences) (d:after <thu> or a word such as <lamdang>, the things that have happened: {thu piangte} are events and {na lamdang piangte} are wonders that took place, not the produce of field or sea) (r:zd:9139/zd:24119/zd:20454) (q:draft)
