pilding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/everyday) (w:to be wise/will be wise) (d:<pil> and <ding> written as one word: to be wise, that one should become wise or learned) (j:pil/ding) (r:zd:20997) (q:draft)
pileh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family) (w:grandmother and) (d:<pi>, grandmother, and <leh>, and, written as one word: {pileh pu} is grandmothers and grandfathers, the forefathers; in {omlo pileh} it is instead <pi> as in {lo pi}, without, joined to <leh>) (j:pi/leh) (r:zd:18081) (q:draft, low confidence)
pilepu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:grandparents/elders) (d:<pi>, <le> and <pu> written as one word: grandmother and grandfather, the old people; {khangham pilepu} is the elderly) (j:pi/le/pu) (r:zd:20997/zd:24649) (q:draft)
pillo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:education/everyday) (w:unwise/uneducated/not clever) (d:<pil>, wise or learned, and <lo>, not, written as one word; {a pillo zawte} is those who are less learned) (j:pil/lo) (r:zd:21661/zd:23780) (q:draft)
pilmahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:education/everyday) (w:very wise/very clever/very learned) (d:<pil>, wise or learned, and <mahmah>, very, written as one word) (j:pil/mahmah) (r:zd:19166/zd:25054) (q:draft)
pilna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/learning/schooling) (d:what is learned at school or college, a present-day use beside wisdom: with <sin>, learn, <pilna sin> is study or get an education, and <pilna siamna> is education and skills) (r:zd:20572/zd:21042/zd:22278) (q:draft)
pilna sangpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:higher education/advanced learning) (d:<pilna>, knowledge, and <sangpi>, very high: learning of a high level, such as a university education; the object of <nei>, have, <sin>, study, or <zo>, complete) (r:zd:11571/zd:10725) (q:draft)
pilna siamna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:knowledge and skill/learning/education) (d:<pilna>, knowledge, and <siamna>, skill, said together as one thing without <leh>: learning, what a person knows and is able to do) (r:zd:21120/zd:20979) (q:draft)
pilna sin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:study/get an education/go to school) (d:<pilna>, knowledge, and <sin>, learn: the usual expression for being at school or university, to study; the place stands before it with <ah>) (r:zd:9250/zd:11163/zd:16779) (q:draft)
pilna sinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/schooling/study) (d:<pilna>, knowledge, and <sinna>, learning: the gaining of knowledge by study, education in general) (r:zd:23590/zd:24252/zd:21780) (q:draft)
pilnanei = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:educated person/learned person) (d:<pilna>, education, and <nei>, have, written as one word: one who has education; after a profession, a qualified one) (j:pilna/nei) (r:zd:18128/zd:11438) (q:draft)
pilnuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:want to be wise/want to be educated) (d:<pil> and <nuam>, want, written as one word: wish to become wise or learned) (j:pil/nuam) (r:zd:16297) (q:draft)
Pilot = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/work) (w:pilot) (d:the person who flies an aircraft, in Zolai <vanlenghawl>, often written beside it) (s:vanlenghawl) (o:English) (r:zd:20680/zd:20248/zd:17846) (q:draft)
pilsa = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:education) (w:already wise/already educated) (d:<pil>, wise, with <sa>, already: wise or learned from the start or by now; {a pilsa a suak} is one born already wise) (b:pil) (r:zd:23554/zd:24303) (q:draft)
pilsin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:study/learn/pursue education) (d:<pil>, wise, with <sin>, learn: study in order to gain knowledge, go through schooling; {pilsin na}, also written <pilsinna>, is education) (r:zd:16245/zd:16457/zd:20443) (q:draft)
pilsinna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:education/learning/study) (d:<pil>, learned, with <sinna>, learning: schooling and study, and after a subject a field of study) (r:zd:22341/zd:16245/zd:12778) (q:draft)
piltawmsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/education) (w:make wise) (d:<pil>, wise, and <tawmsak> written as one word: make someone who is not wise wise, beside {siamtawmsak}, make skilled) (j:pil/tawmsak) (r:zd:21939/zd:23551) (q:draft, low confidence)
pilthei = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:education) (w:clever/able to learn) (d:<pil>, wise or learned, and <thei>, able, written as one word: able to be wise, clever) (j:pil/thei) (r:zd:19897) (q:draft, low confidence)
