puahphading = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/travel) (w:will repair/will restore) (d:<puahpha>, repair, with <ding>, will, written as one word: will repair; with <ki>, will be repaired) (j:puahpha/ding) (r:zd:10968/zd:16735) (q:draft)
puahphakik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:repair again/restore again/put right again) (d:<puahpha>, repair, and <kik>, again, written as one word; with <ki> before it, be repaired or put right again) (j:puahpha/kik) (r:zd:20749/zd:15205) (q:draft)
puahphatding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/home) (w:to be repaired/to repair) (d:<puahphat>, repair, and <ding> written as one word: that is to be repaired or improved, the repairing still to be done) (j:puahphat/ding) (r:zd:14665/zd:15968) (q:draft)
puahpuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:keep repairing/tend/dress up) (d:<puah> doubled: go on mending, improving or dressing something up) (b:puah) (r:zd:22444/ts:3125) (q:draft, low confidence)
puahsiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/home) (w:maintain well/take good care of/groom well) (d:<puah>, repair or put in order, and <siam>, skilled, written as one word: know how to keep something in good order, often said beside <kepsiam> or <kemsiam>) (j:puah/siam) (r:zd:17309/zd:19663) (q:draft)
puahtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:be able to amend/be able to correct) (d:<puah>, amend or put right, and <theih>, be able, written as one word: that can be amended or put right, of laws and of behaviour) (j:puah/theih) (r:zd:23476) (q:draft)
puahzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:way of repairing/way of maintaining) (d:<puah>, repair or tend, with <zia>, way: how something is repaired or kept in good order) (b:puah) (r:zd:19676/zd:23929) (q:draft)
puahzoleng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:if we can repair/if we can tend) (d:<puah> and <zoleng> written as one word: if we manage to repair or put in order) (j:puah/zoleng) (r:zd:17692) (q:draft)
puai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (w:match/game/show) (d:one match of a sports competition; also a show or festival, the Burmese word for <pawi>) (o:Burmese, pwe) (r:zd:22260/zd:25253) (q:draft)
puain = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:carrying/bearing) (d:<pua>, carry, and <in>, the linking word after a verb, written as one word: carrying, and then) (j:pua/in) (r:zd:15417/zd:24119) (q:draft)
puaisa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:agent/broker/middleman) (d:a person paid to arrange documents, work or travel for others, also one who brings people across a border) (o:Burmese, pwe sa) (r:zd:16720/zd:16805) (q:draft)
puak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:send/bring/deliver) (d:send or bring something to someone; {thu puak} is send word) (s:sawl) (q:draft)
puak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:explode/go off/burst) (d:of a bomb or shell: go off, burst with a blast, as in {bomb puak}; the same as <puakkham>, and unlike the senses carry and send) (s:puakkham) (r:zd:15545) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakawikawi = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:carry around/carry about) (d:<pua>, carry, and <kawikawi>, about, written as one word: carry a thing along from place to place; of an insect, carry a disease around) (j:pua/kawikawi) (r:zd:13346/zd:11457) (q:draft)
puakawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:while carrying/carrying along) (d:<pua>, carry, and <kawm>, while, written as one word: while carrying or having with one, followed by <in> and another action) (j:pua/kawm) (r:zd:19116/zd:17694) (q:draft)
puakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:to be sent/to send/to carry) (d:<puak>, send or carry, with <ding> written as one word: will be sent or taken to a place, and something that is to be carried or taken) (j:puak/ding) (r:zd:11568/zd:11874/zd:24234) (q:draft)
puakdingin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel/everyday) (w:in order to deliver/to send/to take to) (d:<puak> and <dingin> written as one word: in order to send, deliver or take something or someone to a place) (j:puak/dingin) (r:zd:11271/zd:19878) (q:draft)
puakkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to carry/bring along) (d:<puak>, carry or bring, with <khak>, happen to: have a thing on oneself or bring it along, also without meaning to) (j:puak/khak) (r:zd:17501/zd:13151) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakkham = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:explode/blow up/erupt) (d:go off with a blast, said of a bomb, a gas cylinder or a vehicle, and with <meimual>, of a volcano erupting; the present-day use beside burst open) (r:zd:14523/zd:19786/zd:17239) (q:draft)
puakkhamding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/media) (w:will erupt/will explode) (d:<puakkham>, burst, and <ding> written as one word: will erupt or explode, of a volcano, a bomb or a gas tank) (j:puakkham/ding) (r:zd:15382/zd:16304) (q:draft)
puakkhamkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature/everyday) (w:erupt again/explode again) (d:<puakkham>, burst, and <kik>, again, written as one word: of a volcano, erupt again; of a blast, go off once more) (j:puakkham/kik) (r:zd:12161/zd:12496) (q:draft)
puakkhamngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/nature) (w:have exploded before/have erupted before) (d:<puakkham>, explode or erupt, and <ngei>, have ever, written as one word: it has blown up once before) (j:puakkham/ngei) (r:zd:20023/zd:20428) (q:draft)
puakkhampen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:the explosion) (d:<puakkham>, burst or explode, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the explosion, as the thing spoken about) (j:puakkham/pen) (r:zd:20668/zd:12651) (q:draft)
puakkhamsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/everyday) (w:detonate/blow up/set off/explode) (d:<puakkham>, burst, with the causative <sak>: make something explode, as a bomb or firecrackers; {ki puakkhamsak} is blow oneself up or be blown up) (b:puakkham) (r:zd:13236/zd:14834) (q:draft)
puakkhamte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:those that erupt) (d:<puakkham>, burst, with the plural <te>: the ones that burst out; {meimual puakkhamte} are volcanoes that erupt, active volcanoes) (j:puakkham/te) (r:zd:20582) (q:draft)
puakkhamthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can explode/be liable to explode) (d:<puakkham>, burst or explode, and <thei>, able, written as one word) (j:puakkham/thei) (r:zd:15382/zd:11764) (q:draft)
puakkhamzai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:explode/blow up) (d:<puakkham>, burst, with an expressive ending for suddenness: go off suddenly with a blast, said of a gas cylinder, a tanker or a bomb) (b:puakkham) (r:zd:16137/zd:19480) (q:draft)
puakkhap = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/nature) (w:explode/blow up/erupt) (d:form of <puakkham>, burst, used before endings such as <ciangin>, <hangin> and {-na}: explode, said of a bomb or an aircraft, and of a volcano erupt) (b:puakkham) (r:zd:22658/ts:10764/zd:17733) (q:draft)
puakkhapna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/nature) (w:explosion/eruption/blast) (d:the bursting of a bomb or the eruption of a volcano, from <puakkhap>, explode, with the noun suffix {-na}; compare <puakkham>) (r:zd:19786/zd:19546/zd:11776) (q:draft)
puakkhiat = (i:2) (t:v) (f:work/travel) (w:send out/export/send abroad) (d:send goods, papers or workers out of a country to another, often after <gamdang> or <gampua>; not of captives or of the dead) (r:zd:22470/zd:19631) (q:draft)
puakkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:have sent/have delivered/have taken to) (d:<puak> and <khin> written as one word: have already sent or brought someone or something to a place) (j:puak/khin) (r:zd:12945/ts:5469) (q:draft)
puakkhinta = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:have already been taken/already sent) (d:<puak> and <khinta> written as one word: already carried or sent; {zato ah naki puakkhinta} is had already been taken to hospital) (j:puak/khinta) (r:zd:12261/zd:12517) (q:draft)
puakkhop = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:send together/submit together) (d:<puak>, send, with <khop>, together: send or hand in one thing along with another, after <tawh>, with; not the load of {puakkhop}, as much as can be carried) (r:zd:23749) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakkikding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/travel) (w:will be sent back/to send back/to be deported) (d:<puakkik> and <ding> written as one word: is to be sent back; in the news, of people who are to be returned to their own country) (j:puakkik/ding) (r:zd:14599/zd:20850) (q:draft)
puakkiksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/travel) (w:send back/deport/have returned) (d:<puak>, send, and <kiksak>, cause to go back, written as one word: have a person sent back to the country he came from) (j:puak/kiksak) (r:zd:20850/zd:20416) (q:draft)
puakkiksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/travel) (w:plan to send back/intend to deport) (d:<puakkik> and <sawm> written as one word: intend to send people back to where they came from) (j:puakkik/sawm) (r:zd:16099) (q:draft)
puakkul = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:need to carry/have to bring/have to send) (d:<puak>, carry or send, and <kul>, must, written as one word: it is necessary to carry, bring or send) (j:puak/kul) (r:zd:20486/zd:23822) (q:draft)
puaklah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/health) (w:hard to bear/burdensome) (d:from <puak>, carry, said of a burden or trouble that is hard to bear; paired with <thuaklah>, hard to endure) (r:zd:25223/zd:21745) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not carry/not send) (d:<puak>, carry or send, and the negative <loh> written as one word: {puakloh phamawh} is it must be carried or sent, and {puakloh hang} is although not carried) (j:puak/loh) (r:zd:12460) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakman = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/travel) (w:carriage/delivery charge/freight) (d:<puak>, carry or send, and <man>, price, written as one word: what is paid for carrying or sending goods) (j:puak/man) (r:zd:16425) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakman = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:bring in time) (d:<puak>, carry or bring, and <man> written as one word: manage to bring someone to a place in time) (j:puak/man) (r:zd:17547) (q:draft, low confidence)
puaknop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to send/want to bring) (d:<puak>, send or bring, and <nop>, want, written as one word) (j:puak/nop) (r:zd:22967) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakpuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep carrying/carry about) (d:<puak>, carry, said twice and written as one word: go on carrying a load, a feeling or a tale) (b:puak) (r:zd:15661/zd:16695) (q:draft)
puaksak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:detonate/explode/set off) (d:<puak>, burst or explode, with <sak>, cause: make a bomb go off; this is the meaning after <bomb>, and {bomb puaksak pa} is a bomber) (r:zd:19659/zd:15080) (q:draft)
puaksakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:will send/will be delivered) (d:<puaksak>, have carried or sent, and <ding>, will, written as one word: will send on, will be delivered) (j:puaksak/ding) (r:zd:18024/zd:13165) (q:draft)
puaksakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:send at once/take immediately/have taken at once) (d:<puak>, send or bring, and <sakpah>, cause at once, written as one word: have someone taken somewhere straight away, usually to a hospital) (j:puak/sakpah) (r:zd:20215/zd:20177) (q:draft)
puaksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:try to carry/attempt to take along/intend to transport) (d:<puak>, carry or send, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: set out or try to carry or take something or someone somewhere) (j:puak/sawm) (r:zd:15911/zd:15560) (q:draft)
puaksawnding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/work) (w:will be passed on/will be transferred/will forward) (d:<puaksawn> and <ding> written as one word: will pass on or send on; with <ki> before it, will be transferred, as a case to a higher court) (j:puaksawn/ding) (r:zd:11540/zd:12741) (q:draft)
puaksuakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/travel) (w:send on at once/take straight to/rush to) (d:<puak>, send or take, with <suak>, on, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: take or send a person straight on to a place without delay, mostly to a hospital) (j:puak/suak/pah) (r:zd:12468/zd:11585) (q:draft)
puakte = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:bearers/carriers/those who bring) (d:<puak>, carry, with the plural <te> for people: those who carry or bring what is named before {puakte}, not the things that are brought) (r:zd:9435/zd:23156) (q:draft)
puakteng = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:all that is carried/everything brought) (d:<puak>, carry or bring, and <teng>, all, written as one word after a noun: all of that thing which someone carries or has brought) (j:puak/teng) (r:zd:19166/zd:15913) (q:draft)
puakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:can send/can deliver/be able to send) (d:<puak>, send or deliver, and <thei>, able, written as one word: be able to send or deliver; {hong puakthei} is can send here, can send back) (j:puak/thei) (r:zd:17822/zd:24641) (q:draft)
puaktheiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:will be able to send/can deliver) (d:<puak>, send, and <theiding> written as one word: will be able to send or deliver) (j:puak/theiding) (r:zd:11198/zd:10936) (q:draft)
puakto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:send up/forward/submit) (d:<puak>, send, and <to>, up, written as one word: send people, money or goods up to a place, and pass a matter or a name up to a higher body) (j:puak/to) (r:ts:12263/zd:25183) (q:draft)
puakzah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:load/carrying capacity/amount carried) (d:<puak>, carry, and <zah>, amount, written as one word: as much as one carries or is able to carry) (j:puak/zah) (r:zd:16871/zd:24142) (q:draft)
puakzia = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/work) (w:way of sending/way of carrying) (d:the plain meaning without <lungsim> before it: the manner in which goods or money are carried or sent) (r:zd:21551) (q:draft, low confidence)
puakziate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:attitudes/mindsets/dispositions) (d:<puakzia> with the plural <te>, mostly in {lungsim puakziate}, attitudes of mind) (b:puakzia) (r:zd:24149/zd:19174) (q:draft)
puakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:be able to send/manage to send) (d:<puak>, send, and <zo>, be able to, written as one word: be able to send something, such as money for relief) (j:puak/zo) (r:zd:14746) (q:draft, low confidence)
pualah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:be unable to bear/be overburdened) (d:find a load too heavy to carry, built on <pua>, carry, like <thuaklah> on <thuak>; said of the mind weighed down by too much to do) (r:zd:17152/zd:17021) (q:draft, low confidence)
puam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/everyday) (w:identity/form) (d:second word of a pair: {min le puam} is a person's name and identity, {mel leh puam} looks and build) (r:zd:24750/zd:21845) (q:draft, low confidence)
puam = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:body/everyday) (w:bulging/swollen/convex) (d:rounded outward; said of cheeks full of food and of a sulking face) (r:zd:24310) (q:draft, low confidence)
puan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:clothes/clothing/cloth) (d:cloth, or anything made of cloth to wear; many words for garments are built on it, such as <puanak>, <puanpi> and <puanbuk>) (s:nikten) (q:draft)
puanak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:shirt/coat) (d:garment worn on the upper body) (q:draft)
puanbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:home/religion) (w:like a garment/as clothing) (d:<puan> and <bang> written as one word: like a garment, a comparison used in songs and in religious writing) (j:puan/bang) (r:zd:19772) (q:draft, low confidence)
puanbawlna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:garment making/clothing manufacture) (d:<puan>, clothes, with <bawlna>, making: the making of clothes; {puanbawlna setzung} is a garment factory) (j:puan/bawlna) (r:zd:16741) (q:draft, low confidence)
Puandum = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/social) (w:puandum/traditional Zomi cloth) (d:a traditional woven cloth of the Zomi, named from <puan>, cloth, and <dum>, blue or dark; it is worn at national occasions and given as a gift of honour, and is named together with {puanlaisan}) (b:puan) (r:ts:3375/zd:10743) (q:draft)
puang = (i:2) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:declare/proclaim/announce) (d:make an order or a decision publicly known, often as {puang khia}: a government declares independence or a curfew such as {144 puang}) (r:zd:22641/ts:3284) (q:draft, low confidence)
puang = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:everyday/body) (w:pale/whitish/grey) (d:of a pale, washed-out white or grey all over, not in spots: said of light hair or eyes and of things covered with dust, often with a sound word after it as {puang phiupheu}) (r:zd:17168/ts:301/zd:19826) (q:draft)
puangkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:declare/proclaim/announce) (d:<puang>, declare, and <khia>, out, written as one word: make an order or decision publicly known) (s:tangko) (j:puang/khia) (r:ts:3284/zd:22641/ts:11162) (q:draft)
puankhaina = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:clothes hanger/clothes hook) (d:<puan>, clothes, and <khaina>, a thing to hang from, written as one word: a hanger or hook on which clothes are hung) (j:puan/khaina) (r:zd:21243) (q:draft)
puankhui = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:sewing/tailoring) (d:<puan> and <khui> written as one word: the sewing of clothes as a skill or trade; also as a verb, sew clothes) (j:puan/khui) (r:zd:23014/zd:19433) (q:draft)
puanlaaisan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/social) (j:Puanlaisan) (r:zd:11110) (q:draft)
Puanlaisan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/social) (w:traditional men's cloth) (d:a traditional Zomi woven cloth worn by men, named together with {puandum}, the cloth of women; it is also given to honour a guest) (r:zd:21102/zd:14579) (q:draft)
puanpawlkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home) (w:some clothes/some clothing) (d:<puan>, clothes, and <pawlkhat>, some, written as one word: some clothes, some pieces of clothing) (j:puan/pawlkhat) (r:zd:12676) (q:draft)
puanphona = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:clothes line/drying rack/place for drying clothes) (d:<puan>, clothes, <pho>, spread out to dry, and the noun suffix {-na}: the line, pole or rack on which washed clothes are hung to dry; {puanphona khau} is a clothes line) (r:zd:15577/zd:17884) (q:draft)
puanpi = (i:2) (t:n) (f:travel) (w:sail) (d:the large cloth of a ship that is spread to catch the wind, after <tembaw>, ship; not a garment) (s:puankhai/puanzaak) (r:zd:21145) (q:draft, low confidence)
puansawpna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home/everyday) (w:laundry/clothes washing/washing machine) (d:<puansawp>, wash clothes, with the noun ending <na>: the washing of clothes, and before a word for a shop, machine or powder the thing used for it, as {puansawpna set}, washing machine) (r:zd:20172/zd:22758/zd:22650) (q:draft)
puansawpset = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:washing machine) (d:a machine that washes clothes, from <puansawp>, wash clothes, and <set>, machine) (r:zd:16752/zd:13056) (q:draft)
puansuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/body) (w:undress/take off clothes/strip) (d:<puan>, clothes, with <suah>, bring out: take off what one wears; {galkap puansuah} is one who has put off the army uniform) (r:zd:22824/zd:24743) (q:draft)
puantawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home) (w:with a cloth/in clothes) (d:<puan>, cloth or clothes, and <tawh>, with, written as one word: with a cloth, or dressed in the clothes named before it) (j:puan/tawh) (r:zd:24276/zd:16809/zd:15935) (q:draft)
puanteen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:longyi/lungi/sarong) (d:the cloth a man wraps round the waist, named beside <niik>, the woman's skirt) (r:zd:24123/zd:21003) (q:draft)
Puanten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:longyi/sarong) (d:a length of cloth wrapped round the waist and worn as a lower garment, the longyi of Myanmar; {puanten teng} is wear a longyi; written with a capital letter mostly in lists of goods) (r:zd:23240/zd:22683/zd:17468) (q:draft)
puantuamtuam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:various clothes/different kinds of clothing) (d:<puan>, clothes, and <tuamtuam>, of various kinds, written as one word) (j:puan/tuamtuam) (r:zd:16970) (q:draft)
puantung = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home) (w:on the clothes/over the clothes) (d:<puan>, clothes, and <tung>, upon, written as one word: on the clothes; {puantung silh} is an outer garment worn over the other clothes) (j:puan/tung) (r:zd:24054/zd:17786) (q:draft)
puanza = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home) (w:blanket) (d:a thick cloth to cover oneself with when sleeping) (r:zai:blanket) (q:draft)
puanzapi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:blanket) (d:<puanza> with the ending <pi>, large: a large thick cloth to sleep under, a blanket) (s:puanza) (b:puanza) (r:zd:12803/zd:22695) (q:draft)
puanzong = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:home) (w:clothes also/even clothes) (d:<puan>, clothes, and <zong>, also, written as one word: not even clothes, when a negative follows) (j:puan/zong) (r:zd:12117/zd:15633) (q:draft)
puanzuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/home) (w:clothes shop/clothing store) (d:<puan> and <zuakna> written as one word: a place where clothes are sold, or the selling of clothes) (j:puan/zuakna) (r:zd:21829/zd:20365) (q:draft)
puaphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:carry across/carry over) (d:<pua>, carry, and <phei>, across, written as one word: carry a load or a person over to another place) (j:pua/phei) (r:zd:17501/zd:20037) (q:draft)
puapial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go out/go outside/leave the house) (d:go out of the house and about; also used as a noun, a going out) (r:zd:14992/zd:25918/zd:25045) (q:draft)
puapua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep carrying/carry on and on) (d:<pua>, carry, said twice: go on carrying, carry for a long time) (b:pua) (r:zd:20028/zd:24086) (q:draft)
Puasa = (i:1) (t:name) (f:religion) (w:Puasa/Ramadan fast) (d:the Malay name of the yearly fasting month of the Muslims) (o:Malay, puasa) (r:zd:12698) (q:draft, low confidence)
puasak = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:give a name/name/call) (d:after <min>, name: make a person or thing bear a name or title, give it that name) (r:ts:3508/zd:23090) (q:draft)
puasaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not let carry/not allow to bring) (d:<puasak>, make or let carry, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not allow someone to carry or bring a thing along) (j:puasak/lo) (r:zd:16696/zd:17501) (q:draft)
puasim = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/politics) (w:smuggle/carry secretly) (d:<pua>, carry, with <sim>, secretly: carry something hidden, smuggle drugs, liquor or other forbidden goods) (b:pua) (r:zd:18876/zd:21471) (q:draft)
puasuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:carry on/carry through) (d:<pua>, carry, and <suak>, right through, written as one word: go on carrying something all through; in notices it also stands for <pusuak>, come out) (j:pua/suak) (r:zd:23443) (q:draft, low confidence)
puasuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:carry down/bring down/take down) (d:<pua>, carry, with <suk>, downward: carry a load, or of a vehicle its passengers, down to a lower place or toward home) (b:pua) (r:zd:19112/zd:24854/zd:15743) (q:draft)
puatheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:cannot carry/may not carry) (d:<pua>, carry, and <theilo> written as one word: be unable or not allowed to carry or take along) (j:pua/theilo) (r:zd:21961/zd:11936) (q:draft)
Puchong = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Puchong) (d:a town in Selangor, Malaysia, near Kuala Lumpur, where many Zomi live and work) (r:zd:18303/zd:16660) (q:draft)
Puchung = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Puchong) (d:town in Selangor, Malaysia, near Kuala Lumpur, in English spelling Puchong) (r:zd:19320) (q:draft, low confidence)
Pudu = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Pudu) (d:a quarter of the city of Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia) (r:zd:15276) (q:draft)
puk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:fall/fall down/stumble) (d:fall down or stumble, of people, animals and things) (s:tuk/kia) (a:tho) (q:draft)
pulaak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/social) (j:pulak) (r:zd:24119/zd:21845) (q:draft)
pulaakkhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (j:pulakkhia) (r:zd:24413/zd:24750) (q:draft)
pulaakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/social) (j:pulakna) (r:zd:14864/zd:23343) (q:draft)
pulakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:will announce/to make known/to report) (d:<pulak> and <ding> written as one word: will announce, is to be made known) (j:pulak/ding) (r:zd:15928/zd:23156) (q:draft)
pulakhia = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (j:pulakkhia) (r:ts:8955) (q:draft)
pulakkhialo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:not disclose/not announce) (d:<pulakkhia>, make known, and <lo>, not, written as one word; with <ki> before it, was not disclosed, as of a name) (j:pulakkhia/lo) (r:zd:15437/zd:18161) (q:draft)
pulakkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:declare/announce/disclose/make known) (d:form of <pulakkhia> used before words such as <ciangin>, <ding> and <theihna>, and as a noun, an announcement; with <ki> before it, declare or identify oneself) (b:pulakkhia) (r:zd:21083/zd:23539/zd:16961) (q:draft)
pulakkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/politics) (w:announcement/statement/declaration) (d:<pulakkhia>, declare, with the noun suffix <na>: what is made known publicly, a statement or report issued) (s:pulakna) (b:pulakkhia) (r:zd:12007/zd:11219/zd:20824) (q:draft)
pulakkhiatna ah = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:media) (w:according to the statement of/as announced by) (d:<pulakkhiatna>, announcement, and <ah>, in: placed after the name of a source with <te>, it opens a news report and means according to what that source has stated; the sentence then ends with <cihi> or {ci uhhi}, it is said) (r:zd:19063/zd:19973) (q:draft)
pulakkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:have announced/have declared) (d:<pulak>, make known, and <khin>, already, written as one word: has already announced or reported) (j:pulak/khin) (r:zd:11383/ts:5326) (q:draft)
pulakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:announce again/announce later/report back) (d:<pulak> and <kik> written as one word: make known again, or make known in turn once more is known) (j:pulak/kik) (r:ts:4298/zd:17750) (q:draft)
pulaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:not disclose/not reveal/not announce) (d:<pulak>, make known, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not make known, withhold a name or a number) (j:pulak/lo) (r:zd:13009/zd:22864) (q:draft)
pulakna nei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/politics) (w:announce/make an announcement/issue a statement) (d:<pulakna>, announcement, and <nei>, have: make an announcement or issue a statement; what is announced stands before it, often as a clause ending in <cih>, and {pulakna nei nailo} is has not yet announced) (r:zd:11602/ts:5171/ts:6108) (q:draft)
pulakngei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media) (w:have reported/have announced) (d:<pulak> and <ngei> written as one word: has made known before, said of a news source) (j:pulak/ngei) (r:zd:19987) (q:draft)
pulakte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:things announced/those mentioned/those who disclose) (d:<pulak>, make known, with the plural <te> written as one word: the things that are announced or mentioned, or the people who make something known) (j:pulak/te) (r:zd:23792/zd:23848) (q:draft)
pulakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/media) (w:can announce/can make known/can declare) (d:<pulak>, make known, with <thei>, able, written as one word; with <ki> before it, can be announced) (j:pulak/thei) (r:zd:23156/zd:20540) (q:draft)
pulehpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (j:pulepa) (r:zd:25569/zd:20537) (q:draft)
pulna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:plague/epidemic/pestilence) (d:<pul>, plague, with the noun suffix {-na}: a deadly disease that spreads among many people, placed after its name as in {Ebola pulna}) (s:pul/pulnatna) (r:zd:24369/zd:23810) (q:draft)
pulpit = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:pulpit) (d:the raised place in a church from which the sermon is preached; {pulpit pan thu gen} is preach from the pulpit) (o:English) (r:zd:19845/zd:25711) (q:draft)
pumgup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:defend wholesale/side blindly with) (d:defend or take the side of someone in everything, without weighing right and wrong; paired with <pumhuat>, hate wholesale; from <gup>, protect) (r:zd:22580) (q:draft, low confidence)
pumhuat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:reject wholesale/oppose blindly) (d:hate or oppose a person or a group as a whole, whatever they do; from <huat>, hate, and named beside its opposite <pumgup>, defend wholesale) (a:pumgup) (r:zd:22580) (q:draft, low confidence)
pumkhatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:unity/oneness) (d:<pumkhat>, one body, with the noun suffix <na>: being united as one; mostly written {ki pumkhatna}, unity with one another) (b:pumkhat) (r:zd:20281/zd:23554) (q:draft)
pummat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/social) (w:abduct/kidnap/seize bodily) (d:take hold of a person by the body and carry the person off by force; with <ki>, be abducted) (r:zd:18061) (q:draft)
pumnial = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:deny outright/reject flatly) (d:<pum>, here wholly, with <nial>, deny: refuse to believe or accept something at all, dismiss it out of hand) (r:zd:14952) (q:draft, low confidence)
pumnialgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:reject wholesale/dismiss outright) (d:<pum>, here whole, and <nialgawp> written as one word: reject a thing entirely without looking into it) (j:pum/nialgawp) (r:zd:12264/zd:15689) (q:draft)
pump = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/work) (w:pump) (d:pump a liquid, as the heart pumps blood; also a noun in English phrases such as Petrol pump and Water Pump) (o:English) (r:zd:20778) (q:draft, low confidence)
pumpiak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:give wholly/devote/dedicate) (d:<piak>, give, with a first part meaning whole: give the whole of something; {ki pumpiak} is give oneself wholly, be devoted) (r:zd:9264/zd:23304) (q:draft)
pumpibup = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:whole body/entire body) (d:<pumpi> and <bup> written as one word: the whole of the body) (j:pumpi/bup) (r:zd:20841) (q:draft)
pumpisung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/health) (w:inside of the body/within the body) (d:<pumpi>, body, and <sung>, in, written as one word: the inside of the body, or inside the body) (j:pumpi/sung) (r:zd:20408/zd:25414) (q:draft)
pumtung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body) (w:body) (d:the body, literally on the body: what is on or belongs to the body of a person or thing) (s:pumpi) (r:zd:22557/zd:19756) (q:draft)
Pumva = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:social) (w:Pumva) (d:village of the <Sihzang> area near <Thuklai> in northern Chin State) (r:zd:15364/ts:11788) (q:draft)
pumzaw = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health) (w:paralysis/palsy) (d:loss of movement in the body or a part of it; mostly as {pumzaw natna}, the illness of paralysis, palsy or stroke) (r:zd:24082/zd:25616) (q:draft)
Pune = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/education) (w:Pune) (d:a city in western India, where a number of Zomi have studied) (r:zd:23743) (q:draft)
punishment = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:punishment/penalty) (d:English word used beside <gawtna> for a penalty laid on someone) (s:gawtna) (o:English) (r:zd:20016/zd:24322) (q:draft, low confidence)
pupate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:ancestors/forefathers) (d:<pupa> with the plural <te>: the forefathers, the people of earlier generations) (b:pupa) (r:zd:23129/zd:25250/zd:25099) (q:draft)
pupi = (i:4) (t:n) (f:social/education) (w:founder/father/originator) (d:the person with whom a movement, a party or a field of knowledge began, as {khanlawhna pupi}, the father of the revival; not an ancestor by blood) (r:zd:20224/zd:21288) (q:draft)
purpose = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:purpose/aim) (d:the English word used in Zolai sentences for what a thing or an act is meant for) (s:ngimna) (o:English) (r:ts:3366/zd:24375) (q:draft, low confidence)
pusa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:ancestral spirit) (d:the spirits of the forefathers, <pu>, to whom offerings were made in the old religion) (r:zd:14804) (q:draft, low confidence)
pusha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (j:pusa) (r:zd:9135/zd:25166) (q:draft)
pusuahding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:to go out/will go out/to leave) (d:<pusuah> and <ding> written as one word: going out or leaving that is to happen, to go out) (j:pusuah/ding) (r:zd:13320/zd:23488) (q:draft)
pusuahkhiat = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:go out/come out/leave) (d:<pusuah>, go out, and <khiat>, out, written as one word: the form of <pusuakkhia> used before another word such as <ding>, <nading> or <khit>: go out of a house, a place or a country) (b:pusuakkhia) (j:pusuah/khiat) (r:zd:11771/zd:14961) (q:draft)
pusuahkhiatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel/everyday) (w:exit/way out/going out) (d:<pusuahkhiat>, go out, with the noun ending {-na}: the act of going out of a place, or the place where one goes out, as the exit of a road or of a country) (b:pusuahkhiat) (r:zd:14537/zd:19353) (q:draft)
pusuahtheih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:be able to get out/be able to leave) (d:<pusuah>, go out, and <theih>, be able, written as one word, mostly before <nadingin>: so as to be able to get out or leave) (j:pusuah/theih) (r:zd:18303/zd:19912) (q:draft)
pusuakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:exit/way out/going out) (d:<pusuak>, go out, with the noun suffix {-na}: the place where one goes out, or the going out; {lutna pusuakna} is entrance and exit) (s:pusuahna) (a:lutna) (b:pusuak) (r:zd:24049) (q:draft)
pusuaksaklo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not let out/keep from coming out) (d:<pusuaksak>, make come out, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not let someone or something come out) (j:pusuaksak/lo) (r:zd:24276/zd:11970) (q:draft)
pusuaksakpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:bring out at once/evacuate at once) (d:<pusuaksak>, make come out, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: get people out of a place right away) (j:pusuaksak/pah) (r:zd:16774/zd:21676) (q:draft)
pusuakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:be able to get out/can come out) (d:<pusuak>, go out, and <thei>, able, written as one word) (j:pusuak/thei) (r:zd:20625/zd:10812) (q:draft)
pute = (i:2) (t:n) (f:family) (w:mother's family/maternal relatives) (d:the living family of one's <pu>, the grandfather or the mother's brother, and so the mother's or wife's side of the family and their household, as in {ka pute inn}, the house of my mother's people; not the dead forefathers) (r:zd:16148/zd:24320/zd:13076) (q:draft, low confidence)
puteekkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:an old man) (d:<puteek>, old man, and <khat>, one, written as one word: an old man, a certain old man) (j:puteek/khat) (r:zd:19178) (q:draft)
putek = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:old man) (d:an old man, <pu>, grandfather, with <tek>, here meaning old; paired with <pitek>, old woman, {pitek putek} is old people) (r:zd:24786/zd:20486) (q:draft)
putekpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:old man/elderly man) (d:<putek>, old man, with <pa>, man: an old man; the same as <puteek>, and paired with <piteknu>, old woman) (s:puteek) (r:zd:17049/zd:25433/zd:23773) (q:draft)
Putrajaya = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:politics/travel) (w:Putrajaya) (d:city south of Kuala Lumpur, the seat of the government of Malaysia) (r:zd:12553/zd:12707) (q:draft)
putu = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:grandfather and grandchild) (d:<pu>, grandfather, and <tu>, grandchild, written as one word: a grandfather with his grandchild or grandchildren, as a pair of relatives) (j:pu/tu) (r:zd:13340/zd:25173) (q:draft, low confidence)
