saisung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:shop/inside of a shop) (d:<sai>, shop, with <sung>, inside, written as one word: the inside of a shop, the shop premises; {saisung ah} is in the shop) (j:sai/sung) (r:zd:22282/zd:21659/zd:12754) (q:draft)
saisungah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:work) (w:in the shop/inside the shop) (d:<saisung>, the inside of a shop, and <ah> written as one word: in the shop) (j:saisung/ah) (r:zd:17232/zd:13145) (q:draft)
saisungteng = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:work) (w:the whole shop/all through the shop) (d:<saisung>, the inside of a shop, and <teng>, all, written as one word: the whole of the shop or of the shops) (j:saisung/teng) (r:zd:12063/zd:15276) (q:draft)
saite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:shops/stalls) (d:<sai>, shop, with the plural <te>: shops, stalls or businesses) (b:sai) (r:zd:25068/zd:16197) (q:draft)
saite = (i:2) (t:n) (f:work/politics/media) (w:department/agency/authorities) (d:<sai>, be in charge of, with the plural <te>, placed after the name of a matter: the people or offices that deal with it, as in {thuthak saite}, news agencies, and {cidamna lam saite}, the health authorities) (b:sai) (r:ts:9048/ts:12053/zd:21066) (q:draft)
saiten = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media) (w:outlets/agencies) (d:<sai>, shop, with the plural <te> and the subject marker <in> written as one word; in news writing {thuthak saiten} is the news outlets, as the subject of saying or reporting) (j:sai/te/in) (r:ts:2461/ts:3446) (q:draft, low confidence)
Saizaang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:social/travel) (j:Saizang) (r:zd:25390) (q:draft)
saizuak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:shopkeeper/stallholder/shopkeeping) (d:<sai>, shop, and <zuak>, sell, written as one word: a person who sells at a shop or stall, or the work of keeping a shop) (j:sai/zuak) (r:zd:13145/zd:14523) (q:draft)
saizuakpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:shopkeeper/seller) (d:<sai>, shop, and <zuakpa>, seller, written as one word: the man who sells in a shop) (s:vanzuakpa) (j:sai/zuakpa) (r:zd:17260) (q:draft)
sak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:consider/regard/find/feel) (d:form of <sa>, feel or think, after a word of quality: {nuam sak} is find pleasant, {thupi sak} regard as important, {lamdang sak} find strange; not the causing {sak} that follows a verb) (r:ts:3375/zd:24217) (q:draft)
sakdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/everyday) (w:way of singing/singing style) (d:{la sak}, sing a song, with <dan>, manner, the two last written as one word: the way a song is sung; the same spelling also joins the causative <sak> and <dan>, the way of making something so) (r:zd:16442) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakden = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <den>, always, written as one word after a verb: keep causing, as in {nawngkai sakden}, keep on troubling) (j:sak/den) (r:zd:12450/zd:12217) (q:draft)
sakding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<sak> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: will make it happen, will do it for someone) (j:sak/ding) (r:zd:17668/zd:21837) (q:draft)
sakdingin = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<sak> and <dingin> written as one word after a verb: in order to make it happen or to do it for someone) (j:sak/dingin) (r:zd:20046) (q:draft)
sakdingpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:what will make it) (d:<sak>, the causative placed after a verb, and <dingpen>, what is to be, written as one word: makes the clause the topic, what will cause the thing to happen, or that it should be made to happen) (j:sak/dingpen) (r:zd:16343) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakeng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:I do not find/I do not consider) (d:<sa.5>, feel or consider, with the ending -keng, a short form of <kei> <ing>, I do not, written as one word: {thupi sakeng} is I do not consider it important) (r:zd:24165/zd:25628) (q:draft)
sakgawp = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak>, make or cause, and <gawp>, severely, written as one word after a verb: cause it badly or do it to someone with violence, as in {lauthawng sakgawp}, frighten badly, and {suksiat sakgawp}, wreck) (j:sak/gawp) (r:zd:14901/zd:17517/zd:20013) (q:draft)
sakha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:suppose/assume/take to be) (d:<sa>, here think or consider a thing to be so, with <kha>: happen to think, suppose, often wrongly; {sakha kei ni} is let us not suppose) (j:sa/kha) (r:zd:22361/zd:12121/zd:25628) (q:draft)
sakhan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:camp/base/post) (d:a camp or post, especially of soldiers or an armed group; {thong sakhan} is a prison camp) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:24231/zd:20315) (q:draft)
Sakhangyi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Sakhangyi) (d:village in Myanmar, named as the home village of Zomi people and as a place of fighting) (r:ts:7881) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:already find/already consider) (d:<sa.5>, feel or consider, and <khin>, already, written as one word: {lamdang sakhin} is already find strange; the same spelling also stands for {sa khin}, have already sung) (j:sa/khin) (r:zd:20627) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakkei = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:not let/not make/not find) (d:<sak>, cause or find to be, and <kei>, not, written as one word after a verb or describing word: not make or let it happen, not find it so; {sakkei in} forbids, do not let) (j:sak/kei) (r:zd:21458/zd:12913) (q:draft)
sakkha = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:cause by accident/happen to make) (d:the causative <sak> with <kha>, happen to, written as one word after a verb: bring something about without meaning to, or happen to do it to someone) (j:sak/kha) (r:zd:19712/zd:20871) (q:draft)
sakkhak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:happen to cause/happen to regard) (d:<sak> and <khak>, happen to, written as one word before words such as <leh> and <man>: after a noun, happen to cause it, as in {mindai sakkhak}, happen to bring dishonour; after a word of quality, happen to regard as) (j:sak/khak) (r:zd:17544/zd:21458) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakkhin = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <khin>, already, written as one word after a verb: has already been made to happen, has already been done to someone) (j:sak/khin) (r:zd:15205/zd:11778) (q:draft)
sakkhop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/religion/social) (w:sing together) (d:sing, as in {la sak}, sing a song, with <khop>, together, written as one word: sing a song together) (j:sak/khop) (r:zd:19168/zd:24217/zd:9225) (q:draft)
sakkik = (i:2) (t:n) (f:religion/media) (w:chorus/refrain) (d:the part of a song or hymn that is sung again after each verse, from <sak>, sing, with <kik>, again; mostly as {a sakkik}, its chorus) (r:zd:9220/zd:9256/zd:9215) (q:draft)
saklai = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:causative <sak> with <lai>, here still, written as one word after a verb: still let something go on, still have it done) (j:sak/lai) (r:zd:17733/zd:15342) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if) (d:<sak> and <leh>, if, written as one word after a verb: if one lets or makes it happen; after <ka>, when I think it so) (j:sak/leh) (r:zd:13144/zd:17060) (q:draft, low confidence)
saklel = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causing <sak> after a verb and <lel>, merely, written as one word: only makes it so, does nothing but cause it) (j:sak/lel) (r:zd:15970) (q:draft, low confidence)
saklo = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <lo>, not, written as one word after a verb: not make, not let, not allow to happen) (j:sak/lo) (r:zd:17409/zd:19262/zd:23977) (q:draft)
sakloding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:will not make/will not cause) (d:the causative <sak> with <lo> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: will not make it so, so as not to cause it) (j:saklo/ding) (r:zd:22293/zd:19563) (q:draft)
sakloh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not cause/not let/not consider) (d:<sak> and the negative <loh> written as one word after a verb: not cause or not let it happen, as in {nawngkai sakloh}, not to trouble; after a describing word it is the form of <sa>, deem, as in {kilawm i sakloh}, we do not think it fitting) (j:sak/loh) (r:zd:8668/zd:14946/zd:21049) (q:draft)
saklohna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:not feeling/not considering) (d:<sak>, here the form of <sa> in its sense feel or consider to be, with <lohna>: the fact of not finding something to be so, placed after a describing word; {nop saklohna} is not feeling happy, {dik saklohna} is not thinking something right) (r:zd:22474/zd:20956) (q:draft)
saklua = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:make too much/cause excessively) (d:the causative <sak> with <lua>, too much, written as one word after a verb or describing word: make someone or something too much so, as {gilkial saklua}, let someone get too hungry) (j:sak/lua) (r:zd:17886) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakmahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find very/feel very much) (d:<sak> and <mahmah> written as one word: after a word of quality, find it very much so, as in {haksa sakmahmah}, find very hard; also the causing <sak> with <mahmah>) (j:sak/mahmah) (r:zd:21075/zd:23985) (q:draft)
sakmawk = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<sak> and <mawk> written as one word after a verb or describing word: a thing is made to happen or is regarded so, said with surprise or regret) (j:sak/mawk) (r:zd:21235) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakmi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:northerner/upland people) (d:people of the upper or northern part of the land, said in a pair with the word for the people of the lower or southern part, {sakmi-khangmi}) (r:zd:22709) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakni = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<sak> and the ending <ni> written as one word after a describing word or verb: let us make it so, let us regard it as, as in {thupi sakni}, let us hold it important; in one sentence it is instead <sak> with <ni>, day) (j:sak/ni) (r:zd:12867) (q:draft, low confidence)
saknop = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to make/want to let/wish to cause) (d:the causative <sak> and <nop>, want, written as one word after a verb: want to make or let that happen, as {muh saknop}, want to show) (j:sak/nop) (r:zd:21125/zd:23978) (q:draft)
saknop = (i:2) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:want to sing) (d:<sak>, here sing, with <nop>, want: want or like to sing) (r:zd:16442) (q:draft, low confidence)
saknuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:want to make/want to cause) (d:<sak>, make or cause, and <nuam>, want, written as one word after a verb: want to make something happen, or to make someone do or become something) (j:sak/nuam) (r:zd:19733/zd:26658) (q:draft)
Sakollaam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Sakollaam) (d:a quarter on the edge of <Tedim> town, where the high school stands) (r:zd:21626) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sakollam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Sakollam) (d:a ward of the town of Tedim in Chin State) (r:zd:23205/zd:17530) (q:draft)
sakolleng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:travel) (j:sakolleeng) (r:zd:15974) (q:draft)
sakpah = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <pah>, at once, written as one word after a verb: have it done at once; {kipuak sakpah} is was sent at once) (j:sak/pah) (r:zd:18036/zd:17856) (q:draft)
sakpan = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:begin to make/start to cause) (d:the causative <sak> with <pan>, begin, written as one word after a verb: begin to make something happen, as {paikhia sakpan}, begin to take out; in other sentences {sakpan} is from the north) (j:sak/pan) (r:zd:12070/zd:17717) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakpen = (i:2) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:the one that caused/the one that made) (d:the causative <sak> after a verb, with <pen>, which marks what is spoken about: the one that made something happen, as {hongngah sakpen}, what made us get it; not {sakpen}, regard as most) (r:zd:22293/zd:13195) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakphot = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <phot>, for the time being, written as one word after a verb: have something done for now, temporarily; {khakcip sakphot} is have it closed for the time being) (j:sak/phot) (r:zd:17622/zd:17707) (q:draft)
sakphotding = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <photding> written as one word after a verb: will have it done, or let it be so, for the time being) (j:sak/photding) (r:zd:15167/zd:15617) (q:draft)
sakpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/religion) (w:sing along with/sing together with/join in singing) (d:<sak>, the form of sing used before an ending, with <pih>, together with: sing a song along with someone) (r:zd:11504/zd:11135) (q:draft)
sakpih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:feel with/share the feeling of/regard likewise) (d:<sak>, the form of feel or consider, with <pih>, together with: feel a thing as someone else feels it or regard it as they do, as {thupi sakpih}, count important with them, and {hoih sakpih}, approve) (r:zd:19662/zd:15527) (q:draft, low confidence)
saksa = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:media/everyday) (w:already sung/sung before) (d:<sak>, the form of <sa>, sing, with <sa>, already: of a song that has already been sung, as in the rules of a singing contest; here <sak> is not the causative) (r:zd:17634) (q:draft, low confidence)
saksak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:keep singing/sing regularly) (d:<sak>, sing, doubled: sing a song again and again or as a habit, with <la>, song, close by, as {tu-a i saksak la}, the song we sing today; not the causative) (r:zd:17854/zd:9258/ts:3506) (q:draft)
saksakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/religion) (w:performance/having something sung) (d:<sa>, sing, with the causing <sak> and the noun ending {-na}: the act or occasion of having a song sung or a piece played) (r:zd:9246) (q:draft, low confidence)
saksawm = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:intend to make/try to have done) (d:<sak> and <sawm> written as one word after a verb: intend or try to make someone do the action, or to have it done) (j:sak/sawm) (r:zd:15467/zd:12331/zd:20263) (q:draft)
sakse = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and the emphatic particle <se> written as one word after a verb: just let or make it happen) (j:sak/se) (r:zd:16893) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:can cause/be able to make) (d:causative <sak> and <thei>, able, written as one word after a verb: can make it happen, can cause to) (j:sak/thei) (r:zd:17262/zd:16415) (q:draft)
saktheiding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be able to cause/could make) (d:<sakthei>, can cause, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: it can or could make that happen) (j:sakthei/ding) (r:zd:17649/zd:11864) (q:draft)
saktheih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:can sing/be able to sing) (d:<sak>, form of {la sa}, sing, with <theih>, can: be able to sing a song; {saktheih kim} is all being able to sing it, not regarding something as so) (r:zd:23365/zd:17634) (q:draft, low confidence)
saktuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:each feel/each find) (d:<sak> and <tuak>, each, written as one word after a word of feeling: each of them feels or finds it so, {lamdang saktuak} is each finds it strange; after a verb of doing, each side does it to the other) (j:sak/tuak) (r:zd:15727/zd:16657/zd:11746) (q:draft, low confidence)
saktuam = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak> and <tuam> written as one word after a verb or describing word: make it so as a further result, cause it all the more; {ziakai saktuam} is cause yet more delay) (j:sak/tuam) (r:zd:15469/zd:20122/zd:23311) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakuang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/social) (w:meat dish/meat trough) (d:<sa>, meat, with <kuang>, bowl or trough: the dish or share of meat at a traditional feast; {sakuang hawm} is the sharing out of the meat portions) (r:zd:25393) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (d:<sak> and <un> written as one word after a verb: a command to several people to do the thing for someone or to make it happen) (j:sak/un) (r:zd:21107) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakzawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to make/can cause) (d:<sak> and <zawh> written as one word after a verb: be able to make that happen; the form of <sakzo> used before <nading>) (j:sak/zawh) (r:zd:22701) (q:draft)
sakzel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep making/do repeatedly) (d:<sak>, cause or let, and <zel>, repeatedly, written as one word after a verb: make or let it be done time after time) (j:sak/zel) (r:zd:21826/zd:16717) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakzia = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:way of causing/manner of doing) (d:<sak> and <zia> written as one word after a verb: the way in which something is made to happen or is done to someone) (j:sak/zia) (r:zd:16373) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakziau = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the causative <sak>, do to or for someone, and <ziau>, quickly and lightly, written as one word after a verb: simply do it to someone or to their thing, just like that) (j:sak/ziau) (r:zd:12742/zd:20039) (q:draft, low confidence)
sakzo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to make/can cause) (d:<sak> and <zo> written as one word after a verb: be able to make that happen, as in {kikhel sakzo}, can make something change) (j:sak/zo) (r:zd:19947/zd:24276/zd:15275) (q:draft)
Salai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:Salai) (d:title placed before the name of a man among some Chin peoples; also said of a man who bears it) (r:zd:10874/zd:15698) (q:draft, low confidence)
salam = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:the flesh/physical side) (d:<sa>, flesh, with <lam>, side: the bodily or worldly side of life, set against <khalam>, the spiritual side) (j:sa/lam) (r:zd:25106) (q:draft)
Salayang = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/health) (w:Selayang) (d:town in Selangor, Malaysia, known for its hospital; the Malay spelling is Selayang) (r:zd:21841) (q:draft)
salel = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:just think/simply feel/just suppose) (d:<sa>, here think or feel a thing to be so, with <lel>, just, written as one word after a describing word: simply find it so, just suppose) (r:zd:17162/zd:19521) (q:draft, low confidence)
Salesman = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (w:salesman/seller) (d:a man whose work is selling goods, as in {Car Salesman}) (o:English) (r:zd:10929/zd:17491) (q:draft)
saliang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food) (w:shoulder of meat) (d:<sa>, meat, with <liang>, shoulder: the shoulder of a slaughtered animal, a share given in honour at a feast) (r:zd:18001/zd:13144) (q:draft, low confidence)
saliang = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:feel so much/find even) (d:<sa>, here feel or find, and <liang>, even, written as one word after a describing word: feel it to that degree, as {lamdang bang saliang}, find it quite strange) (r:zd:15588/zd:19447) (q:draft, low confidence)
salneih = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:slave-holding/slavery) (d:<sal> and <neih> written as one word: the keeping of slaves; {salneih ngeina} is the practice of slavery) (j:sal/neih) (r:ts:4831/zd:25015) (q:draft)
salo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:not consider/not find/not feel) (d:<sa> in the sense of feel or consider, with the negative <lo>, written as one word after a describing word: not find it so, as {hoih salo}, not think it good, and {thupi salo}, not consider important) (j:sa/lo) (r:zd:20516/zd:23075) (q:draft)
salon = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/body) (w:salon/beauty salon/hair salon) (d:a shop where hair is cut and beauty care is given, mostly as beauty salon or hair salon) (o:English) (r:zd:24276/zd:17195) (q:draft, low confidence)
salpha = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:hero/martyr) (d:short for {pasal pha}, a good and brave man: a hero, especially one who gave his life for his people) (r:zd:11262/zd:22658) (q:draft)
salphate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:martyrs/heroes) (d:those who gave their lives for their people or land, the plural of <salpha> with <te>; {Zomi salphate} are the Zomi martyrs) (r:zd:9421/ts:1343) (q:draft)
salua = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:nature/everyday) (w:too hot/very hot) (d:<sa>, hot, and <lua>, too much, written as one word: too hot, extremely hot) (j:sa/lua) (r:zd:23729/zd:24532) (q:draft)
salua = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find too much/feel very) (d:<sa>, here feel or consider to be, and <lua>, too much, written as one word after a describing word: feel that something is very much so, as in {lamdang salua}, find it very strange, and {tam salua}, find it too many) (r:zd:17177/zd:20341) (q:draft, low confidence)
salung = (i:1) (t:n) (f:food/social) (w:heart) (d:<sa>, meat, with <lung>, heart: the heart of an animal as meat; {sasin salung} is the liver and heart, the choice parts taken as an offering for the dead at the Khuado feast) (j:sa/lung) (r:ts:3366/zd:26708) (q:draft)
sam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:call/summon/invite) (d:call a person to come, call out to someone, invite; before a suffix the form is <sap>) (r:1.22.15)
sam hang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even though/although/admittedly) (d:<sam>, here a particle, indeed or admittedly, and not the verb call, and <hang>, although: placed after a verb or a clause that is granted to be true, before or after the statement that limits it, even though it is so) (r:zd:21664/zd:25580) (q:draft, low confidence)
sama = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/everyday) (w:called and) (d:<sam>, call, and the linking <a> written as one word: called someone, and) (j:sam/a) (r:zd:25475) (q:draft, low confidence)
samahmah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:find very/feel very/consider very) (d:<sa> in the sense of feel or consider, with <mahmah>, very, written as one word after a describing word: find something very much so, as {lamdang samahmah}, be greatly amazed, and {thupi samahmah}, consider very important) (j:sa/mahmah) (r:zd:16365/zd:24502/zd:25572) (q:draft)
samai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:front line) (d:found only after <galmai> in the pair {galmai samai}, the front of battle: the place of danger where one faces the enemy; perhaps from <sa>, here wild animal, and <mai>, face) (r:zd:20241/zd:17224) (q:draft, low confidence)
Samaritan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:religion) (w:Samaritan) (d:a person of Samaria or of the Samaritan people and religion; {Good Samaritan} is the helpful stranger of the parable of Jesus) (o:English) (r:zd:20319/zd:24014) (q:draft)
samawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:consider/take to be/suppose) (d:<sa>, here consider or deem, and <mawk>, a marker of something unexpected, written as one word after a describing word: actually regard something as so) (j:sa/mawk) (r:zd:11803/zd:12972) (q:draft, low confidence)
samding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:to call/will call) (d:<sam>, call, and <ding> written as one word: to call or summon someone; in other sentences it is the end of {kisam ding}, will be needed) (j:sam/ding) (r:zd:17279) (q:draft, low confidence)
samhangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:although/even though) (d:<sam>, here the particle also or indeed and not call, and <hangin>, although, written as one word after a verb: although it is indeed so, even though one does say so) (j:sam/hangin) (r:zd:25824) (q:draft, low confidence)
samkei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/not really) (d:an emphatic word, not the verb spelled the same, with the negative <kei> written as one word after a verb: not at all, not really; {hi samkei} is it is not so at all) (r:zd:15259/zd:22451) (q:draft, low confidence)
samkhang = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:body) (w:grey-haired/white-haired) (d:with hair turned grey or white, of old people, beside {khamul khang}, grey-bearded; in one sentence it rather says that hair grows) (r:zd:17295/zd:17049) (q:draft, low confidence)
samkhawmin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:calling together/summoning together) (d:<samkhawm>, call together, with the linking <in>: having called people together, and then) (j:samkhawm/in) (r:ts:3375/zd:14734) (q:draft)
samlai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:still lack/be still short/still need) (d:<sam>, here be lacking, as in <kisam>, with <lai>, still, written as one word: an amount is still wanting, still to come; not <sam> in the sense of call) (j:sam/lai) (r:zd:19210/zd:24354) (q:draft, low confidence)
samlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not really/not exactly/not necessarily) (d:<sam>, here a softening particle and not the verb call, with <lo>, not, written as one word after a verb or describing word: a softened denial, it is not really so, not quite, not as one might think) (r:zd:16844/zd:16892/zd:21918) (q:draft)
samloh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not really/not exactly) (d:form of <samlo>, not exactly, used before <hangin>: {ahih pah samloh hangin} is although it is not exactly so) (b:samlo) (r:zd:24750/ts:3125) (q:draft)
sammet = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/work) (w:haircut/hair cutting/barbering) (d:from {sam met}, cut the hair of the head, written as one word: the cutting of hair; {sammet sai} is a barbershop, {sammet nasep} the work of a barber and {sammet pa} a barber) (r:zd:15278/zd:24112) (q:draft)
sammetsai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/body) (w:barbershop/hair salon) (d:<sammet>, haircut, and <sai>, shop, written as one word: a shop where hair is cut and dressed) (j:sammet/sai) (r:zd:15622/zd:15994) (q:draft)
Sample = (i:1) (t:n) (f:health/work) (w:sample/specimen) (d:a small part taken to test or to show the whole) (o:English) (r:zd:12945/zd:17570) (q:draft, low confidence)
samsam = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:then/in turn/at once) (d:after another verb it is not <sam>, call, but an adverb for an action done promptly or in answer to what came before, as {gen samsam}, {ci samsam} and {pah samsam}) (r:zd:14824/zd:25109) (q:draft, low confidence)
samsawpna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home/body) (w:shampoo) (d:the word for hair with <sawpna>, washing: what the hair is washed with, shampoo) (r:zd:14946) (q:draft)
Samsung = (i:1) (t:name) (f:it/work) (w:Samsung) (d:South Korean company and its brand of phones and household appliances) (o:Korean) (r:zd:12456/zd:11783) (q:draft)
samthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:can call/can invite/can sponsor) (d:<sam>, call, and <thei>, able, written as one word: be able to call someone to come, as a relative to another country) (j:sam/thei) (r:zd:22877/zd:23569) (q:draft)
Samui = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Samui/Ko Samui) (d:an island of Thailand with beaches, visited by many tourists; also written Ko Samui or Koh Samui) (r:zd:17941) (q:draft)
samza = (i:1) (t:n) (f:body/home) (w:hair dye/hair product) (d:a chemical preparation that is put on the hair, such as hair dye; {sam hoihna za} is a hair treatment) (r:zd:21243) (q:draft, low confidence)
san = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:red/scarlet) (d:the colour red, said of a horse, cloth, a cord, wine or the evening sky)
Sanchaung = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Sanchaung) (d:township of the city of Yangon) (r:zd:25027/zd:23641) (q:draft)
sanction = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:sanction/sanctions) (d:a penalty that one country lays on another, as in {sanction bawl}, impose sanctions; in a few places the approval of a budget) (o:English) (r:zd:24990/zd:20394/zd:24945) (q:draft)
sanctions = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:sanctions) (d:penalties that one country places on another to make it change its conduct; writers also say <khalna> or <khaktanna> and add the English word) (o:English) (r:zd:25582) (q:draft, low confidence)
sandahpiah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:demonstration/protest) (d:a public demonstration by a crowd; also as a verb, to demonstrate) (s:lungphona) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:17060) (q:draft, low confidence)
Sandakan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Sandakan) (d:town on the coast of Sabah State in Malaysia) (r:zd:13063/zd:16916) (q:draft)
sandan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/religion) (w:view/understanding/way of accepting) (d:the verb form {san-}, receive or accept, with <dan>, manner: the way a person takes or understands a matter; {updan sandan} is what people believe and hold) (r:zd:20058/zd:23086) (q:draft)
sanding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/work) (w:will accept/to receive) (d:<san>, here the form of <sang>, accept or receive, with <ding>, will or to, written as one word: will accept, to receive, as pay) (r:zd:20850/zd:24420) (q:draft)
sanding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:health/body) (w:will turn red/redden) (d:<san>, red, with <ding>, will, written as one word: will become red, as the skin) (j:san/ding) (r:zd:16919) (q:draft, low confidence)
