sim = (i:4) (t:det) (f:time/everyday) (w:every/each) (d:placed after a word for a time or an event, often followed by <a> or <in>: every one, each time, as in <nisim>, every day, and {meeting sim}, every meeting; not the verb read or count) (r:zd:25127/zd:23727) (q:draft)
sima = (i:2) (t:v) (f:education/religion) (w:reading/read) (d:<sim.1>, read, with the linking <a>: reading a text and then going on to the next action, after the name of what is read and not after a time word) (r:zd:9262) (q:draft, low confidence)
sima = (i:3) (t:v) (f:politics) (w:attacking/attack) (d:<sim>, attack, with the linking <a>: attacking a town or a people and then going on to the next action, as <simin.2> does) (r:zd:25668) (q:draft, low confidence)
simai = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:die/just die) (d:<si> and <mai> written as one word: simply die, die then and there) (j:si/mai) (r:ts:6323/zd:16194) (q:draft)
simawh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (j:simmawh) (r:zd:16254/zd:24011) (q:draft)
simawk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/everyday) (w:die/pass away) (d:<si>, die, and <mawk> written as one word: died, said of a death that came unexpectedly or is reported with regret) (j:si/mawk) (r:zd:14664/zd:16038) (q:draft)
simbeh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education) (w:read more/read further) (d:<sim>, read, with the ending <beh>, in addition: read more about a matter than one has already read) (b:sim) (r:zd:21288/zd:21340) (q:draft)
simbu = (i:2) (t:n) (f:education) (w:reader/primer/textbook) (d:<sim>, read, with the second part of <laibu>, book: a school book for learning to read, not the owl; nearly always {Zolai simbu}, the Zolai reader used in the schools) (r:zd:11891/zd:21179/zd:18171) (q:draft)
simcard = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:SIM card) (d:the small card that connects a mobile phone to a network and carries its number) (o:English, SIM card) (r:zd:21257/zd:25052/zd:14767) (q:draft)
simdan = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:way of reading/reading) (d:<sim>, read, and <dan>, way, written as one word: how something is read, and reading as a skill) (j:sim/dan) (r:zd:12867/zd:24303/zd:21607) (q:draft)
simden = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/education) (w:read constantly/keep reading) (d:<sim>, read, and <den>, always, written as one word: read regularly or go on reading) (j:sim/den) (r:zd:19178/zd:12876) (q:draft)
simding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:education/media) (w:to read/will read/reading matter) (d:<sim>, read, and <ding> written as one word: will read, or something meant to be read; {nungak te simding} is for girls to read) (j:sim/ding) (r:zd:14941/zd:21826) (q:draft)
simding = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social) (w:to attend) (d:<sim> for <siim>, attend a feast, and <ding> written as one word: in order to attend; {mopawi simding} is to attend a wedding) (j:siim/ding) (r:zd:11133) (q:draft, low confidence)
