singkhuah = (i:2) (t:n) (f:everyday/home) (w:stick/club/piece of wood) (d:a length of wood that is not burning, such as a stick taken up to hit with; often paired with stone, as {singkhuah suangtum}, sticks and stones) (r:zd:14901/zd:23424) (q:draft)
singkhuam = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home/social) (w:wooden post/post/pole) (d:any wooden post set upright in the ground, such as the post on which the heads of game and of enemies were once hung, or a carved post that is worshipped; not the cross of Jesus) (r:ts:3375/zd:22159) (q:draft, low confidence)
singkuang = (i:2) (t:n) (f:home/religion) (w:box/chest/case/ark) (d:a box or chest, at first of <sing.2>, wood, for keeping or carrying things; {thukham singkuang} is the ark of the covenant and {tuikhal singkuang} a refrigerator) (r:zd:21337/zd:19621/zd:15274) (q:draft)
singkung lopa = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:vegetation/plants/trees and grass) (d:<singkung>, tree, and <lopa>, grass, named together for all that grows: plants, vegetation, the green cover of the land; often after {gamsa vasa}, beasts and birds, or before <khempeuh>) (r:zd:22650/zd:16254) (q:draft)
singkung lopate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:vegetation/plants/trees and plants) (d:<singkung>, tree, and <lopate>, grasses: a pair that names all plant life together) (r:zd:23729/zd:23554) (q:draft)
singkungkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:a tree/one tree) (d:<singkung>, tree, and <khat>, one, written as one word: a tree) (j:singkung/khat) (r:zd:12902/zd:14547/zd:18005) (q:draft)
singkungnuai = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:nature) (w:under a tree/under the tree) (d:<singkung>, tree, and <nuai>, under, written as one word: the place under a tree) (j:singkung/nuai) (r:zd:17899/zd:11759) (q:draft)
singkungpi = (i:1) (t:n) (c:plant) (f:nature) (w:big tree/large tree) (d:<singkung>, tree, with <pi>, big: a large full-grown tree) (b:singkung) (r:zd:23888/zd:11229) (q:draft)
singlak = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature) (w:woods/among the trees) (d:<sing>, tree, and <lak>, midst, written as one word: a place among trees, woodland) (j:sing/lak) (r:zd:19860) (q:draft)
Singlei = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Singlei) (d:name of a Zomi village, written in brackets after the name of a person to show the home village; the location is not clear from the articles) (r:zd:25165) (q:draft, low confidence)
Singngat = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:travel) (w:Singngat) (d:a town and subdivision in the south of <Manipur>, India) (r:zd:19843/zd:15637) (q:draft)
singnuai = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/politics) (w:forest/bush/jungle) (d:<sing>, tree, with <nuai>, under: the place under the trees, the forest or bush; {singnuai mite} are people who live in the jungle, said of underground armed groups) (s:gamlak) (j:sing/nuai) (r:zd:17583/zd:8668/zd:21379) (q:draft)
singnuaimi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:insurgent/rebel/guerrilla) (d:<singnuai>, jungle, with <mi>, person: a member of an armed group that lives in the jungle and fights the government) (r:zd:25532/zd:13041) (q:draft)
