singtang = (i:1) (t:n) (f:nature/social) (w:hills/highlands/hill country) (d:the hills as against the plain, <zanglei>; placed before a noun it means of the hills, as {singtang khua}, a hill village, {singtang mite}, hill people, and {singtang buh}, hill rice) (r:zd:9426/zd:24375/ts:4569) (q:draft)
Singtangmi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:hill people/highlander/tribal) (d:<singtang>, the hills, with <mi>, person, written as one word: a person of the hill country, used for the English word tribal) (j:singtang/mi) (r:zd:21309) (q:draft)
