taikhiakhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have already fled/have escaped) (d:<taikhia>, run away, with <khin>, already; also said of things swept away by water) (j:taikhia/khin) (r:zd:11568/zd:14301) (q:draft)
taikhiakik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:run back out/flee again/run off) (d:<taikhia>, run away, and <kik>, back or again, written as one word: run out again, flee from the place one came into) (j:taikhia/kik) (r:zd:14656/zd:16617) (q:draft)
taikhiaman = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:escape in time/manage to flee) (d:<taikhia> and <man> written as one word: get out in time, manage to run out) (j:taikhia/man) (r:zd:15033) (q:draft)
taikhiapah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:run away at once/flee immediately) (d:<taikhia>, run away, and <pah>, at once, written as one word: run out or flee straight away) (j:taikhia/pah) (r:zd:12676/zd:20641) (q:draft)
taikhiasuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:run right away/make off/get away) (d:<taikhia>, run away, and <suak>, right through, written as one word: flee and get clean away) (j:taikhia/suak) (r:zd:20629/zd:19536) (q:draft)
taikhiathei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be able to escape/manage to get away) (d:<taikhia>, run away, and <thei>, able, written as one word) (j:taikhia/thei) (r:zd:17361/zd:16739) (q:draft)
taikhiatpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/travel) (w:run off with/make off with/carry away) (d:<tai> and <khiatpih> written as one word: flee taking a person or thing along, as robbers or abductors do) (j:tai/khiatpih) (r:zd:18061/zd:15065) (q:draft)
taikhiatsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:try to flee/try to escape/attempt to run away) (d:<taikhiat> and <sawm> written as one word: try or set out to run away) (j:taikhiat/sawm) (r:zd:20522/zd:12848) (q:draft)
tailai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:travel) (w:moving/running) (d:<tai>, run, with <lai>, while, written as one word after the name of a vehicle: while it is running, a moving car, lorry or train) (j:tai/lai) (r:zd:14528/zd:10931) (q:draft)
tailaikhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:a moving one/one in motion) (d:<tailai>, while running, and <khat>, one, written as one word after the name of a vehicle: a vehicle that is moving) (j:tailai/khat) (r:zd:13330) (q:draft)
taimangkhin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:have already fled/have run away) (d:<taimang>, run away, and <khin>, already, written as one word: had already run off and was gone) (j:taimang/khin) (r:zd:12696) (q:draft)
taimangpih = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:run away with/make off with/abduct) (d:<taimang>, run away, with <pih>, together with: flee taking a person or a thing along, such as stolen money or a car) (b:taimang) (r:zd:11027/zd:19388) (q:draft)
taimangsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:try to run away/attempt to flee) (d:<taimang>, run away, and <sawm>, intend or attempt, written as one word: try to run off) (j:taimang/sawm) (r:zd:14731/zd:21341) (q:draft)
taina = (i:3) (t:n) (f:travel/body) (w:running/run/runway) (d:<tai> in the sense of run or move fast, of a person, a plane or a train, with no thought of fleeing: {vanleng taina} is a runway and {meileng taina} a railway track) (r:zd:12057/zd:17758/zd:14816) (q:draft)
tainading = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:travel) (w:for running/for travelling) (d:<tai>, run, and <nading>, for, written as one word: for running on, said of a runway for planes or a track for fast travel) (j:tai/nading) (r:zd:12124/zd:16851) (q:draft)
Taing = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:region/division) (d:an administrative Region of Myanmar, formerly called a Division, on the same level as a State; follows the name, as in {Sagaing Taing}) (o:Burmese, taing) (r:zd:19239/zd:21590/zd:25400) (q:draft)
Taingen = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Taingen) (d:village in Tedim Township in Chin State, on the road between Kalaymyo and Tedim) (r:zd:14824/zd:16035) (q:draft)
Taipei = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel/politics) (w:Taipei) (d:capital city of Taiwan) (r:ts:3506/zd:11265) (q:draft)
taiphei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:run over to/run across/run toward) (d:<tai>, run, with <phei>, across or over toward: run over to a person or a place) (j:tai/phei) (r:zd:24957/zd:20215/zd:12477) (q:draft)
taipih = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday/health) (w:rush/hurry off with) (d:take someone somewhere in great haste, with no thought of fleeing, as a sick or injured person to hospital; often with {amanlang in}, quickly, and <vingveng>) (r:zd:19033/zd:17768) (q:draft)
taipihpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/travel) (w:rush to/take at once) (d:<taipih> and <pah> written as one word: hurry off with someone at once, above all rush a sick or injured person to hospital) (j:taipih/pah) (r:zd:15067/zd:20136) (q:draft)
Taiping = (i:1) (t:name) (c:city) (f:travel) (w:Taiping) (d:town in the state of Perak, Malaysia) (r:zd:13224/zd:15915) (q:draft)
taisak = (i:3) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:run/operate/drive) (d:<tai>, run, with the causative <sak>, said of a train, bus, boat or car: run a transport service or drive a vehicle, <kitaisak> being be run; not the sense put to flight) (r:zd:12040/zd:17622/zd:15953) (q:draft)
taisakding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:will run/will operate) (d:<tai> and <sakding> written as one word: will make a bus, boat or train run, will operate a service) (j:tai/sakding) (r:zd:17396/zd:15558) (q:draft)
taisanlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:not forsake/not abandon/not desert) (d:<taisan> and <lo> written as one word: not run away from, not forsake) (j:taisan/lo) (r:zd:19600) (q:draft)
taisanna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:abandonment/desertion/leaving) (d:<taisan>, forsake, with the noun suffix {-na}: the act of leaving or abandoning a person or a group) (b:taisan) (r:zd:25447) (q:draft)
taisansuak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:flee the scene/run off/hit and run) (d:<taisan>, flee from, with <suak>, right on, written as one word: run off and leave, said of a driver who drives on after hitting someone) (j:taisan/suak) (r:zd:15074/zd:12089) (q:draft)
taisanziau = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:run off at once/flee straight away) (d:<taisan>, flee from, and <ziau>, at once, written as one word: leave someone and make off quickly) (j:taisan/ziau) (r:zd:19063/zd:12878) (q:draft)
taisawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to flee/try to run away/attempt to escape) (d:<tai>, run away, and <sawm>, intend, written as one word: try or be about to run away) (j:tai/sawm) (r:zd:12490/zd:12523) (q:draft)
taisimsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:try to flee/attempt to escape) (d:<taisim>, run away, with <sawm>, intend, written as one word: try to run away, make to escape) (j:taisim/sawm) (r:zd:16010/zd:15165) (q:draft)
taisuaksak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel) (w:run on/keep going/pass without stopping) (d:<tai>, run, with <suaksak>, here on through: of a train or a car, go on without stopping) (b:tai) (r:zd:17994/zd:20767) (q:draft, low confidence)
taisuaksawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:try to escape/attempt to flee) (d:<taisuak>, escape, and <sawm>, intend or attempt, written as one word: try to get away) (j:taisuak/sawm) (r:zd:11841/zd:20767) (q:draft)
taitai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:keep running/keep fleeing/run on) (d:<tai>, run, said twice: go on running or fleeing, mostly from one who pursues, as {taitai} of people beside <delhdelh>, keep chasing; here it is the main verb and follows no other verb) (r:zd:22046/zd:21251) (q:draft)
taite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/travel) (w:those who run/those who flee) (d:<tai>, run or flee, with plural <te>: the ones running or fleeing; {gal taite} are people fleeing war) (j:tai/te) (r:zd:20919/ts:1395/zd:22686) (q:draft)
taithei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:can run/be able to run) (d:<tai>, run, and <thei>, able, written as one word: able to run, of a person, a vehicle or a train service) (j:tai/thei) (r:zd:16383/ts:3369) (q:draft)
taitheilo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:travel/everyday) (w:cannot run/be unable to run) (d:<tai> and <theilo> written as one word: be unable to run; of a train or vehicle, be unable to travel) (j:tai/theilo) (r:zd:17432/zd:22129) (q:draft)
taivingveng = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/travel) (w:run off/flee/hurry away) (d:<tai>, run, and <vingveng>, straight away, written as one word: run off at once, make off in a hurry) (j:tai/vingveng) (r:zd:11904/zd:14731) (q:draft)
Taiwan = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Taiwan) (d:island country in East Asia) (r:zd:15681/zd:24195/zd:17626) (q:draft)
takaa = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:<tak> with <aa>, written as one word after a describing word to make an adverb of manner, like English -ly, as in {thupi takaa}, grandly; {tulai takaa} is at the present time) (s:takin) (j:tak/aa) (r:zd:19239/zd:17881/zd:17060) (q:draft)
takah = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:in as many as/in fully) (d:<tak> strengthening a number or <tampi>, with the locative marker <ah>: in as many as that number of places, {mun 5 takah} in as many as five places, {khua tampi takah} in very many villages; not the pointing to one exact spot) (r:zd:19699/zd:13020/zd:12311) (q:draft)
takbang = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:media) (w:as many as about/some) (d:<tak> and <bang>, about, written as one word after a number or an amount: stresses that the figure is large and says that it is not exact) (j:tak/bang) (r:zd:12759/zd:14935) (q:draft)
takciang = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:when/once) (d:<tak> and <ciang>, when, written as one word after a verb, often followed by <in>: at the very time when it happens, once it really comes to that) (j:tak/ciang) (r:zd:21426/zd:24242) (q:draft)
takciangin = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:when/once/by the time) (d:<tak> with <ciangin>, when, written as one word and placed after a verb or a date: at the very time when, once it has happened, when that year came) (j:tak/ciangin) (r:zd:17673/zd:11860/zd:21327) (q:draft)
takeileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:even if not/if not/though not) (d:<takei> and <leh>, if, written as one word after a verb: even if it is not so; paired with <taleh>, {hoih taleh, hoih takeileh} is whether good or not) (j:takei/leh) (r:zd:20845/zd:17264) (q:draft)
takhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:one child/a child) (d:<ta> and <khat> written as one word: one child, a child of one's own) (j:ta/khat) (r:zd:15689/zd:12959) (q:draft)
Takhin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:Thakin) (d:Burmese title, master, put before the names of members of the Burmese nationalist movement before independence) (o:Burmese, thakin) (r:zd:25097) (q:draft, low confidence)
takin = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:media) (w:as many as/no fewer than) (d:placed after a number of people in news reports, before a verb such as <sihlawh>, die, or <liamlawh>, be injured, to stress that the count is so large; not the ending that makes an adverb of manner) (r:zd:19182/zd:11296) (q:draft, low confidence)
takkhat = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:one drop/a single drop) (d:<tak>, here a drop of liquid, and <khat>, one, written as one word: one drop of tears, fuel or the like; also of a very small amount) (j:tak/khat) (r:zd:15443/zd:19262) (q:draft)
takkheh = (i:1) (t:intj) (f:social) (w:be brave/come on) (d:cry of resolve or encouragement before a bold act; {pasal takkheh} is said of or to a real man) (r:zd:14731) (q:draft, low confidence)
takleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:and) (d:the particle <tak> and <leh>, and, written as one word: joins two descriptions or amounts of which the first ends in <tak>, as in {siangtho takleh}, holily and) (j:tak/leh) (r:zd:19257/zd:11256) (q:draft, low confidence)
taklo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not really/not quite/hardly) (d:<tak> and <lo> written as one word after a verb or describing word: not really, not properly, hardly) (j:tak/lo) (r:zd:24214/zd:19239) (q:draft, low confidence)
takmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:really/indeed/truly) (d:<tak> and the emphatic <mah> written as one word after a describing word or a number: very much so, indeed; {tampi takmah} is very many indeed) (j:tak/mah) (r:zd:22827/zd:19160/zd:20545) (q:draft)
takpen = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:most/the most) (d:<tak> and the superlative <pen> written as one word after a describing word, as in {etteh takpen}, the most worthy of imitation; <pen> may also be the topic marker) (j:tak/pen) (r:zd:15941) (q:draft, low confidence)
takpha = (i:1) (t:v) (f:media/everyday) (w:reach fully/amount to as much as) (d:<tak> and <pha> written as one word after a number or measure: come to fully that many, as much as) (j:tak/pha) (r:zd:15577/zd:12996) (q:draft)
takpi = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday/social) (w:true/real/sincere/genuine) (d:placed after a noun: real and not pretended, as in <lungsim takpi>, a sincere heart, and {min takpi}, the real name) (r:zd:25136/zd:25462) (q:draft)
takpiding = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:will really/will indeed) (d:<takpi> and <ding> written as one word after a verb: will truly happen) (j:takpi/ding) (r:zd:15382/zd:15447) (q:draft)
takpileh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if really/if indeed) (d:<takpi>, really, and <leh>, if, written as one word after a verb: if that really happens; <leh> can also be and, as in {nasimnop takpileh thuhoih}, truly pleasant to read and good) (j:takpi/leh) (r:zd:20197) (q:draft, low confidence)
takpimawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/media) (w:really/actually/indeed) (d:<takpi>, truly, and <mawk>, here marking surprise, written as one word after a verb: it really did happen, hard as it is to believe) (j:takpi/mawk) (r:zd:12756/zd:15344) (q:draft)
takpita = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:media/everyday) (w:really now/indeed now/at last) (d:<takpi>, really, with the particle <ta>, now, written as one word after a verb: {akipan takpita} is it has now really begun) (j:takpi/ta) (r:zd:13209/zd:17097) (q:draft)
takpite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:those who truly are) (d:<takpi>, truly, with plural <te>, placed after a describing word: the ones who really are so; {a cimawh takpite} are the truly needy) (j:takpi/te) (r:zd:11135/zd:24038) (q:draft)
taksa = (i:2) (t:n) (f:body/religion) (w:body/flesh/physical) (d:the body of flesh as against <kha>, the spirit, or <lungsim>, the mind; {pumpi taksa} is the physical body and {taksa damna} bodily health) (s:pumpi) (r:zd:20784/zd:23989/zd:25749) (q:draft)
taksuah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/politics) (w:come true/become real/be realized) (d:<tak>, real, with <suah>, become: turn into fact; {taksuah sak} is put into effect, carry out) (j:tak/suah) (r:ts:9524/zd:22464/zd:23356) (q:draft, low confidence)
taksuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:drop down/drip down/fall down) (d:fall downward in drops, said of tears, or drop down, with <suk>, downward) (r:zd:12928/zd:16832) (q:draft, low confidence)
taktaka = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:truly/really/in fact) (d:<taktak>, truly, with the adverbial ending {-a}: truly, really, in actual fact, placed before the verb or clause it describes) (j:taktak/a) (r:zd:9453/zd:24341) (q:draft)
taktakbel = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/family) (w:real though/really however) (d:<taktak>, real, and <bel>, as for, written as one word after a noun: the real one, set in contrast, as in {apu taktakbel hisamlo}, not his real grandfather though) (j:taktak/bel) (r:zd:11550) (q:draft, low confidence)
taktakding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:will really/will surely) (d:<taktak>, really, and <ding>, will, written as one word after a verb: will really or surely do so, or the one who will truly do so) (j:taktak/ding) (r:zd:20912/zd:14836/zd:26976) (q:draft)
taktakleh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday) (w:if really/when actually) (d:<taktak> and <leh> written as one word after a verb: if or when it really is so, if it truly happens) (j:taktak/leh) (r:zd:24276/zd:14949) (q:draft)
taktaklo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not really/not truly) (d:<taktak> and <lo> written as one word: not really, not truly; after a noun, not real) (j:taktak/lo) (r:zd:20979/zd:20537) (q:draft)
taktakma = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:time) (w:before actually/just before) (d:<taktak>, really, and <ma>, before, written as one word after a verb and followed by <in>: before the thing really happens) (j:taktak/ma) (r:zd:12662) (q:draft, low confidence)
taktakmah = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:really/truly/indeed) (d:<taktak>, truly, and the emphatic <mah>, written as one word: really and truly so) (j:taktak/mah) (r:zd:12481/zd:12945) (q:draft)
taktakpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the real/the actual/the true) (d:<taktak>, real, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, placed after a noun: the real or actual one, as in {ahang taktakpen}, the real cause) (j:taktak/pen) (r:zd:12512/zd:19973/zd:11839) (q:draft)
taktaktawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:with the real/with true) (d:<taktak> and <tawh> written as one word after a noun or verb: with the real one, with what one truly wants) (j:taktak/tawh) (r:zd:20213/zd:12618) (q:draft)
taktawh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:with true/with real) (d:<tak>, true or real, and <tawh>, with, written as one word after a noun: with real or sincere, as {itna taktawh}, with true love; after a sum of money, for as much as) (j:tak/tawh) (r:zd:20917/zd:11548/zd:15274) (q:draft)
takteh = (i:1) (t:conj) (f:everyday/time) (w:when/once/at the time that) (d:<tak> and <teh> written as one word after a verb or a date: when, at the moment that; the same as {tak ciangin}) (j:tak/teh) (r:zd:24036/zd:23928/zd:25205) (q:draft)
