Talpak = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Meitei/Manipuri) (d:a Zomi name for the <Meitei> people of the Manipur valley) (s:Meitei) (r:zd:18026) (q:draft)
taltak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:social/family) (w:elderly/aged/senior) (d:far on in years and honoured for it, said of the oldest men of a gathering; explained in one article by <putek>, old man; {taltak pen} is the eldest) (r:zd:20520/zd:23394) (q:draft, low confidence)
tam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:many) (d:large in number; {a tam} is the many, set against {a tawm}, the few, and {tam mahmah} is very many) (s:tampi) (a:tawm)
tam = (i:4) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:I wonder) (d:placed at the end of a question that has a question word, as in {ahi tam}: marks the question as one the speaker wonders about; not {tam}, many) (r:zd:23554/zd:19201) (q:draft, low confidence)
tam theithei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:as many as possible/as much as possible) (d:<tam>, many, and <theithei>, as far as can be: mostly {a tam theithei}, as many or as much as possible, placed before the verb or after the noun it counts; <theithei> gives the same sense after other words of quality, as in {a manlang theithei}, as quickly as possible) (r:zd:14826/zd:23175) (q:draft)
tama = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:practitioner/person engaged in) (d:Burmese word placed after the Burmese name of a field of activity for a person engaged in it: {Siipuayii tama} is a businessman and {Naingngaanzee tama} a politician; elsewhere the spelling is {tam a}, many and, written as one word, or part of a place name) (o:Burmese, thama) (r:zd:21117/zd:21235) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tamadah = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:president) (d:the president of a country, used above all of the president of Myanmar) (o:Burmese, thamada) (r:zd:11463/zd:21117) (q:draft)
tamah = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:already indeed/although) (d:the particle <ta>, already, with <mah>, indeed, written as one word after a verb: the thing has indeed happened; with <leh> it concedes, even though it is so, as in {ki cancel tamah leh}, although it is cancelled; not {a tamah}, in much) (r:zd:23784/zd:16788) (q:draft, low confidence)
tamai = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ta> and <mai> written as one word after a verb at the end of a sentence: things have simply come to be so, often said with regret or resignation) (j:ta/mai) (r:zd:11269/zd:10823) (q:draft, low confidence)
tamate = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/politics) (w:practitioners/people engaged in) (d:plural of <tama>, placed after the Burmese name of a field of activity: {nainganyii tamate} are politicians and {siipuayii tamate} are businessmen) (b:tama) (o:Burmese) (r:zd:15709) (q:draft)
tamawk = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<ta>, marking a change that has now come about, and <mawk>, marking what is unexpected or regretted, written as one word after a verb and before <hi> or <uh>: it has now come to this, sadly or surprisingly) (j:ta/mawk) (r:zd:15943/zd:15216) (q:draft)
tambei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work/everyday) (w:cost much/be expensive) (d:<tam>, much, and <bei>, be used up, written as one word: much money is spent, it costs a great deal) (j:tam/bei) (r:zd:25616/zd:25572) (q:draft)
tamcihtak = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:really much/in very great amount) (d:<tam> and <cihtak> written as one word, in {tamcihtak in tam}: there is truly a great deal or a great many) (j:tam/cihtak) (r:zd:20401/zd:12115) (q:draft)
tamdeuh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:rather many/more/quite a lot) (d:<tam>, many, and <deuh>, somewhat, written as one word: somewhat more, rather many or much) (j:tam/deuh) (r:zd:22981/zd:25919) (q:draft)
tamding = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:will be many/will be much) (d:<tam>, many, and <ding>, will, written as one word: there will be many or much) (j:tam/ding) (r:zd:12938/zd:14638) (q:draft)
tamgawp = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/nature) (w:be very much/be excessive) (d:<tam> and <gawp> written as one word: be extremely many or much, said of heavy rain) (j:tam/gawp) (r:zd:20401/zd:20345) (q:draft, low confidence)
tamgen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:say much/speak often of) (d:<tam> and <gen> written as one word: say a lot, or speak of something often; {tamgen lo} is say little of) (j:tam/gen) (r:zd:23191/zd:21991) (q:draft)
tamh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social) (w:name after) (d:give a person or place the name of another; {min tamh} is to bear the name of someone) (r:zd:18920/zd:23767) (q:draft, low confidence)
tamhetlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not many at all/very few/hardly any) (d:<tam>, many, and <hetlo>, not at all, written as one word) (j:tam/hetlo) (r:zd:16490/zd:16949) (q:draft)
Tamil = (i:1) (t:name) (c:people) (f:social) (w:Tamil) (d:a people of south India and Sri Lanka, also living in Malaysia and Singapore, and their language; Tamil Nadu is their state in India) (r:zd:19662) (q:draft)
tamin = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:being many/being much) (d:<tam>, many, with the linking ending <in>: there being many or much of something, giving the reason for or leading on to what follows; not the noun for a child's name) (r:zd:23729/zd:9239/zd:13320) (q:draft)
tamin = (i:3) (t:v) (f:travel/time) (w:staying/spending) (d:{tamin} from a verb for staying with the linking ending <in>, used after a length of time such as {zan 3} or {kal 3}: staying that many nights or weeks in a place) (r:zd:12674/zd:24029) (q:draft)
tamkhin = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:already many/already much) (d:<tam>, many, and <khin>, already, written as one word: already great in number or amount) (j:tam/khin) (r:zd:25461) (q:draft)
tamkhollo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not many/not much/few) (d:<tam>, many, and <khollo>, not very, written as one word: not very many, not much) (j:tam/khollo) (r:zd:20749/zd:15362) (q:draft)
tamkhop = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:quite many/a good many/a fair number) (d:<tam>, many, and <khop>, enough, written as one word: a fair number, quite a lot, said of people or things) (j:tam/khop) (r:zd:13239/zd:25164) (q:draft)
tamlai = (i:2) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be still many/be still much/remain plenty) (d:<tam>, many, with <lai>, still: there is still a lot of something, mostly followed by <mahmah>; not the sense stay) (r:zd:21030/zd:20264/zd:24594) (q:draft)
tamleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:if there is much/when there are many) (d:<tam>, many, and <leh>, if, written as one word: if or when something is much or many, the more there is of it) (j:tam/leh) (r:zd:16060/zd:12938) (q:draft)
tamlo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:few/not many/not much) (d:<tam>, many, and <lo>, not, written as one word: not many, only a few) (s:tawm) (j:tam/lo) (r:zd:24375/zd:14903) (q:draft)
tamloh = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not many/few/not much) (d:<tam>, many, and <loh>, not, written as one word, the form used before words such as <manin> and <hangin>: not being many, not much) (j:tam/loh) (r:zd:24530/zd:24176) (q:draft)
tamlualo = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:not very many/not much) (d:<tam>, many, and <lualo>, not very, written as one word: not very many, not much) (j:tam/lualo) (r:zd:15512/zd:13034) (q:draft)
tamluatna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/nature) (w:excess/too much/overabundance) (d:<tamluat>, be too much, with the noun suffix {-na}: there being too much of something; {guahtui tamluatna hangin} is because of too much rain) (b:tamluat) (r:zd:17628/zd:15342) (q:draft)
tammahmah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very many/very much) (d:<tam> and <mahmah> written as one word: very many, a great deal) (j:tam/mahmah) (r:zd:16061/zd:23896/zd:14959) (q:draft)
tammahmahlai = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:still very many/still a great many) (d:<tammahmah>, very many, and <lai>, still, written as one word: there are still very many) (j:tammahmah/lai) (r:zd:17735/zd:14648) (q:draft)
tamman = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:work/everyday) (w:expensive/costly/high-priced) (d:<tam>, much, with <man>, price: costing much; the opposite is {tawm man}, cheap) (j:tam/man) (r:zd:13161/zd:25043/zd:17133) (q:draft)
tammanh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:work) (w:cost much/be costly/be expensive) (d:<tam>, much, and <manh>, cost, written as one word: cost a lot, use up much money) (j:tam/manh) (r:zd:21259/zd:11431) (q:draft, low confidence)
