tamphadiak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:especially many/particularly frequent) (d:<tam> and <phadiak> written as one word: many or frequent to a special degree, more than elsewhere or at other times) (j:tam/phadiak) (r:zd:12457/zd:11752/zd:15342) (q:draft)
tampi = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:numerous/many/much) (d:a large number or amount of something, placed after the noun: {mi tampi} is many people and {thu tampi} many things) (s:tam/tampite) (a:tawm/tawmno) (b:tam) quantity of being, plural form of <tam>
tampian = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:rather many/quite a lot/somewhat much) (d:<tam>, many, and <pian> written as one word: fairly many or much, or becoming more) (j:tam/pian) (r:zd:23639/zd:16247) (q:draft)
tampimah = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very many/a great many) (d:<tampi> and <mah> written as one word, placed after the noun: a great many, very much) (j:tampi/mah) (r:zd:23590/zd:20023) (q:draft)
tampin = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:many) (d:<tampi> with a shortened <in> written as one word: many, as the doer of the action; {mi tampin} is many people did. With a capital it is also a town in Malaysia.) (j:tampi/in) (r:zd:21939) (q:draft, low confidence)
