tamsemsem = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:more and more/increasing) (d:<tam>, many, with <semsem> written as one word: growing in number all the time) (j:tam/semsem) (r:zd:11401/zd:14665) (q:draft)
tamsim = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:quite many/a good many/fairly many) (d:<tam>, many, with the ending {-sim}, rather: a fair number or amount, more than a few) (b:tam) (r:zd:23661/zd:21974) (q:draft)
tamta = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday/time) (w:already many/many by now) (d:<tam>, many, and <ta>, here the word for a state now reached, written as one word: have become many, as in {akum tamta}, his years are many by now) (j:tam/ta) (r:zd:14579) (q:draft, low confidence)
tamtam = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:very many/a great many/much) (d:<tam>, many, said twice for force: many and many, in great number; {kam tamtam} is talking a great deal) (b:tam) (r:zd:24064/zd:15770) (q:draft)
tamthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be frequent/tend to be many/be common) (d:<tam>, many, and <thei>, can, written as one word: can be many, happen often or in great number) (j:tam/thei) (r:zd:17689/zd:17913/zd:19831) (q:draft)
tamto = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:increase/grow in number) (d:<tam>, many, and <to>, upward, written as one word: become more, rise in number; often followed by <semsem>, more and more) (j:tam/to) (r:zd:14858/zd:18024) (q:draft)
tamtuak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:quite many/a good many) (d:<tam>, many, with <tuak>: there are quite a number, as in {tamtuak mahmah lai hi}, there are still a great many) (j:tam/tuak) (r:zd:22860) (q:draft, low confidence)
tamtuam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:be more/increase/become more numerous) (d:<tam>, many, with a second part meaning all the more: be more than before or more than the others) (b:tam) (r:zd:17060/zd:16817) (q:draft)
