tebang = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:such as/for instance) (d:the plural <te> and <bang> like written as one word after a noun: the likes of these, these for instance; it picks out one group as an example or for emphasis) (j:te/bang) (r:zd:19644/zd:23784) (q:draft)
tebek = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:only those/only) (d:the plural <te> and <bek> written as one word, placed after a noun or clause: only those, they alone) (j:te/bek) (r:zd:15274/zd:23479/zd:22856) (q:draft)
tebel = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:the plural <te> and <bel> written as one word after a noun: as for those, marking a group as the topic, often in contrast with others; <bel> here means as for, not most) (j:te/bel) (r:zd:15606/zd:15187/zd:16720) (q:draft)
