tengkhempeuh = (i:1) (t:pron) (f:everyday) (w:all of/every one of/all these) (d:<teng>, here all those, and <khempeuh>, all, written as one word after a noun or <tua>: every one of them, the whole lot) (j:teng/khempeuh) (r:zd:23037/zd:15099) (q:draft)
tengleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:all and/all the and) (d:<teng>, all of those, and <leh>, and, written as one word: all of the things just named, and also what follows) (j:teng/leh) (r:zd:14628/zd:10735) (q:draft)
tengmah = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:all of/every one of) (d:<teng>, all, and the emphatic <mah> written as one word and placed after a noun phrase: all of those, those very ones without exception) (j:teng/mah) (r:zd:17309/zd:25919) (q:draft)
tengna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (j:tenna) (r:zd:19174/zd:16119/zd:19798) (q:draft)
tengpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:all of these/all those) (d:<teng>, all of the ones named, with the topic marker <pen>, written as one word after a noun or number: all of those, as the topic of the sentence) (r:zd:15317/zd:11635/zd:11148) (q:draft)
tengtawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:with all that/in that state) (d:<teng>, all of those, and <tawh>, with, written as one word; <tuabang tengtawh> is in that condition, with all that) (r:zd:21850/zd:19810) (q:draft)
tengteng = (i:1) (t:det) (f:everyday) (w:all/everything/whatever) (d:<teng>, all, doubled for force and placed after a noun or a verb: every single one, all that there is; {i deih tengteng} is everything we want) (s:khempeuh) (r:zd:16441/zd:24697) (q:draft)
tengtung = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:abruptly/straight away/rashly) (d:placed after a verb for an action done suddenly, without hesitation or second thought) (r:zd:11163/zd:21028) (q:draft, low confidence)
tenguh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:all of their/all that they) (d:<teng>, all, and the plural <uh> written as one word, after a noun or clause: all those that they have or did, as in {amatkhak tenguh}, all whom they caught) (j:teng/uh) (r:zd:19166/zd:25390) (q:draft)
tengza = (i:1) (t:num) (f:work) (w:ten million/hundred lakh) (d:<teng>, lakh, and <za>, hundred, written as one word: one hundred lakh, ten million, used of sums of money) (j:teng/za) (r:zd:15393) (q:draft)
tengzaw = (i:1) (t:v) (f:home/everyday) (w:live mostly/live rather) (d:<teng>, live in a place, and the comparative <zaw> written as one word: live mostly or rather in that place than in another) (j:teng/zaw) (r:zd:9227/zd:9252) (q:draft)
tengzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:all also/even all) (d:<teng>, here in its sense of all of, with <zong>, also, written as one word: placed after a noun, all of it too, the whole of them as well) (j:teng/zong) (r:zd:13324/zd:13129/zd:12717) (q:draft)
tenih = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:the two/both) (d:<te> and <nih> written as one word, after a noun: the two of them; {hih numei tenih} is these two women) (j:te/nih) (r:zd:19396/zd:12290) (q:draft)
