thahlupna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:killing/slaughter/murder) (d:<thahlup>, kill outright, with the noun ending {-na}: the killing of a person or animal, or the place where it was killed) (s:thahna) (b:thahlup) (r:zd:12053/zd:14859) (q:draft)
thahluppen = (i:1) (t:v) (f:politics/media) (w:the killing of/being killed) (d:<thahlup>, kill, and the topic marker <pen>, written as one word; in {aki thahluppen}, the fact that someone was killed) (j:thahlup/pen) (r:zd:15004) (q:draft)
thahlupsawm = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:try to kill/attempt to kill) (d:<thahlup> and <sawm> written as one word: intend or attempt to kill; {amahleh amah ki thahlupsawm} is attempt to kill oneself) (j:thahlup/sawm) (r:zd:11477/zd:12450) (q:draft)
thai = (i:3) (t:n) (f:travel/politics) (w:Thai/Thailand) (d:the country of Thailand or its people, written with a capital letter, mostly before words such as <gamsung>, <kumpi>, <gammi> and <gam>; not the day after tomorrow) (s:Thaigam) (r:zd:17239/zd:15745/zd:11931) (q:draft)
thai kumpi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:Thai government/Thai authorities) (d:{Thai}, of Thailand, and <kumpi>, king, in the news the government: the government of Thailand; a country name before <kumpi> names the government of that country, and it is followed by <in> as the subject or by {thunei te}, the authorities) (r:zd:11931/zd:19442) (q:draft)
Thaiboi = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel/politics) (w:Thaiboi) (d:a village between <Matupi> and Paletwa in the south of Chin State, Myanmar, and the army camp there) (r:ts:4965) (q:draft)
Thaigam = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Thailand) (d:{Thai} with <gam>, country: the country of Thailand) (s:Thailand) (r:zd:18017) (q:draft)
Thailand = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel/politics) (w:Thailand) (d:country in Southeast Asia, east of Myanmar) (r:zd:20889/zd:19100/zd:19285) (q:draft)
thak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:new/fresh) (d:new, not old or used before, also fresh; placed after the noun, as in {la thak}, a new song) (a:lui) (r:42.5.38) (q:draft)
thakding = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:politics/everyday) (w:new/incoming/next) (d:<thak>, new, and <ding> written as one word after a noun: the one who is to be the new holder of an office; after a verb, to do it anew) (j:thak/ding) (r:zd:18882/zd:11275) (q:draft)
thakdingin = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:politics/everyday) (w:as the new/to be the new) (d:<thak>, new, and <dingin> written as one word after the name of an office: as the new holder, to be the new one) (j:thak/dingin) (r:zd:19671) (q:draft)
Thaketa = (i:1) (t:name) (c:place) (f:politics) (w:Thaketa) (d:a township of Yangon in Myanmar) (r:zd:25105) (q:draft)
Thakhin = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:Thakin/master/lord) (d:Burmese word for master or lord; a title written before the name of members of the Burmese nationalist movement before independence, and in {Hpaya thakhin} a Burmese name for God) (o:Burmese, thakhin) (r:zd:14730/zd:15956) (q:draft, low confidence)
thakin = (i:3) (t:adj) (f:politics/media) (w:new) (d:<thak>, new, with the agent marker <in> after a noun or title: the new one as the doer of the action, {President thakin} the new president does something; not the adverb anew) (r:zd:11027) (q:draft, low confidence)
thakkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:a new/a new one) (d:<thak> and <khat> written as one word, after a noun: a new one, as in {ngaihsutna thakkhat}, a new idea) (j:thak/khat) (r:zd:22282/zd:11504) (q:draft)
thakna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:health/body) (w:itching/itch) (d:<thak> in its sense of itch, with <na>: an itching of the skin, named among the signs of an illness as in {ci le sa thakna}; not the sense renewal) (r:zd:23848) (q:draft, low confidence)
thakpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:the new/newest) (d:<thak>, new, and <pen> written as one word after a noun: the new one, as the thing the sentence is about; in some sentences it can also be read as the newest) (j:thak/pen) (r:zd:11587/zd:15517) (q:draft, low confidence)
thaksuakkik = (i:1) (t:v) (f:religion/social) (w:be renewed/be revived/become new again) (d:<thaksuak>, become new, with <kik>, again, written as one word) (j:thaksuak/kik) (r:zd:17634) (q:draft)
thaktawh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday) (w:with the new) (d:<thak>, new, and <tawh>, with, written as one word after a noun) (j:thak/tawh) (r:zd:16600/zd:25090) (q:draft)
thakthak = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:everyday) (w:new/ever new/various new) (d:<thak>, new, doubled: new ones one after another, new things of many kinds, often as {a thakthak}; after a verb, afresh) (b:thak) (r:zd:12948/zd:21605/zd:15652) (q:draft)
thal = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:body/everyday) (w:face up/on one's back/upward) (d:turned or lying with the face upward, mostly as {thal lam}, facing up, and {thal lupsa}, lying on the back; the opposite of <khup.2>, face down, and not the weapon) (r:zd:22658/zd:23554) (q:draft, low confidence)
thala = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:take courage/take heart/be encouraged) (d:<tha> strength taken up: draw strength or courage from something, the opposite of <lungkia>) (r:zd:19245/zd:20697) (q:draft)
thalak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:social/everyday) (w:take strength/draw encouragement/be inspired) (d:<tha>, strength, with <lak>, take, written as one word: draw strength, encouragement or a lesson from something; {thalak kik} is regain strength) (j:tha/lak) (r:zd:24338/zd:22185) (q:draft)
thalakna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/media) (w:encouragement/inspiration) (d:<tha>, strength, with <lakna>, taking: drawing strength or courage from a story, a life or a word, common in titles as {tungpan thalakna}, encouragement drawn from) (j:tha/lakna) (r:zd:20801/zd:20058) (q:draft)
thalawpna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:everyday/social) (w:enthusiasm/zeal/morale/motivation) (d:eagerness and energy for a task, the noun of <thalawp>) (b:thalawp) (r:zd:16695/zd:23554/zd:21362) (q:draft)
thalawpsak = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:encourage/inspire/motivate/energise) (d:<thalawp>, eager, with the causative <sak>: give someone strength and eagerness, lift the spirits) (b:thalawp) (r:zd:24673/zd:20806) (q:draft)
thaleh = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/body) (w:strength and) (d:<tha>, strength, and <leh>, and, written as one word) (j:tha/leh) (r:zd:21876) (q:draft)
thalengal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work/everyday) (w:strength/labour/physical effort) (d:bodily strength and effort given to a work; often paired with <sumlepai>, money, as the two things a person can give) (r:zd:24012/zd:25354) (q:draft)
thalh = (i:1) (t:v) (f:health/food) (w:choke/get stuck in the throat) (d:of food or drink, stick in the throat or go down the wrong way; of a person, choke on it) (r:zd:23543/zd:18110) (q:draft)
Thallam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:body/everyday) (w:face up/upward) (d:<thal> and <lam> written as one word: facing upward; the saying {thallam cilsiat} is spitting upward, which falls back on oneself) (j:thal/lam) (r:zd:21862) (q:draft, low confidence)
Thalloh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:household steward) (d:one of the appointed positions in the traditional Zomi household council, a close kinsman who takes the lead in the affairs of the household; the exact duties are not confirmed) (r:zd:23990) (q:draft, low confidence)
thallup = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:lie on one's back/lie face up) (d:<thal>, face up, and <lup>, lie down, written as one word) (j:thal/lup) (r:zd:9432/zd:17553) (q:draft)
Thalmual = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel/social) (w:Thalmual) (d:a Zomi village; written after the name of a person it shows the village the person comes from) (r:zd:23054/zd:24297) (q:draft)
thalnial = (i:2) (t:v) (f:social/politics) (w:deny/reject/object to) (d:say that an accusation, a decision or a statement is not so, or refuse to accept it; in the articles used of a person who denies charges or objects to what others decided, where the Bible sense is the knocking down of arguments) (s:nial) (r:ts:2438/zd:20477/zd:21908) (q:draft)
thalnialna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:objection/rejection/protest) (d:the act of rejecting or objecting to a decision or a wrong, from <thalnial>, reject, with the noun ending {-na}) (b:thalnial) (r:zd:22595/zd:24943) (q:draft)
thaltuk = (i:1) (t:v) (f:body/everyday) (w:fall backward/fall on one's back) (d:<thal.2>, face up, and <tuk>, fall, written as one word: fall over backward) (j:thal/tuk) (r:zd:12337/zd:22928) (q:draft, low confidence)
tham = (i:3) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:far/much/by far) (d:after a comparative with <zaw>, as in <tamzaw tham> and {hoihzaw tham}, it strengthens the comparison: far more, much better; unlike {tham loin}, not only) (r:zd:23332/ts:3707/zd:12544) (q:draft)
thamanh = (i:1) (t:n) (f:work) (j:thaman) (r:zd:25617/zd:21399) (q:draft)
