ummawhlo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:not suspect/not think likely) (d:<ummawh>, suspect, and <lo>, not, written as one word; {ki ummawhlo} is it is not suspected, it is not thought to be so) (j:ummawh/lo) (r:zd:16391/zd:20331) (q:draft)
ummawhna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social/politics) (w:suspicion/surmise) (d:<ummawh>, suspect, with the noun ending {-na}: what someone suspects or supposes to be so without knowing it for certain) (b:ummawh) (r:zd:16628/ts:2529) (q:draft)
ummawhpa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/media) (w:suspect/suspected man) (d:<ummawh>, suspect, and <pa>, man, written as one word; with <aki> before it, the man who is suspected) (j:ummawh/pa) (r:zd:13059/zd:11217) (q:draft)
ummawhpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:suspect at once/immediately suppose) (d:<ummawh>, suspect, and <pah>, at once, written as one word; {ki ummawhpah} is it was at once suspected) (j:ummawh/pah) (r:zd:12021/zd:13243) (q:draft)
ummawhpen = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/media) (w:what is suspected) (d:<ummawh>, suspect, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word, mostly after <aki>: what is suspected, the thing suspected) (j:ummawh/pen) (r:zd:19191/zd:19699) (q:draft)
ummawhtek = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/media) (w:be suspected/be supposed) (d:<ummawh> and <tek> written as one word, after <ki>: it is suspected or supposed by people in general) (j:ummawh/tek) (r:zd:18145/zd:16665) (q:draft, low confidence)
ummi = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:believer) (d:<um>, believe, with <mi>, person: one who believes; mostly as {thu ummi} or {thu-ummi}, a believer in the word, a Christian) (r:zd:23492/zd:13354) (q:draft)
ummite = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion) (w:believers) (d:<um>, believe, with <mite>, people: those who believe, mostly written {thu-ummite}) (s:umte) (r:zd:14791/zd:19772) (q:draft)
umna = (i:2) (t:n) (f:food/social/religion) (w:meal together/feast/supper) (d:after <ankuang> or <annkuang>, the sitting round a dish to eat together: a shared meal or feast, and in church {Topa Nitak Annkuang Umna}, the Lord's Supper; not a wall or fence) (r:zd:11429/zd:23113) (q:draft)
Umno = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:UMNO/United Malays National Organisation) (d:political party of Malaysia, mostly written UMNO) (r:zd:19602/zd:16637) (q:draft)
umpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:believe at once/believe readily) (d:<um> and <pah> written as one word: believe a thing straight away, without weighing it) (j:um/pah) (r:zd:22116/zd:23492) (q:draft)
umpahpah = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:believe at once/believe readily) (d:<um>, believe, and <pahpah>, at once, written as one word: believe a thing straight away without checking) (j:um/pahpah) (r:zd:17830) (q:draft)
umthei = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/religion) (w:can believe/be able to believe) (d:<um> and <thei> written as one word: be able to believe) (j:um/thei) (r:zd:11974) (q:draft)
umzolo = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday) (w:cannot believe/be unable to believe) (d:<umzo>, be able to believe, and <lo>, not, written as one word) (j:umzo/lo) (r:zd:21850) (q:draft)
un card = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:UN card/UNHCR card/refugee card) (d:UN, the United Nations, and <card>: the card that the refugee office of the United Nations, UNHCR, gives to a registered refugee or asylum seeker; written {UN card}) (r:zd:10892/zd:12695) (q:draft)
un laidal = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics/social) (w:UN document/UNHCR letter) (d:UN, the United Nations, and <laidal>, a sheet of writing: the paper issued by the UN refugee agency to a registered asylum seeker, named beside the {UN card}; used with <nei>, <tawi> or <ngah>, to hold or get one) (r:zd:23446/zd:20168) (q:draft)
UNA = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:United Nationalities Alliance/UNA) (d:alliance of political parties of the ethnic nationalities in Myanmar, named beside the NLD) (r:zd:11103) (q:draft, low confidence)
unaukhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:family/social) (w:one family/brothers of one family) (d:<unau> and <khat> written as one word: siblings who are one, people who belong together as one family) (j:unau/khat) (r:zd:21690/zd:17120) (q:draft)
unaupen = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:the siblings/the brothers) (d:<unau>, siblings, and the topic marker <pen> written as one word: the siblings, as the ones spoken about) (j:unau/pen) (r:zd:17731/zd:11558) (q:draft)
unaupeng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:twins/twin siblings) (d:<unau>, siblings, and a second part meaning twin: brothers or sisters born as twins) (r:zd:15958/zd:16696) (q:draft)
unauteng = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family) (w:all the siblings/all the brothers and sisters) (d:<unau> and <teng>, all, written as one word: all the brothers and sisters of a family together) (j:unau/teng) (r:zd:15767/zd:19098) (q:draft)
Uncle = (i:1) (t:n) (f:family/social) (w:uncle) (d:an uncle, and a polite way to address or speak of an older man) (o:English) (r:zd:11251/zd:13309) (q:draft)
Underwear = (i:1) (t:n) (f:home) (w:underwear) (d:clothing worn under other clothes; mostly written with a capital and often added to explain <bombi sungten>) (o:English) (r:zd:19707) (q:draft, low confidence)
UNDP = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:UNDP/United Nations Development Programme) (d:the development agency of the United Nations, named by its English abbreviation) (o:English) (r:zd:19172/zd:15523) (q:draft)
