University = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:university) (d:a place of higher education that gives degrees, often after its name) (o:English) (r:zd:22981/zd:23780/zd:12244) (q:draft)
universityte = (i:1) (t:n) (f:education) (w:universities) (d:the English word university with the plural ending <te>: universities) (o:English) (r:zd:22803/zd:11548) (q:draft)
unla = (i:2) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:and) (d:<un>, the plural ending of a command, with <la>, and: closes a command to several people when another command follows, as in {pai unla}, go and; <kei unla> is do not, and; not a marker of the subject) (r:zd:9448/zd:25137/zd:23792) (q:draft)
unmaw = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:do/please do) (d:<un> and <maw> written as one word, at the end of a request to several people: do so, will you) (j:un/maw) (r:zd:17353/zd:12611/zd:13072) (q:draft)
UNO = (i:1) (t:name) (f:politics) (w:United Nations/UNO) (d:the United Nations Organization) (r:zd:15905/zd:22381) (q:draft)
unteh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:sentence-final ending for a plural subject, short for {uh inteh}: they will, they probably will; followed by <maw> it asks the hearer to agree) (r:zd:24327/zd:24749) (q:draft)
unzong = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:also/even) (d:<un> and <zong> written as one word: the plural ending <un> that closes the phrase before it, followed by <zong>, also or even) (j:un/zong) (r:zd:19788/zd:16216) (q:draft, low confidence)
upa = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:elder/leader) (d:an elder or leader of a people, a town or a church; {pawlpi upa} is a church elder and {upa vaihawmte} are the ruling council) (s:makai) (r:64.1.1) (q:draft)
upa = (i:2) (t:adj) (f:family/social) (w:elder/older/firstborn) (d:the older one among siblings; {tapa upa pen} is the eldest or firstborn son and {ta upa zaw} the older of two children) (s:uzaw) (a:khangnozaw) (q:draft)
upakhin = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:time/everyday) (w:aged/old/years old) (d:<upa>, older, and <khin>, already, written as one word: having already reached an age, said of people, animals, trees and things; {kum 7 a upakhin} is seven years old, and without a number it means already elderly) (j:upa/khin) (r:zd:20611/zd:15631/zd:19480) (q:draft)
upapenpen = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family) (w:very eldest/oldest of all) (d:<upa> and the doubled <penpen> written as one word: the very eldest of the brothers and sisters or of the children) (s:upapen) (j:upa/penpen) (r:zd:12192/zd:15609) (q:draft)
upazaw = (i:1) (t:adj) (f:family) (w:older/elder) (d:<upa>, elder, and <zaw>, more, written as one word: older than another, the elder of two) (j:upa/zaw) (r:zd:18128/zd:12409/zd:10721) (q:draft)
