Vermont = (i:1) (t:name) (c:land) (f:travel) (w:Vermont) (d:a state in the north-east of the United States of America) (r:zd:9224) (q:draft)
verse = (i:1) (t:n) (f:religion/education) (w:verse) (d:a numbered verse of a holy book, written before or after its number) (o:English) (r:zd:19679/zd:24377) (q:draft)
version = (i:1) (t:n) (f:media/it) (w:version/edition) (d:one form of a text, a translation or a program among several, as an English version of a statement or a version of the Bible) (o:English) (r:zd:23272/zd:14789/zd:12441) (q:draft)
veteh = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:closes an exclamation addressed to the hearer, often followed by <aw>: <ve> with <teh>, here not when; the speaker remarks on what the hearer is or does, as in {manglua veteh-aw}, you really obey too much) (r:zd:25562) (q:draft, low confidence)
vetkei = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all) (d:<vet> and <kei> written as one word after a verb: not at all; before <in> it forbids, do not at all) (j:vet/kei) (r:zd:24029/zd:17060/zd:20652) (q:draft)
vetkeng = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (w:not at all) (d:<vet>, at all, with the first person negative ending that is short for {kei ing}, written as one word after a verb: I do not at all, I never) (r:zd:19603/zd:14583) (q:draft)
vetlo = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/never) (d:the emphatic <vet> and <lo>, not, written as one word: placed after a verb, not at all, not in the least) (j:vet/lo) (r:zd:20484/zd:24742/zd:11163) (q:draft)
vetloh = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:not at all/not even) (d:<vet> and <loh> written as one word after a verb: not at all; the form taken before <ding>, <hi> and <na>, and {gen vetloh} is not even to be spoken of) (j:vet/loh) (r:zd:25923/zd:25917) (q:draft)
veto = (i:1) (t:n) (f:politics) (w:veto) (d:the right of one member or office to stop a decision, mostly as {veto power}) (o:English) (r:ts:3284) (q:draft)
vetse = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:<vet> and <se> written as one word: emphatic particle after a verb or describing word, really, indeed; after <lo>, not at all) (j:vet/se) (r:zd:23113/zd:16356) (q:draft, low confidence)
veuvau = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (d:expressive word placed after a verb such as <tuang>, ride, <tuto>, sit up on, or <dakkhia>, look out: it seems to picture something perched up on top or sticking out above in plain view; the exact sense is to be confirmed) (r:zd:21385/zd:21908) (q:draft, low confidence)
veuveu = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday/food) (d:placed after a verb for something that keeps coming steadily, as steam or a good smell rising from food; also of an action done again and again) (r:zd:19812/zd:25673) (q:draft, low confidence)
veve lel = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:all the same/still anyway/just the same) (d:<veve>, still, nevertheless, and <lel>, just, merely, not the verb lose: placed after a verb and before the sentence-final word, the thing holds all the same in spite of what was said before, often after a clause with <hangin> or <zong>) (r:zd:21254/zd:21081) (q:draft)
veveding = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:will still/will anyway) (d:<veve> and <ding> written as one word, after a verb: will do or be so all the same) (j:veve/ding) (r:zd:11695/zd:11635/zd:14925) (q:draft)
vevelai = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:still/all the same) (d:<veve>, nevertheless, and <lai>, still, written as one word after a verb: the action still goes on in spite of what was said before) (j:veve/lai) (r:zd:20767/zd:15471) (q:draft)
vevemawk = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:still/all the same/nevertheless) (d:<veve> and <mawk> written as one word after a verb: all the same, even so, often of something unwelcome or unexpected) (j:veve/mawk) (r:zd:15496/zd:17067) (q:draft)
vevesam = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:all the same/nevertheless/anyway) (d:<veve>, all the same, with the ending {-sam} written as one word, after a verb: it was done or is so all the same) (r:zd:12979/zd:16365) (q:draft, low confidence)
vevua = (i:1) (t:part) (f:everyday) (d:words of urging at the end of a sentence addressed to several people, <ve> with the plural command ending: do go ahead, please do; often followed by <leh>) (r:zd:23081/zd:22658) (q:draft, low confidence)
vial = (i:4) (t:n) (f:everyday) (w:round/lap/circuit/turn) (d:one going round or one trip there and back, counted with a number as {vial khat}, one round, and {vial nih}, two rounds) (r:zd:23767/zd:25346/zd:25393) (q:draft)
Vialcian = (i:1) (t:name) (c:khua) (f:travel) (w:Vialcian) (d:village in the Tonzang area of northern Chin State in Myanmar) (r:zd:21259/zd:25114) (q:draft)
vialkhat = (i:1) (t:phrase) (f:everyday/travel) (w:one round/one circuit/one lap) (d:<vial>, a turn around, with <khat>, one: one full round, as of the moon around the earth or a train around its loop) (j:vial/khat) (r:zd:19578) (q:draft)
viallum = (i:1) (t:v) (f:nature) (w:coil to death/squeeze to death/strangle) (d:<vial>, coil around, with <lum>, to death: of a snake, kill by coiling around the victim) (j:vial/lum) (r:zd:17446) (q:draft, low confidence)
viatvuat = (i:1) (t:adv) (f:nature) (w:glistening/gleaming white) (d:describes the bright white gleam of snow lying everywhere; meaning inferred from two passages about snow) (r:zd:19814/zd:19812) (q:draft, low confidence)
viauviau = (i:2) (t:adv) (f:everyday/nature) (w:in puffs/billowing) (d:of smoke, rising or being blown out in puff after puff, after {za teep}, smoke tobacco, <khusak> and <meikhu>; the other sense is of a smell spreading) (r:zd:10929/zd:25165/zd:16304) (q:draft)
viauviau = (i:3) (t:adv) (f:everyday) (w:steadily onward/without hesitation) (d:of going forward, on and on without stopping or holding back, after a verb of movement such as <mainawt>, advance, and <kantan>, cross over) (r:zd:25678/zd:24733) (q:draft, low confidence)
viber = (i:1) (t:n) (f:it) (w:Viber) (d:application for messages and calls on a phone, much used among the Zomi) (r:zd:12357/zd:16813) (q:draft)
