zuun = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:tend/maintain/put in order/restore) (d:look after something and keep it in good order, often paired with <puah>, repair) (r:zd:25235/zd:16661) (q:draft)
zuunin = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:tending/maintaining/putting in order) (d:<zuun>, tend or put in order, with the linking <in>, written as one word: tending and, followed by another verb) (j:zuun/in) (r:ts:11679/zd:24673) (q:draft)
zuunna = (i:1) (t:n) (f:social) (w:tending/putting in order/maintenance) (d:<zuun>, tend and put in order, with the noun ending {-na}; {minam zuunna} is the tending and building up of a people) (b:zuun) (r:zd:22140) (q:draft, low confidence)
zuunsiam = (i:1) (t:v) (f:everyday/social) (w:handle well/manage skilfully) (d:<zuun>, tend or put in order, with <siam>, skilled: know how to handle or arrange something well) (j:zuun/siam) (r:zd:23488) (q:draft, low confidence)
